window.AKK_AN_INNOCENT_GIRL_SEEKING_A_HUSBAND_WAS_DECEIVED_AND_MARRIED_A_CHILDLESS_OFFICER_CRYING_WITH_EMOTION_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_AN_INNOCENT_GIRL_SEEKING_A_HUSBAND_WAS_DECEIVED_AND_MARRIED_A_CHILDLESS_OFFICER_CRYING_WITH_EMOTION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":101,"title":"Chapter 101: Injured and Hospitalized","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu thanked Huang Erling and brought the fried dough sticks and goat's milk back inside.","The goat's milk was bought from the street vendors next to the supply and marketing cooperative. That area was dedicated to vendors selling breakfast and agricultural products; some didn't require ration coupons, and the prices were quite reasonable.","However, the goat's milk was cold and had to be boiled before drinking. Otherwise, drinking raw goat's milk could easily make one sick.","Qiao Lanshu poured the goat's milk into an aluminum pot and turned on the stove to heat it up. After washing up, she came back to eat her breakfast.","The fried dough sticks had gone a bit cold, and the goat's milk had a strong gamey smell. Qiao Lanshu took out the honey Qin Yuanzheng had bought for her, added a spoonful of it to the milk, and dropped in a small pinch of tea leaves.","The hot goat's milk steeped the fresh tea leaves, and combined with the sweet honey, it tasted much better.","Qiao Lanshu drank a cup of the goat's milk, finished the fried dough sticks, and then put on her nice clothes, a hat, and a scarf before heading out to work.","Qin Yuanzheng hadn't come back all night, and Qiao Lanshu was starting to miss him.","Before, Qin Yuanzheng was always clinging to her, wanting to hold her as soon as they got into bed, which had made her used to his presence.","When Qiao Lanshu stepped out and reached the main gate of the residential compound, she saw the car Qin Yuanzheng usually drove parked there.","Her heart skipped a beat. She hurried over and looked inside.","Then, she was instantly disappointed.","Because the person sitting in the car was Young Company Commander Yang, not Qin Yuanzheng.","Xiao Yang had also just driven over. Seeing Qiao Lanshu, he smiled and said to her, \"Sister-in-law, our commander is too busy, so he asked me to come pick you up for work.\"","Qiao Lanshu opened the car door and sat in the back. She couldn't help but ask Xiao Yang, \"Xiao Yang, what has your commander been so busy with? Is there suddenly some special mission? He didn't come back at all last night.\"","He had left right after eating, and it had been a whole night now.","Xiao Yang started the car and explained to Qiao Lanshu, \"Sister-in-law, originally we were supposed to finish our meeting at three in the morning and dismiss everyone. But there was an accident at one of the coal mines. The explosives were placed wrong, and it almost collapsed. The commander took people over in the middle of the night to rescue them. Fortunately, nothing major happened.\"","Coal mines were prone to accidents, so everything had to be handled with extreme caution.","As the commander in charge of the mining area, Qin Yuanzheng bore the primary responsibility for these matters.","Qiao Lanshu also knew the severity of these things. She said softly, \"So that's how it is.\"","Xiao Yang added, \"Don't worry, Sister-in-law. The commander will definitely be back tonight. The situation should be resolved by then.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and didn't ask any more questions.","After all, these were military matters, and she usually didn't dare to ask too much.","After arriving at the food factory, Xiao Yang drove back to the mining area.","Qiao Lanshu stood there, watching Xiao Yang leave, before preparing to enter the food factory.","At that moment, Liu Weihong, the supervisor of the pastry workshop, also stepped out of a car, though this one wasn't a military vehicle.","Qiao Lanshu glanced at it but couldn't tell which unit it belonged to.","Liu Weihong was still wearing her beautiful cashmere coat, wrapped in a brand-new checkered scarf, and sporting her newly bought leather boots.","When she saw Qiao Lanshu, she deliberately gloated, \"Oh my, I heard there was an accident at the mining area yesterday? It seems a coal mine was blown up and collapsed?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu paused her steps, looked at her, and asked, \"Is that so? I didn't know. Who did you hear that from?\"","Liu Weihong put her hands in her pockets and walked past Qiao Lanshu, saying as she went:","\"You actually didn't know? Didn't your commander tell you? Oh, right, I almost forgot, he definitely didn't come home last night, did he? Ah, it doesn't matter who I heard it from. What matters is, I heard the situation was critical. When your commander went down into the mine shaft for the rescue, he was crushed by falling rocks and injured. He's still in the hospital right now.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu stopped dead in her tracks. She stood where she was, staring at Liu Weihong.","She didn't know what expression was on her face at that moment, but she felt incredibly cold, as if all the blood in her body had been instantly frozen, and a bitter wind was howling straight into her heart.","Even though she knew Liu Weihong had always disliked her.","Perhaps she was deliberately saying these things to provoke her, to make her suffer, and to laugh at her misery.","But she had to admit, this tactic worked perfectly.","Because the person she cared about most was Qin Yuanzheng.","In her previous life, Qin Yuanzheng had been injured by explosives while carrying out a mission. His life had hung by a thread, and he was barely saved.","It was precisely because of that incident that Qin Yuanzheng's body was left with severe lingering effects.","Only five years after they married, he passed away due to a relapse of his injuries.","At that time, Qin Yuanzheng was only in his forties.","Qiao Lanshu looked at Liu Weihong and said, \"You're lying to me. I won't believe a single word you say.\"","Although she said that out loud, in her heart, she already believed it.","Qin Yuanzheng had asked Huang Erling to help buy breakfast and had Xiao Yang drop her off at work.","He was probably truly injured and couldn't come back, yet worried she would find out, so he had arranged everything in advance.","By the time he couldn't hide it anymore, he would probably leave the hospital early and come back to find her.","He had always been this kind of person, spoiling her like a child, never telling her anything for fear she wouldn't be able to handle it.","Hearing this, Liu Weihong laughed and said, \"Why would I need to lie to you about this? Whether it's true or not, can't you just go to the military hospital and see for yourself? Sigh, it's such a pity. Tell me, are you a jinx to your husband? Commander Qin has always been perfectly fine and has carried out so many difficult missions. How come the moment he marries you, something like this happens?\"","Qiao Lanshu stared at Liu Weihong for a moment before saying coldly, \"Liu Weihong, you dislike me so much, you compare yourself to me at every turn, and you keep talking about Commander Qin. Is it because you like Commander Qin and you're jealous that I was able to marry him and receive his affection?\"","Hearing this, Liu Weihong's expression instantly changed. She said fiercely, \"Bullshit! Who would fancy a man who can't have children? Stop putting gold on his face, it's disgusting.\"","Qiao Lanshu kept a cold face: \"Is that so? I thought you were suffering from unrequited love for Commander Qin, which was why you were acting like this. So that's not it? Did I misunderstand you?\"","Liu Weihong: \"...\"","Liu Weihong flushed bright red with anger at Qiao Lanshu's words.","In truth, Qiao Lanshu had hit the nail right on the head regarding Liu Weihong's secret feelings.","She really was brooding over the fact that Qin Yuanzheng hadn't taken a fancy to her.","In her eyes, there was nothing good about Qiao Lanshu: she was short, skinny, young, and an outsider.","As for herself, her family background was good, she was a workshop supervisor, tall, and good-looking. How was she inferior to Qiao Lanshu?","Could it be that Qin Yuanzheng's tastes were just that bizarre, and he simply liked short girls?","Qiao Lanshu was in no mood to argue with Liu Weihong anymore. She immediately turned around, went into the food factory office, asked the logistics department supervisor for a leave of absence, and then walked out of the factory, preparing to go to the military hospital to see for herself.","The military hospital wasn't close to the food factory; she still had to take a bus to get there.","At this very moment, however, Qiao Lanshu was calmer than she had ever been before. She didn't panic, nor did she cry.","All she felt was an overwhelming sense of guilt and regret. She regretted not warning Qin Yuanzheng in advance, not telling him that he would be injured by explosives in a future mission so that he could be on his guard.","If Qin Yuanzheng really had been caught in another explosion this time, no matter how severe his injuries were, she would never turn her back on him.","She would take care of him herself. He had better not die on her so easily; otherwise, she wouldn't be able to go on living either.","The more Qiao Lanshu thought about it, the faster she walked. By the time she reached the bus stop, as she stood there waiting for the bus, she could feel her hands trembling."]},{"number":102,"title":"Chapter 102: He Has to Be the One to Comfort Me When I Cry","paragraphs":["While Qiao Lanshu was waiting at the bus stop, a car slowly pulled up and stopped right in front of her.","Qiao Lanshu was entirely focused on waiting for the bus and paid no attention to it.","After all, her mind was in total turmoil. Her thoughts were completely consumed by Qin Yuanzheng; she was worried sick about his injuries and had no idea what to do next.","At that moment, the door of the car parked in front of her opened, and Guan Wenjun, whom she hadn't seen in a long time, stepped out.","Guan Wenjun was wearing a black overcoat, his hair slicked back as usual. As he got out of the car, he said to Qiao Lanshu, \"What a coincidence, Comrade Xiao Qiao. Where are you heading?\"","Guan Wenjun had been quite busy lately. Normally at this time, he should have been at work at the Revolutionary Committee.","However, he had also received the news of Qin Yuanzheng's injury.","After all, this matter had not been kept a secret. Everyone in the mining district's military unit, as well as several related key departments, knew about it.","An accident had occurred at the mining area in the middle of the night yesterday. A mine shaft had collapsed, and the troops went to provide support. Qin Yuanzheng, who had taken the lead, was injured.","When Guan Wenjun heard about this, he even said to his subordinate, \"Oh my, how did Qin Yuanzheng get hurt? He didn't die, did he?\"","Looking at the expectant look in Guan Wenjun's eyes, the subordinate realized that Guan Wenjun wasn't asking out of concern for Qin Yuanzheng, but rather as if he was eager for him to be dead.","The subordinate relayed the information he had gathered: \"He's injured, but it's still unclear how bad it is. They are keeping a tight lid on the details over there, so it's hard for us to inquire further. But rest assured, he is definitely not dead.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun said with a hint of regret, \"Ah, so he didn't die? I was just worrying about what his wife would do if he had passed away...\"","The subordinate: \"...\"","What a pity, he really thought Qin Yuanzheng had died.","If Qin Yuanzheng was gone, his little wife was still so young, and her maiden family was thousands of kilometers away. How difficult would it be for a young girl like her to be all alone here?","In that case, as Qin Yuanzheng's good friend, Guan Wenjun would naturally have to pay her a visit to pay his respects and take good care of the young girl.","If it came down to it, he could offer her a warm embrace, a safe harbor...","As Guan Wenjun let his imagination run wild, he started to sigh again.","He grabbed his car keys and said to his subordinate, \"He's at the military hospital, right? I'll go see him.\"","Guan Wenjun then drove out, and halfway there, he spotted Qiao Lanshu waiting for the bus at the station.","When Qiao Lanshu saw Guan Wenjun walking over, she finally snapped back to reality and asked in surprise, \"Director Guan? What are you doing here?\"","She actually hadn't noticed him at all just a moment ago!","Guan Wenjun looked at her surprised expression and said, \"What was going on in that little head of yours just now? I've been here for a while, and you only just noticed?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun gestured with his chin and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Are you waiting for the bus to the military hospital? I happen to be heading there too. Come on, I'll give you a ride.\"","If Qiao Lanshu still had any doubts about Liu Weihong's words, her heart completely sank upon hearing what Guan Wenjun just said.","She didn't even have the courage to ask Guan Wenjun about Qin Yuanzheng's situation.","With a stiff expression, she nodded. \"Alright, thank you, Director Guan.\"","Saying that, she got into the car. She sat inside with ice-cold hands and feet, a look of utter helplessness on her face.","Seeing her wear such an expression, Guan Wenjun couldn't help but feel a pang of heartache for her.","If Qin Yuanzheng saw her like this, wouldn't he just tear his heart out for her?","Guan Wenjun muttered, \"Is this girl toxic or something?\"","How could she be so seductive?","He realized that every time he saw Qiao Lanshu, he would be drawn to her. Seeing her sad made his own heart ache as well.","Wasn't that just like being poisoned?","Guan Wenjun sighed and drove the car toward the military hospital.","...","At this very moment, on the second floor of the military hospital, in Ward 203.","Qin Yuanzheng sat bare-chested on the bed, wearing military trousers and boots. His body and face were covered in black grime. He had rushed out of the mine so hurriedly that he hadn't had time to wash off the coal dust.","A nurse was applying medicine to his arm, while Staff Officer Lin stood beside him, equally blackened and dirty.","Lin Yucheng said, \"My dear Regiment Commander, the doctor just said you need to stay in the hospital for a day of observation to make sure everything is fine before you leave. What's the rush? Where are you trying to go?\"","Qin Yuanzheng's arm had been smashed by a rock, leaving a rather deep wound.","It happened when he went down into the mine to rescue the workers. He had shielded a worker, which was why he got hit.","He had bled quite a bit at the time, and the deep wound had scared everyone.","Carrying the injured worker out of the mine, Qin Yuanzheng had told his worried comrades, \"The bone is fine. It's just a flesh wound.\"","He could check himself. For them, as long as it wasn't a vital spot and no bones were broken, it wasn't a big deal.","So now, he refused to stay in the hospital. He glanced at Lin Yucheng, who was standing nearby burning with anxiety, and said lightly, \"You're not married, and you don't have a wife waiting for you at home. Of course, you don't know what I'm trying to do.\"","Lin Yucheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"Anyway, I can't explain it to you. The perks of having a family member... you just can't imagine.\"","Lin Yucheng: \"...\"","Lin Yucheng was truly exasperated by Qin Yuanzheng.","He said, \"Yes, yes, yes. There are plenty of things I can't imagine. For example, Regiment Commander, you hiding your injury from your family. What if your family finds out and comes looking for you? That scene... oh man, I can't even imagine!\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng pursed his lips. With a dark expression, he said, \"As long as you guys don't say anything, she won't know.\"","Lin Yucheng said, \"I'm saying *if*, what *if*!\"","Qin Yuanzheng snorted coldly and said, \"There are no ifs!\"","Anyway, the wound was on his arm, and the doctor had already bandaged it. Since there was no bone injury, he didn't need a cast or anything.","He would rest in the hospital for a day. When he went back at night, he would wear a long-sleeved shirt and not take off his clothes, so his little wife wouldn't see it.","He figured in his mind that a flesh wound like this would probably take ten days to half a month to heal. What a pity. For this half month, he probably wouldn't be able to do *that* with his wife.","If his wife found out and was scared to tears, he would have to be the one to coax her."]},{"number":103,"title":"Chapter 103: Injured but Silent","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun was very chatty while driving, asking questions non-stop along the way.","He said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, can I ask what you are really thinking? How did you end up falling for that living Yama, Qin Yuanzheng?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu turned to look at him, saying seriously, \"Brother Zheng is a very good person, how could you say that about him?\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun's expression was very complicated. He glanced at Qiao Lanshu: \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, don't think you can wrongly accuse me just because you're pretty. I wasn't the one who said that; it was spread by the people in the army. Back when I worked with him in the army, he already had this nickname.\"","Qiao Lanshu knew that Guan Wenjun was from the military. He used to be in the same regiment as Qin Yuanzheng, and the two of them used to have a fairly good relationship.","Qiao Lanshu was in a bad mood right now, and she wouldn't allow anyone to speak ill of her Brother Zheng.","So, she deliberately said, \"What? Director Guan, so you also have a military background? I really couldn't tell.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun: \"No, what do you mean by that? Are you saying my character is lacking? That I'm not as great and righteous as your Qin Yuanzheng, right?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"I didn't say that. I just said you don't look like a soldier, I didn't mean your character is bad. You said those words yourself, Director Guan, you can't wrongly accuse me.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun was really speechless. He looked at Qiao Lanshu several times, and then concluded: \"I see it now, you've been poisoned by Qin Yuanzheng. Tell me, what kind of potion did he give you? Tell me, and I'll help you figure out if there's still a cure. We can't hide our sickness for fear of treatment.\"","Qiao Lanshu couldn't be bothered to deal with Guan Wenjun. She was worried about Qin Yuanzheng in her heart, and had no leisure to talk nonsense with him here.","Guan Wenjun secretly thought to himself: he was poisoned by Qiao Lanshu, and Qiao Lanshu was poisoned by Qin Yuanzheng. Wasn't this just a complete disaster?","Forget it, forget it, better go to the hospital first to see how badly Qin Yuanzheng was injured.","When the two arrived at the hospital entrance, Qiao Lanshu quickly opened the car door and got out.","Guan Wenjun followed closely behind.","The two entered the hospital building. Guan Wenjun went to the front desk, took out his ID, and then asked for Qin Yuanzheng's ward.","As a result, the hospital staff unexpectedly wouldn't tell him.","The person at the front desk said, \"I'm sorry, Director Guan, without permission, you cannot enter a soldier's ward to visit.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun's face was very ugly. The hospital staff were also afraid of offending him; after all, he was the director of the provincial revolutionary committee, with a lot of power. Who wasn't afraid of the revolutionary committee these days?","So, the female comrade quickly added, \"However, you can wait here for a moment, I'll go over and ask for you.\"","Guan Wenjun put his ID back into his pocket, adjusted his overcoat, and said, \"Fine, fine, go quickly and come back quickly.\"","The female comrade hurried toward the stairs. Just then, Staff Officer Lin Yucheng came down from the stairs on the second floor.","He was covered in dirt. Except for a wiped-clean face, he had coal ash all over his body. He saw that Qin Yuanzheng's wounds were fine, so he was preparing to go back to the dormitory to take a shower and change clothes.","As soon as he came out, he first saw Guan Wenjun, and then, he saw Qiao Lanshu standing behind Guan Wenjun.","Lin Yucheng: \"???\"","The expression on Lin Yucheng's face was shocked for a moment, then he quickly walked over, completely ignoring Guan Wenjun, and went straight to Qiao Lanshu: \"Sister-in-law? Why are you here?\"","The two of them had even gone on a blind date before, arranged by Qin Yuanzheng.","Now meeting again, he had to call her sister-in-law.","Lin Yucheng actually felt a little bit awkward in his heart, and also a little bit regretful.","Qiao Lanshu recognized Lin Yucheng; she knew he was the chief of staff of Qin Yuanzheng's regiment.","She hurried forward and asked, \"Staff Officer Lin, how is your regiment commander? Can you take me to see him?\"","Lin Yucheng: \"...\"","He was suddenly a bit conflicted. Their regiment commander had just said that this matter should be kept from Qiao Lanshu.","How did Qiao Lanshu find her way to the hospital so quickly?","If he took Qiao Lanshu to the ward now, Regiment Commander Qin couldn't blame him, right?","He hadn't said anything at all.","While he was conflicted, he heard Qiao Lanshu ask him again: \"Staff Officer Lin, are you injured? Have you gone to get a physical checkup?\"","While worrying about Qin Yuanzheng, Qiao Lanshu saw Lin Yucheng looking so dusty and dirty, she really couldn't help but express a word of concern.","Lin Yucheng was so moved.","From last night until now, he had seen who knows how many people, and no one had come to express concern for him.","After all, for a soldier, if he could run, jump, eat, and wasn't bleeding, then he was fine.","But having someone care about him felt different.","He suddenly felt a little embarrassed and said, \"I... I'm fine, not injured. It's mainly Regiment Commander Qin who is injured... Come with me, I'll take you in. Without someone leading the way, you can't get to the second floor.\"","Saying this, Staff Officer Lin quickly turned around and led Qiao Lanshu toward the inpatient department on the second floor.","Qiao Lanshu said gratefully, \"Thank you, Staff Officer Lin. Sorry to trouble you.\"","Lin Yucheng: \"No trouble, no trouble.\"","The one in trouble was their regiment commander; let's see how their regiment commander explains things to Comrade Xiao Qiao later.","After walking a few steps, Lin Yucheng suddenly turned back and said to Guan Wenjun, who was following behind them, \"Director Guan, please stay here. You cannot enter the military inpatient department.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun's brows furrowed slightly, a hint of dissatisfaction and annoyance revealing in his eyes, but he suppressed his emotions and said, \"What's going on! I just want to go in and visit Qin Yuanzheng, can't even this small request be met? After all, we have some history together!\"","However, facing Guan Wenjun's slightly questioning tone, Lin Yucheng appeared calm and serious. He replied:","\"I am really sorry, Director Guan, please understand my difficulties. This is the inpatient department of a military hospital. According to the relevant regulations, without permission or unless you are active military personnel, you are strictly prohibited from entering without authorization! You came from the army, you should know this, so please don't make it difficult for me.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun was a little angry. Ever since he went to the provincial revolutionary committee, really no one dared to show him attitude.","But the revolutionary committee and the military were two different systems; the revolutionary committee really had no jurisdiction over military affairs.","If the military people didn't let him in, he really couldn't go in.","Guan Wenjun said impatiently, \"I just want to go in and see how badly Qin Yuanzheng is injured, whether he's dead or not.\"","Staff Officer Lin: \"...\"","Before Staff Officer Lin could speak, he saw Qiao Lanshu glare at Guan Wenjun and say to him, \"Director Guan, thank you for bringing me here. Now please go back, I am going to see my family member.\"","With that, Qiao Lanshu said as she walked, \"Staff Officer Lin, let's not waste time, let's go up quickly.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun stood at the entrance of the corridor, saying angrily, \"You heartless woman, I was the one who just brought you here!\"","Just because he said he wanted to see if Qin Yuanzheng was dead or alive, Qiao Lanshu got angry.","Did she really love him that much?","He suspected that Qiao Lanshu's brain was filled with nothing but Qin Yuanzheng and water!","In the end, Guan Wenjun turned and walked away, suffocating with frustration.","Qiao Lanshu followed Staff Officer Lin to the inpatient department on the second floor.","She saw guards stationed outside several wards on the second floor.","Staff Officer Lin led Qiao Lanshu to the door of one of the wards and said to her, \"Our regiment commander's ward is right here.\"","With that, he knocked on the door.","Qin Yuanzheng's voice rang out, \"What is it?\"","Staff Officer Lin: \"Commander, it's me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng's voice was a bit cold. Listening to the tone he used with Staff Officer Lin, Qiao Lanshu found it rather novel.","So Brother Zheng had such a cold and aloof image in front of others.","Qin Yuanzheng walked over, opening the door as he spoke, \"Why are you back? Is there another emergency?\"","He was shirtless, his left arm wrapped in thick white bandages. Blood seeped through the gauze, and the smell of disinfectant and medicine hung heavy in the air.","Staff Officer Lin said with a beaming smile, \"Reporting to the Commander, nothing's wrong. It's just that sister-in-law is here, and I showed her the way.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"???\"","Qin Yuanzheng furrowed his brows, a flash of panic in his eyes. \"What? Who is here?\"","Lin Yucheng quickly stepped aside from the doorway, and Qin Yuanzheng saw Qiao Lanshu standing there, looking at him with red-rimmed eyes.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu sniffled, looked at him, and said with a hint of grievance, \"Brother Zheng, why didn't you tell me you were injured?\"","It was a rare sight for Lin Yucheng to see shock and panic on Qin Yuanzheng's face.","Qin Yuanzheng swallowed hard, looking at Qiao Lanshu as he asked, \"Wife, w-why are you here?\"","As he spoke, Qin Yuanzheng shot Lin Yucheng a glare.","His gaze was gloomy and even carried a hint of murderous intent.","Lin Yucheng instantly broke out in a cold sweat. He quickly raised his hand and swore, \"Commander, I wasn't the one who told sister-in-law about this! Besides, even if I wanted to, I didn't have the time!\"","Lin Yucheng: \"When I just went out, I happened to run into sister-in-law. She was with Director Guan from the Revolutionary Committee. Without permission, the two of them couldn't get in, so I just conveniently brought sister-in-law up here.\"","Qin Yuanzheng naturally knew that Staff Officer Lin hadn't been the one to tell her.","But couldn't Staff Officer Lin have told a lie and then sent Qiao Lanshu back home?","Why did he have to bring her all the way here?","Lin Yucheng relaxed his shoulders and signaled to Qin Yuanzheng with his eyes: A soldier of the Republic never lies!","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Lin Yucheng quickly said, \"Commander, sister-in-law, I still have to go back to the mining area to handle some business, so I'll take my leave first. Take your time talking.\"","With that, Lin Yucheng quickly slipped away.","Qin Yuanzheng was a bit panicked. He looked at Qiao Lanshu and said in a low voice, \"Wife, come inside first.\"","There were still two guards at his door; he couldn't let his subordinates see a joke.","Qiao Lanshu obediently followed Qin Yuanzheng inside. As soon as the ward door closed, she held onto Qin Yuanzheng's arm to inspect it.","Qin Yuanzheng's arm was injured; in fact, the wound was quite deep.","But it was already bandaged up now. Although there was some blood seeping out, overall, it didn't look too terrifying.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu's red eyes and said softly, \"Wife, why are you crying? Don't cry, it's just a minor injury, it's nothing serious.\"","Qiao Lanshu's eyes were red and watery, tears pooling in them. She looked at Qin Yuanzheng and cried as she asked him again, \"Why didn't you tell me you were injured? Do you know that when I heard from someone else that you were hurt, I was scared to death? I thought something terrible had happened to you.\"","Saying that, she hugged Qin Yuanzheng and said tearfully, \"You can't hide things from me anymore in the future, you hear? Otherwise, I won't forgive you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng hugged her back, patting her back, and said gently, \"It was too late yesterday, and I was afraid of disturbing your rest. After all, it wasn't anything major, so I figured I would just tell you when I got back this afternoon.\"","In reality, he hadn't planned on telling Qiao Lanshu at all.","But since Qiao Lanshu had already come looking for him, he naturally didn't dare say that.","He could only keep explaining, \"Really, if you hadn't come right now, I would have gone to find you a bit later.\"","As he spoke, he quickly changed the subject, asking, \"Were you scared being home alone last night? Did you leave the lights on when you slept?\"","Qiao Lanshu nestled in his arms and cried for a while before nodding. \"I slept with the lights on. I originally wanted to wait for you to come back, but then I got too sleepy and somehow fell asleep.\"","Hearing her say this, Qin Yuanzheng found it somewhat amusing.","He held Qiao Lanshu, sat on the hospital bed, and asked her again, \"I asked Battalion Commander Zhao to go back and bring you breakfast. Did his wife bring it to you?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded again. \"She did. Fried dough sticks and goat milk. There's still some goat milk left, but I finished both fried dough sticks.\"","Qin Yuanzheng habitually reached out to touch her stomach.","Qiao Lanshu was dressed warmly; since entering the room, she hadn't taken off her padded cotton jacket.","Qin Yuanzheng very smoothly slipped his hand in from the hem of her jacket.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu pressed down on his hand and glared at him. \"At a time like this, you're still thinking about that?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng said, slightly speechless, \"I just wanted to see if you were full and if your tummy was bulging, that's all. I wasn't thinking about anything else.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng smiled, leaning in to look at her. \"Wife, what did you think I was thinking about?\"","Qiao Lanshu pushed his hand away. She walked over to a chair on the side and sat down, saying with some anger, \"I haven't forgiven you yet. Don't talk to me.\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't want to pay attention to him.","This was the first time since they got married.","When coaxing one's wife, of course, one had to be shameless.","Therefore, Qin Yuanzheng leaned over again, brazenly hugging Qiao Lanshu, and said, \"I know I was wrong. I definitely won't dare do it next time. Just forgive me, wife?\"","Qiao Lanshu struggled for a moment but couldn't break free; Qin Yuanzheng only hugged her tighter.","Seeing that he was exerting force with both arms, Qiao Lanshu let out a gasp and quickly got up from the chair. Holding his arm, she scolded, \"Your arm is injured, so behave yourself. Don't move this arm.\"","Looking at Qiao Lanshu's distressed expression, Qin Yuanzheng immediately pretended to be in great pain, whispering, \"Hiss, my arm hurts so much. I pulled the wound.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"???\"","Qiao Lanshu hurriedly supported his arm, asking nervously, \"Does it hurt a lot? Brother Zheng, sit down quickly. Should I go call a doctor for you?\""]},{"number":104,"title":"Chapter 104: The Wound Hurts","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng deliberately said his wound hurt, just to keep Qiao Lanshu from being angry.","When his little wife got angry, she was very hard to coax.","Looking at Qiao Lanshu, it seemed she didn't even want to talk to him.","How could that do?","He loosely covered his bandaged wound with one hand, frowned, leaned on Qiao Lanshu's slender shoulder, and whispered, \"There's no need to call a doctor. It will just hurt for a while. Once I rest a bit, I'll be fine.\"","Saying that, he looked up and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Wifey, can you help me over to sit for a while? My arm is hurting more and more.\"","How could Qiao Lanshu still care about being angry?","She nervously supported Qin Yuanzheng, walking toward the hospital bed, saying as they walked, \"Brother Zheng, are you okay? If it hurts terribly, let's call a doctor to take a look, alright?\"","Call what doctor? When the wound was stitched, anesthesia was applied. The numbness hadn't even worn off yet, so it actually didn't hurt much at all.","If they called a doctor over, what if the doctor let the truth slip?","Qin Yuanzheng sat on the hospital bed and pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms. Then, he buried his face in the crook of her neck, took a deep breath, and whispered, \"No need to call the doctor. As long as you're by my side, it doesn't hurt anymore.\"","As he spoke, he lifted his head again, leaning close to Qiao Lanshu. \"Wifey, give me a kiss?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu only hesitated for a second before Qin Yuanzheng immediately groaned and frowned again. \"Ah, it hurts. My arm hurts so much.\"","Qiao Lanshu hurriedly cupped his face and kissed him several times in a row.","Qin Yuanzheng was finally satisfied. Holding Qiao Lanshu, he lay down on the bed, closed his eyes, and said, \"Alright wifey, sleep with me for a while. I haven't closed my eyes for a day and a night.\"","Last night, he had spent the entire night doing emergency rescue work at the mining area. His arm was injured at dawn. After a simple bandaging, he stayed to arrange the work at the mine. It was over an hour later before he finally had someone drive him to the hospital.","Furthermore, not going home last night meant Qin Yuanzheng had actually missed his little wife very much.","He kept thinking about Qiao Lanshu, worrying that she would be scared alone, and worrying that she would stay up all night waiting for him.","Staying up late was very bad for one's health, after all.","Now holding Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng felt somewhat exhausted.","He lay on the bed, holding Qiao Lanshu. \"Let's sleep for a bit together.\"","Qiao Lanshu originally wanted to talk with him a little longer.","But seeing how exhausted he looked, she held back her words. She hugged Qin Yuanzheng's uninjured arm and whispered, \"Go to sleep, I'm right here with you.\"","The two lay hugging on the bed, and before long, Qin Yuanzheng fell fast asleep.","Qiao Lanshu looked at Qin Yuanzheng's face from up close.","There were also scrapes on his cheeks, but they were minor abrasions that didn't bleed.","He hadn't gone back for a night, and looking now, his stubble had already popped up again.","Just how exuberant was this man's energy?","Not shaving for just one night and it was already showing.","She reached out and gently touched it, finding it extremely prickly.","Her palm tingled from being pricked by the stubble.","Not knowing what she suddenly thought of, her face flushed slightly.","She leaned into Qin Yuanzheng's embrace and simply stared at him for a while.","It wasn't long before she fell asleep too.","After all, last night, she had waited up very late for Qin Yuanzheng to return.","She couldn't remember the exact time herself, but it was very late, and she eventually drifted off without realizing when.","Now lying together with Qin Yuanzheng, smelling his familiar scent, she quickly fell asleep as well.","...","When Commander Li brought people over, he saw the two guards at Qin Yuanzheng's door only saluting him but not opening the door for him.","Commander Li stood at the door and asked, \"Who is inside?\"","The guard saluted him and then said, \"Reporting to the Chief, Regiment Commander Qin's family member has arrived and is still inside.\"","Commander Li: \"...\"","Commander Li stroked his chin and smiled, saying, \"It seems Commander Qin married a good wife who knows how to care for him.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had suffered for so many years, and finally married a sweet little wife who knew how to care for him.","It was quite nice.","In his heart, Commander Li felt somewhat gratified.","He said to the guards beside him, \"Put the apples and pears down, let's go.\"","Having heard about Qin Yuanzheng's injury, Commander Li was originally quite worried.","Qin Yuanzheng was, after all, someone he valued highly. He had followed him for over a decade. If anything bad really happened to him, he would feel terrible too.","Now that he knew Qin Yuanzheng was fine, he decided not to disturb the young couple. He left the fruits they brought and left with his men.","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu slept for two hours.","After waking up, Qin Yuanzheng went to find the doctor, saying he wanted to be discharged. He didn't want to stay in the hospital anymore.","He wanted to go home with his little wife and sleep on their heated brick bed.","The doctor checked his wound and could only tell him, \"Regiment Commander Qin, if the wound tears open, you must come to the hospital immediately. Don't endure it by yourself; this kind of wound won't heal easily if you just bear it. It's too deep.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"Alright, I understand.\"","Only then did the doctor let him go. Before he left, the doctor reminded him again, \"Regiment Commander Qin, your arm needs a dressing change every two days. Remember to come to the hospital for it.\"","Such wounds required dressing changes every two or three days at the beginning, and the stitches could only be removed after more than half a month.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded in agreement to all of it, and then took Qiao Lanshu out of the hospital.","Although Qin Yuanzheng was injured, the matters at the mining construction site still needed him to handle them.","As the regiment commander, the burden on his shoulders was heavy, and his responsibilities were great.","This time, the explosives were buried in the wrong location, causing the mine tunnel to collapse. This was a major blunder.","The military region had already brought back several people in charge at the mine, along with the workers, for investigation and interrogation.","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng got into the car. The guard driving asked, \"Commander, are we returning to the mining area?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"Yes.\"","The guard then drove the car in the direction of the mining area.","Qiao Lanshu asked him in a low voice, \"You're already injured, why can't we just go straight home? Do you still have to go to work at the mine?\"","Qin Yuanzheng whispered, \"There's still a little matter left to handle. Once it's taken care of, I'll go home with you.\"","Qiao Lanshu sat there feeling a bit unhappy.","Thinking she was still angry, Qin Yuanzheng coaxed her in a low voice, \"I'll try to be as quick as possible. You can sit in the office for a while, and then we'll go home together, how about that?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded.","She had never been to the mining area before; this would be her first time.","On the way, hesitating in her heart, she still said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, when I married you, I had a nightmare.\"","During the time Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu had just gotten married, Qiao Lanshu seemed to have nightmares frequently.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't know what Qiao Lanshu was afraid of, but he knew she definitely lacked a sense of security.","Therefore, he had always tried his best to spend as much time with her as possible, even though every time he was with her, he couldn't help but do those intimate things with her.","Thinking of this, Qin Yuanzheng felt a bit guilty.","He wrapped his uninjured arm around Qiao Lanshu and asked her in a low voice, \"What kind of nightmare did you have? Tell me about it. Did you dream about someone following you and locking you in a cave dwelling again?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. Looking at Qin Yuanzheng with a serious expression, she whispered, \"I dreamed that when you went out on a mission, you were injured by explosives. You were covered in blood and mangled flesh, and you almost died.\"","She continued softly, \"So when I heard you were injured, I was truly terrified.\"","Qin Yuanzheng patted her back gently and murmured, \"There, there. I'm fine now, aren't I?\"","He felt quite happy that his little wife cared about him so much.","However, seeing her so scared made his heart ache.","All he could do was hold her close and comfort her.","Qiao Lanshu told him, \"If you go out on missions in the future, you must be extra careful. Watch out for explosives, and absolutely do not get hurt again, understand?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"I know. Don't worry.\"","Afraid he wouldn't take it to heart, Qiao Lanshu warned him, \"Let me tell you, if something happens to you, I'll remarry and live my life with another man.\"","Those words were certainly effective. Qin Yuanzheng's arm around her tightened slightly, and his face darkened. He said, \"You actually want to remarry another man?\"","When Qin Yuanzheng had a dark expression and furrowed brows, his aura was quite intimidating.","The guard driving in the front seat sat up a bit straighter, looking ahead with a serious face, terrified of being caught in the crossfire of Qin Yuanzheng's anger.","Qiao Lanshu, however, wasn't afraid of him at all. She nodded and said, \"That's right. If something happens to you, I'll definitely remarry. Then, you won't have a wife anymore.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","He hugged her tightly and whispered fiercely, \"In your dreams. You are my wife, and don't even think about remarrying in this lifetime.\"","Look at how domineering and forceful Qin Yuanzheng was now.","What he didn't know was that in his previous life, just days before he died, he had been running around trying to find a match for his little wife.","He had even called back his nemesis, Guan Wenjun, wanting to marry Qiao Lanshu off to Guan Wenjun.","If she told him all this now, he would probably think she had gone mad.","...","When the two arrived at the mining site, Qin Yuanzheng took Qiao Lanshu to the military office, where Staff Officer Lin surprisingly happened to be as well.","However, he had already changed his clothes and taken a shower. He looked clean and was sitting in the office munching on a steamed bun.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu enter, he asked in surprise, \"Commander, why are you back again? Didn't Commander Li tell you to go home and rest for a couple of days?\"","Under Qin Yuanzheng's command, there were two deputy regimental commanders, five or six battalion and deputy battalion commanders combined, and further down, company commanders and platoon leaders.","Although he had plenty of manpower, when a real incident occurred, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't just wash his hands of it.","He asked Lin Yucheng, \"How are things over at the mine?\"","Lin Yucheng immediately stuffed the rest of the steamed bun into his mouth and walked over with a stack of documents. \"The people have all been apprehended. Here are their files, which we just finished compiling. Take a look.\"","Qin Yuanzheng pulled Qiao Lanshu over to sit in his chair and placed his own insulated water bottle in front of her before finally taking the documents to review.","Lin Yucheng was absolutely amazed.","Qin Yuanzheng had injured an arm, yet with only one good hand left, he was still waiting on his wife.","The last time Commander Li visited, Qin Yuanzheng hadn't even poured him a glass of water.","A short while later, Qin Yuanzheng stood up, threw on his overcoat, and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Wife, sit here for a bit. Wait for me to finish handling this matter, and then we'll go home together.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and watched as Qin Yuanzheng and Lin Yucheng walked out the door.","Qin Yuanzheng went to interrogate the suspects. It didn't take much time before the interrogation was over. The two people in charge were sentenced to reform through labor. A few workers had been implicated because the supervisors had misread the data, resulting in explosives being planted in the wrong locations.","Fortunately, it hadn't resulted in any fatalities; otherwise, it wouldn't have been as simple as just a labor camp sentence.","After Qin Yuanzheng finished dealing with the matter, he finally took Qiao Lanshu home.","He needed to rest at home for a few days to recover from his injuries.","Qiao Lanshu also took time off from work, saying she wanted to take care of him, but in reality, Qin Yuanzheng didn't let her do a single chore.","...","Meanwhile, Chu Liangjun arrived at the main gate of the food factory once again. In his hand, he carried a red gift box containing a mechanical watch he had just bought.","This watch had cost him two hundred yuan.","He didn't actually have that much money himself; he had secretly taken the cash from his second cousin's house.","To him, stealing a little money to use wasn't a big deal.","In his mind, he reasoned that he would definitely pay it back, so he was merely borrowing it in advance.","Therefore, he felt no burden of guilt.","After taking the money, he immediately went to the department store and bought a watch.","Following that, he brought the watch to the food factory gate, intending to wait for Qiao Lanshu to finish work so he could give it to her.","However, unfortunately, Qiao Lanshu was not at work today.","Qiao Lanshu had taken three days off and spent those three days at home taking care of Qin Yuanzheng.","Chu Liangjun came for three consecutive days but never managed to catch Qiao Lanshu.","He knew the factory gatekeeper disliked him, so he asked the factory employees instead. He even tagged along when the supply and marketing cooperative's convoy came to the warehouse to pick up goods.","But he still didn't see Qiao Lanshu. The warehouse keeper covering her shift told Chu Liangjun that Qiao Lanshu had taken a three-day leave.","Chu Liangjun had no choice but to wait until the fourth day to stake out the food factory gate again.","On this day, Qiao Lanshu got off work early, intending to head home soon to cook for Qin Yuanzheng.","After all, with Qin Yuanzheng's arm injured, she couldn't let him do the chores anymore.","As soon as she walked out, she saw Chu Liangjun waiting at the factory gate.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","She felt a bit exasperated.","She had clearly left early today.","How could Chu Liangjun be here so early? Seeing the item he was carrying in his hand, something stirred in Qiao Lanshu's mind.","She shot him a glance and then walked toward the street outside the factory.","Chu Liangjun immediately chased after her, carrying the box.","He caught up to her side and called out, \"I know your name now. You're Qiao Lanshu, right?\"","Qiao Lanshu gave him a look of disgust and said, \"Stay away from me. I don't want to talk to you.\"","Chu Liangjun's face instantly darkened. In his dreams, Qiao Lanshu treated him the exact same way. No matter what he did or said, she refused to speak to him or pay him any attention.","What exactly was so wrong with him?","He felt somewhat angry, yet he was still perfectly willing to try and win her favor.","He said, \"Qiao Lanshu, I bought you a watch. Take a look. Do you like it?\""]},{"number":105,"title":"Chapter 105: He Wouldn't Go So Far as to Steal Money","paragraphs":["The coat Chu Liangjun had someone deliver last time was still sitting on the shelf in Qiao Lanshu's office.","Only last time, Chu Liangjun didn't show up himself; he had a salesperson from the department store deliver it.","This time, however, he delivered it in person.","Qiao Lanshu knew Chu Liangjun well enough to know that he was rotten to the core.","Back in the village, he had done his fair share of petty theft and harassing female comrades.","Now that he was in the city, his true nature was completely exposed.","Especially when provoked, he was even more prone to going to extremes.","In her previous life, Qiao Lanshu had been tormented by him for two years; he was her absolute nightmare.","Lately, Qiao Lanshu had been putting up with him just to see what else he would do to get close to her.","As Chu Liangjun handed over the gift box, Qiao Lanshu said disdainfully, \"You actually have the money to buy me things? I don't care for ordinary items.\"","Chu Liangjun stared at Qiao Lanshu's face. With a face like that, no matter how harsh her words were, he just couldn't bring himself to get angry with her.","He only thought to himself that once he finally got his hands on her, he would teach her a good lesson and show her not to look down on people.","Blocking Qiao Lanshu's way, he looked at her and said, \"Why don't you open it and see for yourself?\"","So Qiao Lanshu took the box, opened it, and saw a Shanghai brand women's mechanical watch inside.","Chu Liangjun stared at her intently and asked, \"Well, do you like it?\"","Qiao Lanshu handed the watch back. \"This is too expensive. I don't want it, take it back.\"","In his mind, Chu Liangjun was thinking that once Qiao Lanshu accepted his gifts, he could use it to demand that she date him.","If she refused, he would threaten to report her for having improper relations with men and using the pretext of dating to swindle his money.","Having planned everything out, he naturally wouldn't take back what he had given. He took a few steps back and said with a smile, \"Since I've given it to you, there's no reason to take it back. Take it home. I'm leaving now.\"","With that, he turned and strode away.","Only after he had walked a good distance away did he pull out the receipts from the department store from his pocket—two in total.","One was the receipt for the cashmere coat, and the other was for the mechanical watch he had just given her.","Looking at the two receipts in his hand, a cold sneer appeared on his face.","When he gave her the watch just now, there were people around watching. The coat from last time was even delivered by a department store salesperson.","He planned to go to the food factory tomorrow to report Qiao Lanshu. He would accuse her of practicing capitalism, being vain, and using the excuse of dating to swindle his belongings. Fearing the negative impact, the food factory would definitely fire her.","By then, Qiao Lanshu's reputation would be ruined. Whenever people mentioned her, they would think of him, and no one would dare to date her. Even if she married someone else, she would be despised. At that point, he would have his cousin, who was the director of the supply and marketing cooperative, find a matchmaker to propose marriage.","If that still didn't work, he would trick Qiao Lanshu into coming out and kidnap her back to his home. Since everyone would know she had cheated him out of his money, no one would care if she became his wife.","Thinking like this, Chu Liangjun could hardly wait for tomorrow to come.","But what he didn't expect was that Qiao Lanshu was also scheming against him.","Watching Chu Liangjun run off with a smile, Qiao Lanshu knew he was up to no good.","Seeing that it was getting dark, she thought about putting the watch back in her office before going grocery shopping to cook for Qin Yuanzheng, who had an injured arm.","When she returned to the food factory, she saw Wang Xue also rushing out.","Wang Xue hadn't seen Qiao Lanshu for a few days. Seeing her now, she immediately ran over and asked with concern, \"Xiao Qiao, I was so busy today I didn't have time to come see you. I heard your man got hurt? How is he? Is it serious?\"","Qiao Lanshu had to stand there and chat with Wang Xue for a bit. \"It's just an arm injury. He's resting right now and can't do any strenuous exercise to prevent the wound from tearing open.\"","Hearing this, Wang Xue frowned and said, \"With a soldier's physical fitness, if he still has to rest for so many days, the wound must be quite deep, right? Did he get stitches?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"He got seven or eight stitches. It's mostly healed over these past few days.\"","Because Qin Yuanzheng was a military officer and the incident involved a military mining area, Qiao Lanshu didn't dare say too much.","Wang Xue also knew that these matters couldn't be casually asked about. Knowing that Qin Yuanzheng was fine, she didn't press further.","She then said to Qiao Lanshu beamingly, \"By the way, Xiao Qiao, after hearing what you said last time, didn't we go to the police station together to report it? That very night, Liu Jianguo really went looking for Haitang. Haitang ignored him, so he followed her all the way. When she left the train station and passed by an alley, Liu Jianguo started getting handsy and tried to drag her into the alley.\"","It was already night time, the weather was cold, and there were no pedestrians on the road at all.","Seeing that Wang Haitang kept ignoring him, Liu Jianguo knew there was no hope of getting back together. He dragged her toward the alley, intending to force himself on her so the deed would be done, figuring Wang Haitang wouldn't dare tell anyone anyway.","Fortunately, Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu had spoken to the police beforehand. The police had arranged for a young officer to patrol the train station, and Wang Xue's husband had also been hiding in the shadows, following them the whole time.","So the moment Liu Jianguo started pulling Wang Haitang and trying to force himself on her, he was caught red-handed!","Liu Jianguo had previously claimed he was dating Wang Haitang, so the police couldn't do anything about him.","But now, he was dragging a female comrade on the street and attempting to assault her. After being caught by the police, he was tied up on the spot and escorted to the police station.","All the way there, he kept crying foul, claiming they were just dating normally.","Absolutely no one listened to him.","Because of this, Wang Haitang breathed a sigh of relief, and Wang Xue was also overjoyed.","She said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Xiao Qiao, your cousin-in-law is treating us to dinner tomorrow night. You should come along too.\"","Deng Xiaozhen had specifically arranged for Deng Weijun and Wang Haitang to meet.","They were supposed to meet a couple of days ago, but since Liu Jianguo was arrested, Wang Haitang had to cooperate with the police investigation, so it was postponed for a few days.","The two young people hadn't met yet, but it seemed that both sets of older sisters were very satisfied with each other.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded. \"Alright, I'll definitely be there.\"","Wang Xue nodded. Seeing it was getting late, she said, \"I have to get going now. Do you want to leave together?\"","Qiao Lanshu hesitated for a couple of seconds before shaking her head. \"No, you go ahead, sis. I still have some things to take care of.\"","Wang Xue said, \"Alright then, see you tomorrow.\"","With that, Wang Xue hurried away.","By this time, most of the workers at the food factory had already left.","Qiao Lanshu returned to her office. She took out her keys, unlocked the door, walked over to the shelf, and first placed the watch gift box next to the cashmere coat.","However, she fell silent for a few seconds and thought it over again.","She remembered that Chu Liangjun was a very impatient person.","He was impulsive and sinister in his methods. Since he had already given her a cashmere coat and today added a mechanical watch, the two items combined were worth nearly three hundred yuan.","That was equivalent to ten months' salary for an ordinary worker.","With such high-value items, if he turned around and claimed this was a bride price for her, forcing her to marry him, it would be a huge problem.","Qiao Lanshu had to strike first.","With this in mind, she grabbed the cashmere coat and the mechanical watch, locked her office door, and hurriedly left the food factory.","Qiao Lanshu didn't go to the Supply and Marketing Cooperative, because Chu Liangjun was surely there at this time.","She went to the vicinity of the cooperative's staff dormitory building and waited there for a long time.","At this hour, people were gradually returning from work.","Qiao Lanshu looked at them one by one, but didn't see the person she was looking for.","As the sky gradually grew dark, Qiao Lanshu became a little anxious. She figured that if she didn't see him by around six o'clock, she would just go home.","Her main concern was making Qin Yuanzheng worry.","Qin Yuanzheng had originally offered to come pick her up, but she refused to let him.","After all, Qin Yuanzheng's arm was injured and he couldn't drive. If he walked over to pick her up, she was afraid he would aggravate his wound.","Besides, it was cold now. He would have to put on heavy clothes to go out and take them off when he got home. With all that moving around, what if his wound tore open?","Thinking of Qin Yuanzheng, Qiao Lanshu lost the desire to wait. Just as she was about to leave, she saw from a distance a slightly plump middle-aged man in an overcoat walking over with a tall, thin woman. The woman was carrying a vegetable basket in her hand.","Behind the two of them followed their three elementary-school-aged daughters.","That is right, this man was exactly Chu Liangjun's uncle, the director of the Supply and Marketing Cooperative, Chu Haiming.","Chu Haiming was in his forties. After marrying his wife, they had three daughters in a row.","This made him, who had always wanted a son, somewhat depressed.","He had once considered adopting Chu Liangjun to be his son.","But Chu Liangjun's reputation in the village was too poor. He engaged in petty theft, was always fighting with others, and acted like a hooligan.","Chu Haiming's wife, Niu Weifen, absolutely disagreed.","Chu Haiming had to settle for the next best thing, bringing Chu Liangjun to the city to work. He figured that if he supported Chu Liangjun more, he might be able to rely on him for his old age.","After all, Chu Liangjun had no father or mother, and no other elders to show filial piety to, right?","Chu Haiming's idea was nice, but he never expected that Chu Liangjun's stealing in the village was just the beginning.","Now, he was actually stealing from him.","When their family of five reached the gate of the courtyard, a young woman wearing an army-green padded jacket and wrapped in a red scarf stopped them.","This person was Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu looked at them and asked politely, Hello, are you Director Chu from the cooperative?","Chu Haiming and Niu Weifen exchanged a glance and nodded. Niu Weifen looked at Qiao Lanshu with some vigilance and asked, He is. Who are you? What do you want with him?","Qiao Lanshu immediately brought forward the items in her hand to show Niu Weifen. Feigning distress, she said:","It is like this. Recently, a man named Chu Liangjun has been harassing me. He often waits for me at the gate of my factory. I ignore him, but he still brings me gifts. I tell him I do not want them, but he just drops them and runs, forcing me to accept them. These things are too valuable, how could I possibly accept them?","Saying this, she shoved the items into Niu Weifen's hands and told her:","Sister-in-law, take a look. This cashmere coat alone costs several dozen yuan, and this watch is even more expensive. It is a Shanghai brand, mechanical too. This must cost around two hundred yuan, right? He is just a temporary worker, where did he get so much money to buy these things? I am scared...","She spoke deliberately, paused for a moment, and then quickly added:","Moreover, I am already married. My husband is a soldier in the military. His pestering me like this counts as undermining a military marriage. I only came to speak with you privately because I figured he might not know; the military does not know about this yet. Please go back and talk some sense into him.","After handing the items to Niu Weifen and observing the shock and uncertainty on her face, Qiao Lanshu turned to Chu Haiming and said, Director Chu, it is getting late, so I will be taking my leave. Please have a good talk with your nephew and tell him not to come looking for me at the food factory anymore.","With that, Qiao Lanshu quickly ran off.","Mostly because it was getting dark, and she was afraid Qin Yuanzheng would worry if she went back too late.","Niu Weifen turned her head, looking at Chu Haiming with a shocked and uncertain expression.","Chu Haiming was equally stunned. He stood there for a long time before finally uttering, So the girl that brat said he wanted to pursue is a military wife?","Niu Weifen looked at Chu Haiming. Suddenly, she handed the vegetable basket in her hand to the daughter beside her. Then, she first picked up the cashmere coat and examined it over and over again.","She confirmed it was a real cashmere coat; it even still had the department store tag on it.","She shoved the cashmere coat back into the bag, took out the watch box, and opened it.","A beautiful, delicate women's watch lay quietly in the box.","Niu Weifen murmured, Such an expensive watch, I would not even bear to buy it for myself, yet he bought it so casually, and gave it away so casually...","As she spoke, Niu Weifen suddenly glared at Chu Haiming and interrogated him on the spot, Chu Haiming! Exactly how much money have you been giving him behind my back?","Niu Weifen was truly furious. After you lent him fifty yuan last time, you promised me you would not give him any more money. It has only been a few days, and you gave him two hundred yuan?","The price of this watch, if one had the ration coupons, was one hundred and eighty yuan.","Without coupons, it would cost over two hundred.","In comparison, this coat worth several dozen yuan suddenly seemed cheap.","Chu Haiming was dumbfounded. He quickly explained, No, no, no! I really did not give him any money! Besides, ever since he came to our house to borrow money last time, he has not been back. I am busy with work normally, and I have not gone to the motor pool to see him either.","Chu Haiming looked at the enraged Niu Weifen and told her, Furthermore, I handed my entire salary for this month over to you. Do you not know exactly how much money I have on me?","Hearing him say this, Niu Weifen indeed became less angry. However, she then asked, Then where did he get so much money? Could he have gone stealing again?","Chu Haiming's expression also turned serious; after all, Chu Liangjun had a prior record.","He said hesitantly, He probably would not go that far, right? He promised me he would not steal things anymore...","Niu Weifen suddenly thought of something, and she hurriedly walked toward their home.","As she walked, she said, I have not checked the money at home for a long time. It could not have been stolen by him, could it?","She kept several hundred yuan in a drawer at home for daily expenses.","But she had not checked on it for a few days. It should still be there, right?","Chu Haiming was still saying, Ah, he would not go that far, he really would not. Chu Liangjun still has some conscience. Even if he were to steal, he could not possibly steal our money.","Niu Weifen said viciously, \"If he dares to steal my money, I'll have him sent to a labor camp!\""]},{"number":106,"title":"Chapter 106: The Clip-Collecting Enthusiast","paragraphs":["Chu Haiming did not believe that his nephew would come and steal his money.","He thought to himself that even if Chu Liangjun loved to steal, he wouldn't steal from him.","He was Chu Liangjun's cousin-uncle, his closest living relative right now.","He had helped Chu Liangjun so much, bringing him to the city and finding him a job. Even though it was just temporary work, it was still much better than his previous situation in the village.","He considered himself Chu Liangjun's benefactor. Even if Chu Liangjun didn't repay him, he should at least treat him well. Stealing money was definitely out of the question.","Just thinking about it made it impossible for him to accept.","Niu Weifen didn't have such a good impression of Chu Liangjun.","She had always felt that Chu Liangjun was up to no good.","Chu Liangjun didn't look like a kind person; even the way he looked at people was off. One glance was enough to tell he harbored bad intentions.","Niu Weifen rushed home hurriedly, while Chu Haiming said, \"Slow down, slow down.\"","He hurried after her with their three daughters.","After the family of five arrived home.","Niu Weifen took off her coat and shoes, heading straight for her bedroom: \"I need to see if my money is missing. I haven't checked on it for over half a month. Could it be gone?\"","Chu Haiming took off his overcoat and hung it up, saying slowly, \"You can put your heart at ease. Liangjun wouldn't steal your money. He hasn't been to our house since his last visit, so how could he steal it? He can't walk through walls, can he?\"","Niu Weifen didn't listen to him, nor was she in a hurry to cook. Seeing this, the three daughters knew their mother had no time for them.","They took off their coats, left them on the sofa, and went back to their room to play.","Niu Weifen rushed into her room. She opened the wardrobe, moved the quilt on the shelf, and revealed a small drawer secured with a padlock.","At first glance, she saw the padlock still hanging there perfectly, and her anxious heart instantly settled halfway.","Fortunately, the lock was still there. It should be fine.","At this time, Chu Haiming also came in. Seeing the padlock intact on the small drawer, he said, \"See, I told you. It's definitely fine. Don't scare yourself.\"","Niu Weifen sneered, \"If he were a good person, would I be so scared? Isn't it because he's light-fingered? Tell me yourself, he was so poor he had to borrow money from you, so where did he get the money to buy a watch? That watch costs at least two hundred yuan!\"","Chu Haiming: \"...\"","Chu Haiming really couldn't figure this out either.","He said hesitantly, \"Could it be that he borrowed money from someone else?\"","Niu Weifen rummaged through her trouser pockets and pulled out a bunch of house keys.","She said, \"What a joke. If he had such a generous friend, he wouldn't have come to you to borrow money last time. When you gave him fifty yuan, he even pulled a long face. Let me tell you, this guy is an ungrateful wretch.\"","Complaining, she picked out a small key from the bunch. Then, she stepped forward and twisted the lock on the small drawer.","As soon as she opened it, she immediately sensed something was wrong.","She cried out, her face instantly turning pale: \"This lock wasn't locked?\"","She panicked. Although the padlock was hanging there nicely, it wasn't snapped shut at all.","She hadn't looked closely just now and didn't even know the lock had already been opened!","She quickly threw the keys down, unhooked the padlock, tossed it aside, and pulled the small drawer open with a yank!","This small drawer was specially used by Niu Weifen to store valuables and living expenses.","In their family, only Chu Haiming worked. Chu Haiming was the director of the Supply and Marketing Cooperative. His salary was decent, and the subsidies were not bad, so it was enough to support the family.","After his salary was paid every month, Chu Haiming would give it to Niu Weifen. Niu Weifen would keep half as living expenses and deposit the other half into their bankbook.","She lived frugally every month, reluctant to spend their money and ration coupons. Over the years, the cash saved in the small drawer amounted to more than five hundred yuan.","Besides the five hundred yuan in cash, the drawer also held their marriage certificate, the children's birth certificates, the household register, and so on.","Niu Weifen rummaged through everything. All the documents were there; the only thing missing was her five hundred yuan!","Fifty ten-yuan notes!","The living expenses she had saved up through strict frugality!","As the director of the Supply and Marketing Cooperative, Chu Haiming's monthly salary was less than one hundred yuan. This five hundred yuan was more than half a year's wages for him!","That heartless bastard had simply taken all the money away!","If a young girl hadn't come over to tell her today, she probably wouldn't have opened the drawer to get money until the Lunar New Year!","Niu Weifen's hands were shaking with anger. She threw the things in her hands right at Chu Haiming's face and cursed hysterically:","\"And you said he wouldn't steal! Look, look for yourself! The money is all gone! Five hundred yuan! I couldn't even bear to buy myself a new scarf, but him? He took my money to buy a cashmere coat and a watch for someone else!\"","Chu Haiming was also dumbfounded.","He knew there was five hundred yuan saved in Niu Weifen's small drawer.","That was saved by Niu Weifen from the living expenses of their family of five. She wanted to save it for the New Year to buy some things for both their parents' families, like some mutton.","And now it was gone?","Chu Haiming said in disbelief, \"Wife, is it really gone? Look carefully again?\"","Saying that, he walked over, pulled the small drawer all the way out, put it on the table, and turned out everything inside. He even flipped their marriage certificate over and over to check.","Finally, he searched the wardrobe several times, confirming that not a single ten-yuan note was to be seen.","Chu Haiming's expression was very complicated. He sat weakly on the bed, looking at the empty little drawer, speechless for a long time.","Niu Weifen kept cursing in anger, cursing Chu Liangjun for being heartless, and also cursing Chu Haiming for being brainless and inviting a wolf into the house.","Niu Weifen cursed for over half an hour, but her anger still hadn't subsided. She stood up abruptly, walked to the front door, and started putting on her coat.","Chu Haiming hurriedly chased after her, grabbed her arm, and asked, \"Wife, what are you going to do this late at night?\"","Niu Weifen said indignantly, \"I'm going to the public security bureau to report the case! I'm going to the Revolutionary Committee to report him! I want Chu Liangjun to return the money to me, and then send him to the distant Haixi Farm for labor reform! It's best if he's reformed for life and never comes back!\"","Chu Haiming: \"...\"","Chu Haiming pulled her arm hard and said with a serious face, \"Wife! Calm down. This matter hasn't been investigated clearly yet. You can't just falsely accuse him. What if he didn't steal the money?\"","Niu Weifen laughed out of sheer anger. She pointed at the cashmere coat and the watch on the table and asked Chu Haiming, \"Evidence? Aren't these stolen goods evidence? Where would he get the money to buy such expensive things? Go ask the police comrades to investigate, and won't we know?\"","Chu Haiming naturally knew this in his heart, but he still said, \"Liangjun is my cousin's child after all. You also know that back in my hometown, he's the only child left. Regardless of whether he stole the money or not, I can't really send him to be paraded through the streets or to a labor camp... Wifey, just consider it for my sake. When I get old and pass away, how am I supposed to face the ancestors of the Chu family?\"","Chu Liangjun's father was Chu Haiming's cousin, specifically the son of Chu Haiming's maternal uncle. Chu Haiming grew up without a father and was raised by his mother, so he took his mother's surname.","Now, within his mother's family line, apart from himself, the only other male was his uncle's son, Chu Liangjun.","Chu Haiming himself had three daughters and no sons, so he had always treated Chu Liangjun as his own heir.","Over the years, Niu Weifen had always felt guilty, blaming herself for not being able to give Chu Haiming a son.","But now, hearing Chu Haiming say this, she was still furious. She sneered and said,","\"Chu Haiming, you yourself took your mother's surname, and you're worried about the Chu family line dying out? Don't you have three daughters? When the time comes, just have them find live-in sons-in-law to give you a few grandchildren with the surname Chu, wouldn't that work? What era are we in now, and you're still talking like this? This is feudal rubbish... Are you really not afraid of being publicly denounced?\"","Chu Haiming quickly covered Niu Weifen's mouth, glaring at her as he said, \"Wife! Don't just say things like that! It'll be trouble if someone hears you.\"","With things having escalated to this point, Niu Weifen didn't go out either. She sat on the sofa and asked, \"Then tell me, what do we do now? Five hundred yuan, that's five hundred yuan!\"","Chu Haiming was silent for a long time before saying, \"First thing tomorrow morning, I'll go find Liangjun and ask him. If he didn't do this, I'll go to the police station to report it and let the comrades there investigate. If he really did do it...\"","Chu Haiming fell silent again.","Niu Weifen said fiercely, \"Then you fire him, drive him back to the countryside, and cut off all ties with him. You are not allowed to associate with him anymore. The further this jinx of a relative rolls away, the better! If you don't listen to me, we'll get a divorce.\"","Chu Haiming: \"...\"","How could Chu Haiming possibly divorce Niu Weifen?","In this era, getting a divorce had a huge impact on a person's career.","If he got divorced, he could forget about ever moving up the ranks in this lifetime, and no good opportunities in the city would ever fall to him.","His life would basically be ruined.","He gritted his teeth and said, \"Fine, I'll listen to you.\"","...","While things were in an uproar on Chu Haiming's side.","Qiao Lanshu, on the other hand, was in a wonderful mood.","After she delivered the items to Chu Haiming's place, the heavy stone in her heart finally dropped.","Chu Haiming was the director of the supply and marketing cooperative, and Chu Haiming's wife, Niu Weifen, had an older brother who was a division commander.","Therefore, to deal with Chu Liangjun, she could only first sever the ties between Chu Liangjun and Chu Haiming.","As for what to do next, that would depend on whether Chu Liangjun's next step was to return to the village or continue staying in the city.","Thinking about these things, Qiao Lanshu arrived at the supply and marketing cooperative.","It was already dark, and the cooperative was about to close. She quickly took out her non-staple food coupons and bought two pillow breads produced by the food factory.","Recently, because Qin Yuanzheng's arm was injured, Qiao Lanshu rarely let him go out, lest he bump his arm while changing clothes.","So naturally, they hadn't bought breakfast. Qiao Lanshu had been cooking porridge and steaming buns at home. Today, since she had coupons, she thought she'd buy some pillow breads to take back.","Holding the two pillow breads, she walked toward the military compound.","Just as she reached the intersection, she saw a tall man walking directly toward her.","Qiao Lanshu took a glance and felt that this figure looked a bit familiar.","Before she could react, she heard the man call out to her, \"Qiao Lanshu!\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Of the rare two times Qin Yuanzheng had called her by her full name, one was when she accompanied Wang Xue to the train station.","The other time was right now.","For no reason, Qiao Lanshu began to feel nervous and guilty.","She hurriedly trotted up to him and said in a soft voice, \"Brother Zheng, why did you come out looking for me?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was wearing an army-green tank top underneath, with a thick military overcoat draped over his shoulders.","Only a few buttons of the overcoat were simply fastened, and the collar was still wide open.","It seemed he had come out in quite a hurry.","Qin Yuanzheng reached over and took the pillow breads from Qiao Lanshu's arms before asking her, \"It's almost seven o'clock. You get off work at five-thirty, so you should have been home by six-thirty at the latest. Why are you so late? What did you go do?\"","In fact, if Qiao Lanshu had rushed home the moment she got off work at five-thirty, she should have arrived before six.","Qin Yuanzheng had taken into consideration that her short little legs couldn't walk fast. After work, she might chat with her colleagues for a bit, then go to the cooperative together to buy some things, before slowly making her way home.","With all that, an hour would have been plenty.","When it hit six-thirty and Qiao Lanshu still wasn't home, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't sit still anymore.","He immediately threw on his overcoat and hurried downstairs. First, he took a stroll around the food factory, but its doors were already locked.","He then went to check the supply and marketing cooperative, but there were hardly any people left, and it was about to close.","Qin Yuanzheng was so anxious.","Every day, he was afraid that his little wife would secretly run away.","If he couldn't find her for even a day, he would panic immensely.","Fortunately, as he was walking back toward the compound, he finally saw his little wife returning.","If Qiao Lanshu hadn't come back soon, Qin Yuanzheng probably would have alarmed the militia patrol group and asked them to help find her.","Qiao Lanshu said with a guilty conscience, \"I was chatting with a colleague for a while and accidentally lost track of time.\"","Qin Yuanzheng carried the pillow breads with his injured arm, and hooked his other arm around Qiao Lanshu's shoulders, pulling her into his embrace.","Qiao Lanshu didn't dare make a sound, simply lowering her head and following him, obediently walking through the compound gates.","Qin Yuanzheng's expression was dark. He tried his best not to frighten her, only asking sternly, \"What time did you see this colleague? What's their name? What did you talk about?\"","He felt that his little wife was lying.","After all, what kind of great storms had he not weathered? What kind of people had he not seen?","From just a single look or movement, he knew that Qiao Lanshu was hiding something from him.","But it seemed Qiao Lanshu wasn't planning on telling him.","Keeping his patience, he told her, \"Think carefully before you speak. If I find out you're lying to me...\"","Remembering the experience of being punished last time, Qiao Lanshu hurriedly said, \"Brother Zheng, I'll tell you, I'll tell you, okay? Stop being so fierce to me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Keeping a straight face, Qin Yuanzheng said, \"I wasn't being fierce to you.\"","How was he being fierce? He was just speaking in a normal tone.","Heaven knew that to coax his wife normally, he practically turned into a soft-spoken sweet-talker.","And yet, his wife thought that was his normal way of speaking, and that he was being fierce to her right now."]},{"number":107,"title":"Chapter 107: Is it a department store","paragraphs":["Although Qiao Lanshu said she would tell the truth, she didn't dare reveal that she had plotted against Chu Liangjun.","Instead, she told Qin Yuanzheng about another matter: \"Brother Zheng, Sister Xue wants to introduce her younger sister, Wang Haitang, to Deng Weijun. They've arranged to have dinner at my cousin's house tomorrow night and invited me to go along. I've already promised Sister Xue. What about you? Do you want to come with us?\"","Qin Yuanzheng thought for a moment and asked, \"Is it the one you guys went to the train station to help that day? The ticket conductor at the station?\"","Qin Yuanzheng knew about this; after all, he was the one who went to Deng Xiaozhen to pass on the message.","He just didn't expect them to meet so soon.","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Cousin-in-law has already met and talked with Sister Xue. They'll let the two of them meet tomorrow night. I wonder if it will work out.\"","Qin Yuanzheng wasn't interested in this matter.","Anyway, he already had a wife, and it was enough that his own life was beautiful. Why should he care about others?","He said, \"Since you promised to go, then of course I'm going.\"","He had to drop his wife off and pick her up later.","He wouldn't feel at ease letting her go alone.","Qiao Lanshu deliberately chose words he liked to hear: \"I knew Brother Zheng was the best. You would definitely accompany me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't maintain his serious expression.","However, he couldn't let his little wife off so easily this time.","He narrowed his eyes at her. \"Is this all you have to tell me? Nothing else?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled sweetly and said, \"I'm done. That's all.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Since his little wife refused to tell him the truth, he couldn't force her. He could investigate it himself; after all, finding things out was quite simple for him.","Thus, he could only nod and say, \"Alright then.\"","His expression was a bit cold, and Qiao Lanshu felt he might be a little angry.","But she couldn't say anything.","Anyway, according to her plan, Chu Liangjun wouldn't be jumping around for much longer.","After returning home, Qiao Lanshu made dinner for Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng had already cooked the sweet potato and millet porridge. Qiao Lanshu put on an apron, rolled up her sleeves, and walked into the kitchen, preparing to stir-fry some hot and sour shredded potatoes and fry a few eggs.","Watching Qiao Lanshu bustling about in the kitchen in her apron, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't help but follow his little wife with his eyes.","His wife wasn't tall, and her figure was petite, but fortunately, she was nicely fleshed out and felt soft and cuddly to hold.","He wondered to himself, how could someone grow up so perfectly?","Not only was her face beautiful and her skin fair, but her figure was also perfectly proportioned—plump where she should be plump, and slender where she should be slender.","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't resist walking into the kitchen, pacing back and forth behind Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu glanced at him several times and said while working, \"Brother Zheng, your arm is injured, so you don't need to help out here. You should go out and rest for a while.\"","Qin Yuanzheng simply said, \"I'm just looking.\"","Actually, he wasn't there to watch Qiao Lanshu cook.","He purely wanted to look at her.","His own wife really got prettier the more he looked at her.","The more he looked, the more he couldn't help but want...","Because of the injury on his arm, Qin Yuanzheng had been abstaining for several days. In fact, he didn't think it was a big deal.","After all, he could hoist his wife over his shoulder with one hand.","If he wanted to do something, he was fully capable.","More than capable, in fact.","But Qiao Lanshu wouldn't let him, insisting that he rest properly.","Qin Yuanzheng felt he had rested more than enough.","If he rested any longer, certain parts of him were going to break from disuse.","So, when it was time to sleep at night, Qin Yuanzheng started getting handsy, rubbing and pressing against her.","Although the kang bed at home was large, and the quilt was big too, Qin Yuanzheng was too clingy. He kept squeezing against Qiao Lanshu, leaving her helpless.","If he squeezed any closer, she would be plastered against the wall.","Moreover, Qin Yuanzheng's body was like a furnace with a very high temperature.","Being squished together was quite hot.","Qin Yuanzheng's behavior was too obvious; Qiao Lanshu knew exactly what he wanted to do.","Qiao Lanshu turned around, pushed him with her hand, and said with a serious face, \"Brother Zheng, didn't I tell you? With your current physical condition, you need to rest. Don't move around recklessly. What if the wound on your arm tears open?\"","His little wife smelled fragrant, the scent of soap.","It was really strange; they obviously used the same soap, so why did it smell different on her?","It smelled incredibly good.","Qin Yuanzheng pinned her down with his uninjured arm and whispered in her ear, \"Wifey, I've rested for four nights already. Do I still need to rest?\"","Since taking up his post on their wedding day, this was the first time he had taken a break, and it had been four days straight, which was really quite long.","Qiao Lanshu pulled the quilt up to cover her mouth, revealing only her eyes as she looked at him and nodded. \"Of course, your arm is badly injured, Brother Zheng. You have to go to work soon, so you still need to focus on recovering. Don't mess around.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","She continued, speaking seriously to Qin Yuanzheng, \"If you don't want to rest at night in the future, then you need to be more careful and not get hurt. Otherwise, it will always be like this!\"","With that, Qiao Lanshu adjusted her quilt. She even made sure she and Qin Yuanzheng had their own single quilts, refusing to share one with him.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng lay beside her in frustration.","Looking at his high-spirited...","He sighed helplessly in his heart.","Under these circumstances, he couldn't sleep at all. With a warm, fragrant beauty right beside him, he wasn't Liu Xiahui.","Besides, wasn't there more than one way to do that sort of thing? It wasn't like there was only one method.","Initially, his little wife completely ignored him, so Qin Yuanzheng could only lie there, staring blankly.","After an hour or so, Qin Yuanzheng still couldn't sleep.","Thus, once Qiao Lanshu fell asleep, he threw off his covers, slipped directly into her quilt, and whispered softly into her ear, \"Wifey? Wifey, can you hear me?\"","Qiao Lanshu was already asleep by this time, so naturally, she didn't respond.","After all, Qiao Lanshu was young, right at the age of having the best sleep quality.","She got sleepy on time and slept very deeply, completely unaware that Qin Yuanzheng was about to do something naughty.","Qin Yuanzheng kissed Qiao Lanshu's ear and whispered, \"Wifey, if you don't answer me, I'm going to bite you.\"","Qiao Lanshu kept her eyes closed, breathing evenly; she was indeed fast asleep.","In the dim light of the oil lamp, Qin Yuanzheng stared at Qiao Lanshu's face for a while.","Qiao Lanshu had an oval face, very fair skin, and rosy lips. Looking at her sleeping face under the oil lamp, she truly got more beautiful the longer he looked.","Qin Yuanzheng stared at his wife for several minutes. Then, he lifted the quilt and began unbuttoning Qiao Lanshu's clothes...","...","In her dream, Qiao Lanshu thought she had boarded a ship. The waves crashed fiercely, one after another, nearly capsizing her little boat.","She lay on the swaying deck and frantically grabbed the railing above her, only to find that the temperature of the railing was scorching hot.","The seawater splashed against her face, and the waves pounded loudly against the hull of the boat, scaring her so much she almost cried.","When she was finally roused from her sleep and opened her eyes, she found herself leaning back, sitting on Qin Yuanzheng's lap. Qin Yuanzheng was leaning against the headboard, holding her with one arm. He whispered, \"Wife, you're finally awake? You were sleeping so deeply.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","...","...","Early the next morning, Qiao Lanshu couldn't stop yawning on her way to work.","She had \"ridden the boat\" far too much last night, leaving her feeling almost seasick.","With not enough rest, she was exhausted today, her back aching and her waist sore. She let out a sigh.","Sure enough, you couldn't leave a man hanging for too long. You had to help him solve his needs every now and then, otherwise, the consequences were quite severe.","Fortunately, Qin Yuanzheng's injured arm limited his performance.","Otherwise, she would probably be even dizzier.","Today, a guard came to escort her to work.","This guard worked under Qin Yuanzheng; he was the one who drove the car when Qin Yuanzheng was discharged from the hospital.","Over the past few days, since Qin Yuanzheng had been busy, this guard was also the one helping out with delivering documents and such.","Seeing him waiting at the door, Qiao Lanshu took out a piping hot sweet potato and handed it to him. \"Comrade, this is for you.\"","She had just steamed the sweet potatoes that morning. They had thin red skins and sweet, bright orange flesh.","The guard was too embarrassed to accept it. He quickly waved his hands and said, \"Sister-in-law, there's no need. I've already had breakfast.\"","Qiao Lanshu knew he would say that. These guards were all very polite and would never casually accept things from others.","So, she added, \"Just take it and eat it. Your commander was worried you hadn't had breakfast, so he specifically asked me to bring this for you. It's the dead of winter and freezing outside; you can put it in your pocket to warm your hands.\"","Hearing this, the guard had no choice but to take it. \"Thank you, Sister-in-law. Thank you, Commander.\"","He took the sweet potato and slipped it into his pocket. Feeling the warmth radiating against his leg, his heart warmed up as well.","He thought to himself, there was no way the commander would actually give him a sweet potato. It was a blessing enough that the commander didn't work them like mules.","Their commander was truly lucky to have married such a good wife.","By the time Qiao Lanshu arrived at the food factory, Chu Liangjun was already staking out the place.","Chu Liangjun had arrived bright and early. He thought about how he was going to report Qiao Lanshu at the factory today, and then execute his chain of schemes to finally get his hands on her.","He was so excited he couldn't sleep.","He barely slept last night, so he came to wait at the factory gates at the crack of dawn.","He just wanted to catch a glimpse of her.","Once everyone at the factory clocked in, he planned to go to the factory director to report her, then to the Revolutionary Committee, and he was even prepared to report her to the police station.","When Qiao Lanshu stepped out of the car, Chu Liangjun immediately stood up, staring straight at her.","Qiao Lanshu saw him too.","But she pretended not to notice.","She quickly hurried into the factory, wondering to herself what was going on with Chu Haiming. Why hadn't he come looking for Chu Liangjun yet?","Could it be that Chu Liangjun hadn't stolen Chu Haiming's money after all?","Just as Qiao Lanshu was pondering this, a man from the supply and marketing cooperative's motor pool arrived at the factory gates.","This man was an official employee of the motor pool. The moment he clocked in today, the motor pool director had ordered him to go find Chu Liangjun.","Several people in the fleet knew that Chu Liangjun had his eye on a female worker at the food factory and had been staking the place out every day recently.","So, it didn't take much effort to find him; he spotted Chu Liangjun right away.","The man ran over, panting, and called out, \"Chu Liangjun, it's early in the morning! Instead of reporting to the cooperative, what are you doing squatting here?\"","Chu Liangjun had the purchase receipts for a cashmere coat and a watch in his pocket.","He was just about to take these receipts to the factory director to report Qiao Lanshu.","Yet, before he could even enter the factory gates, he was intercepted by his coworker.","He looked at his colleague, frowned slightly, and said impatiently, \"I'm here to take care of some business, what about it? Do you need me for something?\"","The colleague didn't want to deal with him either, but since he was ordered by their superior to find him today, he had to bring him back no matter what.","So, he stepped forward, grabbed Chu Liangjun's arm, and said, \"Stop making excuses. Our director has been looking for you all morning. It's past clock-in time and everyone else is present except you. Tell me, do you still want this job? What if you get fired? Jobs aren't easy to come by these days.\"","Hearing this, Chu Liangjun asked, \"Doesn't our director usually stay upstairs? How come he has the time to come down and inspect our work today?\"","The motor pool director's rank wasn't as high as Chu Haiming's.","But he still wielded considerable power, managing the cooperative's fleet, logistics, and warehouses.","The man usually sat in his logistics office, so why did he suddenly come down to the motor pool and specifically ask for him?","Chu Liangjun wondered to himself, could it be because he had been skipping work, arriving late, and leaving early recently, and now that he was caught, they wanted to have a talk with him?","But he was Chu Haiming's man; he didn't give a damn.","Chu Liangjun shook off his colleague's hand and said, \"Go back and tell the director that I'll return as soon as I finish my business here. It should take about an hour.\"","His colleague clicked his tongue in annoyance, quickly grabbed his arm again, and forcefully pulled him along. \"Cut the crap and come back with me right now. If I don't bring you back, the director is going to chew me out later. You might have backing, but I don't, and I don't want to lose my job.\"","Chu Liangjun: \"...\"","Reluctantly, Chu Liangjun was dragged back to the cooperative. Left with no choice, he had to postpone his plan to report Qiao Lanshu.","Anyway, she had already accepted his things; she wouldn't be able to deny it even if she tried.","When he returned to the cooperative, the motor pool director was already gone.","He only left a message for Chu Liangjun to go to the office of the cooperative director, Chu Haiming.","So, Chu Liangjun went to Chu Haiming's office.","Chu Haiming looked at him with a complex expression on his face and asked, \"Liangjun, where did you go so early in the morning? Why didn't you come to work?\"","Chu Liangjun wasn't afraid of his uncle at all. No matter what he said, this uncle would believe him anyway.","He replied, \"Uncle, I had some urgent business to take care of this morning, so I was delayed a bit. I figured there were no new shipments this morning and the fleet wasn't busy, so I went. If we were busy, I definitely would have come back.\"","Chu Haiming looked at him and cut straight to the chase, \"Liangjun, over the past few days, did you go spending money at the department store?\"","Chu Liangjun: \"...\""]},{"number":108,"title":"Chapter 108: Real or Fake Arm Pain","paragraphs":["Chu Liangjun hadn't expected Chu Haiming to ask him this question so soon.","Based on his observations, Chu Haiming never managed the household expenses, and Niu Weifen rarely checked her little drawer.","That little drawer was inside the wardrobe, hidden behind quilts and clothes. She hardly ever touched that spot.","According to Chu Liangjun's guess, Niu Weifen wouldn't notice anything wrong with the little drawer until Chu Haiming's next payday.","But that was still over twenty days away. By then, he should have already taken Qiao Lanshu back to the countryside.","Chu Haiming stared at Chu Liangjun's face and noticed something amiss in his expression.","His heart suddenly went cold. He said coldly, \"Liangjun, didn't I tell you not to steal anymore? Why... why can't you change this bad habit of petty theft?\"","Chu Liangjun was initially feeling a bit guilty, but hearing Chu Haiming say this, he instantly became displeased. With a dark face, he said, \"Uncle, didn't you say you'd take care of finding me a wife? Now that I've taken a fancy to a girl, why aren't you offering to help me?\"","Chu Liangjun had no parents and no money. Whenever he set his sights on a woman, his first thought was always to suppress her until she couldn't hold her head up, ruin her reputation, and then he could marry her and take her home.","Because only in this way could he be a match for her; otherwise, why would she marry him?","Although Chu Haiming said he would help him, with Niu Weifen around, Chu Haiming couldn't really help him with anything.","He understood this perfectly well in his heart.","Hearing him say this, Chu Haiming became even angrier. He said sternly, \"Liangjun, do you even know who the girl you've taken a fancy to is?\"","Chu Liangjun replied, \"Isn't she just a warehouse keeper at the food factory? Who else could she be?\"","Chu Haiming's face darkened, and he said sharply, \"She is a military officer's family member! Her husband is the commander of the 21st Regiment! You've been waiting for her at the food factory every day recently; didn't you notice that she is escorted by soldiers on her way to and from work?\"","Chu Haiming said with a tone of disappointment, \"Would a girl from an ordinary family have such an entourage? Why don't you use your brain and think?\"","Chu Haiming paused, then added, \"You are interfering with a military marriage. Do you know you could be sentenced to prison for that?\"","Chu Liangjun: \"...\"","After hearing this, Chu Liangjun was completely shocked.","He had indeed noticed that Qiao Lanshu was picked up and dropped off by soldiers, and he also knew she lived in the military residential compound.","But he had always thought that it was her family members who were in the military—like her brothers, relatives, or even her parents.","It was precisely because he worried her family was in the military and hard to deal with that he decided to give her gifts and then report her.","That way, the chances of success would be high. Even if he couldn't marry Qiao Lanshu, her reputation in the military compound would be utterly ruined.","No one would be willing to marry her after that.","But now, Chu Haiming was actually saying she was a military officer's wife, that she was already married?","Chu Liangjun stood up abruptly. His eyes were bloodshot, and he looked at Chu Haiming with a gloomy expression. \"Impossible. She looks like a teenager. It's impossible for her to be married this early. Uncle, are you just making excuses because you don't want to help me?\"","Chu Haiming was so angry he felt like he was going to have a heart attack.","He suddenly opened the drawer, took out the cashmere coat and the watch, and placed them on the desk.","As soon as Chu Liangjun saw these items, his gaze froze, and his heartbeat instantly quickened.","Chu Haiming said in a deep voice, \"They've already returned the things to me. Do you still think I'm lying to you?\"","Staring at Chu Liangjun, Chu Haiming advised earnestly, \"Liangjun, before this blows up—since the other party clearly doesn't want to pursue the matter—just go back to the countryside and lay low for a while. If there are job opportunities in the future, I'll write to you...\"","Chu Haiming was also thinking of Chu Liangjun's best interests.","Even though Chu Liangjun had stolen his money, he figured that since Chu Liangjun was still young, only in his twenties, perhaps there was still a chance for him to mend his ways.","He couldn't possibly send Chu Liangjun to a labor camp just for five hundred yuan.","What Chu Haiming didn't know was that he had overestimated Chu Liangjun's character.","He thought Chu Liangjun would be grateful that he wasn't pursuing the theft.","However, Chu Liangjun felt no gratitude at all. At this moment, his heart was filled only with resentment.","He glared at Chu Haiming and said coldly, \"I knew you all looked down on me. You said you'd find me a job and a wife, but now you're taking the job back and telling me to return to the countryside!\"","Chu Haiming: \"...\"","Chu Liangjun pulled two hundred yuan from his pocket, slammed it onto the desk, and stared at Chu Haiming. \"You don't need to drive me away. I'll leave on my own.\"","With that, he turned around and strode out of the office.","Before Chu Haiming could even react, Chu Liangjun was gone.","Looking at the stack of ten-yuan bills on the desk, he hurriedly stood up and chased after him to the door. \"Liangjun, Liangjun! Where are you going? Come back!\"","Chu Liangjun couldn't accept the news that Qiao Lanshu was already married.","Even less could he accept that she had actually married a military officer.","If her husband had been an ordinary worker, he might still have had a chance to fight for her.","But her husband was an officer. How was he supposed to compete with that?","\"It shouldn't be like this, it obviously shouldn't be like this...\"","Coming out of the supply and marketing cooperative, Chu Liangjun muttered to himself the whole way: \"It's not like this. Qiao Lanshu is my woman. She didn't marry any regiment commander. Her fiance was a scammer, not in the military at all... What exactly is going on? Why is it different from the dream?\"","Walking along, Chu Liangjun unknowingly arrived at the main gate of the food factory.","At this time, the workers at the food factory were all on shift.","The iron gates at the entrance were locked. The security guard was sitting in his little booth, drinking tea from a thermos.","He was staring at him while sipping his tea.","Chu Liangjun knew the man looked down on him too, but he couldn't care less about that right now.","He walked up to the door of the security booth. With bloodshot eyes, he stared at the older man inside. \"Mister, let me ask you something.\"","The guard already recognized him; after all, he had been loitering at the factory gates every day, looking at people with strange eyes.","At first glance, he didn't seem like a good person.","The guard ignored him.","But Chu Liangjun kept asking, \"Is Qiao Lanshu married? Is her husband a military officer?\"","The guard nodded, looking at him with some disgust, and said, \"You're just finding out now? The young lady came from the south. Not long after she arrived, she got her marriage certificate with Commander Qin of the 21st Regiment. Everyone knows about this. You really didn't know?\"","Qin Yuanzheng's marriage was considered big news in Longcheng.","Several nearby factories had been discussing it at the time.","The female workers, in particular, had gossiped about it the most enthusiastically.","After all, several female comrades had been on blind dates with Qin Yuanzheng, and everyone knew that he suffered from infertility.","After hearing what the guard said, Chu Liangjun's heart truly turned cold.","It seemed Chu Haiming had not lied to him; Qiao Lanshu really had married a military officer.","Even though in his dream, he was the one who had picked her up and made her his woman.","But in reality, Qiao Lanshu had long since married an officer and was living a happy, harmonious life.","Because of the dream's influence, he had subconsciously assumed she was still unmarried.","\"Commander of the 21st Regiment...\"","Chu Liangjun muttered to himself.","The 21st Regiment was the unit specifically in charge of the mining area.","Not only did they manage the mines, but they were also responsible for building the roads there.","Chu Liangjun knew of that mining area; it was in the suburbs, and he had passed by it a few times.","He heard that a cave-in had recently occurred in one of the mine shafts, caused by a misplaced explosive charge.","The commander had even been injured during the rescue efforts.","The mines were incredibly dangerous places where people could die at any moment. If this commander died, Qiao Lanshu would become a widow.","As Chu Liangjun thought about this, his gaze grew increasingly dark.","It was impossible for him to return to the countryside now.","He had to get his hands on Qiao Lanshu; he needed to take her back to the countryside with him.","...","Chu Liangjun had barely started his job before he was fired again.","Chu Haiming cared about his own reputation, so he did not state the reason publicly.","After all, he was the one who had recommended Chu Liangjun to the supply and marketing cooperative.","The boy was his nephew, but what did this nephew do? He stole money, and he stole it right from under his nose.","If others found out, would they not laugh their heads off?","Where would he put his face?","Chu Haiming took the cashmere coat and the watch back to the department store for a refund. Although he did not have the receipt, the packaging boxes and bags belonged to the department store, and the cashmere coat was exclusively sold there, so the return process went fairly smoothly.","With the items returned and the money back in his hands, Chu Haiming went to look for Chu Liangjun the next day, only to find that he had already moved out of the dormitory.","Chu Haiming assumed Chu Liangjun had gone back to the countryside.","After all, the city was strictly managed now; without a place to live or food to eat, not even a dog would stick around.","Chu Haiming wrote a letter to the production brigade in the countryside, asking the brigade captain to look after Chu Liangjun and, if there were any suitable girls, to help introduce him to one.","What he did not know was that Chu Liangjun had not returned to the countryside at all.","Instead, he went to a road construction site in the mountains to work as a temporary laborer. Every day, he helped carry rocks and sandbags, doing the most grueling work while not even getting enough to eat.","But he did not care, because he was there with a hidden agenda.","Building roads in the mountains required explosives.","There were specialized engineers supervising the work, designing the angles, determining the positions, and then blowing up the mountain to crush the rocks and create flat ground for the road.","In this day and age, explosives were strictly controlled, and Chu Liangjun wanted those explosives.","...","When Qiao Lanshu got off work that day, she did not see Chu Liangjun at the food factory.","The security guard uncle saw her standing at the gate looking around and immediately knew what she was searching for.","Opening the door of the guardhouse, the uncle walked out holding his thermos and said to her, \"Little girl, stop looking. That guy definitely won't be coming back.\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu immediately smiled and walked over. \"Uncle, how did you know who I was looking for?\"","The uncle chuckled. \"Who doesn't know? That pest came here every single day; I was getting sick of seeing him.\"","Qiao Lanshu pulled a warm sweet potato from her pocket and handed it to him. \"Uncle, tell me, why isn't he coming anymore?\"","She had grabbed this sweet potato from the cafeteria at noon and had not eaten it, originally intending to give it to Deng Weijun.","Deng Weijun fetched hot water for her every day and occasionally brought her things like frozen pears.","She could not keep taking advantage of him, so she had to give something back from time to time.","But today, she needed to ask the guard uncle what exactly was going on.","The uncle refused the sweet potato.","Pushing it back toward her, he said, \"No, no, keep such a nice sweet potato for yourself.\"","Lowering his voice, he continued, \"Just this morning, he came by again and asked me if you were a military officer's dependent. I told him the truth. I said you were married, the wife of the 21st Regiment's commander, and told him not to come around anymore.\"","\"I think it scared the life out of him. His face looked completely off, and he walked away looking like he'd lost his soul.\"","The guard uncle gave a cold snort and added, \"Next time you run into that kind of person, just flash your husband's military rank. These street punks might act all tough and cheeky usually, but the second they see a soldier, they're like mice meeting a cat, scared out of their wits. They wouldn't even dare to squeak.\"","Finding this a bit amusing, Qiao Lanshu replied, \"I understand. Thank you, Uncle.\"","The guard waved his hand. \"Alright, head on home. It's getting late.\"","Tonight, Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng were both heading to Yang Wenyan's house for dinner.","Because Deng Weijun was going to meet Wang Haitang, Wang Xue had gotten off work early to pick Wang Haitang up from the train station.","It was quite rare for the woman to go to the man's house for dinner on the very first meeting.","Usually, they would find a chance to meet outside, or the man would follow a matchmaker to the woman's house.","However, Wang Haitang lived in a dormitory, and Wang Xue's house had her parents-in-law and others, making it too crowded and noisy.","Since Wang Xue and Deng Xiaozhen got along so well, they simply decided to have the meeting at Deng Xiaozhen's house.","After the incident with Liu Jianguo, Wang Haitang was a bit afraid of men who tried to hit on her.","She did not have many ideas of her own, so she decided to listen to Wang Xue and find a man with a good personality to date.","If they got along well, there would be plenty of time to discuss marriage later.","...","When Qiao Lanshu came out of the food factory, Qin Yuanzheng was already waiting for her in his car.","Qiao Lanshu quickly ran over, bending down to look at him through the window. \"Why did you drive here? Is your arm better?\"","Last night, while she was asleep, he had done this and that to her...","Tossing and turning for two whole hours without stopping. When Qiao Lanshu got angry and scolded him, he claimed his arm hurt.","It made Qiao Lanshu's heart ache so much that she forgot her anger and just focused on blowing on his arm to soothe it.","And now look at him, driving over here today.","Hearing her words, Qin Yuanzheng coughed with a guilty conscience and said, \"Wife, I feel much better today. It doesn't hurt that much anymore.\"","Qiao Lanshu opened the door, got in, and then looked at his arm, asking, \"It really doesn't hurt? Didn't you say it hurt a lot last night?\"","He had frowned in pain, claiming he had no strength left, and during that intimate moment, he had made her do all the moving herself."]},{"number":109,"title":"Chapter 109: Deng Weijun's Blind Date","paragraphs":["Yang Wenyan's house was quite lively today.","Deng Xiaozhen had dragged Deng Weijun early in the day to start preparing things.","When Deng Weijun heard that his sister had arranged a blind date for him with Wang Xue's cousin, he felt a bit shy.","The shy young man became a man of few words, busying himself inside and out all day.","He helped Deng Xiaozhen buy groceries, went home to cook, and in his free time, he kept busy sweeping and mopping, tidying the house until it was spotless.","When Yang Wenyan returned, he was a little unaccustomed to seeing the house so clean and neat.","After all, there were no elderly family members living with them, and the couple was usually busy with work, leaving no one to do the chores.","The floor was only mopped once every few days. Sometimes when it got dirty, Deng Xiaozhen would just give it a quick sweep with a broom.","Today, Deng Weijun was like a madman, doing chores non-stop.","He swept the entire house and then mopped it twice.","He took in all the clothes hanging on the balcony and put them in the wardrobe, and even scrubbed the bathroom.","Then, he wandered around the living room, tidied up the sofa, wiped down the dining table, and whenever he saw things looking too messy, he conveniently organized them.","Yang Wenyan barely had any room to step.","He stood at the door, having just taken off his coat and hung it up.","Deng Weijun came over, took the coat down, smoothed it out, and then hung it back up.","Yang Wenyan: \"...\"","Yang Wenyan smiled and asked Deng Weijun, \"Excuse me, Comrade Deng Weijun, may I sit on the sofa now?\"","Deng Weijun: \"...\"","Deng Weijun scratched his head in embarrassment and said, \"Brother-in-law, stop teasing me. This is your house, you can sit wherever you want.\"","Yang Wenyan laughed, \"You rascal. Alright, stop cleaning. The house is neat and clean enough. The way you're going at it, I'm afraid to even walk inside.\"","Feeling a bit sheepish, Deng Weijun retreated to the kitchen.","Deng Xiaozhen had managed to buy some rare pork fat today. She rendered the fat and used the crispy pork cracklings to make a large pot of braised stew.","First, she fried potato chunks in the pork cracklings for a while, then added water, throwing in glass noodles, wood ear mushrooms, daikon radish, and napa cabbage to boil together.","Normally, when she made stew, there were no pork cracklings, and it didn't smell this fragrant.","Right before taking it out of the pot, she poured in some aged vinegar. The aroma was simply irresistible.","Smelling the stew, Deng Weijun's stomach rumbled, and his mouth watered. \"Sis, your stew smells the best! I'm starving to death right now.\"","Deng Xiaozhen glared at him and scolded, \"When the girl comes over later, don't act like a reincarnated starving ghost, you hear me? You can eat anytime, but you can't just get a wife whenever you want. You have to seize this opportunity, understand?\"","Deng Weijun nodded sheepishly. \"I know, Sis. You've emphasized this several times already.\"","How could Deng Xiaozhen not know her brother's nature?","When this young man was hungry, he only had eyes for food. Where would a girl fit in?","She thought for a moment, then took out two freshly steamed multigrain buns from the pot, put them in a bowl, and handed them to him. \"Have a bite to hold you over first. Later, you better behave well and try to get yourself a wife this year, got it?\"","Deng Weijun had only been doing chores left and right earlier because he was nervous.","After busying himself all afternoon, he was indeed hungry.","So he held the bowl, sat on a small stool in front of the stove, and ate his bun while helping Deng Xiaozhen tend the fire. He nodded and said, \"Sis, the blind date hasn't even happened yet. I haven't even seen what the girl looks like, and you're already talking about marriage? What if we don't like each other? What if I like her, but she doesn't like me?\"","While chopping pickled cabbage, Deng Xiaozhen replied, \"If it really doesn't work out, then there's nothing we can do. I'll just look around for you another day.\"","Deng Weijun's conditions actually weren't bad.","Although his parents were from the village, his own household registration was in the city, and he had a formal job.","He also had a brother-in-law who was a factory director, so he didn't need to worry about finding a wife.","In the past, Deng Xiaozhen felt that he was still young and there was no need to rush.","Now, however, she felt that he was fooling around every day without a serious demeanor. To prevent him from causing trouble, it was better for him to hurry up, get married, and have children.","Approaching six o'clock, Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu arrived.","Coming over for dinner this time, Qiao Lanshu didn't arrive empty-handed.","She brought two jars of canned fruit and two loaves of bread.","In this era, in northern cities, people generally gave canned fruit and bread as gifts because they were expensive, and most people were reluctant to eat them on a regular basis.","Yang Wenyan was very happy to see Qin Yuanzheng. \"Yuanzheng, ever since you got married, I haven't seen you in ages. How is your wound? Is it getting better?\"","The last time he heard Qin Yuanzheng was injured, Yang Wenyan had made time to visit him once.","A few days had passed, and he hadn't gone to check on him again.","Qin Yuanzheng showed Yang Wenyan his arm and said, \"It's almost completely healed. I can go back to work tomorrow.\"","If this were in the past, how could he rest just for an arm injury?","On the battlefield, there was no such thing as recuperation. As long as you could still move, you had to keep fighting.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't take this wound seriously.","However, he would occasionally use his injured arm to play the victim in front of Qiao Lanshu, getting her to coax him and listen to him when he wanted certain things done. It was actually quite effective.","Hearing the commotion, Deng Xiaozhen walked out. Seeing Qiao Lanshu holding things, she quickly said, \"Oh my, you could have just come over. Why did you bring gifts?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Cousin-in-law, this is the first time Zheng and I have visited since we got married. We definitely had to bring some gifts. It's not much, I hope you don't mind.\"","Deng Xiaozhen exclaimed, \"Not at all, not at all! Go take a seat for a while, I'll go cook.\"","Qiao Lanshu placed the items on the table and then followed her into the kitchen. \"Cousin-in-law, do you need any help?\"","Then, she saw Deng Weijun sitting in front of the stove, eating his bun.","Deng Weijun's mouth was stuffed full, making him look quite comical.","He embarrassedly called out, \"Sister-in-law, you're here.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Sister Xue and Haitang should be here soon too. Sister Xue even got off work early today.\"","Deng Xiaozhen's stew was ready as well. She quickly took off the pot lid and said, \"Perfect timing, the stew is done. Let's clear the table and get ready to eat.\"","Deng Xiaozhen had made a huge pot of stew, prepared a few cold dishes, cooked some coarse grain porridge, and steamed multigrain buns.","She also took one of the loaves of bread Qiao Lanshu brought, sliced it up, and placed it on a plate.","The food was laid out, filling a large table. Right at that moment, Wang Xue and her sister arrived.","Wang Xue didn't bring her husband; she only brought Wang Haitang. She was carrying a bag of eggs in her hand.","In this era, food was precious. It was never good manners to show up empty-handed when going to someone else's house for dinner.","Even though they were the woman's side coming to the man's home for a blind date—where generally no gifts were required.","But who could ignore the fact that Yang Wenyan was the director of the food factory?","Wang Xue worked at the food factory, so even if this matchmaking attempt didn't work out, she still wanted to stay on good terms with the factory manager's family.","Deng Xiaozhen went to open the door and warmly greeted Wang Xue. The two women linked arms and instantly fell into endless chatter.","They couldn't help it; their personalities were just too compatible. Whenever someone mentioned something funny, they would burst into laughter together.","Deng Weijun stood somewhat stiffly by the table, stealing glances toward the front door.","Wang Haitang was very thin. Although her appearance was rather ordinary, she had a certain charm that grew on you.","She wore her hair in two thick braids, dressed in a floral padded jacket and a red scarf. Standing next to Wang Xue, she kept her head bowed, too embarrassed to even look at the people in the room.","After Wang Xue and Deng Xiaozhen exchanged pleasantries for a while, Deng Xiaozhen looked at Wang Haitang behind her and smiled. \"Oh, is this the sweet little sister you mentioned?\"","Wang Xue smiled and nodded. Pulling Wang Haitang forward, she said, \"Haitang, hurry up and say hello to your sister-in-law.\"","Since Wang Xue called Deng Xiaozhen sister-in-law, Wang Haitang naturally had to follow suit.","Blushing, Wang Haitang softly called out, \"Sister-in-law.\"","Her voice was so quiet that it barely left her mouth.","Seeing her acting like this, Wang Xue felt a bit anxious and nudged Wang Haitang with her elbow.","Deng Xiaozhen looked Wang Haitang up and down, knowing the girl was just shy. She smiled and said, \"You came at the perfect time. I just finished making dinner. Come on, sit down and eat. Weijun, hurry and bring a stool over for Haitang.\"","Deng Weijun quickly agreed, grabbed a chair, and moved it over. Blushing, he said, \"Comrade, please sit.\"","Only then did Wang Haitang lift her head and glance at him.","Their eyes met, and Deng Weijun smiled awkwardly.","Wang Haitang lowered her head again and took a seat.","The room wasn't very large, so it felt a bit crowded with everyone inside.","Yang Wenyan and Qin Yuanzheng also walked over. After another round of greetings, everyone sat down.","Qiao Lanshu occasionally glanced at Deng Weijun, then at Wang Haitang.","It was her first time witnessing someone else's blind date, and she found it quite interesting.","Meanwhile, Qin Yuanzheng chatted with Yang Wenyan while placing food into Qiao Lanshu's bowl.","When they were almost done eating, Deng Xiaozhen suddenly spoke up. \"Oh my, there are still a few roasted sweet potatoes in the stove, and I haven't checked on them. I wonder if they're done. Weijun, go in and take a look for me.\"","Before Deng Weijun could grasp the hidden meaning, he quickly stood up and said, \"Sure, sis, I'll go right now.\"","Wang Xue immediately caught on and told Wang Haitang, \"Haitang, go in and help Weijun out. He can't carry that many all by himself.\"","Wang Haitang was speechless.","Having no choice, she stood up and silently followed Deng Weijun into the kitchen.","When Deng Weijun saw Wang Haitang following him in, he was startled.","He glanced outside and said, blushing, \"I don't need... I don't need your help. I can manage it on my own.\"","Wang Haitang looked up at him but didn't say a word.","Deng Weijun said awkwardly, \"Really, I used to roast sweet potatoes all the time when I was a kid in the village. I'm really good at this.\"","Wang Haitang remained standing beside him, showing no intention of leaving.","Deng Weijun felt even more awkward.","He rarely interacted with female colleagues and honestly had no idea how to communicate with women.","After a moment, it suddenly dawned on him that this was a blind date. What was he supposed to say on a blind date?","Squatting in front of the stove and staring at the roasting sweet potatoes inside, he scratched his head and asked, \"What's your name?\"","Wang Haitang also squatted down, looking at the sweet potatoes. In a low voice, she replied, \"I'm Wang Haitang.\"","Deng Weijun said, \"I... I'm Deng Weijun.\"","Wang Haitang glanced at him again and said, \"I know.\"","Deng Weijun was at a loss for words.","He cleared his throat and continued, \"I'm 22 years old. I work as a boiler man at the food factory. I'm a regular employee, and my monthly salary is 35 yuan.\"","Hearing this, Wang Haitang assumed that reporting one's salary was standard procedure for a blind date. She replied, \"I work as a ticket seller at the train station. I'm also a regular employee, and my salary is 30 yuan.\"","After a brief pause, she added, \"I'm 21 years old.\"","Wang Xue had already told Deng Xiaozhen about the incident between Wang Haitang and Liu Jianguo.","Deng Xiaozhen had passed it on to Deng Weijun, and he didn't mind it at all.","After all, it was Liu Jianguo's fault, not Wang Haitang's.","After exchanging these few sentences, Deng Weijun felt much less nervous.","He turned his head and snuck a few glances at Wang Haitang.","Wang Haitang also peeked at him a few times.","After a moment of silence between them, Deng Weijun asked, \"As a ticket seller, you have to work night shifts, right? What time do you get off work at night?\"","Wang Haitang replied, \"The latest I get off is eight in the evening.\"","Deng Weijun immediately offered, \"Then how about I pick you up from work from now on?\"","Wang Haitang pursed her lips. Looking at the sweet potatoes in the stove, she neither nodded nor shook her head. She simply said, \"The sweet potatoes are done. Let's take them out together.\"","Deng Weijun felt a wave of disappointment, thinking Wang Haitang wasn't interested in him.","He silently dug out the roasted sweet potatoes, blew the ash off them, and placed them in a basket.","Just as they were walking out the door, Wang Haitang suddenly spoke up again. \"I get off the night shift tomorrow.\"","Then, she ran out as soon as the words left her mouth.","Deng Weijun stood there, stunned.","He scratched his head, still trying to process what Wang Haitang meant by that.","He carried the roasted sweet potatoes out and placed them on the table. By this time, everyone was full and sitting around chatting.","Wang Xue didn't hold anything back and directly brought up the matter with Liu Jianguo, cursing him out for quite a while.","Wang Xue said, \"That Liu Jianguo actually dared to block Haitang on her way home from work! If Xiao Qiao hadn't reminded me to file a report at the public security bureau, I wouldn't have even thought of it!\"","Deng Xiaozhen chimed in indignantly, \"People like Liu Jianguo should be sent to struggle sessions and paraded through the streets so everyone can see what happens to hooligans!\"","Wang Xue continued, \"You have no idea, there are plenty of people like that in our factory. Just a few days ago, a temporary worker from the supply and marketing cooperative was following Xiao Qiao. Good thing he hasn't shown up these past few days, or he'd be sent off to a labor camp too.\"","Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen were unaware that Chu Liangjun had been following Qiao Lanshu.","However, Qin Yuanzheng knew about it because Xiao Yang reported everything to him.","Qin Yuanzheng had even instructed Xiao Yang to have someone keep an eye on Chu Liangjun.","It was just that Qin Yuanzheng had injured his arm recently and was recovering at home instead of going to the office, so Xiao Yang hadn't updated him on the progress yet.","Hearing this, Deng Xiaozhen said in surprise, \"Xiao Qiao is a military officer's family member. Everyone in the neighborhood knows that. Who would be so fearless of death as to target a military family member?\"","The military wielded significant power. Bullying a military officer's family member was basically asking for a bullet."]},{"number":110,"title":"Chapter 110: The Qiao Lan Book Case","paragraphs":["Hearing them talk about her, Qiao Lanshu immediately felt embarrassed. She said, \"This matter has already been resolved, so please stop teasing me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng leaned close to her ear and whispered, \"I heard from Xiao Yang about that person. He hasn't been coming around lately?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and replied in a low voice, \"He hasn't.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded thoughtfully.","He was returning to the mining area tomorrow. He would find Xiao Yang then and ask him what exactly was going on with that man.","After the meal, it was getting late. Deng Xiaozhen and Wang Xue politely bid each other farewell.","When Wang Xue arrived, she had brought a bag of eggs. Now, as she was leaving, Deng Xiaozhen brought out a package of biscuits for her to take back.","Standing at the door as she was about to leave, Wang Xue was still declining the gift. \"The two of us sisters came over for a meal today, and you prepared such a rich feast. How could I possibly accept more things from you? Hurry up and take it back, please don't insist.\"","Deng Xiaozhen kept stuffing the biscuits into her arms, putting on a stern face. \"Look at you. With our relationship, let's not act like strangers.\"","Saying that, she smiled at Wang Haitang and said, \"Haitang, when you have free time in the future, you can still come over with your sister to hang out with me. Don't be a stranger.\"","Wang Haitang smiled a little shyly.","She glanced inside the house and saw Deng Weijun standing behind Deng Xiaozhen, secretly looking at her too.","After declining a few times, Wang Xue eventually accepted the biscuits.","She said with a smile, \"Then, sister-in-law, we'll be leaving first.\"","Deng Xiaozhen nodded and asked, \"Your husband is coming to pick you up, right? Has he arrived?\"","Wang Xue: \"He should be here. I told him to be at the compound gate at eight o'clock sharp, and it's already a quarter past eight.\"","It was pitch black outside now. Although homes had electric lights, there weren't many streetlights, and some alleys were completely dark.","Deng Xiaozhen said, \"I'll have Weijun walk you two down. If your husband hasn't arrived, Weijun can wait with you for a while. He's not doing anything anyway.\"","Wang Xue glanced at Wang Haitang and nodded. \"Alright, then we'll trouble Weijun.\"","Deng Weijun quickly put on his padded jacket and walked out. \"Sister, it's no trouble. It's what I should do.\"","With that, Deng Weijun took the lead into the hallway, guiding Wang Xue and Wang Haitang downstairs.","Once they went downstairs, Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng also prepared to take their leave.","Everyone had enjoyed today's meal very much.","It was just unknown whether Deng Weijun and Wang Haitang had taken a liking to each other.","Returning inside, Deng Xiaozhen said, \"I don't know what's going on with those two. When they came out of the kitchen, you couldn't read anything from their expressions.\"","Yang Wenyan was sitting there drinking tea. Hearing this, he told her, \"There's no need to rush. I'll just ask Wang Xue tomorrow and we'll know.\"","Deng Xiaozhen sat there and added, \"This girl is indeed too introverted. She doesn't like to talk and barely looks up at people. A personality like that is bound to suffer losses.\"","Qiao Lanshu thought to herself: Isn't that the truth? Wang Haitang had already suffered at the hands of Liu Jianguo.","If it weren't for her sister Wang Xue being fierce enough, Wang Haitang might have already been completely taken advantage of by Liu Jianguo.","Every time Qiao Lanshu thought of Liu Jianguo, she would associate him with Chu Liangjun.","She always felt that Liu Jianguo and Chu Liangjun were the same kind of people.","The fundamental nature of such people was bad, and at their age, they couldn't be set straight anymore. They should either be sent to a labor camp or sent six feet under.","In short, they couldn't be left here to harm others.","Seeing that it was about time, Qin Yuanzheng stood up and said goodbye to Yang Wenyan. \"Cousin, it's getting late. We'll be heading back now too.\"","Yang Wenyan immediately stood up. \"Alright. It's dark and the roads are slippery, so drive slowly.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He had already taken down Qiao Lanshu's padded jacket and scarf.","Although his arm was injured, it didn't stop him from attending to his wife.","He unfolded the padded jacket and personally helped Qiao Lanshu put it on.","Seeing this, Yang Wenyan: \"...\"","Deng Xiaozhen: \"...\"","Deng Xiaozhen looked at Qin Yuanzheng, and then she cast a disdainful glance at Yang Wenyan.","Yang Wenyan was baffled by her look and asked, \"What's wrong? Why are you looking at me like that?\"","Deng Xiaozhen felt uncomfortable in her heart, thinking that it wasn't that men were unreliable, but rather she just hadn't met a reliable one.","Look at Qin Yuanzheng. Even with an injured arm, he still helped his wife put on her coat and wrapped her scarf around her, being incredibly attentive.","She heard that at home, it was also Qin Yuanzheng who did the chores, washing clothes and cooking.","It was said that he washed the clothes because he was afraid the cold water would chill his wife, and he cooked because he was afraid she would cut her fingers.","Deng Xiaozhen had never seen a man in such a high position who was still willing to do housework like this.","She rolled her eyes at Yang Wenyan and said, \"If you don't even know why I'm looking at you, then what else is there for me to say?\"","Yang Wenyan was exasperated. \"If you don't tell me, how am I supposed to know why you're looking at me?\"","Deng Xiaozhen couldn't be bothered to talk to him anymore.","Men were truly most afraid of being compared.","She went to the kitchen, took a small basket, and put six free-range eggs inside. She grabbed some fresh red dates, wrapped them in kraft paper, placed them on top of the eggs, and brought the basket out to give to Qiao Lanshu, saying:","\"Xiao Qiao, these are red dates my maiden family sent me. They're from the date trees grown in our own private plot, and they're very sweet. Take them back to eat, or make them into date cakes or date buns. The taste is absolutely top-notch.\"","Qiao Lanshu was just about to decline when Deng Xiaozhen interrupted her, \"Alright, we're all family, don't be so polite. If Weijun's marriage works out this time, I'm going to give you a big red envelope.\"","Qiao Lanshu was actually considered half a matchmaker, and Deng Xiaozhen kept all of this in her heart.","Qiao Lanshu had no choice but to accept it.","As she and Qin Yuanzheng went downstairs and drove toward the compound gate, they saw Deng Weijun riding a bicycle, carrying Wang Haitang. Wang Xue was sitting on the back of a bicycle ridden by a man in a black padded jacket, who was likely Wang Xue's husband.","The four people on two bicycles had already gone quite a distance.","Qiao Lanshu leaned against the car window, looked out for a while, and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"It looks like this match will work out.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and gave a hmm of agreement.","He wasn't very interested in this matter.","Right now, he rather wanted to investigate Chu Liangjun and see what exactly was going on with that man.","After returning home, the couple briefly washed up and prepared to go to bed.","Seeing that Qiao Lanshu didn't take a bath and didn't call him to take one either, Qin Yuanzheng knew that nothing was going to happen tonight.","However, Qin Yuanzheng knew he was in the wrong;","Who asked him to take advantage of his little wife while she was sleeping last night...","In the middle of the night yesterday, after Qiao Lanshu was woken up by him, she was quite angry.","Although even when she was angry, it looked more like she was acting coquettishly.","Then, to keep his little wife from being mad at him, he lied and said his arm hurt, and then complained about how hard it was for him to hold back. Not long after, he claimed he couldn't use any strength in his arm, coaxing Qiao Lanshu into taking the lead herself.","Relying on his arm injury, he coaxed and tricked his little wife into cooperating with him to unlock many new positions.","Qiao Lanshu probably realized that she had been tricked by Qin Yuanzheng, so as soon as she came back tonight, she rolled out the two quilts again.","She even used clothes to draw a boundary line in the middle of the kang bed. Sitting there with her hair draped over her shoulders and wearing loose, thin pajamas, she said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, tonight we sleep separately. You are not allowed to come over.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Looking at Qiao Lanshu, who was so far away from him, Qin Yuanzheng asked somewhat helplessly, \"I promised not to touch you and that's that. Do you really need to lie so far away?\"","A 2.4-meter-wide kang bed, with each of them sleeping at opposite ends—that was indeed too far.","Qiao Lanshu lay down, adjusted her quilt, and said, \"It's better to be a bit farther apart. Go to sleep, Brother Zheng. Good night.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng could do nothing about his little wife, so he had no choice but to lie down.","Once Qiao Lanshu fell asleep, he went straight over, slipped into her quilt, pulled his wife into his arms, and let out a comfortable sigh.","Sure enough, he could only fall asleep while holding his wife.","...","The next day, when Qiao Lanshu woke up, Qin Yuanzheng had already gone to make breakfast.","Qin Yuanzheng had to go to work today, so after breakfast, the couple left the house together.","He dropped Qiao Lanshu off at the main gate of the food factory and then headed to the mining area, planning to look for Xiao Yang.","As for Qiao Lanshu, she also had things on her mind. After Qin Yuanzheng left,","she went to the logistics department to ask for half a day off, then walked out of the food factory alone and got on a bus.","Qiao Lanshu didn't go to the supply and marketing cooperative to ask about Chu Liangjun.","She guessed that Chu Liangjun had probably already quit his job at the cooperative, although she hadn't gone to confirm it.","However, based on her understanding of Chu Liangjun, the moment he was questioned by Chu Haiming, he wouldn't return to the cooperative again.","Chu Liangjun was very vengeful; he hated anyone who looked down on him.","In her previous life, Chu Liangjun brought a girl he found back to the village and locked her up. When Niu Weifen found out, she made Chu Haiming sever ties with him.","Because of this, Chu Liangjun stole a pack of explosives from the construction site where he worked and buried it on the path Niu Weifen frequently took, nearly blowing her to death.","Later, it was Niu Weifen's brother, a division commander in the military, who found out about this and went to arrest Chu Liangjun.","Chu Liangjun was planning his escape, which led to his negligence, giving Qiao Lanshu a chance to run away.","It could be said that in her previous life, Qiao Lanshu's ability to escape from the cave dwelling was due to multiple factors.","In this life, Qiao Lanshu felt that since Chu Liangjun had been schemed against by her, he would probably hate her and use the explosives to blow her up instead.","She took the bus to the suburbs, where a highway was being built.","She didn't go to the construction site to ask around. Instead, she went to the temporary tin-roofed office at the site and found the logistics staff inside.","The office was crammed with desks and chairs, with men and women sitting together working. There was no heating in the room, so everyone relied on a stove for warmth.","A female comrade sitting near the door saw Qiao Lanshu come in and asked, \"Miss, who are you looking for?\"","Qiao Lanshu walked in with a smile and said somewhat shyly, \"Sister, I'm a worker from the food factory. Here is my employee card. I came here because I want to ask you about someone.\"","Hearing that her accent was not local, the female comrade looked at her employee card to confirm she was from the food factory. Seeing that she was young, fair-skinned, and wearing a new padded jacket and scarf, she could tell at a glance that she was a girl from a good family.","She smiled and asked, \"Who is it? I have a list here, I can check for you. Is it your relative?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Yes, he's my brother from my maiden family. His name is Qiao Liangjun: Qiao as in the Qiao Family Courtyard, Liang as in excellent, and Jun as in soldier. Could you help me check if someone by this name came to work at the construction site in the past few days?\"","The female comrade then took out a labor manual from a cabinet.","Building roads at their construction site involved hard physical labor, requiring a large number of workers to help out.","Some of the laborers were temporary workers, so the requirements were not that strict.","After all, on a construction site under military jurisdiction, no one dared to cause trouble.","The female comrade flipped straight to the back and started looking from the last worker hired. Then, she suddenly said, \"Oh, there's a man named Chu Liangjun, 25 years old, who joined yesterday. Is this the person you're looking for?\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu immediately knew what was going on.","She smiled and said, \"Not this one, comrade. My brother's name is Qiao Liangjun, and he's 35 years old this year. Is there such a person?\"","The female comrade searched through the list of new hires for the past month but couldn't find such a person. \"Oh my, there really isn't. Little girl, are you sure your brother came to this site? We have three road construction sites here for three different roads. Why don't you go ask at the other two sites?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, thanked the female comrade with immense gratitude, and then left the office.","She walked outside facing the cold wind. The construction site was completely bare, and it was very dusty. When the cold wind blew, the dust flew right into her face.","Qiao Lanshu pondered in her heart. If Chu Liangjun was going to use explosives to blow her up, just like he did to Niu Weifen in her previous life,","where would he bury the explosives?","The roads she usually took were all busy streets with people coming and going.","From the food factory to the cooperative, and from the cooperative to the military residential compound.","There were many people on every route.","If he was audacious enough to bury the explosives on the street, wouldn't he accidentally injure many innocent passersby?","It was true that Qiao Lanshu wanted Chu Liangjun dead, but she didn't want to hurt innocent people either.","Chu Liangjun had gone to the construction site yesterday, and she didn't know when he would manage to steal the explosives.","This matter couldn't wait; it had to be dealt with as soon as possible.","When Qin Yuanzheng came back in the afternoon, she would tell him about this and have him arrange for people to investigate.","Besides, she also needed to go to the police station to report the case.","Qiao Lanshu turned her steps and walked in the direction of the police station.","As she walked, she pondered again. Suppose it took Chu Liangjun a few more days to steal the explosives, or what if he didn't steal them at all and gave up on seeking revenge against her? Wouldn't she be filing a false police report then?","The police comrades were already short-staffed; she couldn't deceive the police like this.","While thinking, Qiao Lanshu arrived at the entrance of the police station.","The comrades at the police station were already familiar with Qiao Lanshu.","After all, she had just come here with Wang Xue last time.","Qiao Lanshu walked into the police station and said to a young police officer on duty, \"Hello, comrade. I would like to report a case.\""]},{"number":111,"title":"Chapter 111: With Explosives","paragraphs":["The police officer on duty was surnamed Jiang. Seeing Qiao Lanshu hurrying into the police station, he immediately stood up and asked politely, \"Comrade, what kind of case do you want to report?\"","Officer Xiao Jiang still remembered Qiao Lanshu.","After all, it was hard to forget such a beautiful girl with a southern accent.","It was no exaggeration to say that in their neighborhood, Qiao Lanshu was the only one with this accent.","Officer Xiao Jiang thought that the case Qiao Lanshu wanted to report was about the harassed ticket conductor from before.","He asked Qiao Lanshu, \"Is it for your friend who works as a ticket conductor at the train station? Has she been harassed again these past few days?\"","Unexpectedly, Qiao Lanshu's words gave the police officer quite a fright.","She shook her head and said with a serious expression, \"No, comrade officer. I came to report a case today because someone wants to steal explosives to take revenge on me.\"","Officer Xiao Jiang: \"...\"","The young officer thought he had misheard. He froze for a moment and repeated with a shocked expression, \"Someone wants to steal explosives to take revenge on you?\"","Explosives?","Was that something that could even be stolen?","To be honest, even Officer Xiao Jiang himself didn't know where to steal such a thing.","Qiao Lanshu stood there without taking a seat. Gripping the hem of her shirt with both hands, she nodded worriedly. Frowning, she said:","\"Yes, comrade officer. This matter goes back to a few days ago. Previously, a temporary worker from the supply and marketing cooperative approached me. Not only did he wait for me at the gate of the food factory every day, but he also tailed me on my way home from work. My colleagues and some soldiers can testify to this.","A couple of days ago, this person gave me a coat and a watch. They were both bought at the department store and were very expensive. I didn't dare to accept them, so I returned everything to his uncle. His uncle must have criticized him and even fired him from his job! Oh, right, his uncle is Chu Haiming, the director of the supply and marketing cooperative. You can go and verify this.","Because of these things, he was very angry. He stopped me on the road and said he was going to blow me up. I was very scared, so I came to you to report the case.\"","Qiao Lanshu spoke clearly, explaining the cause and effect, and even naming witnesses.","It sounded so convincing that the police officer was somewhat impressed.","However, stealing explosives still sounded a bit unbelievable.","Hearing this, Officer Xiao Jiang pondered while taking notes.","A few minutes later, the fountain pen in his hand stopped. He looked up at Qiao Lanshu and comforted her with a gentle expression:","\"Little girl, don't be afraid first, and don't worry. The other party might have just said it out of anger, and he may not really dare to steal explosives. Besides, explosives are controlled by specialized departments, and they can't be stolen just like that. Don't be nervous.\"","Qiao Lanshu wasn't exactly nervous; it was just that Chu Liangjun was currently a ticking time bomb. What if he accidentally injured someone else?","Although explosives were controlled by specialized personnel, Chu Liangjun really could steal them.","Qiao Lanshu said, \"Comrade officer, it's better to be safe than sorry. What if he really steals the explosives, what if...\"","As she spoke, she stopped, looking as if she wanted to say something but hesitated, appearing deeply worried.","Officer Xiao Jiang jotted down a few more notes in the report log. Then, he thought for a few seconds before asking again, \"Then, little girl, do you know where he is now? You just said he had been fired, meaning he's no longer at the supply and marketing cooperative, right?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Yes, he's no longer working at the supply cooperative.\"","With that, she told him about Chu Liangjun working at the road construction site.","Finally, she added:","\"Comrade officer, I heard that when building roads in the mountains, there are special explosives used for blasting. I'm worried he will sneak some out. So, comrade officer, can you quietly go over and keep an eye on him? Or check with the construction site to have them strengthen the management of explosives. If no explosives are missing, then there is no problem, but if they are lost...\"","Although Qiao Lanshu said this, the police officer still felt that Chu Liangjun's threat to blow her up was likely said in a fit of pique and shouldn't be taken seriously.","Of course, Chu Liangjun had never actually said the words \"blow her up\" to Qiao Lanshu;","This was something Qiao Lanshu had fabricated herself in order to file the report. After all, the police wouldn't be able to verify it anytime soon.","Moreover, what Qiao Lanshu said was also the truth;","Because in her previous life, Chu Liangjun had indeed stolen explosives from the construction site and buried them on the road to blow up his aunt, Niu Weifen.","Since Qiao Lanshu had reported the case, the police couldn't just sit idly by.","Although in this era, the role of the police station was not as significant as that of the Revolutionary Committee, they still had the corresponding authority.","After Qiao Lanshu reported the case, Officer Xiao Jiang told her to go back to work at the food factory for now.","He said, \"Little comrade, rest assured. Leave this matter to me. We will go to the construction site to inspect.\"","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu left the police station.","However, she was still thinking about the matter in her heart, planning to tell Qin Yuanzheng about it when he came over in the afternoon.","The construction site was under the jurisdiction of the engineering corps. Perhaps Qin Yuanzheng would have a better solution.","...","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng stepped into the mining area, the cold wind blew dust into his face.","Without stopping, he went straight to the office and called Xiao Yang over to ask some questions.","Xiao Yang stood up straight. \"Regimental Commander, Chu Liangjun has already resigned from the supply and marketing cooperative. He hasn't secretly followed the sister-in-law these past few days. Right now, he is carrying bricks and working on the highway near our mining area. We couldn't keep too close an eye on him to avoid gossip. Seeing that he was working steadily and hard, we temporarily withdrew the people keeping watch.\"","After all, Chu Liangjun had merely lost his job and was working quietly. He hadn't actually done anything illegal or undisciplined, so the military personnel couldn't just indiscriminately keep a tight watch on him.","Xiao Yang paused, as if suddenly remembering something, and hurriedly added, \"Oh right, Regimental Commander, a couple of days ago, Chu Liangjun seemed to have given the sister-in-law some things, but she returned them untouched to Chu Haiming.\"","Qin Yuanzheng frowned slightly, a hint of surprise flashing in his eyes.","His face subconsciously darkened a bit, and he asked in a deep voice, \"What did he give Xiao Qiao?\"","\"It seems... a watch.\"","Xiao Yang answered cautiously.","Qin Yuanzheng snorted coldly, his tone carrying a subtle hint of possessiveness and disdain. \"The day I got my marriage certificate, I bought my wife a watch. She has no shortage of such things.\"","Knowing that Chu Liangjun was now honestly carrying bricks at the construction site and working hard, Qin Yuanzheng didn't press the matter further.","Although Chu Liangjun had previously secretly followed his wife and now rashly gave her gifts, which really made him feel disgusted and unhappy.","But Qin Yuanzheng had always been a reasonable man; he couldn't just drive someone to a dead end simply because they admired his wife.","His wife was young and so beautiful; it was only natural that she would attract people's affection.","As long as Chu Liangjun knew his limits, didn't cross the line, and didn't disrupt their peaceful lives, he could hold off on pursuing the matter for now.","He slowly stood up. Xiao Yang, quick on the draw, immediately stepped forward, took down the military greatcoat hanging on the office wall, and carefully draped it over his shoulders.","Although the injury on Qin Yuanzheng's arm had healed somewhat, it still required daily dressing changes. The bandages were fresh, and any large movements would pull at the wound and cause pain.","Staff Officer Lin, Xiao Yang, and the others who stayed by his side all treated him like a fragile object, caring for him meticulously, terrified that he would experience even the slightest inconvenience in his movements.","Let alone taking the initiative to help him dress, even during lunch, Staff Officer Lin would come over holding a spoon, practically itching to feed him personally.","Just as Xiao Yang finished putting the coat on him, before Qin Yuanzheng could even speak, Staff Officer Lin quickly grabbed his military cap and plopped it onto his head without a word.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Staff Officer Lin looked deeply concerned, though his tone was somewhat asking for a beating as he said, \"Regiment Commander, where are you heading? Can your body hold up? If it's too much, we can carry you there on our backs.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was both annoyed and amused. He raised his foot and gave him a light kick, scolding with a laugh, \"Get lost!\"","Staff Officer Lin chuckled and quickly scurried out.","Qin Yuanzheng was going to inspect the mining area.","A few days ago, a mistake in the placement of explosives at the mine had caused a series of serious accidents, which had only barely been resolved over the past couple of days.","Because of this, the military had arrested several people in a row—the engineer in charge, the blaster who handled the explosives, and a few on-site supervisors. Not a single one was spared.","It was currently a critical juncture in the espionage war, and no one could guarantee that the enemy hadn't secretly infiltrated the mining area.","Therefore, even with his injured arm, Qin Yuanzheng simply couldn't rest easy. He had to come over and inspect the area himself several times to feel reassured.","Workers came and went constantly in the mining area; it was bustling and noisy. There were also several large, fierce-looking wolfdogs kept there.","These wolfdogs were all retired military dogs—smart, alert, and possessing a keen sense of smell. When they got aggressive, their presence was truly intimidating.","The logistics soldiers had specially built spacious doghouses out of thick wood next to the mine's dormitories for them to rest in.","And next to the doghouses, a somewhat simple-minded man could always be found crouching. He spent all day with the dogs, sometimes even eating with them. It was a particularly heartbreaking sight.","When Qin Yuanzheng walked past and saw him, he paused his steps and turned to ask Xiao Yang, \"Why is Lao Wu back again? Wasn't it arranged for him to be sent to the military district sanatorium a long time ago?\"","Xiao Yang quickly stepped forward to reply, \"Regiment Commander, we did send him there, but he sneaked back on his own. I originally thought he couldn't bear to part with these military dogs, so I sent the dogs over to him too. But guess what? He brought the dogs and ran back overnight.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","In his youth, Lao Wu was a military dog trainer in the army. He had spent his whole life dealing with military dogs, raising them carefully and training them strictly.","Later, amidst the fires of war, an explosive detonated right next to him. He was instantly deafened in one ear, and his brain suffered severe trauma, leaving him alternating between moments of lucidity and confusion.","The military dog he had raised with his own hands back then was also lost in that war.","The military dogs he was guarding now were all retired after the war ended, and they were all exceptionally attached to Lao Wu.","Seeing Lao Wu guarding the doghouses day after day, Qin Yuanzheng was somewhat concerned about his health.","Fortunately, the mining area had dormitories and a cafeteria, so at least he wouldn't freeze or go hungry.","He didn't say much else, just calling out to Lao Wu from a distance, \"Lao Wu, walking the dogs?\"","With that said, he prepared to walk past.","Hearing someone call him, Lao Wu slowly raised his head. He was holding a large dog in his arms, his rough hands continuously stroking its fur as he muttered repeatedly, \"Explosives... explosives... someone is going to blow up the mine...\"","Qin Yuanzheng chuckled and turned to Xiao Yang and Staff Officer Lin, saying, \"Who says Lao Wu is simple-minded? I think he's very clear-headed. It's been days since the mine explosion incident, and he still remembers it.\"","Xiao Yang was also a bit puzzled. \"Strange, how did Lao Wu know the mine was blown up? Didn't we specifically lock down the information?\"","Staff Officer Lin thought for a moment and said casually, \"No matter how tight the lockdown is, insiders will always talk about it in private. Lao Wu wanders around the dormitories and cafeteria every day. What rumors could get past him?\"","Seeing the three men in military uniforms turning to leave without the slightest intention of stopping to investigate, Lao Wu suddenly grew anxious.","He let go of the dog in his arms, stumbled to his feet, and raised his voice, laced with an urgent panic, \"Explosives! Someone is going to blow up the mine! The mine is going to blow up, it really is!\"","Fearing he might have an episode from the excitement, Staff Officer Lin quickly shouted to appease him, \"We know, we know! Lao Wu, hurry back and rest. We'll go over to the mine and take a look right now!\"","Lao Wu stood rooted to the spot, wearing a dusty, old military greatcoat. His hair was messy, his beard was scruffy, and his whole person looked unkempt.","He tucked his hands into his sleeves, his body shivering slightly, as he kept muttering, \"Explosives... there are explosives... the mine is going to be blown up...\"","After mumbling a few more times, he slowly crouched back down and hugged the large dog beside him again. As he gently stroked it, he repeated in a low voice to the dog, \"Explosives... there are explosives...\"","After Qin Yuanzheng took his subordinates on a patrol around the mining area, he went to process some documents and held a meeting with the engineers at the site. Following that, he drove himself to the headquarters.","After a busy day, it was getting dark, so Qin Yuanzheng prepared to go to the food factory to pick up Qiao Lanshu.","...","Qiao Lanshu had reported the case in the morning, but by the time she got off work in the afternoon, she hadn't seen any comrades from the Public Security Bureau come looking for her.","She wondered to herself, could it be that Chu Liangjun didn't plan to take revenge on her, and actually hadn't gone to steal the explosives?","However, speak of the devil.","Before Qin Yuanzheng arrived, the comrades from the Public Security Bureau drove over.","Two young public security officers stepped out of the car with serious expressions. Upon seeing Qiao Lanshu standing at the entrance of the food factory, they immediately walked over.","The appearance of the public security officers immediately attracted the attention of many people.","Wang Xue saw it too and thought Qiao Lanshu had committed some crime. She hurried to Qiao Lanshu's side and whispered, \"Xiao Qiao, what happened to you? Do you need me to deliver a message to your family?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. \"No need...\"","Seeing the public security officers approaching, Qiao Lanshu had a bad premonition.","Sure enough, one of the unfamiliar young officers said to Qiao Lanshu with a solemn expression, \"Comrade Qiao Lanshu, we are here to pick you up from work. Please come with us.\"","The officer's meaning was very clear—the case Qiao Lanshu had reported had become a reality."]},{"number":112,"title":"Chapter 112: Catching People","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu didn't even have time to say goodbye to Wang Xue before she hurriedly followed the police officers into the car. It was only when she was inside that she dared to ask, \"Comrade, did Chu Liangjun really steal the explosives?\"","The police officer sitting in the passenger seat, while another officer drove, said with a serious expression, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, we cannot be certain yet if it was Chu Liangjun who stole the explosives; however, what we can confirm is that two packs of explosives are indeed missing from the construction site.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Good heavens, two packs were actually missing!","Originally, Comrade Xiao Jiang from the police bureau thought Qiao Lanshu was just frightened, and that the other party was certainly just trying to scare her rather than actually planning to blow her up.","The explosives at the construction site were strictly accounted for, and using them required multiple layers of approval.","Ordinary workers stayed far away from the explosives; hardly anyone dared to approach them casually.","Moreover, anyone who secretly stole and hid explosives would face the firing squad.","Who would be so tired of living as to steal explosives?","The police officers also thought that since a comrade from the public had reported the case, they had to go to the construction site to check it out.","Just a casual walk-through would suffice; they figured nothing would actually happen.","Therefore, Comrade Xiao Jiang spoke to the engineering corps managing the construction site as a matter of routine.","He asked the military personnel to give him an accurate answer as to whether the quantity of explosives was correct.","Everyone felt there wouldn't be any problems. The police officers at the site even chatted with the engineers about the food and the weather.","The atmosphere was relaxed.","As a result, in less than half an hour, it was discovered that two packs of explosives were missing from the site!","In an instant, the entire construction site exploded into an uproar, and the military unit was alarmed.","The people from the police bureau were now taking Qiao Lanshu to the mining area's military unit. Firstly, they needed her to provide testimony to the military personnel.","Secondly, the police comrades were worried that the man might actually come to blow up Qiao Lanshu. With only three of them, they wouldn't be able to protect a military officer's family member.","It was safer to send Qiao Lanshu to the military base.","The police bureau couldn't bear this responsibility.","So, just as Qin Yuanzheng was getting ready to get off work and pick up his wife to go home, he saw the police car pull up to the entrance of the mining area, delivering his wife to him.","The entrance to the mining area was already bustling with people. Off-duty workers, sentries changing shifts, and trucks coming and going were all drawn to the conspicuous police car at this moment.","The wheels crunched over the gravel road and stopped. The door opened, and Qiao Lanshu stepped out of the car, her face still showing a bit of nervousness.","Qin Yuanzheng's originally relaxed brows furrowed slightly.","Why was his wife arriving at the mining area in a police car?","Immediately after, Company Commander Xiao Yang rushed over with several soldiers, their breathing a bit ragged from running. As soon as he saw Qin Yuanzheng, he shouted anxiously, \"Commander, Commander! Something happened!\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","He had originally started the car, planning to pick up his wife and go home. Without a word, he backed the car up and turned off the engine.","Pushing the car door open and stepping out, the evening breeze blew past, carrying the unique dusty scent of the mining area. He looked at his panicked subordinates, his face darkening a few degrees, and asked in a deep voice, \"What happened now?\"","Xiao Yang subconsciously glanced to the side and lowered his voice, unable to suppress his urgency, \"Commander, the explosives! Two packs of explosives are missing from the mountains!\"","Their mining area was in the suburbs, and one of the roads being built was in the mountains.","That area was the road construction site under the charge of the engineering corps. To cut through mountains and dig tunnels, explosives were an indispensable resource, and they were guarded extremely strictly on normal days.","What everyone referred to as \"the mountains\" meant that construction road in the mountains.","Qin Yuanzheng's face instantly darkened. It was a coldness that seeped from his bones, dropping the air pressure around him by several degrees.","Qiao Lanshu, standing beside him, was startled by his suddenly terrifying expression.","She had been with him for so long and had never seen Qin Yuanzheng look this furious.","Usually, no matter how busy or tired he was, he always restrained his sharp edges in front of her. But at this moment, the commanding presence and hostility of a soldier bore down without any concealment.","Qiao Lanshu had gone to report to the police immediately after confirming that Chu Liangjun had gone to the construction site.","Qiao Lanshu had only gone to report the case after confirming that Chu Liangjun had gone to the construction site to move bricks, but she hadn't had time to tell Qin Yuanzheng yet.","She also hadn't expected Chu Liangjun to succeed so quickly. Was no one guarding the explosives at the site?","Fortunately, she had gathered information and reported it in time; otherwise, the consequences would have been unimaginable.","Xiao Yang was so angry his face flushed red, and he couldn't help but curse in a low voice, \"Those guys are really useless! Losing something like explosives, they need their hides tanned!\"","Qin Yuanzheng immediately spoke in a deep voice, his tone carrying an unquestionable command: \"Notify all surrounding military districts and militia regiments about the stolen explosives immediately. Have all mining areas, construction sites, and residential areas conduct a comprehensive search! Inform the mining corps that this is an emergency mission. Start a full search overnight. If the explosives aren't found, no one is sleeping tonight!\"","\"Yes, sir!\"","Xiao Yang responded and turned around, hurriedly taking his men to assign the tasks.","For a moment, the entire mining area was enveloped in a tense atmosphere. Everyone sprang into action. Lights flicked on one after another, and the sounds of whistles, footsteps, and passing orders rose and fell as the overnight search began.","Fortunately, Qiao Lanshu had provided Chu Liangjun's information in advance. With a clear target, the search was much easier than running around blindly like headless flies.","With two packs of explosives missing from the site, the administrator in charge of guarding them was scared out of his wits.","They had no idea when the explosives were stolen, let alone who stole them. Their hearts were in their throats, filled with panic.","If it was just an ordinary worker acting foolishly and stealing them for a personal grudge, the problem wouldn't be the most severe.","But what if enemy spies had infiltrated the site and stolen the explosives for sabotage or a terrorist attack? Then the sky would truly fall.","If such consequences really occurred, all these administrators would face a military tribunal. Labor reform would be a light punishment; the greatest fear was facing the firing squad directly.","In an instant, everyone was searching like crazy for the explosives and hunting down Chu Liangjun.","Qin Yuanzheng suppressed his inner emotions and led Qiao Lanshu all the way to his office.","Along the way, neither of them spoke.","Once inside the office, he closed the door behind him, shutting out the noise from outside.","He pointed to a chair, his voice low: \"Sit down.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu obediently sat down, looking up to meet his deep, serious gaze.","Qin Yuanzheng stood before her, looking down at her, his tone not softening in the slightest: \"What is the meaning of today's police report? The other party threatened to blow you up, so why didn't you tell me?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Of course she couldn't say anything about that. After all, that was just a temporary excuse she made up when reporting the case to make the police take it seriously.","Seeing her silence, Qin Yuanzheng's gaze darkened. He leaned forward slightly, staring into her eyes. His voice grew heavier, carrying an intimidating sense of pressure. Qiao Lanshu, you had better tell the truth. I am interrogating you right now.","Qiao Lanshu could feel that Qin Yuanzheng was truly angry this time.","She had never seen him get angry with her before. Even when she was occasionally willful or threw little tantrums, he had always been tolerant and accommodating.","But this time, the anger was real, mixed with worry, lingering fear, and a bit of dissatisfaction at being kept in the dark.","When Qin Yuanzheng got angry, the aura of someone used to being in authority pressed down on her. Qiao Lanshu subconsciously tensed up, her heartbeat losing its rhythm. It was genuinely quite scary.","Actually, with things having reached this point—the explosives were lost, a report had been filed, and everyone knew about it—there was no longer any need to hide it from Qin Yuanzheng.","Previously, Chu Liangjun hadn't committed any major crimes. Even if she had told Qin Yuanzheng, he wouldn't have been able to do much about him besides a verbal warning. Going up against a petty villain like that would only bring unnecessary impact and trouble to Qin Yuanzheng.","But now, everything was different.","Looking at Qin Yuanzheng, Qiao Lanshu told the truth. Actually, he never said he was going to blow me up. That was a lie I made up so I could file a report and get the police comrades to investigate the construction site.","Qin Yuanzheng: ???","When Qin Yuanzheng heard this, he looked surprised.","Because in his eyes, his little wife was obedient, innocent, and kind.","He never could have imagined that she would be bold enough to make up a lie to file a police report.","Before Qin Yuanzheng could speak, he saw Qiao Lanshu looking at him with teary eyes. She asked softly, Brother Zheng, do you think I am very bad? Will you despise me because of this?","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Wait, he hadn't even said anything yet.","Why was Qiao Lanshu crying already?","He habitually sat down, pulled her into his arms, and patted her back. Be good, don't cry.","He paused for two seconds before releasing her, but his tone was no longer as stern as before.","Qin Yuanzheng said, So, you were certain that Chu Liangjun was going to steal explosives, but since you had no proof, you made up a lie so the police would investigate the site. Is that right?","Qiao Lanshu nodded. Right.","Qin Yuanzheng knew it. His wife was deeply kind; she definitely wouldn't lie for no reason.","She must have felt very conflicted when lying to the police comrades.","Qin Yuanzheng's heart softened. He decided he had been too fierce just now and had probably scared his little wife.","His voice turned gentle again as he looked at her and asked, How did you know he would steal explosives?","Qiao Lanshu wiped the corners of her eyes. She sneaked a glance at Qin Yuanzheng, and seeing that he was no longer as angry, she secretly breathed a sigh of relief.","It seemed her crying just now had been timed perfectly.","There was no one else in the office, just the two of them, so Qiao Lanshu answered directly, I dreamt about it.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng's expression, which had just softened, slowly grew serious again.","Qiao Lanshu shrank her neck back and explained, I mentioned before that I dreamt of a man with a scar on his face. On my first night in Longcheng, he kidnapped me to a village and locked me in a cave dwelling... for two years.","Qin Yuanzheng knew this; Qiao Lanshu had told him a long time ago.","Qiao Lanshu continued, In my dream, I saw that this person was Chu Liangjun. The Chu Liangjun in my dream not only locked me up, but he also stole explosives from the construction site and buried them on the way home of his cousin's wife, Chu Haiming's wife, injuring her in the blast.","I thought at the time, this dream is so real, and this man actually exists. He even followed me and tried to give me things. So, would he really go steal explosives too? I felt uneasy, afraid of what would happen if he really stole explosives and hurt someone again. So I thought about filing a report to have the police check it out. If he hadn't stolen anything, I could at least have peace of mind.","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng instantly stopped being angry with Qiao Lanshu.","Because he recalled the time right after they got married, when Qiao Lanshu had nightmares all day and would wake up startled in the middle of the night.","Who could have thought that a mere dream could be so incredibly real?","The wicked man from her dream was actually someone she encountered in real life.","Thinking about it, it was indeed quite terrifying.","Qin Yuanzheng held Qiao Lanshu and said in a low voice, When we get back, you need to tell me all about your dream.","Right now, he had to go catch Chu Liangjun first.","Qiao Lanshu nodded. Okay.","Qin Yuanzheng personally inspected the area around the office, confirming that the surroundings were safe and free of explosives.","Then, he arranged for guards to watch over the office and protect Qiao Lanshu.","As for himself, he took his men and went to catch the culprit in person.","...","Chu Liangjun had only found his opportunity late in the afternoon when work was ending. Taking advantage of everyone going to eat dinner, with only one person left guarding the warehouse, he made his move.","The structures on the construction site were haphazardly built from sheet metal, and some doors didn't even have locks.","Although the management of the explosives was very strict, it wasn't entirely impossible to find a loophole.","The explosives came in small packages. He didn't know much about them, only noticing that one package was about the size of two bricks, thinking its power might not be enough to kill someone.","So, he stole two packages.","Carrying the two packs of explosives, he hurriedly ran out of the construction site, not even bothering to eat dinner.","The explosives were detonated with a fuse. He figured the things were pretty much like firecrackers, so he wasn't afraid.","He stuffed the explosives inside his padded cotton jacket and hastily left the site.","He wanted to return to the city, assuming that the military management in the mining area was too strict for him to find a chance to strike.","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu lived in the military residential compound, but he couldn't go blow up the compound, right? He was afraid of accidentally hurting Qiao Lanshu.","He still wanted to kidnap Qiao Lanshu and take her home; he had no intention of inadvertently injuring her.","After thinking it over, he decided to lie in wait on the road leading back to the city from the mining area.","Before that, he needed to find a place to bury the explosives. When Qin Yuanzheng drove past, he would ignite the fuse!","However, to his surprise, not long after he ran out of the construction site and before he even entered the city, he saw a police car!","With the explosives tucked in his jacket, Chu Liangjun was scared half to death.","At this hour, heading back to the city was troublesome. The weather was too cold, and there were no buses.","He originally lived in the temporary workers' dormitory at the construction site, but now, he didn't dare go back.","Chu Liangjun quietly approached the vicinity of the mining area, only to see the soldiers of the mining district's military unit beginning to assemble.","He immediately knew that his theft of the explosives had been exposed.","In the pitch-black winter night, Chu Liangjun's hands and feet went numb from the cold.","He squatted on a mountain path near the mining area. At this point, he could neither advance nor retreat.","Chu Liangjun fell silent for a long time before gritting his teeth and muttering, Damn it, if you won't leave me a way out, I won't let you have it easy either!","He was going to blow up the mining area right now!","..."]},{"number":113,"title":"Chapter 113: Chu Liangjun is dead.","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu walked to the door of the office and looked outside, her heart leaping into her throat.","Inside and outside the entire corps stationed area, soldiers were hurrying about everywhere. Squad after squad marched past her in dense formations. It was obvious that these weren't just local troops; they must be reinforcements temporarily transferred from other military regions.","It was likely that the city's militia had also been fully mobilized, stepping up patrols in every street and alley, searching the whole city for the stolen explosives.","On the tall watchtower in the center of the mining area, several high-powered searchlights had already been turned on. Brilliant beams of light pierced the night sky, sweeping back and forth, illuminating the entire construction site as bright as day.","The site's loudspeakers were also broadcasting a notice on a loop, over and over again. The voice was loud and stern, clearly calling out Chu Liangjun's name, issuing a public wanted poster to all workers and nearby villagers, urging everyone to report immediately if they found any trace of him.","Qin Yuanzheng had just taken some men out for an inspection and returned not long after.","As soon as he entered the door and saw Qiao Lanshu waiting quietly in the office, his expression remained steady, and his tone softened. \"Are you hungry? I'll take you to the cafeteria for something to eat.\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","At a time like this, how could Qin Yuanzheng still look completely unhurried?","She quickly stood up, walked briskly over to him, and reached out to gently hug his arm. She couldn't hide the worry in her voice. \"Brother Zheng, I'm not hungry right now... I'm just anxious. If that batch of explosives isn't recovered, what if he really uses them to hurt people?\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked down at her tense little face and chuckled softly, his tone reassuring:","\"Don't worry. Based on the timeline, Chu Liangjun left the construction site around six o'clock, and it's seven in the evening now. Only a little over half an hour has passed; he simply wouldn't have had time to rush back to the city. The entrances and exits of the city have been blocked by the militia, and the only shuttle bus is under control. He can't escape even if he had wings. Right now, he must still be around the construction site and the mining area.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had already made his judgment.","Nine times out of ten, Chu Liangjun was hiding in a nearby villager's home, or he was hiding in the temporary workers' dormitories around the construction site.","These were the only two places he could stay, but right now, both locations had already been taken over by the military. As long as he dared to show up, he would be caught.","Furthermore, if he couldn't be found in either of these places, then he must have slipped into the nearby mountains.","But the searchlights on the watchtower were on all night. As long as he dared to take half a step closer to the mining area, he would be spotted immediately.","Without leaving room for argument, Qin Yuanzheng gently took her hand. \"Let's go. I'll take you to the military cafeteria for some food first.\"","He knew what he was doing, so naturally, he wasn't panicking.","It didn't matter if he skipped a meal, but he couldn't let his little wife suffer.","He led Qiao Lanshu all the way to the military cafeteria.","Qin Yuanzheng was accompanied by an orderly, who usually ran errands for the regiment commander and was very sharp.","As soon as he saw the regiment commander's family member arrive, he immediately ran ahead into the kitchen and whispered a few words to the cooking squad.","Most of the soldiers in the unit had eaten dinner at six o'clock. At this time, the cooking squad had already cleaned up and was preparing to get off work and rest.","But the regiment commander's wife was eating at the cafeteria for the first time—this was a major event. Several people immediately fired up the stoves again, lit the fires, poured the oil, and got busy.","The grain supply in the army wasn't exactly abundant, so it couldn't be called a lavish feast, but there were enough steamed white buns and mixed-grain buns to go around.","The cooking squad worked quickly, and it wasn't long before they served the food:","A plate of steaming hot white steamed buns, a dish of refreshing stir-fried pickled vegetables, and a large bowl of fragrant dough drop soup.","They had specially cracked an egg into the dough drop soup, stirred in white flour, and added a few drops of sesame oil before taking it out of the pot. As soon as it was served, the savory aroma filled the air.","Qiao Lanshu was truly hungry by now. She picked up a soft white bun and took a few gentle bites.","Qin Yuanzheng took a bowl, ladled out some dough drop soup for her, and set it aside to cool, afraid it might burn her, telling her to drink it slowly with her bun.","After keeping Qiao Lanshu company through the meal, there was still no news from outside.","Qin Yuanzheng instructed the orderly to take Qiao Lanshu back to the office to rest, while he turned and went out to continue commanding the search.","The orderly escorted Qiao Lanshu back to the office, had her sit in Qin Yuanzheng's seat, brewed her some tea, and brought her some biscuits.","The tea and biscuits were scrounged up by the orderly from the other officers' offices.","Qin Yuanzheng's 21st Regiment was an independent regiment, with no division commander supervising it, managed directly by headquarters.","Therefore, Qin Yuanzheng was the top boss in the regiment, and it was a rare occasion for his family to visit.","The orderly didn't care about anything else; his only concern was serving Qiao Lanshu well.","He had rummaged through the drawers of the deputy regiment commanders, the political commissar, and the chief of staff, making tea for Qiao Lanshu, bringing biscuits, and even fetching a bag of walnuts.","Qiao Lanshu said, a bit embarrassed, \"You don't need to bring me anything else. I just ate a full meal and can't eat this much.\"","The orderly brought over a nutcracker, wanting to crack the walnuts for her.","He smiled, his expression endearingly naive, and said, \"Ma'am, please don't be polite. Our regiment commander finally has a family, and we are all thrilled. It's just a pity that we don't have many good things here. Please don't take offense, Ma'am.\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","How could Qiao Lanshu possibly take offense?","She felt that the people in the military were simply too enthusiastic.","Sitting at Qin Yuanzheng's desk, Qiao Lanshu noticed an unlocked drawer. She casually pulled it open and glanced inside.","Seeing a calendar card inside, she took it out and looked at it. Several dates were circled in red pen.","Looking closer, Qiao Lanshu immediately understood.","Those circled dates were the day they met, the day they married, and her birthday.","Looking at these, Qiao Lanshu's heart softened. Her Brother Zheng was truly wonderful; he had always kept her in his heart.","Smiling, Qiao Lanshu placed the calendar card back into the drawer and didn't touch any more of Qin Yuanzheng's belongings.","After all, this was an office, not a dormitory. These were his work items and were confidential. Even though she was a family member, she shouldn't rummage around casually.","...","After nearly an hour of carpet-searching, news was finally rushed back.","Chu Liangjun was hiding in the temporary workers' dormitories near the construction site.","Seeing that the roads back to the city were completely blocked and hearing his wanted notice echoing everywhere, Chu Liangjun finally realized that the consequences of stealing explosives were not something an ordinary person like him could handle.","But at this point, it was too late for regrets.","He had originally hardened his heart, wanting to take a desperate risk and bomb the mining area, but he was dumbfounded as soon as he got close:","Four searchlights were turned on simultaneously, illuminating the inside and outside of the mining area as brightly as day. Even the surrounding mountain forests were clearly visible. The lights swept back and forth; if he even dared to show his head, he would be subdued by the soldiers on the spot before he could even make a move.","Driven into a corner, Chu Liangjun had no choice but to turn around and scurry toward the construction site. However, the site was equally swarming with public security officers and soldiers. Not daring to linger, he frantically ducked into the temporary workers' dormitory area, just wanting to find a place to hide first.","At this moment, the dormitory area was dead silent. Everyone had been temporarily evacuated to the air-raid shelter. Doors and windows were tightly shut, without the slightest sound coming from within.","At a critical time like this, everyone knew that stealing explosives was a capital offense, and they were terrified of being implicated.","Chu Liangjun used to live here, squeezed into a mud-brick room with over a dozen other people, sleeping on a large communal bed.","He rushed to the door of his dormitory. Seeing it tightly shut, he raised his hand and pounded heavily on it.","The noise was particularly piercing in the quiet night.","From the guardhouse next to the dormitory, a guard immediately rushed out holding a flashlight. The beam of light shone on him as the guard shouted sternly, \"Who is it? Who's knocking? What time do you think it is, running around like this? Come here right now!\"","Chu Liangjun suddenly turned around, his eyes terrifyingly sinister, staring fixedly at the guard.","The guard took a few steps forward with the flashlight. The beam fell right on his face. The moment he saw his features clearly, the guard's blood ran cold.","The broadcast had been playing the wanted poster over and over again. He had heard the name so many times his ears were almost calloused—it was Chu Liangjun, the man who stole the explosives!","The guard's legs gave way in sheer terror, barely able to stand. He screamed like a madman, \"Found him! Found him! Chu Liangjun is here!\"","As he shouted, he scrambled away, desperately calling for help toward the patrolling soldiers, \"Help! Come quick! Chu Liangjun is in the dormitory area! He's right here!\"","Chu Liangjun completely panicked in an instant and roared hysterically, \"Don't come any closer! Or I'll light the explosives! We'll all die together!\"","He indeed had two packs of construction explosives tucked in his arms, but this kind of explosive, used for blasting mountains, required an open flame to ignite the fuse. He didn't have any matches or a lighter on him.","He couldn't light them at all.","Pushed to a dead end and with his mind completely blank, he could only use these words as a blind threat.","Unfortunately for him, there was no one in the dormitory area at this moment, so his threats were useless.","The army had long since evacuated the people from the dormitory area; they couldn't just leave them there as hostages for him.","Chu Liangjun fiercely pulled out the two packs of explosives from his arms, holding one in each hand. With bloodshot eyes, he roared at the approaching soldiers, \"Let me go! Let me leave here right now! Otherwise, I'll blow this up and we'll all die together!\"","On the other side, two headlights pierced the night. Qin Yuanzheng was driving the car himself, rushing over with the Minister of Armed Forces.","Just as the car reached halfway up the mountain, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly slammed on the brakes, pushed the door open, and got out.","The Minister of Armed Forces followed closely behind him and asked in confusion, \"Regiment Commander Qin, aren't we going straight there?\"","Qin Yuanzheng said calmly, \"There's no need.\"","Saying this, Qin Yuanzheng had already stepped onto a large protruding rock by the road. He raised his binoculars, looked toward the dormitory area, and fixed his gaze on Chu Liangjun.","He lowered the binoculars, pointed at the rifle in the Minister's hands, and asked in a low voice, \"Is the range of your rifle long enough?\"","The Minister of Armed Forces squinted to estimate the distance and replied in a hushed tone, \"The range is enough... it's just a bit far.\"","Even as he spoke, he half-crouched, mounted the rifle, and aligned the crosshairs with the figure at the bottom of the hill.","Chu Liangjun was still standing in the open space a few meters away from the dormitory, holding the explosives up with both hands and shouting wildly. He was almost completely unhinged.","But the soldiers present knew very well that this kind of civilian explosive used on construction sites only feared an open flame. It wasn't like the ones on the battlefield that would explode just by pulling a pin.","Without fire, they simply wouldn't explode.","Moreover, if Chu Liangjun had a fire source, he would have brought it out long ago instead of just relying on verbal threats.","Qin Yuanzheng continued to lock onto the target with his binoculars. The Minister of Armed Forces already had his finger on the trigger, waiting only for the command.","Just at this critical moment, from the shadows behind Chu Liangjun, an agile figure lunged out like a cheetah!","Chu Liangjun didn't have the slightest time to react before he was fiercely tackled to the ground.","Frightened out of his wits, he struggled desperately to push the person off him, scrambled up, and ran madly toward the nearby mountains without looking back.","The person who tackled him was Company Commander Xiao Yang. The dormitory area was under his temporary control, and he had been lying in ambush in the dark for a long time.","His target was the explosives, so he didn't chase after the man at all. He bent down and firmly grabbed the two packs of explosives in his hands.","Just as he stood up, a crisp gunshot suddenly rang out in the night sky: \"Bang!\"","In the silent night, this sound made people's eardrums tremble, and even the earth seemed to shudder slightly.","Everyone's hearts leaped into their throats, feeling somewhat terrified.","Xiao Yang patted the dirt off his body, tightened his grip on the explosives, and walked toward the direction where Chu Liangjun had fled.","The soldiers in the distance also quickly closed in. Just as the group rushed to the foot of the mountain, they saw Chu Liangjun already lying on the ground, a pool of dark red seeping out beneath him.","Xiao Yang stepped forward, quickly checked him over, stood up straight, and shouted in a deep voice, \"Danger cleared! Notify everyone to fall in and withdraw!\"","...","After the crisis was resolved, it was time for the various wrap-up tasks.","The mining area and the construction site returned to normal.","However, all the explosives at the construction site were centrally confiscated and returned to the army for management.","Previously, to facilitate the work and improve efficiency, and because there were engineering soldiers stationed at the site, some of the approved explosives had been stored in the site's warehouse for management.","That was no longer possible now.","With such a serious incident occurring today, several of the people in charge at the construction site were going to be arrested.","Due to their dereliction of duty, they would never be able to return to work at the site again.","The employment methods at the construction site also changed. Instead of gathering large numbers of temporary workers as before, recruitment would now be handled jointly by the city's Labor Bureau and Personnel Department. After investigating their personnel files and confirming there were no issues, they would be centrally assigned to the site.","This was to prevent people with criminal records from entering the construction site for work.","Although it wasn't particularly important work, road construction was a key provincial project, and they absolutely could not afford to have a second Chu Liangjun.","Qin Yuanzheng and the Minister of Armed Forces drove back to the mining area office.","Seeing that the crisis was resolved, the Minister of Armed Forces shouldered his rifle and withdrew with his soldiers.","After strengthening the patrol forces at the mining area and construction site, Qin Yuanzheng returned to the office to find Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu was sitting in the room drinking tea when she heard Qin Yuanzheng's voice coming from outside the door. He was asking the orderly at the door, \"Where is my wife?\"","The orderly immediately replied, \"Commander, Ma'am is in the office!\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and strode into the office.","It was already past eight o'clock in the evening. On a winter night in the north, this was no longer early.","Outside, it was not only pitch black, but the winter wind was howling, and it was freezing cold.","Qin Yuanzheng actually had many follow-up matters to deal with.","Because the explosives at the construction site had been stolen and a person had died, he had to write a report personally and then head to headquarters overnight to report on the situation.","But before that, he had to take his little wife home first."]},{"number":114,"title":"Chapter 114: Xiao Qiao is pregnant.","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu paced back and forth nervously in the office. Suddenly, seeing the office door being pushed open, she quickly turned around to look.","As expected, it was Qin Yuanzheng returning. She hurried forward to meet him: \"Brother Zheng!\"","Even though it was far away, she had heard that gunshot just now from inside the office.","She looked at Qin Yuanzheng somewhat nervously, her hands unconsciously rubbing the hem of her clothes. With complex emotions in her heart, she asked in a low voice, \"Brother Zheng, how did it go? Did you catch him?\"","Qin Yuanzheng walked in briskly, still carrying the biting, snowy breath of the outdoors. A thin layer of snow rested on the shoulders of his military overcoat. The frost clinging to the tips of his hair met the warm air of the room and condensed into tiny water droplets.","He had walked in a hurry, and a gust of piercing cold wind swirled in behind him when he pushed the door open. Afraid the cold wind would blow on Qiao Lanshu, he quickly stepped in front to shield her.","He reached out and grasped Qiao Lanshu's hands. The warmth of his palms instantly enveloped her fingertips. He nodded and said, \"It's been handled, everything went smoothly... It's getting late. I'll take you home to rest first. Once you're settled, I have to come back to write a report and head to headquarters overnight to report the situation.\"","He felt that Qiao Lanshu's hands were very cold.","The office clearly had a coal stove burning and was comfortably warm, with even the air carrying a cozy heat, yet Qiao Lanshu's hands were icy cold, devoid of any warmth.","Her fingertips even had a faint, pale bluish tint.","He quickly tightened his grip, using his large, thick hands to completely envelop her small ones. His thumb pads gently rubbed the back of her hands and fingertips, slowly transferring his warmth to her. His movements were gentle, and even his eyes were tinged with a bit of heartache.","Qin Yuanzheng asked, \"Why are you so cold?\"","Qin Yuanzheng lowered his eyes to look at her, his gaze sweeping over her floral padded jacket. His tone was full of concern, \"Did you not wear enough clothes? The wind and snow are heavy outside, don't catch a cold.\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at the undisguised worry in his eyes and forced a smile, the curve of her lips a bit stiff. She shook her head gently, her voice soft: \"No, I'm not cold.\"","Pausing for a moment, she looked up at Qin Yuanzheng, her eyes carrying a bit of hesitation and a trace of unconcealable urgency, \"Brother Zheng, that Chu Liangjun who stole the explosives, is he...\"","Qin Yuanzheng lowered his eyes to gaze at her face, taking in all of her expressions.","Qiao Lanshu's face was a bit pale, yet it revealed a strange complexity.","There was the relief of the dust settling, the joy of a hidden danger being eliminated, and mixed within was an indescribable sense of liberation, like a heavy stone that had weighed on her heart for a long time finally hitting the ground, yet carrying a bit of disbelief.","She lowered her head slightly, her gaze falling on their intertwined hands. Her long eyelashes fluttered gently, as if trying to hide something. Her voice was kept extremely low, carrying a barely perceptible tension: \"Is he... dead?\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't hide it. He nodded, then reached out and pulled her tightly into his arms. His large hand gently landed on her back, patting softly, thinking she had been frightened by the gunshot and the thrilling scene just now. His tone was full of comfort:","\"Yes, he got what he deserved. From the moment he dared to steal military explosives, he had no way out. It's a capital offense, and no one could save him.\"","Qiao Lanshu leaned against his chest, her nose filled with his unique scent—a mix of wind, snow, and the coal mine. Her long-tense shoulders finally relaxed slowly, and she let out a deep sigh of relief in her heart.","Of course she knew that stealing military explosives was a capital offense.","She had been crystal clear about this from the moment she made up her mind to guide Chu Liangjun down this path.","From the very beginning, she only had one thought: to let Chu Liangjun die.","Although she had originally intended for Chu Liangjun to steal the explosives to take revenge on her, and it ended up being revenge on Qin Yuanzheng instead, the outcome was good regardless.","Chu Liangjun was dead, and he hadn't caused any casualties to others.","The explosives hadn't detonated, and no damage was done to the construction site or the troops.","Everything went smoothly.","Qiao Lanshu breathed a sigh of relief in her heart.","It had been several months since her rebirth, and only at this very moment did she feel a sense of relaxation in both body and mind.","In her previous life, Chu Liangjun had imprisoned her with chains. In this life, although she hadn't been tied up,","her heart had still been trapped in those endless mountains.","Now, she had finally truly walked out of those mountains.","Qin Yuanzheng gently patted her back and said in a low voice, \"Let's go, I'll take you home.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and followed Qin Yuanzheng out of the office.","The wind was strong outside. Qin Yuanzheng happened to be wearing a cloak, so he held Qiao Lanshu in his arms and wrapped the cloak around her.","As the two came out of the office, Qiao Lanshu suddenly stopped in her tracks and looked at Qin Yuanzheng with a blushing face.","Qin Yuanzheng looked down at her: \"What's wrong?\"","Qiao Lanshu said with some embarrassment, \"I, I need to use the restroom.\"","That orderly just now had been too diligent, constantly pouring tea for her.","She had been very nervous at the time, constantly thinking about Chu Liangjun's matter, so she kept drinking water.","Then she needed to go, but didn't know where the restroom was.","She was too embarrassed to ask the orderly.","After all, this was a mining unit with soldiers everywhere. As a woman, she felt awkward going to the restroom; what if she bumped into other men?","Qin Yuanzheng looked down at her for a moment, suddenly leaned close to her ear, and whispered, \"Need to pee?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","It was strange. It was clearly a very normal sentence, so why did it sound so indecent coming out of Qin Yuanzheng's mouth?","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but think of when they were on the heated brick bed before, and he had leaned into her ear to ask this same question.","Her face instantly flushed red with embarrassment, and feeling both shy and exasperated, she reached out and pinched his waist.","Qin Yuanzheng quickly dodged, laughing, \"Alright, alright, I won't tease you anymore. Come on, I'll take you to...\"","He didn't get to finish his sentence before Qiao Lanshu glared at him.","Qin Yuanzheng chuckled. As he led her toward the restroom, he teased her, \"We are all rough men in the military camp. This is just how we speak, very crude. Tell me, how did a gentle and refined little girl like you end up marrying a rough guy like me? Hmm? You can't even handle a single sentence. Why didn't you know to be afraid when you married me?\"","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu replied, \"Because I had a dream. In the dream, you married me and treated me incredibly well.\"","The Qin Yuanzheng in her dreams was just like this. He often liked to tease her, enjoying the sight of her blushing in embarrassment.","Although his desire for her was also very strong, it was usually just once a day, not nearly as frequent as it was now.","Perhaps this was also related to his physical condition.","Thinking of this, Qiao Lanshu said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, you shouldn't have any missions right now, do you?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head: \"Not at the moment.\"","Even though he had married his little wife and wanted to guard by her side every moment,","if the country needed him, he would definitely go.","Qiao Lanshu didn't know during which mission he had been injured, so she paid special attention to his assignments.","Qin Yuanzheng brought Qiao Lanshu to the restroom door. He asked in a low voice, \"Do you want me to go in with you?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. \"No, I'll go by myself.\"","Qin Yuanzheng stood guard at the door for her.","After a while, Qiao Lanshu came out of the restroom, suddenly grabbed a nearby tree, and began to retch, feeling nauseous.","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","Qin Yuanzheng hurried over and said, somewhat puzzled, \"Does the restroom smell really bad? It shouldn't.\"","The septic tank was regularly cleaned out for farming, and besides, it was the dead of winter right now, so it shouldn't smell, right?","Qiao Lanshu didn't know what was going on either; she just felt a sudden wave of nausea and a churning stomach.","Her stomach was doing flips. She endured it for a moment, suppressing the nausea.","Fortunately, she didn't throw up her dinner. She leaned against Qin Yuanzheng's chest to recover for a moment before saying, \"I might have just swallowed some cold wind. I'm fine.\"","The wind was too cold; if it accidentally got into the stomach, it could easily cause a gastrointestinal cold.","Qin Yuanzheng quickly adjusted her scarf again, wrapping it around half of her face so that not even her mouth or nose was exposed.","Then, he scooped Qiao Lanshu up into his arms and said, \"Let's go. We need to hurry home.\"","Recently, Qiao Lanshu had been feeling a bit nauseous from time to time, as well as very tired.","But she hadn't thought much of it. After all, Qin Yuanzheng tossed her about in bed every day, countless times a day.","She also had to go to work during the day, so it would be strange if she wasn't tired.","After returning home, Qin Yuanzheng was truly worried about her. He placed her on the sofa, squatted on the floor to look at her, and asked, \"Are you feeling any better? Do you want me to call someone over to keep you company?\"","Qin Yuanzheng still had to go back to report on his work, but he couldn't put his mind at ease leaving Qiao Lanshu alone.","He felt very conflicted.","Qiao Lanshu sat up and comforted Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, I'm fine. Just go to work with peace of mind.\"","Qin Yuanzheng hesitated for a moment but still said, \"I'll ask the wife of Lao Zhao next door to come over and keep you company. Both of them are home today.\"","Without waiting to hear what Qiao Lanshu would say, Qin Yuanzheng stood up and went to knock on the neighbor's door.","While knocking, Qin Yuanzheng called out, \"Lao Zhao, are you there?\"","Zhao Jiannong had also just returned and hurried over to open the door.","As soon as he opened the door and saw Qin Yuanzheng in his military uniform with a serious face, his heart skipped a beat. Thinking something had happened, he quickly asked, \"What's wrong? Did my southern suburbs forestry center get bombed?\"","That shouldn't be the case. The mining area was over twenty kilometers away from the southern suburbs forestry center. There was no way an explosion could reach his forestry center, right?","Qin Yuanzheng briefly told Zhao Jiannong about the situation in the mining area.","Then he said, \"My wife is feeling a little unwell, but I still have to go back and report to the chief. Could your wife come over and keep my wife company? I'll be back in three hours at the latest.\"","It was already nine o'clock at night; it would probably be late into the night by the time he returned.","If he left Qiao Lanshu alone at home, he wouldn't be able to rest easy at all. But having his orderly or other men come to keep her company wouldn't be appropriate either.","There were no female soldiers in his unit. As for the female military doctors and other civilian female staff, he wasn't familiar with them and rarely interacted with them.","The only people he could think of were his good neighbors.","Naturally, Zhao Jiannong wouldn't refuse such a request.","He immediately said, \"Go with peace of mind. For trivial things like this, just give us a holler in the future; no need to ask.\"","Qin Yuanzheng patted Zhao Jiannong on the shoulder and said, \"Thank you.\"","This \"thank you\" gave Zhao Jiannong goosebumps all over.","He was truly speechless.","After getting a wife, Qin Yuanzheng was acting as if he had been possessed by a ghost.","After Qin Yuanzheng left, Huang Erling came over carrying a few balls of yarn. She sat down on the sofa with a smile and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Oh my, your sofa is so much more comfortable. It's soft, cozy, and warm.\"","As she spoke, she placed the yarn on the table, picked up her needles, and started knitting a sweater. She continued, \"The sofa at my house is old and rock hard. My back hurts if I sit on it for too long. In the future, whenever you need someone to keep you company, just call for me. I'd come over just for your sofa alone.\"","Qiao Lanshu sat on the sofa, leaning against the backrest, and said with a smile, \"Sister Ling, I'm really troubling you. Actually, I don't need anyone to keep me company, but Brother Zheng insisted that he was worried.\"","When it came to Qin Yuanzheng, there was truly nothing bad to say.","While knitting a sweater for her daughter, Huang Erling said, \"Your Regiment Commander Qin has always been a very reliable person. Even my Lao Zhao has said that no matter what the mission is, as long as Regiment Commander Qin is there, he will definitely not let his teammates get hurt. For someone so responsible, wouldn't he be even more attentive to his own wife? Xiao Qiao, you really married a good man.\"","Qiao Lanshu also felt that she had married a good man.","She only hoped that Qin Yuanzheng could safely make it through his upcoming mission crisis; only then would she be able to completely relax.","Qiao Lanshu watched Huang Erling knit, the two needles in her hands moving up and down with lightning speed.","Feeling a bit envious, Qiao Lanshu said, \"Sister Ling, you knit so well. Could you teach me? I want to knit a sweater for Brother Zheng too.\"","Huang Erling replied, \"It's very simple. Go buy some yarn from the supply and marketing cooperative another day, and I'll teach you myself. When knitting a sweater, you just need to be careful when finishing off the edges; the rest is very easy. Look here if you don't believe me.\"","Saying that, she slowed down her pace and knitted slowly for Qiao Lanshu to see.","Qiao Lanshu was watching intently. Just as she was about to speak, the feeling of nausea in her stomach suddenly surged up again.","Qiao Lanshu gagged. She quickly covered her mouth with her hand and ran to the restroom.","Looking at her retreating figure, Huang Erling nervously put down the sweater and followed her to the restroom door. She asked anxiously, \"Xiao Qiao, are you okay? Are you really sick? Do you want me to call Lao Zhao over to drive you to the hospital for a check-up?\"","At this hour, there were still doctors on duty at the military hospital, so they could have a doctor look at her.","Qiao Lanshu retched for quite a while and then took a moment to recover before coming out of the restroom.","Qiao Lanshu's face was a bit pale. She shook her head and said, \"Sister Ling, I'm fine. I didn't throw anything up. I probably just swallowed some cold wind outside tonight. I'll be fine after resting for a bit.\"","Huang Erling supported her arm, looking at her rather awful complexion, and asked softly, \"Do you want to drink some hot water or something? Or go rest in bed?\"","Worried that something might happen to Qiao Lanshu, Huang Erling was no longer in the mood to knit. She helped Qiao Lanshu sit down on the sofa and was about to go pour her some water.","Qiao Lanshu leaned against the sofa, wrapping herself in a small blanket, and murmured, \"I'm so tired.\"","She felt like going to sleep.","Huang Erling was speechless.","Looking at Qiao Lanshu, a thought suddenly crossed Huang Erling's mind.","This Xiao Qiao, could it be that she was... pregnant?"]},{"number":115,"title":"Chapter 115: Keep squirming, and you'll get a spanking.","paragraphs":["Huang Erling poured a cup of warm water and came over, sitting beside her. She asked with concern, \"Xiao Qiao, did this illness come on suddenly tonight? Are you sure you didn't eat something bad?\"","Qiao Lanshu replied, \"I had dinner in the military canteen, and Brother Zheng ate with me, so it shouldn't be food poisoning.\"","She then added, \"I was also feeling nauseous a few days ago, but it wasn't too serious back then.\"","As she spoke, Qiao Lanshu suddenly felt a little scared. She said, \"Sister Ling, tell me, could I be sick?\"","She hadn't been with Qin Yuanzheng for very long, and she hadn't yet enjoyed enough of these good days.","She really didn't want to get sick.","In her previous life, Qiao Lanshu had wished to die early.","But in this life, she was far from having lived enough.","Just as Qiao Lanshu was thinking this, she noticed Huang Erling looking at her with a strange expression.","Qiao Lanshu paused, looking at Huang Erling, and asked, \"Sister Ling, what's wrong? Why are you looking at me like that?\"","Huang Erling put down the water cup in her hand. She hesitated for a moment and carefully asked, \"Xiao Qiao, these symptoms of yours, do you think...\"","She hesitated to speak for a long time before lowering her voice, as if afraid others would hear, and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Do you think you might be pregnant?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu froze, staring blankly at Huang Erling. She subconsciously denied it, saying, \"No way, right? Sister Ling, stop teasing me. How could I possibly be pregnant?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was infertile, and she hadn't gotten pregnant in her previous life either.","But then again, her body had been ruined in her previous life, whereas this time, she was perfectly healthy.","Could it be...","Qiao Lanshu had never allowed herself to even consider the possibility of being pregnant.","But now that Huang Erling brought it up, she couldn't help but start wondering.","Qiao Lanshu subconsciously reached out and touched her stomach, asking Huang Erling, \"Could I... could I be pregnant?\"","Huang Erling clicked her tongue and told her, \"Why couldn't you be? Even though Regiment Commander Qin has infertility, he was never married before, and there's no factual proof that he is truly infertile. What if the doctor misdiagnosed him? Or perhaps you just have a highly fertile constitution. In that case, it's entirely possible.\"","Huang Erling analyzed it for Qiao Lanshu, saying, \"Look, normally you might get pregnant after one or two tries. But after being with Regiment Commander Qin, it might take ten, twenty, or even a hundred times to conceive. Looking at it this way, doesn't it just mean it's harder to conceive?\"","Huang Erling added, \"If it were any other woman, with Regiment Commander Qin's condition, they really might not be able to have a child.\"","Huang Erling was truly straightforward when she spoke.","Her words made Qiao Lanshu blush hotly.","She wanted to defend herself, but on second thought, ever since she and Qin Yuanzheng got married, the number of times Qin Yuanzheng went at it every day couldn't be counted on one hand.","If they were talking about a hundred times, it wasn't entirely impossible...","Huang Erling only had a vague guess in her heart and didn't dare to speak with absolute certainty. If it turned out to be a misunderstanding, it would be hard to smooth things over.","But she was someone who had given birth to two children after all. Having experienced the ten months of pregnancy and childbirth twice, she knew everything there was to know about a woman's pregnancy, giving her a bit more confidence than others.","She shifted her stool closer to Qiao Lanshu, nimbly winding the loose yarn on the edge of the kang into a ball, and gently placed the bamboo needles into the sewing basket. Only then did she lower her voice, speaking with a mix of caution and irrepressible excitement: \"I'm just guessing based on experience, so don't get your hopes up too high just yet. No one can say for sure about these things... How about this, I'll have Lao Zhao go get the car right now, and we can go straight to the hospital to get it checked out and put your mind at ease?\"","Although Huang Erling spoke conservatively, her heart was already churning with excitement.","If Qiao Lanshu was really pregnant, once the news got out, the whole of Longcheng would explode.","Not only would the military compound be in an uproar, but even the nearby factories, department stores, and supply and marketing cooperatives—anyone who had heard of Regiment Commander Qin's formidable reputation and knew about the couple's situation—would be shocked to the core.","This would be a monumentally joyous occasion.","As Qiao Lanshu listened, her heart also warmed slightly. An indescribable sense of anticipation quietly emerged, softly wrapping around her heart.","But she forcefully suppressed that spark of joy, not daring to think too much about it, afraid that the greater the hope, the harder the disappointment would be if it fell through.","She gently held Huang Erling back, steadying her voice. \"Sister Ling, there's no rush for right this moment. What if I'm just overthinking it and there's nothing to it? If we rush off to the hospital in such a flurry, wouldn't it be a wasted trip?\"","If people saw them and the word spread from one to ten, and ten to a hundred, until everyone knew, only for it to end in empty joy, how embarrassing would that be?","Qiao Lanshu subconsciously raised her hand and gently covered her flat abdomen. Her fingertips trembled slightly, and she lowered her voice to a whisper, as if afraid to disturb something. \"Let's wait a bit. Tomorrow, I'll go to the hospital to get checked by myself.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, she inexplicably felt a wave of panic.","The feeling was somewhat like the apprehension one feels when nearing home. She had hoped for this for so long, but when she was truly close to the answer, she didn't dare to take a step forward.","Wasn't her biggest regret in her previous life not being able to have a child with Qin Yuanzheng?","But now, with the opportunity seemingly right in front of her, she grew timid.","If she wasn't pregnant, she was afraid she wouldn't be able to bear the feeling of falling from the clouds.","Qiao Lanshu sat on the edge of the kang, her eyes filled with complex emotions. Her fingertips curled slightly, and she didn't say another word for a long time.","Seeing her looking both expectant and anxious, Huang Erling's heart softened. After pondering for a moment, she suddenly leaned in closer and lowered her voice even more, sounding a bit embarrassed. \"Xiao Qiao, let me ask you a private question. It's okay if you don't want to answer.\"","Qiao Lanshu snapped out of her daze and replied softly, \"Sister Ling, go ahead and ask.\"","It was clearly just the two of them in the room, and the doors and windows were shut tight, not letting even a breath of wind through.","Yet Huang Erling still subconsciously glanced around left and right, as if doing something highly secretive. After confirming no one was eavesdropping, she leaned even closer to Qiao Lanshu, almost pressing against her ear, and asked in a low voice, \"Let me ask you, is Regiment Commander Qin's... amount... a lot?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","She absolutely hadn't expected Sister Ling to ask such an intimate question. Her cheeks instantly burned hot, flushing red from her face to the tips of her ears, and even her neck felt warm.","She stammered, her voice as quiet as a mosquito: \"Sister Ling, w-why are you asking this...\"","Huang Erling herself felt a bit embarrassed and scratched her cheek, but she persisted, \"Oh, don't be shy! I'm just trying to help you analyze things properly!\"","Qiao Lanshu kept her head down, her heart racing. She remained silent for a good while before giving a small nod.","A lot. Of course it was a lot.","So much that she could barely handle it.","Qin Yuanzheng always said he wanted to feed her well, plump her up, and pamper her in the palm of his hand.","Her figure hadn't changed much, but she was indeed being fed very full every single day.","Seeing her nod, Huang Erling's eyes immediately lit up, feeling even more confident. However, she still kept her words measured: \"Then the way I see it, there's a sixty percent chance you're pregnant.\"","Qiao Lanshu's heart tightened, and she subconsciously pressed, \"What about the other forty percent?\"","Huang Erling couldn't help but laugh. She cast a light glance at her and teased, \"That forty percent chance is just an upset stomach, a little minor ailment, right?\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","In fact, Huang Erling had long been certain in her heart that Qiao Lanshu was most likely pregnant.","It was just that she didn't dare to speak too absolutely. What if it really was just a gastrointestinal issue? That would leave Xiao Qiao happy for nothing and make things even more awkward when the truth came out.","Huang Erling stopped worrying about knitting her sweater. She sat on the edge of the heated brick bed, took Qiao Lanshu's hand, and began to chatter about her own experiences when she was pregnant.","The symptoms of pregnancy were actually quite easy to distinguish. The most obvious one was fatigue, feeling completely drained of energy, wanting to lie down instead of sit, and sit instead of stand, feeling exhausted after standing for just a little while.","Of course, everyone's constitution was different, and their reactions varied greatly.","Some people were drowsy all day long and incredibly lazy.","Others, on the contrary, were in good spirits and not sleepy at all.","Then there were the nausea, vomiting, and loss of appetite. Morning sickness also varied from person to person. Some threw up until the world spun, while others were completely comfortable from start to finish, not suffering in the least. It was quite miraculous.","Qiao Lanshu had originally harbored a trace of secret joy, but after hearing Huang Erling's analysis, those symptoms seemed to match somewhat, yet also seemed a bit off. Her heart was suddenly in turmoil again, unable to make up her mind.","Huang Erling just stayed with her like this, chatting casually. Before they knew it, she had sat there for over two hours.","It wasn't until a burst of familiar footsteps came from outside the courtyard gate, steady yet carrying a bit of urgency.","It was Qin Yuanzheng, who had finished his debriefing and hurried home, finally returning.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng's footsteps sounded at the door, Huang Erling, holding the bamboo basket with her balls of yarn, almost immediately stood up, instinctively wanting to leave.","She knew clearly in her heart that once this man returned, it would be private time for the young couple. As a sister-in-law, it naturally wouldn't be appropriate for her to overstay.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng pushed the door open, the cold air and a layer of travel dust rushed into the room. At a glance, he saw Huang Erling about to leave, and a look of genuine gratitude immediately appeared on his face.","His voice was steady, carrying a bit of exhaustion, yet still sincere. \"Sister-in-law, thank you so much for this time. If you hadn't been here keeping her company, my heart would have been hanging in suspense while I was working outside.\"","This was the first time Huang Erling had seen Qin Yuanzheng act so polite and solemn, and for a moment, she actually felt a bit awkward.","She quickly waved her hand and replied softly, \"Your Xiao Qiao is fine, she's just feeling very tired and a bit unwell. It's good that you're back. Spend more time with her, I'll head back first.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded without trying to stop her and personally saw Huang Erling to the door.","It wasn't until the door next door gently closed that he turned around, returned to his own house, and latched the door behind him.","He took off his military cap, casually hung it on the hook on the wall, took off his heavy military overcoat, shook off the cold air, and changed into cotton slippers before walking into the inner room.","After rushing all the way, his face carried the weariness of travel, but it couldn't hide the urgency in the depths of his eyes.","Walking over to the sofa, he gently crouched down. Because he had been running around outside and hadn't had time to wash his hands, he forced himself not to step forward and hug Qiao Lanshu. He just tilted his head up slightly, his gaze gentle and worried as it fell on her face. \"Wife, how are you? Is your body still uncomfortable?\"","Qiao Lanshu just looked at him quietly, not knowing how to speak for a moment.","She was afraid that she was just overthinking things. What if she went to the hospital for a checkup and there was no such thing at all? Not only would it make a huge joke of things, but it would also leave Brother Zheng happy for nothing.","After thinking about it, she eventually swallowed her words back down and only spoke softly, her voice weak, \"I'm much better now.\"","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng's tense shoulders instantly relaxed, and he let out a long sigh of relief. \"That's good, you scared me to death. I'll go wash my hands and face first.\"","He stood up and went straight to the washroom.","In the freezing weather, he didn't care, simply using cold water to quickly wipe his hands and face.","Then he took off his inner clothes and used a dry towel to carefully wipe his body.","When he came out again, he was only wearing a pair of shorts. He walked quickly to the sofa, bent down, and gently scooped Qiao Lanshu up into his arms.","He softened his voice, carrying a bit of apology, \"It's very late, sorry to keep you waiting. Let's sleep.\"","Qiao Lanshu's heart was still heavy, and she lacked energy, only nodding silently.","Qin Yuanzheng looked down at her distracted appearance and asked, \"What's wrong? What are you thinking about, looking so preoccupied?\"","Qiao Lanshu was silent for a moment before she raised her eyes, her voice soft. \"Brother Zheng, do you have time tomorrow?\"","Such a big incident had just happened at the mining area, and he had a pile of work to deal with on hand. How could he spare a large block of time?","But as long as Qiao Lanshu asked, no matter how busy he was, he could squeeze out the time.","He asked softly, \"What's wrong? What do you need?\"","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice even more. \"I want to go to the hospital and have a doctor take a look.\"","Actually, even if Qiao Lanshu hadn't brought it up, Qin Yuanzheng had planned to take her to the hospital.","Her sudden nausea, vomiting, and frighteningly pale face that night had really given him quite a scare, and his heart still hadn't completely settled.","He carried Qiao Lanshu slowly to the edge of the heated bed, carefully set her down, reached out to tuck the blanket around her, and said steadily, \"Okay, tomorrow morning after breakfast, I'll take you to the military region hospital for a proper checkup.\"","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu smiled a little.","Whether she was really pregnant or not, it was better to go to the hospital and have a doctor look at it, to hear a professional opinion, rather than blindly guessing on her own.","Seeing her subconsciously gently rubbing her stomach with her hand, Qin Yuanzheng's heart tightened. He immediately reached out his large, rough hand, gently covered her lower abdomen, and slowly rubbed it.","Qin Yuanzheng asked, \"What's wrong? Is your stomach still uncomfortable?\"","As soon as that callused palm pressed against her, Qiao Lanshu trembled slightly, her cheeks instantly turning red. Her body twisted slightly in a somewhat unbearable manner, and her voice was low. \"Brother Zheng, don't touch me like that.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","He originally didn't have the slightest ulterior motive. Qiao Lanshu was still unwell, and he was too busy feeling sorry for her to bear bullying her.","But with her twisting so gently, her soft body pressing against him, that little bit of well-behaved intention was instantly stirred into a mess.","Qin Yuanzheng's Adam's apple rolled slightly. His palm remained gently pressed against her stomach, and his voice deepened a bit, carrying a trace of imperceptible huskiness. \"Don't squirm.\"","If she kept squirming, she was going to get a spanking.","..."]},{"number":116,"title":"Chapter 116: What Prenatal Supplements to Take","paragraphs":["Fortunately, Qiao Lanshu was quite obedient and indeed didn't dare to squirm around anymore.","Just quietly nesting in Qin Yuanzheng's arms, smelling his scent, Qiao Lanshu blushed, feeling a bit of anticipation in her heart.","She said softly, \"Good night, Brother Zheng.\"","Holding his sweet and soft little wife in his arms, Qin Yuanzheng felt incredibly content.","If Qiao Lanshu hadn't been feeling unwell, he definitely would have gone at it a few times today.","Their kang bed was still lined with the waterproof sheepskin fleece. It was a pity that they had only used it once since buying it so long ago.","Qin Yuanzheng's mind was wandering a bit.","Looking down at his little wife, he found that she had actually fallen asleep.","A bit surprised, Qin Yuanzheng reached out to tidy her hair and called out in a low voice, \"Wife? Are you asleep?\"","Qiao Lanshu's breathing was even, and she gave him no response.","Obviously, she was truly asleep.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng thought to himself that his wife must be really tired to have fallen asleep so quickly.","He sighed slightly. This time, he didn't dare to bully her while she was sleeping.","After all, his little wife was feeling unwell, so he couldn't mess around.","After thinking for a moment, he looked at his own hand. Well, it seemed he would have to take care of himself this time...","...","In the room next door, the earthen kang was heated nice and warm. There was still a bit of unswept wood ash on the edge of the bed, and the dim wick of the kerosene lamp flickered slightly.","The room was so quiet that one could hear the howling of the wind blowing through the window cracks outside.","Huang Erling lay on her side on the kang, gently nudging Zhao Jiannong beside her with her elbow. Keeping her voice low and acting a bit sneaky, she said, \"Lao Zhao, if you don't have anything urgent tomorrow, you should go to the hospital with Regiment Commander Qin to see if Xiao Qiao and the others are alright.\"","Zhao Jiannong had just taken off his coat and draped it over the head of the bed. Hearing this, he turned his head to look at her in bewilderment, his brow slightly furrowed. \"I still have a pile of things to do at the forestry farm. Why should I follow him to the hospital?\"","Besides, it was Regiment Commander Qin's family member seeing a doctor. Would it be appropriate for him to tag along?","Zhao Jiannong had been busy from morning to night. Once he got home, all he wanted to do was collapse on the bed, close his eyes, and sleep.","He and Huang Erling were an old married couple. They were long past the age of being overly affectionate. Their days were as plain as water, and he had long lost any interest in romance and intimacy; he just wanted to catch his breath.","Too lazy to say more, Zhao Jiannong shifted further into the bed, rested his head on the pillow, closed his eyes, and planned to go straight to sleep.","Before he could fall into a deep sleep, his arm was gently pushed by Huang Erling again.","He grunted impatiently but still didn't open his eyes.","Huang Erling gave him another hard shove. In the dark, her eyes were wide, and she lowered her voice, showing a bit of impatience. \"Oh, just go when I tell you to! If something really happens, you, a grown man, can lend a hand, can't you?\"","Zhao Jiannong reluctantly opened his eyes. He stayed silent in the dark for a good while before clicking his tongue. With a tone carrying some annoyance at being woken up, he sat up.","He also lowered his voice, sounding a bit puzzled. \"Are you my wife or Regiment Commander Qin's wife? Why are you worrying about him so much? If his wife needs to go to the hospital, he can just take her. What does it have to do with you?\"","Huang Erling was truly left speechless by his thick skull, almost unable to hold back what was on her mind.","She leaned closer to him, lowering her voice even more, almost explaining right against his ear. \"Comrade Xiao Qiao wasn't feeling well today, and didn't I go over to keep her company tonight? Looking at how nauseous and lethargic she was, it's exactly the same as when I was pregnant with our child back then...\"","Hearing this, Zhao Jiannong, who had just been sitting up straight, fell right back down flat.","Huang Erling: \"...\"","Zhao Jiannong covered himself with the quilt, shrank his head into the covers, closed his eyes, and spoke with a somewhat serious tone:","\"I think you should stop overthinking these baseless things. It's not like you don't know about Regiment Commander Qin's situation. You're too bold to spout nonsense about this. Just keep this talk between us, and absolutely do not let Regiment Commander Qin hear it, or who knows how annoyed he'd be with you.\"","Huang Erling had been quite certain in her heart, feeling that nine times out of ten, Qiao Lanshu was pregnant.","But having cold water poured on her like this by Zhao Jiannong, her heart hung in suspense again, and she started to feel uncertain.","She also lay back down properly, shifting closer to Zhao Jiannong until their arms touched. Still not giving up, she asked softly, \"Is Regiment Commander Qin really incapable? Are you sure?\"","Zhao Jiannong nodded, his voice deepening a bit. \"Of course I'm sure. You know about that mission we went on together back then. We were exposed to some radiation. After we came back, everyone was taken to the provincial military hospital for a full-body checkup. Everyone else was fine, but he was diagnosed with oligospermia. No one expected that.\"","Originally, routine physical exams for soldiers like them didn't even require checking that.","But because that mission had radiation hazards, the doctors needed to collect data to see if it would affect the soldiers' fertility, which was why they added a few extra tests.","After a round of checkups, aside from some superficial wounds, everyone else was perfectly healthy.","Only Qin Yuanzheng was diagnosed with infertility.","At that time, Qin Yuanzheng was young and promising, handsome, and had a boundless future.","He had long caught the eye of a commander's daughter, and the higher-ups intended to play matchmaker for them. The marriage was almost on the table.","But because of that one medical report, the marriage quietly fell through.","Zhao Jiannong sighed and cautioned again, \"The provincial military hospital's checkup definitely wasn't wrong. So, whatever you do, don't go spreading this around. Don't mislead Regiment Commander Qin's family member and give her false hope, only to end in embarrassment.\"","Huang Erling: \"...\"","After a good while, she snorted indignantly. \"You said it yourself, it's oligospermia, not azoospermia! As long as there's still some, there's a chance of getting pregnant. Are you stupid?\"","Zhao Jiannong was too lazy to argue with her about such things under the covers.","No man would be happy lying in bed with his wife in the middle of the night discussing another man's private affairs. Just thinking about it felt awkward.","Zhao Jiannong rolled over, turning his back to her, making it clear he didn't want to chat anymore.","With something weighing on her mind, Huang Erling felt as if a cat were scratching at her heart. She tossed and turned, unable to sleep.","If it were any other time, she would have long since grabbed a handful of sunflower seeds, run to the courtyard of the military compound, and gossiped with the aunts and sisters-in-law for half the day, spelling the whole thing out clearly.","But on second thought;","She couldn't.","Regiment Commander Qin's matter was top secret and a man's sore spot. How could she casually gossip about it?","If it really got out, not only would Regiment Commander Qin lose face, but their Lao Zhao would also be implicated.","Oh, this was really...","Hiding such a big secret in her heart, unable to speak of it or chat about it, Huang Erling lay on the bed, feeling that she would be too frustrated to sleep at all tonight.","...","Early the next morning, after finishing breakfast, Qin Yuanzheng prepared to take Qiao Lanshu out.","Before heading out, he was still asking, \"Wife, does your stomach still feel uncomfortable?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded.","In fact, she hadn't eaten much for breakfast; she just had a poor appetite and was still feeling a bit nauseous.","Qin Yuanzheng looked worried. He helped Qiao Lanshu put on her cotton-padded coat, put a hat on her head, and bundled her up in a scarf.","He even helped her put on her shoes himself.","He was practically treating Qiao Lanshu like a child.","Qiao Lanshu had her own thoughts weighing on her mind, and she followed Qin Yuanzheng out of the room, preoccupied.","Qin Yuanzheng said in a low voice, \"I'll carry you down.\"","Qiao Lanshu was a bit embarrassed. \"There's no need, Brother Zheng. I can walk by myself.\"","Qin Yuanzheng insisted on carrying her down. \"Aren't you feeling unwell? Then I'll give you a piggyback ride down.\"","Saying that, he bent down slightly and hoisted Qiao Lanshu onto his back.","They had just gone down two steps when the door to the neighboring room opened.","Zhao Jiannong, wearing a military overcoat, walked out.","Zhao Jiannong immediately saw Qin Yuanzheng carrying Comrade Xiao Qiao on his back.","He smiled and said, \"Oh, Regiment Commander Qin, what's wrong with your wife? Is she seriously ill?\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu's face and ears instantly turned red.","If she had known, she wouldn't have let Qin Yuanzheng carry her.","Now that they were seen by someone, it was too embarrassing.","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"It's nothing, she's just feeling a bit unwell. We're heading to the hospital to get it checked out.\"","Zhao Jiannong followed behind them as they exited the stairwell. Thinking of what Huang Erling had said, he offered, \"Do you need any help? Should I drive you guys over?\"","Qin Yuanzheng declined. \"No need. Go on and do your own things.\"","Zhao Jiannong: \"...\"","Zhao Jiannong's finally ignited gossiping spirit was instantly extinguished.","He adjusted his hat and watched as Qin Yuanzheng carried his wife to the car, and then the two of them chatted affectionately for a while.","Only then did Qin Yuanzheng open the driver's side door and drive away.","Zhao Jiannong sighed and muttered, \"A tribute to youth, a tribute to love!\"","...","Sitting in the car, Qiao Lanshu said with an awkward expression, \"Brother Zheng, from now on when we're outside, you are not allowed to carry me in your arms or on your back anymore. It's too embarrassing if people see.\"","Qin Yuanzheng replied, \"What's the big deal? If they have the ability, they can go carry their own wives. What's there to be embarrassed about?\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't know whether to laugh or cry.","She said, \"Anyway, it's just not appropriate.\"","The newly built dormitory area of their military base was entirely occupied by officers and their families.","Everyone knew each other.","When Qiao Lanshu married and moved here, she became the popular person in the area. Huang Erling had even mentioned that when people had free time, they would discuss her in the courtyard every day.","She had to keep a low profile now and couldn't be hugging and cuddling with Qin Yuanzheng in front of outsiders.","The nearby hospital was the mining district hospital, located not far from their residence. It only took a few minutes by car.","There was snow on the road, so Qin Yuanzheng drove slowly. When they arrived at the hospital, he wanted to carry Qiao Lanshu out of the car again.","He was rejected by Qiao Lanshu.","The two arrived at the hospital and had just gotten out of the car.","Qin Yuanzheng saw that Zhao Jiannong had also driven over and followed them.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Zhao Jiannong got out of the car and said with a smile, \"Regiment Commander Qin, I came over to see if you needed any help.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu's awkward face. He had originally planned to carry her into the hospital.","Now he could only drop the idea.","He said to Zhao Jiannong, \"No need, go ahead and busy yourself with your own things.\"","Zhao Jiannong brazenly followed along. \"I'm not busy, not busy at all.\"","Huang Erling had told him to come take a look. He had verbally refused, but his body was quite honest.","He eagerly trotted over behind Qin Yuanzheng.","The three of them entered the hospital, and Qin Yuanzheng said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Let's go find Doctor Liu, her medical skills are exceptionally good.\"","As soon as they arrived at the hospital, thinking that she would know the result soon.","Qiao Lanshu became extremely nervous. She bit her lower lip, her expression tense, and even her hands were ice cold.","She didn't even hear clearly what Qin Yuanzheng said, merely nodding and following him toward the consultation room.","Doctor Liu was a female doctor in her fifties. She looked amiable and approachable, and spoke very gently.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng lead Qiao Lanshu in, she smiled and said, \"Regiment Commander Qin, is this your family member?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He helped Qiao Lanshu sit down and said to Doctor Liu, \"Doctor Liu, my wife's stomach started feeling uncomfortable last night. She was constantly nauseous and felt like throwing up, but didn't actually vomit anything. She slept quite well last night though, didn't wake up in the middle of the night, and had no symptoms. But she woke up early this morning, ate breakfast, and still said she felt unwell and a bit nauseous.\"","Doctor Liu looked at Qin Yuanzheng with a smile.","This seemed just like a parent bringing a child to see the doctor.","Zhao Jiannong chuckled and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"When I bring my daughter to see the doctor, it's exactly like this.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Doctor Liu looked at Qiao Lanshu's complexion and said gently to her, \"Let me check your pulse first. Stick out your tongue and let me take a look.\"","Qiao Lanshu stuck out her tongue and then extended her arm.","Qin Yuanzheng stared at Qiao Lanshu intently, thinking that his wife looked so adorable even when sticking out her tongue.","He wanted to eat her up.","At this moment, he was still staring at his cute little wife, his mind wandering to all sorts of things, and the two little figures in his head had already gone through eighteen different positions.","Little did he know that Qiao Lanshu was already incredibly nervous.","While taking Qiao Lanshu's pulse, the smile on Doctor Liu's face was gradually replaced by a look of doubt.","She checked this pulse for quite a long time.","In this era, it was already possible to confirm whether a woman was pregnant through a urine test.","But Doctor Liu was still more skilled at taking pulses.","Her pulse-taking was very accurate.","For so many years, she had never doubted her own judgment.","But now, she was somewhat doubtful.","She looked at Qin Yuanzheng, and then at Qiao Lanshu.","Confirming that Qiao Lanshu was indeed Qin Yuanzheng's wife.","So, she was a bit hesitant.","Both Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng started to feel nervous.","Qin Yuanzheng asked, \"Doctor Liu, what's wrong with my wife? It's nothing serious, right?\"","Why did Doctor Liu have this expression?","Qin Yuanzheng was a bit scared.","Doctor Liu withdrew her hand and said cautiously, \"I need to confirm this pulse again. Wait a moment, I'll invite another senior doctor over to help take a look.\"","Actually, they could just do a urine test, but right now, Doctor Liu was also a bit impatient and wanted to know the result immediately.","Although she had already read the pulse.","But having another person check it would make her more certain.","Saying this, Doctor Liu quickly stood up to head outside.","Qin Yuanzheng was startled. Doctor Liu's medical skills were already top-notch, so why did she need to invite a senior doctor?","He hurriedly grabbed Doctor Liu's arm and said in a deep voice, \"Doctor Liu, just tell me directly what the situation is. I can handle it.\"","Doctor Liu: \"...\"","Of course he could handle it, since it wasn't a bad thing after all.","Qin Yuanzheng had a strong grip, and Doctor Liu couldn't break free.","She hesitated for a moment, then said, \"Regiment Commander Qin, you can rest assured. Your wife isn't sick; it's just very likely that she is already pregnant. Because of your special physical constitution, I need to have my teacher come over to take Xiao Qiao's pulse and see what kind of pregnancy-nourishing medicine she should take from now on.\"","Saying this, Dr. Liu added, \"Of course, just to be safe, Comrade Xiao Qiao will need to do a urine test in a little while. For now, you can have her drink some more warm water.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Zhao Jiannong stood there, completely stunned. He muttered, \"Oh my goodness, did my wife actually guess it right?\""]},{"number":117,"title":"Chapter 117: It Has Been Two Months","paragraphs":["After Doctor Liu left, the three people present stood there with complex expressions. For a long while, no one spoke.","Qin Yuanzheng looked even more dazed. He stood there, staring blankly at Qiao Lanshu. His eyes were completely empty, and he looked as if he had lost his mind.","Qiao Lanshu sat up straight and stiff. Sitting there, she remained completely motionless, her expression also revealing her shock.","She and Qin Yuanzheng locked eyes.","Qin Yuanzheng's throat bobbed, but no words came out.","After recovering from his initial shock, Zhao Jiannong said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Lao Qin, do you think your previous medical report might have been a misdiagnosis?\"","Zhao Jiannong looked at Qin Yuanzheng, but Qin Yuanzheng ignored him.","Zhao Jiannong reached out, waved a hand in front of his face, and called out, \"Hey, snap out of it!\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Zhao Jiannong had finally found an opportunity to tease him. He said, \"Regiment Commander Qin, oh Regiment Commander Qin, I really never thought there'd be a day you'd be scared stiff! This is truly a rare sight. It's a pity the commanders aren't here to see it.\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at Zhao Jiannong, then completely ignored him.","He hadn't even heard a word Zhao Jiannong said.","It took him quite a while to recover. He then squatted down in front of Qiao Lanshu, his expression complicated. For a moment, he didn't even know what kind of face to make.","He stared blankly at Qiao Lanshu for a moment before asking, \"Wife, are... are you pregnant?\"","The word \"pregnant\" came out of his mouth with great difficulty.","It sounded so incredibly strange!","For so many years, he had been labeled with the diagnosis of infertility.","The doctor's test results shouldn't have been wrong.","He had already prepared himself for a life without children.","Moreover, after having Qiao Lanshu, he didn't really want children anyway.","After all, with such a sweet and soft wife by his side, who would want kids?","He hadn't even had enough of their married life together yet.","Wait a minute, a child?","It seemed he and Qiao Lanshu were having a child.","Qin Yuanzheng's mind was a complete mess.","Squatting in front of Qiao Lanshu, he held her hands and repeated, \"Wife, are you pregnant?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head nervously. \"I... I don't know either.\"","In truth, both of them were completely bewildered.","Qin Yuanzheng muttered, \"This is so strange, how could you be pregnant?\"","Was it real or fake?","Qiao Lanshu also said, \"Could the doctor have misdiagnosed it? Didn't they say we could do a urine test? Let's wait until the test results come out before we say anything.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded, pretending to be calm. \"Right, maybe the doctor made a mistake. It's not impossible...\"","Standing to the side, Zhao Jiannong: \"...\"","Zhao Jiannong told them, \"Relax, being pregnant is a good thing. Don't be so nervous.\"","Qin Yuanzheng immediately replied, \"I am not nervous.\"","He appeared very composed.","However, Zhao Jiannong deliberately brought over a handkerchief, wiped the sweat from Qin Yuanzheng's forehead, and smiled. \"Yes, yes, yes, you're not nervous. You're not nervous at all.\"","He was sweating profusely from nervousness, yet he still claimed he wasn't nervous.","Looking at his expression, Zhao Jiannong didn't even know how to describe it.","In short, he had never seen Qin Yuanzheng lose his composure like this.","He figured the man was probably panicking to death on the inside.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't say anything else; he just stared blankly at Qiao Lanshu's stomach.","At that moment, Doctor Liu returned, supporting a gray-haired doctor wearing a white coat as they walked in.","This doctor was in his sixties and usually didn't see patients anymore.","When Doctor Liu went to invite him over today, he initially thought they had encountered some rare and difficult medical case.","As a result, upon entering, he saw two soldiers in military overcoats standing there and a young woman sitting in a chair.","All three looked perfectly normal and didn't seem to be critically ill at all.","Doctor Liu smiled and said, \"Teacher, please help check this young lady's pulse.\"","The old doctor sat down, first observed Qiao Lanshu's complexion, and then checked her pulse.","For a moment, the room was so quiet you could hear a pin drop.","Qiao Lanshu could even hear her own heartbeat.","She was also very nervous, but looking at Qin Yuanzheng's face, he seemed even more nervous than she was.","Qin Yuanzheng felt his palms sweating.","The usually awe-inspiring Regiment Commander Qin stood there right now, not even daring to breathe too loudly.","Zhao Jiannong had originally just tagged along to see what was going on.","Now, he wasn't leaving either.","He and Qin Yuanzheng stood on either side of Qiao Lanshu, staring fixedly as the old doctor checked her pulse.","The old doctor gave them a calm, knowing look, then said to Doctor Liu, \"Isn't this the most basic pulse? You couldn't read it?\"","The old doctor released Qiao Lanshu's hand and asked, \"Which of you two is her husband?\"","Zhao Jiannong: \"...\"","Zhao Jiannong instantly took several steps back, pointed at Qin Yuanzheng, and said, \"He, he is!\"","Everyone: \"...\"","The old doctor looked at Qin Yuanzheng and said, \"Your wife is pregnant. I'd estimate she's about two months along. You can't have intercourse for the first three months, so pay attention to that yourselves.\"","Saying that, the old doctor stood up, ready to leave. \"There's nothing else. The young lady's body has no problems. Just make sure she gets more nutrition over these next few months, and have her dress warmly so she doesn't catch a cold.\"","After the old doctor finished speaking, he waited for a few seconds. When he didn't hear the couple say anything, he shook his head in slight puzzlement and walked out of the room himself.","Doctor Liu quickly walked over and said, \"Teacher, I'll walk you out.\"","Zhao Jiannong also hurried forward, smiling as he said, \"Thank you for your hard work, old sir. Take care on your way out.\"","Inside the room, Qin Yuanzheng was still in a daze.","However, a grand sense of joy bloomed within Qiao Lanshu's heart.","She gently stroked her stomach. She truly never expected that she would actually be pregnant, and with Brother Zheng's child at that.","She stroked it tenderly for quite a while.","Then, Qin Yuanzheng's rough, broad palm covered her hand.","The two looked at each other, both seeing complex emotions in the other's eyes.","Qin Yuanzheng still couldn't quite believe it; he felt like he was dreaming.","He gently caressed Qiao Lanshu's stomach and whispered, \"Are you really pregnant? I'm not dreaming, am I?\"","Doctor Liu, having returned from seeing the old doctor out, heard him say this and laughed. \"Don't worry, Regiment Commander Qin, you're not dreaming. If you're really not at ease, you can also do a urine test. However, the results won't be out until tomorrow. After leaving a sample in a bit, you guys can go back and rest.\"","Doctor Liu looked at Qin Yuanzheng, sighed, and said, \"It wasn't easy for this young lady to conceive this child.\"","With Qin Yuanzheng's physical condition, for them to actually conceive a child meant that after getting married, Qin Yuanzheng must have put in a lot of effort.","Doctor Liu added, \"You heard what was said just now. No intercourse for the first three months, and you also need to pay attention to her diet. If there's nothing else, you can head back first.\"","Qin Yuanzheng helped Qiao Lanshu up, and the two walked outside in silence.","Seeing them like this, Zhao Jiannong found it somewhat amusing. He said, \"Regiment Commander Qin, since you guys are fine, I'll be taking off first.\"","Qin Yuanzheng ignored him, and it was unknown whether he had even heard him.","Zhao Jiannong didn't mind, smiling as he drove away.","They couldn't wait to get back to the base and share this juicy gossip with their comrades."]},{"number":118,"title":"Chapter 118: Joy","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng half-supported and half-embraced Qiao Lanshu, his movements as gentle as if he were holding a fragile piece of porcelain. He carefully shielded her as she settled into the passenger seat.","Before the car door was even fully closed, he lowered his head to double-check if she was sitting comfortably and if the seatbelt was too tight, his fingertips trembling slightly without him even realizing it.","He hadn't said a single word on the way out of the hospital.","It wasn't that he didn't want to speak, but his mind was a tangled mess, buzzing constantly. He was still trapped in a massive state of bewilderment, and even his breathing felt unreal.","The doctor's instructions from just moments ago echoed repeatedly in his ears, leaving him in a trance.","Qin Yuanzheng gently closed the passenger door and walked around to sit in the driver's seat.","The car remained parked at the hospital entrance. Without starting the engine, he just sat there, his fingertips resting on the steering wheel, motionless for a long time.","The interior of the car was completely silent, making even the sound of the wind outside seem exceptionally clear.","Qiao Lanshu turned her head to look at him. The man's jawline was pulled tight. His usually calm and decisive demeanor now revealed a hint of helplessness.","She could not help but speak softly, her voice delicate and gentle, Brother Zheng, what is wrong?","Qin Yuanzheng's Adam's apple bobbed, unable to find his voice for a moment.","He raised a hand and wiped his face hard, as if trying to dispel the muddled feeling. Then, he slowly reached over and gently pinched Qiao Lanshu's slightly cool fingertips.","The warmth of his palm was startlingly hot. His voice was kept extremely low, carrying a tremor he tried hard to conceal, Wife, you are pregnant.","This time, it was no longer an uncertain question, but a statement he forced himself to deliver word by word after calming down.","Seeing his tense expression, Qiao Lanshu could not help but curl her lips. A faint smile rippled in her eyes as she nodded gently, Yes, I am pregnant. Brother Zheng, this is your child. Are you not happy?","Qin Yuanzheng's face remained incredibly tense, his lips pressed into a thin line, and his voice was hoarse, I am happy, of course I am happy.","How could he not be happy?","He used to fantasize about a beautiful life with a wife, kids, and a warm home.","It was just that over the past few years, he had accepted the fact that he could not have children.","He had even once thought he would live out his life alone.","But now, heaven had blessed him. Not only had it brought him Qiao Lanshu, but it had also given him a child.","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent for quite a while before saying, Wife, starting tomorrow, you should stop going to work.","He continued, Just stay home and focus on your pregnancy, what do you think?","Qiao Lanshu did not really want to stay at home.","She was not a local. She had no relatives, friends, or acquaintances here.","Qin Yuanzheng had to run to the mining area and the military base every day. His tasks were heavy, and when he was busy, he was nowhere to be seen.","Leaving her alone in an empty house all day, without even someone to talk to, while it was cold outside and the streets were deserted... she would not even be able to find a place to clear her mind.","Just thinking about those days made her feel suffocated.","She remained silent for a moment, then looked up at Qin Yuanzheng and said, Brother Zheng, I am just watching the warehouse right now. The work is light, and there is not much to do every day. When someone comes to pick up goods, I just open the door and register it. It is not tiring at all. Why not let me keep doing it, and when I reach seven months, I will take maternity leave early.","Once her maternity leave was over and she had mostly recovered, the college entrance examination would be about to start.","By then, she could test into a university in the city. She could study while taking care of the family and the child, living a fulfilling life.","Qin Yuanzheng's mind was still in a mess right now, his thoughts drifting everywhere, making it impossible for him to consider things carefully.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu's earnest attitude, he subconsciously nodded and went along with her, Alright, then I will talk to my cousin and ask him to look after you more. No one will be allowed to make you suffer.","After saying that, he finally started the car and slowly drove away from the hospital.","The wheels had not driven far in the direction of home when Qiao Lanshu suddenly remembered something and quickly tugged at his arm, Brother Zheng, we still have to go to work. Do not go home yet.","Qin Yuanzheng paused, suddenly snapping back to reality. His mind had been so full of the pregnancy that he had completely forgotten about her work.","He did not say anything, just silently turned the steering wheel, turned the car around, and drove to the main gate of the food factory.","When the car stopped, he was still uneasy and insisted on escorting Qiao Lanshu inside.","Walking all the way through the factory area to the small room where she managed the warehouse, Qin Yuanzheng's eyes never left her, and his footsteps were extremely light.","As Qiao Lanshu reached out to unlock the door, he wrapped his arm around her waist, protecting her, terrified she might trip over the threshold.","Throughout the day, Qin Yuanzheng spoke very little, his gaze deep, making it impossible for anyone to guess what he was thinking.","Perhaps the surprise came too suddenly, and the heavy responsibility fell just as fast, causing this usually composed man to panic.","Qiao Lanshu pushed the door open, turned to look at him, her eyes gentle, Brother Zheng, did you not say the base is very busy? Chu Liangjun's theft of the explosives caused such a huge uproar, and now several construction sites are being inspected. The engineering corps definitely needs people. You should go to work first, you do not need to stay with me.","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng gently shook his head. His gaze fell on her lower abdomen, then moved back to her face, There is no rush.","I will stay here and keep you company for a while.","He and Qiao Lanshu were having a child.","It was only two months along, tiny, without even a shape yet, but it was truly rooted deep in his heart.","The way Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu was incredibly soft, mixed with a disbelief and gratitude that was too thick to melt away.","He had never been this panicked in his life, nor had he ever felt this grounded.","He reached back and gently closed the door, took a step forward, and carefully pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms. His hold was so light, as if he were afraid of breaking her. His voice was low, carrying an indescribable sense of remorse, I am sorry. I did not expect to get you pregnant so quickly.","He sighed softly, resting his chin on the top of her head, and said in a muffled voice, If I had known, I definitely would have used protection.","He had not had enough of their time as just a couple yet.","He was nearly thirty years old and had finally managed to marry a wife so perfectly suited to his heart. He had just tasted the sweetness of married life, his heart full of warmth, thinking every day about how to dote on her more, but the little one had come so impatiently.","Holding her, Qin Yuanzheng could not help but look down, his gaze gently landing on her still-flat stomach, his eyes complex yet soft.","You are still so young, and now you have to suffer through becoming a mother.","His voice was strained, I have wronged you.","Qiao Lanshu did not know whether to laugh or cry.","She looked up at him and said earnestly and softly, You do not need to apologize. I love children. I am more than happy to be pregnant.","She had previously felt regret that she might not be able to give him a son or a daughter;","Now that her wish had come true, her heart was filled with joy.","Qin Yuanzheng's heart ached. He suddenly tightened his arms, holding her firmly against his chest. His embrace carried a restrained tremble, and his voice was terribly hoarse, Xiao Qiao, thank you. I will be good to you for the rest of my life...","Qiao Lanshu could feel the slight rise and fall of his chest, and the faint trembling of his shoulders.","This tough man, who would shed blood in the military without blinking an eye, actually had red eyes and was shedding tears in her arms at this moment.","Her heart instantly melted. She gently raised her hand, patted his back, and said softly, \"I know. You already treat me so well.\"","Just then, a rapid knocking came from outside, accompanied by a man's shout, \"Is the warehouse manager in? Please open the door, I need to pick up some goods!\"","The two of them immediately stiffened and quickly pulled apart.","Qiao Lanshu pressed a finger to her lips, gesturing for Qin Yuanzheng to keep quiet. \"Stay in the room for a bit and don't go out,\" she whispered. \"We don't want anyone to see you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Sitting in the deepest corner of the small room, Qin Yuanzheng watched as Qiao Lanshu left him behind, grabbed her keys, and opened the door to step outside.","Qin Yuanzheng felt a bit displeased. He was Qiao Lanshu's husband, after all, not a secret lover. Why did they have to act so sneaky?"]},{"number":119,"title":"Chapter 119: What brings the factory director here","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng originally wanted to stay with Qiao Lanshu a little longer.","However, there were indeed matters at the military base waiting for him to handle.","After all, it was an independent regiment. Without a division commander to supervise, he had to attend to everything personally and couldn't afford a single mistake.","Having spent a little time with Qiao Lanshu at the food factory, he was now getting ready to leave.","Yet, he was still reluctant to part with her, his gaze involuntarily darting to her stomach every now and then.","He was terrified that something might happen to her while he wasn't around.","He took a moment to observe Qiao Lanshu's work duties.","Being a warehouse keeper was actually a very easy job.","Whenever someone came to pick up goods, Qiao Lanshu would just take the keys and open the door for them.","Then, she only needed to wait at the door. Once the goods were collected, she would check the items against the receipts, lock the door, and head back.","Qin Yuanzheng was extremely satisfied with Qiao Lanshu's job.","When Qiao Lanshu returned, he said softly, \"Wife, I need to go to the mining area for a meeting.\"","He had already delayed for most of the morning. If he dragged it out any longer, he was afraid he wouldn't be able to get off work on time tonight.","He still wanted to come home early to cook for his wife.","Qiao Lanshu nodded, looking at Qin Yuanzheng with equal reluctance, and whispered, \"Then be careful on the road.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He looked at Qiao Lanshu, hesitating as if he wanted to say something more.","Qiao Lanshu gave him a gentle push. \"Hurry up and go. If you delay any longer, it'll be time for lunch.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","Only then did Qin Yuanzheng step out, looking back at her with every step he took.","However, after leaving the warehouse, Qin Yuanzheng didn't immediately leave the food factory to rush back to work at the mining area.","He turned his steps and headed straight toward the factory manager's office.","He was looking for his cousin, Yang Wenyan.","It was already the end of the year, and matters big and small in the factory were piling up. Yang Wenyan was busy sorting through stacks of materials and verifying various data in preparation for the year-end report to his superiors.","Once this busy period was over and the report was successfully approved, everyone would be able to breathe a sigh of relief and peacefully prepare for the New Year.","Qin Yuanzheng walked up to the door of the factory manager's office and raised his hand to knock.","Before he married Qiao Lanshu, he had almost never come to the food factory to find Yang Wenyan.","Even when his cousin repeatedly invited him over for meals, he always made excuses and rarely showed up.","At that time, he was entirely devoted to the mining area. He left home before dawn and didn't return until it was pitch dark, making it hard for Yang Wenyan to even catch a glimpse of him.","But things were different now.","Since marrying his wife, the number of times he had run to the food factory was more than the past few years combined.","Yang Wenyan's slightly exhausted voice came from inside the office, \"Come in, the door is unlocked.\"","Qin Yuanzheng gently pushed the door open and walked in. His gaze swept over the documents piled high on the desk as he spoke, \"Cousin, are you busy?\"","Yang Wenyan was burying his head in organizing thick report materials, his pen scratching against the paper. Hearing the voice, he jerked his head up. When he saw who it was, a clear look of surprise appeared on his face. \"Yuanzheng? Why are you here?\"","Qin Yuanzheng closed the door behind him, shutting out the noise from the corridor outside, before speaking. \"I was dropping my wife off at work, so I came over to see you while I was at it.\"","Hearing this, Yang Wenyan was initially startled, and then began to mutter in his heart.","Why did those words sound so unbelievable?","Came to see him while he was at it?","Did Qin Yuanzheng seem like the kind of person who would intentionally take a detour and make time just to see him?","In the past, he couldn't even be dragged over. Today, however, he had shown up on his own initiative. Something was definitely up.","Yang Wenyan didn't call him out on it. He quickly put down his pen and said enthusiastically, \"Then take a seat and rest for a bit. Once I finish this up, we'll go to the cafeteria for lunch together.\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't move, merely shaking his head. \"I won't sit, Cousin.\"","He paused, his tone growing a bit heavier. \"I came to find you because I wanted to tell you something.\"","As he spoke, his usual steady demeanor faded slightly, revealing a rare hint of hesitation.","Seeing this, Yang Wenyan grew even more curious. He immediately put down the documents and pen in his hands and said casually, \"What is it? Just say it. Why be so polite with me?\"","Qin Yuanzheng paced around in a small circle, his fingers unconsciously clenching. He looked conflicted for a good while before finally speaking, his voice very soft. \"I want to... ask you to take extra care of Xiao Qiao.\"","Hearing this, Yang Wenyan instantly breathed a sigh of relief and waved his hand with a smile. \"Hey, I thought it was something major. Haven't you already asked me to do that? What, has Xiao Qiao suffered some grievance over at the warehouse?\"","Logically speaking, that shouldn't be the case.","Qiao Lanshu was the only warehouse keeper assigned over there, with her own little room. It was called a warehouse keeper's room, but it was practically no different from a private office.","She didn't have to squeeze in and toil with the people in the workshop, nor did she have to deal with anyone's attitude. She could just stay quietly in her room every day, counting inventory and keeping the books. It was one of the few leisurely and respectable jobs in the entire food factory.","Just as Yang Wenyan was thinking this, he heard Qin Yuanzheng lower his voice, his tone exceptionally serious. \"Yes, I did say that before, but this time, the situation is a bit special.\"","Qin Yuanzheng took two steps forward, leaning close to Yang Wenyan's desk, his voice dropping even lower. \"Xiao Qiao is pregnant. I'm worried her body won't be able to handle it.\"","\"What?!\"","Yang Wenyan slapped the desk hard, his voice instantly shooting up. His eyes widened into circles as he stared at Qin Yuanzheng in shock, unable to believe his ears. \"Who did you say is pregnant?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was momentarily stunned by his shout and didn't immediately reply.","He couldn't blame his cousin for having such a huge reaction. Actually, when he was at the hospital today and heard the doctor say those words, he had also frozen for a long while before coming back to his senses. He felt like he was walking on clouds, and for a moment, he thought he was dreaming.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng remaining silent, Yang Wenyan grew even more anxious. He immediately walked around the desk, went up to him, and gently nudged him with his elbow, urging him with wide eyes. \"Ah, why do you always stop halfway through a sentence? Who exactly did you say is pregnant?\"","Qin Yuanzheng touched his nose, a rare look of discomfort appearing on his face. His tone carried a hint of daze that even he hadn't noticed. \"Maybe... my wife?\"","Yang Wenyan was speechless.","He really had to hand it to this cousin of his.","\"Maybe?\"","Yang Wenyan pointed at him helplessly. \"Yuanzheng, you usually speak and act with absolute decisiveness. You've never been so wishy-washy before. If you aren't sure about something, you wouldn't breathe a word of it. What's wrong with you today?\"","Qin Yuanzheng's brows furrowed tightly, his expression solemn. \"Yes, my mind is a bit of a mess today... Xiao Qiao should be pregnant.\"","Yang Wenyan stared at him again. \"Should be?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded with a serious face. \"Should be.\"","Yang Wenyan was so frustrated by his back-and-forth words that his heart itched with anxiety.","Too lazy to waste any more breath on Qin Yuanzheng, he pushed him aside, grabbed his coat draped over the back of the chair, and headed for the door. \"Forget it, I can't make sense of you. I'll go ask Xiao Qiao myself!\"","Before his voice even faded, he had already rushed out of the office in a hurry, heading straight in the direction of the warehouse.","Qin Yuanzheng stood where he was, watching his cousin's hurried back. He opened his mouth to say something, but ultimately just sighed and silently followed behind him.","The factory workers they encountered along the way all grew tense in unison upon seeing Yang Wenyan looking so anxious.","They began to whisper among themselves: \"What's going on? Has something major happened at our factory again?\"","\"The last time the factory manager was in such a rush, it was when a murder happened at our factory.\"","\"We're doomed. It's already the end of the year, could something terrible have happened again? Can't they just let us have a peaceful New Year?\"","...","Yang Wenyan arrived at the entrance of the food factory's warehouse, where Qiao Lanshu was sitting inside reading a book.","Yang Wenyan knocked on the window: \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, Comrade Xiao Qiao?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","What wind blew the factory manager here? She pondered to herself, certain that she hadn't made any mistakes in her work."]},{"number":120,"title":"Chapter 120: I Heard My Sister-in-Law Is Expecting","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu opened the door to the small house and asked Yang Wenyan with a smile, Factory Manager, what brings you here? Do you have any work instructions?","Seeing Qiao Lanshu, Yang Wenyan chuckled, rubbed his hands together, and said somewhat sheepishly, Xiao Qiao, well, it's like this.","Getting a bit anxious, Yang Wenyan spoke more directly. He asked, I heard from Yuanzheng that you're pregnant?","Hearing Yang Wenyan ask this, Xiao Qiao was taken aback for a moment. Seeing Qin Yuanzheng walking over from a distance, she knew he hadn't left just now, but had gone to the factory manager's office.","Qiao Lanshu immediately nodded, feeling a bit shy, and said, Yes, I just went to the hospital today. The doctor said I'm already two months along.","A look of pleasant surprise instantly appeared on Yang Wenyan's face.","Along with the surprise, there was a hint of excitement.","In the past, Qin Yuanzheng's marriage was the most worrying thing for the Qin family.","After Qin Yuanzheng finally managed to marry Qiao Lanshu, his parents were overjoyed. If they hadn't thought they couldn't get away for the time being, they probably would have come over to see their daughter-in-law.","However, it was snowing heavily at the time and the trains were suspended. Yang Wenyan wrote a letter to Qin's parents, advising them not to come, thinking it would be enough for Qin Yuanzheng to bring Qiao Lanshu home to visit during the New Year.","Now that Qiao Lanshu was pregnant, Qin Yuanzheng probably wouldn't be able to go back to visit for the New Year.","Yang Wenyan said, This is a good thing!","Yang Wenyan excitedly clenched his fists, repeating several times, A good thing, this is a great thing!","After his excitement, Yang Wenyan felt a bit of regret.","Qin Yuanzheng, who had been diagnosed with infertility, was having a child.","Yet he, who had never been diagnosed, still had no children.","So, which of them was actually the infertile one?","Qin Yuanzheng walked over at this time.","He stood at the door, looking at Qiao Lanshu together with Yang Wenyan.","Qiao Lanshu blushed under their gaze.","Qin Yuanzheng knew his wife was feeling shy.","So, Qin Yuanzheng pulled Yang Wenyan away and whispered, Cousin, it's better not to talk about this matter for now. The fewer people who know, the better.","Yang Wenyan nodded with an excited expression, Right, right, right. If this gets out, it will only affect Xiao Qiao's rest. After all, you have a reputation out there, right? Better to avoid people gossiping.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Yang Wenyan pondered for a moment and then said, Pregnant women still need to eat more nutritious things. Tomorrow, I'll have the logistics department put in a request to give Comrade Xiao Qiao an egg every day to nourish her body.","In these times, food was incredibly precious.","Aside from the New Year, people had no meat to eat on ordinary days. Eggs were also very rare, generally reserved for children and pregnant women.","Even most of the elderly didn't have eggs to eat.","As Qiao Lanshu was now a pregnant woman, she could eat one egg a day and receive an extra pound of white flour in her monthly grain ration.","Of course, she could also opt out of the white flour and exchange it for five pounds of coarse grains or red flour.","In short, because of her pregnancy, her food subsidies were greater than usual.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't understand this either, so he asked, What do pregnant women generally need to pay attention to? What can she eat, and what can't she eat? Is there anything I need to do?","Yang Wenyan: ...","Yang Wenyan glanced at him and said grumpily, You're asking me? I don't have children either, how would I know? You'd be better off asking your good neighbor, that military officer named Zhao. He definitely knows more than we do.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded with a serious expression, Right, I almost forgot about him. I'll go find him right now.","Seeing him about to leave, Yang Wenyan quickly reminded him, By the way, Yuanzheng, don't tell your parents about this just yet.","Qin Yuanzheng's parents only had him as their son.","Over the years, they had worried endlessly about his marriage.","The old couple had finally accepted the fact that Qin Yuanzheng was infertile.","They couldn't let them get their hopes up for nothing.","Yang Wenyan walked up to Qin Yuanzheng and lowered his voice, Keep this under wraps for now. Wait until Xiao Qiao is stable, maybe after six or seven months? Or maybe eight months, right before she's due to give birth, then send them a telegram. You know what I mean?","In this era, many girls had a hard time getting pregnant due to malnutrition or having their bodies damaged by the freezing winters.","Even if they did conceive, the first pregnancy wasn't always stable.","Miscarriages were actually quite common.","As a factory manager with so many female workers in the food factory, Yang Wenyan knew all about this.","Qiao Lanshu's pregnancy was a good thing, but he was afraid the pregnancy might not be stable and some accident might happen...","Yang Wenyan didn't go into too much detail, but of course, Qin Yuanzheng understood.","He nodded, his expression turning a bit heavier, and said, I understand, Cousin. I've only told you about this. I haven't told anyone else, so no one else knows yet.","Yang Wenyan breathed a sigh of relief and said, That's good, that's good. Then I can rest easy. Alright, leave Xiao Qiao to me. If there's nothing else, go to work. Your cousin-in-law's maiden family seems to be raising a few hens. I'll ask if they have any free-range eggs and buy some for you. When she's three or four months along, I'll buy a hen from them so you can stew some soup to nourish Xiao Qiao.","There weren't many hens anyway. Deng Xiaozhen's maiden family kept four or five hens, all for laying eggs, and they couldn't bear to slaughter them for meat.","It was hard to find them elsewhere too.","Yang Wenyan figured he would buy two from them.","One to nourish her body during the pregnancy, and one to eat during her postpartum confinement.","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng nodded and said, Thank you, Cousin. I'll pay for it. Please help me ask around to see where else we can buy hens. Xiao Qiao also likes drinking soup.","Yang Wenyan nodded, Alright, I got it. You go to work first, don't worry.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded, and this time he really left.","On the military base's side, they could actually find pastures to buy mutton.","He pondered where to buy meat, eggs, goat's milk, and fruit to bring back to nourish Comrade Xiao Qiao's body.","He arrived at the entrance of the mining area weighed down by his thoughts. Just as he stepped out of the car, a group of people from the troops suddenly popped out.","It gave him a start.","Looking at the dozen or so comrades-in-arms surrounding him, he frowned and asked in a deep voice, What are you all doing? What happened?","Lin Yucheng leaned in and asked loudly, Reporting to the Commander! We heard that our sister-in-law is expecting! We came specifically to celebrate with you!","Following that, with a bang, a small, military-made firework exploded right above Qin Yuanzheng's head.","Qin Yuanzheng: ..."]},{"number":121,"title":"Chapter 121: Spread All Over","paragraphs":["The news of Qin Yuanzheng's wife being pregnant spread through the entire military camp like a gust of wind in just one morning. Even the neighboring garrison had heard about it.","He was stationed at the mining area all year round, but the news traveled faster than people could.","Walking on the road, soldiers and officers, whether he knew them or not, would come up from time to time, smiling and congratulating him: \"Regimental Commander Qin, congratulations! Congratulations on expecting a baby!\"","The people in the army were honest and straightforward; they didn't play empty games.","As soon as the words of congratulations were spoken, they would stuff money, food coupons, or half a bag of white flour and millet directly into his arms.","These were all saved up from their frugal daily lives. No one hid anything; they all held onto one belief: an addition to the Regimental Commander's family was a great joyous event for the entire regiment.","When the news reached the regiment's political commissar, he took it even more to heart.","Goodness knows where he got a plump and sturdy milk goat, but he led it personally all the way to Qin Yuanzheng's office.","\"Regimental Commander Qin,\"","The commissar handed the goat's rope to him, smiling radiantly, \"Keep this goat. When it produces milk, it will be good for nourishing Comrade Xiao Qiao's body, and the baby will benefit too.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at the docile goat in front of him, then turned his head to look at the corner of the office where there were a few lively free-range chickens and a large goose that stretched its neck to peck at anyone it saw. The originally spacious and tidy office had been stuffed into something resembling a makeshift livestock shed.","For a moment, he didn't know what to say, feeling both touched and amused.","Usually, everyone lived on a tight budget and could only afford a bit of meat during festivals. But now, chickens, geese, goats, grain, money, and coupons were all being sent to him in droves.","He knew very well in his heart that these things were the heartfelt intentions his comrades had squeezed out through gritted teeth.","In the past, with discipline at the forefront, Qin Yuanzheng wouldn't have accepted them no matter what.","But at the thought of his young wife at home who had just gotten pregnant, his heart softened.","It didn't matter if he suffered a bit of hardship and fatigue, but he absolutely could not let his wife suffer any grievances.","He would remember these favors in his heart and slowly repay them in the future.","The most important thing right now was to properly nourish his wife.","Qin Yuanzheng called his orderly and asked him to load the things that could be put into the vehicle and take them home first.","However, for live animals like chickens, geese, and goats, there was no place to keep them at home, and it was inconvenient.","He thought it over and simply ordered the orderly to temporarily house them in the shed built for retired military dogs over in the mining area.","The military dog kennel was spacious and sturdy; partitioning off a section would do. It was winter right now, and they couldn't just let these livestock freeze outside.","Having finally dealt with wave after wave of people coming to congratulate him, Qin Yuanzheng had just picked up his thermos to take a sip of water, wanting to quietly read a report, when the office door was pushed open again.","A travel-worn Guan Wenjun walked in, his face not looking too good.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't even lift his eyelids, already feeling a bit impatient in his heart.","Guan Wenjun, however, walked straight to his desk, stared directly at him, and got straight to the point: \"Comrade Xiao Qiao is pregnant?\"","Qin Yuanzheng slowly raised his eyes, his tone cold: \"What does it matter to you?\"","Guan Wenjun immediately raised his voice, as if he had seized upon some massive justification: \"Of course it matters to me! This child is mine!\"","Before he even finished speaking, Qin Yuanzheng's face suddenly sank, his eyes instantly turning cold. His hands unconsciously clenched into fists as he stared at Guan Wenjun: \"Yours? Say that again?\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Seeing that the situation was turning bad, Guan Wenjun hurriedly changed his tune, speaking as fast as pouring beans: \"I mean, I'm the child's godfather! Godfather!\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at him speechlessly and said, \"Get lost.\"","But Guan Wenjun didn't leave; he was feeling quite upset inside.","Thinking back to those days, Qin Yuanzheng had stolen his girlfriend.","Now, he couldn't steal Qin Yuanzheng's wife away from him.","Moreover, Qin Yuanzheng actually had a wife now.","The more he thought about it, the more unbalanced he felt. Holding it in for a long time, he deliberately provoked Qin Yuanzheng, saying, \"No, I say, Old Qin, don't let yourself be fooled. You have infertility, so how could Comrade Xiao Qiao possibly be pregnant?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was in a good mood today, so he didn't get angry upon hearing this. He deliberately said to Guan Wenjun, \"I did have infertility originally, but because I worked hard enough, Comrade Xiao Qiao got pregnant. What, are you envious? If you're envious, go find a wife for yourself and work hard at it. Don't spend all day staring at other people's wives, understand?\"","Qin Yuanzheng's words were also spoken with a hint of a threat.","Because of some past events, Guan Wenjun used to always keep an eye on Qin Yuanzheng's wife.","Guan Wenjun still had a bottom line; he just had a foul mouth. But if he were really asked to do something to Qiao Lanshu, he probably wouldn't dare.","But now, Qiao Lanshu was pregnant.","If Guan Wenjun dared to run up to Qiao Lanshu again and spout nonsense, Qin Yuanzheng would not be polite.","Guan Wenjun stared at him for a long while, feeling angry and stifled, and finally left in a huff.","As he went out the door, his face was as black as the bottom of a pot.","After driving Guan Wenjun away, Qin Yuanzheng didn't delay for a single moment. He grabbed his military cap and hurried to the headquarters.","Keeping in mind that he had to go pick up his young wife from work, he handed over all the matters that didn't require immediate decisions to the vice regimental commander and Staff Officer Lin, and headed straight to the headquarters right on time.","But he never expected that the news of Qiao Lanshu's pregnancy would travel faster than he could run; it had already reached the headquarters a step ahead of him.","Logically speaking, it was a common occurrence for a military officer's family member to get pregnant in the army. An addition to anyone's family was a joyous event, and there was no need to spread it around like a storm.","But with this happening to Qin Yuanzheng, it was completely different.","It wasn't a small matter; it was a huge deal.","It wasn't just a joyous event; it was major news.","Back when the news of his marriage to Qiao Lanshu came out, the entire military district, along with the surrounding factory areas, had gossiped about it for nearly half a month, and the hype had never died down.","Now that his wife was pregnant, judging by this momentum, the gossip wouldn't dissipate for at least half a year.","When Qiao Lanshu eventually gave birth, people might gossip for another half a year.","Just thinking about it made Qin Yuanzheng's scalp tingle.","As soon as he entered Commander Li's office, his eyes immediately caught sight of a bulging bag of rice at the corner of the desk—a full fifty catties!","Just as he walked in, Commander Li smiled and said, \"Yuanzheng is here. Take this bag of rice back with you later for your wife to eat. Doesn't she like eating rice? I specially had someone prepare it.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","He felt utterly helpless: \"Chief, how did you find out about this too?\"","Commander Li laughed heartily, \"The whole military district is talking about it now. It'd be hard for me not to know.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was completely speechless.","Commander Li then asked with concern, \"Could the previous diagnosis have been a mistake? Why don't you go get it checked properly again, just for peace of mind.\"","Qin Yuanzheng gently shook his head, his tone calm: \"I'm not going, I don't have time.\"","At this point, whether he got checked or not was no longer important.","The child had truly arrived; it was an unexpected joy, a special grace from the heavens.","He asked for nothing else. He just wanted to peacefully guard Qiao Lanshu and the little life in her belly, living a solid and steady life.","Seeing his absent-minded look, as if his soul had already drifted back home, Commander Li didn't force him to stay longer. He waved his hand and said, \"Alright, it won't be too late to discuss the rest of these trivial matters tomorrow. It's getting late, you go on back first.\"","As soon as those words were spoken, the heavy gloom in Qin Yuanzheng's eyes vanished, instantly lighting up.","He stood up immediately, straightened his back, and gave a crisp, standard military salute. \"Thank you, Chief! Goodbye, Chief!\"","The moment the words left his mouth, he turned on his heel and headed for the door.","But after taking barely two steps, he abruptly spun back around.","Without standing on ceremony, he grabbed the fifty-pound bag of rice. Then, his gaze swept across Commander Li's desk, and he casually swiped the two large, round oranges sitting there, pocketing them as well.","Commander Li sat frozen in his chair, staring at the man's smooth, practiced movements, taking a long moment to process what had just happened.","He was truly left speechless. Those oranges had been a respectful gift from one of his longtime subordinates to honor him in his old age. And now? Swiped by another longtime subordinate.","He didn't even leave him the orange peels."]},{"number":122,"title":"Chapter 122: Cloying","paragraphs":["Compared to the hustle and bustle on Qin Yuanzheng's side at the military base, Qiao Lanshu's day at the food factory was quite peaceful.","News from the base wouldn't reach the factory anytime soon, and Yang Wenyan was keeping his mouth shut, not breathing a word to anyone.","Qiao Lanshu went through her workday as usual, and everything was incredibly calm.","What was different from usual, however, was that Qin Yuanzheng was already waiting at the factory gate long before it was time for her to get off work.","Qiao Lanshu's shift ended quite early, yet he was even earlier. He had already been waiting at the gate for several minutes.","The moment Qin Yuanzheng saw her, he immediately strode over. The hem of his overcoat billowed in the cold wind. Wearing his military cap and gloves, with his tall figure, long legs, and striking presence, he stood out from the crowd.","Qiao Lanshu stared at him for a moment, suddenly wondering to herself whether the baby in her belly was a boy or a girl. Would the baby look like its father or its mother?","If it was a boy, she hoped he would take after his father. She worried that if he took after her, he wouldn't grow very tall.","That's right, Qiao Lanshu was already starting to fret over her child's future height.","When Qin Yuanzheng walked up and saw her spacing out, he put an arm around her and asked, \"What are you thinking about so intently?\"","Qiao Lanshu felt a bit too embarrassed to say, so she shook her head. \"Brother Zheng, how come you got off work so early today?\"","At the mention of this, Qin Yuanzheng sighed and said, \"The news of your pregnancy has already spread all over the military district. Commander Li found out too, and he told me to get off work early to accompany you.\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","People these days really were too bored. Aside from work, they just gossiped about other families to pass the time.","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng had practically provided them with enough gossip material to last a whole year.","Qin Yuanzheng took Qiao Lanshu home.","As soon as they arrived, he helped her take off her coat and carried her to the sofa.","Qiao Lanshu was left wearing only a thin knit sweater. She asked, a little shyly, \"Brother Zheng, what are you doing?\"","Qin Yuanzheng lifted her sweater to look at her belly.","After looking for a while, he turned his head to press his ear against it and listen.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qin Yuanzheng's stubble was hard and thick, and it tickled her so much she quickly dodged away. \"Ah, Brother Zheng, stop poking me with your beard.\"","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent.","He looked up, his gaze deep and quiet as he stared at her. \"I just wanted to listen and see if I could hear the heartbeat.\"","Qiao Lanshu asked curiously, \"So, did you hear it?\"","Qin Yuanzheng silently shook his head. \"No.\"","From his expression, he actually seemed a bit disappointed.","Qiao Lanshu quickly comforted him, \"The baby is probably still too small. Once it gets a bit bigger, you'll probably be able to hear it.\"","Qin Yuanzheng naturally knew this logic. He was just a bit too excited. His heart was so full of swelling emotions that he didn't know how to let them out.","Looking at Qiao Lanshu, he truly felt that she was a gift sent to him from heaven.","He even felt that without her, he really might have ended up alone for the rest of his life.","Qin Yuanzheng rested his chin against Qiao Lanshu's belly and gently rubbed it.","Qiao Lanshu immediately started trying to dodge again.","Qin Yuanzheng chuckled and asked her, \"Wife, is it really that prickly?\"","As he spoke, he reached up and touched his own chin. He hadn't shaved for just two days, how had it grown out again so quickly?","The short stubble was very hard, leaving a prickly, numb sensation against his hand. It was no wonder Qiao Lanshu reacted like that.","Qin Yuanzheng thought of the past few times they were on the bed, how Qiao Lanshu had reacted when she was pricked by his stubble, and his heart stirred.","Suddenly, he felt a little hungry?","Qin Yuanzheng took off his outer clothes, leaned in close to Qiao Lanshu, and whispered, \"Wife, what did the doctor say today? Nothing for the first three months, right?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, her face flushing. \"That's what the doctor said.\"","Qin Yuanzheng hadn't had any action for the past few days and was holding it in.","Last night, Qiao Lanshu had said her stomach felt uncomfortable, and he had been thinking about putting on a good performance when he got back tonight.","But now, he had to practice complete abstinence.","Qin Yuanzheng kissed Qiao Lanshu and murmured, \"Three months... You're already two months pregnant now, which means there's only one month left, right? One month, thirty days, hiss...\"","Thirty days, that was going to be too hard to endure, wasn't it?","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu with a slightly aggrieved expression and whispered, \"Wife, I'm hungry. How about you feed me a little something?\"","At first, Qiao Lanshu didn't understand what he meant and asked, \"Eat what?\"","Qin Yuanzheng proceeded to help her take off her pants.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","...","Over an hour later, Qin Yuanzheng carried Qiao Lanshu to rest. He said, \"Be good, wife. I'll go make dinner. You get some good rest.\"","The corners of Qiao Lanshu's eyes were red. She nodded. \"Okay, I'm so hungry.\"","Qin Yuanzheng brought over some fried dough twists. \"Then have a little bit of this first. I'll boil some millet porridge for you.\"","Qiao Lanshu was exhausted, but Qin Yuanzheng was even more energetic.","The more he ate, the more energetic he became, yet he had no way to fully release it.","Qin Yuanzheng felt restless all over.","Qiao Lanshu scolded him softly, \"Brother Zheng, isn't it time you shaved?\"","She had told him so many times to shave his beard.","From now on, if he didn't shave, he wasn't allowed to get close to her.","Yet, Qin Yuanzheng would agree perfectly on the surface, only to intentionally let his beard grow out behind her back.","He knew that the stubble was prickly and uncomfortable.","But it was exactly because he knew it that he deliberately kept it.","Qin Yuanzheng teased her, \"I think you quite like it.\"","He leaned close to her ear and whispered, \"Do you need to use the bathroom?\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu's face and ears instantly burned red.","She stubbornly denied it, \"I do not. Hurry up and go cook.\"","Qin Yuanzheng stood up with a smile and headed toward the kitchen. \"I know, I know. I'm going to cook right now.\"","However, before cooking, Qin Yuanzheng made a trip to the bathroom first.","He had no choice; if Qiao Lanshu wasn't going to the bathroom, he had to.","He had a big appetite and couldn't hold it in."]},{"number":123,"title":"Chapter 123: Discussion","paragraphs":["The news of Qiao Lanshu's pregnancy spread like wildfire overnight.","Early the next morning, the neighbors came knocking with gifts in hand.","Everyone was an officer in the military base, so they were all well-acquainted with one another.","Although Qiao Lanshu went to work every day and rarely saw these neighbors, meaning she wasn't very close to them...","...these neighbors certainly knew her!","Yesterday, everyone at the base had heard about the happy news in Qin Yuanzheng's family.","Now that a night had passed, the families of these military officers naturally all knew about it too.","Huang Erling was the first to knock. After Qiao Lanshu opened the door, Huang Erling walked in carrying a bag of red dates, smiling brightly as she said, \"Xiao Qiao, congratulations! I heard you're expecting?\"","Huang Erling's hunch had been spot on.","Qiao Lanshu was indeed pregnant.","When Zhao Jiannong came back and told her last night, she had been overjoyed.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Sister Ling, I haven't even thanked you yet. If it weren't for your reminder, I never would have thought to go to the hospital for a check-up.\"","Honestly, she never would have guessed she was pregnant in a million years.","Huang Erling laughed and said, \"Well, I've been through it before, after all. One look at your symptoms and I knew exactly what was going on.\"","As she spoke, Huang Erling stepped further into the house, followed by five or six other women. She smiled and added, \"Xiao Qiao, you probably haven't met them yet, but these are our neighbors. They all heard your good news and came over specifically to see you.\"","The neighbors who came all carried small gifts like eggs, red dates, or dried noodles.","The group of women squeezed into the living room, sharing pregnancy tips and advice with Qiao Lanshu.","These women really dared to say anything. They even told Xiao Qiao to sleep separately from Qin Yuanzheng, saying they needed to abstain from intimacy for at least three months. They also praised Regiment Commander Qin, saying he was truly impressive for getting her pregnant just a few months after their wedding, joking that his speed was faster than a normal man's.","Listening to their lively chatter, Qiao Lanshu sat there blushing furiously, completely at a loss for words.","Huang Erling was already very familiar with them and happily joined in the gossip.","Seeing this, Qin Yuanzheng, who was in the kitchen, felt too awkward to go out and simply stayed put.","After more than half an hour, the female comrades finished their chatting, left their gifts, and departed.","Only then did Qin Yuanzheng emerge from the kitchen. He looked at Qiao Lanshu and asked with a smile, \"What's wrong? Why is your face so red?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu glared at him. \"You have the nerve to ask.\"","She then muttered under her breath, \"It's all because of you.\"","Despite his supposed infertility, Qin Yuanzheng had managed to get his little wife pregnant after only three or four months of marriage.","Qiao Lanshu could well imagine how those people were going to gossip about them behind their backs.","They would definitely say that Qin Yuanzheng worked hard plowing the fields every night or something like that.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu's expression, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly became curious.","He leaned in and lowered his voice, \"Why are you blaming me again? Is it my fault for being too capable?\"","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu glared at him. \"Stop talking.\"","As she spoke, she reached out to cover his mouth. \"It's fine if you say these things at home, but absolutely do not say them outside. It wouldn't be good if someone heard.\"","Qin Yuanzheng suddenly pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms and rubbed his stubble against her face.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Weren't they just having a normal conversation? Why was he bullying her again?","Qiao Lanshu tried to push him away but failed, so she could only let him rub his stubble against her, whispering, \"Ah, stop rubbing, it hurts.\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't know when he had developed this habit, but he loved to rub his stubble against her at every opportunity.","Not just her face... he wanted to rub it everywhere.","His stubble was so tough that it was prickly even if he didn't shave for a single day, yet he deliberately let it grow for two days just for this.","What kind of weird fetish was this? Qiao Lanshu was completely helpless against him.","In their previous life, he definitely hadn't been like this.","Qin Yuanzheng had been in a great mood these past two days, though he simply hadn't shown it while outside.","Holding Qiao Lanshu, he buried his face in the crook of her neck, taking a deep breath against her chest, and said in a muffled voice, \"Wife, you smell so good.\"","He really loved the scent on Qiao Lanshu now; it was almost as if the smell was addictive.","If possible, he truly wanted to stay home every day and be all lovey-dovey with Qiao Lanshu.","He sighed and whispered, \"Wife, what should we do? There's still a month left. I'm afraid I won't be able to hold back.\"","Going even a single day without it was unbearable for him.","And now he had to wait a whole month.","Qiao Lanshu also felt a bit bad for Qin Yuanzheng. She knew just how energetic he was.","His needs in that area were incredibly vigorous.","She hesitated for a moment before whispering, \"Do you want me to...?\"","As she spoke, she reached over and tugged at his waistband.","The hint was very obvious.","Qin Yuanzheng froze for a second. Wow, was he really getting this lucky?","Qin Yuanzheng was very tempted.","However, he glanced at the time and said with some regret, \"We've already wasted a lot of time this morning. We need to go to work.\"","Qiao Lanshu glanced at the small desk clock and whispered, \"Isn't there still over half an hour left?\"","Qin Yuanzheng replied, \"Half an hour isn't enough.\"","In half an hour, he wouldn't even be able to get started properly.","Wouldn't that be a waste of such a good opportunity?","The couple was incredibly clingy with each other, though it was mostly Qin Yuanzheng clinging to Qiao Lanshu.","He was already clingy to begin with, but now that he knew Qiao Lanshu was pregnant, he was even worse.","He hugged her and refused to let go.","With great difficulty, the two finally got dressed and ready to head out.","He still leaned into Qiao Lanshu's ear, wrapping an arm around her waist, and whispered, \"Wife, does this mean I'll have milk to drink in the future?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu really couldn't stand him anymore. She glared at him and hissed, \"Shut up already, we're about to head out!\"","What if Huang Erling next door heard him?","Huang Erling was very close with the older women in the neighborhood, and their gossip could be quite terrifying.","Don't be fooled by how mature and steady Qin Yuanzheng appeared in front of outsiders.","It was all an illusion!","In front of Qiao Lanshu, not only was he clingy, but he also loved to say those kinds of things and tease her. His personality wasn't steady at all.","Qiao Lanshu was only a little over two months pregnant now, and her morning sickness symptoms were actually very mild.","It must be because the baby was so well-behaved and didn't want to make its mother uncomfortable.","Aside from feeling a little nauseous a couple of days ago, Qiao Lanshu had been perfectly fine since then, with no issues at all.","Her appetite during meals was normal, though she did get hungry more easily than before.","Afraid that his wife would go hungry, Qin Yuanzheng grabbed a small cloth bag before they left. He packed it with some red dates, fried dough twists, walnuts, an apple, and an orange, and even filled her thermos halfway with warm goat's milk.","Qiao Lanshu felt he was exaggerating a bit. She whispered, \"I won't be able to finish all this food.\"","Qin Yuanzheng insisted on bringing it, saying, \"Even if you're not hungry, the baby will be. Eating more is good for you. With so many people coming over today, I completely forgot, but tomorrow I'll boil an egg for you to take to work.\"","They had plenty of food at home, especially with so many people dropping off gifts over the past couple of days.","Qin Yuanzheng made a mental note of everyone who had brought him gifts; these were favors he would certainly have to repay in the future.","Qin Yuanzheng escorted Qiao Lanshu to the entrance of the food factory. Since they had spent so much time being affectionate at home today, he decided not to walk her all the way inside. He simply watched her enter the factory grounds before driving off.","However, the moment Qiao Lanshu stepped into the factory courtyard, she noticed that a lot of people were staring at her.","There was something off about their gazes. They looked at her with strange expressions, and some were even whispering among themselves, occasionally stealing pointed glances at her stomach."]},{"number":124,"title":"Chapter 124: Big-Character Poster","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu felt that the gazes and whispers of these people were quite off.","Although she usually ran into many colleagues during her commute, she rarely interacted with strangers, and she had only been working at the factory for a few months, which was not a long time.","Furthermore, she stayed alone in her room over at the warehouse. The only people she dealt with were the salespeople from the business department or the transport fleet crew.","Therefore, she wasn't familiar with the regular workers of the food factory, let alone had anything to talk about with them.","Being stared at and gossiped about by so many people was indeed a first for her.","Qiao Lanshu walked into the food factory with a calm expression.","Having lived two lifetimes, her state of mind was actually very stable.","Other people's stares and words could not hurt her.","The food factory manager was Qin Yuanzheng's cousin, and she also knew Wang Xue, Deng Weijun, and a few others. At worst, she could just go ask them what was going on later.","However, Qiao Lanshu soon found out what was happening.","When she passed by the bulletin board in the factory courtyard, she saw a large crowd gathered around it, as if there was some big news today.","In this era, individuals couldn't just go buy newspapers to read. Newspapers were delivered directly to the workplace, and then posted on the bulletin board by the management for everyone to see.","New newspapers were posted on the factory's bulletin board every day. When the workers had free time during their commute, they would go take a look.","Qiao Lanshu rarely went over to look, because Qin Yuanzheng often brought newspapers and various magazines home for her to read.","After all, he knew she loved to read.","But today, Qiao Lanshu watched as those people gathered in front of the bulletin board, gossiping animatedly: \"I knew she got in through the backdoor, but I didn't expect it was this kind of backdoor! I was wondering how she became a permanent employee so quickly. It's only been a few months!\"","\"Oh my, compared to her pregnancy, becoming a permanent employee is nothing to even mention. Tsk, tsk, tsk. With her cheating like this, does her military officer husband really have no objections?\"","\"Are you stupid? It must be to borrow some seed! Isn't that man infertile? Finding someone to borrow a seed from to have a son...\"","\"Oh, if you put it that way, I think it shouldn't be Deng Weijun then. It should be our factory manager, right? After all, they are cousins. At least they are related by blood. No matter what, it would still be a child of their own family...\"","...","These people were getting more and more outrageous with their words.","Otherwise, why would Qiao Lanshu always say that she was most afraid of people gossiping behind her back?","Look at these people; they could really spout any kind of nonsense.","At this moment, Deng Weijun popped out from who knows where and shouted loudly, \"Why are you all so free? Do you not have any work to do? Gathering here to gossip about others!\"","Deng Weijun wasn't angry about being gossiped about himself; he was angry because Qiao Lanshu was being slandered.","He felt that his life had been saved by Qiao Lanshu, so she was his benefactor.","If anyone dared to gossip about Qiao Lanshu, he naturally couldn't just stand by and listen to it.","Someone saw that it was Deng Weijun and immediately confronted him: \"Deng Weijun, I heard that for the past month or so, you've been running over to the warehouse workshop every morning, helping the warehouse keeper comrade fetch water. Is this true?\"","Deng Weijun said with a dark expression, \"So what if it is? So what if it isn't? Rest assured, even if you cultivated for another eight lifetimes, I still wouldn't fetch water for you.\"","That person: \"...\"","Someone else chimed in with a sarcastic tone, \"Come on, Deng Weijun. We're all men here, who doesn't know what you're really thinking? If there was genuinely nothing going on, would you go fetch water for her every single day? When the previous warehouse keeper was around, how come we never saw you fetching water for her?\"","Deng Weijun was not a smooth talker and simply could not out-argue this crowd.","He could only shout back at the top of his lungs, \"I'll fetch water for whoever I please! Does fetching water for someone mean I must be having an affair with them? I fetch water for Director Liao too, so why don't you say I'm having an affair with Director Liao?\"","Director Liao was the head of the Quality Control Department. He was in his fifties and was known to be incredibly strict during inspections.","Many people wanted to curry favor with him, and Deng Weijun was far from the only one who fetched his water.","Therefore, Deng Weijun pointed his finger straight at one of the men and said, \"I saw you get food for Director Liao the other day. Are you trying to have an affair with Director Liao?\"","\"And you, I saw you give Director Liao hawthorn berries. Are you trying to have an affair with him too?\"","That man immediately shook his head frantically and said, \"Deng Weijun, don't you go dragging innocent people down with you! Are you trying to get me killed?!\"","Was Director Liao someone they could just casually joke about?","The crowd gathered around, making a noisy ruckus.","Deng Weijun pushed his way through the people, walked over aggressively, and said, \"Then stop gossiping behind people's backs. It's an absolute disgrace.\"","As he spoke, he reached out, ready to tear down the big-character poster pasted on the bulletin board.","Just then, Qiao Lanshu called out to stop him. \"Weijun, wait a moment.\"","As soon as Qiao Lanshu spoke, everyone turned their heads and finally noticed her standing not far away.","Some people felt a wave of awkwardness, realizing that the very person they were just gossiping about had heard them.","Others thought of Qiao Lanshu's military officer husband and felt a pang of fear, terrified of potential retaliation.","The group exchanged nervous glances, and someone said to Qiao Lanshu with an awkward smile, \"Comrade Warehouse Keeper, you're here?\"","A few were eager to clear their names. \"Oh my, we didn't say any of those things just now. It's all written on the poster. We were just looking at it, but honestly, we don't even believe it.\"","Qiao Lanshu's expression was slightly cold. She did not bother speaking to these people, but instead walked straight to the front, wanting to see exactly what was written on the poster.","Deng Weijun quickly intervened. \"Sister-in-law, you shouldn't look at this thing. Don't dirty your eyes. You go on to work, and I'll handle this for you.\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head and said, \"Let me see what it says.\"","In this day and age, if someone wanted to report you, they would write a big-character poster and paste it everywhere for the public to see.","Therefore, having your name written on one of these posters was quite a frightening ordeal.","Many people did not care about the truth at all; they just wanted to enjoy the drama and watch a good show.","Then, they would spread the rumors by word of mouth.","Qiao Lanshu looked at the poster. Written in stark black and white, it read:","Qiao Lanshu, the warehouse keeper of the food factory, has an improper lifestyle and engages in promiscuous relationships. Not only did she rely on her family connections to get in through the back door to work at the food factory, but she also used shady, underhanded means to secure the opportunity to become a regular employee, monopolizing a prime position that should have been given to pregnant women or senior workers.","Qiao Lanshu admitted to herself that she was indeed able to enter the food factory because of her family connections.","However, the only reason she was able to become a regular employee was that she had caught the former workshop director reselling the factory's fried dough twists. By exposing his embezzlement, she had saved the food factory tens of thousands of yuan in losses.","That was the sole reason she had earned her official status.","Furthermore, the accusations written on the big-character poster about illicit affairs and underhanded tactics were nothing but pure slander.","Deng Weijun said angrily, \"Sister-in-law, I'm going to tear this down. Please don't take it to heart. The innocent have nothing to hide.\""]},{"number":125,"title":"Chapter 125: I have to be investigated too, right","paragraphs":["Deng Weijun was truly furious. He never expected someone to spread malicious rumors about Qiao Lanshu, especially dragging Factory Manager Yang Wenyan and himself into it.","Recently, Deng Weijun had just been set up on a blind date with Wang Haitang, and the two were currently in the phase of getting to know each other.","He felt things were going well and was thinking about making it official before the New Year, so he could take his future wife home to visit his parents during the holidays.","But now, someone was actually spreading rumors that he fetched water for Qiao Lanshu every day because they had an improper relationship.","Deng Weijun was so angry that his brain was practically smoking.","He stepped forward, ready to tear down that big-character poster.","However, he was stopped by Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu held down Deng Weijun's arm and said, Weijun, do not tear it down. Just let it stay there.","Deng Weijun was shocked. He looked at Qiao Lanshu and said, Sister-in-law, why keep this piece of nonsense?","He would even think it too rough to wipe his behind with if he tore it down for toilet paper.","Qiao Lanshu looked at the people gathered around and slightly raised her voice, It seems everyone still has doubts about my transition to becoming a regular worker. I thought after Director Wei was sentenced for embezzlement, everyone knew the reason behind my promotion. Since you do not know, I will explain it to everyone right here.","The reason I could become a regular worker is that when I was transferred from the pickle workshop to help in the warehouse, I noticed the chaotic inventory data and the missing fried dough twists. This led to finding evidence of Director Wei's embezzlement, recovering tens of thousands of yuan in losses for our factory.","Therefore, after a meeting and discussion among the factory manager, the secretary, and the HR chief, they gave me an extra quota for regularization. I did not take up any of the regular quotas for our food factory this year, so you do not need to hold such a big grudge against me.","Changing the subject, Qiao Lanshu added, As for those saying I have improper morals, that is pure slander. I heard that the crime of slander can also result in a labor camp sentence. This big-character poster is the evidence. Let it stay right here as proof. I am going to find the factory manager right now, and we will definitely find out who posted it!","With that, Qiao Lanshu strode away.","Hearing Qiao Lanshu say this, Deng Weijun immediately straightened his back.","As expected of his sister-in-law, she really had guts!","He would not have thought of all this himself.","He immediately pointed at the people around and said, Nobody tear it down! Whoever tears it down is feeling guilty!","The crowd was left speechless.","The crowd stood there, looking at each other in dismay, feeling a bit nervous.","Someone whispered, We were just gossiping a bit, just casually talking. It does not count as slander, right?","Oh, that is hard to say. Forget it, let us stop talking. Anyway, whether she took up a regular quota or not has nothing to do with us regular workers. It is all those temporary workers causing a fuss. Let us just stay out of it.","Hiss, speaking of which, how can this warehouse keeper be so self-righteous? Isn't her husband infertile? She is pregnant, and she isn't feeling guilty at all?","Who knows? Besides, the infertility thing was just a rumor spread by everyone. How would you know if he is capable or not? Why don't you go to the military base and ask?","Do not scare me. Who would dare go to the military base to ask about that? Just say it directly if you want to get me killed.","Talking among themselves, the crowd quickly dispersed.","Deng Weijun followed behind Qiao Lanshu, wanting to say a few words to her, but remembering the contents of the big-character poster, he did not dare get too close.","Right at that moment, Wang Xue, who had just arrived for work, rushed over.","Deng Weijun quickly called out, Sister, you are here too?","Wang Xue hurried over and said to Deng Weijun, Alright, go do your work. I will handle this.","She rolled up her sleeves as she spoke and said to Qiao Lanshu, Xiao Qiao, let us go. I will walk you to the warehouse. I would like to see who dares to wag their tongues!","Looking at Wang Xue like this, Qiao Lanshu felt a bit touched.","She said, Sister, no rush. Let us go to the factory manager's office first to talk to him about this.","After all, the big-character poster also spread rumors that the child in Qiao Lanshu's belly belonged to Yang Wenyan.","The thoughts in these people's heads were simply unbelievable.","Meanwhile, in Factory Manager Yang Wenyan's office, some female workers were also making a scene.","These female workers were all family dependents working at the factory. Some of them had worked there for a year or two and still had not gotten the chance to become regular workers.","Originally, when they heard that Qiao Lanshu had become a regular worker, many people were dissatisfied.","After all, the quota for becoming a regular worker in the factory was limited each year.","Those who did not perform outstandingly could only keep waiting; some had waited for years.","Qiao Lanshu had only been here for a few months, and she had already become a regular worker. Moreover, she was not promoted from a dependent worker, but from a temporary worker.","This naturally drew jealousy.","Those female workers all came to Yang Wenyan's office. Even Secretary Wen of the factory heard about the matter and hurriedly came over to the office.","The leading female worker was quite smart and did not dare make an issue out of Qiao Lanshu's promotion. She said to Yang Wenyan, Manager Yang, certain female workers in our factory have improper morals and ethical issues. Keeping such people in our factory will ruin the discipline of our food factory. Such people should be criticized in a general assembly, fired, and never hired again.","Another female worker also chimed in, That is right. We all know how strict our factory's requirements for regular employees are. Over the years, it has not been easy for us to become regular workers. Many people lost their qualifications just for saying something unpleasant. Why should someone like her, who engages in improper relationships with men, be allowed to stay in our factory?","The female workers crowded in the office, chattering endlessly, giving Yang Wenyan a headache.","Yang Wenyan had finally been happy all night because of Qiao Lanshu's pregnancy, only to run into this mess today.","He was left speechless.","Secretary Wen had previously gone to the provincial capital for a study meeting and had only returned a few days ago.","He had also seen the big-character poster, but he doubted its contents.","He pushed up his glasses, turned to look at Yang Wenyan, and asked, Lao Yang, what exactly is the background of this warehouse keeper?","Yang Wenyan replied, You know about our factory's Director Wei embezzling the fried dough twists, right?","Secretary Wen nodded. I know about that. This female comrade earned merit because of this incident, which is why she was made a regular worker. Everyone is clear on that. I am talking about her moral conduct.","Those female workers quickly echoed, Yes, Manager, we are not questioning her promotion. We are talking about her moral conduct.","Exactly. It is obvious that her husband is infertile, we all know this. So how did she suddenly get pregnant? Something is fishy here.","Speaking of which, Manager, that Deng Weijun runs over to the warehouse every day, fetching hot water and delivering food to that warehouse keeper. We have seen it many times. We suggest you investigate Deng Weijun thoroughly.","\"It wasn't just Deng Weijun, you know. A while ago, there was another man waiting at the factory gate every day for the warehouse keeper to get off work. Who knows what they went off to do together after her shift?\"","\"That's right, Factory Manager. We aren't trying to stir up trouble on purpose. We are purely doing this for Commander Qin's own good. He probably has no idea what's been going on in our factory and is still completely in the dark.\"","Hearing the crowd say this, Yang Wenyan let out a cold laugh. \"What?\" he said. \"Are you saying my conduct is problematic too? I'm her cousin, and I invite her over to my house for dinner every day. I suppose I need to be investigated as well, right?\"","The female workers exchanged glances. The woman leading the group spoke up, \"Factory Manager, we weren't the ones who said that. It was written on that big-character poster. It has nothing to do with us.\""]},{"number":126,"title":"Chapter 126: Report to the Military for Investigation","paragraphs":["Yang Wenyan, as the factory director, certainly couldn't let this matter continue to escalate.","With a dark expression, he said to the female workers, \"This matter is not for you to manage. If anyone is to manage it, it should be the military. It's their family affair; is it your place to stick your necks out?\"","One of the female workers said sarcastically, \"Director, what we are talking about is her moral problem. We don't care about their family affairs. Are you trying to make excuses for her? If you ask me, a person like this should be fired, and her position should be reassigned.\"","After all the talk, these people were still just thinking about the official worker position.","Squeezing out one person meant one more position, which meant one more opportunity for them, didn't it?","At this moment, Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue walked in.","The crowd looked at Qiao Lanshu, exchanged glances, and entirely fell silent.","Yang Wenyan looked at Qiao Lanshu and said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, why are you here?\"","Secretary Wen had also heard about Qiao Lanshu's pregnancy and originally wanted to congratulate her.","Now, he didn't dare to say it.","Secretary Wen looked at Qiao Lanshu; she was young, not very tall, and quite pretty, looking almost like a child.","A girl like this seemed well brought up, not like someone who would engage in illicit affairs.","He said to Qiao Lanshu, \"We will hold a meeting to discuss the matter of the big-character poster. You should go back to work first, alright?\"","Anyway, Qiao Lanshu had a military officer husband. No matter how the factory decided to handle this matter, they would still have to notify the military and see how the military would approve it.","Qiao Lanshu looked at the female workers present and said calmly, \"Director, Secretary Wen, I haven't been in the factory for long. During this time, I believe I haven't offended anyone. Being suddenly targeted today, I am also very surprised. I'm worried if the other party might be targeting my family member?\"","The crowd: \"???\"","Wang Xue had come together with Qiao Lanshu. Hearing Qiao Lanshu say this, she gasped, rubbed her chin, and said, \"Oh my, ever since I heard about the explosives being stolen from the construction site last time, I've been pondering this. Director Yang, Secretary Wen, the espionage warfare has become increasingly intense these past few years. Do you think our place might have already been infiltrated by enemy agents?\"","The more Wang Xue spoke, the more she felt it made sense: \"Commander Qin is responsible for managing the mining area, transporting coal, and building roads. These are all key provincial projects! Their military base is heavily guarded like an iron bucket, so if the agents want to attack Commander Qin, they have no choice but to turn around and deal with Comrade Xiao Qiao instead. Tell me, am I right?\"","The crowd: \"...\"","Secretary Wen rubbed his chin, his expression turning serious. \"Comrade Wang Xue makes sense. It seems the matter behind this big-character poster is not simple. Lao Yang, why didn't we think of this?\"","Yang Wenyan also started to worry. \"Every worker in our factory has had their identity verified. It shouldn't be to that extent, right?\"","If their factory had really been infiltrated, it would be terrifying.","Yang Wenyan wouldn't even be able to keep his job as the factory director.","Wang Xue said, \"Why wouldn't it be? If someone could steal the explosives from the construction site, what's so hard about coming to our food factory to put up a big-character poster?\"","Hearing this, the leading female worker couldn't help but say, \"Wang Xue, stop saying these things to scare people. It's just a big-character poster, and it can't affect a military officer anyway. How did it suddenly involve spies and agents?\"","Wang Xue immediately retorted, \"You say it has no effect, so it has no effect? Comrade Xiao Qiao's reputation has been ruined by you all, and you still dare to say it has no effect? Wait a minute, why do you have so much to say? Did you put up this big-character poster?\"","As soon as Wang Xue said this, Secretary Wen and Yang Wenyan's eyes fixed on that female worker.","The female worker jumped in fright and quickly said, \"Don't spit blood on people! Where would I find the time to do this? Besides, do I look like that kind of person?\"","Secretary Wen also couldn't help but scold her: \"Since you didn't put it up, why are you acting as the bird that sticks its head out? Among so many people, you talk the most. Later, when the military investigates, you'll be the first one taken in for questioning.\"","The female worker was indeed frightened. Not only her, but the other female workers also became a bit scared.","They were just dissatisfied that Qiao Lanshu was converted from a temporary worker to an official worker.","After all, they wanted to become official workers themselves but couldn't.","So they thought about taking the opportunity to make a fuss, hoping they could squeeze Qiao Lanshu out and free up a quota for an official worker.","Then they could fight for the chance, right?","Now, scared by Secretary Wen and Wang Xue, they immediately wanted to leave: \"I didn't put up the big-character poster. You definitely shouldn't come question me. I don't know anything.\"","\"That's right, when we came to work, the big-character poster was already up there. We don't know who put it up either.\"","Hearing them say this, Qiao Lanshu said to Yang Wenyan:","\"Director, I request a strict investigation into the person who put up the big-character poster. This person fabricated facts and maliciously slandered the reputations of me and Commander Qin. This matter cannot be let go lightly. You must know that once this matter blows up, it will have a huge impact on Commander Qin, the mining area, and even the military. The person behind this harbors ulterior motives, and their true identity is highly suspicious. Once caught, they must be severely punished.\"","Qiao Lanshu was deliberately using the names of Qin Yuanzheng and the mining area to make the matter sound very serious.","Because she knew that the current factory leaders were afraid of causing trouble, and even more afraid of things blowing up.","Based on the principle that less trouble is better than more trouble, whether it was Yang Wenyan or Secretary Wen, their final solution might just be to tear down the big-character poster, stop the crowd from discussing it, and then criticize the person who put it up during a general meeting.","In private, they would pacify Qiao Lanshu, and the matter would be over.","Wasn't Deng Weijun's first reaction just to tear down the big-character poster?","Qiao Lanshu couldn't let this matter pass easily.","She wanted to blow it up, drag out the person who put up the big-character poster, and have them accept punishment.","Otherwise, even if people didn't dare to say it to her face, they would talk behind her back about her poor lifestyle and illicit affairs.","Why should she have to endure this?","Secretary Wen and Director Yang exchanged a glance, both of their faces very serious.","Secretary Wen said, \"If this matter really involves spies, then we must report it to the military for investigation.\"","Saying that, he turned to Yang Wenyan, \"Lao Yang, we can't bear this responsibility.\""]},{"number":127,"title":"Chapter 127: How could it turn out so fancy","paragraphs":["Yang Wenyan had originally intended to take extra care of Qiao Lanshu anyway.","Not to mention, this matter also involved Qin Yuanzheng and himself.","As the factory director, this was the first time he had been the subject of such rumors, and with his own brother-in-law's wife, no less.","Who could tolerate this!","Now that Secretary Wen had also spoken up, he immediately nodded:","\"This matter definitely needs to be thoroughly investigated. Some people dare to put up big-character posters without distinguishing right from wrong, recklessly slandering a female comrade's moral character and causing a huge impact on her reputation! If this isn't thoroughly investigated, wouldn't anyone be able to randomly post big-character posters in the future?\"","Secretary Wen didn't dare offend the military officers. Plus, during his recent study trip to the provincial capital, he had indeed heard that certain important departments had been infiltrated by spies. A crisis had even erupted recently where classified documents from a certain department were transferred away.","There was even a dam under construction that was almost blown up.","The situation was extremely serious.","Therefore, when Yang Wenyan said this, he also immediately said sternly, \"Yes, this matter must be thoroughly investigated.\"","As he spoke, Secretary Wen's gaze swept over the surrounding female workers one by one.","The female workers looked baffled under his stare.","They quickly distanced themselves, saying, \"Secretary Wen, why are you staring at us like that? We weren't the ones who put up that big-character poster.\"","\"Exactly, exactly. We still have to get back to work, so we'll be leaving now.\"","With that, the workers quickly turned and ran off.","The crowded office instantly emptied out.","Qiao Lanshu also said to Yang Wenyan, \"Director, it's getting late. I should head back to my post to work as well.\"","Yang Wenyan nodded and comforted her, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, just rest assured. We will definitely investigate this matter thoroughly and issue a public notice to clarify things.\"","Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue then left the office too.","Wang Xue linked arms with Qiao Lanshu and lowered her voice to tell her, \"If you ask me, this was definitely done by those family-dependent workers. They're just jealous that you became a regular employee. They couldn't find an opportunity before, and now they finally have one...\"","At this point, Wang Xue suddenly paused, as if she had just realized something. She stopped walking, held onto Qiao Lanshu's arm, and looked at Qiao Lanshu's stomach.","It made Qiao Lanshu feel quite embarrassed.","After looking for a moment, Wang Xue lowered her voice and asked, \"Are you really pregnant?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded shyly. \"Yes, it's true.\"","Wang Xue's eyes instantly widened. She clicked her tongue and whispered, \"Well, this was completely unexpected!\"","Wang Xue was very happy for Qiao Lanshu.","At the same time, she felt quite emotional and whispered, \"Now that the news of your pregnancy has spread, I bet a lot of people behind the scenes are regretting it so much their intestines are turning green. There were quite a few female comrades who went on blind dates with Regiment Commander Qin back then. And some people, upon hearing he was infertile, directly refused to even meet him.\"","Setting aside the ones Qin Yuanzheng himself didn't fancy, many female comrades had actually rejected him through matchmakers.","There were also some daughters of military officers who originally had their eyes on Qin Yuanzheng, and some who even chased after him, but they were all scared off because of the infertility issue.","Well, look at how things are now.","Qin Yuanzheng wasn't infertile at all. The moment he got married, his wife got pregnant.","Wang Xue smiled and said, \"The news of your pregnancy hits harder than a slap to the face. I wonder what those girls who rejected Regiment Commander Qin are thinking now?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"I didn't expect to get pregnant either.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had always believed he couldn't have children, so he never used any protection during those intimate moments.","Having finally tasted the pleasures of the flesh, the man was all over her every single day.","If he had known she could get pregnant, Qin Yuanzheng definitely wouldn't have let it happen so soon.","This time was truly the most unexpected of accidents.","Wang Xue asked again, \"Have you written to your family yet? Pregnancy is a joyous occasion. Tell your family so they can be happy too.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded.","Ever since he found out she had gotten married to a regiment commander, Father Qiao hadn't believed it at first.","It was only after Qin Yuanzheng sent him a telegram from the military base that Father Qiao confirmed it was indeed from someone in the army.","Once his mind was at ease, Father Qiao would occasionally send her things. If she wrote a letter, he would also reply quickly.","Thinking about it, it had been a month since Qiao Lanshu last sent a letter to her father.","She pondered that she should write a letter to her father today and send some walnuts back while she was at it.","Wang Xue accompanied Qiao Lanshu to the food factory's warehouse. She said, \"Don't take the big-character poster thing to heart. Since the director and the secretary both said they're going to investigate, they'll definitely find out the truth. Just relax.\"","Qiao Lanshu actually wasn't worried. Compared to the previous incident with Chu Liangjun, she didn't care about this kind of big-character poster at all.","She nodded. \"I know. Thank you, Sister. Don't worry, I'm fine.\"","Wang Xue sighed and said, \"Aren't I just worried you might disturb the fetus? You're only a little over two months along. Generally speaking, it's only considered stable after three months.\"","As Wang Xue spoke, the two of them arrived at the small hut by the warehouse entrance. Wang Xue still had to work, so she bid Qiao Lanshu farewell.","Deng Weijun didn't dare to come fetch water for Qiao Lanshu anymore either.","He felt that he was the one who caused people to gossip about Qiao Lanshu, and he felt very guilty about it.","He didn't dare to come near her side anymore.","Thus, Qiao Lanshu took her thermos and went to the boiler room to fetch hot water herself.","When she arrived at the boiler room, there were quite a few people fetching water.","When everyone saw Qiao Lanshu approaching, they all looked at her with strange expressions.","Qiao Lanshu ignored these gazes. When it was her turn, she went ahead and filled her thermos with hot water.","At this moment, Liu Weihong came over with two thermoses to fetch water.","Liu Weihong was finally not wearing her cashmere coat today. After all, it had gotten genuinely colder over the past few days. No matter how much she wanted to show off, she was afraid of freezing herself.","Liu Weihong was wearing a newly made army-green padded jacket and fleece-lined leather boots on her feet. They looked like deerskin boots, which probably weren't cheap.","This Liu Weihong used to dress quite ordinarily. But ever since she found a boyfriend, she suddenly looked like a newly rich upstart.","Qiao Lanshu had already seen three different scarves wrapped around her neck. In a time when cotton and fabric were so precious, she bought these things as if they cost no money at all.","Qiao Lanshu was considered someone who wasn't overly frugal, yet she only had two scarves.","One she bought when she first arrived, and the other was bought for her by Qin Yuanzheng.","Alternating between the two was enough, so there was no need to buy more.","Liu Weihong loved showing off these things. She enjoyed basking in the flattery of others, and she had been living quite comfortably lately.","But early this morning, right after she got to work, many people ran over to tell her, \"Supervisor Liu, Regiment Commander Qin's wife is pregnant. Did you know about this?\"","These people were all intentionally coming to laugh at Liu Weihong.","Who asked Liu Weihong to go around broadcasting that Qin Yuanzheng was infertile after her blind date with Regiment Commander Qin failed back then?","Originally, not many people knew about Qin Yuanzheng's infertility at the time. The fact that it later spread until the entire factory area knew was all thanks to Liu Weihong.","Liu Weihong had not only spread rumors about Qin Yuanzheng being infertile, but even claimed he was inadequate in bed.","In short, karma had just slapped her hard in the face.","Everyone was laughing at her now.","Someone mocked her, \"If only you had managed to marry Regiment Commander Qin back then, wouldn't that have been wonderful? What a pity you just didn't have that kind of luck.\"","Others blamed her, \"Liu Weihong, you were the one who leaked the news about Regiment Commander Qin's infertility. Were you lying to us all along? You just couldn't stand to see us do well, could you? You were terrified we'd marry Regiment Commander Qin and live a good life, so you made that up to stop us from going on blind dates with him! I knew it, you have a wicked heart!\"","Liu Weihong had already gotten into several arguments first thing in the morning.","She was seething with pent-up rage.","She had actually found out the night before that Regiment Commander Qin's wife was pregnant.","After all, the news had spread throughout the military base. The people in the army hadn't deliberately kept it a secret; it wasn't exactly classified military intelligence anyway.","Liu Weihong had been so consumed by spite that she hadn't slept a wink all night.","Coming into work early this morning, she had been subjected to even more grievances.","So, seeing Qiao Lanshu now, she naturally didn't have a pleasant expression.","Holding two thermos flasks, Liu Weihong looked at Qiao Lanshu and said sarcastically, \"Well, well, if it isn't our comrade warehouse keeper. Why are you fetching your own water today? Didn't you call your man to help you? If you ask me, you shouldn't be doing this kind of heavy lifting yourself. You wouldn't want to destabilize your pregnancy. If you miscarry, it'll be a real hassle, you'll have to borrow a man all over again...\"","She paused deliberately and smiled sweetly, \"Oh my, I'm so sorry. I accidentally misspoke. Please don't take it to heart.\"","Qiao Lanshu gave her a cold glance, didn't say a word, and walked away with her thermos.","Liu Weihong was left speechless.","It felt exactly like punching a pile of cotton, leaving Liu Weihong thoroughly frustrated.","She had been holding in a stomach full of anger since last night and was itching for a good shouting match with Qiao Lanshu.","Wasn't Qiao Lanshu supposed to have a sharp tongue?","Why wasn't she saying anything now?","Liu Weihong immediately slammed her two thermoses down on the windowsill and followed Qiao Lanshu out. \"I say, Qiao Lanshu, why aren't you saying anything? Could it be that I hit the nail on the head? My goodness, I really couldn't tell. You look so pure and innocent, but who knew you were playing the field so wildly?\"","Since it was early in the morning, there were quite a few workers at the boiler room getting hot water.","Liu Weihong's words were heard by everyone around them.","However, the crowd had also heard what Qiao Lanshu said in front of the bulletin board earlier that morning.","Everyone was being cautious now, not daring to gossip about Qiao Lanshu.","A group of people just stood by, watching the drama unfold.","Qiao Lanshu carried her thermos a few steps but simply couldn't tolerate Liu Weihong's incessant squawking any longer.","She stopped, looked at Liu Weihong, and said with a polite smile:","\"Supervisor Liu, I know you're very bitter that you couldn't marry Regiment Commander Qin, but it can't be helped. A blind date requires mutual interest. Regiment Commander Qin happens to like gentle girls. You are so fierce, domineering, and love to gossip about others. You fight with people every single day. Let alone Regiment Commander Qin, even the male workers in our factory would find it very hard to fall for you.\"","Liu Weihong was stunned into silence.","She was absolutely flabbergasted. Listen to what Qiao Lanshu was saying!","Other people would at most think these things in their heads, but Qiao Lanshu actually had the nerve to say them out loud?","A few male workers watching the commotion nearby couldn't help but nod in agreement.","Liu Weihong was incredibly arrogant and looked down on the factory workers, little knowing that the factory workers also looked down on her.","Very few men could actually tolerate such a domineering personality.","Liu Weihong gritted her teeth in fury. \"What kind of nonsense are you spouting? I was the one who didn't fancy Qin Yuanzheng back then! It wasn't that he didn't fancy me. You'd better get your facts straight.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled again:","\"I understand, I completely understand. As an unmarried woman and a supervisor at the food factory, you have your pride to maintain. It's normal for you to say that. But you'd better not say things like that in the future. Otherwise, if you offend the military officers, those lovers of yours might get scared and not dare to associate with you anymore. Then wouldn't you be left with no one to buy you wool coats, leather shoes, and watches?\"","Hearing this, Liu Weihong immediately snapped back, \"Bullshit! Do you think everyone is afraid of military officers? My partner is in the Supply...\"","As soon as the words left her mouth, she hurriedly covered it. Oh no, she had almost been tricked into confessing by Qiao Lanshu.","Her partner had strictly warned her not to reveal his identity!","Qiao Lanshu narrowed her eyes, staring intently at Liu Weihong. \"Who is your partner? Supply? He wouldn't happen to be from the Supply Section, would he?\"","Qiao Lanshu then turned to the people around her and asked, \"I don't quite understand, so I wanted to ask everyone. How many Supply Sections are there in our city? Is the Section Chief of the Supply Section the highest-ranking administrator there? How much is his monthly salary? Can he afford to buy cashmere coats, watches, and leather shoes?\"","In this day and age, a regimental-level cadre's monthly salary was only a little over a hundred yuan. That amount could buy a watch at most.","Things like wool coats and leather shoes would have to be bought separately over the course of several months.","To take out so much money to buy all these things at once, one would probably have to save up for years.","After all, apart from saving money, one also had to save up the necessary ration coupons.","Liu Weihong's partner had only just started dating her; they hadn't even gotten their marriage certificate yet.","Was he really so generous that he was willing to spend all his life savings to buy her these luxury items?","Qiao Lanshu felt that something wasn't quite right.","That was exactly why she had deliberately baited Liu Weihong just now, to see if she could trick her into slipping up.","As it turned out, she had very nearly succeeded.","Hearing Qiao Lanshu's probing questions, Liu Weihong instantly began to panic.","She quickly denied it, \"Don't spout nonsense, I don't know anyone from the Supply Section.\"","Saying this, she hurriedly turned back to fetch her water. \"God is watching what people do! Qiao Lanshu, you know very well in your own heart how you managed to get pregnant! You will get your retribution sooner or later.\"","With that, she quickly turned around, intending to head into the boiler room. However, seeing the large crowd of people gathered around, she decided to forgo the hot water entirely, spun on her heel, and marched away in a fluster.","A worker watching the spectacle kindly called out to remind her, \"Supervisor Liu, you haven't even filled your thermoses yet! Why are you running off in such a panic?\"","A few men chuckled at that.","Liu Weihong was so furious she didn't even bother to retrieve her thermos flasks, simply striding away at a brisk pace.","Holding her thermos, Qiao Lanshu ignored the stares of the crowd.","She took her time strolling back to the warehouse workshop.","Sitting down in her little office, she began to organize some receipts. Her job was very leisurely anyway, with not much to do.","She took out the red dates that Qin Yuanzheng had packed for her, grabbed a piece of brown sugar, and dropped them into her mug with hot water from the thermos to steep.","It was a pity she had forgotten to bring some ginger. On such a freezing day, a cup of ginger tea was exactly what she needed to stay warm.","Qiao Lanshu took her cup, poured herself some red date tea, and then pulled out a book to start reading.","By the time the afternoon rolled around, Yang Wenyan sent someone to call her to the office.","They had been investigating all morning, and it seemed they finally had some results.","That was why they needed Qiao Lanshu to head over to the office for a talk."]},{"number":128,"title":"Chapter 128: Fingerprint Extraction","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu came out of the warehouse and walked toward the building where the factory manager's office was located.","Inside Yang Wenyan's office, Secretary Wen was also sitting there. Besides him, the head of the personnel department, as well as the directors and supervisors of other departments, were all present.","Liu Weihong, who had just argued with Qiao Lanshu that morning, was also standing in the crowd.","They had just finished a management meeting.","As soon as Qiao Lanshu entered, she saw the large group of people. She walked in without changing her expression, \"Factory Manager, you were looking for me?\"","Yang Wenyan nodded, his expression complex as he said, \"Xiao Qiao, we've already had someone investigate the big-character poster incident. Preliminary estimates suggest the poster was put up late last night, but we haven't figured out exactly who did it yet.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Hearing this result, Qiao Lanshu wasn't terribly disappointed.","She had anticipated this outcome long ago.","Since the other party dared to do something that smeared someone's innocence, they must have taken measures to stay hidden.","It was impossible for them to be seen.","It was the dead of winter right now. The wind was strong and freezing in the middle of the night, so basically no one went out.","There was a guard on duty in the food factory's guardhouse, but the guard was old, and it was cold at midnight, so he couldn't keep an eye on the factory at all times.","Plus, in this day and age, there were basically no thieves. After all, the Revolutionary Committee was right in the city; who would be reckless enough to risk their lives stealing from the food factory?","With the lax security and low walls, it was actually quite easy for someone to climb in and put up a big-character poster.","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"I understand. Then, Factory Manager, what are we going to do next?\"","Qiao Lanshu continued, \"Are we going to the public security bureau to report the case, or going to the military to find someone? Or perhaps to the Revolutionary Committee?\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Secretary Wen hurriedly said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, let's not get agitated. The factory will definitely give you an explanation for this matter. Let's not report it to the police first; it would have a bad impact on our factory.\"","Qiao Lanshu only held off on reporting the case out of respect for Yang Wenyan.","Otherwise, the moment she saw the big-character poster, she would have run to the public security bureau to report it. Why would she wait until now?","Yang Wenyan was quite unlucky. Being a factory manager was busy enough, but the factory workers kept getting into trouble every few days.","However, on second thought, Yang Wenyan felt that these big-character posters were relatively minor issues.","He had heard that other work units in the province even had spies infiltrating them. Those section chiefs and directors were not only stripped of their positions but also faced labor reform.","Yang Wenyan felt he had let Qiao Lanshu down.","After getting off work, he would have to go explain things to Qin Yuanzheng, lest Qin Yuanzheng blame him.","Yang Wenyan said with a solemn expression, \"I've already had the broadcaster announce that the person who put up the big-character poster should turn themselves in, and we will deal with them leniently. Otherwise, we will have the military intervene tomorrow. If they are dragged out then, the situation will be much more serious.\"","The head of the personnel department also chimed in, \"Yes, all workshop supervisors should also go back and tell the workers in their workshops about this. If our factory handles this matter, it will just be a slight pay cut at most. But if the military takes over, it will be considered slandering a military officer, and I have no idea how that will be punished.\"","In this day and age, regular workers were generally not easily fired. If the person stepped forward now and admitted to it, they could actually keep their job.","Hearing this, the workshop supervisors nodded one after another, indicating they would go back and talk to the workers in their workshops.","While everyone was discussing animatedly, someone muttered, \"If they can't find the person, what does it matter if the military comes? They just use military officers to scare people.\"","Qiao Lanshu was close by and heard it. Liu Weihong had deliberately said this for her to hear.","She turned her head to look and, sure enough, saw Liu Weihong rolling her eyes at her.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Didn't you know? The military has special investigation methods. As long as the person who put up the big-character poster wasn't wearing gloves, the military has a way to extract their fingerprints from the poster. When the time comes, they will ask all the employees of our food factory to compare fingerprints. Whoever doesn't show up is feeling guilty, and they can be arrested and interrogated.\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Without anyone noticing, Liu Weihong's face grew slightly tense.","Secretary Wen slapped his forehead and said in shock, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, you even know how to extract fingerprints?\"","Qiao Lanshu wasn't entirely sure of the exact process, but if one had the heart to learn, it was definitely something that could be learned.","After all, she had read about it in a book when she was in high school in Yangcheng.","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"This method of extracting fingerprints isn't difficult, but it requires some tools, making it hard to do today. After I get off work, I'll have my family prepare it, and tomorrow we'll have the military come over to extract them.\"","Yang Wenyan sighed in admiration, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, you really live up to your reputation. You are so smart. Since we have this method, we don't need to investigate anymore. Tomorrow, we'll just have everyone compare their fingerprints!\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and added, \"However, workshop supervisors, please still pass this message along, so no one takes a leave of absence and delays the investigation.\"","Yang Wenyan immediately said, \"Right! We'll do just that!\"","Since the factory manager and secretary both agreed, the others naturally had no objections.","However, everyone returned to their workshops with their own thoughts, feeling deeply worried.","Everyone was worried that the person who put up the big-character poster might be a worker from their own workshop.","After all, the year-end evaluations were just around the corner.","The supervisors had worked diligently and tirelessly all year—wasn't it all just to be evaluated as a model worker, a 'Five-Good' worker, or an outstanding employee at the end of the year?","If the workers in their workshops caused any trouble, all of those chances would be gone.","After everyone in the office had dispersed.","Qiao Lanshu walked up to Yang Wenyan and whispered, \"Factory Manager, I have something to tell you.\"","Yang Wenyan couldn't be happier that Qiao Lanshu had thought of such a great method like fingerprint verification.","As long as they caught the person who put up the poster, this matter could be resolved promptly.","The New Year was approaching, and he wanted to rest peacefully for a couple of days.","He stood up and asked, \"What is it?\"","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice and whispered a few words in his ear.","The more Yang Wenyan listened, the more serious he became.","He lowered his voice and asked, \"Didn't we say we were going to extract fingerprints and have all the factory workers verify them? What's wrong, are we not doing that anymore?\"","There was no one else in the office now, just the two of them, but the office door was open, so Qiao Lanshu kept her voice very low.","She said, \"That is the clumsiest method. If the method I just mentioned doesn't work, it won't be too late to use the fingerprint extraction method.\"","Extracting fingerprints wasn't hard; the hard part was verifying and questioning the hundreds of workers in the factory one by one.","After all, there were no machines to do this work for them, so it was indeed a massive workload.","Furthermore, if the person wasn't from the food factory but an outsider, they would be even harder to find.","If there was a simpler method, they certainly wouldn't need to waste so much manpower and resources.","After all, it was just a big-character poster. Qiao Lanshu didn't want to blow things out of proportion and waste the time and energy of the military personnel.","After listening to what Qiao Lanshu had to say, Yang Wenyan lowered his voice and said, \"I understand what you mean. Don't worry, I will personally bring my men to keep watch at the factory tonight!\""]},{"number":129,"title":"Chapter 129: I know exactly what he's like.","paragraphs":["After Qiao Lanshu and Yang Wenyan came to an agreement, she reminded him, \"Cousin, don't let anyone else hear about this. If word gets out, it won't work.\"","Yang Wenyan nodded. \"Xiao Qiao, don't worry, I know what I'm doing.\"","This time, he had to catch that person himself. He wanted to see who had so much free time on their hands to write a big-character poster behind someone's back, smearing a female comrade's innocence and slandering a military officer's family member.","They must have a death wish.","After Qiao Lanshu left the factory director's office, she heard people discussing the fingerprint extraction all along the way.","Many people didn't know how fingerprints were extracted.","But just hearing that the military had a way to do it, surprisingly, no one doubted it.","Because the soldiers in the military were just that formidable.","Even more formidable than the public security officers. After all, the current Public Security Bureau had fewer than five people in total, and one of them was just an old gatekeeper.","Some people who had seen the poster in the morning and gossiped about Qiao Lanshu were whispering, \"Oh my, I was so close to that poster at the time. They won't extract my fingerprints, will they? I wasn't the one who put it up!\"","Someone asked her, \"Let me ask you, did you touch the poster?\"","\"Oh, I pointed at the big characters with my finger, does that count?\"","\"Of course that doesn't count. They are extracting the fingerprints of the person who pasted it, which would definitely be on the four corners and the four edges of the poster. When pasting it, wouldn't you have to stick the four corners first?\"","There were quite a few people discussing it.","Qiao Lanshu could hear people talking about it around the pantry and the restroom.","Now it was great. No one was talking about Qiao Lanshu being exceptionally made a regular worker, nor was anyone discussing how the child in her belly came to be.","Everyone was talking about how the military personnel were coming tomorrow to extract and compare fingerprints to catch the culprit.","After listening for a while, Qiao Lanshu went back to work, feeling satisfied.","In the afternoon, driver Du Erniu from the motor pool came over. He brought people to pick up goods, and Qiao Lanshu opened the door for him.","After Du Erniu finished loading the goods and was about to leave, he suddenly brought over a bag of red dates and placed it on Qiao Lanshu's windowsill. He said to her, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, don't listen to those gossiping women spouting nonsense. They just have too much free time. Don't take it to heart, alright?\"","Driver Du found Qiao Lanshu very pleasing to the eye now.","He felt she was meticulous in her work, sweet-talking, and beautiful.","With such a pretty little wife, her man at home must dote on her endlessly. Borrowing seed? Only those people could come up with such a ridiculous idea.","Qiao Lanshu did not refuse this kindness. She took the red dates and smiled, \"Thank you, Master Du. That's very thoughtful of you.\"","Saying that, she took an apple from her drawer and handed it to Du Erniu. \"Master Du, take this apple back to eat. It's very sweet.\"","How could Du Erniu accept it? He waved his hands and said, \"No need, no need, keep it for yourself. My red dates aren't worth much, they were grown back in my hometown. You eat them, and if you like them, I'll bring you some more next time.\"","With that, Du Erniu hurried away.","He didn't take Qiao Lanshu's apple.","Du Erniu probably heard a lot of gossip about Qiao Lanshu and was afraid she would feel bad, so he specifically came to comfort her.","Qiao Lanshu silently praised him in her heart; Master Du was truly a kind-hearted and good comrade.","It was a pity she couldn't say it out loud because Du Erniu had already left in a hurry.","Deng Weijun didn't dare walk toward the warehouse all day today.","Gossip is a fearful thing, and he was truly scared of those people who loved to wag their tongues.","If Commander Qin found out that others thought his wife's child belonged to Deng Weijun, how could Deng Weijun even survive?","Before Qiao Lanshu even got off work, Qin Yuanzheng was already waiting in his car at the main gate of the food factory.","He used to be very busy with official duties, and the command headquarters would call him over for matters big and small, requiring him to attend meetings from time to time.","And he had no way to decline.","Now it was great. His wife was pregnant, so he could openly push his tasks onto others.","Commander Li also didn't assign him much work anymore.","Everyone tacitly agreed to let him go home early to help his little wife rest and nourish her pregnancy.","As the workers of the food factory gradually came out after work, Qin Yuanzheng noticed that the way many people looked at him was a bit off.","Being a soldier, he was still very sensitive to these gazes and expressions.","The way those people looked at him was a bit strange, but mostly it was fear.","Qin Yuanzheng pondered it in his heart for a moment, but he soon couldn't be bothered to think about it anymore.","Because his wife came out.","His lovely little wife, wearing a military-green padded jacket, wrapped in a red scarf, with a delicate little face and two small dimples when she smiled, was already waving at him.","Qin Yuanzheng strode forward, took off his cloak, draped it over Qiao Lanshu's shoulders, and wrapped his arm around her, pulling her into his embrace.","The more he looked at this beautiful little wife, the more he liked her.","They had been married for several months now, and his love for Comrade Xiao Qiao had not diminished at all; instead, it had grown even stronger.","Qiao Lanshu blushed and pushed him lightly. \"Mind the impact, people are watching.\"","It was exactly the time when the food factory got off work, and there were quite a few workers around. It would be so embarrassing if people saw them.","Qiao Lanshu had lost count of how many times she had reminded Qin Yuanzheng, but he always loved to hold her hand and embrace her in public.","He didn't care about other people's stares at all.","The people around the food factory exchanged meaningful glances.","Look at their relationship, how loving they are.","And someone actually claimed Qiao Lanshu was having an affair with another man?","Commander Qin watched his little wife all day like she was the apple of his eye. Even if Qiao Lanshu had such thoughts, she wouldn't even have the time!","Sure enough, the person who put up the big-character poster was purely jealous of Comrade Xiao Qiao and wanted to use some of the unregularized family workers as pawns!","It was truly too sinister.","Qin Yuanzheng opened the car door for Qiao Lanshu, and after letting her sit properly inside.","He then got into the driver's seat next to her.","Qin Yuanzheng had been in no mood to work today. He had sought out his comrades who were already fathers to learn some knowledge about pregnancy and childbirth.","Of course, he also went looking for books, though he hadn't found any yet.","After getting into the car, he reached out and pinched Qiao Lanshu's cheek, leaning close to whisper to her, \"Are you feeling swollen here?\"","As he spoke, he gently squeezed with his hand.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly swatted his hand away, blushing as she said, \"Brother Zheng, what are you doing? We're still outside.\"","Qin Yuanzheng said seriously, \"No one can see inside the car. Have you started feeling swollen and sore these past few days, but were too embarrassed to tell me?\"","Qiao Lanshu glared at him, a bit embarrassed. \"Why are you asking this?\"","Qin Yuanzheng lowered his voice, leaning into her ear and saying, \"I want to drink *, didn't I tell you that a long time ago?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu suspected he was acting like a hooligan.","She was indeed feeling uncomfortably swollen. The main issue was that the thermal vest that used to fit well now felt a bit tight over the past two days.","She felt that the change was indeed quite drastic, but she didn't mention it to Qin Yuanzheng.","She knew exactly what he was like. If she told him, he would probably just end up tormenting her again."]},{"number":130,"title":"Chapter 130: I Will Examine Your Body","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng didn't feel like he was tormenting his wife; he was caring for her!","As he drove, he said to Qiao Lanshu, \"I made a special effort to learn about this today. The first three months of pregnancy can be uncomfortable. I'll give you a massage when we get back, and you'll feel much better.\"","Continuing, Qin Yuanzheng added, \"By the way, in another two months, you probably won't be able to fit into your pants anymore, right? Shouldn't we make some new ones?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. \"No need, I just need to replace my waistbands with longer strings.\"","Her pants all had sewn-in waistbands. When her belly was small, she could tie them tight, and when it got bigger, she could just tie them a bit looser.","There weren't many cotton or fabric ration coupons left at home. Qiao Lanshu planned to save them up to make spring clothes when the season turned. After all, she hadn't been here for long, and none of the clothes she brought from Yangcheng could be worn in this weather.","Thinking about it, it really was better back in Yangcheng. You could wear short sleeves and shorts in spring, summer, and autumn, and just make a small jacket for the winter.","It was nothing like here, where you needed cotton-padded jackets and pants, woolen sweaters and pants, thermal underwear, knitted clothes, and oh right, a warm vest too.","On top of all that, she had to make gloves, hats, scarves, and face masks.","Oh, and even for socks, she had to make three different kinds: one for summer, one for autumn, and one for winter.","More than half of the cotton produced by the motherland had to be supplied to the north, otherwise there really wouldn't be enough to wear.","Qiao Lanshu's mind started to wander again. Since getting pregnant recently, she tired easily, and whenever she was tired, she tended to zone out and let her imagination run wild.","She actually wanted to go back to Yangcheng a little. Although she had spent many years here, counting both her past and present lives, she still missed her hometown.","She also missed her dad a bit.","Seeing her suddenly go quiet again, Qin Yuanzheng asked, \"Wife, what are you thinking about?\"","Qiao Lanshu slowly spoke, \"I was wondering what the weather is like in Yangcheng right now.\"","Qin Yuanzheng smiled and said, \"It's the place you grew up in, you definitely know.\"","Qin Yuanzheng knew that Qiao Lanshu was feeling homesick.","But it was the dead of winter right now, snowing constantly, and trains were frequently suspended. Even if she wanted to go back, there was no way.","Furthermore, Qiao Lanshu was carrying a baby in her belly. Now she absolutely couldn't endure the exhaustion of taking a long-distance train.","Qin Yuanzheng added, \"I haven't been to Yangcheng yet. Once the baby is born, I promise to accompany you back for a visit.\"","The two were married, but neither had met the other's parents yet.","Qin Yuanzheng had long been thinking of finding an opportunity to visit Qiao Lanshu's family.","As a son-in-law, this was absolutely necessary.","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded. \"Okay.\"","Qin Yuanzheng drove Qiao Lanshu back to their neighborhood. Then, the two of them went home briefly to grab their oil and meat ration coupons, preparing to go to the supply and marketing cooperative near their neighborhood to buy groceries.","Cities nowadays all had state-run vegetable markets, but the one here was quite far away.","Qiao Lanshu was used to buying groceries at the nearby cooperative. After all, supplies were divided by zones, and she just happened to be in this zone, so all her coupons were valid there.","When the two came out, Qin Yuanzheng chided her, \"I told you to rest at home and that I could go buy them myself. Why did you insist on coming along?\"","Qin Yuanzheng felt that his little wife was a bit too clingy.","However, he was secretly thrilled. He just loved spending time with Qiao Lanshu.","If he had to go buy groceries alone, his heart would still be constantly longing for Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu let him hold her hand. Her scarf wrapped around half of her small face, revealing only a pair of eyes curved in a smile.","She said, \"I've heard older folks say that when you're pregnant, you should walk around more. It's good for the baby.\"","It was too cold here in the north. She usually liked to sit in her small room at work, and when at home, she always wanted to lie down.","She felt that things couldn't go on like this.","The couple walked to the nearby cooperative. Today, the market was supplying fresh small red radishes.","They were limited to one catty per coupon, so the two lined up and bought a catty, planning to go back and make a cold salad with it.","Qin Yuanzheng then went to line up at the meat counter and came back with half a catty of mutton.","Mutton was also rationed; otherwise, he would have bought more to help Qiao Lanshu nourish her body.","Although his soldiers had gifted him a lot of poultry, he wasn't ready to slaughter them for food just yet.","He planned to slaughter them to nourish her body when Qiao Lanshu was in her postpartum confinement. After all, at that time, the baby would need to breastfeed, and the mother would be even more exhausted and need to eat meat.","While Qin Yuanzheng was lining up to buy meat, Qiao Lanshu waited beside him. Then, she spotted a familiar face.","She stared at the person for a few seconds, then walked to the other side to watch their back.","She saw Liu Weihong carrying bags full of things in both hands, walking out of the cooperative.","Qiao Lanshu thought to herself, this Liu Weihong is really rich to be able to buy so many things.","So, where exactly did her money come from?","She watched Liu Weihong exit the cooperative and then get into a car.","Qin Yuanzheng came over to find her with the meat, saying with a hint of displeasure, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, didn't I tell you not to run around? Why aren't you listening again?\"","At this time of day, there were many people in the cooperative, all lining up to buy things. What if Qiao Lanshu wasn't careful and got bumped into?","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice and asked, \"Brother Zheng, do you recognize that car?\"","Qin Yuanzheng followed her gaze and only saw a car driving away in the distance. The sky was grey and getting a bit dark. He took a look and said in a low voice, \"I think I've seen it before.\"","Qiao Lanshu's eyes lit up as she looked at him. \"Do you know whose it is?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"I don't know.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng rubbed her head and said softly, \"Silly girl, there are so many cars from various units in the city, I don't know every single one. But I'll keep an eye out and let you know when I find out something.\"","He didn't ask why Qiao Lanshu was paying attention to that person. Anyway, whatever Qiao Lanshu wanted to know or do, he would just support her.","Carrying the radishes, mutton, along with some canned food, fried dough twists, and bread, he held Qiao Lanshu's hand and said, \"Let's go, we'll head home to eat first.\"","After eating, he still had to give his little wife a massage. He could hardly wait.","How could Qiao Lanshu know what he was thinking?","She only knew that Qin Yuanzheng seemed a bit anxious and looked eager to try something.","After getting home and changing clothes, Qin Yuanzheng went to the kitchen to cook, wearing an army green vest and loose pajama pants.","He also asked Qiao Lanshu, \"Wife, do you want to take a bath tonight?\"","Qiao Lanshu hesitated for a moment, but Qin Yuanzheng had already quickly added water to the pot and turned on the fire to heat it up. \"Better take one. I can give your body an examination while we're at it.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu glared at him. \"Examine what? Don't think I don't know what you're thinking.\"","Qin Yuanzheng laughed. \"Since you know, then you definitely have to wash.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","In his heart, Qin Yuanzheng was still sighing.","What a pity. Why did his wife have to get pregnant?","He still had so many poses he hadn't put into practice yet."]},{"number":131,"title":"Chapter 131: Kneading Dough","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu hadn't taken a bath in quite a while, originally in an effort to save water.","Qin Yuanzheng had previously custom-ordered a wooden bathtub, which was now sitting in the bathroom.","It was perfect for taking a bath.","Later on, when Qiao Lanshu's belly got bigger and showering became inconvenient, she could also use the wooden tub.","The more Qin Yuanzheng thought about it, the smarter he felt for buying the tub so early.","Oh right, and that waterproof sheepskin mattress could also be used for the baby; they wouldn't even need to buy a new one.","As he cooked, he thought about all this, growing happier by the minute.","Qiao Lanshu changed her clothes and walked over in a loose-fitting loungewear set, wanting to see what he was doing and if he needed any help.","As a result, she saw him washing radishes while grinning foolishly to himself.","Who could have imagined that Qin Yuanzheng, who was strict, cold, and unsmiling in the military, secretly called Yama Qin behind his back, would be smiling like a fool at home.","Qin Yuanzheng wore an army-green tank top, revealing thick, sturdy arms with a wheat-colored complexion and beautiful muscle lines.","He also wore loose black casual pants and sported a buzz cut. Under the warm yellow light, his sharp facial features seemed somewhat gentle.","It was just that his stubble had grown out again.","Why did his beard grow so fast? Even bean sprouts didn't sprout as quickly as his stubble.","Qiao Lanshu walked up beside Qin Yuanzheng and watched him wash the radishes.","Then, her gaze involuntarily drifted toward Qin Yuanzheng's waist and abdomen, and down to his pants...","She looked for a moment, then suddenly reached out, gave his bulge a pat, and whispered, \"Brother Zheng, what are you thinking about? How come...\"","How could just washing a radish get him all worked up?","Qin Yuanzheng reacted strongly. He immediately dropped the radish, took two steps back, and glared at Qiao Lanshu, looking somewhat shocked: \"You, wifey, what are you trying to do?\"","Pulling a stunt like that out of nowhere nearly scared him to death.","His wife was usually very shy, and she was quite reserved in bed, too.","Why was she being so brazen now?","He narrowed his eyes and said in a low voice, \"Are you deliberately teasing me just because you're in your first three months?\"","Knowing he couldn't do anything to her, she started acting up.","This was exactly the kind of thing Comrade Xiao Qiao loved to do most.","Previously, when Qin Yuanzheng drove her to work, she liked to tease him right before getting out of the car. Seeing him get all worked up and suffering from restraint, she would just open the door, hop out, and run into the factory for work.","Tell me, isn't this little wife wicked?","Now that he caught an opportunity, shouldn't he teach her a good lesson?","Qiao Lanshu picked up a small red radish and took a bite. It was crisp, sweet, and delicious.","Her eyes curved into a smile as she whispered, \"Hubby, the doctor said we have to wait until after three months. You can't mess around right now, oh.\"","Look at that, she even called him hubby.","If this wasn't deliberate teasing, what was?","Qin Yuanzheng walked over, grabbed her in his arms, pressed her against the wall, and pretended to be fierce as he whispered, \"Are you asking for it again? So fearless? Go count the days yourself, how many more until it's been three months?\"","Qiao Lanshu was wearing thin clothes, and because of her pregnancy, she was already feeling a bit tender and swollen.","Being pressed by Qin Yuanzheng a few times, she twisted her body trying to escape, deliberately saying, \"I won't count, I don't know how to read.\"","How could Qin Yuanzheng let her run away?","He held her down, giving her a 'massage' while whispering in her ear, \"There are 12 days left until it's a full three months, remember that?\"","Qiao Lanshu actually felt a little scared now;","Think about it, a vigorous man with heavy desires suddenly being asked to practice abstinence and unable to vent—how frustrated must he be?","She knew she shouldn't tease him because he simply couldn't withstand it.","Normally, just calling him hubby would leave him excited for half the day.","Let alone the fact that she had just patted him with her hand.","But she couldn't help it either.","Teasing a man like this was so much fun.","A casual look or gesture would immediately draw a reaction.","She really couldn't resist playing with him.","Qiao Lanshu's voice grew soft from his handling as she said, \"Twelve more days, that's still a long way off. Brother Zheng, let me go first, I want to eat a radish.\"","The small red radishes Qin Yuanzheng had just bought from the supply and marketing cooperative were round and plump. A bite was crunchy, sweet, and juicy—incredibly delicious.","Qiao Lanshu loved eating them. She had just eaten one, and now she wanted another.","Qin Yuanzheng continued to 'massage' her while staring at her, whispering, \"You want to eat a radish? Alright, I'll let you eat your fill.\"","Saying that, he picked Qiao Lanshu up and walked off.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","No, she didn't mean that kind of radish!","...","Speaking of which, the two had only been married for about four months; they were still newlyweds.","They were in the honeymoon phase of passionate love.","Although Qin Yuanzheng used to go on blind dates often, he had never actually been in a relationship.","Qiao Lanshu was his first woman, and encountering such a stunner right off the bat, how could Qin Yuanzheng control himself?","You couldn't blame him for having his mind full of these bedroom matters all day long.","It was truly because he only got to experience this at his age; he couldn't hold back.","Qiao Lanshu said she liked eating red-skinned radishes, so Qin Yuanzheng let her eat them.","Qin Yuanzheng had said he would let her eat her fill all at once.","Over half an hour later, Qiao Lanshu couldn't eat anymore. With red eyes, she looked pitifully at Qin Yuanzheng and said, \"Brother Zheng, I don't want to eat anymore.\"","She felt like she was going to throw up if she kept eating.","Even though they hadn't gone all the way to the end, Qin Yuanzheng was already incredibly satisfied.","This kind of experience was indeed a first.","He had been thrilled several times over.","Holding Qiao Lanshu, he whispered, \"You don't like eating radishes anymore?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, somewhat regretting why she had teased him earlier. \"I don't like them anymore.\"","Qin Yuanzheng said with some regret, \"Why don't you like them anymore? I waited in line for ages to buy a pound of small red radishes. They're crisp, sweet, and very juicy. Aren't they your favorite?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Sure enough, against this two-faced and lustful man, Qiao Lanshu was truly no match.","In the end, Qin Yuanzheng still washed the small red radishes clean one by one, placed them on a white plate, and carried them over to the table in front of the sofa.","He smiled and said, \"Good wife, eat up.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng washed the half-pound of mutton clean and used it to stew mutton soup. Then he went to knead dough, preparing to cook mutton soup noodles for Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu watched his dough-kneading technique, and thinking of what had just happened on the sofa;","She instantly flushed red to the tips of her ears and looked away from Qin Yuanzheng.","Whether Qin Yuanzheng was doing it on purpose or not, he brought the dough to the living room table, sat right next to Qiao Lanshu, and kneaded the dough while watching her.","His palms were broad and rough, his fingers long, and he kneaded the dough with great force.","Grabbing the dough, pressing and kneading it back and forth a few times, he soon had the dough completely submissive—not sticking to the bottom or to his hands at all.","Qin Yuanzheng even asked, \"Wifey, what do you think of how I kneaded this dough?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\""]},{"number":132,"title":"Chapter 132: Dear, how can you be so wonderful","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng made a light mutton noodle soup for Qiao Lanshu.","Because Qiao Lanshu's taste was different from the locals, she ate her food with almost no salt or seasonings. When Qin Yuanzheng stewed the mutton, it was practically boiled in plain water; he didn't even dare to add green onions.","After all, Qiao Lanshu already preferred light meals, and now that she was pregnant and prone to morning sickness, he was worried she wouldn't be able to keep anything down.","Qin Yuanzheng's cooking skills were decent, but when it came to making light-flavored dishes, he often wasn't sure about the right amount of oil and salt.","He brought out the mutton noodle soup, sprinkled a tiny bit of chopped green onions on top, and brought out the vinegar and salt along with it.","He said, \"Wife, I didn't put any salt in your bowl. See how much you want and add it yourself.\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't know whether to laugh or cry. She added a little salt to her bowl and said, \"This mutton is stewed so soft and tender. Brother Zheng, you are really amazing at cooking.\"","She hadn't even taken a bite yet, and she was already praising him.","Qin Yuanzheng quite enjoyed the compliment. He said smugly, \"Of course, it goes without saying that my skills are top-notch, right?\"","As he spoke, he couldn't help but add a cheeky remark, \"My skills at kneading dough and making radishes are also pretty good, right?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu replied, \"I don't know, don't ask me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng sat next to her, pressing close and practically squeezing her into the corner of the sofa.","This big guy didn't seem to realize he was squishing her at all. As if he wasn't close enough, he squeezed even closer to Qiao Lanshu.","He whispered, \"However, there is one thing I must criticize you for, Comrade Xiao Qiao.\"","Seeing his serious expression, Qiao Lanshu put down her chopsticks and asked softly, \"What is it?\"","She quickly reflected on herself in her mind. What had she done wrong?","It seemed like nothing.","Other than the matter with Chu Liangjun, she hadn't hidden anything else from Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng had no excuse to punish her again!","She pondered for a long time, only to hear Qin Yuanzheng lower his voice and whisper in her ear, \"Your radish-eating technique isn't very good. It's far inferior to mine.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng felt that he was very good at eating and understood it well.","But his little wife was still a bit lacking.","But that was fine. Over the next dozen days or so, they could practice a lot more.","Qiao Lanshu glared at him. \"Stop talking and eat your food!\"","If he kept talking, the noodles were going to get soggy and clump together.","After finally finishing their meal, the two rested for a while and read the newspaper. Then, Qin Yuanzheng prepared to take Qiao Lanshu to the bathroom for a bath.","He had boiled hot water today and they had a new bathtub, which was perfect to use.","However, Qiao Lanshu put down the newspaper and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"By the way, Brother Zheng, I forgot to tell you something.\"","Qin Yuanzheng went to the kitchen to fetch water and asked at the same time, \"What is it?\"","Qiao Lanshu stood at the bathroom door, watching Qin Yuanzheng mix cold water into the wooden tub, and said slowly, \"When I went to work this morning, someone had posted a big-character poster about me on the food factory's bulletin board.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"???\"","Qin Yuanzheng paused his water-mixing, turned to look at Qiao Lanshu with a slightly darkened face, his brows knitted together. \"Someone posted a big-character poster about you? Why didn't you tell me this afternoon?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was very protective of his wife.","He was fiercely protective of his own. If anyone dared to bully his wife, he would definitely go knocking on their door to demand answers.","It wouldn't do if they didn't give him a proper explanation.","Qiao Lanshu explained to him, \"I've pretty much handled this matter. Cousin is taking people to keep watch at the factory tonight.\"","She told Qin Yuanzheng everything that happened today and what was discussed in the meeting, including the part about extracting fingerprints.","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng's tightly furrowed brows relaxed a bit. He continued to mix cold water into the tub and smiled, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, I didn't expect you to be so smart. You even know how to extract fingerprints?\"","Qiao Lanshu immediately puffed out her little chest, deliberately putting on a proud look, and said, \"Of course. I also know that to extract fingerprints, you have to use iodine and heat it up, and then the fingerprints will appear.\"","Looking at her smug appearance, Qin Yuanzheng really couldn't hold back and burst out laughing.","Having mixed the hot water in the tub to about the right temperature, he walked over, hugged Qiao Lanshu, kissed her on the cheek, and asked, \"This incident was definitely done on purpose by someone. I thought about it, and I should still find time in a few days to go to the hospital for a check-up. What if the infertility diagnosis last time was a misdiagnosis? That way, you wouldn't have to be gossiped about anymore.\"","In any case, Qin Yuanzheng would never doubt his little wife.","In the past, he never minded what gossip others said about him.","It didn't matter that people said he was infertile, or even impotent, because he knew these rumors couldn't hurt him.","Moreover, rumors had a time limit. After a few months at most, the gossip would vanish.","But now, his wife was being gossiped about because of him.","His heart ached terribly.","Qiao Lanshu, however, shook her head. \"Brother Zheng, there's no need for a check-up. What if you get checked a second time and the result is still infertility? What then?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Then Qiao Lanshu would probably be gossiped about even more.","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice and analyzed the situation for Qin Yuanzheng: \"I didn't tell you about the big-character poster this afternoon because I was afraid you'd get angry and go straight to the food factory to confront the factory director and the secretary. If you did that, the nature of the matter would change completely.","\"I thought about it carefully. This matter seems simple, as if someone is just jealous of me and reported me. But thinking deeper, something isn't right. Just think about it, I am your wife, and you are the commander of the 21st Regiment. In this day and age, ordinary people wouldn't dare to easily slander a military officer's family member.\"","The image of soldiers was very great, glorious, and correct in people's hearts.","Plus, the country had just begun rebuilding from the chaos of war. Soldiers had sacrificed so much for the nation and the people. Ordinary people wouldn't have the heart to baselessly slander a regiment commander who had been to the battlefield and executed countless dangerous missions.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"I feel that the person behind this definitely doesn't have a simple motive. I want to root them out and then send them to the public security bureau for a proper interrogation, to see if there's some conspiracy going on.\"","Of course, it was also possible that she was purely overthinking it.","Perhaps that person was just purely jealous of her, and having a good family background themselves, they weren't afraid of her military husband's retaliation.","That was also highly possible.","But what if?","In her heart, Qiao Lanshu kept thinking about how Qin Yuanzheng was almost blown to death while executing a mission in her past life.","Now, no matter what she encountered, she had to be extra vigilant and think things through more carefully.","Qin Yuanzheng reached out and cupped Qiao Lanshu's face, looking left and right, up and down, and muttered in confusion, \"How strange. You haven't grown a second brain, so how did my little wife suddenly become so smart?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng said in all seriousness:","\"Comrade Xiao Qiao, how are you so outstanding? Hmm? You are young, beautiful, educated, you make money, and now you're even thinking ahead with such foresight. With you as a contrast, it makes me look a bit useless, you know? Hmm?","Compared to your mind full of wisdom, my head seems to be filled only with things unsuitable for children. You wouldn't despise me, would you? Despise me for being old, rough, and good for nothing but cooking?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu shot him a reproachful glance and said, \"How are you useless? You are quite amazing.\"","Qin Yuanzheng thrust his waist slightly: \"Amazing at this?\"","Qiao Lanshu was teased by him until her face and ears turned entirely red.","Qin Yuanzheng then said with a straight face, \"That's true, at least I am still amazing in some areas, worthy of your praise, right? Wifey, it's a good thing you are a girl, and my wife at that. If you were a man, I wouldn't be able to compare to you in any aspect.\"","This older man, not knowing what got into him, started showering Qiao Lanshu with compliments.","And the compliments were endless.","One moment he would say, \"Wifey, your clothes still smell so fragrant even after wearing them all day. As expected of my wife.\"","The next moment he would say, \"Wifey, although you aren't very old, you are certainly quite big in all the right places. It's so nice. Look, I don't have that.\"","When they got into the wooden tub for a bath, Qin Yuanzheng massaged Qiao Lanshu while saying, \"Your skin is simply whiter and softer than dough, unlike me, all dark and swarthy. Please don't despise me.\"","Qiao Lanshu felt he was being a bit too noisy. She said helplessly, \"Brother Zheng, stop talking, the water will get cold soon.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had Qiao Lanshu sit on his lap; this way, it was more convenient for him to give his wife a massage.","He whispered, \"I'm praising you. Look, my palms are big enough, but these of yours are even bigger...\"","His palm could grab a ball of dough. He made a comparison in his mind; yes, his wife was just about like dough.","His wife was truly beautiful, she had grown up perfectly.","Fleshy where she should be, and quite slim where she should be.","Truly perfect.","Although Qin Yuanzheng said he was massaging her body, there was actually no proper massaging going on at all.","But Qiao Lanshu was still forced to accept this service.","Qin Yuanzheng serviced his wife for an hour before finally carrying her back to the bedroom to sleep, completely satisfied.","...","When going to work the next day, Qin Yuanzheng escorted Qiao Lanshu to the main gate of the food factory. Just before she got out of the car, he said to her,","\"Since you have already handled this matter, I won't ask any more questions. However, for the subsequent investigation, I will arrange for someone to coordinate with the food factory. Weren't you worried that the mastermind behind this isn't simple? I will investigate it personally. You just focus on resting and taking care of the baby, understand?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Okay, I know. I'll go to work now.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and watched Qiao Lanshu enter the food factory.","Only then did he drive back to the mining area military base.","What Qiao Lanshu said was indeed worth pondering.","If someone really wanted to target him and set their sights on his wife instead, that was definitely an issue that warranted serious attention.","Therefore, as soon as he arrived at the mining area office, Qin Yuanzheng called Young Company Commander Yang over, asked him to change into civilian clothes, and sent him to the food factory to find Yang Wenyan discreetly.","...","As soon as Qiao Lanshu arrived at the food factory today, she saw Uncle Guard standing at the gate. He said to her, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, great news! That bastard who posted the big character poster has been caught by the factory director!\"","Qiao Lanshu's spirits were instantly lifted. She said excitedly, \"They really caught them? Was it last night?\"","Uncle Guard nodded. \"That's right. In the middle of the night yesterday, someone climbed over our food factory's wall and headed straight for the bulletin board. I reckon they were worried that fingerprints would be collected today, exposing their identity, so they came in the middle of the night to tear down the poster.\"","Initially, Qiao Lanshu had worried that if the person who posted the big character poster had worn gloves, the excuse of extracting fingerprints might not be enough to bluff them.","Now it seemed that regardless of whether the other party wore gloves or not, they were guilty and afraid.","Sure enough, the bluff worked perfectly.","Qiao Lanshu asked anxiously, \"They really caught them! Who is it? Do I know them?\"","Uncle Guard clicked his tongue and sighed. \"You definitely won't guess who it is. This person actually has a bit of a connection with you.\"","Qiao Lanshu couldn't wait any longer. She said, \"Uncle, just tell me directly. Stop keeping me in suspense. If you don't tell me, I'm going to rush to the factory director's office.\"","Actually, by this time, quite a few food factory workers had already gathered around the factory gate.","Because many people wanted to hear exactly who had posted the big character poster.","How could they be so bold as to slander even a military officer's family member?","And even use the workers as their weapon.","Uncle Guard deliberately lowered his voice and said, \"That person is Wei Hongmei.\"","Someone asked, \"Wei Hongmei? Who is Wei Hongmei?\"","Hearing this name, Qiao Lanshu was extremely shocked.","She hadn't expected it to be Wei Hongmei either; this was truly unexpected.","Qiao Lanshu pushed her way through the crowd and jogged towards the food factory director's office.","Behind her, Uncle Guard held his thermos cup, slowly took a sip of red date water, and then said, \"Oh my, Wei Hongmei is the daughter of our factory's former workshop director, Wei Zhengye. Have you all forgotten? Wei Hongmei came to our factory to work as a family dependent worker. Later, it seemed she didn't perform well? So she was transferred to the family service team.\"","At that time, Yang Wenyan had originally intended to fire Wei Hongmei.","It was Wei Zhengye who pleaded for his daughter, saying that his son-in-law had deceived their family and had already been sent to a labor camp.","His daughter needed a job, even if the salary was a bit lower, otherwise she wouldn't be able to support her two children.","Therefore, Yang Wenyan transferred Wei Hongmei to the family service team.","Later on, Wei Zhengye was dismissed from his position and lost his job due to the incident of speculating and selling fried dough twists.","Everyone thought Wei Hongmei would leave the family service team.","In the end, after all the fuss, a few days later, Wei Hongmei came back to work again.","And now look at this, she actually went and posted a big character poster about Qiao Lanshu.","Someone couldn't help but speak up: \"This Wei Hongmei, could it be that she also went on a blind date with Regiment Commander Qin? Like Liu Weihong? And that's why she's jealous of Comrade Xiao Qiao?\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Someone else said, \"Come on, she was never very bright to begin with, and her work performance was always mediocre. Now that she's caused this mess, I think she shouldn't stay in the service team anymore. She'd better find a man to marry as soon as possible so she can at least get a bite to eat.\"","The crowd was buzzing with discussion.","Meanwhile, in Yang Wenyan's office, he looked at Wei Hongmei with a face full of confusion:","\"Wei Hongmei, tell me, instead of properly doing your service work in the family team, why on earth did you come and post a big character poster about Qiao Lanshu? Do you have a grudge against her? Or is there some conflict between you two that I don't know about?\""]},{"number":133,"title":"Chapter 133: Interrogation 02","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu was also quite surprised. The person who put up the big-character poster about her was actually Wei Hongmei?","No matter how she thought about it, something didn't seem quite right.","But then again, Wei Hongmei's husband, Sun Mingyong, was sent to a labor camp because of Qiao Lanshu.","Wei Hongmei's father, Wei Zhengye, also lost his job and was expelled from the Party because Qiao Lanshu discovered he was reselling fried dough twists from the food factory.","Looking at it this way, it seemed quite normal for Wei Hongmei to have a grudge against her, didn't it?","When Qiao Lanshu arrived at the food factory director's office, she saw that it was packed with people.","Besides the factory director Yang Wenyan, Secretary Wen, and various department heads, the logistics minister in charge of the family service team and others were also present.","Everyone stood in the office, looking at Wei Hongmei in the middle, and listening to Factory Director Yang Wenyan questioning her.","Standing there, Wei Hongmei stiffened her neck and shouted, \"Don't you all know what grievances I have with her? She ruined my husband, and she was the one who reported my dad. I just can't stand the sight of her, so what? Is that a crime?\"","Yang Wenyan slammed the table and pointed at Wei Hongmei, saying, \"Your husband committed marriage fraud and impersonated a military officer, and now he has another charge of embezzlement for stealing our factory's fried dough twists! Sending him to a labor camp is already letting him off easy. What, you still have a problem with that?\"","Yang Wenyan continued, \"And as for your dad, I don't even want to talk about it! The announcement was made, and we emphasized it several times in meetings. If you think your dad was wronged and you are dissatisfied with the previous verdict, I can apply for a retrial for you! Let me tell you, if this case is retried, Wei Zhengye will definitely be sent to a labor camp!\"","Last time, Wei Zhengye was lucky and wasn't sent to a labor camp.","He was only fired from his job and expelled from the Party, with a lifetime ban from being hired by any major work units.","That was only because the food factory decided not to pursue his legal responsibility. Yang Wenyan considered that he was an old employee who had worked hard even if he had no great merits. Plus, Wei Hongmei didn't have her husband around and had two children to raise, so the family needed someone to help out, which was why he showed leniency.","But now, Wei Hongmei had stirred up this kind of trouble again.","Yang Wenyan was furious. He pointed directly at Wei Hongmei and asked, \"Tell me, do you want a retrial? Are you still not convinced?\"","Wei Hongmei was speechless.","She shrank her neck, lowered her head, and stopped talking.","Anyway, she was just a member of the service team, not an official worker at the factory.","At most, they would just fire her; they couldn't really do anything else to her.","The work in the service team was hard and tiring. She had to mend clothes and shoes for the factory workers every day, and her hands were almost pierced into sieves by needles. The pay was also very low, only a few yuan a month!","She suffered and worked so hard just to earn these few yuan!","If she wanted to mend clothes, didn't she have clothes to mend at home? Why come to the service team to do it?","Wei Hongmei had wanted to quit for a long time.","Therefore, she stood there now, acting like a dead pig that is not afraid of boiling water, and said, \"Director, I put up the big-character poster. If you want to punish me, then just punish me. My dad has already been fired, so please stop holding onto his matter.\"","Yang Wenyan snorted coldly, \"I thought you weren't satisfied with your dad just being fired and wanted to send him to a labor camp too.\"","Wei Hongmei had nothing to say.","The people present were also very speechless.","The head of the logistics department scolded her, \"Hongmei, your dad fought hard to get you this job. Why don't you know how to cherish it?\"","When Wei Hongmei was in the family service team, she didn't actually work hard.","However, the service team always moved and worked together as a group, so Wei Hongmei's laziness didn't affect the overall progress.","It was just that the people in the team had a lot of complaints about her.","Several people had already reported Wei Hongmei, saying they didn't want to be in the same team with her.","Wei Hongmei now only had one sentence to say, \"I admit that I put up the big-character poster. Just tell me directly how you want to deal with me, and don't waste everyone's time.\"","Yang Wenyan and Secretary Wen exchanged a glance. Secretary Wen pondered for a moment and said, \"Putting up a big-character poster to report a colleague is not a huge deal, but it's not small either. Why don't we just fire her and be done with it?\"","After all, it was impossible to give a heavy sentence for this kind of thing.","At most, it would just be a dismissal and a public criticism.","Yang Wenyan felt quite annoyed. He really didn't expect Wei Hongmei to be so unreasonable.","Her father had lost his job, and now she had lost hers too. Was her whole family going to live on thin air in the future?","Just as Yang Wenyan was about to speak, Qiao Lanshu stepped forward.","Qiao Lanshu said to Yang Wenyan, \"Director, I suggest we hand this matter over to the military for processing. Because the content of the big-character poster involves slandering a military officer, our food factory should handle this matter jointly with the military.\"","Hearing this, Wei Hongmei immediately became anxious and said, \"I am a worker in the food factory's family team. The food factory can just deal with me directly. Why do you have to hand me over to the military? The military has no authority to punish me.\"","Neither Yang Wenyan nor Secretary Wen spoke; they both subconsciously looked at Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu was the person involved, and her husband was a military officer. If she wanted to blow the matter out of proportion, Yang Wenyan couldn't do anything about it.","When Qiao Lanshu had just entered, she had observed for a while. Wei Hongmei saw her coming but didn't pay attention to her, let alone curse at her.","Even Liu Weihong would curse a couple of times when she saw her. Why was Wei Hongmei so calm?","Obviously, deep down, Wei Hongmei didn't hate Qiao Lanshu as much as she claimed.","Then why did she put up the big-character poster?","Qiao Lanshu looked at Wei Hongmei and said, \"If you dare to slander a military officer, you should expect the consequences. The crime of impersonating a military officer gets six years. Do you know how many years you get for slandering a military officer?\"","At this point, Wei Hongmei began to panic.","Her face turned slightly pale, and she asked in a panic, \"How, how many years?\"","Secretary Wen spoke up, \"It should also start at six years. This kind of thing is no joke.\"","The head of the personnel department also chimed in, \"Yes, if it was just an internal matter of our food factory, it would be easy to handle. But since it involves the military, she might even have to face a military court.\"","Everyone chimed in one after another, making the situation sound increasingly serious.","Wei Hongmei was badly frightened.","Yang Wenyan roughly understood Qiao Lanshu's intention. She was trying to bluff her and see if she could get some information out of her.","So Yang Wenyan added fuel to the fire and said, \"Speaking of which, when I went to a meeting in the provincial capital before, I heard about an incident. In a unit in the neighboring city, someone put up a big-character poster reporting a military officer and was subsequently shot.\"","This was complete nonsense.","Yang Wenyan deliberately made it up to trick Wei Hongmei.","Yang Wenyan, who rarely lied, coughed guiltily a few times, feeling a bit awkward.","Secretary Wen looked at Yang Wenyan in confusion and asked in surprise, \"Huh? Did that really happen?\"","Why didn't he know about it?","Yang Wenyan was speechless.","How could Wei Hongmei know that everyone was just scaring her?","She was so nervous that her face turned pale, and she started to stutter, \"Y-y-you can't arrest me! I didn't put up the big-character poster! It has nothing to do with me!\""]},{"number":134,"title":"Chapter 134: I Didn't Write the Big-Character Poster","paragraphs":["When Wei Hongmei said this, everyone was a bit shocked.","Secretary Wen pointed at her and asked in a deep voice, \"You just admitted with your own mouth that you pasted the big-character poster. Why are you denying it now? Wei Hongmei, tell me the truth, did you paste this big-character poster or not!\"","Wei Hongmei was actually very timid and not very bright.","In the past, with Sun Mingyong and Wei Zhengye supporting her, she didn't have to worry about making a living.","Later, when Sun Mingyong was sent to a labor camp, she still had Wei Zhengye to rely on.","Now, even Wei Zhengye had lost his job and could only work as a temporary laborer at a nearby construction site every day to earn some money and ration coupons.","Naturally, he had no time to take care of Wei Hongmei's affairs.","Having committed this offense, Wei Hongmei was truly frightened now.","Pale-faced, she stammered, \"I, I...\"","She struggled for a long time, watching as the glares of the crowd seemed ready to spit fire at her.","She hurriedly said, \"I did paste the big-character poster, but I didn't write it! It was Liu Weihong! Liu Weihong made me do it.\"","The crowd: \"!!!\"","The people present instantly broke into an uproar. Secretary Wen and Yang Wenyan were also shocked.","Yang Wenyan: \"Liu Weihong? Liu Weihong, come in here and speak!\"","Liu Weihong had been hanging around the door with the others, watching the drama unfold. Now suddenly called in, she immediately defended herself loudly, \"It wasn't me! I didn't paste that big-character poster.\"","Wei Hongmei immediately cursed back at her:","\"Supervisor Liu, do you dare swear to heaven that you didn't ask me to paste that big-character poster?","The night before last, you came to me and said you would give me fifty yuan just to paste the big-character poster for you. You even said I was just a temporary worker in the service team and didn't want to work anymore anyway, so if I got caught, the worst that would happen is getting fired, not sent to a labor camp. That's why I helped you do this! You have the heart of a snake and a scorpion, you actually tried to get me killed! You didn't say a single word about the crime of slandering a military officer!\"","Liu Weihong had found Wei Hongmei around eight or nine in the evening. Originally, Wei Hongmei wasn't that familiar with her.","It was just that their two families lived close by and had known each other for many years.","And Liu Weihong had said she could give her fifty yuan.","Fifty yuan was almost equivalent to Wei Hongmei's annual salary in the family dependents' team.","She agreed without a second thought.","Wei Hongmei lunged at Liu Weihong, grabbed her newly bought army-green padded jacket, and started tearing at it, cursing as she tore, \"You ruined me! You ruined me! If you had told me earlier that slandering a military officer was a crime, I definitely wouldn't have taken your fifty yuan. You black-hearted, venomous woman, I'm going to beat you to death!\"","Liu Weihong was furious. As she fended off Wei Hongmei, she said, \"Oh, what are you panicking for! The worst is just getting fired, don't let them trick you!\"","Liu Weihong indeed hadn't lied to Wei Hongmei.","Pasting a big-character poster would at most result in dismissal. As for slandering a military officer, the contents of the poster didn't amount to that at all.","But Wei Hongmei was timid, hadn't worked a proper job for long, and didn't understand these convoluted matters at all.","Right now, she was terrified of being taken away by the military and getting shot.","At this moment, she didn't believe Liu Weihong's words at all. Tearing at Liu Weihong's clothes, she cursed loudly, \"Like hell I believe you! If I admit it now, I'll be the one taken away by the military! You clearly told me to paste this big-character poster, it has nothing to do with me!\"","Liu Weihong was also angry. She said, \"Then give me back the fifty yuan! It's just pasting a big-character poster, isn't it? Look at how scared you are, you're really useless!\"","Wei Hongmei immediately covered her pockets and took several steps back: \"No way. I already pasted the big-character poster for you, and you want me to refund the money? Keep dreaming.\"","Liu Weihong: \"...\"","Liu Weihong's temper flared up too, and throwing caution to the wind, she started pulling Wei Hongmei's hair right then and there.","The crowd: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu silently retreated behind Yang Wenyan, far away from the battlefield.","This wild hair-pulling was too intense and quite scary.","It was better for her to hide somewhere safe.","Yang Wenyan, Secretary Wen, and the others were all left speechless by this spectacle.","Yang Wenyan shouted, \"Stop it, both of you! If you don't stop, I'm calling the security team!\"","When they got dragged away by the security team, they'd see if they still had any face left.","Sure enough, at the mention of the security team, Liu Weihong and Wei Hongmei stopped immediately.","Both of them now had disheveled hair and untidy clothes.","For some reason, Wei Hongmei just kept tearing at Liu Weihong's new padded jacket.","She had even pulled out the cotton stuffing.","Liu Weihong's heart ached. Clutching the tear in her clothes, she gritted her teeth in anger: \"Wei Hongmei! You can just starve in the future! You deserve to be destitute and have to wear a padded jacket from five years ago.\"","Wei Hongmei pointed at her: \"Say another word, and I'll tear at you again.\"","Yang Wenyan stared at Liu Weihong: \"Liu Weihong, why did you paste this big-character poster?\"","Liu Weihong couldn't deny it now, so she could only admit it, saying, \"I just find her an eyesore, what other reason could there be?\"","Everyone knew that Liu Weihong and Qin Yuanzheng had gone on a blind date.","Everyone also knew that she and Qiao Lanshu didn't get along.","Someone whispered, \"She must be jealous that Qiao Lanshu is pregnant, which is why she pasted the big-character poster.\"","\"Tsk, she didn't get chosen on the blind date, and now she blames Qiao Lanshu. If everyone were like you, wouldn't the world be in chaos?\"","The crowd buzzed with discussion, all scolding Liu Weihong for being petty, narrow-minded, and vindictive.","They chattered on, scolding Liu Weihong for quite a while.","Liu Weihong just let them talk. She wasn't afraid anyway; she was a regular employee and wouldn't be fired.","She knew very well that this matter wouldn't reach the military headquarters.","She wasn't like Wei Hongmei, who couldn't handle anything and was just a useless piece of trash.","In the end, Liu Weihong was demoted from her supervisor position, going from workshop supervisor to an ordinary worker.","Her salary was also reduced from a supervisor's level-four pay to level-two pay.","She had worked hard for so many years to earn a level-four salary, and now, she was at the same level as the newly hired Qiao Lanshu.","After the matter was settled, everyone dispersed and went back to their workshops to work.","Young Company Commander Yang, dressed in plain clothes, came to Yang Wenyan's office to ask him about the big-character poster.","Meanwhile, Qiao Lanshu went back to work at the warehouse.","Wang Xue had also come to watch the drama this time, but she didn't enter the office and could only watch from the outside.","Qiao Lanshu spent quite a while explaining everything to her.","In these times, there wasn't much for entertainment, so listening to other people's gossip was quite interesting.","As they walked, Wang Xue said to Qiao Lanshu:","\"This Liu Weihong is really strange. She used to pull strings everywhere just to become a workshop supervisor. It hasn't been long, so how did she manage to ruin her supervisor position?","She's a veteran in the factory. She knows perfectly well that pasting a big-character poster to report a colleague will result in a demotion if it's found to be a malicious report.\"","Haven't you noticed the supervisors in the other workshops? They are always so cautious with their words and actions, terrified of giving anyone something to use against them.","Qiao Lanshu found it strange too. She said, \"Judging by Liu Weihong's outfits, she doesn't seem to be short on money. Her family must be quite well-off, right? That's probably why she couldn't care less about a pay cut. She just does whatever pleases her.\"","Wang Xue scoffed. \"Her? Her family is just average. They aren't wealthy by any means. She just started dating a new guy recently, which is why she's suddenly acting so rich.\"","As for how her boyfriend's family got all that money, well, nobody had a clue."]},{"number":135,"title":"Chapter 135: Show Her What You're Made Of","paragraphs":["Now that the truth of the matter had come to light, Yang Wenyan had the broadcaster announce it to the entire factory that very day.","At the same time, he convened a staff meeting for all the factory employees. Not only did he report on the big-character poster incident, but he also brought up several previous incidents and addressed them one by one.","It was the end of the year, and in order to have a peaceful New Year, Yang Wenyan really did not want any more trouble in the factory.","Furthermore, Yang Wenyan shared some major news concerning Longcheng.","The higher-ups were going to dispatch an inspection team to review the city's work.","For the city's leadership team, this was no walk in the park.","If any major incident were to occur in the city, it was highly likely that the entire leadership team would be replaced.","This had happened previously in a county town; due to a vicious assault case, everyone from the county party secretary to the county magistrate and deputy magistrates had been entirely replaced.","Yang Wenyan warned the food factory employees not to cause any trouble and to behave themselves. Whatever issues they had could wait until after the New Year.","After the meeting, Qiao Lanshu was full of anxiety, her mind preoccupied with thoughts.","In her previous life, she remembered that the city's party secretary had indeed been replaced, and because the top leader changed, the rest of the leadership team was naturally swapped out as well.","It was also that year when many things happened in Longcheng.","However, because Qiao Lanshu's own physical and mental health had been poor at the time, she hadn't paid much attention to these matters.","Thinking back on it now, could it be that some major event took place in Longcheng towards the end of the year, which led to the replacement of the leadership team?","Everything in Longcheng was currently very stable. If the city party secretary were to be replaced, it would cause a domino effect, leading to the replacement of many others.","Espionage was so rampant these days; what if some bad actors were brought in?","Qiao Lanshu pondered inwardly, wondering if these events had anything to do with Qin Yuanzheng almost being bombed to death in her previous life.","Wang Xue walked out of the hall with Qiao Lanshu, accompanying her toward the warehouse. She asked, Xiao Qiao, what are you thinking about?","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. Nothing.","Wang Xue smiled and said, We've been in meetings all morning, and I completely forgot to congratulate you. You're going to be a mother.","Qiao Lanshu nodded, feeling a bit shy. I didn't expect it either.","Wang Xue continued, By the way, Deng Weijun and our Haitang are getting along quite well. I figure by the end of the year, the two families will start discussing marriage. I asked Haitang, and she thinks Deng Weijun is a good man and is willing to be with him.","Qiao Lanshu said, Really? That's great news. They make a lovely couple.","Wang Xue said happily, Isn't it? Deng Weijun's sister is also a nice person. We're about to have our holidays soon, and Haitang might go back to our hometown. I even suggested having Deng Weijun see her off, so they could have a bit more time alone together.","Wang Xue chattered on, and it wasn't until they were almost at the warehouse door that she finally said goodbye to Qiao Lanshu.","After Wang Xue left, the smile on Qiao Lanshu's face faded.","She didn't know if she was just overthinking things, but she couldn't shake the feeling that something bad was going to happen in Longcheng by the end of the year.","Because of this, Qiao Lanshu was distracted for the entire afternoon.","...","Meanwhile, after the general factory meeting concluded, Liu Weihong left the factory in tears.","She had been demoted, her salary was reduced, and she was being gossiped about by people in the factory.","Always one to care about saving face and enjoying being flattered, she simply couldn't bear it.","So, she ran all the way home crying.","Liu Weihong's younger brother, Liu Weidong, happened to be at home.","Liu Weidong was in his early twenties this year. His hair was slightly long, his face was covered in acne, and his facial features closely resembled Liu Weihong's.","He was wearing a green military overcoat with a military cap sitting askew on his head. He was sitting on the heated brick bed in the room, drinking tea and cracking sunflower seeds with another young man dressed in a similar fashion.","As soon as he saw Liu Weihong come in, he called out, Sis, why are you back at this hour? Aren't you going to work?","Wiping away her tears, Liu Weihong replied, What work? I'm being bullied to death at the factory. My good supervisor position is gone, and I've been demoted to a regular worker. I can only earn a level-two salary now.","Upon hearing this, Liu Weidong immediately blew up. His face darkened, and he said fiercely, What? That Yang Wenyan dared to demote you? Why didn't you go find my brother-in-law? My brother-in-law is a section chief; just have him step in for you, and it'll be sorted.","Liu Weihong sat down on a nearby chair, her eyes red as she said, What brother-in-law? We haven't even gotten our marriage certificate yet.","Liu Weidong immediately said carelessly, You two are already living together, so what else should I call him? I'm telling you, Sis, you're just putting on too many airs. I've told you before, men like gentle women. Just coax my brother-in-law gently...","Liu Weihong usually doted on this younger brother, so Liu Weidong often spoke without a filter.","Now, not knowing which specific phrase lit the fuse of Liu Weihong's suppressed anger, she suddenly stood up, pointed at Liu Weidong, and scolded:","Gentle, gentle, that's all you know! Can being gentle feed you? You lie on the kang all day, eating and waiting to die, too lazy to move your limbs or tell one grain from another. If it weren't for me giving you money, you wouldn't even be able to afford a smoke, and you still have the nerve to complain that I'm not gentle enough?","Liu Weidong: ...","Liu Weidong and the buddy next to him were completely baffled by Liu Weihong's sudden outburst.","Liu Weidong casually tossed the sunflower seed shells in his hand onto the floor. He stood up and said, Sis, why are you so angry? It's not like I'm the one who dislikes you, I'm talking about my brother-in-law... Alright, alright, don't glare at me like that. I'll stop talking, is that okay?","Liu Weihong sat back down in her chair angrily, still feeling deeply wronged.","Liu Weidong walked over and asked her, Sis, is the person who bullied you still the same one? That warehouse keeper surnamed Qiao you mentioned?","Crying, Liu Weihong replied, Who else could it be? She relies on her military officer husband and looks down on everyone else. If it weren't for her, I would still have my supervisor position.","This Qiao Lanshu, why was she so despicable!","In her heart, Liu Weihong hated her to death.","Liu Weidong had been loitering on the streets for a long time, and he had a group of familiar buddies around him.","They were all street punks who relied on their family connections to avoid being sent down to the countryside, yet refused to work properly, only wanting to eat, drink, and play.","Seeing his sister being bullied, Liu Weidong immediately slammed his hand on the table and said ferociously, She's just a cheap tramp from out of town with no family here, and she thinks she can ride on our heads just because she has a military officer husband? Sis, don't worry. I'll go teach her a lesson right now. I guarantee I'll make her bow and kowtow to apologize to you.","Making her bow and kowtow in apology was impossible; after all, she was a military officer's family member, which carried some power.","But scaring Qiao Lanshu a bit to teach her a lesson wasn't entirely out of the question.","Thinking of this, Liu Weihong did not stop Liu Weidong.","Liu Weidong took his buddy, stepped out of the room, grabbed the car keys, and drove his father's car out.","His father was the director of the personnel section in a key county, with a wide network of connections that even reached the provincial level.","His brother-in-law was a section chief in the provincial supply department, and Liu Weidong himself had been messing around for so many years that he also knew some brothers in the Revolutionary Committee.","...along with some buddies who had family in the military. He figured that with his extensive network, power, and influence, there was no way he couldn't intimidate a girl from out of town.","The buddy sitting next to him said, \"Brother Dong, they haven't gotten off work yet, have they? Even if we head over there now, we won't be able to get inside the factory to find her.\"","Liu Weidong sneered. \"Getting her to come out will be a piece of cake. When we get there, we'll just say her family has come to visit, or that her husband sent someone to find her. There are plenty of excuses we can use. We just need to lure her out first, and then she'll be in for a rude awakening.\""]},{"number":136,"title":"Chapter 136: Someone is looking for you again.","paragraphs":["Liu Weidong had been spoiled at home, developing a somewhat arrogant and domineering personality.","Over the years, running the streets with his buddies, everyone flattered him and praised him, which made him lose his sense of proportion.","Originally, people already toadied to him because of his father, and now, with his brother-in-law added to the mix, his gang looked up to him as their leader.","Liu Weidong drove his car, chattering to his friend all the way:","\"This woman named Qiao—she’s from the south, has a terrible reputation, always butting heads with my sister. Now she’s even gotten my sister’s supervisor position taken away. I’m going to teach her a lesson today on my sister’s behalf, or else she’ll think the Liu family has no backbone.\"","His friend sounded worried: \"But Weidong, your sister just said that woman’s husband is a military officer. Maybe we should just skip it?\"","In those days, the military carried a lot of power.","Not just anyone could become an officer, either;","the title of regiment commander could make anyone think twice.","Liu Weidong wasn’t scared, but his friend was.","After all, Liu Weidong had a section chief as his brother-in-law; his friends didn’t have that kind of advantage.","If trouble came, no one would bail them out.","Liu Weidong grew annoyed with his friend. He cursed: \"What’s with the gutlessness? Riding with me and still hanging back like a turtle—what use are you to me?\"","With that, he slammed on the brakes, stopping the car in the middle of the road. He kicked his friend, who was sitting beside him, and yelled, \"Useless piece of trash! Get out of my car. Don’t follow me anymore. Just your face brings bad luck.\"","His friend, too afraid to speak his mind, was kicked out and stood by the roadside, silently watching Liu Weidong drive off.","Liu Weidong mused as he drove: It’s just dealing with a woman. He was tall and strong—what did he need help for?","Others feared officers, but not him.","His dad knew plenty of officers—regiment commanders, brigade commanders. He’d grown up meeting many of them. So what if they wore a military uniform? What was so impressive about that?","With that thought, Liu Weidong stepped on the gas, speeding toward the food factory’s iron gate. He jumped out of the car and strode up to knock on the factory gate.","The factory’s security guard, an older man, saw this young fellow rushing up in a car, not even bothering to close the door or check if the key was pulled out, and going straight for the gate—what could be so urgent?","The guard tensed up, hurried out of his booth, and shouted, \"Hey! Hey! What’s the big rush? You trying to beat the hell out of someone?\"","As he approached, the guard looked Liu Weidong up and down and asked, \"Who are you? What’s so urgent?\"","He was about to ask if the guy was rushing to reincarnate, but figuring anyone who could drive a car wasn’t just anyone, he swallowed the words.","Liu Weidong’s expression darkened. Though he was holding back, his tone was harsh. He said to the guard, \"Uncle, do you have a warehouse attendant named Qiao in your factory? Could you call her out? I need to see her urgently.\"","The guard remembered that the last time, Chu Liangjun had been visiting Qiao Lanshu every day.","Xiao Qiao was young and pretty—probably had all kinds of shady characters chasing after her.","So the guard got cautious and asked, \"What’s your work unit? What are you here for? Without proper ID, why should I call her out?”","Liu Weidong was speechless.","He held back his anger, not wanting to make a scene with this guard. If the guard got upset and locked the iron gate, he’d have wasted a trip.","After a short pause, Liu Weidong said, \"Wait here. I’ll look around.\"","He ran back to his car and rummaged through it.","The car belonged to his father’s unit.","But his father would leave the car at home for Liu Weidong to use, while arranging a chauffeur to drive him in a different car.","Liu Weidong had driven it for so long that he knew there were some documents inside.","They were from his father’s unit.","After a bit of searching, he found a vehicle assignment certificate from the personnel department.","He pulled it out and handed it to the guard, saying, \"I’m from the personnel department. I need to talk to Comrade Qiao about something. I’m in a hurry, so go call her—don’t waste my time.\"","The guard looked at the document and more or less believed him.","In those days, an average person couldn’t afford or even drive a car.","Those who drove cars were usually children of cadres, military personnel, or drivers in major units.","The guard fetched a registration form and had Liu Weidong sign it before telling him, \"Wait here. I’ll go call her.\"","Then the guard jogged inside to the warehouse to find Qiao Lanshu.","The last time the guard had come to Qiao Lanshu, it was for Chu Liangjun to have a department store employee deliver a coat to her.","Now, the guard said, \"Xiao Qiao, someone’s at the gate looking for you. Says he’s from the personnel department, very young, and drives a car—probably here to talk business.\"","Qiao Lanshu opened the door to her little room. She was wearing a padded jacket, a scarf wrapped around her, and holding a hat in her hand. She looked puzzled: \"Why would someone from the personnel department want to see me? I don’t know anyone there.\"","The guard analyzed it for her: \"Could it be about your probation-to-permanent job switch? Maybe they want to talk to you?\"","He added, \"Of course, your position should already be approved. But with that big-character poster put up about you recently, maybe they need to check on it?\"","Qiao Lanshu wasn’t sure. She didn’t know what was going on.","She put on her black wool hat, adjusting her two thick braids, and said as she walked, \"If they’re here about that, they shouldn’t be looking for me. They should go through the food factory’s personnel department to verify things.\"","After all, her hiring and job transfer were handled by the factory’s HR, not something she arranged on her own.","Procedures had to be followed.","The guard suddenly saw what she meant and said, \"Ah, Xiao Qiao, you bookish people are sharp. I didn’t think of that. What should we do? Want me to head back inside and report it to the personnel office?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and smiled. \"Let’s both go to the personnel office, then step out together with someone from there to see who this person is and figure out what’s going on.\""]},{"number":137,"title":"Chapter 137: Driving a Car","paragraphs":["In the office of the food factory's personnel department, Clerk Zhou happened to be present.","After hearing Uncle Guard's words, he immediately stood up and said, \"Since that's the case, I'll go out with you for a trip.\"","On the way, Clerk Zhou added, \"Logically speaking, it shouldn't be like this. The onboarding and regularization of internal employees in the food factory are all handled by us. Except for management-level personnel changes, ordinary workers generally don't need to go through the municipal personnel department.\"","This was just Uncle Guard not seeing things clearly.","Actually, the form Liu Weidong showed him belonged to the county personnel department under the city's jurisdiction.","Uncle Guard grew even more nervous and said, \"Could the other party be a scammer? Was I tricked by him? That shouldn't be, he was driving a car, looking quite impressive.\"","Sometimes, Uncle Guard's work was quite difficult to carry out.","For instance, when certain people came to the food factory, if he stopped them, he feared offending powerful and influential officials from the outside.","If he didn't stop them, he worried that something might happen to the factory workers, and he would have to bear the responsibility.","Clerk Zhou comforted Uncle Guard, saying, \"Uncle, don't worry. I'll go take a look with you. If the other party is a scammer, we'll just chase him away. You don't need to blame yourself.\"","Wasn't Uncle Guard just afraid that something might happen to Qiao Lanshu?","Qiao Lanshu was the family member of a military officer, and she was even pregnant with the child of an officer who was previously thought to be infertile.","She was currently the key focus of care in the factory.","Uncle Guard lowered his voice and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, just stand behind me later. Let's see what this is all about first.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded, \"Okay, thank you, Uncle. You are such a good person.\"","Saying that, she also praised Clerk Zhou, \"Clerk Zhou, thank you for coming out with us. If it weren't for you, we wouldn't be able to figure out what's going on with the other party. Thank you for your hard work this time.\"","The young Clerk Zhou quickly waved his hands and said shyly, \"No need, no need, it's what I should do. Comrade Xiao Qiao, please don't be so polite.\"","Qiao Lanshu really had a sweet mouth; she smiled at everyone she met, praised everyone, looked beautiful, and had a lovely voice.","Fortunately, she had married early. Otherwise, with her personality, who knows how popular she would be in the food factory. Those male comrades would probably fight over her.","When the group of three arrived at the main gate of the food factory.","They saw Liu Weidong standing at the gate from afar, with a cigarette dangling from his mouth.","Clerk Zhou just took one look and frowned, \"Uncle, the person from the personnel department you mentioned, is that him?\"","The uncle nodded, \"Yes, that's him. He was looking for Comrade Xiao Qiao.\"","Qiao Lanshu also glanced at Liu Weidong and silently shook her head in her heart. She didn't know him. Who was this person?","Seeing them approach, Liu Weidong immediately threw away his cigarette butt and asked with a dark face, \"I'm just looking for a woman, why did you call a man over for me?\"","Qiao Lanshu hid behind Clerk Zhou and Uncle Guard. Liu Weidong didn't look carefully and just stared at Clerk Zhou.","Clerk Zhou's expression instantly darkened, and he told him, \"Comrade, if you have something to say, say it nicely. Don't be so rude.\"","Liu Weidong's tone became a bit impatient, \"I can't be bothered to talk nonsense with you. Where is that warehouse keeper surnamed Qiao? Tell her to come out...\"","As he spoke, he paused and suddenly locked his eyes on Qiao Lanshu.","Because Qiao Lanshu was not tall and had a slim figure, walking behind the two men just now, Liu Weidong really hadn't noticed her.","Now that he saw her, he was stunned.","This little girl was quite pretty. In his life, he had never seen anyone so good-looking, and he was momentarily dazed.","He stared at Qiao Lanshu's face for several seconds.","Uncle Guard immediately said, \"This is a hooligan, get out of here right now!\"","Clerk Zhou also frowned and said to Liu Weidong, \"Are you from the municipal personnel department? Which office in the personnel department, and what's your name?\"","Liu Weidong suddenly rushed over and pushed Clerk Zhou aside. He pointed at Qiao Lanshu and cursed, \"So you're the one who bullied my sister, right? You're pretty arrogant, aren't you? Calling you out requires bringing two bodyguards? You think you're quite impressive?\"","Qiao Lanshu had just felt that the way Liu Weidong looked at her was wrong, so she hid far away.","With Liu Weidong rushing over so suddenly, Clerk Zhou was dumbfounded and was directly pushed aside by him.","Uncle Guard reacted quickly. He immediately grabbed a stick and shouted loudly, \"What do you want to do? Back off right now, or I'll call the patrol team!\"","Liu Weidong was tall and sturdy. He hung around outside and had been in plenty of fights, so he wasn't afraid of Uncle Guard's stick at all.","Uncle Guard was already quite old and definitely wasn't his match.","He charged directly over, kicked Uncle Guard, and cursed impatiently, \"I just want to say a word to Comrade Qiao. Why are you all so fierce? Even grabbing a stick, what, you want to hit me? If you have the guts, hit me then. What's the point of yelling endlessly here?\"","Seeing how fierce Liu Weidong was and how ruthlessly he acted, Clerk Zhou was a bit scared, but he was worried something would happen to Qiao Lanshu and he wouldn't be able to bear the responsibility.","After all, he had come out with her.","Therefore, he looked around, trying to find a stick to fight Liu Weidong.","This was really putting him, a refined person, in a tough spot. He usually wouldn't even say a swear word, but now he had to fight.","When he finally found a stick and looked up, his heart skipped a beat, and he cried out, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao? Where is Comrade Xiao Qiao? Where did Qiao Lanshu go?\"","How could Qiao Lanshu disappear in just the blink of an eye?","Liu Weidong had already chased her out the gate, roaring, \"Stop right there! I haven't finished speaking yet. You better stop bullying my...\"","Uncle Guard was also shouting anxiously, \"Xiao Qiao! Come back quickly, you should run into the factory. Why are you running outside? There's nowhere to hide out there.\"","While saying this, Uncle Guard and Clerk Zhou hurriedly chased after her together.","Qiao Lanshu had already run swiftly to the side of the car. The car door wasn't closed, and the keys hadn't been pulled out.","She got straight into the car and closed the door with a loud bang.","Liu Weidong chased her out and saw that Qiao Lanshu had actually run into the car.","He suddenly felt an inexplicable sense of panic.","He ran over, pulling hard on the car door while cursing fiercely, \"You bitch, get out of my car right now, or I won't hold back!\"","As he shouted, he forcefully pulled at the car door, causing the whole car to shake continuously.","Qiao Lanshu kept a straight face, looking calm. She turned the key and started the car.","Liu Weidong was startled. Before he could figure out how this woman from the south suddenly knew how to drive a car...","He saw the car suddenly reverse, then turn around and charge straight in his direction!","Liu Weidong: \"!!!\"","Liu Weidong's heart jolted in shock, and he hurriedly backed away."]},{"number":138,"title":"Chapter 138: No One Believes Liu Weidong","paragraphs":["In this day and age, people who knew how to drive a car were almost as rare as those who knew how to fly a plane.","In an era when there were barely any cars on the streets, a young girl from the south actually knew how to drive.","This time, not only was Liu Weidong dumbfounded, but even Clerk Zhou and Uncle Guard, who had chased after them, were completely stunned.","The two of them stood by the side of the road, leaning tightly against a utility pole. Looking through the car window at Qiao Lanshu in the driver's seat, Clerk Zhou swallowed hard. He shakily reached out a hand, pointed toward the driver's seat, and asked in a trembling voice, Uncle, is the person sitting in that car Comrade Xiao Qiao?","Uncle Guard rubbed his eyes vigorously and said nervously, It... it looks like her... Wait, does Xiao Qiao know how to drive? She couldn't just be driving blindly, could she? That's too dangerous.","Upon hearing Uncle Guard say this, Clerk Zhou immediately grabbed his arm and backed away. Step back, step back! This car doesn't have eyes. If it hits us, we won't have anywhere to go to reason it out...","Before Uncle Guard could react, he was pulled several steps back by Clerk Zhou.","The two of them watched Qiao Lanshu in silence, and then helplessly watched as the car charged in Liu Weidong's direction.","Clerk Zhou's forehead was covered in cold sweat. Thank goodness it's not coming for us...","Uncle Guard swallowed hard and said, At a critical moment like this, Comrade Xiao Qiao still thought to avoid hitting us. She really is a good kid.","Clerk Zhou: ...","Meanwhile, in the driver's seat of the car, Qiao Lanshu looked calm, her expression unchanging.","She calmly held the steering wheel, slowly stepping on the gas pedal. The car maintained a steady speed, chasing after Liu Weidong as he ran forward.","When had Liu Weidong ever seen such a spectacle?","He was instantly scared pale and could only run for his life.","Right in front of the food factory was a street. It wasn't very wide, just enough for a single car to pass through.","Every time Liu Weidong tried to dodge to the side, the car would speed up. If he stumbled and slowed down, the car's speed would also slow down.","He kept feeling like the car was about to hit him, but it never actually did.","It was as if the person driving the car was chasing him just to mess with him.","He could only run wildly, shouting at the top of his lungs as he ran, You surnamed Qiao! Get out of my car right now! Let me tell you, this car is public property. If you break it, you won't be able to afford the compensation!","Qiao Lanshu ignored him. She simply kept driving, chasing Liu Weidong down the road.","Liu Weidong grew tired, but the car was still chasing him. He had run for a full mile.","Panting heavily, Liu Weidong continued to yell, Qiao, I'm telling you, my dad is Liu Zhengxing! Do you even know who he is? If you offend me, you won't get away with it! Even your husband will face retaliation!","Just as he was speaking, the car behind him suddenly accelerated and rammed toward him.","Liu Weidong's back was nudged by the car. He screamed and dodged to the side, then lost his footing, tripped, and rolled into the stinky ditch by the street.","It was the dead of winter, and the ditch was frozen solid. He fell flat onto the ice and didn't actually sink into the foul water, which Qiao Lanshu found quite regrettable.","That was letting him off too easy.","After tumbling down, Liu Weidong suddenly hugged his leg and howled in pain, screaming at the top of his lungs, My leg! My leg is broken! Help! Somebody come quickly! Qiao, you broke my leg! I want you to pay me back with one of your own!","Qiao Lanshu parked the car by the side of the road.","She first glanced cautiously out the window, making sure that Liu Weidong wouldn't be able to climb up anytime soon.","Only then did she open the door and step out. Standing by the road with her hands in her pockets, she looked down expressionlessly into the ditch.","Liu Weidong furrowed his brows in agony. Having rolled around on the ground, he was covered in black dirt and looked utterly pathetic.","Clutching his leg with one hand and gasping in pain, he pointed at Qiao Lanshu and cursed breathlessly, Qiao, I'm going to report you! You murderer! You hit me with a car and broke my leg! I want you to pay with your life!","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu's expression turned cold.","Liu Weidong was still swearing in the ditch. He thought Qiao Lanshu would at least argue back with him a bit.","After all, she dared to run someone over with a car. What else was this woman not capable of?","However, one second Qiao Lanshu was staring at him with icy eyes.","The very next second, her eyes suddenly turned red as she spoke to Clerk Zhou, who was rushing over, Clerk Zhou, who is he? Why is he targeting me? I'm so scared.","As Qiao Lanshu spoke, she hid behind Clerk Zhou, looking terrified and uneasy.","It was as if the person who had just been chased by a car for a mile and broken a leg in a ditch wasn't Liu Weidong, but her.","Liu Weidong: ???","Liu Weidong was absolutely dumbfounded by her sheer audacity.","Clerk Zhou hurried over, panting. He first stood by the road and glanced at the pale-faced Liu Weidong, who was lying in the ditch clutching his leg. Then, he looked at the car nearby and asked Qiao Lanshu in a low voice, Comrade Xiao Qiao, you actually know how to drive a car?","Qiao Lanshu quickly shook her head and said shyly, I don't. I was just too scared just now, so I tried driving it. I didn't expect it to actually move. It was an accident. I was terrified at the time.","Clerk Zhou: ...","Clerk Zhou took her words for it and said with lingering fear, Thank goodness no one was killed! Comrade Xiao Qiao, this kind of thing is far too dangerous. You must never drive a car so recklessly again. If anything, you should ask Regiment Commander Qin to teach you, and only drive once you've learned properly, alright?","Just now, he hadn't dared to get too close to the car, afraid that it might lose control and hit him too. It was incredibly horrifying.","Qiao Lanshu nodded somewhat sheepishly. Okay, I understand.","At this moment, Uncle Guard, who had run back to the factory to deliver the news, hurriedly rushed over with the food factory's inspection team. He asked anxiously, Comrade Xiao Qiao, are you alright?","Qiao Lanshu shook her head and said shyly, Uncle, I'm fine.","The leader of the inspection team had hurried over with his men as soon as he heard someone was causing trouble.","Now, looking at the situation, everyone from the food factory was perfectly fine, while the troublemaker was lying in a stinking ditch?","The inspection team members went down and hauled Liu Weidong up. The team leader stared sternly at Liu Weidong. After watching him for a good while, he asked in a deep voice, Which unit are you from? What's your name? Why did you come to the food factory to cause trouble? You'd better confess honestly, or else I'll break your legs!","Liu Weidong: ...","These people from the food factory were such bad luck; every single one of them seemed to have a grudge against his legs!","Enduring the immense pain shooting from his leg, Liu Weidong said angrily, Do you have eyes? Do you have a brain? I'm the one who's injured! I am the victim! Why are you interrogating me? You should be questioning that woman surnamed Qiao! She just ran me over with a car! She's a murderer, you know!","Hearing this, the team leader immediately turned his head and glanced at Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu blinked, and tears welled up instantly. Crying, she said, \"I'm not, I didn't! As soon as this man saw me, he tried to hit me. I was so scared that I just wanted to hide in the car. But I don't know what happened, the car just started moving on its own... I, I really don't know what happened.\"","The crowd was speechless.","Liu Weidong hissed and cursed, \"You're lying! You obviously know how to drive! You liar, don't think people will believe you just because you made up some excuses. You clearly knew how to drive just now!\"","Uncle Guard couldn't listen to this anymore. He angrily kicked Liu Weidong and scolded, \"When you got out of the car, you didn't even take out the keys or close the door. The young lady doesn't know anything about cars. In her panic, she must have stepped on something, so of course the car started moving!\"","Clerk Zhou immediately joined in the scolding, \"A car is public property, how can you ruin it like this? Whose kid are you anyway, and what work unit do you belong to? Tell the truth, did you steal this car?\"","Liu Weidong was so angry at these people that he saw stars.","He shouted furiously, \"I already told you I didn't steal it! I'm not a fucking thief!\"","Qiao Lanshu quietly fanned the flames from the side, \"You're just a jobless hooligan, you've definitely stolen plenty of things. You must be a thief.\"","Uncle Guard also said, \"This bastard looks exactly like a street punk. You must spend a lot of time loitering on the streets, right? Maybe he really did steal this car from some work unit and just refuses to tell the truth!\"","Qiao Lanshu continued, \"Exactly, exactly. A person like him should be sent to the police station. Let's see if he still refuses to tell the truth then.\"","Liu Weidong simply couldn't defend himself. He was about to say more when a member of the patrol team twisted his arm and shoved him into the car. Then the patrol team leader said:","\"Since you refuse to tell the truth, you can go tell it at the police station. We'll drive your car over there too. We'll investigate and see which work unit this car belongs to, then contact them to come pick it up. Let's go.\"","Liu Weidong was speechless.","Liu Weidong was still struggling madly inside the car. The patrol team members, who already disliked him, simply gave him an elbow strike to the stomach.","Liu Weidong let out a muffled groan and whimpered while clutching his stomach, finally settling down.","He just couldn't figure it out. He had clearly come to get revenge for his sister, so how did he end up getting himself sent to the police station instead?","Qiao Lanshu, Clerk Zhou, and Uncle Guard also had to go to the police station.","The matter needed to be investigated, and the three of them were witnesses.","Besides, Liu Weidong had come specifically for Qiao Lanshu, so this matter had to be thoroughly investigated, right?","To see exactly what kind of grudge existed between the two of them.","And because it involved a military family member, who knew if this was actually targeted at the military?","That would completely change the nature of the issue.","Qiao Lanshu and the other two first went back into the food factory to pack up their things. After all, it was almost time to get off work. Once they packed their belongings, they wouldn't need to come back and could just go straight home after leaving the police station.","Neither Yang Wenyan nor Secretary Wen were at the factory. Clerk Zhou himself was from the personnel department, so he recorded the attendance for the three of them. The incident report would just have to wait until they came back to work tomorrow to be written.","Before leaving the food factory, Qiao Lanshu also spoke to another guard, telling him that when Qin Yuanzheng arrived, he should tell Qin Yuanzheng to go directly to the police station to pick her up.","This way, Qin Yuanzheng wouldn't wait around for nothing.","Then, the three of them walked to the police station.","At the police station, Liu Weidong had already been handcuffed.","There were only four officers in total at the station, and currently, only two were on duty.","They were already familiar with Liu Weidong. One of them looked at him and asked, \"Liu Weidong, why is it you? Did you commit a crime again?\"","The patrol team leader immediately said, \"I guessed right, he actually is a repeat offender!\"","Liu Weidong had limped his way in. He clamored, \"My leg is broken from being hit! Hurry up and take me to the hospital, otherwise I'll be crippled! Will you be able to take responsibility when that happens?\"","The police comrade then asked the patrol team leader, \"What exactly is going on with this Liu Weidong? How did his leg get injured?\"","The patrol team members recounted the process to the police comrade, \"Later, that female comrade was scared and hid in the car, accidentally starting it. It's all Liu Weidong's own fault for courting death by bullying a female comrade and not even taking the car keys out.\"","Liu Weidong was so angry he was practically going crazy. He repeatedly shouted at the top of his lungs, \"I said she knows how to drive! She knows how to drive, she knows how to drive, why won't any of you believe me!\"","However, his character was so poor that no matter what he said, no one would listen.","A long time passed, and no matter how much Liu Weidong yelled in the police station, claiming that he didn't lay a hand on her and that Qiao Lanshu did it on purpose, absolutely no one believed his words.","The police comrade said to Liu Weidong, \"You were brought in last time for harassing women. Didn't you write a letter of guarantee saying you would be a good person from then on? It's only been a few days, how did you get arrested again? It's already the end of the year, tell me, can't you just settle down a bit?\"","If it had been anyone else harassing women, they would have been sent to a labor camp long ago.","But when Liu Weidong harassed women, he only had to write a letter of guarantee.","He just relied on the fact that his father had connections and influence, which allowed him to act recklessly and lawlessly.","This hadn't been going on for just a day or two.","He was already in his twenties, his personality was set, and it was unlikely he would ever change.","Liu Weidong wasn't afraid of the police comrades at all. Sitting there with a slouching, careless attitude, he said to them:","\"I am being a good person right now! I already said I didn't do anything. That woman surnamed Qiao made the first move. She drove the car into me, trying to kill me! Fortunately, I'm lucky to be alive, so she didn't succeed! But my leg is broken from the crash, shouldn't you hurry up and take me to the hospital!\"","Seeing this, the patrol team leader frowned and asked the police comrade next to him, \"Does this Liu Weidong have a big background? Do you know him? Who exactly is he?\"","The police comrade lowered his voice and told him, \"Liu Weidong's father is Liu Zhengxing, the head of the personnel department in Wenxing County. He knows a lot of people. Anyway, every time Liu Weidong gets into trouble, someone bails him out. This matter is going to be tricky to handle.\"","With just one sentence, the patrol team leader understood a bit.","Their Longcheng City actually wasn't big; it had four counties under its jurisdiction, the largest of which was Wenxing County.","Many people in the city's departments had been promoted and transferred from Wenxing County.","Liu Weidong's father had worked in the personnel department for over a decade. Although he hadn't been transferred to the city yet, he was more familiar with the people in the city than anyone else.","Among them were many who had once received favors from him."]},{"number":139,"title":"Chapter 139: Why Are You Bullying My Wife","paragraphs":["No matter how much Liu Weidong yelled in the police station, claiming he did not lay a hand on anyone and that Qiao Lanshu did it on purpose, absolutely no one believed a word he said.","The police officers said to Liu Weidong, You were brought in last time for harassing women. Did you not write a letter of guarantee promising to turn over a new leaf?","If anyone else had harassed women, they would have been sent to a labor camp long ago.","But when Liu Weidong harassed women, all he had to do was write a letter of guarantee.","Looking completely nonchalant and arrogant, Liu Weidong retorted, I am turning over a new leaf right now! I already told you I did not do anything, yet my leg got broken. Why are you not hurrying to send me to the hospital!","Seeing this, the leader of the inspection team frowned and asked the police officer beside him, Does this Liu Weidong have a powerful background? Do you know him?","The police officer lowered his voice and told him, Liu Weidong's father is the head of the personnel section in Wenxing County.","With just that one sentence, the inspection team leader somewhat understood.","Their Longcheng City was actually not that big. It had four counties under its jurisdiction, the largest of which was Wenxing County.","Many people in the city's departments had been promoted and transferred from Wenxing County.","Liu Weidong's father had worked in the personnel section for over ten years. Although he had not been transferred to the city yet, he was more familiar with the people in the city than anyone else.","Among them, there was no shortage of people who had once received favors from him.","Therefore, even though Liu Weidong was so arrogant and domineering in Longcheng, he had always been perfectly fine. Even when he committed offenses, he was not sent to a labor camp. It was likely that people spared him out of respect for his father.","The inspection team leader said with a dark face, If he keeps this up, the reputation his father has built up over the years will sooner or later be completely ruined by him.","The young police officer lowered his voice and said, It is just that no one has investigated Liu Weidong yet. A person like him could not withstand an investigation at all. Who knows how many bad things he has done behind the scenes.","Liu Weidong was still clamoring to go to the hospital, while the police officers were still waiting for the people from the food factory to come and cooperate with the interrogation.","After all, this case was reported by the food factory's inspection team, so they definitely had to interrogate both sides before closing the case.","At this time, naturally, they could not send Liu Weidong away.","However, the people at the police station were also worried that Liu Weidong's leg might actually be broken. If that were the case, no one would dare take the responsibility.","So, after thinking it over, the police went to a nearby hospital and brought a doctor over to examine Liu Weidong's leg injury.","Liu Weidong sat triumphantly on a chair in the lobby, resting his injured leg on another chair. Pointing at the inspection team leader, he said, You are from the food factory's inspection team, right? What is your name? Let me tell you, if you kneel down and apologize to me right now, I might consider forgiving you. Otherwise, just you wait. I have got my eye on you.","The inspection team leader said with a dark expression, You were the one who started the trouble this time. You better think carefully about what to do now. Intentionally causing trouble at the food factory and bullying female comrades, you should be sent to a labor camp.","Liu Weidong sneered, In this entire Longcheng, there really is no one who dares to send me to a labor camp. As for you, with no backing, you still want to fight with me?","The people from the inspection team stopped talking to him.","After all, there was no point in continuing the argument; Liu Weidong indeed had strong backing.","Because of this, he and his sister had been used to being arrogant and domineering since childhood.","They took others' compliments and flattery for granted.","At this time, Qiao Lanshu, Clerk Zhou, and the security guard uncle from the food factory all arrived.","Liu Weidong's leg injury had also been bandaged. The doctor said to him, Your leg bone is fine, it is just a superficial wound. I have bandaged it for you.","The police officers were all speechless. It was clearly just a superficial wound, yet he claimed his leg was broken. This kind of person was just doing it on purpose.","Liu Weidong had just stood up and looked at his bandaged leg when he turned and saw Qiao Lanshu walking into the police station. Pointing at her, he said fiercely, You broke my leg! I am going to sue you for intentional injury. This time, no matter who it is, no one can save you!","Clerk Zhou frowned and scolded, It was clearly you who impersonated someone from the personnel section to look for someone at the food factory, and then started hitting people as soon as you saw us. We were all hit by you. Who exactly is committing intentional injury?","Regardless of what they said, Liu Weidong just propped his injured leg on the table and said stubbornly, You say I hit people? Do you have proof? I am the one who is injured, not you! I am the victim. Anyway, today I demand an explanation from your food factory, otherwise, I will not let this go.","Clerk Zhou and the security guard uncle were both a bit speechless.","They had never seen such a shameless person.","It was clearly him who started the trouble, but just because he got injured, he acted like he was in the right.","The police officer walked over and asked Qiao Lanshu, Comrade Xiao Qiao, what exactly happened? You had better tell the truth, we need to record it here.","Qiao Lanshu's eyes were slightly red. She reached out to hold her stomach, her face a bit pale as she said, I... I do not know either. My stomach hurts so much...","Before the police officer could react, Clerk Zhou, the security guard uncle, and the others hurriedly gathered around. Supporting Qiao Lanshu, they asked nervously, Comrade Xiao Qiao, are you okay? How do you feel?","Holding her stomach, Qiao Lanshu whispered, I do not feel very well. He is too scary. My stomach hurts as soon as I see him.","Liu Weidong: ...","In disbelief, Liu Weidong pointed at his own nose and asked, Who? Me?","The security guard uncle said grumpily, If not you, could it be me?","Liu Weidong: ...","Liu Weidong felt that this woman, Qiao Lanshu, was truly too wicked.","She obviously had such a pretty and obedient face, but she was so scheming, and everyone around her was fooled by her! Yet not a single person saw her true colors!","No wonder his sister was no match for her.","Look at these tactics, it was simply too sinister!","Hearing Qiao Lanshu say her stomach hurt, the people from the food factory were all very anxious. The inspection team members said urgently, Quick, quick, hurry and take her to the hospital for a check-up. We absolutely cannot let anything bad happen to her.","With that, the group of people hurriedly escorted Qiao Lanshu out of the police station and headed to the hospital.","Before leaving, Clerk Zhou pointed at Liu Weidong and said, You just wait right here in the police station. If anything happens to Comrade Xiao Qiao, you just wait to eat a bullet.","Liu Weidong: ...","Liu Weidong limped to the main entrance and said in exasperation, Are these people from the food factory sick in the head? My leg is crippled, and they did not even apologize; but that chick says her stomach hurts, and they panic and run off?","Seeing how nervous the people from the food factory were, the police officers were also afraid something might happen, so they quickly dispatched two officers to follow them.","Liu Weidong stood up angrily, wanting to follow them too, but he was grabbed by a police officer. The officer said, Liu Weidong, do not follow them. Did you not hear her say she gets scared just seeing you?","Liu Weidong cursed, Bullshit! She is faking it. Can you not tell it is so fake?","Saying that, he forcefully pushed the officer away and limped out on his own.","The public security officers quickly chased after him to the main gate, trying to pull Liu Weidong back.","Just as the group was scuffling at the gate, a military vehicle pulled up at the entrance of the public security bureau.","Qin Yuanzheng, who had just gotten off work at the military base, arrived.","Qin Yuanzheng had gotten off work early and went to the food factory full of anticipation to pick up his little wife.","However, when he arrived at the factory, he was told that his wife had been taken to the public security bureau.","Upon further questioning, he learned the whole story.","Someone impersonating a personnel section clerk had come looking for Qiao Lanshu. The moment they met, the person started hurling insults and even tried to hit her. Fortunately, some comrades helped block the attack, otherwise, his wife would have been in danger.","The critical part was that his wife had panicked, hid in a car, and accidentally started the vehicle.","Hearing this news, Qin Yuanzheng broke out in a cold sweat on the spot.","He immediately drove toward the public security bureau.","Before the car even came to a complete stop, he saw Qiao Lanshu being supported by some male comrades. She was clutching her stomach with one hand, and her complexion looked quite poor.","Qin Yuanzheng's heart clenched. He jumped out of the car before it even stabilized and sprinted toward her. Qiao Lanshu!","Whenever Qin Yuanzheng was anxious, he would call Qiao Lanshu by her full name.","Hearing him yell like this, Qiao Lanshu quickly stood up straight. I'm here.","She stood straight for exactly one second before quickly clutching her stomach again, saying awkwardly, Brother Zheng, why are you here so early?","Qin Yuanzheng's face was dark. He pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms and looked at the hand covering her stomach, asking with a tense expression, Is your stomach uncomfortable? Does it hurt?","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Qiao Lanshu wasn't actually in pain. She just couldn't stand seeing Liu Weidong acting as if his leg injury put him in the right.","Liu Weidong was clearly the one who came to make trouble, yet he had the audacity to claim he was the victim.","So she deliberately said her stomach hurt. She was a pregnant woman, after all. If she was scared into having stomach pains, shouldn't Liu Weidong admit his mistake and apologize to her?","But she had terrified Qin Yuanzheng, and Qiao Lanshu felt guilty.","She whispered, Brother Zheng, actually I'm not...","Her voice was too quiet, and the security guard uncle was far more anxious than she was. He recognized Qin Yuanzheng, considering Qin Yuanzheng came to pick up his wife every single day.","So, the security guard uncle loudly complained, Commander Qin, today was a real disaster! Comrade Xiao Qiao was terrified by that bastard Liu Weidong, and it disturbed her pregnancy! You have no idea, the moment Liu Weidong saw Comrade Xiao Qiao, he threatened to hit her, saying he wanted to vent his sister's anger. Oh, and his sister is no good either. She's the one who posted those big-character posters targeting Comrade Xiao Qiao.","Qin Yuanzheng's face grew incredibly grim and dark. He stared at Qiao Lanshu and asked, Your pregnancy was disturbed? Does your stomach hurt a lot?","Just then, Liu Weidong also chased his way out, limping and cursing under his breath.","Qin Yuanzheng suddenly turned his head and glared at Liu Weidong. Then, with a dark expression, he walked over and, without a word, kicked Liu Weidong right in the stomach.","Liu Weidong was sent flying backward.","Everyone: ...","The crowd shrank their necks in fear.","Liu Weidong clutched his stomach and collapsed to the ground, his face turning pale.","He hadn't even registered what had happened before he felt himself flying through the air.","In all his years of running wild, this was the first time he had taken a beating.","Now look at him. He originally just had an injured leg, but now his stomach had been kicked. It hurt like hell, and he might have even suffered internal injuries.","He felt as if his internal organs had been shattered by the kick. Writhing in agony, he howled, Who the hell kicked me! Do you know who my dad is? I'll fucking kill you!","Qin Yuanzheng walked over with a dark face, his eyes cold enough to kill. Staring at Liu Weidong, he said frostily, Section Chief Liu of the Wenxing County Personnel Section, right? I'd like to go ask him exactly how I, Qin Yuanzheng, have offended him, that both his son and daughter feel the need to bully my wife like this!","Saying this, Qin Yuanzheng turned to the public security officers. Handcuff Liu Weidong. Until this case is thoroughly interrogated and cleared up, he is not to be released. Otherwise, I will drag him straight to the military base and interrogate him myself.","He actually wanted to interrogate the man personally, but he had to accompany his wife to the hospital, so he could only wait until tomorrow to see the results.","The public security officers could easily tell that Liu Weidong had kicked an iron plate this time.","Daring to bully a military officer's family member, he was simply audacious beyond belief.","Even if his father knew a lot of officials, so what? The military was entirely different from those local cadres.","The military certainly wouldn't let Liu Weidong off the hook just because of a personnel section chief.","Qin Yuanzheng scooped Qiao Lanshu up into his arms and placed her in his car. He thanked the security guard uncle, Clerk Zhou, and the others, telling them to head back first while he accompanied Qiao Lanshu to the hospital.","On the way, Qiao Lanshu said, feeling a bit embarrassed, Brother Zheng, we don't need to go to the hospital. My stomach is fine.","Qin Yuanzheng's dark expression still hadn't eased. He turned to look at Qiao Lanshu and asked in a low voice, Your stomach doesn't hurt anymore?","Qiao Lanshu nodded. It doesn't hurt. It never hurt in the first place. It's just that Liu Weidong was bullying people too much, so I pretended on purpose.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng had actually noticed that his wife didn't really look like she was in pain. It was just that she was pregnant, so he was a bit worried.","He slowed the car down and asked again, They said you accidentally drove a car away? What was that all about?","Qiao Lanshu: ..."]},{"number":140,"title":"Chapter 140: Father Liu Comes to Apologize","paragraphs":["Once Qin Yuanzheng knew Qiao Lanshu's stomach no longer hurt, his previously tense mood instantly relaxed.","He drove slowly and asked Qiao Lanshu, \"I just heard from the guard at your food factory. He said that in a moment of panic, you hid in a car, accidentally drove it forward, and knocked that Liu Weidong into a ditch?\"","Qiao Lanshu felt a bit guilty. She didn't want to lie to Qin Yuanzheng, but she hadn't quite figured out how to explain this matter yet.","Seeing that Qiao Lanshu remained silent, Qin Yuanzheng turned his head and cast a glance at her.","Then, he immediately pulled the car over.","Seeing him stop the car, Qiao Lanshu grew incredibly nervous. She immediately sat up straight, her back perfectly erect and her hands resting on her thighs, looking the picture of perfect obedience.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her, completely at a loss for what to do with her.","He asked, \"When did you learn how to drive? How come I've never heard you mention it?\"","Qiao Lanshu said, feeling somewhat embarrassed, \"Brother Zheng, what makes you think I know how to drive?\"","Qin Yuanzheng gave her a small smile and said, \"If you didn't know how to drive, you wouldn't have hidden inside a car.\"","After spending this period of time together, Qin Yuanzheng had come to understand his little wife quite well.","Although Qiao Lanshu was young, she was surprisingly sensible and well-versed in the ways of the world.","On the surface, she appeared sweet and soft, like a naive youth who knew nothing of the world.","But in her heart, she had a clear plan for everything.","Qin Yuanzheng guessed that her hiding in the car was probably the best way to protect herself under the circumstances at the time.","The only thing Qin Yuanzheng didn't know was when Qiao Lanshu had learned to drive.","He asked her, \"Did you learn to drive back in your hometown in Yangcheng? Did your father teach you?\"","Qiao Lanshu's father was the manager of a department store; it was perfectly normal for someone in his position to know how to drive.","Just as Qin Yuanzheng was thinking this, he heard Qiao Lanshu say, \"I think I learned it in a dream.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her silently, his face devoid of expression.","Qiao Lanshu felt a bit guilty. She whispered, \"It's, it's just like when I dreamed about that man with a scar on his face before. In my dreams, I can drive too.\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't speak. He just looked at her silently for a good while, probably not knowing what to say.","He wanted to properly interrogate her, but he also had to take her pregnancy into consideration.","Observing his expression, Qiao Lanshu added, \"Brother Zheng, everything I'm saying is true. In the dream, you were even the one who taught me how to drive. When I drove the car into a ditch, you didn't even scold me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","She made it sound so real.","He sighed inwardly, reached out to rub Qiao Lanshu's head, and said softly, \"Alright then.\"","As he spoke, he started the car again and said, \"I'll take you to the hospital to get checked out.\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. \"There's no need. I'm really fine.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was still worried, so he took Qiao Lanshu to the hospital anyway. After finally confirming that she was fine, he picked up some medicine to protect the pregnancy and they headed back.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't return to the police station; he took Qiao Lanshu straight home.","Qiao Lanshu asked him with some concern, \"Brother Zheng, how are we going to deal with that Liu Weidong matter?\"","Having brought her home, Qin Yuanzheng heard her question and asked in return, \"What do you think? How do you want to handle it?\"","Qiao Lanshu fell silent for a moment before saying quietly:","\"I don't think this Liu Weidong is a good person. He doesn't even respect military dependents, bullying them on a whim. Who knows how many people he usually bullies. It would be great if we could send him to a labor camp. He refuses to go to the countryside and doesn't work, just spending his days in the city bullying men and oppressing women. His existence is just a waste of the country's grain.\"","Qiao Lanshu truly despised Liu Weidong.","In fact, in her previous life, she had heard of Liu Weidong.","At that time, Liu Weihong wasn't at the food factory, and no one knew where she had gone, so Qiao Lanshu didn't know Liu Weihong.","But as for Liu Weidong, he had been a director at the Longcheng Labor Bureau. In her previous life, he had profited by selling jobs.","Under the guise of recruiting workers for construction sites, he sold construction jobs to young people who didn't want to go to the countryside or who wanted to work in the city. He charged five hundred yuan for a single job!","Qiao Lanshu had only heard this in passing, knowing that there was such a person named Liu Weidong in the Labor Bureau.","As for how Liu Weidong obtained that position and what happened to him later, Qiao Lanshu had no idea.","Qin Yuanzheng listened to Qiao Lanshu as he hung his changed clothes on the wall.","He nodded thoughtfully. \"You're right. This Liu Weidong doesn't seem like a good person. I'll arrange for someone to investigate him tomorrow. I reckon he's committed quite a few offenses.\"","No matter how well-connected Liu Weidong's father was, crossing paths with Qin Yuanzheng meant he had hit a brick wall.","Qin Yuanzheng never cared about other people's status when handling matters.","The military and the government were two separate systems. These interpersonal connections might work across various government departments, but in the military, they were completely useless.","Qin Yuanzheng said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Leave Liu Weidong's matter to me. Don't worry about it for now. Get some good rest while I go make you something to eat.\"","With that, Qin Yuanzheng gave Qiao Lanshu a kiss and went into the kitchen to cook.","In this day and age, there wasn't much entertainment to be had at home.","Qiao Lanshu turned on the radio and started listening to the broadcast.","The radio content nowadays was actually quite rich. Besides the news, it also covered international current affairs, which were the programs Qin Yuanzheng loved to listen to.","Qiao Lanshu preferred listening to the Reading Appreciation segment, which guided listeners through classic literature.","Aside from that, there were also opera performances, singing, and storytelling.","Qiao Lanshu tuned the radio to the local news station and sat on the sofa, listening as she drank some goat's milk.","Upon hearing one particular news report, Qiao Lanshu's expression suddenly turned serious. She quickly jumped off the sofa and, without even taking the time to put on her shoes, ran into the kitchen and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, Brother Zheng, come listen quickly! The news says there was an explosion somewhere in Longcheng.\"","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng heard this, his face instantly grew stern. \"Where was the explosion?\"","Ever since Chu Liangjun stole explosives from the construction site last time, the already strict management within the engineering corps had become even stricter.","Explosives were uniformly managed by the military. Any construction site that needed explosives had to get an approval slip from the troops. The officer who approved the explosives had to accompany them on-site during use and could only leave after the detonation was complete.","Even though he knew there were definitely no issues with the military's management.","But hearing this news now, Qin Yuanzheng's heart still subconsciously tightened, worried that a problem had occurred at a construction site under his jurisdiction again.","Qin Yuanzheng walked briskly from the kitchen to the living room. Standing in the hall with Qiao Lanshu, he frowned as he listened to the radio.","On the radio, the announcer's tone was also very serious, stating that shortly after six o'clock in the evening, a residential house on West Street in Longcheng had suddenly exploded. Fortunately, there were no fatalities, but two people had been injured and were already rushed to the hospital.","The public security officers and the militia from the street patrol team had arrived at the scene immediately. Their preliminary assessment was that the explosion was not an accident, but a deliberate act.","They could determine at the scene that it was caused by explosives, but the source of the explosives remained unknown.","Furthermore, it was unclear who had planted the explosives or if there were any personal grudges involved. Everything was still under investigation.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"It happened just after six in the evening, right when we were heading home.\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at the clock in their house; it was already around half past seven.","It seemed the explosion occurred while they were on their way back.","Qin Yuanzheng said with a serious expression, \"It's the end of the year, and an explosion happens in the city just as the inspection teams are about to arrive. This matter must be handled well. If not, a large number of officials in the city will probably be replaced.\"","Qiao Lanshu was also very worried about the situation.","Qin Yuanzheng stood there in silence for a moment before saying, \"The military hasn't notified me, so let's not worry about it for now. I'll make dinner for you first; eating is more important.\"","With that, he returned to the kitchen to cook, his heart still heavy with concern.","However, because of the incident with Liu Weidong and the explosion, the couple both had a lot on their minds. After dinner, they listened to the radio together for over an hour but didn't hear any further reports of explosions.","Qin Yuanzheng sighed and turned off the radio, then said to Qiao Lanshu, \"It's getting late. Let's go to bed. Tomorrow will probably be very busy.\"","As he spoke, he picked Qiao Lanshu up in his arms, and the two of them went back to the kang bed and lay down.","Qin Yuanzheng habitually wrapped his arms around her, buried his face in her neck, took a deep breath, and murmured, \"Wife, you smell so good.\"","Qiao Lanshu felt a tickle on her neck. She pushed his face away slightly and scolded him, \"Stop messing around, your stubble is scratching me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng touched his chin, realizing he hadn't shaved in two days. Usually, at this time, he would be having his midnight snack.","Unfortunately, too much had happened today, and he didn't want to exhaust his wife.","So he simply held her in his arms. Qiao Lanshu had a petite yet curvaceous figure. He lay on his side and had her lie on hers, pulling her into his embrace. The position was just perfect.","They truly were a match made in heaven.","Thinking this, his hand habitually slipped under her clothes.","His large, rough hand carried a scorching heat. Unable to resist him, Qiao Lanshu could only let him be.","Qin Yuanzheng closed his eyes, his hot breath brushing against her ear as he whispered, \"Wife, they seem to have gotten bigger again.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"Will I be able to taste them soon...\"","Qiao Lanshu covered his mouth. \"Shut up.\"","Qin Yuanzheng's hand moved further down to caress her belly.","Her belly was still very flat; in fact, it felt no different from usual.","But Qin Yuanzheng just felt like it had grown, even imagining he could feel a heartbeat inside.","His hand slowly stroked her stomach as he thought about how he was going to be a father.","However, he actually had no idea how to be a father.","Truthfully, he wasn't fully prepared yet.","...","Early the next morning, Zhao Jiannong from next door came knocking.","He said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"There was an explosion on West Street last night. Did you know about it?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"I know.\"","Zhao Jiannong lowered his voice and said, \"Let's go. Don't head to the mining area today. We both need to make a trip to the headquarters. This matter probably isn't simple; it might be a terrorist attack.\"","As soon as these words were spoken, both of their expressions turned grim.","Qiao Lanshu also sensed the tense atmosphere between them, which made her even more worried.","It seemed this incident was quite serious.","After Qiao Lanshu arrived at the food factory, Qin Yuanzheng and Zhao Jiannong drove off together toward the headquarters building.","When Qiao Lanshu arrived at work, the security guard uncle was also on duty. Seeing her walk through the gate, he immediately came out and said to her, \"Xiao Qiao, how is that case with Liu Weidong going? Can your military husband send him to a labor camp?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","She sighed softly and said, \"Just based on what happened yesterday, I'm afraid we can't send him to a labor camp.\"","To send him to labor reform, they would need to find other leverage against him.","The guard said regretfully, \"That bastard, he really is a piece of work. If he dares to come back next time, I'll definitely let the dogs loose on him!\"","The guard had dogs at home and was planning to bring them to the factory to keep for a few days.","If Liu Weidong dared to show his face again, he would lock the gates and release the hounds!","Lowering his voice, the guard continued, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, you must be careful from now on. Don't go out alone. I asked around with the public security comrades, and this Liu Weidong is truly bad news.\"","His voice dropped even lower, as if afraid of being overheard, and he added with a hint of nervousness, \"This Liu Weidong often uses making revolution as an excuse to bully young girls and wives. Anyway, just watch your back.\"","Nowadays, people threatened to report others and make revolution over the slightest things. Ordinary folks were terrified of these people and wouldn't dare cross them.","Even the security guard felt a lingering fear.","Fortunately, when Liu Weidong came to cause trouble yesterday, he wasn't wearing his green uniform. Otherwise, they might not have dared to fight him.","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu immediately understood.","She pondered in her heart: Making revolution? Isn't that under the jurisdiction of the Revolutionary Committee?","And isn't the head of the Revolutionary Committee Guan Wenjun?","Then could Guan Wenjun control Liu Weidong?","With these thoughts in mind, she walked toward the workshops inside the factory.","Halfway there, she was stopped by a colleague from the office.","The colleague told her, \"Warehouse Manager, go to the factory director's office. The director is looking for you.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Left with no choice, Qiao Lanshu changed her route and headed to the director's office.","At this very moment, in the director's office, Liu Weidong's father, Liu Zhengxing, was sitting in Yang Wenyan's office.","Both Yang Wenyan and Secretary Wen were in the office, drinking tea with Liu Zhengxing.","When Qiao Lanshu walked in, the three of them were talking. It was obvious that Secretary Wen wore a very polite expression, looking as though he didn't dare offend the other man.","Yang Wenyan's face looked a bit grim. He had only found out that Liu Weidong came to cause trouble for Qiao Lanshu after returning last night.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu enter, Yang Wenyan quickly stood up and said to her, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, this is Section Chief Liu Zhengxing. He is Liu Weidong's father, and he has come here today to apologize to you.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu wondered if she had heard correctly.","Liu Zhengxing was the section chief of the personnel department; usually, others were the ones flattering him.","Why would he come to apologize to an ordinary female worker like her?","However, Liu Zhengxing's purpose in coming to the food factory this time was indeed to apologize to Qiao Lanshu.","He stood up, looked at Qiao Lanshu, and smiled. \"You must be Comrade Qiao Lanshu. I am truly sorry. I only just found out today that Weidong came and caused trouble for you. It is my failure as a father for not disciplining him properly. I will definitely teach him a good lesson later. I hope you can forgive him this once and not hold it against him.\""]},{"number":141,"title":"Chapter 141: The Old Fox","paragraphs":["No one expected that Liu Zhengxing would personally come to apologize.","When Yang Wenyan arrived at work in the morning and heard he had come, he was quite shocked.","Most people would feel embarrassed to receive his apology, and then the matter regarding Liu Weidong would just be let go.","After all, as the chief of the personnel section, he had personally come to apologize to a lowly female worker. If this female worker refused to accept it, she would be considered too ungrateful.","This Liu Zhengxing was indeed smart, but unfortunately, his son and daughter were both good-for-nothings.","Everyone was waiting for Qiao Lanshu's reply.","Liu Zhengxing was slightly plump and tall. He always had a smile on his face, but the look in his eyes when observing people was very profound.","At first glance, he was an old fox who knew exactly how to manipulate people.","Qiao Lanshu remained silent for a moment. Secretary Wen grew a bit anxious and urged her, Comrade Xiao Qiao, what are you thinking now? Say something.","Liu Zhengxing smiled and said, No rush. Comrade Xiao Qiao can take her time to think about it. I am not in a hurry.","Saying that, he added,","This matter is indeed the fault of my unfilial son. I have been too busy with work these past two years, so I neglected the two children at home, which allowed them to make these mistakes. Comrade Xiao Qiao, I have also heard about my daughter putting up big-character posters about you. Rest assured, I will have the two of them come over tomorrow to apologize to you in person.","Since Liu Zhengxing had come personally, Qiao Lanshu certainly could not keep dwelling on this matter.","Otherwise, if word got out, who knew what would happen to her reputation.","Qiao Lanshu then said, Section Chief Liu, I don't really blame them, but what I don't understand is why they targeted me. First the big-character posters, then pretending to be personnel section staff to call me out... Without clarifying the reason, I am worried they will come looking for trouble again next time.","Liu Zhengxing stared at Qiao Lanshu for a few moments before saying,","Well, I haven't asked yet either. Weidong has been at the police station since last night, and I haven't even seen him. But rest assured, I can guarantee that the two of them will not cause you trouble again. If they do, just come tell me, and I will deal with them for you.","Since he had said this much, Qiao Lanshu nodded and said, Section Chief Liu, with your word, I am relieved.","At this point, the matter was considered settled. Liu Zhengxing even offered to treat Qiao Lanshu to a meal, but how could she dare to go.","She might end up being poisoned by him.","As soon as Liu Zhengxing left the food factory, Liu Weidong was released from the police station.","Although Qin Yuanzheng had previously said that he wanted the police to investigate the case thoroughly, and he was planning to find time to go to the police station to question Liu Weidong himself.","However, before the military could intervene, Liu Zhengxing personally went to apologize to Qiao Lanshu, and then took Liu Weidong home on the grounds that the two parties had reconciled.","Deng Weijun, who hadn't been to the warehouse workshop for a long time, rushed over to talk to Qiao Lanshu after hearing the news, Sister-in-law, I heard that guy surnamed Liu was released?","Qiao Lanshu nodded.","Deng Weijun slapped his thigh and said angrily, You shouldn't have accepted their apology. Letting them off so easily is too cheap for him.","Saying that, he lowered his voice, I just went to check. That Liu Weihong still didn't come to work today. She probably doesn't have the face to show up. If she dared to come, I would definitely go over and give her a piece of my mind.","The moment Qiao Lanshu saw Liu Zhengxing, she knew the police station couldn't hold Liu Weidong.","She whispered, Brother Zheng said that just based on Liu Weidong impersonating someone from the personnel section to call me out, he can't be sentenced to labor reform. The military is the most fair and just, and they wouldn't impose a heavy sentence for a minor offense. So, since he was going to get out anyway, it was better to accept Section Chief Liu's apology, to avoid giving them another excuse to target me and Brother Zheng.","Liu Zhengxing looked like someone who was hard to deal with, completely different from the siblings Liu Weihong and Liu Weidong.","As long as Liu Weidong was released, he would naturally expose his own flaws later on.","Deng Weijun actually understood this reasoning too.","After all, Section Chief Liu had personally come to apologize. If Qiao Lanshu still refused to let it go, it would cause a lot of trouble.","Deng Weijun was still cursing, This Liu Weidong, I've heard of him before. He is very well-connected in the Longcheng area. He loves playing cards, frequently changes girlfriends, and has bad luck, so he often loses money. But he has a lot of money and isn't afraid to lose.","Qiao Lanshu immediately asked, Weijun, do you know this Liu Weidong?","Deng Weijun replied, I know him, but he doesn't know me.","After all, Liu Weidong was very popular, and many young people in Longcheng had heard of him.","His reputation wasn't very good either. Whenever he saw a pretty girl, he would force her to date him. Some girls were scared just hearing his name.","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice and said, He is out of the police station now. Please keep an eye out for any news about him these next few days. I want to see what he is up to.","Qiao Lanshu spoke tactfully, but Deng Weijun understood.","Qiao Lanshu wanted to watch for Liu Weidong to make a mistake so she could report him and have him arrested for labor reform.","Deng Weijun immediately said, Sister-in-law, don't worry! Leave this matter to me, I will definitely get it done perfectly for you.","Saying that, Deng Weijun hurried off.","...","On the other side, as soon as Liu Weidong was released from the police station, he immediately went home.","Upon arriving home, he saw that his father, Liu Zhengxing, and Liu Weihong were both there.","Liu Weihong was staying at home because she had been demoted and felt too ashamed to go to work.","Liu Zhengxing, on the other hand, was specifically waiting at home for Liu Weidong to return.","Liu Weidong limped into the house. Looking at Liu Zhengxing, he asked in surprise, Dad? Why didn't you go to work today? It's already this late, why are you still at home?","Liu Zhengxing looked at Liu Weidong with a cold and dark expression. Suddenly, he slammed his hand on the table and scolded, If I weren't at home today, do you think you could have come back in one piece?","Liu Weidong said nonchalantly, Dad, I'm not in one piece either. My leg is injured.","Liu Zhengxing was speechless.","Liu Zhengxing stood up, took a few steps to Liu Weidong, pointed at him, and said, Didn't I warn you? I don't care how you mess around outside normally, but there is only one thing: do not offend the military personnel. Why didn't you listen?","Liu Weidong replied, Dad, I've always remembered that. I didn't offend anyone from the military.","Liu Zhengxing sneered, You didn't? Then how did you get arrested and taken to the police station this time? And why were you kept overnight without the police releasing you? Wasn't it because you offended a military family member?","Liu Weidong felt a bit guilty, but he still said, It's just a military family member, it shouldn't matter that much, right? Besides, look, haven't I come back now?","Speaking of this, Liu Weidong said rather smugly, I knew it, Dad, you would definitely have a way.","Slap.","Liu Zhengxing slapped Liu Weidong across the face.","Liu Weidong was beaten silly. Liu Weihong, who had been sitting in the living room watching the drama unfold, instantly changed her expression upon seeing this. She quickly stood up and hurriedly retreated to her room.","Liu Weidong looked at his father in disbelief. Dad, why did you hit me? I didn't even do anything wrong, what was that for?","Looking at his son, Liu Zhengxing suddenly felt a deep wave of exhaustion.","He lowered his voice and said sternly, You need to lay low for a while. Stop selling that powder for now. Wait a month or two until the new municipal party secretary takes office, then we will see.","Somewhat baffled, Liu Weidong asked, Dad, how do you know our municipal party secretary is being replaced? Besides, I am very careful when I sell that powder. No one will ever find out.","Liu Zhengxing's expression grew grave. Haven't you been listening to the radio news? The inspection team is coming soon, and they are tightening security everywhere. If your business gets discovered, not even God himself could save you!","Liu Weidong still did not take it seriously. He argued, You are telling me not to sell the powder, but you always come to me for money. If I don't sell that stuff, where is our family going to get money from? Weren't you pretty supportive of it before?","Liu Zhengxing had indeed taken quite a bit of money from his son.","Because of this, his tone lost some of its edge. He just said with a hint of impatience, Anyway, for the time being, you had better just stay home and recover from your injuries. Do not go out, and definitely do not sell that stuff. Wait until this blows over before you think about doing it again, understand?","Liu Weidong did not take these words to heart at all, but on the surface, he nodded. After all, he was still somewhat afraid of his father.","He nodded and said impatiently, I know, I know. I won't sell it, alright?","Seeing his son agree, Liu Zhengxing finally felt relieved. He turned around and left the house to go to work.","Liu Weidong returned to his own room, pulled back his bedding, and lifted the wooden bed board underneath. A large stash of items was piled beneath it.","The goods were wrapped in oil paper, forming small rectangles about two fingers wide, all arranged in neat, tidy rows.","He took out a packet, examined it, and murmured with a tinge of regret, What a pity. Such valuable stuff!","Just one tiny piece could sell for an astronomical price of over a hundred yuan, making it even more profitable than gold.","Over the past two years, the money he had earned from selling this had been exchanged into thick stacks of cash, all hidden beneath another section of his bed board.","Even though he had promised Liu Zhengxing that he would stop selling.","He still felt he had to deliver the orders his customers had already placed.","Besides, he had made countless drops before. Surely, nothing would go wrong with just one or two more deliveries.","With that thought in mind, Liu Weidong took two pieces from the stash, slipped them into his pocket, and prepared to head out once it got dark."]},{"number":142,"title":"Chapter 142: Tracking Liu Weidong","paragraphs":["Because of the dynamite explosion on West Street in Longcheng, Qin Yuanzheng and Zhao Jiannong both went to the headquarters building for a meeting.","All military units and construction sites were thoroughly checked, but no dynamite was reported missing.","This made the problem even more serious.","Because it meant that certain people in the city possessed an unknown quantity of explosives.","Moreover, the use of these explosives was beyond their control.","If they dared to bomb West Street today, they might bomb other streets tomorrow.","The danger level was simply too high. All surrounding military districts and troops had to raise their alert levels and begin patrolling their respective jurisdictions until the culprits were caught.","After the meeting, Qin Yuanzheng and Zhao Jiannong walked out with several people from other battalions. Everyone wore stern and solemn expressions.","Zhao Jiannong said in a low voice, \"It seems our side here in Longcheng has been infiltrated as well.\"","Another battalion commander frowned and said, \"Of all times for an explosion, it had to happen right when the inspection team came down. Who knows, they might be trying to turn Longcheng upside down.\"","Longcheng was a major coal-mining hub. Troops were stationed here to mine coal and build roads, and the neighboring city even had plans to construct an airport in the next few years.","If such an important city were infiltrated and its leading cadres replaced by their people, the consequences would be unimaginable.","Zhao Jiannong added, \"The main issue is that we currently have no clues. We don't even know how the perpetrators managed to bury the dynamite on West Street. According to nearby residents, they didn't hear any commotion day or night, nor had they made any enemies.\"","In short, it was utterly baffling. West Street wasn't an important street, and leaders rarely passed through there.","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent for a long time, listening to their discussion, before finally speaking up. \"Or perhaps it's because West Street has fewer people, and military personnel rarely go there, making it an easy target. They might just be intentionally causing a stir to force the inspection team from above to launch an investigation.\"","Zhao Jiannong quickly asked, \"Will they strike West Street again next?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"West Street has already drawn attention, and the militia will step up their patrols. They probably won't go there again.\"","Zhao Jiannong asked, \"Then where do you think they'll go next?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head again. \"It's hard to say.\"","The group fell into a brief silence. Although patrols had been strengthened throughout the city...","...if the enemy really wanted to cause a disturbance, it would still be very difficult to prevent.","The men parted ways with heavy hearts.","They each had to return to their units to arrange their work, and Qin Yuanzheng also had to keep a close eye on the time to pick up his wife from work.","Especially under such special circumstances, he felt it was absolutely necessary to escort Qiao Lanshu to and from work.","Otherwise, he simply wouldn't have peace of mind.","When work ended in the afternoon, Wang Xue and Deng Weijun came looking for Qiao Lanshu to take her to Yang Wenyan's house for dinner.","Wang Xue was carrying some sheep offal and radishes, while Deng Weijun was holding some flour.","Since they were going to dine at Yang Wenyan's house, it wouldn't be polite to show up empty-handed, so they had all bought some things in advance.","Qiao Lanshu was a bit surprised to see them. \"Sister, Weijun, what brings you two here?\"","As she spoke, she checked the main door of the warehouse and locked the door to the small cabin as well.","Deng Weijun looked a bit embarrassed by the question. He stood aside, scratching his head, waiting for Wang Xue to explain.","Wang Xue glanced at him and said to Qiao Lanshu with a smile, \"What else could it be? It's about Haitang and Weijun, of course. Originally, this matter was supposed to wait until the New Year, when Weijun would visit Haitang's home to meet her parents before discussing it...\"","At this point, Wang Xue sighed. She rested a hand on Qiao Lanshu's arm, and the two walked out side by side.","Deng Weijun followed behind them, carrying his items.","He used to be quite talkative and didn't pay much attention to the physical distance between men and women.","However, he had been thoroughly spooked by the big-character poster incident from last time. Now, whenever they were outside, he didn't dare get too close to Qiao Lanshu, nor did he dare speak too much.","Hearing Wang Xue's words, Qiao Lanshu asked in a low voice, \"What's wrong? Did something major happen suddenly?\"","Feeling a bit upset, Wang Xue sighed and whispered, \"Sometimes I think I've really dragged Weijun into a mess. Haitang's parents are truly awful people.\"","Wang Haitang was Wang Xue's cousin, and Haitang's father was Wang Xue's biological uncle.","Despite such a close blood relation, Wang Xue had never liked Haitang's parents.","She said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Originally, Haitang and Weijun were getting along quite well. Weijun's family background is also good. Even though his parents live in a village, both he and his sister hold urban household registrations. His brother-in-law is a factory director, and he himself has a formal job. With such great conditions, you'd think Haitang's parents would be satisfied, right? But guess what?\"","Playing along, Qiao Lanshu asked softly, \"What happened? Are her parents dissatisfied with Weijun and refusing to let them date?\"","Wang Xue scoffed coldly and said indignantly, \"Not exactly. But they demanded a bride price of five hundred yuan from Weijun, saying they wouldn't accept a single cent less!\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","When Qiao Lanshu married Qin Yuanzheng, they didn't seem to have discussed a bride price at all. She didn't even know what the standard bride price was for marriages around here.","Wang Xue said quietly, \"In this day and age, how much is a person's monthly wage? When city folks get married, the bride price is usually fifty or a hundred yuan. Then there's the three spinning items and one ticking item—if you can afford it, you buy them; if not, providing thirty-six legs of furniture is fine too. Like when I got married, my family only asked for a fifty-yuan bride price and a sewing machine.\"","A sewing machine wasn't cheap; a single one could cost one or two hundred yuan.","But sewing machines were bought for the new small family. Nowadays, supply and marketing cooperatives rarely sold ready-made clothes. Everyone just bought fabric to take home and made their own clothes to wear.","Having a sewing machine at home made mending and sewing much more convenient.","Wang Xue cursed as she spoke, \"Who ever heard of such black-hearted parents? Demanding a five-hundred-yuan bride price from Weijun right off the bat! They haven't even met Weijun; they just wrote a letter to Haitang and me, telling us to ask Weijun for the money. They said if he has the bride price, they can discuss marriage, and if not, the deal is off. They are flat-out selling their daughter! They don't care about her at all.\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu also felt troubled.","She glanced back at Deng Weijun, who just smiled at her without saying a word.","Deng Weijun was probably worrying about it too, likely still weighing whether he should marry this girl or not.","It wasn't that he didn't have feelings for her, but encountering such parents-in-law meant that no matter how deep his feelings were, he had to think twice.","Qiao Lanshu fell silent as well, not knowing what to say.","After a while, she finally asked, \"What does my cousin-in-law say?\"","Wang Xue: \"Deng Xiaozhen discussed it with me, and I went to ask Haitang. Haitang said she doesn't want a bride price; she has decided to follow Weijun. Now, let's all go have a meal together to bear witness for the two of them. They will go get their marriage certificate in a few days. Haitang said she will only contact her maiden family after they are married and have a child.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","To think that the usually cowardly Wang Haitang could have such resolve—it truly made her see the girl in a whole new light.","Wang Haitang's parents were farmers in the village. They also had a son at home, who was their absolute treasure.","The son didn't earn any work points in the village and was gluttonous and lazy all day long.","When his parents went with the production team for agricultural work, he would lie at home, making up excuses about this or that hurting. In short, he just wanted to avoid labor and didn't want to work.","Seeing that he was getting older, it was about time for him to find a wife.","But his family hadn't managed to secure a wife for him yet.","Anyway, everyone in the same village knew what kind of character he had, so no one was willing to marry him.","His parents could only look for someone from another village.","If girls from other villages were to marry out, they would definitely demand a high bride price; otherwise, what would be in it for them?","Qiao Lanshu said in a low voice, \"As long as they have thought it through, it's fine. I'm just worried there will be trouble later.\"","Wang Xue sneered, \"Don't worry. Household registration is strictly managed now. My uncle and aunt have never even been to the city. Even if they came, they wouldn't be able to find their way. As long as we don't tell them the address, what can they do?\"","Wang Xue continued, \"What we've discussed now is that the two kids think highly of each other and both want to get married. So, as their older sisters, we'll help them settle the engagement in advance. Haitang won't go back for the New Year either; she'll just say she has to be on duty at the train station.","By the time next New Year rolls around, they might even have a child. If she wants to keep hiding it, she can just keep saying she's on duty. Anyway, as long as she sends her wages back, my uncle doesn't really want Haitang to go home for the New Year. Haitang hasn't been back for the New Year for two years now, and they didn't miss her.\"","If Haitang went home for the New Year, she wouldn't even have a place to sleep and would have to sleep on the floor.","Her father even complained that her coming home wasted food and wouldn't let her eat at home.","Wang Xue sighed as she spoke.","They could only worry more about their own younger siblings. What other way was there?","The three of them chatted as they walked out of the food factory. Qin Yuanzheng hadn't arrived yet, so Wang Xue and Deng Weijun waited with Qiao Lanshu for a few minutes.","Not long after, Deng Weijun suddenly jogged over to Qiao Lanshu and lowered his voice, \"Sister-in-law, I think I saw Liu Weidong!\"","Wang Xue's ears perked up, and she immediately asked, \"Liu Weidong? Which Liu Weidong? The one who came to make trouble at the food factory before?\"","Deng Weijun nodded, pointing to an alley opposite the food factory, and said to the two of them, \"I just saw him passing by over there, limping along. He looked quite comical.\"","Dragon City was only so big. Walking on the streets, one would often run into acquaintances.","Not to mention, Liu Weidong was someone Deng Weijun was specifically keeping an eye on.","Wang Xue sneered, \"His leg is crippled, so what is he doing out? Didn't they say he just got out of the police station? It hasn't been long, and he's out wandering again?\"","Deng Weijun whispered, \"Sister, Sister-in-law, should I quietly follow him and see where he's going?\"","He just felt that Liu Weidong wasn't up to anything good.","Although Qin Yuanzheng said he would find someone to keep an eye on Liu Weidong.","But a bombing had just occurred in the city, and Qiao Lanshu didn't know if Qin Yuanzheng had arranged for someone to come over.","So, she whispered, \"How about we all go over and take a look?\"","She also wanted to know what Liu Weidong was doing out at this time.","After all, it was the dead of winter. It had even snowed a little today, it got dark early, and it was cold outside.","Besides workers going to their shifts, who else would want to go out?","Wouldn't it be better to lie on the heated brick bed at home, crack sunflower seeds, and chat with family?","Wang Xue also thought about the fact that they were going to Factory Manager Yang Wenyan's house for dinner later. She was afraid that if Deng Weijun went alone, it would be hard to meet up later.","She said, \"Alright, let's go together, and then we'll head to Factory Manager Yang's house together.\"","Qiao Lanshu figured they would just go look for a bit, which would probably only delay them by about ten minutes. Coming back to find Qin Yuanzheng later would be fine.","Qin Yuanzheng was probably too busy today and wouldn't arrive that early.","The three of them teamed up and ran toward the alley Liu Weidong had walked down.","It was just past five-thirty in the afternoon, not yet six. The sun had long since set, and the sky was already getting dark.","The alley Liu Weidong took was quite remote, and rarely did anyone walk through it.","There was hardly anyone around. Occasionally someone would pass by, but no one paid any attention to Liu Weidong.","Liu Weidong was wearing a cotton hat with ear flaps and a thick black padded jacket. With his hands tucked into his pockets, he limped down the street.","He usually drove out, but now, his car had been confiscated by Liu Zhengxing. His leg hurt too much to ride a bicycle, so he could only walk.","Delivering one order today and another the day after tomorrow. One order could earn a hundred yuan, which was equivalent to an ordinary worker's salary for three months.","After wandering around, Liu Weidong actually arrived at the entrance of the train station.","There were quite a few people around the train station, so Qiao Lanshu and the other two didn't have to be sneaky anymore.","The three of them stood across from the train station, watching Liu Weidong talk to a tightly bundled-up man at the entrance.","Afterward, the two of them walked side by side into a certain small alley.","Deng Weijun wanted to keep following, but Wang Xue pulled him back. Wang Xue whispered, \"We can't go any further. If we do, they'll spot us.\"","Qiao Lanshu stared at Deng Weijun along the way; she kept feeling like there was something in Deng Weijun's pocket.","People here liked to walk with their hands tucked into their sleeves.","This was mainly to save fabric. Many padded jackets didn't have pockets, and even if they did, the pockets weren't padded with cotton. They were just a thin layer of cloth, which was quite cold.","Hiding one's hands in the sleeves was much warmer.","But Liu Weidong had kept his hands in his pockets the entire way just now.","What was in his pockets?","Why did that man look so excited when he saw Liu Weidong just now?","Wang Xue pulled back the anxious Deng Weijun and the curious Qiao Lanshu.","As she walked back, she said, \"Enough, we really can't go any further. It'll be a disaster if we're discovered. Liu Weidong has strong backing; we absolutely must not clash with him head-on.\"","Qiao Lanshu naturally knew this, so she silently followed Wang Xue back.","Deng Weijun then said, \"Sister, I'm going to pick up Haitang. You and Sister-in-law head back. We'll meet at my cousin's house later.\"","Wang Xue nodded. \"Alright, go ahead. I'll walk Xiao Qiao back first.\"","Saying that, Wang Xue turned to Qiao Lanshu, \"Your Regiment Commander Qin should have arrived at the factory gates by now. Hurry back and find him, otherwise, if he doesn't see you, he'll probably start worrying about you again.\"","Everyone in the food factory already knew just how much Qin Yuanzheng cared about his wife.","Qiao Lanshu was eager to tell Qin Yuanzheng about Liu Weidong, so feeling a bit anxious, she jogged back to the food factory with Wang Xue."]},{"number":143,"title":"Chapter 143: Fishing","paragraphs":["When the two of them returned to the main gate of the food factory, they sure enough saw Qin Yuanzheng's car already parked across the street.","Qin Yuanzheng was wearing a military overcoat and a military cap, with fine snow particles resting on his shoulders. He stood at the factory's main gate, talking to the security guard uncle.","At this time, the workers in the food factory had mostly all left.","There was no one else at the main gate. Qin Yuanzheng stood there, his expression a bit serious, his tall body standing perfectly straight, making him look somewhat cold and stern.","Wang Xue only took a quick glance and didn't dare to go over. She said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Xiao Qiao, I'll be leaving first then. Remember to go to Director Yang's house for dinner tonight!\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded. \"Don't worry, I know.\"","The last time they went to have dinner together was during Deng Weijun and Wang Haitang's blind date.","Going for dinner again now meant they would be discussing Deng Weijun and Wang Haitang's marriage.","In fact, both sides had already agreed to the young couple's marriage. Deng Xiaozhen and Wang Xue, acting as their older sisters, had also discussed and settled all the details.","Today's dinner would serve as Deng Weijun and Wang Haitang's wedding banquet.","They were going to get their marriage certificate in a few days, and then Deng Weijun could apply for housing. Having a house meant having their own little home.","Wang Haitang had no dowry, and she didn't plan on asking for a bride price either.","The couple would pool their money to buy furniture, and their two older sisters and brothers-in-law would chip in a bit more. This way, their little life together would prosper and thrive.","After Wang Xue left, Qiao Lanshu trotted over towards Qin Yuanzheng.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng saw Qiao Lanshu actually running, the cold and stern expression he maintained in front of outsiders instantly broke.","He quickly walked towards her as well.","With his long legs and large strides, he reached Qiao Lanshu in just a few steps. He reached out to steady her and then naturally pulled her into his arms.","He scolded in a low voice, \"Don't you know you're pregnant now? Why are you running? There's still snow on the road. What if you fall?\"","Qiao Lanshu hugged Qin Yuanzheng's arm and smiled. \"I was just afraid you'd been waiting too long.\"","Qin Yuanzheng's brows remained furrowed as he said, \"No running from now on. You can only walk slowly, do you hear me?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Got it.\"","Chatting, the two got into the car.","Qin Yuanzheng helped Qiao Lanshu into the car, fastened her seatbelt for her, and even pulled a big, bright red apple from his pocket, pressing it into her hands.","He said, \"It's an apple grown at the military base. Try it.\"","The fruit from the trees grown at the base was always sent directly to the military cafeteria.","There were too many soldiers at the base, so when distributed evenly, each person would only get about two or three a week.","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't bear to eat a single one. Every time fruit was handed out, he would bring it back for Qiao Lanshu to eat.","Qiao Lanshu took the apple and turned it over and over in her hands.","The apple was big and red, and it smelled incredibly sweet.","Reluctant to eat it right away, she placed the apple into the pocket of her padded jacket.","Qin Yuanzheng asked her, \"Where did you go just now? Why didn't you wait for me at the factory gate and run off on your own?\"","Qiao Lanshu had no intention of hiding anything from Qin Yuanzheng. She immediately told him about tailing Liu Weidong that afternoon, as well as her own speculations.","Sitting in the driver's seat, Qin Yuanzheng remained silent for a moment before saying, \"If that's the case, he must be involved in some sort of shady transaction.\"","A sudden thought crossed Qin Yuanzheng's mind: could the recent bombing case be related to Liu Weidong?","When Qin Yuanzheng returned to the base that morning, he had already arranged for someone to investigate Liu Weidong.","It would probably take a few days before they could dig anything up.","Since Liu Weidong had conducted transactions near the train station, starting the investigation from there might yield some results.","...","At this very moment, Liu Weidong had already stopped in an alleyway outside the train station with a buyer.","It wasn't that they absolutely had to trade here.","Rather, the buyer lived nearby, and Liu Weidong had to deliver it personally.","He didn't want the buyers to know where his goods were stored, lest these people decide to report him in the future and leave him with no time to escape.","The buyer handed him the money, and he pulled the goods from his coat pocket, passing them into the other man's hands. Then, in the pitch-black alley, Liu Weidong whispered, \"We'll have to pause for the next two months. If you run into the others, let them know too. Don't come looking for me for a while.\"","Hearing that they had to stop for two months, the buyer immediately grew anxious. \"No, how can you stop? If you stop, what are we supposed to do?\"","Liu Weidong said somewhat impatiently, \"Haven't you heard that the higher-ups sent an inspection team down? With things being this tense, can't you lay low for a bit? Don't worry, going without a smoke for two months won't kill you.\"","The buyer said anxiously, \"Two months is really too long. Will one month do? If you're not selling anymore, then introduce us to someone else. We can buy from someone else.\"","Too lazy to entertain him, Liu Weidong shoved the money into his pocket and told him, \"Then wait a month first. We'll see what the situation is like in a month.\"","Hearing him say this, the buyer finally breathed a sigh of relief and watched Liu Weidong leave.","After coming out of the alley, Liu Weidong's eyes suddenly turned cold, and he looked behind him. \"Who's there!\"","Behind him was the main gate of the train station. At this hour, there weren't many people left outside the gate.","There was only a young couple, bundled up tightly, walking shoulder to shoulder toward another street.","Liu Weidong: \"...\"","He stared silently at the couple for a moment, suspecting he was overthinking things.","It was all his paranoid father's fault, making him start acting paranoid too.","He had clearly sold countless times before without any issues.","Liu Weidong tucked his hands into his sleeves and limped away under the cover of the night.","On the other side, Deng Weijun was scared into a cold sweat.","Wang Haitang lowered her voice and asked, \"Weijun, what were you looking at over there just now?\"","When she had just gotten off work and come out, she saw Deng Weijun sneaking around the entrance of some alley.","She was just about to walk over and see what was going on when she saw Deng Weijun suddenly run back, grab her, and run.","It frightened her into running hurriedly along with him, thinking something major had happened.","Deng Weijun lowered his voice and said, \"This matter is of great importance. It's better if you don't know. The more you know, the more trouble it is. Later, when we get back to my brother-in-law's house, I have to go talk to Regiment Commander Qin about this.\"","Wang Haitang never had many opinions of her own. Since Deng Weijun said so, she really stopped asking and only said, \"Then be careful yourself. Don't do such dangerous things in the future.\"","Deng Weijun nodded.","He was about to marry a wife and start a family; he cherished his life very much now.","Besides, the incident with Zheng Daliu last time had already taught him a lesson. He was much more cautious in how he did things now than before.","With something weighing on his mind, Deng Weijun felt a bit anxious.","He took Wang Haitang back to the food factory, then went to the bike shed to wheel out his bicycle, and carrying Wang Haitang, rushed toward Yang Wenyan's house.","He pedaled so hard that the bicycle chain was about to spark, with the cold wind howling directly against his face.","Without a face cover, Deng Weijun felt as if his face had been slapped several times by the wind, leaving it stinging and numb.","As soon as he returned to Yang Wenyan's house, he saw Qin Yuanzheng's car downstairs. Deng Weijun handed the bicycle to Wang Haitang, asking her to help park it.","Then, he ran over to find Qin Yuanzheng: Regiment Commander Qin, Regiment Commander Qin, wait a moment! I have something important to tell you!","Qin Yuanzheng was holding Qiao Lanshu's hand, carrying two cans of luncheon meat in his other hand.","Hearing this, he stopped and asked, What is it?","Deng Weijun looked left and right. There was no one in the yard; it was pitch black, freezing cold, and extremely windy.","He walked up to Qin Yuanzheng and leaned in close to his ear, wanting to whisper to him.","As a result, Qin Yuanzheng reacted strongly, pulling Qiao Lanshu back a few steps and looking at Deng Weijun with a vigilant gaze: What are you doing?","Deng Weijun: ...","Deng Weijun also realized that his actions were a bit presumptuous.","But he was still anxious inside. He stood a little further away from Qin Yuanzheng and lowered his voice: Regiment Commander Qin, I just saw it with my own eyes. Liu Weidong, he... he is selling opium!","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng's eyes instantly turned cold: Are you sure?","Deng Weijun nodded frantically: I am sure, I am absolutely sure! I heard them with my own ears. Liu Weidong also said that the authorities are cracking down recently, so he wants to stop selling for two months, but the other party wants him to stop for only a month.","Deng Weijun was deeply shocked in his heart.","Why did such a thing still exist nowadays?","Has not the country banned it?","Was the destruction of opium at Humen all for nothing?","A substance that the people of the country avoided like the plague, yet Liu Weidong was actually selling it secretly for profit.","He really deserved to die!","Qin Yuanzheng hated these things the most.","He said in a deep voice, If Liu Weidong is really selling this stuff, then what awaits him will not be as simple as labor reform.","He could be executed by firing squad on the spot.","Even now, Deng Weijun's heartbeat had not returned to normal.","It was just too nerve-wracking.","He was almost discovered by Liu Weidong just now.","He had truly witnessed how ruthless and cruel Liu Weidong's family was over the past few days.","Qin Yuanzheng said deeply, I understand. I will arrange for someone to investigate tomorrow.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, Brother Zheng, how about letting Director Guan investigate this matter first? He is the director of the Revolutionary Committee. If he steps forward to investigate, even if he does not find anything, others would not dare say anything about him. Moreover, that Liu Weidong is involved in the revolution; strictly speaking, he can be considered his subordinate.","Qin Yuanzheng was a soldier. If he led people to investigate, it would actually be quite difficult to carry out. Because of their status, they could not just casually go into residents' homes to investigate; this was a matter of discipline.","If the boundaries were not handled well, it would be very easy for people to seize on it and report him. If it blew up, others would say he was bullying people with his power, or that soldiers were beating people up, which would severely damage the military's image. When that time came, Qin Yuanzheng would be in a lot of trouble.","However, the military and the Revolutionary Committee were two different systems, and the Revolutionary Committee could absolutely handle this matter.","After all, Guan Wenjun had done his fair share of house raids in the past, and his reputation could not possibly get any worse.","Hearing Qiao Lanshu's words nearby, Deng Weijun immediately gave her a thumbs-up and whispered, Sister-in-law, you are the smart one to even think of this!","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng thought for a moment and said, Alright, I will go find Guan Wenjun tomorrow.","...","This guy, Guan Wenjun, had nothing to do recently. His subordinates were quite busy day by day, but he could not stand staying idle in his office. Instead, he would run off to sponsor the orphanage whether he had business there or not.","Not only did he send money and food to the orphanage, but he also completely repaired the orphanage's buildings and heated brick beds.","He renovated the beds where the children slept, scraped off the old newspapers on them, pasted beautiful kraft paper, and rebuilt the chimneys with bricks to ensure the flues were not blocked.","After all these repairs were done, he realized that the orphanage did not have enough firewood to burn. Having the beds but no firewood would still leave the children freezing, would it not?","Going all out, Guan Wenjun found someone to haul back a cartload of dry firewood, filling the orphanage's warehouse to the brim.","When Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu came to the Revolutionary Committee to look for Guan Wenjun, he was holding a sack of fabric scraps, preparing to deliver them to the orphanage.","He did not know what these fabric scraps could be used for, but Sister Director would definitely know.","He spotted Qiao Lanshu at a glance, automatically ignoring Qin Yuanzheng. He set down the sack in his hand, reached out to smooth his hair, and blinked at Qiao Lanshu.","He said smugly, Oh, Comrade Xiao Qiao, long time no see. Did you come specifically to see me?","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qiao Lanshu smiled and nodded: Yes, we came specifically to see Director Guan today.","Hearing this, Guan Wenjun was instantly even happier: What is it? Tell me about it.","He happened to be free lately.","Qin Yuanzheng put his arm around Qiao Lanshu, walked over, and said to Guan Wenjun, This is a matter of great importance. Let us talk in your office.","Guan Wenjun deliberately said, Oh my, Regiment Commander Qin is here too? Please forgive my lack of a proper welcome. I am sorry, I did not see you just now; I only saw Comrade Xiao Qiao.","Qin Yuanzheng could not be bothered to entertain him and led Qiao Lanshu straight to Guan Wenjun's office.","After returning to his office and closing the door, Guan Wenjun even said to Qiao Lanshu, Comrade Xiao Qiao, as soon as you arrive, my shabby office is graced with your radiant presence.","Qiao Lanshu knew he was just doing it on purpose.","Deliberately trying to anger Qin Yuanzheng.","Who knew when the grudge between the two of them would ever pass.","With the office door closed, Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu told Guan Wenjun about Liu Weidong's situation.","Once he got down to serious business, Guan Wenjun became entirely earnest, no longer acting as frivolous as before.","He stroked his chin and said to Qin Yuanzheng, So according to your idea, should I go search the alleys near the train station, or should I directly search Liu Weidong's house?","Qin Yuanzheng replied, It would be best to confirm where Liu Weidong stores his goods before conducting a search. Until then, do not act rashly.","The three of them discussed in the office for a long time.","They formulated an initial plan.","When dusk arrived in the afternoon, a middle-aged man wearing a worn-out padded jacket wrapped himself up tightly.","He was arranged by Guan Wenjun to act as bait. He had done this kind of work many times before and was already very skilled at it.","He wandered through the alleys where Liu Weidong had made transactions. Based on Deng Weijun's description, he had a rough idea of what kind of buyers dealt with Liu Weidong.","This middle-aged man looked around, and whenever he encountered a suspicious person, he would lean in and lower his voice: Brother, I can smell it. How about introducing me to a supplier?","He tested three people in a row and was treated like a lunatic by two of them.","The third man looked at him warily and instinctively raised his arm to smell his own sleeve.","Seeing that he had a bite, the middle-aged man suddenly hooked his arm around the skinny man's neck, half-dragging and half-pulling him into a corner, and whispered, How about introducing me to a supplier, brother? I will pay three times the price.","The man couldn't help but speak up. \"It's no use even if you offer ten times the price. The seller has backed out.\"","The middle-aged man immediately replied, \"Then I'll offer ten times the price. Could you at least pass on the message and ask for me?\"","Since Guan Wenjun was the one footing the bill anyway, the middle-aged man didn't feel the slightest pinch of hesitation when making such an outrageous offer.","After all, Guan Wenjun had made it clear: as long as he could lure their target out into the open, he would be credited with a major accomplishment!"]},{"number":144,"title":"Chapter 144: Fishing Fail","paragraphs":["To be honest, Liu Weidong might not even care for three times the price.","But if it were ten times the price, he would very likely be tempted.","The man had his neck hooked by the other party. He had been smoking opium for a long time and his body was terribly weak, leaving him with absolutely no strength to break free.","The other man lowered his voice and said, How about this: you help me ask him if he will sell for ten times the price. Do a brother a favor. Things are tight right now, and I cannot find a supplier anywhere.","With that, the man stuffed ten yuan into the addict's hand.","In truth, the addict had already been made; even if he did not want to help, he had no choice, as he was terrified of being reported.","Left with no other options, he could only nod and say with immense frustration, Fine, fine, I will go ask him for you.","The other man anxiously urged him, Go ask today. I will wait for you right here at six o'clock tonight, alright?","The addict replied with some irritation, Alright, I will go right now.","He shoved the ten yuan into his pocket, feeling like he was having the worst luck in the world.","How could he get caught right after finishing a smoke?","It was too dangerous. If he got reported, would he not be completely ruined?","Filled with fear, he hurried to the Liu residence to find Liu Weidong.","Liu Weidong had one more order that he needed to deliver tomorrow.","He did not dare let his father know, lest he get scolded again.","After coming home today, he had been lying in bed nursing his leg injury and sleeping. He had not gone out to hang around with his shady friends either.","Liu Zhengxing was worried that Liu Weidong would be disobedient and sneak out with opium at such a critical juncture. Therefore, halfway through his workday, he made a special trip back home to check. Only after confirming that Liu Weidong was indeed at home did he drive back to work.","However, not long after he left, someone came knocking on the door.","Liu Weidong limped out of the house. When he saw the man standing before him, his expression instantly changed, and he said sharply, How did you find my house? Are you looking for death?","If it were not for his crippled leg, Liu Weidong would have already rushed up to beat him.","The man quickly whispered, I came to you because I need something...","He then told Liu Weidong about someone willing to pay ten times the price for opium.","Liu Weidong's opium was already very expensive; a small piece sold for a hundred yuan.","Ten times the price—would that not be a thousand yuan?","In this day and age, an ordinary worker's monthly salary was only twenty-five yuan.","Even after Liu Weihong became a supervisor, her salary was only forty yuan.","A hundred yuan was already exorbitant, as it amounted to nearly half a year's wages for a regular person.","And this buyer came right out offering ten times the price...","To be honest, Liu Weidong was moved.","But he maintained some vigilance. He stared at the man and asked, Who is this person? Do you know him?","The man replied, I do not know him, but he seems to have a heavy addiction. I had been smoking all day, and he could still smell it on me. I reckon he is not lying. He probably really cannot find a supplier and came to me out of desperation.","Liu Weidong thought about it. Even though he knew he should be cautious, the temptation of a thousand yuan was simply too great.","So, he said, Wait here. I am going back inside for a moment.","With that, Liu Weidong turned and went back into the house. It was not long before he came out again, his hands shoved into his pockets. He closed the door and walked outward with the man.","Meanwhile, in the house opposite theirs, Guan Wenjun was keeping watch with four or five men.","As soon as he saw Liu Weidong come out, he immediately led his men to rush out. Quick, tie Liu Weidong up!","The four men swarmed out and pinned both Liu Weidong and the addict to the ground on the spot.","Before Liu Weidong could even utter a single cry, the men from the Revolutionary Committee gagged him, held him to the ground, wrenched his arms behind his back, and tied him up with a rope.","Guan Wenjun walked out with his hands in his pockets, looking down at Liu Weidong from above. He ordered the men beside him, Search him. Let us see what good stuff he is hiding in his pockets.","Liu Weidong kept whimpering and struggling, but the men from the Revolutionary Committee were used to doing this and were highly skilled. They thoroughly searched his entire body. Not only did they check his pockets and sleeves, but they also eventually took off his padded cotton jacket and searched it several times.","In the end, Guan Wenjun's subordinates only found a pack of cigarettes, a box of matches, and a dozen or so yuan.","Looking at these items, Guan Wenjun's expression turned incredibly grim. He asked, This is all you found? Nothing else?","A subordinate nodded. Director, that is it.","The addict was also searched, but they only found ten yuan on him, which was the exact money Guan Wenjun's subordinate had shoved into his hand to bribe him.","There was absolutely nothing else.","Guan Wenjun was in disbelief. Had he misjudged the situation?","With a dark expression, he walked over and personally searched Liu Weidong again, even pulling off his padded cotton trousers.","Liu Weidong stood up, clutching his crotch, and glared fiercely at Guan Wenjun.","Guan Wenjun said speechlessly, What are you looking at me like that for? Relax, I have no interest in men.","Liu Weidong was speechless.","Failing to find anything on Liu Weidong left Guan Wenjun somewhat disappointed. This was not how he had planned things.","Without any evidence, it was hard for Guan Wenjun to justify arresting Liu Weidong.","Guan Wenjun removed the gag from Liu Weidong's mouth, and Liu Weidong immediately cursed viciously, Guan Wenjun! Do not think that just because you are the Director of the Revolutionary Committee you can do whatever you want! I have not committed any crimes, on what grounds are you arresting me?","Guan Wenjun was frustrated as well. He had thought his sting operation was a success, but Liu Weidong had pulled a fake-out and had not actually put anything in his pockets at all.","Now they had alerted the snake in the grass. If they let Liu Weidong go back, it would be much harder to investigate him later.","Guan Wenjun immediately waved his hand and declared, Someone reported Liu Weidong for speculation and profiteering. Take him back for a proper interrogation.","Liu Weidong was speechless again.","Liu Weidong shouted, What speculation and profiteering? Do you have any evidence to slander me like this? Guan Wenjun, you dare arrest me? You better think this through. If you offend my dad, your chances of getting transferred will go up in smoke!","Guan Wenjun had been with the Revolutionary Committee for several years, and he actually knew that there was no real future there; it was not a long-term career path.","Moreover, he had offended quite a few people over the years. If the political climate changed in the future and the revolution ended, leaving him without power or influence, would he not end up getting stabbed in the back?","Therefore, for the past year, he had been pulling strings everywhere, taking people from the Personnel Section and the Labor Bureau out to dinner, trying to see which department was short-staffed and could arrange a formal position for him.","He had even sought out Liu Zhengxing before, but Liu Zhengxing had refused to see him.","Now that he had arrested Liu Weidong, was he not offending Liu Zhengxing?","Guan Wenjun was actually feeling a bit conflicted inside. He remained silent for a few seconds before deciding to use a stalling tactic. He told Liu Weidong, It is just to cooperate with an investigation. Do not worry, nothing will happen to you.","Although he said this aloud, in his heart he was thinking that if he could uncover evidence of the man privately selling opium, he would arrest Liu Weidong and claim the merit.","If he could not find anything, he would just release Liu Weidong and publicly claim it was merely a routine investigation based on a tip-off.","This way, he would not offend either side.","With these words, Liu Weidong felt much more at ease. He gave a cold snort and said, \"Guan Wenjun, you had better release me as soon as possible. Otherwise, you know the consequences of offending my father!\"","Guan Wenjun was incredibly annoyed.","He had originally wanted to earn some merit and get a promotion.","But now look at it, things had only gotten more complicated.","He might end up getting no credit at all, and instead offend everyone involved.","...","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng were currently eating at home.","Qiao Lanshu sat on the sofa, holding a bowl of sweet potato and millet porridge. After taking a few sips, she asked Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, do you think things are going smoothly on Director Guan's side with that baiting plan?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was listening to the radio while eating steamed buns. Hearing this, he said softly, \"I am just worried that Guan Wenjun will not be able to keep his composure. He is too impatient.\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly asked, \"Then what should we do if things do not go smoothly?\"","Qin Yuanzheng replied, \"Rest assured, we will deal with whatever comes our way. There will always be a solution, so do not worry about it.\"","Ever since the explosion occurred in the city, Qin Yuanzheng had been paying extra attention to the radio news.","Every time he came home, he would turn on the radio to listen to the news.","Only after making sure there were no more explosions would he breathe a sigh of relief.","After dinner, Qin Yuanzheng went to wash the dishes, then sliced an apple for Qiao Lanshu and placed it on the table for her.","Over the past two days, because of the city explosions, Qin Yuanzheng had not been able to properly care for Qiao Lanshu.","He squatted in front of her, watching her eat the apple, and asked in a low voice, \"How has your stomach been these past few days? Are you feeling uncomfortable anywhere?\"","It was really strange. He had heard that other women vomited severely during pregnancy, with some throwing up everything they ate, utterly tormented by the baby.","But looking at Qiao Lanshu, apart from feeling nauseous for a couple of days at the very beginning, she did not seem to have any reactions now. She could eat and sleep well, and even skipped around when walking. She did not look pregnant at all.","Qin Yuanzheng said with some hesitation, \"Wife, how about we go to the hospital again tomorrow to have a check?\"","Qiao Lanshu fed him a piece of apple and smiled. \"Did we not just get it checked half a month ago? Why go again now?\"","Qin Yuanzheng lowered his voice, \"Wife, I was thinking, could it be a misdiagnosis?\"","He still felt it was a bit surreal.","Was his wife really pregnant?","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Seeing Qiao Lanshu's expression, Qin Yuanzheng quickly explained, \"I do not mean anything else. It is just that you have not had any reactions, and your symptoms are quite different from what others describe.\"","He had been thinking about this since yesterday. If it were not for the fact that he had to go to the headquarters for a meeting and return to the mining area troops to deploy work, he would have already taken Qiao Lanshu back to the hospital to have the doctor check her pulse again.","Qiao Lanshu reached out to touch her belly and said softly, \"Brother Zheng, do not worry, it is not a misdiagnosis.\"","Her period had not come for three months, and she could feel the changes in her own body.","Her breasts were indeed swollen, and she felt exhausted and sleepy every day. These changes could not deceive anyone.","She murmured, \"Everyone's symptoms are different. Maybe our baby is just too well-behaved and cannot bear to see me suffer.\"","Qin Yuanzheng reached out and gave her chest a gentle massage, whispering, \"Then let me massage you for a bit?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","...","Qin Yuanzheng had indeed held back for too long recently, and tonight he did not want to deprive himself anymore.","After massaging Qiao Lanshu for a long time, he leaned close to her ear and asked if the radish from last time was tasty.","Did she want to eat it again?","Before Qiao Lanshu could speak, he carried her onto the bed and made the first move.","He said he had not eaten his fill yet, and that she could eat after he was full.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng originally thought he would be able to eat his fill tonight.","But as it turned out, Guan Wenjun came knocking on their door in the middle of the night."]},{"number":145,"title":"Chapter 145: Overnight Search","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng hadn't been intimate with his wife for several days.","He happened to come home quite early today and had some free time, so he just wanted to hold his wife and warm up the bed.","But Guan Wenjun came knocking on their door again.","Qin Yuanzheng sighed. He walked to the door, opened it, and looked at Guan Wenjun with a rather displeased expression.","Guan Wenjun was thick-skinned enough to squeeze right in. Frowning, he said, \"Regiment Commander Qin, something isn't right here. I lured Liu Weidong out, but he didn't have the goods on him. Do you think we made a mistake? Maybe Liu Weidong actually doesn't carry that stuff on him?\"","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent for a moment before shaking his head. \"Deng Weijun shouldn't have heard wrong. The things Liu Weidong trades in private are definitely not ordinary. Did you go back and interrogate him?\"","It was exactly because he had interrogated him that Guan Wenjun was so angry.","He said, \"I interrogated him. The buyer confessed, saying he went to Liu Weidong to buy tobacco, and Liu Weidong admitted it too, claiming he sold shredded tobacco sun-dried by farmers in the village, not the kind of smoke we were thinking of. The situation is a bit tricky now. Without evidence, I can't just go and search a cadre's home. After all, he is the Director of the Personnel Department.\"","Hearing this, what else could Qin Yuanzheng possibly not understand?","Guan Wenjun had lost his patience and failed to catch Liu Weidong red-handed during the transaction. Now that they hadn't found anything on Liu Weidong, why would Liu Weidong ever confess?","Moreover, Guan Wenjun was wary of Liu Weidong's background, so he didn't dare to play hardball. He didn't even want to take responsibility, which was why he had come to find Qin Yuanzheng.","With a dark face, Qin Yuanzheng pointed at Guan Wenjun and scolded him, \"Guan Wenjun, if you continue to be so timid and hesitant, you might as well quit this job right now! Just stay in your Revolutionary Committee for the rest of your life!\"","Guan Wenjun looked conflicted as he said, \"Oh man, I'm just worried about misunderstanding Liu Weidong, aren't I? Besides, there's no evidence, right?\"","Qiao Lanshu walked out. Listening to their argument, she chimed in, \"So Director Guan is this timid? To think you're actually afraid of Liu Weidong.\"","Even she wasn't afraid, yet Guan Wenjun was.","Didn't he always seem like he feared absolutely nothing in this world?","He usually acted so arrogant and cocky when talking to people.","As soon as Guan Wenjun heard Qiao Lanshu say this, he immediately jumped up in agitation. He said, \"Who said I'm timid? I just think it's not good to act recklessly without evidence. This is called being reasonable, not being afraid, understand?\"","Qin Yuanzheng then said, \"In that case, let's go find the evidence.\"","Saying that, he stood up and started putting on his coat.","As things stood, they had to hurry up and find the evidence, and then get Liu Weidong sentenced.","Otherwise, after tonight, once their goods were destroyed, finding evidence would be incredibly difficult.","Guan Wenjun had been sitting there all this time without even taking a sip of tea, only to see Qin Yuanzheng already walking to the door and putting on his jacket.","He hesitated and said, \"It's late at night, and Liu Weidong is still locked up in the Revolutionary Committee. You said you want to find evidence, but where are we going to find it?\"","Qin Yuanzheng replied, \"You will take your men right now and search Liu Zhengxing's house, especially Liu Weidong's room. You must search it thoroughly.\"","Guan Wenjun was speechless.","Guan Wenjun opened his mouth wide in shock. \"What did you say? You want me to go search the home of Liu Zhengxing, the Section Chief of the Personnel Department? And right now?\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at Guan Wenjun and casually remarked, \"Director Guan, are you scared?\"","Guan Wenjun remained silent.","Guan Wenjun immediately stood up. He flicked his hair and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Scared? How is that possible? Since Liu Weidong has already been arrested anyway, let's just do the search.\"","With that, he followed Qin Yuanzheng out the door.","Qin Yuanzheng said to Qiao Lanshu, \"You rest at home first. I'll be back soon.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, feeling a bit worried inside.","However, she trusted Qin Yuanzheng's judgment and only whispered, \"Brother Zheng, you must be very careful out there.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and reached out to rub her hair.","Guan Wenjun said from behind, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, why didn't you tell me to be careful too?\"","Before Qiao Lanshu could speak, Qin Yuanzheng shut the door.","He stared at Guan Wenjun and said, \"Talk to my wife less in the future. Otherwise, I'll report you for sabotaging a military marriage.\"","Guan Wenjun was speechless again.","Guan Wenjun knew Qin Yuanzheng was serious.","He instantly backed down and said, \"I was just saying it casually. Why are you taking it so seriously?\"","The two walked into the pitch-black stairwell.","When they reached the main gate and stood by the car, Guan Wenjun looked at Qin Yuanzheng, who was dressed in civilian clothes, and asked him with a glimmer of hope, \"Regiment Commander Qin, how about you act as the captain for this search mission?\"","Qin Yuanzheng gave him a speechless look. \"You will lead your men inside to search, and I will lead my men to keep watch outside.\"","Guan Wenjun's last shred of hope was shattered.","It seemed that today, he was bound to offend Liu Zhengxing.","But with his fence-sitting ideas dashed, Guan Wenjun had no choice but to go all the way.","He gritted his teeth and said in a deep voice, \"Fine, let's do this.\"","As Guan Wenjun spoke, he got into his car. Qin Yuanzheng also got in, sitting in the back seat.","He didn't drive his own car, as there were many people who recognized it.","Under the cover of night, the two returned to the Revolutionary Committee together.","Then, Qin Yuanzheng got out of the car, not going along with them.","Guan Wenjun went back that very night, gathered seven or eight men, and headed straight for Liu Zhengxing's house.","Meanwhile, Qin Yuanzheng arrived near Liu Zhengxing's house. Xiao Yang, also dressed in plainclothes, brought two subordinates to rendezvous with Qin Yuanzheng.","The four men stood on the roof of a residential building opposite Liu Zhengxing's house.","Xiao Yang lowered his voice and said:","\"I've been keeping an eye on Liu Weidong since yesterday. After Liu Weidong came out of the hospital, he went straight home. He went out once before dark yesterday afternoon and came back about an hour later. Apart from trading with that person, he didn't go anywhere else.","Therefore, the goods he traded must be hidden in his house. We just don't know what that stuff is or how much of it he has in stock. If we rush in to search recklessly and end up finding nothing, we'll be in big trouble. Liu Zhengxing is not someone to be trifled with; he will definitely strike back fiercely.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and whispered, \"Arrange for two men to keep watch near the backyard of the Liu residence. If anyone is seen leaving, detain them first.\"","Xiao Yang nodded, left one person to assist Qin Yuanzheng, and then left with the other.","He went downstairs, crossed the street, and detoured to the alley outside the backyard of Liu Zhengxing's house to stand guard.","...","It was already dark when Liu Zhengxing returned from work. After all, he had been very busy lately with a lot of things to do.","However, when he got back and found that Liu Weidong was not at home, he had a bad premonition.","He went to Liu Weihong's room, called her out, and asked her, \"Where is your brother? Where did he go?\"","Liu Weihong had been sleeping in her room all afternoon. Hearing Liu Zhengxing's question, she rubbed her eyes and said, \"Isn't Weidong sleeping in his room? What's wrong, is he not home?\"","Liu Zhengxing's face darkened as he returned to his own room. His wife, Sun Qiaofen, didn't have a job; she dressed up gorgeously every day and went out to play with her friends, not caring about household affairs.","She had only just returned.","Liu Zhengxing asked her without much hope, \"Where is Weidong? Do you know where he went?\"","His wife, Sun Qiaofen, measured her newly bought fabric against herself and said uncaringly, \"Isn't he out of the house every day? How should I know where he went?\"","Liu Zhengxing: \"...\"","Liu Zhengxing walked out of the room, frowning in thought.","Feeling a lingering sense of unease, he thought for a moment before heading to Liu Weidong's room.","In truth, he didn't know where Liu Weidong had hidden those things either.","But they had to be in Liu Weidong's room.","Keeping those things around was a hidden danger. In the past, he could turn a blind eye, but not anymore.","The city had been conducting strict inspections lately. If they traced anything back to Liu Weidong, it would be big trouble.","He only had this one son, and he didn't want anything bad to happen to him.","With this in mind, Liu Zhengxing began searching Liu Weidong's room.","He first rummaged through the wardrobe for a while but found nothing.","Just as he was about to check elsewhere, he suddenly heard his daughter, Liu Weihong's voice.","Liu Weihong ran over looking nervous and cried out, \"Dad, Dad, this is bad! The people from the Revolutionary Committee are at our door!\"","His wife, Sun Qiaofen, also said in a panic, \"Why did those damned thugs come to our door? Old Liu, they aren't here to raid our house, are they?\"","Liu Zhengxing's face darkened. He glanced at Liu Weidong's room and said in a low voice, \"Don't open the door. Stall them for a bit...\"","Liu Weihong said nervously, \"I already opened it.\"","Liu Zhengxing: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun led his men into the house and said loudly, \"Section Chief Liu, have you eaten yet? Long time no see, did you miss me?\"","Liu Zhengxing: \"...\"","Realizing the urgency of the situation, Liu Zhengxing whispered a few instructions to Liu Weihong and Sun Qiaofen, then went out to meet Guan Wenjun himself.","Liu Zhengxing went out to deal with Guan Wenjun. \"Director Guan, what brings you here today? Is it about that previous matter?\"","As he spoke, he added another sentence, \"Our county's public security bureau actually has a vacancy for a deputy chief recently. I think you should try for it.\"","This was indeed a position Guan Wenjun had been striving for a long time.","But previously, Liu Zhengxing hadn't revealed any information to him at all.","Remembering Qin Yuanzheng's instructions, Guan Wenjun didn't fall for the bait this time. He said to Liu Zhengxing, \"Section Chief Liu, let's cut the small talk. This afternoon, someone reported Liu Weidong for illegally selling opium. I am just here to conduct a search according to the rules today, please understand.\"","With that, Guan Wenjun made a hand gesture and told his subordinates, \"Go search the rooms.\"","Seven or eight men instantly rushed into the house, scattered, and began searching everywhere.","Liu Zhengxing had never suffered such an insult before; his hands were trembling with anger.","He pointed at Guan Wenjun and said, \"Guan Wenjun, don't push things too far! You dare come to search my house without any evidence, just based on a single report? I am going to sue you in military court!\"","Since Guan Wenjun had already taken things this far, what was there to be afraid of?","He simply replied, \"Section Chief Liu, don't get so worked up. If Liu Weidong is innocent, I will definitely clear his name. Why are you so nervous? Could it be that your Liu Weidong is actually hiding something shady?\"","Liu Zhengxing: \"...\"","At this moment, Sun Qiaofen and Liu Weihong came out shouting, \"What are you doing? What are you doing? Are you trying to act like hooligans?\"","The two of them came out wearing padded cotton jackets, bundled up so thickly that they looked bloated.","The heated kang was burning in the room, so it wasn't cold at all.","Yet the mother and daughter were each wrapped in a large padded jacket, swearing as they walked out.","The men from the Revolutionary Committee said to Guan Wenjun, \"Director Guan, we saw these two in the room. They are wearing thick clothes and refuse to let us search them.\"","They hadn't intended to conduct a body search originally, but the two women were bundled up so tightly that it was highly suspicious.","Sun Qiaofen shouted loudly, \"Guan, search me if you dare! A grown man like you wanting to body search a woman, how shameless! If you dare to search me, I will report you for hooliganism and sue you for rape! And the rest of you, try it if you have the guts.\"","As she spoke, Sun Qiaofen put her hands on her hips and thrust her chest out in Guan Wenjun's direction.","Guan Wenjun: \"...\""]},{"number":146,"title":"Chapter 146: Conviction","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun never expected Sun Qiaofen and Liu Weihong to pull a stunt like this.","Offending Liu Zhengxing by showing up in the middle of the night to search his house had already left him feeling a bit unsure.","He had been worried that Liu Weidong didn't have much stock or hadn't hidden the goods at home, meaning this raid might turn up empty.","But now, seeing Sun Qiaofen acting like this, his confidence surged.","Liu Zhengxing and his wife were definitely hiding something; otherwise, why would they put on such a show?","Guan Wenjun sized up Sun Qiaofen and said to Liu Zhengxing, \"Section Chief Liu, this is uncalled for. Having your wife and daughter pull this stunt—are you resisting our search?\"","Liu Zhengxing naturally wouldn't admit to that. Knowing Guan Wenjun wouldn't dare lay a hand on his wife and daughter, he relaxed.","Smiling, he said, \"Director Guan, don't go throwing false accusations around. I'm not refusing to cooperate with the Revolutionary Committee. Look at you, barging into my house with your men in the dead of night, tearing the place apart without a word—and haven't I just let you search as you please?\"","Sun Qiaofen sneered and chimed in, \"Director Guan, if you're so capable, go ahead and search, be my guest! But if you don't find anything, just wait for me to file a complaint against you! Don't think that just because you're the director of the Revolutionary Committee, you can run roughshod over everyone!\"","With that, Sun Qiaofen grabbed her daughter Liu Weihong's arm and said, \"Weihong, let's go!\"","Guan Wenjun frowned and blocked their path. \"Hold on, where do you think you're going?\"","Sun Qiaofen said angrily, \"A bunch of men are tearing my house apart, so I'm taking my daughter outside to get out of the way. What, do you actually want to strip-search me and my daughter?\"","To be honest, Guan Wenjun really didn't dare.","If he so much as touched them and they started screaming that he was acting like a hooligan or accused him of rape, even as the director of the Revolutionary Committee, he wouldn't be able to handle the fallout.","Unsure of what to do for a moment, Guan Wenjun pointed at Sun Qiaofen and Liu Weihong, saying, \"The Revolutionary Committee is conducting a search. None of you are allowed to leave.\"","As soon as he said that, Sun Qiaofen ripped open her padded jacket and thrust her chest toward Guan Wenjun. \"Fine, fine, fine! If you want to search, do it right now! Hurry up! I'll take off my clothes for you to search, will that satisfy you?\"","This was the first time Liu Weihong had seen her mother act like this, and she was utterly stunned.","Seeing Sun Qiaofen pulling at her jacket and repeatedly rubbing herself against Guan Wenjun, he was frightened into backing away continuously.","Guan Wenjun crossed his arms over his chest, retreating several steps in a row, and pointed at Sun Qiaofen. \"Stop right there! Stay there! If you rub against me again, I'll report you for rape!\"","Guan Wenjun had never seen a woman as shameless as Sun Qiaofen.","It was truly terrifying.","He even suspected that Sun Qiaofen was taking advantage of him.","After all, he was so young, handsome, suave, and exceptionally talented...","...","Inside the house, it was noisy and chaotic. Qin Yuanzheng and a subordinate had originally been keeping watch from across the street. Seeing the argument break out inside, Qin Yuanzheng brought his subordinate over to crouch by the main gate of Liu Zhengxing's house to listen to the commotion.","It was pitch dark at this hour, with no streetlights nearby, and the weather was freezing.","Qin Yuanzheng missed his sweet, soft little wife at home and was already growing impatient.","He felt that Guan Wenjun was too slow in getting things done. If a single shrew like Sun Qiaofen could intimidate him, what else could he be expected to accomplish?","Qin Yuanzheng turned his head and whispered a few words into his subordinate's ear.","The subordinate crouching beside him immediately nodded. \"Understood, Commander. I'll go right now.\"","Qin Yuanzheng added in a low voice, \"Take my car.\"","The subordinate nodded and quickly ran off.","Longcheng wasn't large, so going to the suburbs wasn't too far.","Driving from here to the mining area would only take about ten minutes.","All Guan Wenjun had to do was stall Sun Qiaofen inside the house.","Meanwhile, inside, Sun Qiaofen held onto Liu Weihong and tried to leave several times, but Guan Wenjun's men stopped them every time.","Guan Wenjun's men had turned every room upside down but found absolutely nothing.","Liu Weidong's room was especially clean; there was nothing there at all.","Once Guan Wenjun's men finished searching, Liu Zhengxing said to him, \"Director Guan, the search is over now. Can you leave?\"","Guan Wenjun looked at the half-smile on Liu Zhengxing's face.","He knew he had thoroughly offended him this time.","He decided to be straightforward. \"Section Chief Liu, someone reported that your son, Liu Weidong, is selling opium out there. Did you know about this?\"","Guan Wenjun stared intently at Liu Zhengxing's expression.","But Liu Zhengxing's face remained unchanged; not even his gaze flickered.","With a dark expression, he said, \"Director Guan, I suspect this person is intentionally framing my son. As you know, when my son is out having fun, he offends a lot of people. Those people are jealous of his good life, so they often try to trick him out of his money. He's still young and ignorant, so he often gets framed. That's exactly what's happening this time. The person who reported him did it on purpose. You should arrest the informant and interrogate them properly.\"","Guan Wenjun was somewhat speechless. \"I heard Liu Weidong is already twenty-two. Is that still considered young?\"","Liu Zhengxing nodded. \"The boy is immature. I've made a fool of myself in front of you.\"","Guan Wenjun was a bit unwilling to give up; he felt something was definitely off.","His subordinates ran back one by one to report to him, \"Director, the search is complete. We haven't found any suspicious items.\"","Guan Wenjun led his subordinates into Liu Weidong's room. He looked around and asked, \"Has everything been searched?\"","A subordinate nodded. \"The wardrobe, the kang bed—we flipped everything open and checked. We practically dug three feet into the ground.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun looked at the floor and stomped his leather boots on the tiles, wanting to see if the floor was solid.","At this moment, Liu Zhengxing, standing outside in the main room, suddenly shot a meaningful glance at Sun Qiaofen and Liu Weihong.","It was a signal for them to leave quickly.","Sun Qiaofen immediately caught on. She and Liu Weihong exchanged a glance, grabbed each other's hands, and ran out into the courtyard.","Seeing them make it to the courtyard, the heavy weight in Liu Zhengxing's heart finally lifted a little.","However, he soon realized he had relaxed too early.","Just as Sun Qiaofen and Liu Weihong ran into the courtyard and were about to head out the door, they suddenly heard a chorus of barking.","Before they could react, they suddenly saw three large wolfdogs charge into their courtyard from the darkness, sprinting straight toward them and lunging right at their faces!","Sun Qiaofen and Liu Weihong shrieked instantly.","Sun Qiaofen's voice was very shrill, and her screams were piercingly loud.","Panicking, Sun Qiaofen screamed, \"Wolfdogs! Where did these wolfdogs come from?! Get away!\"","Hearing the commotion, Guan Wenjun quickly rushed out with his men. He soon discovered that Sun Qiaofen and Liu Weihong were in the courtyard. The mother and daughter had just been arguing with him, but taking advantage of his trip to Liu Weidong's room, they had tried to sneak away.","But as luck would have it, three muscular, robust dogs had mysteriously appeared in their courtyard.","The three large dogs lunged at Sun Qiaofen and Liu Weihong. Sun Qiaofen screamed in terror and turned to run, but before she could take two steps, she was tackled to the ground by the big dogs.","Liu Weihong cried and called for help: \"Dad, Dad, save me!\"","Standing inside the house, Liu Zhengxing looked at the ferocious dogs in the courtyard. His hand subconsciously rested on the door, and he took a few steps back, actually looking as if he was about to shut the door.","Guan Wenjun's hand instinctively went to his waist, ready to draw his gun. But then, he suddenly realized that these three large wolfhounds looked a bit familiar.","He muttered, \"Oh, aren't these...\"","Weren't these the military dogs that Qin Yuanzheng kept at the mining area?","Did Qin Yuanzheng send the military dogs over to help?","...","Qin Yuanzheng originally had no intention of using the military dogs, but when he heard Sun Qiaofen making a scene outside, he felt that using them would be more appropriate.","He had a subordinate go to the mining area to fetch the military dogs, and then went to the Revolutionary Committee to let the dogs sniff the scent of Liu Weidong and that drug addict.","Then he hurriedly brought them over.","As soon as the military dogs arrived, they saw Sun Qiaofen pulling Liu Weihong and rushing out the door.","Judging by the dogs' reactions, Sun Qiaofen and Liu Weihong definitely had something on them. At the very least, they must have had a similar scent, otherwise the dogs wouldn't have reacted so strongly.","Both Liu Weihong and Sun Qiaofen were pinned to the ground. They screamed and cried in panic, kicking their legs. \"Get lost, get lost! Stay away!\"","Liu Weihong was still calling out to Liu Zhengxing: \"Dad! Come save me, hurry up and chase these dogs away!\"","Liu Zhengxing was getting anxious. He had wanted to wait for Guan Wenjun to make a move, but Guan Wenjun was taking his time.","On the contrary, after recognizing the familiar military dogs, Guan Wenjun pulled his hand back.","His subordinate asked in a low voice, \"Director, aren't we going to help?\"","Liu Zhengxing was also starting to panic now. He walked up to Guan Wenjun and said, \"Director Guan, hurry up and tell your men to help. My wife and daughter are going to be bitten to death!\"","Guan Wenjun said with a smile, \"Section Chief Liu, your wife just said that it's inappropriate for a group of grown men like us to touch them. What if they accuse us of being hooligans? We can't bear that responsibility.\"","Liu Zhengxing: \"...\"","Liu Zhengxing darkened his face, suppressing all his displeasure and unease.","He whispered to Guan Wenjun, \"Director Guan, please do me this favor. Consider it a debt I, Liu Zhengxing, owe you.\"","Liu Zhengxing knew that Guan Wenjun carried a gun. If he just pulled out his piece, there would be no need to fear those dogs.","Moreover, although those dogs looked vicious and had tackled Sun Qiaofen to the ground, they were not actually biting anyone.","Instead, they kept tearing at Sun Qiaofen's clothes.","Liu Zhengxing had already sensed that something was wrong.","Now he lowered his head, trying to trade a favor for Guan Wenjun's help.","He knew what Guan Wenjun wanted, so right now, he was also making a deal with him.","He thought Guan Wenjun would agree.","However, Guan Wenjun kept his hands in his pockets, looking like he was enjoying a good show. He said, \"Section Chief Liu, don't be nervous. Look, the dogs aren't biting at all. Your wife and daughter aren't hurt in the slightest.\"","Liu Zhengxing: \"...\"","In the courtyard, the three wolfhounds were still tearing at Sun Qiaofen's and Liu Weihong's padded jackets.","After tearing at them for a while, they moved on to tear at Sun Qiaofen's and Liu Weihong's padded trousers.","Before Sun Qiaofen could pull her pants up, they were ripped off by the military dogs. Along with the pants, small yellow boxes spilled out and scattered all over the ground.","It was the same situation for Liu Weihong. After her padded pants were torn open, the boxes hidden inside could no longer be concealed and scattered across the ground.","Liu Zhengxing was an old fox.","Under such urgent circumstances, he had still managed to come up with the idea of having his wife and daughter find the items and hide them close to their bodies.","And they had indeed almost managed to bluff their way through using this method.","Guan Wenjun stood there, watching the disheveled Sun Qiaofen and Liu Weihong in the courtyard.","He realized that since they had hidden the items so closely to their bodies, even if he had stripped off their padded pants and jackets, he wouldn't have found anything.","Because after stripping off the padded clothing, he would have had to strip off a layer of woolen sweaters and pants to see them.","He stared at Sun Qiaofen with lingering fear and said, \"You are too sinister. I was almost tricked by you!\"","With that, Guan Wenjun waved his hand angrily, \"Tie them both up and take them back!\"","Liu Weihong instantly grew terrified. She cried, \"This has nothing to do with me! They made me do it. I don't even know what these things are.\"","Sun Qiaofen was already nervous and scared. Hearing Liu Weihong say this, she also stammered, \"Yes, I... I don't know what this is either...\"","Guan Wenjun couldn't be bothered to waste words on them!","Now that the items had been found, this whole family was going to jail!","Guan Wenjun immediately ordered his men to arrest Sun Qiaofen and Liu Weihong and take them back.","Liu Zhengxing firmly claimed ignorance. He had stayed out of it from beginning to end, so at this moment, Guan Wenjun couldn't arrest him.","So they just arrested Sun Qiaofen and Liu Weihong first.","After the three military dogs completed their mission, a whistle blew outside. The three dogs grinned, tongues lolling, and ran out joyfully.","They had charged in like a gust of wind, and now they ran out like one.","They left behind a courtyard in complete disarray and opium scattered all over the ground.","Liu Zhengxing closed his eyes briefly, watching Guan Wenjun take his wife and daughter away, and watching the Revolutionary Committee members collect all the boxes from the ground to take with them.","He knew in his heart that his son, Liu Weidong, was probably in grave danger this time.","This wasn't something that could be resolved with a simple stint in a labor camp.","He might face the firing squad.","No, he had to think of a way to save Liu Weidong.","...","Out on the pitch-black street, Qin Yuanzheng leaned against his car, petting the military dogs' heads one by one. He told them, \"You performed very well tonight. Tomorrow I'll reward you with meat.\"","Xiao Yang brought a subordinate over to meet him and asked, \"Commander, are you heading back to the mining area?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"No, it's getting late. I need to go home.\"","After all, someone was waiting for him at home.","He said to Xiao Yang, \"Keep a close eye on Liu Zhengxing recently. He'll probably make a move.\"","Xiao Yang nodded. \"Don't worry, Commander, I know what to do.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and got into his car, not caring how Guan Wenjun would handle the case or conduct the interrogations.","He drove straight home.","By the time he returned, it was already very late.","He thought Qiao Lanshu would already be asleep.","Tonight's farce had truly been chaotic enough.","Qin Yuanzheng carefully opened the door to his house, only to find a small oil lamp sitting on the table inside.","Qiao Lanshu was sitting on the sofa wrapped in a small blanket, learning to knit a sweater with needles while listening to the late-night radio broadcast.","Qin Yuanzheng said, somewhat surprised, \"Wife, it's so late, why haven't you gone to bed yet?\"","Qiao Lanshu immediately put down what she was holding, threw off the blanket, and was about to get up from the sofa. \"Brother Zheng, you're finally back. How did things go?\"","Qin Yuanzheng smiled and said, \"Everything went smoothly. Liu Weidong probably won't be able to escape this time.\"","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice and asked, \"Is he really selling opium?\"","Qin Yuanzheng's expression darkened again, and he nodded. \"I really didn't expect that in this day and age, there would still be people selling this kind of thing.\"","Thinking of this, Qin Yuanzheng felt that Liu Weidong was completely courting death.","No one could save him.","Qiao Lanshu thought of the Liu Weidong from her previous life; his future position had not been low at all.","If he was already selling opium now, how did he climb to such a high position?","With such a cadre in the city, the kind of shady deals going on behind the scenes was truly something one didn't dare to think about too deeply.","Qin Yuanzheng took off his shirt and trousers, then went to wash his hands and face.","When he returned, he pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms, asking in a low voice, \"Why are you knitting a sweater? Do you know how to knit?\"","Qiao Lanshu said, feeling a little embarrassed, \"I didn't know how to at first. I've been learning from Sister Ling next door recently, but I haven't quite mastered it yet.\"","Living in a northern city, it simply wouldn't do not to know how to knit sweaters.","After all, the supply and marketing cooperatives had very few ready-made clothes; you could say they basically didn't sell them at all.","She was about to become a mother soon, and she would need to knit sweaters for her own child in the future.","Qin Yuanzheng turned off the radio and carried Qiao Lanshu back to the bedroom. \"It's getting late, let's go to sleep. We still have to work tomorrow.\"","It was a pity. With the whole evening delayed, his intimate time with his wife was gone once again.","If he wanted any, he could only wait until tomorrow night.","Qin Yuanzheng sighed and muttered, \"I hope I can come back earlier tomorrow night. Let's hope nothing else happens.\"","Lately, one incident after another had been happening in the city, leaving everyone completely exhausted."]},{"number":147,"title":"Chapter 147: Xiao Qiao Defends Herself","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun's side handled the interrogation quite quickly. With conclusive evidence against him, Liu Weidong was sentenced to death and would be facing the firing squad before long.","Sun Qiaofen and Liu Weihong, the mother and daughter, stubbornly insisted that they had no idea what that stuff was.","They pinned all the blame on Liu Weidong. After all, Liu Weidong was already beyond saving; they couldn't let him drag his sister and mother down with him, could they?","Consequently, the mother and daughter were sentenced to six years in a labor camp and would be sent away in a couple of days.","Every day at the Revolutionary Committee, Liu Weidong made a fuss about seeing Liu Zhengxing, but the committee members completely ignored him.","In this day and age, he still dared to sell opium, wasn't this driving his own compatriots to their deaths?","A person like him definitely could not be kept around any longer.","Some people could be reformed through labor and corrected, but someone like Liu Weidong was already beyond redemption.","Liu Zhengxing tried to pull a lot of strings, but most of his connections were just leaders or cadres from various bureaus. In front of the director of the Revolutionary Committee, their words carried absolutely no weight.","Sitting in his office, Guan Wenjun leisurely sipped his tea, finally experiencing what it felt like to have people lining up to beg him for favors.","It was simply too satisfying for words!","...","The workers at the food factory had all heard about Liu Weihong's situation.","It was almost time for the year-end holidays, and the female workers in the pickle workshop had all found themselves with free time.","With her pockets full of melon seeds, Wang Xue leaned against Qiao Lanshu's window bright and early in the morning to gossip about the matter. I heard Liu Weihong is being sent to a labor camp? Do you know what she did?","Standing by the window, Qiao Lanshu slowly knitted a sweater and whispered, I heard it is because of her brother. She helped him move opium.","The moment Wang Xue heard this, she instantly started cursing. Then they really deserve to die! How many years has it been since our country stood up, and they are actually doing these dirty deeds again. Getting shot is exactly what he deserves!","Originally, Wang Xue had felt a bit of pity that Liu Weidong was going to be executed.","Now, not a single shred of pity remained in her heart.","She only felt that the siblings, Liu Weidong and Liu Weihong, had purely brought it upon themselves and sought their own doom.","Qiao Lanshu thought of something and suddenly asked, I heard Liu Weihong's partner is quite capable. Do you think he might bail her out?","It was said that Liu Weihong had been sentenced to labor reform.","However, where she would go, how many years she would serve, or whether she might even avoid going altogether, was still up in the air.","In a society built on connections, favors mattered everywhere.","This was especially true for those with power.","Hearing Qiao Lanshu say this, Wang Xue's expression soured. Well, that is really hard to say. Her father is capable, and her partner is capable too, so it is really hard to tell. Sigh, look at this person, she clearly had such a good life, but she just had to do wicked things. She must have had enough of her good days and wanted to taste the bitterness of a labor camp.","Wang Xue rambled on, scolding the Liu siblings for quite a while, and before they knew it, it was already past three in the afternoon.","Although it was still early before their shift ended.","But with only a couple of days left until the holidays, there really was not much work left in any of the workshops.","Wang Xue grabbed a broom, swept up the melon seed shells on the floor, and said, It is almost the New Year. The supply and marketing cooperative has mutton and pork in stock, as well as apples and persimmons. Let us head over early, or we will not be able to get a spot in line later.","Around this time, many people in the factory were sneaking out to buy New Year goods, and the factory supervisors were turning a blind eye to it.","Qiao Lanshu thought for a moment, then nodded. \"Sure, I'd like to buy some apples too.\"","Ever since she got pregnant, she had developed a real craving for fruit.","However, in this era, the vast majority of arable land was dedicated to growing staple crops, making fruit production quite scarce.","Not to mention they were in the north, where fresh fruits and vegetables were already hard to come by during the winter.","If Qiao Lanshu weren't pregnant, she probably wouldn't be so picky.","But now that she was expecting, she wanted to do her best to eat well so the baby growing inside her could develop properly.","Qiao Lanshu packed up her yarn and knitting supplies, placed them in a cloth bag to carry, grabbed a grocery basket, and headed out with Wang Xue.","Wang Xue asked her, \"Are you knitting a sweater for the baby?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled a little shyly. \"I don't know how to knit a sweater yet, it's too difficult. I'm just trying to knit a beanie right now to see if I can manage it.\"","Besides, if it didn't turn out well, she could always unravel it and start over.","There was no need to worry about wasting yarn.","Wang Xue told her, \"If you're in a hurry, just bring the yarn over to me and I'll knit it for you. Babies need a lot of clothes, especially pants... By the way, have you bought diapers yet? Babies wet the bed like crazy. You'll be washing the sheets every single day. It's much easier to just use diapers. After all, you only have the one set of bedding, and it won't be pleasant to sleep on if it smells like pee.\"","Thinking of the large sheet of waterproof flannel Qin Yuanzheng had bought, Qiao Lanshu's face flushed slightly.","She replied in a low voice, \"I haven't prepared the diapers yet...\"","Wang Xue immediately offered, \"Oh, I have two kids at home, and I haven't thrown away their old diapers and little clothes. I'll bring them all over for you later. Don't worry, I've washed them thoroughly and dried them in the sun, so they're perfectly fine to use.\"","In these times, supplies were scarce and people weren't very wealthy. Children's clothes were altered, patched, and mended over and over as they grew.","When they were too worn out to be worn anymore, they would be repurposed into little shorts, undershirts, or even mittens and socks.","People didn't just give away old clothes lightly.","If someone was willing to give them away, it meant they considered the recipient as family.","Qiao Lanshu immediately smiled and said, \"Thank you, Sister.\"","Before this, her neighbor Huang Erling had also given Qiao Lanshu some old diapers and clothes her children used to wear.","At first, Huang Erling had been worried that Qiao Lanshu might find them distasteful, so she had asked tentatively. Once she realized Qiao Lanshu didn't mind at all, she happily brought them over.","Wang Xue added, \"Having a baby is no easy feat. You're about three months along now, right? Have you told your parents yet?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. She wanted to wait until the pregnancy was more stable before writing to her father.","Qin Yuanzheng felt the same way. After all, he had previously been rumored to be sterile, so he also wanted to wait until Qiao Lanshu's pregnancy was secure before writing to his parents, just in case he got their hopes up for nothing.","Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu arrived at the supply and marketing cooperative together. Sure enough, long lines had already formed in front of every counter.","Wang Xue immediately told Qiao Lanshu, \"You're pregnant, so don't go squeezing in with them. Just follow behind me.\"","Saying that, Wang Xue led Qiao Lanshu into the crowd to line up.","They needed to buy meat, as well as sheep fat and lard.","Sheep fat could be used to make oil tea, while lard was perfect for stir-frying vegetables, making the dishes fragrant and appetizing.","There were also fresh white radishes available today, but unfortunately, just like the meat, they were all strictly rationed.","Qiao Lanshu bought some meat, then some apples, and finally, she and Wang Xue each bought a radish.","When the two of them came out of the supply and marketing cooperative, just as they reached the main entrance, they were suddenly stopped.","The person was wearing a police uniform and looked exactly like the police comrade they were familiar with.","When the police comrade saw Qiao Lanshu, he was also a bit surprised, as they were familiar faces to each other after all.","The police comrade, Xiao Jiang, looked at Qiao Lanshu with a serious expression and said, Hello, comrade. Someone reported that you are illegally trading contraband. Please cooperate with our inspection.","Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu exchanged a glance.","Qiao Lanshu said hesitantly, We were just buying groceries at the cooperative. We didn't make any private trades with anyone.","Wang Xue also nodded and quickly explained, That's right, police comrade. We haven't been doing any of that profiteering stuff. Did you mistake us for someone else?","At this point, the two of them still thought the police comrade was referring to profiteering.","They thought they had been reported for buying things from black market vendors.","But in reality, the situation was far more serious than they imagined.","Since they were acquaintances, Police Officer Xiao Jiang whispered to Qiao Lanshu, Comrade Xiao Qiao, it's like this. Someone reported that you were trading opium with someone near the cooperative. This is a very serious matter, so we have to investigate.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu's heart skipped a beat, and she suddenly felt that something was very wrong.","Why was the police comrade bringing up opium, and even saying she was trading it secretly?","Let alone opium, she couldn't even stand the smell of regular tobacco.","Ever since Qin Yuanzheng married her, he had even quit smoking.","She whispered, Police comrade, this must be a misunderstanding. No one in our family smokes, and I haven't even bought shredded tobacco before. How could I secretly trade with others?","Not to mention something like opium.","That was an offense punishable by the firing squad, and it wasn't like she didn't know that.","Wait, the firing squad...","Wasn't there just someone recently who was about to be executed by firing squad for secretly trading opium?","Qiao Lanshu fell silent again.","She suddenly began to understand what was going on.","But understanding it now was already too late.","Because Police Officer Xiao Jiang had already taken Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue's shopping baskets and rummaged through them.","Soon, Police Officer Xiao Jiang pulled out a two-finger-wide roll wrapped in black cloth from Qiao Lanshu's basket.","He brought it to his nose and sniffed it. His expression instantly changed, and he looked down at Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu defended herself with a calm expression. Police comrade, I don't know when this thing was put into my basket. There are too many people in the cooperative. If someone secretly slipped something into my basket, I wouldn't have noticed.","Besides, we were queuing up to buy things the whole time. You know that the meat supply at the meat counter is limited; if you come late, it's gone. I barely had enough time to line up and grab some meat, so how would I have the time to do this? If you don't believe me, you can go ask the security guard at the meat counter. He is responsible for maintaining order and should have seen how long I was in line. What's more, with so many people here, it wouldn't be the best time for a trade anyway.","As she spoke, Qiao Lanshu stroked her belly and continued, \"Furthermore, I am three months pregnant. No matter what, I have to think of my child. I couldn't possibly do something so risky. I hope you can investigate this matter thoroughly. This is complete slander and a frame-up against me, and I demand that the culprit be severely punished.\"","Qiao Lanshu was clear and logical, and her words were well-founded. Originally, Wang Xue had been anxious, afraid that Qiao Lanshu would be at a disadvantage, and had wanted to speak up to defend her.","Hearing her say all this, Wang Xue had nothing left to add. She just glared at the police officers and said, \"Yes, it's exactly as she said! If you don't believe it, go ask the security guards maintaining order at the raw meat counter. The act of casually slandering a young woman like this is too despicable and must be heavily punished!\"","Officer Xiao Jiang also admired Qiao Lanshu's fearlessness in the face of danger. After all, if others had encountered such a situation, they would have long been panicking and crying out.","Qiao Lanshu was truly very calm.","Moreover, she was able to defend herself clearly and logically.","Her words had even convinced the two police officers.","Officer Xiao Jiang solemnly put the item into a transparent bag before saying to Qiao Lanshu, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, although I personally believe what you say, according to procedure, you still have to take a trip to the police station with us.\"","Pausing for a moment, he added in a low voice, \"But don't worry. The report we received didn't just involve you alone. The police station has already brought in three others.\"","Those three people all had family members working as cadres in various departments; they were all family members of high-ranking officials.","Where Qiao Lanshu differed from them was that her husband was a military officer, making her a military officer's family member.","But the commonality was that their families all held some power and influence.","Hearing Officer Xiao Jiang say this, Qiao Lanshu's thoughts became even clearer.","This was likely someone trying to save Liu Weidong, not wanting him to die.","That was why they came up with this trick.","Didn't the Revolutionary Committee say that secretly trading opium would result in execution by firing squad?","Then what if the family members of these military men and officials were also trading it secretly?","Would the Revolutionary Committee dare to shoot them all together?","If they didn't dare, and the police station dared to let even one go, then there would be room to maneuver in Liu Weidong's case.","This move was too sinister and completely impossible to guard against.","Even if Qiao Lanshu hadn't gone out with Wang Xue today, if she were standing at the entrance of the food factory waiting for Qin Yuanzheng to pick her up, as long as she was distracted for a single moment, the other party could have found an opportunity to stuff the item into her basket.","The city was strictly managed now, so people didn't have much of a guard up.","Who knew someone would be so insidious as to pull a trick like this directly?","Qiao Lanshu knew she couldn't avoid it this time; she couldn't just refuse to cooperate with the police officers' work.","Furthermore, she also wanted to go to the police station to take a look and communicate with the other three victims to see if they could find the person who had framed them.","Qiao Lanshu nodded and said to Officer Xiao Jiang, \"Alright, then I will go to the police station with you.\"","Hearing her say this, Officer Xiao Jiang immediately breathed a sigh of relief.","He had originally been afraid that Qiao Lanshu would refuse to cooperate with his work.","After all, the previous three had been unwilling to cooperate and even tried to use the leaders in their families to pressure him.","Little did they know, he was just a low-ranking police officer merely doing his duty.","Officer Xiao Jiang immediately said, \"Okay then, let's get in the car first.\"","The police car from their public security bureau was parked in the intersection opposite the supply and marketing cooperative. It was dilapidated, looking almost like a scrapped vehicle.","Wang Xue quickly reached out, held onto Qiao Lanshu's arm, and whispered, \"Xiao Qiao, are you really going with them? You are clearly being framed. It should be fine if you don't go, right? How about you wait here, and I will go get Regiment Commander Qin for you?\"","Wang Xue felt that simply calling Qin Yuanzheng over would solve everything.","He was a military officer, after all; these police comrades would not dare make things difficult for Qiao Lanshu with him around.","However, Qiao Lanshu said, \"It is not easy for the police comrades to carry out their work. This matter is full of suspicious points, and I believe the police comrades have basic judgment. They wouldn't truly believe that I would secretly trade opium, right?\"","Officer Xiao Jiang and his colleague exchanged a glance.","She had just flattered them so highly; how could they possibly admit to lacking judgment?","The two immediately nodded. Xiao Jiang said, \"Of course. It is obvious that someone did this on purpose. Comrade Xiao Qiao, rest assured, going to the police station is just to cooperate in making a statement. We will conduct a thorough investigation afterward.\""]},{"number":148,"title":"Chapter 148: Let's All Just Prove Ourselves Then","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu followed Officer Xiao Jiang to the police station.","Inside the police station, sure enough, there were already three family members of government officials making a fuss.","Among these three, one was the mother of the deputy director of the Education Bureau. Already in her sixties, she felt terribly wronged, claiming she had merely gone out to buy groceries, only to be arrested by the police on her way back.","The second was the wife of a minor section chief from the Commerce Bureau. This section chief's position wasn't actually that high, but who told his wife to happen to go lining up at the supply and marketing cooperative?","With so many people lining up at the cooperative, the culprit probably just targeted whoever they saw. Whose basket ended up with illicit goods was purely a matter of luck.","The third was the younger brother of the Deputy Chief of the police station, Li Jianlin. A young man in his twenties, his factory had let out early, so he went out to stroll around the mall with nothing to do, and ended up with something extra in his pocket on the way back.","Deputy Chief Li Jianlin crossed his arms and looked at his younger brother, Li Jiangang.","Li Jiangang said nervously, Bro, I am really innocent. How could I smoke this stuff? I still want to join the police force, would I do such a thing?","Li Jiangang was over ten years younger than Li Jianlin and was practically raised by him.","Naturally, he was heavily influenced by Li Jianlin.","When Li Jianlin was in the military, his brother Li Jiangang wanted to enlist. Later, when he was old enough, Li Jianlin had transferred to the police station.","So then he wanted to become a police officer instead.","How could a young man who was entirely focused on becoming a soldier or a policeman smuggle opium?","It wasn't that Li Jianlin was being overly protective of his brother; it just didn't make logical sense.","Li Jiangang scrunched up his face and said to Li Jianlin, Bro, this must be a misunderstanding. Why don't you just let me go? If people find out about this, it will have a bad impact on me.","He had just been set up on a blind date and was really into the girl. If this ruined it, where would he go to cry?","Li Jianlin said with a stern face, You need to call me Deputy Chief Li!","Li Jiangang was speechless.","Looking at his older brother, Li Jiangang said aggrievedly, Alright, Deputy Chief Li. Deputy Chief Li, I am truly innocent. I hope you will look into this clearly.","The mother of the deputy director of the Education Bureau, who was in her sixties, was also very nervous after being brought here. She had exhausted herself explaining earlier, but now that she had rested, she came over and said, Deputy Chief Li, I am truly being framed. You have to believe me! I don't even know when this thing fell into my basket.","These people came from well-off families and were intellectuals, so they wouldn't quarrel like street shrews.","But as they surrounded Li Jianlin, each crying foul, they made his head buzz with noise.","Frowning, he said to the three of them, I know there must be a misunderstanding here, but don't worry for now. Have a seat, drink a cup of tea, and calm down.","Saying this, Li Jianlin instructed his brother Li Jiangang, Go pour them some water and bring over a chair.","Li Jiangang was speechless.","Li Jiangang said in disbelief, Deputy Chief Li, I am a victim too.","Li Jianlin was short-handed right now. Aside from the old man guarding the gate, he was the only one in the entire police station; the other two had been sent out to arrest people.","He glared at Li Jiangang and said, Just go when I tell you to!","Li Jiangang was speechless.","Resigning to his fate, Li Jiangang brought a chair for the sixty-year-old woman and the crying young wife, and poured each of them a cup of hot water.","Of course, he didn't forget to pour a cup of hot water for himself.","Because he needed to calm down too.","Today's experience was simply too thrilling and terrifying.","He was still in shock even now.","Unfortunately, he was a man and couldn't cry and weep.","At this time, the other two young police officers had also returned with Qiao Lanshu.","Li Jianlin felt so frustrated. That made four. Could there be more after this?","Sitting there, he asked toward the door, Officer Xiao Jiang, are there any more reports?","He was asking if there was a fifth one.","Officer Xiao Jiang walked in looking travel-worn and immediately said, Chief Li, no more. This is the last one for now.","Because there was no official chief in the police station, only Deputy Chief Li Jianlin, Officer Xiao Jiang and the others usually just called him Chief Li, omitting the word deputy.","Hearing this, Li Jianlin, who was sitting in the hall, breathed a sigh of relief. He said, That's good. Four is already too many...","However, before he could fully relax, he abruptly stood up again upon seeing the fourth suspect.","He stared at Qiao Lanshu in disbelief. Comrade Xiao Qiao? Why are you here?","This was Yama Qin's family member. Could she also be secretly smuggling opium?","Officer Xiao Jiang also felt somewhat helpless.","He placed the stolen goods he was carrying onto Li Jianlin's desk and said, Chief Li, Comrade Xiao Qiao is the fourth reported suspect.","Li Jianlin was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu walked into the room, glanced at the crying woman next to her, and actually managed to smile.","She smiled and said to Li Jianlin, Chief Li, I went to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy groceries this afternoon. As soon as I came out, I was brought back by the police comrade. I have no idea who put that thing in my basket. I am completely unaware of it.","Li Jianlin was speechless.","Actually, the family members of other officials were easier to handle, but if it involved a military family member, the situation was a bit different.","A military officer's family member being framed, this...","Wait, Li Jianlin suddenly thought, having a military family member involved was perfect.","His police station was short-handed, so he could just hand this over to the military department to handle!","Li Jianlin immediately clapped his hands and said with a smile, Good, good, good...","Everyone was confused.","Li Jianlin realized his gaffe and quickly said, Oh, no, I don't mean it's good that you're here. I mean... come, Comrade Xiao Qiao, sit down for a while. You are pregnant and shouldn't stand for long. Right, Officer Xiao Jiang, hurry up and pour a cup of water for Comrade Xiao Qiao. Why are you just standing there?","Officer Xiao Jiang hurried to pour water for Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu sat together with the other two female relatives of the officials, and they each gave their statements.","Basically, they were all completely unaware, inexplicably arrested, and then falsely accused of smuggling opium and the like.","Li Jianlin waited gleefully in his heart for Qin Yuanzheng to come looking for his wife.","As a result, before Qin Yuanzheng arrived, the people from the Inspection Department came.","Four or five people from the city's Inspection Department arrived. As soon as they entered the police station, they said to Li Jianlin with serious expressions, Deputy Chief Li, we received a report that a group is smuggling opium. The behavior is extremely egregious. These suspects will be taken over by our Inspection Department.","Li Jianlin was a bit dumbfounded. He quickly said, How about handing them over to the Revolutionary Committee first? They also have...","The person from the Inspection Department said very seriously, The people over there will also be taken over by us. This matter is of great importance and is not something your police station can handle. Don't ask any more questions.","Li Jianlin was speechless.","Li Jianlin wanted to say more, but the people from the Inspection Department wouldn't listen to him.","Strictly speaking, the people from the Inspection Department did indeed have the authority to take over this case.","Because the smuggled goods were strictly controlled opium, the Public Security Bureau was now considered a marginalized department. They had few personnel and, naturally, not much power.","Qiao Lanshu looked at these aggressive people. She knew that if she left with the people from the Inspection Department, she would definitely not be able to wash away the stigma on her. These people would immediately convict the four of them and sentence them.","She immediately said, \"Chief Li, I am a military dependent. I have the right to apply for a military takeover.\"","The people from the Inspection Department immediately retorted, \"This is opium, a contraband item. It falls under the jurisdiction of our Inspection Department and has nothing to do with the military.\"","However, before he could finish his tough words, more than a dozen soldiers carrying guns suddenly swarmed in from outside the door.","Qin Yuanzheng walked in wearing his military uniform, his expression so gloomy it looked as if he was going to kill someone. \"Who said it has nothing to do with us?\"","He really didn't expect someone to dare bully his wife like this. Besides the Liu family, there was probably no one else.","He walked up to the person from the Inspection Department, stared at him with a dark face, and asked coldly, \"Does your woman have nothing to do with you? Do your children have nothing to do with you? Who sent you here? Where is the investigation warrant? Show it to me.\"","The other party: \"...\"","The already small lobby of the Public Security Bureau suddenly seemed very crowded with all these big men squeezed in.","The officer from the Inspection Department looked at these soldiers and immediately became a little nervous.","The person had instructed him to take all these suspects away before the military arrived.","But who knew these soldiers would come so fast?","It was only past four in the afternoon, far from the end of the workday.","Looking at the furious Qin Yuanzheng, the several people from the Inspection Department suddenly felt the urge to retreat.","Staff Officer Lin Yucheng frowned and stared at them, saying, \"Are you mute? Our regiment commander is asking you a question! Which leader sent you here? Where is the investigation warrant?\"","The leading officer of the Inspection Department smiled awkwardly and said, \"We came in a hurry this time and forgot the investigation warrant. We didn't bring it...\"","If it weren't for the fact that soldiers couldn't hit people, Qin Yuanzheng would have wanted to kick him.","If he had known, he wouldn't have worn his military uniform.","These bastards who bullied his wife, he really wanted to slaughter them all one by one.","Staff Officer Lin was also speechless.","After listening to Wang Xue hurriedly explain the course of events, he was also very worried about Qiao Lanshu.","He immediately ran out together with Qin Yuanzheng.","Fortunately, they came early. If they had come a little later, wouldn't Comrade Xiao Qiao have been taken away by them?","Qin Yuanzheng's voice was freezing cold as he said, \"Arrest all of them. Coming to the Public Security Bureau to arrest people and investigate a case without an investigation warrant is a serious violation of the law. Throw them in jail and interrogate them thoroughly!\"","These bastards usually occupied their posts without doing any real work, but now that his wife was being framed, they were jumping around actively.","Keeping them in their posts was just a waste of the country's money and rice. It would be better to send them to a labor camp farm, where they could at least create some value for the country.","The military men didn't even need the public security comrades to act. They directly stepped forward, pinned those people down, and escorted them all to the interrogation room at the back of the Public Security Bureau.","Those few people were still shouting, \"We are doing things according to formal procedures. You can't do this!\"","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't be bothered to listen to their sophistry.","He guessed the person behind this didn't want to expose their identity, which was why they didn't sign and approve an investigation warrant. But just this one point was enough to throw all these people in jail.","Qin Yuanzheng's actions stunned the public security comrades as well as the other three victims.","For a moment, the lobby was very quiet, and the weeping young wife didn't dare to cry anymore.","The sighing old lady who had been saying she wanted to die didn't dare to make a sound either.","Li Jiangang, holding a cup of hot water, quietly moved behind his older brother.","No one dared to speak.","After all, these soldiers were all tall and mighty, and they were all carrying guns.","Mother of God, this was too majestic, too handsome, too stylish!","Li Jiangang's eyes went straight.","He suddenly felt that being a public security officer was really boring; once the military arrived, they were nothing.","Qin Yuanzheng ignored these people. He had come in a hurry, burning with anxiety, terrified that his little wife would be frightened by this kind of scene. What if it affected her pregnancy?","It was his fault. He knew that Liu Zhengxing definitely couldn't bear for his son Liu Weidong to die, and would inevitably make some moves.","But he didn't expect the other party to act so fast and use such insidious tricks.","He quickly walked up to Qiao Lanshu. She was sitting in a chair, still holding that cup of hot water, quietly looking at Qin Yuanzheng.","Today was also the first time she had seen Qin Yuanzheng angry.","Strangely enough, she wasn't scared at all.","Although Qin Yuanzheng was very fierce and scary when he was angry, because she knew he would not hurt her, even if he raised his hand in front of her, she would only think of a hug, not a beating.","Everyone at the scene saw this tall, mighty, gloomy, and fierce officer with a frosty face suddenly get down on one knee in front of Qiao Lanshu.","This officer's voice, which had just been rough and cold as if rolled in sand.","Now, it was gentle and low, as if he had drank honey.","He looked up at Qiao Lanshu and said in a low voice, \"Wife, you weren't scared, were you?\"","As he spoke, he first checked Qiao Lanshu's complexion, then reached out and gently placed his hand on her abdomen.","The people around them were screaming in their hearts: exactly who was the one being scared?","They were the ones who were scared, okay?","Staff Officer Lin looked at everyone's nervous expressions and tactfully led the soldiers out, guarding the main gate of the Public Security Bureau to prevent any other tactless people from coming over.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and shook her head, whispering, \"Brother Zheng, I'm fine. Don't be nervous.\"","Saying that, she handed over the water cup in her hand. \"Look at you, your lips are peeling. Quickly drink some water to moisten them.\"","Qiao Lanshu wasn't deliberately showing off their affection; she purely felt sorry for Qin Yuanzheng.","She couldn't bear to see him uncomfortable.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't want to drink water; he wasn't in the mood.","But since his wife was feeding him, this water would probably be a bit sweeter, so he might as well take a sip.","The tall officer knelt in front of his wife, took a sip of water directly from her hand, and added, \"It's really delicious.\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Watching this scene, Li Jiangang silently downed the warm water in his hand in one gulp.","He even smacked his lips, and subsequently received a fierce glare from his own older brother.","Just when Li Jianlin thought that Qin Yuanzheng would forcefully take his wife home and this matter would be left unsettled.","He heard Qiao Lanshu suddenly say with a serious expression, \"Sir Officer, I want to report the head of the county personnel department, Liu Zhengxing, for peddling opium to me. When I refused to buy it, he tried to force the sale on me. I suspect he has profited a lot from this, and I suggest he be arrested and thoroughly interrogated.\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu and blinked.","His wife had been slandered by others, and now she was turning around and slandering someone else in return.","Since she had to prove her innocence, then everyone might as well prove their innocence together. Even if he couldn't be sentenced in the end, wasting a day or half a day of Liu Zhengxing's time would still be pretty good.","Hearing this, Li Jianlin immediately nudged his younger brother Li Jiangang with his elbow, winking at him frantically, and said, \"Brother, didn't you say earlier that you also wanted to report Liu Zhengxing? Hurry up and tell this officer, let him seek justice for you.\"","Li Jiangang: \"...\"","Wait, when did he ever...","Poked again by his own older brother, Li Jiangang did not know for a moment whether this Liu Zhengxing was really the mastermind, or if his brother simply wanted to curry favor with the military officer.","He quickly stammered, watching his brother's expression as he spoke, \"Oh, oh, right, right, it is that Li Zhengxin, right? He...\"","Li Jianlin cursed in a low voice, \"It is Liu Zhengxing!\"","Li Jiangang said nervously, \"Liu Zhengxing, he forced me to buy and sell, he forced me to smoke opium, wanting to lead me down the path of crime. I definitely could not do that, right?\"","After finishing, he added, \"Sir Officer, I am truly innocent! Why don't you just let me go.\"","Everyone: \"...\"","The sixty-year-old lady had thought she was just getting old and her eyes were failing her, which was why she had not spotted the culprit.","But two of the victims had already pointed the finger at Liu Zhengxing.","Then the person who framed them must be Liu Zhengxing!","The sixty-something-year-old lady stood up and cursed loudly:","\"It is this Liu Zhengxing! Putting things in my basket. He is from the personnel department, I know him! This bastard, he usually looks so gentle and refined, I never expected him to be such an animal! Sir Officer, I suspect he is a secret agent, a spy, an enemy element endangering our national security! You must arrest him and rid the people of this menace!\"","As the saying goes, repeated rumors become facts, and public clamor can melt gold.","In this era where a mere report could lead to a prison sentence.","With three people reporting Liu Zhengxing, even if he did not do it, he would still be locked up and interrogated for several days."]},{"number":149,"title":"Chapter 149: What, didn't catch the person","paragraphs":["Because three people had reported Liu Zhengxing, coupled with the items previously confiscated from Liu Weidong's room, an arrest warrant was immediately issued for Liu Zhengxing.","Of course, Qin Yuanzheng did not carry it out himself.","It was Chief of Staff Lin Yucheng from the military who took the lead, bringing along people from the Public Security Bureau and the Revolutionary Committee to his door.","Guan Wenjun had initially been quite pleased with himself for cracking Liu Weidong's case.","After all, it counted as a meritorious service on his part. But who could have known that the incident of Qiao Lanshu and the others being framed for opium trafficking would happen right after?","When Guan Wenjun heard that Qiao Lanshu had also been taken to the Public Security Bureau, he instantly grew displeased. He glared at Deputy Chief of Public Security Li Jianlin and said,","\"Li Jianlin, if you don't know how to sit properly in this Deputy Chief position, then get up and let me sit there. What kind of things are you doing day in and day out? Little Qiao is such a good girl, she doesn't even dare to tell a lie, and you think she would secretly smuggle opium?\"","Li Jianlin felt truly wronged. \"I also know they were framed. But wasn't it because someone reported them, and then we just so happened to find the 'stolen goods' on them?\"","Guan Wenjun gritted his teeth and cursed, \"These people from the Liu family are really nothing good!\"","Upon arriving at the gate of Liu Zhengxing's workplace, Guan Wenjun looked at the several soldiers following beside him and asked Chief of Staff Lin, \"In a moment, will you guys make the arrest, or should I?\"","Chief of Staff Lin was a military man. They had come along this time because military dependents were involved; their role was to accompany and assist in the investigation, and if necessary, transfer the military dependents to the military base.","As for actually arresting civilians, the military certainly couldn't be the ones to do it.","Chief of Staff Lin replied, \"You two go ahead.\"","Guan Wenjun then took his men and went into the county's Personnel Department with Li Jianlin.","Guan Wenjun even said aggressively, \"Later, when we catch Liu Zhengxing, just hand him over to our Revolutionary Committee for interrogation.\"","Li Jianlin was more than happy to avoid offending anyone. He immediately said, \"Of course, no problem. I'll listen to Director Guan.\"","However, when the group arrived at the Personnel Department, they did not find Liu Zhengxing.","After asking around, they discovered that Liu Zhengxing had not come to work today.","The group then took a detour to Liu Zhengxing's house, only to find that no one was home either.","Liu Zhengxing had disappeared to who knows where.","At eight o'clock in the evening, everyone returned to the lobby of the Public Security Bureau empty-handed.","By this time, the other three framed cadre family members had already been allowed to go home early, so as to spare their families from worrying.","However, the Public Security Bureau instructed them not to go out recently; they had to stay at home and be ready for summoning at any time.","Qiao Lanshu had not returned yet, because Qin Yuanzheng was still at the Public Security Bureau.","The Public Security Bureau usually only had a few people working, and there was no cafeteria or anything of the sort.","But there was a kitchen in the backyard, where Li Jianlin and the others would normally cook and eat while on duty.","When Guan Wenjun, Li Jianlin, Chief of Staff Lin, and the rest returned, they smelled the aroma of food wafting through the Public Security Bureau.","Guan Wenjun immediately clutched his stomach and said loudly, \"Oh my, Deputy Chief Li, I didn't expect your Public Security Bureau to have a chef! We've been busy all evening and I'm starving. Let's hurry up and eat.\"","Li Jianlin said hesitantly, \"That shouldn't be. We definitely don't have a chef in our bureau.\"","Moreover, the only two public security subordinates he had were taken out with him tonight.","The only people left at the Public Security Bureau were the military personnel and Qin Yuanzheng.","When the group of men walked into the police station, they saw Qiao Lanshu sitting at the long table in the lobby, eating her meal.","Qin Yuanzheng sat right beside her, constantly putting food into her bowl. \"Wife, the mutton you bought today is really good. Eat a little more, it's nutritious. Oh, how is this pickled shredded radish? I added some vinegar, is it too sour? Be a good girl, even if it's not the best, try to eat a bit more. The baby needs nutrition...\"","Qin Yuanzheng was coaxing his little wife to eat with gentle, soft whispers.","His voice was sickeningly sweet, so overly affectionate that it gave the three grown men who had just walked in the chills.","Staff Officer Lin covered his eyes, looking as if he couldn't bear to witness the scene.","Their regiment commander was acting way too shamelessly cheap. Looking at the face the commander made while coaxing his wife, Lin felt too embarrassed to even look!","Guan Wenjun felt a sour pang in his heart, filled with both jealousy and envy.","Not going to lie, seeing a scene like this suddenly made him want to get married, too.","He walked straight over and took a look at the meal Qin Yuanzheng had cooked for Qiao Lanshu.","There was a plate of cold pickled shredded radish, followed by a steaming hot bowl of mutton noodle soup.","The mutton noodle soup smelled incredibly appetizing. Guan Wenjun, his stomach rumbling, said, \"Not bad, Commander Qin! I didn't expect you to have such culinary skills! Are there any more noodles left? I'm starving to death.\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at them and, as if flipping a switch, his expression instantly turned cold and deadpan. He said in a deep voice, \"No more. If you want to eat, go make it yourself.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Lin Yucheng had long known what kind of character their regiment commander was. The only reason he would ever step into a kitchen to cook was entirely for his own wife.","Otherwise, under normal circumstances like this, they wouldn't even bother eating.","Qin Yuanzheng then turned to Li Jianlin and said, \"Deputy Chief Li, I apologize for using your flour just now. I'll have someone bring some flour back tomorrow.\"","Li Jianlin hurriedly waved it off. \"No need, no need, Commander Qin. It's just a little bit of flour. What's eaten is eaten, just consider it my treat. There's really no need to be so polite.\"","Even though flour was quite precious in this era.","However, officials like them received subsidies, so they wouldn't necessarily feel heartbroken over a small amount of flour.","But Qin Yuanzheng was not the type of person willing to owe anyone a favor. Since he said he would return it, he absolutely would.","Not willing to give up, Guan Wenjun took a stroll around the kitchen, only to discover that this guy, Qin Yuanzheng, hadn't even left a single drop of noodle broth. He had already washed the pot completely clean.","It was simply outrageous!","Guan Wenjun had thought that coming in to drink some leftover broth would be fine, but now, he could only down a glass of water. He walked out and ordered his subordinates to go to the nearby state-run restaurant to buy some food to bring back.","He couldn't just stay hungry, and besides, he had money. He certainly wasn't going to mistreat himself.","Li Jianlin and a few young police officers had already skillfully dug out some dry steamed bun slices or flatbreads from their drawers and started eating.","Qiao Lanshu had pretty much finished eating. She put down her bowl and chopsticks, asking in confusion, \"What's wrong? Did you guys not catch Liu Zhengxing?\"","Qin Yuanzheng had stayed at the police station precisely because he wanted to watch them interrogate Liu Zhengxing.","As a result, everyone was a little surprised that they hadn't caught the man.","While gnawing on a slice of dry bun, Li Jianlin said, \"Sigh, we went to the personnel department and the Liu residence, but he wasn't at either place. I have no idea where he went.\"","Staff Officer Lin guessed, \"He's probably out pulling strings for his son's case, which is why he's not home?\"","Guan Wenjun immediately suggested, \"Then we should go check the state-run restaurant. If he's looking for people to pull strings, wouldn't he have to treat them to a meal?\"","With that, he dispatched another subordinate, sending them to the state-run restaurant to take a look.","Sure enough, Guan Wenjun's guess was spot on. That Liu Zhengxing really was at the state-run restaurant."]},{"number":150,"title":"Chapter 150: See How Tough Your Fate Is","paragraphs":["The people from the Revolutionary Committee found Liu Zhengxing near the state-run restaurant.","Liu Zhengxing hadn't actually been eating in the state-run restaurant.","However, upon being found, he didn't resist at all and cooperated fully, following them straight to the police station.","As soon as they arrived at the police station, everyone smelled the aroma of roasted sweet potatoes.","Qiao Lanshu was sitting in the adjacent office with the door open. When she caught the scent, she commented, \"Smells so good. It makes me want to eat a roasted sweet potato.\"","Qin Yuanzheng, sitting beside her, said, \"Liu Zhengxing probably just ate one. There's a roasted sweet potato stall in the alley behind the state-run restaurant that's pretty good. It's a bit late today, but I'll go buy you one tomorrow.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded.","She thought to herself: Liu Zhengxing was getting on in years; who would have expected him to go out and buy roasted sweet potatoes late at night?","How surprising.","The surprising Liu Zhengxing sat in the interrogation room. When interrogated by Li Jianlin and the others, he naturally flatly denied the allegations of forced buying and selling.","He said, \"I am a cadre, a Party member. How could I possibly do such a thing?\"","Guan Wenjun slammed the table in anger, pointing at him and scolding, \"You have the nerve to say that? Isn't Liu Weidong your son? I now reasonably suspect that Liu Weidong did all those things entirely under your orders!\"","Liu Zhengxing sat there. He had a lean figure and a gentle, refined aura. Even when yelled at by Guan Wenjun like this, his expression remained perfectly calm.","He said, \"Director Guan, if you are out to condemn someone, you can always trump up a charge. I am innocent anyway, and you can forget about extracting a confession through torture.\"","With that, Liu Zhengxing even bit back. He said disdainfully, \"Director Guan, if a mere report is enough to convict me, then I report Li Jianlin and the 21st Regiment officer Qin Yuanzheng. They instructed their younger brother or wife to smuggle opium for profit. They should be arrested and interrogated together as well. What do you think about that?\"","Li Jianlin's face flushed red with anger. He shouted, \"Nonsense! How could I possibly do such a thing!\"","Liu Zhengxing said with a composed look, \"Then it's equally impossible for me to do such a thing. On what grounds are you arresting me?\"","Guan Wenjun and Li Jianlin interrogated him for over an hour, going back and forth, but they couldn't get anything out of him.","At this rate, they would have to let Liu Zhengxing go.","After all, he was a cadre; they couldn't just detain him without cause.","Qin Yuanzheng saw that it was already nine o'clock in the evening. He originally wanted to take Qiao Lanshu home first.","But he was worried that if the interrogation failed and Liu Zhengxing was released, the man would come after his wife again.","So he patiently sat in the police station office, bringing Qiao Lanshu plenty of newspapers to read.","Staff Officer Lin and the others had long since returned to the military base.","Guan Wenjun walked into the office cursing. He said, \"Damn it, this Liu Zhengxing really has some tricks up his sleeve. He's hard to deal with. Lao Li and I interrogated him for so long, but he stubbornly refused to reveal a single word. If this continues, we'll have no choice but to let him go.\"","Since Liu Zhengxing was a cadre, without hard evidence, they needed his own confession; otherwise, it would be difficult to make a case.","Qin Yuanzheng saw that it was getting late, and his little wife had already yawned twice.","He had lost his patience too.","He stood up and said, \"I'll go give it a try.\"","Saying that, he took off his military uniform, leaving only his black undershirt on. He let Qiao Lanshu know, then opened the office door and walked out.","Qiao Lanshu sat in her chair, still holding the newspaper. She asked curiously, \"Director Guan, if my Brother Zheng goes in, will he be able to get anything out of Liu Zhengxing?\"","Look at this young couple deeply in love, always saying my this and my that at every turn.","Guan Wenjun felt a bit sour in his heart. He sat opposite Qiao Lanshu, took a sip from a glass of water, and then said, \"Hard to say. Qin Yuanzheng's abilities are about the same as mine, and in some areas, he's not even as good as me. If I couldn't get him to talk, he'll probably fall short too.\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu knew that nothing good would ever come out of Guan Wenjun's mouth.","So she continued reading her newspaper, ignoring Guan Wenjun.","Guan Wenjun couldn't stay here forever either. After all, Qiao Lanshu was here, so he tactfully stood up, opened the door, and left.","Ten minutes later, Qin Yuanzheng emerged from the interrogation room.","He walked into the office to pick up Qiao Lanshu and said, \"The matter is settled. Let's go, we're going home.\"","As he spoke, he grabbed his clothes and started putting them on.","Then he picked up Qiao Lanshu's coat and scarf to help her dress.","Qiao Lanshu was indeed sleepy and really wanted to go home and sleep.","But she was even more curious. While stretching out her arms and cooperating with Qin Yuanzheng as he dressed her, she whispered, \"Brother Zheng, you got the answers out of him that quickly? Did that Liu Zhengxing confess?\"","Guan Wenjun and the others had interrogated him for over an hour and couldn't get a thing out of Liu Zhengxing.","Qin Yuanzheng finished the interrogation this fast?","Looking at Qiao Lanshu's sparkling eyes, filled with curiosity and admiration, Qin Yuanzheng felt a surge of sweet delight in his heart.","Truth be told, being looked at by his little wife with such an expression made him even happier than when he earned merits in the military.","He tied her scarf, then put her hat on, and said in a low voice, \"He confessed. He paid off a few young, ignorant thugs to slip the items into the baskets of you and the others.\"","The list of those three people wasn't fixed; they would drop the items on whoever presented the right opportunity.","However, Qiao Lanshu was specifically targeted by Liu Zhengxing. He instructed the thug that it absolutely had to be placed in Qiao Lanshu's basket.","Liu Zhengxing was doing this to get revenge on Qiao Lanshu because of the matters concerning his son and daughter.","Qin Yuanzheng had handed the list of those thugs over to Li Jianlin and Guan Wenjun so they could coordinate an arrest.","Once those individuals were arrested and thoroughly interrogated, the case could be officially closed.","As they walked out, Qiao Lanshu heard Liu Zhengxing's somewhat weak voice coming from inside the interrogation room: \"Qin Yuanzheng, you can't be this ruthless! You are going to be a father too; you should understand my painstaking efforts! As long as you let my Weidong go, I'd even accept having our whole family sent to a labor camp...\"","Qin Yuanzheng acted as if he hadn't heard a thing.","Other matters might be negotiable, but there was absolutely no leniency for smuggling opium. No one could save Liu Weidong.","Liu Zhengxing remained in the interrogation room. At this moment, he had no physical wounds on his body, but he was sweating profusely, completely drenched.","He shouted weakly, \"Qin Yuanzheng, you will get your retribution. Tomorrow, the central investigator will arrive in Longcheng. Just you wait and see...\"","He had already sent out the report letter. Qin Yuanzheng had a clean family background with no stains.","So he reported that Qin Yuanzheng was shielding and collaborating with his spy of a wife to steal classified information from various departments and the military.","He claimed that the previous bombings on the streets were also secretly orchestrated by this young woman from the south.","Liu Zhengxing had already set up his backup plan. As long as this move worked, he still had a chance.","No one else knew about these things; he was the only one who knew.","He had handled this matter personally. Tomorrow, as soon as the investigator arrived at the state-run restaurant, there would be a loud bang.","When that time came, how many people died would simply depend on how tough their luck was."]},{"number":151,"title":"Chapter 151: The Investigator Arrives","paragraphs":["On the way home with Qin Yuanzheng, Qiao Lanshu was still very curious, so she asked him, \"Brother Zheng, how exactly did you interrogate Liu Zhengxing just now? Why did he confess so quickly?\"","This was completely out of character for Liu Zhengxing.","Liu Zhengxing was a sly old fox. He was so cunning that even Li Jianlin and Guan Wenjun couldn't do anything about him.","So how come the moment Qin Yuanzheng went over, he confessed?","Could it be that Qin Yuanzheng used some special method to make him talk?","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice and asked, \"Brother Zheng, did you hit him?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was driving slowly while listening to Qiao Lanshu.","Hearing this, he immediately turned to look at her and said with a straight face, \"How could I? I never hit people.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"That's true, Brother Zheng, you are the most reasonable.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded without changing his expression. \"Of course. We soldiers don't hit people.\"","Qiao Lanshu deeply agreed, but then she immediately asked, \"Then Brother Zheng, how did you interrogate him? Tell me, please, I really want to know.\"","How could Qin Yuanzheng resist his little wife acting spoiled?","His heart softened, and he wanted to tell her right then and there.","But he immediately held back. What if something like this frightened Comrade Xiao Qiao?","Qin Yuanzheng smiled, glanced at Qiao Lanshu, and asked, \"You want to know?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, looking at him with round, bright eyes that made his heart melt.","He freed one hand to hold hers, and then said, \"Then, Comrade Qiao Lanshu, are we going to eat 'radish' when we get back?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu's face instantly turned red. She glared at him and said, \"Everything was perfectly fine, why are you bringing this up again?\"","She felt a bit embarrassed, but she also knew that Qin Yuanzheng had indeed been wronged recently.","He was already a man with a very vigorous appetite in that regard. He had finally married his little wife, but not long into their married life, she accidentally got pregnant.","Then came abstinence, and it had been twenty days already.","He was probably feeling extremely frustrated right now.","Qin Yuanzheng did it on purpose; he actually didn't really want to say how he interrogated Liu Zhengxing.","So he deliberately brought up the \"radish,\" thinking his little wife would get shy and the matter would just be dropped.","As a result, Qiao Lanshu blushed and whispered, \"Then... let's take a bath first when we get back.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng gulped, his grip on the steering wheel tightening.","Was there actually such a good thing waiting for him tonight?","Then, should he tell her or not?","...","After the couple returned home, it was already quite late.","Qin Yuanzheng said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Wifey, let's skip it today. It's late, and you need to rest early.\"","He cared deeply for his wife. She was still young and really needed her sleep.","Not to mention she was pregnant.","Qin Yuanzheng heated some water, and the couple took a simple wash.","Then Qin Yuanzheng carried Qiao Lanshu to bed to sleep.","Qiao Lanshu leaned on his shoulder. In the dim candlelight, she looked at his sharp, well-defined jawline.","She asked softly, \"Brother Zheng, aren't we going to eat the rad...\"","Qin Yuanzheng's large hand immediately covered her small mouth. He was already relying purely on willpower to endure, and he couldn't let his little wife tease him anymore.","He whispered, \"Another day. It's late today, go to sleep quickly.\"","Qiao Lanshu picked up the watch by the bedside to take a look. It was already ten o'clock at night; it really was late.","She put the watch down, hugged Qin Yuanzheng, and whined, \"But I still don't know how you interrogated Liu Zhengxing. Tell me quickly, or I won't be able to sleep.\"","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent for a moment, and Qiao Lanshu started shaking his arm again. \"Hubby, tell me quickly.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng held down her mischievous hand and whispered, \"Stop messing around.\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't listen, and her hand moved further down...","Qiao Lanshu: \"No, let's still eat a rad*sh.\"","Qin Yuanzheng's manhood was grasped by her, and sweat broke out on his forehead. He quickly said, \"My little ancestor, lie down properly first. I didn't say I wouldn't tell you.\"","Qiao Lanshu knew exactly how to handle him.","Now satisfied, she lay flat, obediently placed her mischievous hands on her small belly, and then said, \"Brother Zheng, I'm lying down properly. Tell me now.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng took a good while to calm himself down, but his arousal wouldn't subside.","He was really going to be tortured to death by Qiao Lanshu.","He got up to drink a glass of cold water before coming back to lie down. He said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Actually, Liu Zhengxing wasn't that hard to interrogate. As long as he's afraid of death, he has a weakness. Not to mention, he still wants to save his son.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"Did you threaten him with Liu Weidong?\"","Qin Yuanzheng said coldly, \"Liu Weidong is already as good as dead. How can a dead man be used as a threat?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng turned on his side and whispered to Qiao Lanshu, \"Actually, a hemp rope is all it takes.\"","Qiao Lanshu asked in confusion, \"A hemp rope?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"A hemp rope. You start wrapping it tightly from the person's feet, leaving no gaps. When it's wrapped tightly enough, the blood in the body stops flowing, and the skin turns red and purple instantly. As it's wrapped higher and higher, the bound person becomes increasingly terrified, even to the point of a breakdown.\"","This method doesn't leave wounds and won't kill anyone, but it's very effective for extracting information.","Because the target's mind will break down first.","Qin Yuanzheng had used this method to interrogate spies in the past.","Hearing no response from Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng looked down at her. He reached out, pinched her chin to lift her face, and asked softly, \"Are you scared? See, I told you it was best if you didn't know. You're timid, and I was afraid of scaring you.\"","Qiao Lanshu wasn't exactly scared, but it was indeed her first time hearing of such a method.","It sounded quite torturous.","Qiao Lanshu suddenly thought of their intimate married life, when Qin Yuanzheng had also used a rope on her once.","She immediately said, \"You are not allowed to bring ropes into the house anymore. I don't want to see them.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng sighed silently in his heart.","See? He knew he shouldn't have told his little wife about this.","Sigh.","...","When the couple woke up the next day, Qiao Lanshu went to work, and Qin Yuanzheng returned to the mining area military base.","Liu Zhengxing was jointly supervised by the Public Security Bureau and the Revolutionary Committee. Currently, Guan Wenjun was leading people on a citywide hunt for the thugs hired by Liu Zhengxing.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't plan to involve himself in this matter anymore.","Because the investigator sent down from higher-ups had arrived at the train station today, and someone from the military needed to pick him up.","Qin Yuanzheng's 21st Regiment was stationed right in the city, making no one more suitable for the job than him.","Qin Yuanzheng assigned a battalion commander to take a few guards to the train station to pick up the guest.","He himself headed to the mining area to work.","The investigator held a high status and had a rather bad temper. Everyone was on high alert, deeply afraid of offending this big shot.","However, no matter what, they were bound to be scolded.","After all, a bombing incident had recently occurred in the city. The investigator's visit this time would definitely focus on questioning them about it.","This was also why Guan Wenjun was so proactive in catching the criminals.","He was afraid of being scolded, so he found a perfectly reasonable excuse to hide outside."]},{"number":152,"title":"Chapter 152: Roasted Sweet Potatoes","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun had run off to hide and enjoy some peace and quiet, but officials like Li Jianlin couldn't escape so easily.","Along with the municipal party secretary and others, a group of officials waited in full readiness at the train station to receive the arrival.","The investigator arriving this time was of no low status. His name was Si Zhemao, a man of thirty-five or thirty-six from the capital. He was quite tall and had a rather bad temper; not only was his voice loud, but his tone was also quite aggressive.","The officials responsible for receiving him were criticized by him the entire way. Everyone felt guilty and didn't dare to argue with him, only nodding along.","Si Zhemao scolded them for a long time. Finally, sitting in the car, he asked Qian Weiming, the municipal party secretary of Longcheng who was sitting next to him, \"It's been so many days since the explosion in the city. Have you found the cause yet?\"","Cold sweat almost dripped from Qian Weiming's forehead. It was precisely because they hadn't found anything that he hadn't dared to breathe a word.","He shook his head and said, \"The incident happened at night, and it's the end of the year. In winter, the night wind is freezing, and the streets were practically empty. When the explosion suddenly occurred, no one saw it at all. We are also quite helpless.\"","It was obvious that the perpetrator wasn't aiming to hurt anyone, but purely to cause trouble intentionally.","Without the slightest clue, and with it snowing at the time, it was truly difficult to investigate anything.","Si Zhemao didn't care about any of that. He just said coldly, \"Are all of you just useless freeloaders? Such a major explosion happened, and you still don't have a single clue! Can you do anything practical besides sitting in your offices drinking tea and reading the newspaper every day? Go back and pass down the notice: there will be a meeting at eight o'clock tomorrow morning, and everyone is to report their work to me!\"","Si Zhemao paused for a moment and added, \"If a similar explosion happens again, you can all pack up and quit!\"","After the car parked at the guesthouse, Qian Weiming had the others get out of the car and hurriedly led them back to the office to work overtime.","Setting everything else aside for now, they first needed to organize the work reports.","Also, they desperately hoped that no more explosions would occur in the next few days, otherwise, their entire group would be out of a job.","After the men from the military unit escorted Si Zhemao to the guesthouse, they also quickly slipped away.","They finally understood why their regiment commander and chief of staff had refused to come.","It turned out they would just get scolded.","The military unit left four guards for Si Zhemao, and Si Zhemao kept Qian Weiming and another leader from the commercial bureau to accompany him.","During this time, Si Zhemao also asked about the Revolutionary Committee: \"Where is Guan Wenjun? Why didn't he come to see me?\"","The provincial Revolutionary Committee was directly located in the urban area of Longcheng, so there was no municipal Revolutionary Committee here, only the county-level ones below it.","After all, manpower was an important resource. Manual labor was needed right now, so not everyone could join the Revolutionary Committee.","As it was, the Revolutionary Committee already had more personnel than other departments.","Si Zhemao was very dissatisfied with Guan Wenjun.","Because Guan Wenjun was too high-profile and dressed flashily all day long.","Si Zhemao had come this time to see if Guan Wenjun had actually accomplished any real work.","Qian Weiming quickly said, \"A case recently emerged in the city regarding opium. Director Guan is currently investigating it.\"","Saying this, Qian Weiming hurriedly explained the matter, thinking it would perfectly divert Si Zhemao's attention so he wouldn't keep scolding him alone.","After hearing this, Si Zhemao sneered and said, \"These scums have infiltrated our cadre ranks. It seems I will have to investigate thoroughly this time.\"","Qian Weiming: \"...\"","Oh no, things seemed to have gotten even more serious.","Si Zhemao was going to start doubting every single one of them.","When their discussions lasted until noon, Qian Weiming said, \"Comrade Si, it's getting late. Why don't we go to the state-run restaurant for a meal first, and talk about work after eating?\"","After all, there was a meeting in the afternoon, and they couldn't afford to delay.","Si Zhemao nodded and followed Qian Weiming's group to the state-run restaurant to eat.","...","Right at this time, it was the last day of work at the food factory, and the holiday started at noon.","Qiao Lanshu told Qin Yuanzheng that she was going to buy New Year's goods with Wang Xue at noon, and then have Wang Xue walk her to the main gate of the military compound.","Qin Yuanzheng agreed, as he was indeed too busy to get away today.","Qiao Lanshu was cautious this time. She didn't even dare to carry a basket, keeping her hands in her pockets and occasionally casting vigilant glances at the people around her.","Now that it was the year-end holiday, the streets had become lively.","The nearby department stores and supply and marketing cooperatives were packed with people lining up to rush-purchase goods.","In this era, people were very simple and kind. If they found money, they would hand it in; if they saw an unattended child, they would help look after them.","People didn't have much vigilance either.","Wang Xue carried a basket as usual today. She said to Qiao Lanshu, \"I want to see if anyone dares to throw things into my basket today. If I catch them, I'll skin them alive.\"","Although Wang Xue said this, she was actually still a bit nervous inside.","So today she had called four or five sisters from the food factory, and the six or seven of them went shopping for New Year's goods together.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Everyone is busy going home for the New Year now. Probably no one would want to do such a thing anymore.\"","Previously, Liu Zhengxing had bribed a few street hooligans, but those people were now either caught or locked up by Guan Wenjun. There was still one who hadn't been caught, but he probably wouldn't be able to hide for much longer.","Thus, the six or seven women began chattering about Liu Zhengxing, and then moved on to talk about Liu Weihong.","When women got together, they always had endless things to talk about.","Qiao Lanshu was the youngest and had thin skin, so she couldn't join in on many topics. She just stood quietly by the side and listened to them talk.","When they walked near the state-run restaurant, Qiao Lanshu smelled the aroma of roasted sweet potatoes.","Her heart stirred as she thought about it—hadn't Liu Zhengxing come to buy roasted sweet potatoes last night?","Just how delicious could these roasted sweet potatoes be, to make Section Chief Liu crave them in the middle of the night at a time like this?","Anyway, they smelled incredibly fragrant.","Qiao Lanshu patted her stomach and said to her sisters, \"Are there roasted sweet potatoes over there? I want to go over and buy a couple of pounds. They smell really good.\"","One of the female workers immediately said, \"Oh my, Xiao Qiao, you really have a good eye. This is the only roasted sweet potato stand in our city, but the taste is absolutely phenomenal—so sweet and delicious! The price isn't expensive either, just five cents a pound, so you can get two pounds for a dime, enough for the whole family to share a bit. Oh, right, we just got our ration tickets. I'll go buy some for my kids too.\"","They had just finished the year-end general meeting, appraised the model workers, and distributed bonuses. Everyone was happy to spend some money to buy tasty treats for their children.","This roasted sweet potato stall belonged to the state, so you didn't need ration tickets to buy just a pound or two.","Tickets were only collected if you bought a lot, which was why so many people came here to buy them.","However, it was still early, so there weren't too many people around yet.","Among the women, everyone except Qiao Lanshu had children at home. Since they were already there, they decided to all take a few pounds with them; after all, the price wasn't expensive.","Qiao Lanshu followed them to the entrance of the alley. The roasted sweet potato stall was located right in the alley on the side of the state-run restaurant.","From her vantage point, she could also see the main entrance of the state-run restaurant not far away, where two cars were just pulling up and coming to a halt by the side door."]},{"number":153,"title":"Chapter 153: The Little Hooligan at the Sweet Potato Stall","paragraphs":["The car Qiao Lanshu saw happened to belong to Si Zhemao and his group.","They had come over to eat. Since it was hard to park in the open space by the entrance, the guards had to park the car on the side of the state-run restaurant.","Qiao Lanshu had a rough guess about their backgrounds, so she took a few extra glances out of curiosity.","She even wondered if her Brother Zheng might be in that car. Since an investigator had come down from above, it was highly likely that military personnel would be assigned to escort them.","Qin Yuanzheng's 21st Regiment was located right in the city, unlike other units stationed in the suburbs, so it was entirely possible that he was accompanying them.","However, to Qiao Lanshu's disappointment, when the car doors opened, only two guards stepped out, along with a tall, bearded man who looked like a high-ranking cadre.","Was this man the investigator?","As soon as Si Zhemao got out of the car, he looked sharply in Qiao Lanshu's direction.","Qiao Lanshu quickly withdrew her gaze and went to buy roasted sweet potatoes with Wang Xue and the others.","Si Zhemao had just sensed someone watching him. He glanced over, but only saw a group of female workers buying roasted sweet potatoes.","He took a sniff. Truth be told, the roasted sweet potatoes smelled quite good.","It made him even hungrier.","Si Zhemao turned and led his people into the state-run restaurant.","Wang Xue whispered to Qiao Lanshu, Having guards escort him just to come out for a meal, it seems this person has a pretty high status. He is probably some high-ranking cadre.","Qiao Lanshu also replied in a low voice, I am guessing it is the investigator sent from above.","Previously, it was said that an inspection team was coming down to do routine year-end inspections, which would have been relatively straightforward.","But later, because a street here in Longcheng suddenly exploded, the higher-ups suspected that enemy spies were lurking about, so they sent an investigator instead.","The female workers buying sweet potatoes had all seen Si Zhemao.","They were all quite curious about him.","After all, they rarely saw officials in their daily lives, so spotting one now sparked their gossipy nature.","Someone said, This investigator looks like quite the big shot. I wonder how people like him usually catch enemy spies?","Another said nervously, Oh my, do not scare me. Our Longcheng is just a tiny place, are there really enemy spies here? If there are, it will not lead to another war, will it?","The older ones among them had all lived through the war years.","War was too bitter; no one wanted to experience it again.","Peace was hard-won and they all cherished it. Just hearing about enemy spies filled them with absolute disgust.","Someone gritted her teeth and said, I had better not find out who this enemy spy is, or I will smash his head in.","All of them had ordered roasted sweet potatoes, but since there was only one person running the stall, they had to wait and could not leave right away.","As Qiao Lanshu listened to their chatter, she suddenly noticed a young man in the corner, suspiciously sizing her up.","It was broad daylight, there was a big leader and guards at the state-run restaurant, and she was surrounded by five or six female comrades, so Qiao Lanshu was not afraid of him.","With a scarf wrapping half of her face and a cotton hat on her head, Qiao Lanshu glared back at the hooligan with her bright dark eyes.","Glared at by Qiao Lanshu, the hooligan subconsciously shrank his neck and retreated further into the corner of the alley.","The hooligan looked quite young, probably only in his teens. Under normal circumstances, a boy his age should still be in school.","Otherwise, a young man like him should have been sent down to the countryside.","The teenage hooligan was young and thin as a beanpole. He was covered in dirt, wearing no hat or gloves, and looked so grimy that he resembled a beggar.","Qiao Lanshu immediately became vigilant.","What did this person want? He better not be trying to steal something.","Things were strictly controlled these days. If he dared to steal, not only would he be beaten half to death, but he would also be sent to a labor camp for life, perhaps never to return.","The hooligan seemed a bit afraid of her, constantly trying to hide in the alley.","However, after a while, he suddenly walked out of the corner again.","He approached the female workers, swallowed hard at the aroma of the roasted sweet potatoes, and then circled around them.","There were many people coming and going on this street, and many buying sweet potatoes, so at first, no one paid attention to him.","Only Qiao Lanshu kept her eyes on him.","He seemed to struggle with himself for a long time. Finally, he walked up to Qiao Lanshu. Not daring to meet her eyes, he stared at the ground and said, You... you are a military dependent, right?","Qiao Lanshu glanced at him but ignored him.","The young hooligan spun around in place a couple of times and added, That day at the supply and marketing cooperative, the thing in your basket...","He said this, glanced at Qiao Lanshu, and finished, ...I put it there.","Qiao Lanshu: ???","Qiao Lanshu immediately looked around for a stick or a rock, wanting to beat this guy up first before saying anything else.","Wang Xue had been standing close to Qiao Lanshu, but the hooligan's voice was so low she did not catch what he said.","However, she noticed that a hooligan was harassing Qiao Lanshu.","She immediately stopped her chatting, turned to glare at the hooligan, and scolded, You little scoundrel, harassing a decent woman in broad daylight! Do you want to be sent to a labor camp? Huh?","The boy clearly panicked. He quickly backed up several steps and said in a fluster, I-I do not want to go to a labor camp.","They had only helped Liu Zhengxing do that deed for money.","In fact, before slipping the item into the basket, they had no idea what it even was.","They just knew they would get paid.","As a result, the next day they were chased all over the city by people from the Revolutionary Committee.","Now his brothers had all been caught, and he was the only one still hiding.","He did not want to be sent to a labor camp. His family was poor, and his grandfather was old and could not survive without someone looking after him.","He had been saving up money, trying to use connections to buy a job so he could stay in the city.","Now look what happened. He had not saved enough money, had no prospects for a job, and was about to be locked up.","Wang Xue had a loud voice. With her hands on her hips, she glared at the young hooligan and scolded, You do not want to? If you do not, then why are you circling around us female comrades? Why are you hitting on this young girl? Who do you think you are? Take a walk and stop being an eyesore here.","The young hooligan: ...","The young hooligan had finally gathered the courage to say something to Qiao Lanshu.","But he ended up getting a fierce tongue-lashing from Wang Xue.","He shrank his neck and retreated like a turtle pulling into its shell.","Qiao Lanshu felt that this boy had something he wanted to say.","Or at least, he had a favor to ask of her.","Otherwise, why would he approach her? He had been hiding for so many days, and while everyone else had been caught by Guan Wenjun, he was the only one who had not.","He could have just kept hiding. Why come to her to confess?","Qiao Lanshu thought of the smell of roasted sweet potatoes on Liu Zhengxing earlier. Could Liu Zhengxing have come looking for this hooligan?","Qiao Lanshu's heart stirred. She said to Wang Xue, Sister, I am going to ask him a question. Wait for me here.","Hearing this, Wang Xue immediately voiced her disapproval. Do not do it, Xiao Qiao. You have a simple mind, but do not assume everyone else is simple too. None of these street thugs are any good. You had better stay away from him.","Qiao Lanshu said softly, It is fine. I will just stand far away, ask him one thing, and be right back.","Wang Xue was still unwilling.","She now treated Qiao Lanshu like her own younger sister. Feeling that she was young, she couldn't help but want to look after her.","Besides, Qiao Lanshu was a military officer's family member and was pregnant. If anything happened to her, Wang Xue wouldn't be able to withstand Qin Yuanzheng's wrath.","Wang Xue hesitated for a few seconds, then said, Alright, I'll go with you.","With that, Wang Xue linked her arm through Qiao Lanshu's, greeted the female comrades in front of the roasted sweet potato stall, and the two walked toward the hooligan.","The hooligan had just been scolded by Wang Xue, and the courage he had finally mustered was about to dissipate.","He had originally planned to leave.","But after walking a few meters away, his footsteps slowed down again.","Because he knew that even if he left now, he had nowhere to go.","There were so many people from the Revolutionary Committee, and they were looking to catch him everywhere.","Where else could he run?","He hadn't dared to go home for several days.","He didn't know how the old man at home was doing.","The people from the Revolutionary Committee must have already found his home, and he didn't know if they had made things difficult for his old man.","Also, if his old man knew he had committed a crime, would he be angered to death?","Thinking about this, the hooligan suddenly felt like crying.","He just wanted to earn some money to buy a job so he could stay in the city. How did he suddenly commit a crime?","Just then, someone called out from behind him, Hey, wait a minute.","The hooligan turned his head and saw Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu walking toward him again.","The hooligan was a little afraid of Wang Xue. She was too fierce; when she scolded people, her imposing manner was quite scary.","Wang Xue looked him up and down and suddenly said, Why are you crying? Did I scold you to tears? Are you that fragile?","The hooligan was speechless.","Embarrassed and indignant, the hooligan turned his head away.","Wang Xue was speechless.","Well, he really was scolded to tears by her.","It seemed these hooligans weren't completely heartless ghosts. They still knew how to feel ashamed after a few words, which meant they were still somewhat salvageable.","Qiao Lanshu walked up to the hooligan and said to him, What did you want to say when you were looking for me just now?","The hooligan looked at Qiao Lanshu and said hesitantly, I do have something to tell you.","But he glanced at Wang Xue and added, However, I will only tell you. No one else can know.","Wang Xue pointed at him. Speak if you want, forget it if you don't. Do you really think you're that important?","The hooligan was speechless.","Seeing that Wang Xue was about to drag Qiao Lanshu away.","The hooligan felt as if he could hear the voices of the people from the Revolutionary Committee again. Terrified, he quickly chased after them and said, I'll tell you, I'll tell you, okay?","He looked left and right sneakily, then backed into a corner, using the base of the wall to hide himself.","Wang Xue whispered to Qiao Lanshu, Xiao Qiao, this guy doesn't look quite right. Could he be one of the criminals the public security comrades are catching recently?","Qiao Lanshu nodded. Indeed.","Indeed he was. He probably couldn't hide anymore and was afraid of dying.","So he came to negotiate terms with her.","Why come to her of all people? Perhaps he felt that since her family member was a military officer, they had more power?","The hooligan whispered, I... I want to atone for my crimes by doing a good deed. Putting that thing in your basket before was my fault, I...","Hearing this, Wang Xue was about to flare up, but fortunately, Qiao Lanshu held her back.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, Let's hear what he has to say first.","The hooligan said nervously, I didn't know that thing was opium either. I only found out yesterday.","After all, his brothers had all been arrested, leaving only him.","The wanted posters were out, and the whole street was talking about the Revolutionary Committee arresting people.","Wang Xue sneered. Just because you didn't know, you can casually put things into a girl's basket?","The hooligan didn't know how to explain it.","After all, this matter was indeed their fault.","He said again, I know now. I heard that smuggling opium gets you shot. I... I don't want to die.","If he died, what would happen to the old man?","He felt he could still be saved.","He said to Qiao Lanshu, I can atone for my crimes. I'll tell you some news, and you see if you can let me off.","The hooligan knew the fearsome reputation of the Revolutionary Committee. He was afraid that once arrested, he would be beaten to death.","That was why he came to find Qiao Lanshu.","But in reality, Qiao Lanshu couldn't make decisions for him. If he wanted to atone for his crimes, he should go to the public security officers.","Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue exchanged a glance, both tacitly choosing not to point this out.","Qiao Lanshu said, Tell me, what is the news? I can consider it.","The hooligan couldn't help but look around again. Finding no one nearby, he walked up to Qiao Lanshu and whispered, That Liu Zhengxing, before he was arrested, buried all his belongings nearby. I caught a glimpse from afar, there were a lot of gold bars.","Qiao Lanshu: ???","Wang Xue: !!!","Wang Xue's mouth fell open. She muttered in a low voice, Oh my goodness, did he bury a treasure chest here to prevent the Revolutionary Committee from confiscating his property?","Wang Xue was a bit excited, though she didn't know what she was excited about. After all, even if there was a treasure chest, it had nothing to do with her. She just sighed and said:","They all say that Section Chief Liu is quite scheming, and now it seems he really thinks ahead. Afraid that his wife and children wouldn't have jobs or a way to live after he was caught, he hid the money for them.","Qiao Lanshu was also a little surprised. To save his son, Liu Zhengxing had come up with a foolish plan to find these hooligans and slander the family members of several cadres.","As a result, when the plan failed and he found himself exposed, he packed up his valuables so quickly and even buried them?","Qiao Lanshu was somewhat doubtful. A cautious person like him, how could he happen to be seen by you?","Qiao Lanshu stared at the hooligan in front of her. You're not lying to me, are you?","The hooligan became anxious. I'm really not, I'm telling the truth. After I saw him that night, I saw him burying two boxes nearby. One of the boxes was filled with gold bars. If you don't believe me, I'll dig it up for you to see right now, but you have to promise me that as long as I dig it up and hand the things over, it counts as me atoning for my crimes, okay?","With that, he walked up to a wall.","This wall belonged to the state-run restaurant. It was very long, about twenty meters or so, taking up half the length of this alley.","On the left side of the alley were some vendors or residential areas, while on the right side was the state-run restaurant.","Separated by a single wall, inside were the private rooms of the state-run restaurant, which was usually the place where leaders were hosted for meals."]},{"number":154,"title":"Chapter 154: Mine Detector","paragraphs":["The street punk recognized Liu Zhengxing that night.","Liu Zhengxing had hired them to do a job and gave each person ten yuan, which was extremely generous.","Having been poor for so many years, the punk had never seen such a generous person. So, subconsciously, he followed Liu Zhengxing for a distance and then saw him digging a hole here to bury something.","It was late at night, the cold wind was howling, the roasted sweet potato stalls had closed, and there were no pedestrians around.","Liu Zhengxing squatted on the ground and specifically opened the box to count the gold bars inside.","He had brought two boxes at the time, but only opened one to count.","Even in the pitch-black winter night, the punk was still blinded by the gold inside.","He absolutely did not see it wrong!","At that time, the punk thought to himself that he would find a chance to steal this stuff.","But Liu Zhengxing stayed guard until very late, and was suddenly arrested by the people from the Revolutionary Committee.","The punk was frightened and hid as well.","But he couldn't resist the itch in his heart, always thinking about that box of gold bars, so he came over again today.","He just couldn't help wanting to dig it up.","The punk paced back and forth at the base of the wall, searching for a while, but he wasn't sure of the exact location either.","Wang Xue nervously whispered to Qiao Lanshu, \"Xiao Qiao, do you think what he said is true?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head, \"Sister, why don't we call the police?\"","Wang Xue nodded hurriedly, \"Right, right, right, let's call the police first.\"","Saying that, she pointed at the punk and asked, \"Then what about him?\"","Qiao Lanshu was silent for a moment, then said, \"How about we tie him up right now, in case he runs away. If nothing is dug up later, they might blame us for making a false report.\"","Of course, if something was really dug up, whether it counted as making amends for his crimes would be the police bureau's business.","So, while the punk was still looking for things at the base of the wall, he suddenly found himself surrounded by several female comrades from the food factory.","Four or five female comrades surrounded him, punching and kicking him, directly beating him senseless.","He stared at Qiao Lanshu in shock, his eyes full of disbelief.","Hadn't they agreed on making amends for his crimes? Why did they start beating him again...","Qiao Lanshu coughed and looked away, feeling a bit guilty.","Wang Xue pinned the punk to the ground, then took a handkerchief and gagged his mouth, saying fiercely, \"If you committed a crime, go to a labor camp! Making amends? In your dreams!\"","The several female comrades scolded him there, telling him to undergo labor reform properly in the future and strive for a chance to turn over a new leaf.","Their constant chattering scolded the punk until he shut down completely.","Soon, the police comrades who received the report also rushed over.","Li Jianlin and Guan Wenjuan both came.","Because Guan Wenjuan had been trying to catch this last punk.","In the end, he couldn't find the person, but Qiao Lanshu found him.","He circled the punk, kicked him twice in a row, and said angrily, \"You bastard, you're pretty good at hiding! Speak, where have you been hiding these past two days?\"","The punk's legs were tied, his mouth was gagged, and he lay on the ground like a dead fish.","No matter how much Guan Wenjuan kicked him, he didn't make a sound.","Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue had already relayed what the punk had said.","Li Jianlin stood next to Guan Wenjuan and asked, \"Director Guan, do you think what he said is credible?\"","Guan Wenjuan immediately said, \"I don't know if it's credible, but if Liu Zhengxing really has that much wealth, his identity is far from simple.\"","The cadres in this era were all poorer than the next, how could they possibly have these things.","Even if they did, they would have handed them over to the state long ago. How could they keep them in their own homes, and a whole box of them at that?","Right now, there are only two possibilities. Either this punk is lying.","Or Liu Zhengxing is corrupt.","Guan Wenjuan led Li Jianlin and said, \"He said he isn't sure of the location, let's have people start searching from here.\"","Li Jianlin said, \"This area isn't small, and it's the foundation of the state-run restaurant. Who knows if digging up the ground will affect their walls. How about we ask Regiment Commander Qin for help? Aren't the people in their unit really good at finding things? It would save us from having to search place by place.\"","Coincidentally, Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu were still waiting here as the informants.","With her here, Li Jianlin felt that Qin Yuanzheng would come over even if he was busy.","Hearing this, Guan Wenjuan wanted to refuse:","\"What Qin Yuanzheng can do, I, Guan Wenjuan, can do too! Deputy Director Li, it's not that I want to criticize you, but this case is our business. If it's done well, the credit goes to us two. Why are you always thinking about Qin Yuanzheng? If he does it well, the credit is his. If he messes it up, doesn't the responsibility fall on us?\"","Li Jianlin: \"...\"","Although Guan Wenjuan's words made a lot of sense.","But Li Jianlin still said, \"But relying just on the two of us, we can't really dig up this entire area, right?\"","Guan Wenjuan started rolling up his sleeves, \"You wait, I'll go look.\"","Guan Wenjuan searched while having people dig, but after digging in three or four places in a row, none were right.","Hearing the commotion, the people from the state-run restaurant hurriedly ran out, found Li Jianlin, and said, \"Police comrades, what are you doing? Why are you digging up the ground of our restaurant?\"","Li Jianlin couldn't say it explicitly, only explaining, \"Comrade, we are doing this out of the necessity of the case. We can't disclose it right now, I hope you can understand.\"","The staff of the state-run restaurant said somewhat awkwardly:","\"Police comrades, it's really not that I don't understand you, but today is a special day. The investigator from above is currently sitting and eating in the innermost private room of the restaurant.","You guys digging around here, they can hear it clearly in the private room. I was afraid the investigator would get angry, so I hurried out to see what was going on... How about you wait another half an hour, wait for the investigator to leave, and then dig, is that okay?\"","Li Jianlin: \"...\"","Guan Wenjuan: \"...\"","The two looked at each other, both somewhat speechless.","Because both of them had forgotten about the investigator.","Originally, both of them were avoiding the investigator, just afraid of getting scolded.","But now, the investigator was eating in the state-run restaurant, and neither of them had gone in to say hello.","Guan Wenjuan quickly stopped the digging action.","He whispered to Li Jianlin, \"Deputy Director Li, then how about we dig a bit later?\"","Li Jianlin also wiped the sweat from his forehead and nodded, \"I think that works.\"","The two tacitly turned around and walked away, still not going to the state-run restaurant.","Qiao Lanshu and Wang Xue were sitting on a stone pier not far away, eating sunflower seeds while watching their digging work get paused.","Qiao Lanshu asked Guan Wenjuan, \"Director Guan, why did you stop digging?\"","Guan Wenjuan cared about his face, so of course he couldn't say that he wanted to pause the digging because he was afraid of the investigator.","He especially couldn't say that he didn't want Qin Yuanzheng to take the credit, so he refused to go to the military unit to borrow professional talents.","Otherwise, once the professionals arrived at the scene with their professional equipment, they could probably find the stuff in less than ten minutes.","He wiped the dirt off his hands, walked over to Qiao Lanshu, leaned against the wall, crossed his arms, and said with a deep expression, \"According to my professional investigation, there is nothing in this area.\"","He pointed to the place they had just dug.","Wang Xue did not dare to make a sound, but Qiao Lanshu spoke the truth, You have already dug around, so there is definitely nothing there.","What professional investigation? Does a professional investigation just rely on digging up the ground to search?","Guan Wenjun, ...","Guan Wenjun added, We are pausing the digging right now because I feel that Liu Zhengxing's motive for burying something here is not right.","Li Jianlin looked at Guan Wenjun in confusion, Director Guan, how is the motive not right?","Guan Wenjun coughed, making up an excuse on the fly, Look, if Liu Zhengxing really wanted to hide something, there is no need to hide it at the base of the state-run restaurant's wall. Inside are all top leaders. If he really buried something here, it is definitely not money. It would be easily discovered and secretly dug away.","Qiao Lanshu nodded, thinking Guan Wenjun's analysis made sense. Director Guan is right. Then what would he bury?","She pondered, He could not have buried explosives, right? If explosives are buried, can they still detonate?","Guan Wenjun, ...","Li Jianlin, ...","The two suddenly looked at each other, both seeing horror in the other's eyes.","Qiao Lanshu was still eating melon seeds on the side, asking curiously, I remember last time, was it West Street or somewhere, did an explosion not happen one night?","It was because of that explosion that the investigators came over.","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice, How did that explosive detonate? Was it lit by a fuse? Or how was it done? Could Liu Zhengxing be a suspect...","Before Qiao Lanshu could finish, Guan Wenjun had already bolted.","Li Jianlin remained where he was with a serious expression, quickly running to the base of the wall. He shouted to the Revolutionary Committee personnel holding hoes and pickaxes, Stop, everyone stop!","His expression was grave, his face a bit pale. Pointing at everyone, he said, Now, everyone, step back. Step back slowly, slowly, do not rush.","Qiao Lanshu, ...","Wang Xue and Qiao Lanshu exchanged a glance, lowering their voices. Xiao Qiao, could it be that what is buried here is really explosives?","Qiao Lanshu swallowed hard, saying nervously, I do not know, I was just saying that casually...","Without another word, Wang Xue grabbed Qiao Lanshu's arm and dragged her toward the intersection. Let us go, let us go, we need to leave right now.","Who cares if it is gold or silver buried there, it had nothing to do with them.","Life was the most important thing; running away was the priority.","Thinking about how they actually believed two boxes of gold were buried underneath just moments ago, and how they had happily talked about seeing the boxes dug up.","After all, neither of them had ever seen gold bars.","Now look at this.","What gold bars? That thing was very likely a bomb.","The two ran all the way to the direct opposite side of the state-run restaurant, leaving Qiao Lanshu panting heavily.","The more she thought about it, the more terrified she felt. No way? Really...","She had merely followed Guan Wenjun's words and made a casual remark.","Because Guan Wenjun said this place was not suitable for burying gold and valuables, it was definitely suitable for burying explosives.","After all, if it blew up, the victims would not just be passersby, but also the cadres eating inside the state-run restaurant.","Separated by a wall, if they were lucky, the cadres would not die.","Then they would arrest people, hold them accountable, and replace a batch of leading cadres in Longcheng.","If they were unlucky and the cadres were blown up, it would be even worse.","The entirety of Longcheng would become a major focus, and by then, even the provincial cadres might have to be replaced.","How insidious.","Wang Xue broke into a cold sweat thinking about how she had sat all morning in a place where a bomb might be buried.","Her arms were trembling a little now. Xiao Qiao, thank goodness you are smart. Director Guan dug for a long time without finding anything; we are lucky to be alive.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, Sister, it could also really be gold and valuables. It might not necessarily be explosives. I was just talking casually.","Although now, the more she thought about it, the more likely it seemed.","Wang Xue swallowed hard, saying nervously, Hard to say. I saw Director Guan got scared off, and Deputy Director Li's face changed completely. They definitely have more experience than us.","Guan Wenjun was not exactly scared off.","He sprinted to drive his car, heading straight for the mining area troops.","In less than twenty minutes, he was back.","Followed by Qin Yuanzheng's car.","Qin Yuanzheng got out of the car, bringing a company-level military officer behind him.","This company commander was carrying a Type 69 electromagnetic induction mine detector on his back.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu across from the state-run restaurant, Qin Yuanzheng merely nodded at her from a distance, then hurriedly led his subordinate into the alley behind the restaurant.","When Qiao Lanshu saw Qin Yuanzheng arrive, she stood up abruptly. Frowning with a worried face, she said, Why is Brother Zheng here?","Could it really be a bomb buried there?","Then would Qin Yuanzheng not be injured by the explosion?","The incident from her past life where Qin Yuanzheng was injured by an explosion during a mission had not happened yet.","Qiao Lanshu never knew which mission caused the injury, so she had been on edge ever since she married him.","Now seeing him here, she began to worry again.","Could it be this time?","But this time, Qin Yuanzheng already suspected Liu Zhengxing had buried explosives and even brought a mine detector. Did that mean he would not get hurt?","But what if?","Qiao Lanshu paced in circles anxiously, wanting to go over and look, but afraid of distracting Qin Yuanzheng and making it more dangerous for him.","Wang Xue comforted her, Oh, Xiao Qiao, do not worry. Your Regiment Commander Qin is a professional, he should be very good at this. Do not scare yourself.","Qiao Lanshu nodded, saying worriedly, I know...","Knowing was one thing, but she still felt nervous in her heart.","By the time Qin Yuanzheng brought his men over, Li Jianlin had already cleared the area, having people set up ropes at the intersection to keep ordinary citizens out.","At the same time, he did not let anyone near the dug-up spots at the scene, fearing an accident.","The little thug was still tied up lying on the ground, unable to understand why these people suddenly stopped digging.","Wiping the cold sweat from his forehead, Li Jianlin ran up to Qin Yuanzheng and Guan Wenjun, telling them, Regiment Commander Qin, Director Guan, I have cordoned off the surroundings, but I have not gone inside the state-run restaurant to tell them yet. Should we go inform them?","He could not make up his mind, mainly because he did not know if this suspected buried explosive incident could be reported to the investigators.","What if the investigators found out and fired them in return?","Before Guan Wenjun could speak, Qin Yuanzheng immediately said, Tell them. Go right now and evacuate everyone from the state-run restaurant, just in case.","Saying that, he turned to his subordinate carrying the mine detector. Begin the scan."]},{"number":155,"title":"Chapter 155: How Many Mines Were Buried After All","paragraphs":["If what was buried here was truly a landmine, then Liu Zhengxing was a purely evil man.","The punk had mentioned that when Liu was burying the gold bars, he had deliberately opened the box to count them.","This made his behavior seem highly calculated.","He might have intentionally opened the box to attract attention.","He knew he was going to be arrested and would have no way to detonate the explosives himself.","So he deliberately lured people to steal his things. Once someone dug up the box, it would ignite the explosives, just like setting off a landmine.","The number of casualties it would cause by then wouldn't be his concern.","Furthermore, he had buried it last night. By the time he was taken away, it was already late at night.","The state-run restaurant had a patrol team, so no one would likely come digging in the middle of the night. However, the patrol team didn't work during the day, and there were pedestrians around. If someone wanted to dig it up, they would probably come looking when no one was patrolling.","If it were found and exploded, the consequences would be catastrophic.","Liu Zhengxing's insidiousness made even Qin Yuanzheng shudder.","If this kind of person hadn't been caught committing a crime out of sheer desperation to save his son...","...he would be truly difficult to deal with.","Qin Yuanzheng, Guan Wenjun, and Li Jianlin stood nearby, watching the subordinates Qin Yuanzheng had brought over use mine detectors to sweep along the base of the state-run restaurant's wall.","The diners and staff inside the state-run restaurant had all been notified. Everyone stopped eating and working, and completely evacuated the building.","Si Zhemao's stomach was rumbling with hunger. He had finally waited for his meal to be served, but after barely taking two bites, he heard some unknown clanking noises outside the window.","He sent someone out to check, but shortly after, the public security comrades came directly to notify everyone to evacuate.","Si Zhemao put down his chopsticks with a dark expression and asked the accompanying Municipal Party Secretary, Qian Weiming, \"What did they just say? Why are they suddenly asking us to leave?\"","Qian Weiming quickly replied, \"I'll go out and ask.\"","While the two of them were eating in the private room, the guards and secretaries were eating out in the main hall.","As for the other accompanying officials, Qian Weiming had already sent them back to the office building to prepare their work reports.","This also saved them from being scolded by the investigator alongside him.","After finding out the situation, Qian Weiming returned, wiping cold sweat from his brow. He said:","\"Investigator, this is bad. The public security comrades said that someone likely buried explosives outside this window. Until safety is confirmed, the entire state-run restaurant and nearby residents must be evacuated. A cordon has been set up around the area to keep people away. How about we change places to eat?\"","Si Zhemao had been sent here specifically to investigate the previous explosion.","Now, hearing about explosives, how could he possibly sit still!","He stood up abruptly, pushing his chair far back with such force that it made a piercing screech.","With a cold and gloomy face, he snapped, \"Eat, eat, eat! Is there anything else in your head besides eating? Explosives have been discovered, and you're still thinking about food?\"","Scolding him, he strode out the door.","Qian Weiming looked utterly crestfallen from the scolding.","Qian Weiming thought to himself, Weren't you the one whining about being hungry just a moment ago, even complaining that the restaurant staff was serving the food too slowly?","Now he was being scolded for only knowing how to eat. Who did he offend to have to serve this demanding boss?","The crux of the matter was that Qian Weiming was already in his forties, while Si Zhemao was still young, only in his thirties.","Being scolded every day by a superior younger than himself made Qian Weiming feel truly awful.","Sighing inwardly, he followed Si Zhemao, and the two hurriedly walked to the main hall.","The guards and two secretaries waiting in the hall quickly stood up and followed them out of the restaurant.","They headed straight toward the detection site behind the state-run restaurant.","Guan Wenjun caught a glimpse and immediately recognized Qian Weiming.","He quickly whispered in Qin Yuanzheng's ear, \"Lao Qin, the investigator is here. I'll leave this to you. I'm taking off.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and didn't stop him, letting him slip away with his men.","Li Jianlin and three public security officers were at the scene.","Qin Yuanzheng had brought a company commander in charge of mine detection. Six people in total were enough.","Having too many people would actually be more dangerous.","Li Jianlin said with some envy, \"Why did Director Guan leave? Sigh, I really envy him. The investigator probably won't bother his department.\"","In truth, the investigator wouldn't bother the military either.","Because the investigator had no jurisdiction over military affairs.","The investigator generally couldn't easily interfere with the Revolutionary Committee either. They were independent systems, operating autonomously and not interfering with each other.","The investigator only had authority over officials like Qian Weiming.","Afraid that Li Jianlin might feel uncomfortable, Qin Yuanzheng explained, \"This investigator, Si Zhemao, has a family feud with the Revolutionary Committee, so it's better not to let them meet.\"","Li Jianlin said in surprise, \"So that's how it is...\"","He really hadn't known about this.","Si Zhemao had risen through the ranks very quickly, which was also related to his family.","During the most turbulent years, his family had been misunderstood, and their home was raided by the Revolutionary Committee.","Even he had been sent to a labor camp.","Si Zhemao absolutely despised the people from the Revolutionary Committee.","He almost never dealt with them, and if he did, it was always the Revolutionary Committee that made concessions. After all, Si Zhemao's methods were quite formidable.","Guan Wenjun had also been very prestigious in previous years; everyone was afraid of him.","However, over the past two years, he felt the situation wasn't quite right. The Revolutionary Committee might be abolished in the future, and the form of the revolution would change.","He had offended too many people. For the past year, he had been pulling strings, trying to transfer his job into the regular civil service system. This was also why he had been acting so timidly lately, not even daring to offend a county personnel section chief.","After Guan Wenjun slipped away.","Si Zhemao came over with Qian Weiming. Recognizing Qin Yuanzheng, he asked, \"Regiment Commander Qin, how is it? Have you found the explosives?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"We are still searching.\"","Si Zhemao asked again, \"Who reported the explosives? Are there witnesses?\"","Li Jianlin quickly replied, \"Yes, yes, over there.\"","Saying this, he pointed to a corner, directing Si Zhemao's attention to the punk lying on the ground.","Si Zhemao only took a glance and didn't go over to question him.","With a dark face, he watched the soldiers using the mine detectors to find the explosives, his expression serious.","Several people stood there, not daring to speak much. A police cordon had been drawn around the area, and public security officers were guarding the entrances and exits of the alley to prevent ordinary people from entering.","About half an hour later, the company commander holding the mine detector suddenly stopped.","The red light on the mine detector flashed on and off. With a serious expression, he said, \"Commander, there's something underneath!\"","Qin Yuanzheng immediately said to Si Zhemao and the others beside him, \"Stay where you are. I'll go take a look.\"","Si Zhemao: \"Alright, alright, go check quickly, and be careful.\"","Qian Weiming was so nervous that cold sweat broke out on his forehead, and his legs instinctively wanted to step back.","But seeing that Si Zhemao and Li Jianlin were standing still, he forced himself to stand his ground, afraid of looking like a coward.","Thinking to himself, these men truly came from the military, just look at their discipline!","As Qin Yuanzheng walked forward, he suddenly felt a telepathic connection and glanced over to the other side.","Sure enough, he saw his wife standing near the police cordon, looking at him with a face full of worry.","Behind Qiao Lanshu, Wang Xue kept urging her to leave, but she refused, saying, \"This is outside the cordon. It's safe. I haven't even gone inside.\"","Wang Xue certainly knew this was a safe area.","But she was just scared.","In this day and age, who wouldn't be afraid of explosives? It was terrifying.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu there, Qin Yuanzheng waved at her, signaling for her to go back first and not just stand around.","Qiao Lanshu waved back at him, but she remained standing far away, refusing to leave.","There were other onlookers around, all curious about what could be dug up from this spot.","Since she was far away, Qin Yuanzheng didn't go over to her.","He walked over to the scene with a solemn expression. The company commander slowly pulled back the detector and whispered, \"Commander, we've detected something here, but we're not sure what it is.\"","He added in a low voice, \"It could also be a rock or a piece of metal.\"","This Type 69 mine detector was prone to false alarms; it would flash its warning lights even if it merely detected certain rocks or metal fragments.","Qin Yuanzheng grabbed a pickaxe and said, \"We'll know once we dig it up.\"","The two of them began to dig the soil gently. Everyone around watched from a distance; no one dared to move closer.","Even Si Zhemao, despite being incredibly anxious, didn't step forward.","For one, he was afraid of stepping on something he shouldn't and causing trouble for the soldiers' work.","Secondly, he worried that going over would distract the soldiers.","He paced around nervously, then glanced in Qiao Lanshu's direction and asked Qian Weiming, \"Who was Regiment Commander Qin looking at just now? Who is that young woman to him?\"","Qian Weiming was panicking inside. He silently took two steps back before saying, \"Oh, her? That's Regiment Commander Qin's wife. They just got married a few months ago, and I heard she's even pregnant.\"","Hearing that she was pregnant, Si Zhemao took another look at Qiao Lanshu and said, \"This girl is quite impressive, making an infertile man a father. She must have been a pomegranate spirit in her past life.\"","Qian Weiming: \"...\"","This joke was way too dry; he really couldn't bring himself to laugh right now.","Over there, Qin Yuanzheng and his subordinate finally dug out the box.","They had long since tossed aside the pickaxe and were digging with their bare hands.","At this point, the subordinate didn't dare to use his hands anymore, leaving Qin Yuanzheng to dig alone.","Qin Yuanzheng wasn't wearing gloves, and his hands were freezing red. He carefully brushed the dirt away and slowly unearthed the box.","Suddenly, his movements paused, and his subordinate quickly cried out, \"Commander!\"","Both men were kneeling on the ground. Cold sweat formed on Qin Yuanzheng's forehead. He remained perfectly still for a full two seconds before saying in a deep voice, \"What are you yelling for? Trying to scare me to death?\"","The company commander's face was pale, his forehead covered in sweat. He knelt beside him, not daring to breathe loudly.","Right next to the box, a landmine was pressed tightly against it!","The mine was buried deeper than the box, so they hadn't seen it when they first reached the box.","If an ordinary person had been digging up the box at this moment, there would only be two possibilities.","Either they would strike the mine with a shovel, causing it to explode.","Or they would hit the box and, while digging it out, bump into the adjacent mine, triggering an explosion.","Encountering such a situation, even Qin Yuanzheng's forehead was dripping with cold sweat.","The company commander asked in a low voice, \"Commander, what kind of mine is this?\"","After Qin Yuanzheng inspected it thoroughly and confirmed his hands hadn't triggered anything, he slowly withdrew his hands.","The cold sweat from his forehead dripped down and vanished into the soil. He casually wiped his brow with his sleeve, then lay on his stomach to examine it closely.","This terrified the company commander beside him, turning his face stark white.","Although the company commander had seen his fair share of action and had led troops in clearing many landmines.","Today's situation still sent chills down his spine.","This wasn't a battlefield, a mountainous area, or a training ground.","This was the urban district, a bustling downtown area, a state-run restaurant—a place where people lived and walked every day!","And yet, there was a landmine here!","And planted in such an insidious way! Was this a trap designed to lure someone over and blow them up?","What a sinister tactic!","The mine was buried deep, right at the base of the wall, where few people would normally walk.","Therefore, from the very beginning, Qin Yuanzheng had ruled out pressure-release and pressure-activated triggers. Naturally, his judgment was correct.","He saw a very thin thread tied to the mine—he wasn't sure if it was fishing line—and attached to the box. If the box moved even a little, it would explode instantly.","He let out a breath of relief and whispered, \"It's a tripwire mine.\"","Liu Zhengxing must have had a specific target and a time requirement, which was why he tied the line to the box.","Otherwise, he could have just left the wire on the surface of the dirt, and it would have exploded the moment an animal or person passed by.","The explosion on the street in the middle of the night last time was perhaps done using a similar method.","However, his target this time was likely the people dining in the state-run restaurant. Therefore, he calculated the timing, using gold bars to lure the punk into digging for treasure.","The depth of these spies' scheming and the ruthlessness of their methods were simply appalling.","Qin Yuanzheng said in a deep voice, \"Continue scanning, and be careful.\"","The company commander nodded and continued to scan the nearby area with the detector.","Qin Yuanzheng unzipped the tool bag hanging at his waist, took out a small trowel, and continued to scoop away the dirt. Once the entire mine was exposed, he pulled out a pair of tweezers. Applying slight pressure with his fingertips, he clamped the thin wire near the detonator to hold it steady. With his other hand, he took out specialized wire cutters and aimed them at the point on the wire closest to the detonator.","The atmosphere at the scene was incredibly tense. Everyone kept their eyes glued to Qin Yuanzheng's movements.","Standing in the distance, Qiao Lanshu's heart raced with anxiety, and her face turned pale.","Because she was so nervous, Qiao Lanshu even felt a little dizzy and nauseous.","She hadn't experienced morning sickness in a long time, but now, due to the stress, she suddenly felt the urge to vomit and began breaking out in a cold sweat.","But she forced herself to endure it without showing any signs, just staring unblinkingly in Qin Yuanzheng's direction, completely motionless.","Wang Xue looked at her with some concern, but at a moment like this, she didn't dare to speak.","It was just too thrilling. To actually witness soldiers defusing a bomb in her lifetime—she could brag about this for the rest of her life.","Qin Yuanzheng's expression was grave and completely focused. The only sound in his ears was the howling of the cold wind.","His wrist exerted a slight force, and with a \"click,\" the thin wire was snipped.","He didn't stop there. He immediately used the tweezers to pull the two ends of the wire out to the sides, keeping them far away from the detonator. After confirming there was no chance of them snapping back, he finally let out a slow sigh of relief.","Afterward, he used the small trowel to clear away the dirt around the mine, revealing the entirety of the detonator.","Qin Yuanzheng skillfully pinched the detonator's latch and gave it a gentle snap, completely removing the detonator from the mine. Only at this moment did he truly breathe a sigh of relief.","Without a detonator, the landmine was nothing more than an ordinary lump of iron, posing no further danger.","This thing would later be sent back to the military base for centralized disposal.","Honestly, if they were out in the field, they would have just blown it up directly.","But here, they couldn't risk a detonation; the collateral damage would be far too severe.","However, there was more than one landmine. It wasn't long before the company commander's detector went off again. \"Commander, there's another one here!\"","Si Zhemao cursed furiously, \"Son of a bitch! Just how many of these things did that bastard plant?\""]},{"number":156,"title":"Chapter 156: His wife is quite attractive.","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng had just finished defusing the mine on this side when another one was quickly detected over there.","Qin Yuanzheng went over to continue defusing it.","This whole process took a long time. Qiao Lanshu stood there watching from a distance, and before she knew it, the sky had grown dark.","But none of the onlookers left, including Wang Xue. She stayed as well.","She stood close to Qiao Lanshu and said nervously, \"My goodness, just how many are buried here? Is Liu Zhengxing trying to turn the world upside down?\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't speak.","She wasn't feeling very well at the moment.","Perhaps it was because she recalled Qin Yuanzheng getting injured in her past life, which made her feel deeply unsettled.","This discomfort also manifested physically, as if even the baby in her womb was affected and started kicking restlessly.","Qiao Lanshu's forehead was covered in cold sweat, which even soaked her hat. As the chilly dusk wind blew, her entire body felt freezing and clammy.","Seeing her pale face and tense state, Wang Xue whispered, \"Xiao Qiao, are you feeling unwell? How about we head back first?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head and whispered, \"Sister, I'm worried about him. I... I still want to keep an eye on things.\"","How could she feel at ease if she wasn't here watching over Qin Yuanzheng?","She didn't want to leave at all. Not being able to see Qin Yuanzheng would only make her heart ache more.","Wang Xue sighed and then said to her, \"Then let's go sit over there for a while.\"","The steps on the side of the street were a bit cold, but it was better than standing.","Wang Xue found two pieces of cardboard to pad the ground, and then sat down closely beside Qiao Lanshu to continue watching Qin Yuanzheng clear the mines.","There were many onlookers around. Since everyone was on holiday for the New Year and had plenty of free time, they gathered in small groups outside the police cordon, looking from afar in the direction of Qin Yuanzheng and the others, discussing animatedly:","\"What on earth is going on over there? Why are there not only police officers, but soldiers too?\"","\"Oh, haven't you heard? People are saying that explosives were buried at the base of the state-run restaurant's wall, and the PLA comrades are defusing them.\"","\"Good heavens! Are there really explosives?\"","\"Thank goodness they didn't go off, otherwise, who knows how many people would have died. This area is usually the busiest.\"","...","As people gossiped and the news spread, more and more people came to watch.","Qin Yuanzheng defused two mines and dug out two boxes.","There was no gold in the boxes; they were only filled with rocks.","The company commander in charge of mine detection searched the surroundings, then circled back to continue sweeping.","He swept the area three times. Finally, he put away the mine detector and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Commander, the detection is complete. No further targets have been found.\"","In other words, Liu Zhengxing had buried a total of two boxes and two landmines.","The landmines had already been defused by Qin Yuanzheng, and two iron lumps now sat in front of him.","He nodded and called over Deputy Police Chief Li Jianlin. He said to him, \"The preliminary sweep is complete, and the landmines have all been defused. However, this area still needs to be cordoned off. Once we return to the base, we will arrange for a clearance team to come over and thoroughly inspect the nearby residential areas and surrounding alleys again.\"","Li Jianlin nodded and quickly replied, \"I understand. I will assist the clearance team with their work.\"","Si Zhemao also came over with Qian Weiming. Looking at the two lumps of iron on the ground, he asked Qin Yuanzheng, \"What are their serial numbers? Where did they come from?\"","Qin Yuanzheng frowned and said, \"There are no serial numbers, and their origin is unknown. We'll have to take them back for a thorough investigation.\"","They were likely homemade. In fact, as long as the materials were available, making such things wasn't difficult for certain people.","However, not many people knew how to make them, so the maker's identity was definitely not simple.","Si Zhemao's face darkened. He said coldly, \"Liu Zhengxing, right? Where is he? I want to interrogate him myself!\"","Li Jianlin quickly said, \"Investigator, Liu Zhengxing is currently locked up at the police station. It's already dark today. How about you go tomorrow?\"","Si Zhemao shook his head. \"No, I need to interrogate him right now! He definitely has subordinates!\"","With that, Si Zhemao turned to leave. After taking two steps, he turned back to look at Qin Yuanzheng and said, \"Regiment Commander Qin, come with us to the police station.\"","Qin Yuanzheng refused without a second thought. \"I'm sorry, Investigator. My work hours are over. I have to go home now; my family is waiting for me.\"","Si Zhemao: \"...\"","Si Zhemao's face instantly fell. \"This involves enemy spies, and your military needs to assist in the investigation. How can you go home when something like this has happened?\"","Those were two landmines buried right in the middle of a busy street!","The matter was incredibly serious, yet Qin Yuanzheng actually had the mind to go home.","Si Zhemao was so angry he wanted to curse.","Qin Yuanzheng was silent for two seconds before saying, \"Investigator, with you stepping in, this matter will definitely be resolved smoothly. I believe in you!\"","Si Zhemao: \"...Stop flattering me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had the company commander behind him pack up the equipment and take the two dismantled landmines. He told him, \"Take these things back to the base. You can go back now, and arrange for another squad to come over and conduct a sweep after dinner.\"","The company commander quickly nodded. \"Understood!\"","Saying that, he immediately grabbed the detector, put the two landmines into a sack, and hurried back to the base.","Si Zhemao saw that Qin Yuanzheng really had no intention of going to the police station with him, and instead strode toward his wife.","Speechless, Si Zhemao muttered, \"This guy has changed ever since he got married. Seriously, he just got a wife. Is it really necessary to act like this?\"","Still single, Si Zhemao didn't yet understand the joys of having a wife.","He frowned in incomprehension and stared at Qin Yuanzheng's back for a moment.","Then, he took Li Jianlin, Qian Weiming, and the others, and hurried off to the police station.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng coming over, Wang Xue immediately breathed a sigh of relief and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"It looks like the crisis is over. Xiao Qiao, I'll be leaving first then. You can go back with Regiment Commander Qin.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Okay, sister. Be careful on your way back.\"","The heavy anxiety in Qiao Lanshu's heart finally settled down at this moment.","Heaven knew how nervous she had been for the past few hours, from the afternoon until now!","Qin Yuanzheng knew that Qiao Lanshu had been here all along and hadn't gone back.","He was worried about her, which was why he had refused Si Zhemao.","Si Zhemao, Li Jianlin, and the others were more than enough to handle the interrogation of Liu Zhengxing. He belonged to the military, so even if he didn't go, they couldn't say anything about it.","After all, he had already completed the most difficult part just now.","He walked up to Qiao Lanshu and squatted down to look at her. \"Why aren't you getting up? Are your legs numb?\"","As he spoke, he reached out and rubbed Qiao Lanshu's head.","Qiao Lanshu's face looked a bit pale. She reached her hand out. Qin Yuanzheng took a look, wiped his own hands on his clothes first, and only then held her hand.","Qiao Lanshu was wearing cotton gloves. He gently squeezed her hand through the gloves and asked in a low voice, \"Did you catch a cold? I told you to go back earlier, but you wouldn't listen. The wind is strong here. What if you get sick?\"","Saying this, he took off his overcoat, draped it over Qiao Lanshu, and then picked her up in his arms.","Wrapped in the overcoat, Qiao Lanshu nestled into Qin Yuanzheng's embrace.","It wasn't until this moment, smelling the familiar scent on Qin Yuanzheng, that Qiao Lanshu finally felt at ease.","The discomfort in her body eased a bit. Leaning against Qin Yuanzheng's chest, she whispered, \"Brother Zheng, I was really worried about you earlier. You...\"","She originally wanted to say, could you stop taking on such dangerous missions in the future?","But on second thought, he was a soldier.","The very identity of a soldier inherently represented danger.","Many people envied the prestige of soldiers and the good treatment they received.","But who could imagine how dangerous and arduous the missions behind the scenes truly were?","Qiao Lanshu paused, then silently leaned back into Qin Yuanzheng's embrace without saying another word.","Qin Yuanzheng knew that his little wife was truly frightened this time.","Look at how scared she was, falling silent and losing her desire to speak.","He sighed softly and murmured, \"Don't worry, I know my limits and I'll be fine. In the past, on the battlefield, we didn't even have mine detectors. We just used a wooden stick to clear mines. If nothing happened to me in that kind of environment, you can rest even more assured now.\"","The conditions now were much better than before.","In the past, they were so poor they didn't even have a decent tool.","No matter what they did, they had to forge ahead with nothing but their flesh and blood. Now, the military base had everything, and they didn't have to go to the battlefield anymore. It was actually much better than before.","Qiao Lanshu leaned silently against his chest and said no more.","Seeing her stay quiet, Qin Yuanzheng felt an even sharper ache in his heart.","He felt a bit guilty for failing to give his wife a sense of security.","But he had no choice. This was his duty. If he encountered a situation like today's again, he would still be the first to charge forward.","He carried Qiao Lanshu to the car. Their affectionate display made Si Zhemao, who was just about to leave, clench his teeth in exasperation.","Si Zhemao was in the same car as Qian Weiming. As the car slowly drove away, he looked through the window and saw Qin Yuanzheng holding his little wife. He shook his head and sighed, \"This Qin Yuanzheng has completely fallen into the honey trap. He is hopeless, totally hopeless.\"","Qian Weiming: \"...\"","Qian Weiming also had a wife and child, so he could completely understand Qin Yuanzheng.","However, it was best for married men not to discuss marriage with unmarried men.","Just like people with children shouldn't talk about parenting with those who don't have any.","They were completely from two different worlds. It was like a chicken talking to a duck; they would never understand each other.","Qian Weiming could only smile awkwardly and say, \"After all, Regiment Commander Qin is nearly thirty and finally married a little wife. It hasn't been easy for him. It is understandable, completely understandable.\"","Si Zhemao sneered coldly, \"I am already thirty-five, and I haven't gotten married either, have I? But I am not like him, losing my ability to walk the moment I see a woman.\"","As he spoke, he added, \"Truly spineless!\"","Qian Weiming: \"...\"","Qian Weiming fell silent.","Continuing this conversation would inevitably touch upon sensitive topics.","After all, the reason Si Zhemao remained unmarried at his age was tied to his parents being falsely accused in the past.","He himself had been sent to a labor camp. After being exonerated and returning, he pushed himself relentlessly to climb the ranks, finally reaching his current position.","His youth had been wasted, and dragging things out until now, marriage had become a daunting challenge for him.","His superiors had tried to set him up with a wife, but unfortunately, his fierce temper and intimidating appearance made matchmaking quite difficult.","Si Zhemao stared out the window for a while. It wasn't until the car turned a corner and he could no longer see them that he withdrew his gaze and muttered, \"Qin Yuanzheng's wife is quite a beauty.\"","Quickly changing the subject, he told Qian Weiming, \"When we interrogate Liu Zhengxing later, there's no need to show any mercy. He's a spy, so we'll interrogate him exactly how a spy should be interrogated.\"","Hearing this, a chill rose from the depths of Qian Weiming's heart.","He couldn't imagine what kind of suffering Liu Zhengxing was about to endure, but he had brought it upon himself. Spies never met a good end.","After a moment, Si Zhemao added, \"In the two days since I arrived, the guesthouse seems to have received several whistleblower letters. My secretary has them. You'll assist him in handling this matter later.\"","As soon as Qian Weiming heard about whistleblower letters—and several of them at that—he grew tense. He had no idea who had reported what or whom.","He hadn't done anything wrong himself, had he?","He had accepted a roast duck from someone before; did that count as bribery?","Could someone have reported him for that?","At this thought, Qian Weiming wiped the cold sweat from his forehead and nodded. \"Understood, Investigator. Rest assured, I will definitely handle this matter well.\"","On this trip to Longcheng, Si Zhemao had brought along a secretary and an assistant who doubled as a bodyguard.","The secretary assisted him with his work and held a rather high position himself.","Qian Weiming sat in the car with a solemn expression, discussing the upcoming tasks with the secretary in the passenger seat.","...","While these men were busy with their affairs.","Qin Yuanzheng had already taken his wife home.","His little wife had been badly frightened today, and Qin Yuanzheng wanted to comfort Qiao Lanshu properly.","The moment they got home, he shut the door, washed his hands thoroughly, and pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms.","He pressed her gently against the sofa, kissing her as he began to undress her.","Qiao Lanshu was very obedient, following his lead.","Qin Yuanzheng always felt his little wife was quite petite, but she had put on a little weight recently, making her soft and cuddly to hold.","Especially because of her pregnancy, her curves had become much fuller, which Qin Yuanzheng loved.","He simply couldn't keep his hands off her.","Her previously slender, fragile waist had grown rounder with her pregnant belly, giving her an entirely different feel.","After kissing Qiao Lanshu for quite a while, Qin Yuanzheng murmured, \"Wife, you've grown bigger here again.\"","It was like dough rising, suddenly swelling up.","He felt this dough was even better to knead.","His hands kept busy as he asked her in a low voice, \"Why aren't you speaking? Still haven't recovered from the shock?\"","His little wife hadn't said much the entire way back.","But she didn't seem sad either. He had no idea what she was thinking, and she wasn't saying.","Qin Yuanzheng noticed that in moments like this, Qiao Lanshu was almost entirely submissive to him.","When he held her, she took the initiative to pull at his clothes.","He almost couldn't handle her enthusiasm.","Mainly because his stamina was failing him. It was completely useless.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, Brother Zheng, why did you stop?","Qin Yuanzheng lay beside her and said in a husky voice, Continue what?","The fermented dough was almost perfectly kneaded, and he was very satisfied.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu shot him a reproachful glare.","He obviously knew exactly what she was talking about, yet he deliberately chose to tease her.","It had been a long time, and she actually missed Qin Yuanzheng.","Furthermore, at a time like this, she felt a rather urgent need to share some intimacy with him, just to put her own heart at ease."]},{"number":157,"title":"Chapter 157: Dangerous Mission","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng realized that his little wife was truly terrified.","The incident of him going to dismantle a landmine today must have given Qiao Lanshu a huge fright.","She was much clingier than before.","In the past, she would always use being too tired as an excuse, often making him abstain from intimacy.","But now, she was actually taking the initiative.","Even though she was already over three months pregnant, and would be four months along in just another week.","Qin Yuanzheng had always been deeply protective of his wife, so they mostly just cuddled and touched; they never went all the way.","He had planned to do the same today, thinking he would just hold his wife to satisfy his cravings without going any further.","As a result, the little wife in his arms became dissatisfied first.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng stop, she found it somewhat unbelievable.","She directly reached out and grabbed him, looking at Qin Yuanzheng. Brother Zheng, are you going to sleep just like this?","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","Qin Yuanzheng's forehead was covered in sweat. He looked at Qiao Lanshu with a hoarse voice, truly feeling that this little wife of his didn't know the meaning of danger.","He asked in a deep voice, If not sleeping, what else do you want to do?","Qiao Lanshu rolled over and sat on top of him. She whispered, Brother Zheng, it's been almost four months. It's fine.","At this moment, his little wife was simply like an enchanting little siren radiating charm.","He normally had zero resistance against her every frown and smile.","Let alone now, under the dim yellow oil lamp, the two of them facing each other bare, with her straddling him, saying it was fine, and even questioning if he wasn't capable.","Qin Yuanzheng was almost angered into laughing by his own wife.","Wasn't she the one who knew best whether he was capable or not?","Of course, it was also possible that because he hadn't done this with her for so long, she had forgotten the times she used to cry and beg for mercy.","Qin Yuanzheng flipped over and pinned Qiao Lanshu down. Wife, don't you cry later.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","...","Because Qiao Lanshu was pregnant, already four months along.","Qin Yuanzheng was extremely careful, terrified of making Xiao Qiao uncomfortable, so he held back...","With him dawdling like this, Qiao Lanshu couldn't quite take it anymore. Brother Zheng, haven't you eaten?","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless once again.","Qin Yuanzheng was practically laughing out of pure exasperation. Even if I haven't eaten for two days, I can still do you until you can't get out of bed!","Then, in a fit of anger, Qin Yuanzheng let out his fury.","But at any rate, he managed to serve his wife until she was thoroughly satisfied.","Only after his wife fell asleep did Qin Yuanzheng head to the bathroom, still feeling somewhat unfulfilled.","Sigh, it seemed he really would have to wait until the baby was born.","Qin Yuanzheng finally finished up, came out of the bathroom, and returned to the kang bed to sleep.","Holding the sleeping Qiao Lanshu, he pondered in his heart. It was almost four months now; he should find someone to help ask around and get a nanny for Qiao Lanshu in advance.","His parents' hometown was quite far from here, a good thousand kilometers away.","Both of his parents also had formal jobs and couldn't come over to help him take care of the child.","Qiao Lanshu had married far away from home to accompany him in the military, and she had no relatives or friends here.","Moreover, Qiao Lanshu was young and didn't know much about many things, let alone giving birth and raising a child.","He didn't know how to raise a child either. How were they supposed to bring up a baby?","He felt somewhat worried.","It would be better to hire an experienced older woman. When the time came, she could help Qiao Lanshu look after the baby and cook meals, so Qiao Lanshu could get proper rest.","With this in mind, Qin Yuanzheng brought the matter up to Qiao Lanshu early the next morning.","Qiao Lanshu had just woken up and could barely open her eyes.","Qin Yuanzheng had gone at it twice last night. Although he hadn't tossed her around too much, she still felt a bit tired.","After all, pregnancy naturally made one lethargic.","As Qin Yuanzheng helped her get dressed, he said, Your belly is gradually getting bigger. I thought about it last night, and I decided it would be best to hire a nanny to take care of you.","Qin Yuanzheng originally wanted to take care of Qiao Lanshu himself, but obviously, the nature of his work made it impossible for him to stay at home and accompany her.","More often than not, he couldn't even get off work on time.","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu immediately agreed. I was thinking the same thing, but where should we find one?","After having the baby, she would probably resign to stay home and raise the child, while reviewing her studies on the side.","When the child was about a year old, she planned to take the college entrance examination.","Her dream was to get into university and study a major she liked. If she had to juggle working and taking care of a child, she was afraid she wouldn't have enough energy.","Qin Yuanzheng finished dressing her before saying, Don't worry, I'll find someone reliable.","It would be best if it was someone introduced by an acquaintance. Actually, many of the accompanying military family members around their base hired nannies.","After all, the ones accompanying the soldiers were the wives, while the parents usually stayed in their hometowns.","With the wives needing to look after the children and the husbands unable to help, they would hire a live-in nanny, or one who came during the day and left at night.","By asking around in this residential compound, one could gather quite a bit of information.","Qin Yuanzheng said he would keep an eye out for this matter. However, when Qiao Lanshu went to work, she also mentioned it to Wang Xue, who promised to help her look out for candidates.","...","The news of the state-run restaurant being rigged with landmines spread throughout Longcheng that very day.","As the soldier who cleared the mines, Qin Yuanzheng had earned merit. The first thing he did upon arriving at work today was to head to the headquarters to report on his work.","Qin Yuanzheng had initially thought this work report would be simple and he would be able to leave quickly.","Instead, he was asked to stay behind by Commander Li.","This time, Commander Li's expression was somewhat serious. Furthermore, sitting in his office were not only a few military officers, but even the investigator Si Zhemao was present.","Si Zhemao hadn't even bothered to eat yesterday, interrogating Liu Zhengxing overnight.","All the schemes Liu Zhengxing had carefully laid out were unraveled by this bizarre coincidence.","He had been waiting expectantly in the public security bureau for the explosion to occur, waiting for news of the investigator being injured, or those cadres being wounded or killed in the blast.","In the end, nothing happened.","Liu Zhengxing was having a bit of a breakdown. Not only had he failed to save his son, but he had now dragged himself down with him.","Commander Li said to Qin Yuanzheng, This is Liu Zhengxing's confession. Take a look.","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at Si Zhemao.","Si Zhemao hadn't slept all night, and as soon as dawn broke, he rushed non-stop to the headquarters to find people. He had likely encountered a major incident.","Qin Yuanzheng silently began to read the confession.","In truth, Liu Zhengxing was a very difficult person to deal with. Without using some special methods, he wouldn't be easy to handle.","Previously, Guan Wenjun had been wary of his identity, so he hadn't managed to interrogate anything out of him.","But now that he had committed a crime and was suspected of being a spy, Si Zhemao showed no mercy during the interrogation.","And this interrogation actually brought some things to light.","Qin Yuanzheng also roughly understood why Commander Li had kept him behind to talk: Liu Zhengxing still has a superior contact?","These people were likely trying to transmit classified information outward, but due to their current positions and identities, their methods of communication were extremely covert.","The person coordinating with Liu Zhengxing was in a mountain village tens of kilometers away from here.","Si Zhemao said in a deep voice, These people sure know how to hide, actually holing up in the mountains. Places like that are not easy to find.","Qin Yuanzheng had executed many similar missions in the past.","He said in a low voice, \"These people might very well be villagers. They have been hiding in the village for decades, born and raised there, and have already blended in completely with the local farmers. It won't be easy to root out people like that.\"","They pass on the information they collect using covert methods. The people in the mountains are busy clearing wasteland and farming, so they wouldn't pay attention to this.","Furthermore, the mountainous area is vast, and many people never go deep into the mountains, so they wouldn't be discovered.","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent. Commander Li said in a deep voice, \"Xiao Qin, I originally didn't plan to assign you to this mission. After all, you've only been married for a few months, and your wife is pregnant. I should have let you stay home for the New Year.\"","Now, all the factories and units were on holiday, and it was only three or four days until New Year's Eve.","On the streets, everyone was joyfully buying New Year's goods. Qin Yuanzheng had originally planned to take his wife to the department store in a couple of days to buy her some things.","At this moment, he grew somewhat quiet.","Commander Li looked at him and added, \"But this mission is extremely dangerous. I thought it over and over, and it's still most appropriate for you to go. With you stepping up, our chances of success are higher.\"","If anyone else were assigned, it might result in casualties, which was not something Commander Li wanted to see.","Qin Yuanzheng's overall strength ranked first year after year. Before he got married, he frequently executed similar dangerous missions. Whether in terms of experience or ability, he was outstanding.","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent for a long time before saying, \"This place is nearly a hundred kilometers away, and the mission is dangerous. My wife is still young, and she is pregnant. She can't be without someone to take care of her.\"","The officer sitting next to Commander Li then said, \"Commander Qin, you can rest assured about that. When the time comes, I will transfer two female soldiers from the logistics department to take turns caring for your wife. They can move directly into your home and accompany her 24 hours a day. We absolutely won't let anything happen to her, so just set your mind at ease.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Si Zhemao knew the mission was perilous. As an investigator, he had seen his fair share of traitors like Liu Zhengxing.","He said, \"I will personally assist you this time. Don't worry, we will set out together when the time comes.\"","Commander Li also said, \"In addition to that, I will arrange for another squad to go to the village to back you up.\"","Because it was a covert operation, Qin Yuanzheng and Si Zhemao were to depart in secret and enter the village with concealed identities. The two of them would proceed in two separate directions, one operating in the open and the other in the shadows.","The third squad arranged by Commander Li would be specifically responsible for backing them up, acting as reinforcements.","If Qin Yuanzheng and his partner could complete the mission, the third squad would not reveal themselves.","But if they encountered any accidents, the third squad would come out to assist them.","This was also just in case.","After all, this mission was indeed dangerous and difficult to accomplish.","Moreover, they were acting in secret, and there were no garrisoned troops in the surrounding mountain villages.","Because they were unsure of the extent of the enemy's infiltration, they did not dare to easily mobilize personnel from various departments in the surrounding counties and cities.","It could be said that whether the matter succeeded or not depended entirely on the few of them.","This was an order, a mission. Qin Yuanzheng could not refuse.","He only asked one question: \"When do we depart?\"","Si Zhemao immediately said, \"Tonight at eight o'clock. We will travel there by night.\"","Commander Li also said, \"Xiao Qin, arrange your work first today, then go back and have a good talk with your wife. Pack your things, and gather here at seven-thirty tonight. I still have some instructions for you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded, composed himself, and said, \"Received.\"","...","The mission was classified and could not be disclosed to anyone, including one's own family.","Qin Yuanzheng went back to handle some work at the mining area, and then he went to pick up Qiao Lanshu from work.","Passing by the supply and marketing cooperative, Qin Yuanzheng took Qiao Lanshu inside to buy some things.","Qiao Lanshu, slowly knitting a sweater in the car, said, \"Brother Zheng, we still have vegetables at home, why are we buying more?\"","Qin Yuanzheng parked the car, then held Qiao Lanshu's hand as they got out. He wrapped her scarf a bit tighter around her before saying, \"I have to go out tonight, and it might take seven or eight days before I come back. So, I'm buying some food for you to stock up on. That way, you won't have to come out to buy groceries while you're home alone.\"","As he spoke, he added, \"When the time comes, the logistics department will send personnel over to take care of you, buy groceries, and cook for you. Do you want them to live at our house? Or just come over every afternoon?\"","Hearing his words, the expression on Qiao Lanshu's face grew somewhat disappointed.","Her originally smiling eyes blinked and slowly became a bit more serious. \"Brother Zheng, are you going on a mission?\"","She and Qin Yuanzheng had been married for a few months, and Qin Yuanzheng had almost never left home.","The couple had not been apart for more than a day. They were together every day, going home after work to cook, eat, and sleep together.","Life was very stable and incredibly warm.","Qiao Lanshu had thought that since they were married and she was pregnant, Qin Yuanzheng wouldn't have to go on missions anymore.","She said softly, \"Didn't you tell the organization? I'm pregnant. Can you apply to stay at home and not go on the mission?\"","What Qiao Lanshu said was too idealistic.","Qin Yuanzheng stopped and looked at his somewhat saddened little wife. He reached out and rubbed her hair, saying softly, \"Silly wife, I am a soldier. A soldier only needs to follow orders.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng said in a low voice, \"This mission is very arduous and not easy to complete. Aside from me, there really isn't a suitable person here in Longcheng right now.\"","Even he did not dare to say he could complete it with one hundred percent certainty.","Liu Zhengxing himself didn't even know who his superior was.","He just occasionally passed on the information he collected through certain methods. As for what the other party looked like, their age, or what kind of person they were, he knew absolutely nothing.","He only knew a general location, but there were four or five mountain villages there, and investigating them would not be easy.","Furthermore, the other party might very well have explosives and landmines, or they likely had guns.","In short, the danger level was not low.","Qin Yuanzheng said softly, \"I will finish the mission as quickly as possible and strive to come back to spend the Spring Festival with you.\"","This was the first Spring Festival they would spend together after getting married.","Qin Yuanzheng still valued it highly.","He hoped that everything would go smoothly with this mission so that he could return early to accompany his wife for the New Year.","What else could Qiao Lanshu do? She sighed softly, her mood dropping. \"Brother Zheng, you must be careful. Don't get hurt.\"","She didn't ask what the mission was either. After all, it was classified; even if she asked, Qin Yuanzheng wouldn't tell her.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"I know.\"","As he spoke, his heart ached for his wife again, so he took Qiao Lanshu into the cooperative and bought a lot of food.","He bought five pounds of flour, two pounds of glass noodles, a box of sweet potatoes, and a box of apples.","Afterward, he went to the non-staple food counter and bought a few pounds of biscuits and candies, as well as two pounds of sweet fried dough twists.","These things were enough for Qiao Lanshu to eat for a long time.","Qiao Lanshu hurriedly said, \"Brother Zheng, stop buying, I won't be able to finish it all. There will still be time to buy more when you come back.\"","Qin Yuanzheng said softly, \"These things keep well. Let's buy a bit more so we will have plenty for the New Year.\"","He bought so many things that the car was completely stuffed and could not hold another item. Only then did he finally take Qiao Lanshu back home.","The moment they arrived, he immediately started on the household chores and began packing his bags, as he had to leave on a trip very soon."]},{"number":158,"title":"Chapter 158: Nightmare","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng packed very lightly. He brought a change of clothes and some dry rations; these items did not even fill his backpack.","He still had to make a trip to the military base shortly to pick up some weapons and tools.","After finishing this, he took off his military uniform and changed into a black outfit.","They would be setting off overnight tonight, and upon arrival, they would have to operate in the dark.","He also brought a camouflage jacket, as they would still need disguise for daytime operations in the mountains and forests.","Qiao Lanshu watched him pack, feeling a bit uneasy. \"Brother Zheng, is this mission very dangerous?\"","Qin Yuanzheng walked over with his backpack and gently hugged Qiao Lanshu. He said in a low voice, \"It is not very dangerous. Do not worry, I will be careful. Wait for me at home, and do not go running around by yourself. If you want to go out shopping, have the people from the logistics department accompany you. They should be coming over tomorrow.\"","Because Qiao Lanshu was not used to having outsiders in the house, Qin Yuanzheng did not have them stay over.","The logistics department would arrange for a driver to pick up and drop off Qiao Lanshu for work every morning and evening.","Then, a female comrade specifically assigned to take care of her would come over every afternoon to deliver food. The meals, packed from the headquarters cafeteria, would be brought to her every evening. The comrade would stay with her for an hour or two, and only leave with the lunchbox after Qiao Lanshu finished eating and was ready to rest.","Although Qiao Lanshu felt this was a bit exaggerated—having someone drive her to and from work was already good enough, and she could cook for herself—Qin Yuanzheng worried about her being alone and did not allow her to refuse.","So, Qiao Lanshu just followed Qin Yuanzheng's arrangements.","Qin Yuanzheng told Qiao Lanshu, \"When I am not home, if you need anything, go find my cousin or our neighbors. They will all help you. Do not be shy about it, okay?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, looking at Qin Yuanzheng with reluctance to part.","Qin Yuanzheng also could not bear to leave his little wife.","He walked to the door, kissed Qiao Lanshu again, and said to her, \"It is cold outside. Go back in.\"","With that, he turned to leave, telling Qiao Lanshu, who was standing at the door, \"Be good, go back inside.\"","Then, he closed the door.","Hearing the footsteps echoing in the stairwell, Qiao Lanshu confirmed that Qin Yuanzheng had truly left.","She ran to the kitchen window and looked outside.","In the darkness, she saw his tall figure walk into the night, quickly disappearing at the intersection.","Qiao Lanshu sighed softly, feeling a sense of emptiness in her heart.","This was the first time she had watched Qin Yuanzheng leave for a distant mission.","Qiao Lanshu sighed again, went back inside, and tightly closed the front door and windows. After making sure they were deadbolted, she straightened her clothes and went to the kitchen to cook herself some simple porridge.","Afterward, she sat on the sofa, turned on the radio, and read her high school textbooks while listening to the broadcast.","Not long after, Huang Erling from next door came knocking.","Huang Erling actually quite enjoyed chatting with Qiao Lanshu, especially after Qiao Lanshu got pregnant—there were just so many topics about children to discuss.","However, when Qin Yuanzheng was home, he was intensely protective of his wife, so Huang Erling usually did not dare to come over at all.","Now that she knew Qin Yuanzheng had left, she immediately came knocking, holding a bowl of braised meat and vegetables in her hands.","Qiao Lanshu opened the door and smiled instantly upon seeing her. \"Sister Ling, you are here?\"","Huang Erling came in with the bowl of piping hot braised food, smiling. \"I heard Regiment Commander Qin is going on a long trip? Did the people from the logistics department come over?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. \"They should be coming tomorrow evening. They said they will bring me dinner.\"","Huang Erling immediately said, \"Our men protect our homes and defend our country, and the military treats us family members very well. In the past, when my Lao Zhao went on a long trip, the military even arranged for two older sisters to come over and help me watch the kids.\"","At that time, Zhao Jiannong had just been promoted to battalion commander, and Huang Erling had only recently joined him at the military base. She had no relatives or friends in this city and had two children with her, one three years old and the other a year old.","The military needed Zhao Jiannong for a task, and to ensure he had no worries back home, they arranged for two female comrades from the logistics department—both mothers themselves—to come and help her take care of the children. Even after Zhao Jiannong returned, those two comrades would still drop by occasionally to see the kids.","Huang Erling placed the bowl on the table and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"I guessed you had not eaten yet, so I saved a bowl of this braised dish for you. Eat it while it is hot. I just made it tonight, with potatoes and pork.\"","The New Year was approaching, so the supply and marketing cooperative had a small amount of pork available.","Over the past few days, everyone had been lining up to snatch up meat. Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng had also bought quite a bit of pork and mutton.","Moreover, in Qin Yuanzheng's mining area unit, they were raising some chickens, ducks, and geese that his comrades had given to Qiao Lanshu to nourish her body.","Qin Yuanzheng had originally planned to slaughter a chicken for the New Year, as Qiao Lanshu loved eating chicken.","But he had to leave for a mission today, and it was unknown if he could make it back in time for New Year's Eve to prepare the chicken for her.","Looking at the fragrant bowl of food, Qiao Lanshu did not stand on ceremony. \"It smells amazing. Thank you, Sister Ling. I have not cooked any dishes yet, so you have really done me a huge favor.\"","With Qin Yuanzheng going far away, she was not in a great mood and had no desire to cook.","She had originally planned to just make do with whatever for tonight.","As a result, receiving the food from Huang Erling made her very grateful, and she pondered what to give in return later.","In the afternoon, Qin Yuanzheng had bought her a box of apples, so she could definitely give Huang Erling a couple of those.","Huang Erling smiled and said, \"You do not need to be so polite. We are neighbors, so helping each other is only natural. You eat first; I will stay here and chat with you for a bit.\"","Her Lao Zhao had returned. The two kids were close in age and both in elementary school now. Usually, when the sisters came home, they would read and do homework together, or listen to the radio together, so Huang Erling did not have to worry much.","Now that Huang Erling had more free time, she spent her days doing some sewing and mending, living quite a leisurely life.","Qiao Lanshu pulled up a small stool, served herself some sweet potato porridge, and asked Huang Erling, \"Sister Ling, have you eaten yet?\"","Huang Erling sat on the sofa, listening to the radio while examining the sweater Qiao Lanshu had half-knitted. She nodded and said, \"I have eaten. Hurry up and eat, do not worry about me. It is going to get cold soon.\"","Qiao Lanshu placed the small stool next to the sofa and ate her porridge with the braised dish.","On the radio, the news was reporting that the state-run restaurant would be unsealed tomorrow and could officially reopen for business.","However, the broadcast did not mention why the state-run restaurant had been sealed off, nor did it reveal anything about the mine clearance.","Qin Yuanzheng had earned merit for clearing the mines. As for what class of merit it was, Qiao Lanshu did not know yet because the approval had not come down.","And now, Qin Yuanzheng had gone off to execute another mission.","As Qiao Lanshu slowly ate, Huang Erling asked her, \"How does it taste? I added Sichuan peppercorns for seasoning. Are you used to the flavor?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and said, \"I am used to it. Sister Ling, your cooking is really delicious.\"","She actually wasn't quite used to the food, as it was a bit salty, but it went perfectly with the porridge. Huang Erling was a good cook, and the dishes she made were quite delicious.","Before she knew it, Qiao Lanshu had eaten all the food and porridge.","Huang Erling then started chatting with her. Not many people know about the mine clearance at the state-run restaurant this time. Look, even the radio hasn't mentioned it. It seems there must be something else behind all this.","Qiao Lanshu's expression also grew somewhat serious.","Huang Erling picked up the sweater Qiao Lanshu had half-knitted and naturally helped her continue knitting it.","Huang Erling knitted very fast; she didn't even need to look at it.","Listening to the radio and gossiping with Qiao Lanshu at the same time, her hands moved at lightning speed. Qiao Lanshu was stunned watching her.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu's expression, Huang Erling couldn't help but smile and say, Practice more in your free time. Practice makes perfect. In the future, you might even knit better than me.","As she spoke, she flipped the sweater over. Looking at the light yellow garment, she asked, Is this for the baby? Is it a top or a onesie?","Qiao Lanshu replied, I want to make a onesie, the kind that covers the feet, so the baby will be warm.","It was just a bit difficult to knit, and Qiao Lanshu really struggled to learn how to do it.","Huang Erling smiled and said, Alright, I'll help you knit it.","Saying that, she thought of something else and whispered to Qiao Lanshu, Xiao Qiao, the mission Regiment Commander Qin went out for this time might be related to the mine clearance at the state-run restaurant.","Qiao Lanshu had actually thought about this, but she hadn't asked Qin Yuanzheng.","She whispered back, Maybe he went to catch Liu Zhengxing's accomplices?","Huang Erling nodded, lowering her voice even more. When I was in the courtyard this afternoon, I heard the neighbors say that the spy warfare seems to have intensified recently. Investigators have even come to Longcheng. I'm guessing they discovered something here in Longcheng. Your Regiment Commander Qin suddenly going on a long trip is probably to catch spies.","People in their military unit tended to know more news.","Of course, they only chatted about it in the courtyard and wouldn't go out and spread rumors.","Huang Erling added, The radio didn't mention the mine clearance at the state-run restaurant, probably to block the news and prevent it from spreading outside.","Both Huang Erling and Qiao Lanshu guessed that this mission would be very dangerous.","Qiao Lanshu fell completely silent.","Sitting on the small stool, listening to the sounds from the radio, she suddenly felt a wave of unease.","If Qin Yuanzheng's mission this time was indeed related to Liu Zhengxing...","Liu Zhengxing had been able to plant landmines everywhere right here in Longcheng.","Wouldn't it be even more dangerous for Qin Yuanzheng going out of town, especially into those remote mountain villages?","Would they have planted landmines everywhere over there too?","Qiao Lanshu's palms sweated from tension, and she began to panic.","Huang Erling knitted the sweater and comforted her, But Xiao Qiao, you don't need to worry too much. This isn't the first time for such a mission; they've been happening constantly over the past few years. My Lao Zhao has carried out several himself. They are experienced and have enough manpower, so don't worry.","What Huang Erling didn't say was that if Qin Yuanzheng successfully completed the mission this time, he would probably earn a first-class merit upon his return.","By the time he reached the right age, he would undoubtedly be a division-level cadre.","Although she loved gossiping about these things, she figured Qiao Lanshu wouldn't want to gossip about Qin Yuanzheng earning merits at a time like this.","Huang Erling quickly suggested, Xiao Qiao, how about we change the channel?","Qiao Lanshu nodded. Alright.","Saying that, she moved to the sofa, switched to a classical literature appreciation channel, and then studied how to knit the sweater with Huang Erling.","When it got late, Huang Erling prepared to head back.","Qiao Lanshu gave her two apples to take back for her children.","Huang Erling didn't refuse. Just as she had said before, as neighbors, there was no need to be overly polite;","only with give and take could they get along in the long run.","Before leaving, Huang Erling asked Qiao Lanshu, Xiao Qiao, are you scared being alone at night?","Qiao Lanshu smiled and shook her head. I'm not scared.","The military compound was the safest neighborhood in the city; there was no fear of bad guys sneaking in.","At most, she was just a little afraid of the dark, so whenever Qin Yuanzheng wasn't home, Qiao Lanshu slept with a small oil lamp lit.","Hearing her say this, Huang Erling went back next door. Before leaving, she added, I'll come over to keep you company tomorrow night if I'm free.","Qiao Lanshu gratefully thanked her again, watched Huang Erling return home, and then closed her door.","...","Qiao Lanshu read until very late before finally lying down and pulling up the covers.","She placed the small oil lamp on the bedside table and didn't fall asleep until the late hours.","However, after tossing and turning until midnight and finally falling asleep, she had a nightmare.","Since her rebirth and getting together with Qin Yuanzheng, and after Sun Mingyong was sent to a labor camp and Chu Liangjun was executed by firing squad...","she had barely dreamt about anything from her past life.","But tonight, for the first time in a long while, she dreamt of it again.","She dreamt of the forty-year-old Qin Yuanzheng. After they got married, while they were lying in bed together, he revealed the massive scars on his back.","In the dream, Qiao Lanshu stroked his scars and asked him, Brother Zheng, how did you get all these scars?","These hideous scars covered almost his entire back, even extending down to his buttocks and thighs.","With such extensive wounds, could they be burn marks?","In the dream, Qin Yuanzheng gently held her hand and whispered, I got them during a mission. They're all healed now. Did I scare you? Don't be afraid, they're just scars.","Qiao Lanshu felt a stinging sensation in her eyes; she wanted to cry.","After this dream sequence, she suddenly dreamt of a Qin Yuanzheng who was ten years younger. Dressed entirely in black and carrying a bag, he left the house. Then, just as he reached the main gate of the compound, there was a sudden boom, and an explosion went off right outside the gate.","Qin Yuanzheng, who had just walked past, was instantly engulfed in a sea of fire.","Qiao Lanshu woke up with a start!","She sat bolt upright in bed, her face covered in tears, and her pillowcase soaked.","Sitting on the bed, Qiao Lanshu breathed heavily, her heart in a frantic panic.","She instinctively got out of bed, ran barefoot to the kitchen window, and looked down at the courtyard below.","The courtyard was pitch black and completely silent.","At this hour, there was no one in the courtyard. Only the guardhouse was still lit, with a guard on duty inside.","The guard also kept a military dog, which lay quietly at the compound gate, not barking like other dogs.","Qiao Lanshu stared in the direction of the main gate for nearly ten full minutes.","Then, feeling a bit cold, she gently stroked her belly, turned around, and went back to the bedroom.","Only then did she notice the small desk clock on the bedside table. The time showed that it was already five o'clock in the morning.","She wondered if her Brother Zheng had reached his destination by this time."]},{"number":159,"title":"Chapter 159: She Is Also Going on a Long Journey","paragraphs":["After Qiao Lanshu woke up, she couldn't fall back asleep.","Her mind was filled with thoughts of Qin Yuanzheng and the nightmare she had just had.","She was in no mood to sleep at all.","Lying alone on the kang bed, she watched the world outside the window grow brighter and brighter.","When it was fully daylight, she got out of bed, got dressed, washed up, and prepared to head out.","She had gotten up at seven and was ready to leave around half past seven.","Just then, someone knocked on the door. Qiao Lanshu opened it to see a young female comrade in military uniform standing there, holding a thermal lunch box. She smiled and said, \"Hello, you must be Comrade Xiao Qiao, right? I'm from the logistics department of the 21st Regiment. You can just call me Xiao Li. I'm here to bring you breakfast.\"","The 21st Regiment was Qin Yuanzheng's regiment.","However, there didn't seem to be any female comrades in the logistics department in the mining area. The logistics department this Xiao Li belonged to must be somewhere else.","But at this moment, Qiao Lanshu was in no mood to ask too many questions. She took the thermal lunch box and thanked her, \"Thank you, Comrade Xiao Li. Would you like to come in and sit for a while?\"","Xiao Li smiled and walked in.","Today's breakfast included soy milk, two lamb-stuffed buns, a small plate of pickled shredded radish, and a purple sweet potato bun.","Qiao Lanshu was somewhat surprised that there were lamb-stuffed buns to eat.","It wasn't a holiday or festival, so wasn't this food a bit too good?","It seemed that Qin Yuanzheng's current mission was extremely dangerous, considering the organization was treating her so well.","Qiao Lanshu silently picked up a bun and took a couple of bites.","Comrade Xiao Li didn't stay idle. Upon entering the room, she started sweeping and mopping the floor. Then she checked the kitchen, found nothing to clean up, and went to the washroom to help Qiao Lanshu wash her clothes.","Qiao Lanshu was stunned.","She thought this comrade was just here to deliver food. How did she end up doing a nanny's job?","She quickly said, \"Comrade Xiao Li, leave it alone. I can clean it up myself.\"","Xiao Li was still very young, looking to be only in her early twenties.","She smiled and said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, don't be embarrassed. The organization instructed me that since you are pregnant and it's hard for you to do chores, I should help you out more. After all, you are home alone, and it's inconvenient for you to do anything.\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't have many clothes to wash because Qin Yuanzheng had already washed and hung most of them up to dry.","She had only changed out of her thermal top and pants last night, which were still unwashed.","While helping her wash the clothes, Comrade Xiao Li said, \"The water is cold in winter, and it's hard for you to bend over with your pregnant belly. So please don't be polite. Just let me wash them for you. If there's anything else you need help with, you can tell me. Please don't hesitate.\"","The organization also saw that there was no one else in Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu's home, just Qiao Lanshu alone, which was why they took special care of her. For some officers who had parents or siblings at home, they wouldn't arrange for anyone to come over.","Qiao Lanshu still felt very embarrassed.","If she had known earlier that a comrade from the logistics department would help her do chores and wash clothes, she wouldn't have changed her clothes.","Sigh, it was really a bit embarrassing.","Comrade Xiao Li worked very fast. She washed the clothes and hung them up to dry.","Seeing that Qiao Lanshu had finished eating, she started clearing the dishes.","Qiao Lanshu had finished drinking the soy milk and eating the pickled shredded radish.","She ate one lamb bun, leaving one lamb bun and the purple sweet potato bun.","Comrade Xiao Li took the buns to the kitchen, put them in a bowl, and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Xiao Qiao, I'll leave these buns in the kitchen for you. You can have them as a midnight snack if you get hungry at night.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded.","Around eight o'clock, Comrade Xiao Li left with the lunch box, having also agreed with Qiao Lanshu on the time to deliver lunch.","The food factory was already on holiday, so Qiao Lanshu didn't have to go to work.","During the time Qin Yuanzheng was not at home, she didn't have to do anything. She just needed to lie at home and wait for him to return.","After all, with three meals a day delivered to her door, as long as she was thick-skinned enough, she wouldn't even have to wash her own clothes.","But Qiao Lanshu couldn't sit still.","Her mind kept flashing back and forth to the images from last night's nightmare.","And the ugly scars that covered Qin Yuanzheng's entire back.","Qiao Lanshu couldn't sit still anymore. She put on proper clothes, went out the door, and walked all the way to the office building of the provincial revolutionary committee.","The revolutionary committee's office building wasn't far from her home. It took her about twenty minutes of walking to get there.","It wasn't even nine o'clock yet, but Guan Wenjun should be at work by now.","When she arrived outside the office building, she happened to see Guan Wenjun stepping out of the building. He was wrapped in a black trench coat, wearing sunglasses, carrying a bag in his hand, and looking exceptionally cool and handsome.","He placed the bag on the back seat of the car, then opened the car door and got in.","Usually, when he went out on business, he would take several people with him.","Today, however, he was going out alone. He usually did so many wicked things, how come he suddenly wasn't afraid of someone hitting him from behind with a brick?","Seeing him get into the car, Qiao Lanshu quickly trotted over, yanked open the passenger door, and got right in.","Guan Wenjun: \"???\"","Guan Wenjun turned to stare at her. Two seconds later, he pushed his sunglasses up onto his head, stared at Qiao Lanshu, and even winked at her: \"Oh, Comrade Xiao Qiao, as soon as your Lao Qin leaves, you come looking for me. Isn't this a bit inappropriate?\"","As he spoke, he said gleefully, \"How about it? Do you think I'm better after all, and Lao Qin is unreliable?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","This guy, Guan Wenjun, was quite cowardly in front of Qin Yuanzheng, probably because he thought he couldn't beat Qin Yuanzheng in a fight.","But in front of Qiao Lanshu, he was rather cheeky, as if he would feel uncomfortable if he didn't say a few glib and flirtatious words.","Qiao Lanshu automatically ignored his nonsense and asked, \"Director Guan, carrying a bag this early in the morning, are you going on a long trip?\"","She had actually come to find Guan Wenjun to ask him about Qin Yuanzheng.","She felt that Guan Wenjun should know something about the mission.","Although she also knew that even if Guan Wenjun told her about this mission, or if he told her that Qin Yuanzheng would be fine and she shouldn't worry...","She would still worry.","She simply couldn't set her mind at ease.","Even though her original intention in coming to find Guan Wenjun was to seek some peace of mind.","Qiao Lanshu looked at Guan Wenjun: \"Wasn't the recent case of Liu Zhengxing and his son handed over to the revolutionary committee and the public security bureau for a joint investigation? You are so busy, why are you suddenly leaving? Are you going home for the New Year?\"","Guan Wenjun said somewhat smugly, \"The case of Liu Zhengxing and his son was wrapped up a long time ago. My trip this time is because I received a new mission.\"","Qiao Lanshu's heart stirred, and she tried to trick him into revealing the truth: \"You're going to assist Brother Zheng with his case, aren't you?\"","Guan Wenjun was surprised. He looked at Qiao Lanshu and blurted out, \"How did you know? Damn, Qin Yuanzheng even told you this? This is classified! Classified!\"","There were a total of three groups of people going to execute the mission this time.","Qin Yuanzheng was in the dark, and Si Zhemao was in the open. The two of them were cooperating and had already set off last night.","Guan Wenjun was to assist them, going to the mountain village over there to stay for a few days and wait for an opportunity to act, which could also be considered a hidden chess piece.","He was like a brick, moved to wherever he was needed.","Therefore, he also got himself a temporary identity. His current identity was a forestry administrator from a certain town in a certain county. This time, he was going to a mountain village forestry farm for a study exchange, and also to look for some drought-tolerant and cold-resistant tree, flower, and medicinal seedlings to bring back for cultivation and planting.","This kind of work exchange happened frequently.","So his temporary identity wouldn't arouse any suspicion, and it would give him the perfect excuse to stay there for a few days, waiting for the right moment to act.","This mission was very important to him.","It was rare for him to receive a mission with such a good opportunity to earn merits.","As long as he completed the mission and earned a merit, his status and position could be elevated. By then, he might even be transferred to the Public Security Bureau or the Labor Bureau. He wouldn't have to stay in the Revolutionary Committee anymore, worrying every day about having nowhere to go in the future.","Qiao Lanshu looked at Guan Wenjun's expression and said thoughtfully, \"I really guessed it right. You are indeed going too.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun glared at Qiao Lanshu and said in disbelief, \"Wait, you tricked me again?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled, looked at Guan Wenjun, and said, \"Director Guan, why don't you take me with you this time? I'm worried about Brother Zheng...\"","Guan Wenjun immediately said, \"No way!\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly added, \"I promise I won't interfere with your work. Once we get there, you can just do your own thing. I'll stay at the guesthouse and I promise not to run around.\"","Guan Wenjun retorted, \"You're a female comrade, what are you going there for? Even if you stay in the guesthouse, you won't be able to see Qin Yuanzheng. It doesn't make much difference whether you go or not.\"","Qiao Lanshu certainly knew she wouldn't be able to see Qin Yuanzheng, but she just wanted to be closer to him. In case an explosion really happened...","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"I suspect this mission is very dangerous. There might be explosives or something over there. I'm worried.\"","Guan Wenjun nodded. \"That is indeed a possibility. After all, even the state-run restaurant was planted with explosives. What else is impossible?\"","He added, \"I'm going over there as a forestry administrator for a work exchange this time. I'm afraid I won't have time to take care of you.\"","Qiao Lanshu replied, \"Then I'll go work at the forestry farm and do your job for you. You can use your time to assist them. Wouldn't that be better?\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun still shook his head. \"No, if I really take you with me, won't Qin Yuanzheng kill me when he gets back? No, absolutely not.\"","Qiao Lanshu was somewhat disappointed.","She sat there in silence for a long time.","Regarding the mission Qin Yuanzheng carried out in her previous life, he had never gone into detail.","So she didn't know exactly which mission it was that left him injured.","What if it was this one? What would she do? She definitely wouldn't be able to handle it.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu remain silent for so long, Guan Wenjun hurriedly comforted her, \"I say, you don't need to be so clingy. Lao Qin is just going to carry out a mission. He'll definitely be back in a few days, so stop worrying.\"","Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but worry, but she couldn't say what was on her mind.","In her previous life, Qin Yuanzheng had only revealed that during that mission, he was injured by an explosion while trying to save someone, but that person wasn't worth saving.","That was all Qiao Lanshu knew, which made her even more anxious to get over there.","She looked at Guan Wenjun and said, \"Director Guan, if you don't take me with you, I'm going to report you for leaking classified information.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun said in disbelief, \"You can't be serious, Comrade Qiao Lanshu. We have no grudges against each other, so why are you trying to ruin me like this!\"","Qiao Lanshu said with a solemn face, \"Just take me with you. I promise I won't hold you back. I'll stay obediently in the forestry farm dormitory and do your work for you every day. You won't have to worry about the job and can focus entirely on your investigation.\"","Adding to that, Qiao Lanshu said, \"I can act as your secretary, no one will suspect a thing.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun: \"My cover identity is a grassroots clerk. I don't have a secretary.\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at him and offered another idea. \"Then I'll be your wife. We are a married couple, and I'm accompanying you on your business trip this time. Wouldn't that be even more reasonable?\"","Hearing her say this, Guan Wenjun's ears instantly turned red. He said somewhat bashfully, \"You're my, my, wi-wife?\"","Qiao Lanshu stared at him. \"Pretend, do you understand? We'll pretend to be husband and wife going to the forestry farm together for the work exchange. This way, our credibility will be higher, and it will arouse less suspicion than if you went alone.\"","For a young man like Guan Wenjun to drive over for a work exchange, it would inevitably put people on guard.","After all, he was young, tall, and highly skilled, having come from the military. His demeanor in every gesture could easily make people suspicious.","But if he brought his wife along, it wouldn't raise any eyebrows.","After all, no one goes to catch spies with a delicate little wife in tow.","Si Zhemao had already gone ahead to draw their fire, so if Guan Wenjun went over with his wife, he might actually be able to carry out his work more smoothly.","The desire to earn merits gained the upper hand.","Guan Wenjun started the car and drove off. He said, \"Alright, I'll take you, but don't run around, you hear me?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"I know. I'll stay at the forestry farm. I promise I won't go anywhere.\"","In her heart, she was wondering who exactly the person Qin Yuanzheng said he shouldn't have saved could be.","Without knowing anything clearly, would she be able to change the outcome of this event?","She actually had no idea, but since she had been reborn, she had to go and see for herself. Otherwise, if Qin Yuanzheng got injured in an explosion again just to save someone, she would never be able to forgive herself for the rest of her life.","As he drove, Guan Wenjun asked, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, do you need to go back and pack your things?\"","Qiao Lanshu was afraid Guan Wenjun would change his mind. After all, he was a very impulsive person and easily persuaded.","But he was also very fickle. Even though he had agreed now, what if he came to his senses in a little while and backed out?","So Qiao Lanshu said, \"I don't need to bring anything. I have money and ration coupons on me. Whatever I lack, I can just buy at the supply and marketing cooperative over there.\"","Guan Wenjun nodded. \"Alright then, it's getting late, so let's head out directly.\"","Qiao Lanshu was right. Guan Wenjun indeed regretted his decision very quickly.","Just after leaving Longcheng and getting onto the national highway, he suddenly slowed the car down and said hesitantly, \"Xiao Qiao, aren't you pregnant? How about you stay home instead? We have female comrades at our cooperative too; I could just find one of them to pretend to be my wife.\"","Qiao Lanshu knew Guan Wenjun would pull something like this.","Sitting in the passenger seat, she said expressionlessly, \"Sure, then drop me off at the headquarters building. I'm going to report you for leaking military secrets.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun felt that he must have offended Qiao Lanshu in his past life.","Otherwise, why was he always being manipulated by her in this life?"]},{"number":160,"title":"Chapter 160: Forest Farm","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun had no choice. They were about to leave Dragon City, and he couldn't possibly send Qiao Lanshu back now.","Not to mention the wasted time, if Qiao Lanshu really reported him, even if he achieved something great on this trip, it wouldn't be called earning merit—it would be called atoning for his crimes.","Guan Wenjun parked in a county town on the outskirts of Dragon City. Qiao Lanshu shot him a wary look and asked, \"What, you're not planning to just dump me here, are you?\"","Guan Wenjun was truly afraid of her. He said, \"How could I dare? If I left you here, Qin Yuanzheng would hack me to death with a knife.\"","Even though taking Qiao Lanshu along on a mission meant Qin Yuanzheng would still want to hack him to death when he got back.","Guan Wenjun was no longer sure which would result in a more gruesome death: sending Qiao Lanshu back, or dragging her along on the mission.","Since he was damned if he did and damned if he didn't, he made up his mind to take Qiao Lanshu with him. If he managed to earn some merit, it would be a major milestone in his life!","As for Qin Yuanzheng, the man was whipped anyway. As long as Qiao Lanshu didn't blame him, he would be fine.","Guan Wenjun said to Qiao Lanshu, \"You haven't told anyone at the base that you're leaving, right? If the logistics department can't find you, won't that be a lot of trouble? I'll go ask the county revolutionary committee to make a trip into the city and deliver a message to the food factory and the logistics department, telling them you've gone out of town with me.\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu finally breathed a sigh of relief. She looked at Guan Wenjun with a beaming smile and said, \"Director Guan, you really are thoughtful. You're amazing.\"","With that, she even gave Guan Wenjun a thumbs-up.","Guan Wenjun was speechless.","Standing by the car, Guan Wenjun reached up to smooth his hair, fighting back a wildly twitching smile, and said, \"Not at all, I'm just averagely amazing.\"","Saying so, he stuffed his hands into his pockets and strolled into the county revolutionary committee's office.","Qiao Lanshu stayed in the car to wait for him.","Guan Wenjun jogged into the revolutionary committee looking radiant. After asking them to deliver the message to Dragon City and arranging a few work matters, he came back out and hit the road again with Qiao Lanshu.","Their destination was several dozen kilometers away from Dragon City. Since it was a small town, they had to take mountain roads.","Cars in this era didn't have heating, so it was freezing inside. Fortunately, Qiao Lanshu had dressed warmly before leaving. She wore thick fleece-lined snow boots, a cotton hat on her head, and a scarf wrapped around her neck. With her hands shoved deep into her pockets, she stared silently at the scenery outside the window.","The mountains in the north were different from those in the south.","Southern mountains were always lush and green, with white mist coiling through the peaks, possessing a hazy, graceful beauty.","But the northern mountains stretched on for thousands of miles, scarred everywhere by deep ravines.","In winter, the mountains were incredibly desolate, presenting a vast, grayish expanse as far as the eye could see.","Dry and bleak, with the north wind howling, unthawed snow lay piled up all throughout the ranges.","From a distance, it looked like an ink wash painting composed of black, gray, and white, completely devoid of green.","Sitting in the car, Qiao Lanshu looked at the endless mountains outside the window and wondered if Qin Yuanzheng was also somewhere in these mountains.","In mountains like these, it shouldn't be easy to stay hidden, right?","How was he carrying out his mission? How were his enemies hiding? Would there be explosives in the mountains?","If explosives went off, would it trigger a landslide?","Guan Wenjun glanced at her and asked, \"What are you thinking about? Why so quiet?\"","Qiao Lanshu was in a bad mood and didn't want to talk.","She told him, \"Don't talk while driving. The mountain roads are treacherous, you need to watch the road.\"","Guan Wenjun was speechless again.","This woman had been plenty talkative when she was clinging to him earlier.","And now that she didn't want to deal with him, she still had a sharp tongue.","Guan Wenjun grabbed a canteen and handed it to her. \"You must be cold. Have some hot water.\"","Qiao Lanshu had indeed left in a hurry this time and brought absolutely nothing with her.","Unlike Guan Wenjun, who was the type of person who never let himself suffer.","So when he went out, he brought everything, even filling two canteens with hot water.","Qiao Lanshu took the military canteen and glanced at it.","Guan Wenjun clicked his tongue and said, \"I just washed it yesterday, and I haven't used it yet. Don't worry, it's clean.\"","He added, \"I filled two canteens for this trip, so you can just use this one.\"","Hearing him say that, Qiao Lanshu finally twisted off the cap.","Guan Wenjun was speechless once more.","He knew he was being disdained, and felt a twinge of sourness in his heart.","After taking a sip of the hot water, Qiao Lanshu asked him, \"Do we have any information on the target for this mission? What kind of person are they?\"","At the mention of this, Guan Wenjun's expression turned serious. He said, \"We don't know much, because Liu Zhengxing didn't know their identity either.\"","He paused mid-sentence, turned to glare at Qiao Lanshu, and said, \"Are you trying to fish for information again? Comrade Qiao Lanshu, you are too wicked.\"","Qiao Lanshu remained silent.","Guan Wenjun stated with a deadpan expression, \"From now on, I'm not telling you anything!\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","\"Fine,\" she said. \"Then just focus on driving.\"","She sighed silently in her heart, dug a fruit drop out of her pocket, unwrapped it, and popped it into her mouth.","The mountain roads were rough, and it wasn't until a little past one in the afternoon that they finally reached their destination: a place called Longxing Town.","The town wasn't large, with a population of twenty thousand at most, though it oversaw a dozen or so villages whose exact populations were unknown.","Guan Wenjun's main destination this time was a place called Quanan Village. It was the largest village in the town, and the local forestry station was located there.","Coming all this way, Guan Wenjun originally wanted to use a cover identity from a school or some other department.","However, Quanan Village didn't even have a school; the children all went to the town to study.","So, he had no choice but to go with the forestry station.","He took Qiao Lanshu to the town's supply and marketing cooperative to buy some flatbreads and steamed buns for rations, which they ate with hot water upon returning.","Then, he parked the car in the playground of the town's school and took Qiao Lanshu to ride an ox cart heading into the village.","He whispered to Qiao Lanshu, \"We can't drive into the village, it's too conspicuous. You'll just have to rough it a bit and take the ox cart.\"","Qiao Lanshu sat on the ox cart with him. The local's cart was loaded with some grain and hay. He was the production brigade captain from the village, who happened to be in town gathering supplies, so the town mayor arranged for him to take the two of them into the village.","This Captain Niu asked Guan Wenjun, \"Comrades, where are you folks coming from?\"","Guan Wenjun replied, \"We're from Li County.\"","Captain Niu immediately said, \"Oh my, so you're from the county town! I was just thinking your accent didn't sound local.\"","Captain Niu asked, \"What brings you young couple to Quanan Village?\"","Hearing this, Guan Wenjun looked a bit embarrassed.","He said coyly, \"I'm here to work at the forestry station. My wi... my wife here, she hasn't traveled far before, so I brought her along to have a look around.\"","As he said this, Guan Wenjun actually looked bashful, acting like a shy young bride himself.","Qiao Lanshu wrapped a scarf around half of her face, leaving only her dark eyes exposed. She stared at Guan Wenjun curiously several times.","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Captain Niu, hearing that he was here to work at the forestry farm, enthusiastically introduced the team's forestry farm to him for quite a while.","Upon arriving at the village entrance, Captain Niu took them directly to the forestry farm and handed them over to the farm's ranger.","The forestry farm was massive, employing four or five rangers.","The ranger in charge of receiving Guan Wenjun was quite young and surnamed Zhou. Ranger Zhou smiled, shook Guan Wenjun's hand, and said, \"Comrade Guan, the long journey must have been exhausting, right?\"","Guan Wenjun glanced at Qiao Lanshu and replied, \"I'm alright, but my wife is tired.\"","Ranger Zhou immediately looked at Qiao Lanshu and said, \"Our forestry farm has dormitories. I've already cleaned a room for you. I'll take you there to rest now. By the way, have you eaten?\"","Guan Wenjun nodded. \"We've eaten.\"","Ranger Zhou said, \"Our forestry farm has few people, so we don't have a cafeteria. We usually cook for ourselves. I've prepared some ingredients in your room, so you'll have to cook your own meals for the next few days.\"","Guan Wenjun nodded, wondering what to do since he didn't know how to cook.","Ranger Zhou continued, \"We have five rangers at the forestry farm. Two have already taken early leave to go home for the New Year. Including me, there are three of us on duty for the Spring Festival. You can just coordinate with me for the next few days. As for the other rangers...\"","He paused and lowered his voice, \"Some of the rangers here have been in the mountains for so long that their tempers have grown a bit eccentric. If you need anything, just come to me.\"","Guan Wenjun nodded. \"Alright, then we'll go take a look at the forestry farm this afternoon.\"","Ranger Zhou added a warning, \"We keep dogs at the forestry farm. They're raised by the veteran staff to patrol the mountains and hunt. When you want to go into the mountains, let me know in advance. Whatever you do, don't go into the mountains by yourselves. Those wolfdogs bite.\"","Guan Wenjun frowned slightly and asked in a low voice, \"How can the dogs raised by the forestry farm bite people? What if the villagers go in?\"","Ranger Zhou smiled and said, \"Don't worry, everyone in the village knows there are dogs in the forestry farm. Under normal circumstances, no one goes into the mountains.\"","As they spoke, Ranger Zhou led them to a row of low houses at the entrance of the forestry farm. He said, \"Here we are. These are our dormitories.\"","This row of dormitories had been renovated in recent years; previously, they were so dilapidated that they were uninhabitable.","Because many educated youths had come to help with construction in recent years, the village had completely run out of living space, so the production brigade brought people to specifically repair the houses.","Ranger Zhou wasn't a local either. He was an educated youth from the city who had been assigned to the forestry farm and had been here for three or four years.","He looked at Guan Wenjun with some envy, asking how he got his job in the city, and remarked how great it was that neither husband nor wife had to be sent down to the countryside.","Guan Wenjun chatted with him for a while. Upon reaching the dormitory area, Ranger Zhou handed Guan Wenjun a key and said, \"This room belongs to a previous ranger who went home for the New Year. You can stay here for the next few days. I'll come find you at two o'clock this afternoon.\"","Guan Wenjun nodded and led Qiao Lanshu into the room.","The room indeed showed signs of being lived in. It had a table, two chairs, and a heated kang bed. The kang was fired up, making the room cozy and warm, though there were no sheets or bedding on it. Fortunately, Guan Wenjun had brought his own bedsheets. He spread the sheet over the kang and said to Qiao Lanshu:","\"There are no quilts here. I'll ask around the village later and borrow one for you.\"","The conditions at the forestry farm were truly harsh. It was nothing to Guan Wenjun, but he worried that Qiao Lanshu wouldn't be used to it.","Qiao Lanshu sat on the kang, looking around at the room's environment.","The windows were sealed, but they still let in drafts.","The door was a plain wooden board with a latch. There were rooms on both sides, though they were currently unoccupied.","Ranger Zhou lived in the room at the very end, not far from them.","Guan Wenjun brought his luggage bag over and took out a change of clothes, some daily necessities, as well as some biscuits and flatbreads.","He placed two thermoses side by side on the table and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"How about it, regretting it now? I told you we were coming to the village to work. The conditions here can't compare to the city. Since you grew up in the city, you definitely can't stand this, right?\"","Qiao Lanshu was indeed a bit unaccustomed to it, but her mind wasn't on these things right now.","She whispered to Guan Wenjun, \"Is this it? Our destination?\"","Guan Wenjun lowered his voice and said, \"Roughly in this village. They are probably here too, but we won't be able to meet them.\"","The they he referred to, of course, meant Qin Yuanzheng and Si Zhemao.","They had arrived a night earlier than Guan Wenjun and Qiao Lanshu, and it was unknown if they had made any progress.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"Why would the forestry farm keep wolfdogs, especially ones that bite? It's so dangerous; does the brigade allow it?\"","Guan Wenjun scratched his head and said, \"Don't be so paranoid, seeing something wrong with everything. The rangers at the forestry farm often have to patrol the mountains, and there are many venomous insects and wild beasts out there. Keeping dogs is for survival, which is permitted.\"","Qiao Lanshu remained silent for a moment before saying, \"But if everyone knows there are wolfdogs in the mountains that bite, then no one will dare to go in. If someone were doing something in the mountains, wouldn't it go completely unnoticed?\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun fell silent for a while before saying, \"This afternoon, I'll have Ranger Zhou take me into the mountains. I'll go have a look.\"","He then added to Qiao Lanshu, \"You stay in the dormitory by yourself, and don't go running around.\"","Qiao Lanshu said, \"I can take a walk around the village, right? I already met Captain Niu just now, didn't he say I could go look around the village?\"","Their forestry farm dormitory was right at the village entrance. Stepping out of the dormitory and walking forward just a dozen meters or so would bring you into the village.","With several hundred people, it was a large village.","The production brigade here mainly grew sorghum, wheat, and corn.","There were also jujube and pear orchards in the mountains, with pretty decent yields.","However, with so many people in the village, finding someone hiding here would not be easy.","Moreover, there were many surrounding villages. If their target wasn't in this village, their efforts this time would be entirely in vain.","Guan Wenjun said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Don't go off on your own. You stick with me; wherever I go, you follow. How about this: you come with me to look around the forestry farm this afternoon, and tomorrow we'll both head into the village together.\""]},{"number":161,"title":"Chapter 161: Chased by a Dog","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu didn't say anything at this time; she just went along with whatever Guan Wenjun suggested.","She was simply worried about Qin Yuanzheng, and her heart was filled with a constant sense of unease.","She didn't know where this unease came from. Perhaps it was because she had dreamed of the scars on Qin Yuanzheng's back, or maybe because she had dreamed of him being injured in an explosion.","In short, she had spoken much less over the past two days, always maintaining a silent demeanor.","Guan Wenjun even felt embarrassed to joke around with her.","Ranger Zhou assumed they were a real married couple, so he had prepared a single room for them.","Qiao Lanshu sat in the room, and Guan Wenjun felt too awkward to go in. He asked, \"Are you hungry? Should I go start a fire and cook some food?\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at him curiously. \"You know how to cook?\"","Guan Wenjun immediately replied, \"No.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun scratched his head and said, \"Forget it, I don't know how to start a fire either. Let's just eat whatever and get through these next few days.\"","Close the case early, go back early.","Guan Wenjun was anxious to start investigating the case.","Qiao Lanshu held a dry flatbread and ate it slowly.","She knew how to build a fire and cook, but she wasn't in the mood right now. She would just cook dinner later tonight.","Right now, she wanted to take a walk around the village.","She wondered where Qin Yuanzheng was at this very moment.","Si Zhemao was probably at the town police station.","Guan Wenjun went out to find Ranger Zhou, and the two of them chatted about the forestry farm and the village.","Seeing that it was about time, Ranger Zhou said, \"Let's go. I'll take you for a walk around the forestry farm.\"","Guan Wenjun went to call Qiao Lanshu. Holding a notebook and pen, and wearing gloves, Qiao Lanshu followed behind Guan Wenjun.","Ranger Zhou led them up the mountain along a small path to patrol their section of the forestry farm.","Ranger Zhou said, \"Our area here is large. Several mountains are connected. There are jujube and pear orchards nearby, which are also under our management. There are hundreds of medicinal herbs in the mountains, mostly wild. Ordinary people aren't allowed to come in and pick them, and we usually don't go over there much if there's nothing going on.\"","Guan Wenjun nodded. \"It's winter now, so there shouldn't be much to do in the mountains, right?\"","Ranger Zhou replied, \"Not much. Mainly collecting firewood. The village doesn't have enough coal, so most villagers still have to use firewood to heat their brick beds.\"","Since Guan Wenjun's stated purpose for coming here was to look for fruit saplings, tree saplings, and medicinal herb seedlings, Ranger Zhou specifically took him around those areas.","The mountains were too vast, and the temperature dropped sharply in the afternoon, making it very cold.","So they only wandered around the mountains for two hours before preparing to head back out.","Qiao Lanshu walked slowly, observing her surroundings as she went. Guan Wenjun also slowed his pace to wait for her.","Ranger Zhou said enviously, \"Comrade Guan, you and your wife are so affectionate. Do you have children yet?\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun glanced at Qiao Lanshu awkwardly, only to find her expressionless, showing absolutely no reaction to those words.","Sometimes, Guan Wenjun truly admired Qiao Lanshu's psychological fortitude.","She didn't react to this at all.","Guan Wenjun and Ranger Zhou talked for a while about marriage, children, and love.","One guy who had been single since birth imparted dating advice to another guy who had been single since birth, complaining about the hardships of marriage, throwing in a comment about how hard it is to raise kids, and finally summarizing: Life is too hard, men suffer too much, taking a wife is fine, but don't have kids lightly!","Ranger Zhou nodded continuously. \"Comrade Guan seems very experienced. Comrade Guan sees things very clearly. I envy your happy marriage and family, and that you have something to look forward to in life.\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at Guan Wenjun, then at Ranger Zhou, not knowing what expression to make.","She really hadn't expected this guy, Guan Wenjun, to have such a flair for the dramatic.","Seeing that it was getting late, Ranger Zhou said, \"It's getting late. Let's head down the mountain now. Otherwise, it'll get really cold once it gets dark, and the road will be hard to walk on.\"","They needed to hurry down the mountain and back to the dorms while the sun was still up.","Guan Wenjun nodded. \"Alright, we'll come back tomorrow.\"","As the three of them were preparing to head down, Qiao Lanshu suddenly asked, \"Comrade Zhou, didn't you say there were wolfdogs raised in the mountains and other rangers around? How come we didn't see them on our way up?\"","Ranger Zhou quickly replied, \"Our veteran employees all live in the mountains over by the orchards. There are wooden cabins there specifically for the forest rangers to live in, and the wolfdogs are over there too.\"","Qiao Lanshu asked curiously, \"Do the rangers live there all the time? Do you guys rotate shifts? How many dogs do you have?\"","Ranger Zhou: \"Usually we don't rotate shifts. Each of us has our own designated area of responsibility. Plus, those two dogs have always been kept over there and they only recognize certain people. Even I don't dare to go over there.\"","Even though the dogs were tied up, they were very vicious. Probably because they often hunted for food in the mountains, they had a ferocious nature.","Ranger Zhou was just an educated youth sent down to the countryside. He only wanted to do his job peacefully and didn't want to risk his life.","After all, he still wanted to return to the city. If he got bitten by a dog here, it would be a huge trouble.","After all, this mountain village didn't even have a clinic.","When villagers got sick, apart from toughing it out or looking for herbs in the mountains, their only option was to go to the town clinic. It took over an hour just to get there by ox cart, which was too far.","Qiao Lanshu looked in the direction Ranger Zhou was pointing.","That orchard was on another mountain peak. They couldn't get there from here; they would have to detour along a mountain road. A round trip would take even longer.","So Qiao Lanshu didn't say anything more and went back with Guan Wenjun.","Upon returning to the dormitory area, Ranger Zhou and Guan Wenjun chatted a bit about the medicinal seedlings and tree saplings.","Guan Wenjun actually didn't understand any of this; he was just biting the bullet and talking about work with Ranger Zhou.","After talking about work, Ranger Zhou said it was getting late and he needed to cook. He took the opportunity to invite Guan Wenjun and his wife to eat with him, saying he would boil some noodles.","Guan Wenjun didn't refuse, since he didn't know how to cook.","While Ranger Zhou went to his own dorm to cook, Guan Wenjun asked Qiao Lanshu in a low voice, \"What's wrong? Did you discover something?\"","Qiao Lanshu looked toward the mountains and whispered, \"I think you should take a walk over to the orchard. Who knows, there might be some unexpected discoveries over there.\"","Guan Wenjun was speechless. \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, are you trying to get me killed? There are dogs over there that bite!\"","Qiao Lanshu advised him in a low voice, \"It's exactly because there are dogs that you have to go take a look. Think about it, if the other party didn't have a guilty conscience, why would they keep dogs?\"","Guan Wenjun: \"To guard the door and protect themselves, obviously. You have no idea how dangerous it is in these mountains.\"","Qiao Lanshu just looked at him, not speaking for a good while.","Guan Wenjun immediately said, \"Don't go calling me useless again. I'm not being useless, I'm doing rational analysis!\"","Qiao Lanshu gave him a silent look, then simply replied with an \"Oh.\" She lowered her head, went back into the room, grabbed a thermos, and walked toward Ranger Zhou's room.","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun followed behind her. \"Wait, what do you mean, 'Oh'? Do you not believe what I'm saying?\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't make a sound. Pretending not to hear him, she walked straight into Ranger Zhou's room.","And saw Ranger Zhou inside cooking.","By the window in the room was a stove with two pots on it. One was used for steaming buns, and the smaller one for boiling noodles.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu come in, he smiled and said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, are you hungry? I steamed some multigrain buns, they'll be ready to eat in a bit.\"","Guan Wenjuan was here on a business trip, so the forestry center was responsible for his accommodation and meals.","Ranger Zhou had already gone to collect their grain rations, so he made the buns, bought the noodles, and also brought back some cabbage and radishes.","Qiao Lanshu asked him, \"Do you need any help?\"","Ranger Zhou quickly replied, \"No need, I'm almost done.\"","He made sour soup noodles and steamed a pot of multigrain buns. This would be the dinner for the three of them.","The sour soup noodles had wood ear mushrooms and cabbage in them, and they tasted pretty good.","Ranger Zhou didn't know how to cook anything else; he could only make these simplest of dishes.","After the three of them finished eating, it was getting late. Guan Wenjuan followed Qiao Lanshu back to their room.","He said to Qiao Lanshu, \"It's too cold today, I can't sleep on the floor. I'll go next door and squeeze in with Xiao Zhou. You sleep here by yourself.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, still not speaking to him.","Guan Wenjuan scratched his head, sighed, and went next door to Xiao Zhou's place.","Xiao Zhou was a bit surprised to see him. \"Comrade Guan, why did you come over?\"","Guan Wenjuan sighed and said with a solemn face, \"My wife is at odds with me. I'm telling you, women are just difficult. They get angry over nothing. If I could do it all over again, I definitely wouldn't marry her!\"","Ranger Zhou was speechless.","Ranger Zhou felt that Comrade Xiao Qiao had a pretty good temper and was quite easy to talk to.","He figured Guan Wenjuan must have been the one to make her angry, but he was too polite to say it out loud.","That night, the two grown men squeezed together on the same heated brick bed.","Qiao Lanshu didn't bother about Guan Wenjuan. She couldn't sleep either, so she lit an oil lamp and sat on her bed, suffering from insomnia.","...","The next morning, Qiao Lanshu came out of the room. She didn't see Ranger Zhou, nor did she see Guan Wenjuan.","Strange, where did Guan Wenjuan go? He didn't even tell her.","Qiao Lanshu wandered around the dormitory area. Just as she was looking toward the entrance of the forestry center, she suddenly heard a commotion coming from the mountains, followed by the increasingly fierce barking of dogs.","Qiao Lanshu was startled.","Qiao Lanshu quickly stepped back. She originally wanted to retreat to her own room, but after a moment's thought, she turned and ran into Ranger Zhou's room.","Ranger Zhou's dormitory door wasn't locked; it pushed open easily.","Xiao Zhou probably left it unlocked in case Qiao Lanshu needed to cook or boil water.","This made things convenient for Qiao Lanshu.","When she had come in earlier, she had noticed a hunting rifle hanging on the wall. She happened to know how to use it.","Qiao Lanshu came out holding the gun. In the distance, on the mountain path of the forestry center, she saw a man holding a stick, swinging it backward while running for his life.","Behind him, four or five dogs were in hot pursuit.","Guan Wenjuan had never been in such a sorry state. From childhood to adulthood, he had never been chased by dogs.","Now, having traveled all the way to this mountain village, he was finally experiencing it.","Four or five fierce wolfhounds were snapping at his heels.","As luck would have it, Director Guan, who usually carried a pistol with him, had disguised himself as a grassroots cadre this time and was unarmed.","He could only use a long stick to scare the dogs while running madly down the mountain.","Guan Wenjuan was panting heavily; he had never run this fast in his life.","He suddenly felt as if he had awakened a hidden athletic talent and could represent his country across the ocean at the Olympic Games.","Even at a time like this, he was still thinking to himself that if he won an Olympic gold medal, he could leap from being a universally despised Revolutionary Committee director to a national hero.","Then, would he still need to worry about not being able to change jobs or join the organization?","Guan Wenjuan shouted at the top of his lungs, \"Help! The dogs are eating me!\"","Just then, a loud bang rang out.","Startled by the gunshot, Guan Wenjuan stumbled and fell flat on his face.","The wolfhounds chasing him came to a sudden halt. They froze in place, ears pricked up, looking in terror toward the source of the gunshot.","Qiao Lanshu was crouching on the roof of the forestry center dormitory, watching the fierce wolfhounds on the mountain path. She aimed the hunting rifle diagonally at the sky and fired another shot with a loud bang.","The dogs jumped in fright, their fur standing on end. Tucking their tails between their legs, they turned and fled quickly into the forest. In no time, the large wolfhounds vanished without a trace.","Only then did Guan Wenjuan scramble up from the ground.","He had scraped his left leg on a rock when he fell, and it hurt like crazy.","He brushed the grass clippings off his clothes, shook his messy hair, and limped back in a completely disheveled state.","Afraid that the wolfhounds might return, Qiao Lanshu remained crouched on the roof, still clutching the hunting rifle.","She looked at Guan Wenjuan and shouted, \"What happened? Didn't Xiao Zhou go with you?\"","Guan Wenjuan was furious. Standing below, he looked up at Qiao Lanshu, pointed at her, and said, \"You tell me what happened! Weren't you the one who told me to go to the orchard?\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Guan Wenjuan's handsome image was completely ruined.","At this moment, he looked utterly pathetic, even worse off than the dogs from earlier.","He sat dejectedly on the front steps, rubbing his left leg and grimacing in pain.","Qiao Lanshu quickly climbed down the nearby ladder, still holding the gun. She walked over to Guan Wenjuan and asked in a low voice, \"Where is Xiao Zhou?\"","Guan Wenjuan replied, \"He went to town to run some errands. I sneaked in by myself...\"","Qiao Lanshu asked quietly, \"And? Did you see that old employee? Is there anything strange about that house?\"","This was another reason why Guan Wenjuan was so annoyed.","He said, \"I had just gotten near the place and only saw a wooden cabin from a distance. Before I could even get closer, those dogs spotted me. Those dogs are truly vicious. They chase people like crazy, it was terrifying.\"","He almost thought he was going to be bitten to death just now.","He was still shuddering at the thought.","Qiao Lanshu sat down next to him and lowered her voice, \"Didn't they say there was only one dog? Why are there five? Are they really allowed to keep so many dogs?\"","Guan Wenjuan was equally puzzled. \"That Xiao Zhou didn't tell the truth. Damn it, he almost got me killed!\"","As he spoke, he suddenly noticed the gun in Qiao Lanshu's arms.","He quickly reached over, pushed the barrel of the gun toward the ground, and glared at her. \"Where did you get that gun? Do you even know how to use it? That thing is dangerous!\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Guan Wenjuan had clearly been scared silly, completely forgetting how he had just been saved."]},{"number":162,"title":"Chapter 162: Gunshots in the Night","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun originally had no intention of going to the orchard in the mountains.","But if he did not go, Comrade Xiao Qiao would probably secretly curse him for being useless in her heart.","He had not slept well last night, constantly feeling that Qiao Lanshu was comparing him to Qin Yuanzheng in her mind. Qin Yuanzheng was so capable, while he was so useless.","No wonder his former partner had abandoned him and chosen Qin Yuanzheng instead.","He deserved to be dumped!","The more Guan Wenjun thought about it, the more indignant he became.","He had to prove that he was no worse than Qin Yuanzheng!","So when he got up the next day, since Ranger Zhou happened to be heading to the supply and marketing cooperative in town for errands, he went into the mountains all by himself.","After all, Ranger Zhou had taken him wandering around the mountains yesterday, and the people from the forestry center and the production team all knew he was here on a business trip.","He figured it would not be a big deal.","As a result, just as he reached the entrance of the orchard and took a distant glance at the wooden cabin where the forest ranger lived, he heard the barking of dogs.","He initially thought there was only one dog, so there was no need to worry too much.","However, in less than a minute, four or five dogs were barking and chasing after him in his direction.","Terrified, Guan Wenjun turned around and ran.","Fortunately, he ran fast and was half a mountain away from the dogs, otherwise, he would have been tackled by them before he could even make it down the mountain.","Guan Wenjun said to Qiao Lanshu, We cannot go into that orchard. It is too dangerous. Those dogs did not look right; they were incredibly fierce.","Qiao Lanshu sat there, also feeling a bit troubled.","She wondered if Qin Yuanzheng and Si Zhemao had made any progress on their end.","Guan Wenjun sat there to catch his breath for a while, then muttered, I will have Xiao Zhou take me in again this afternoon to take a look. I do not believe it. Would those dogs bite Xiao Zhou too?","Qiao Lanshu was not very optimistic. Before seeing those dogs, she had only been somewhat suspicious.","But now, she felt that something was definitely wrong with that orchard.","Even if the forest ranger inside was not a spy, he probably was not a good person either. Otherwise, what kind of forest ranger would break the rules to keep so many wolfhounds, especially at a forestry center?","What if they bit someone to death?","Having been chased by the dogs for so long, Guan Wenjun's legs were still like jelly. He said, No, I need to catch my breath. I need to go back to the room and rest for a bit.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","She felt that Guan Wenjun was really too delicate. To think that someone like him had previously said he wanted to join the public security bureau.","She thought Guan Wenjun was better suited for an office job, just sitting inside, drinking tea, and reading newspapers.","Joining the public security bureau? He would probably struggle just to catch a criminal.","Guan Wenjun rested in the room for a while and drank a large glass of water. He saw Qiao Lanshu sitting on the steps outside the door, lost in thought.","He walked back out and said to her, Let us go. We should take a walk around the village.","Qiao Lanshu glanced at him and asked, Have you recovered?","Guan Wenjun said stubbornly, Recover from what? I was just thirsty and had some water. It was just being chased by dogs for a bit, wasn't it? There is nothing to recover from.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless again.","The two of them walked together towards the village.","The village was actually quite large, with plenty of children and elderly people around.","Seeing strangers arrive, they all stared at the two of them with vigilance.","Guan Wenjun took Qiao Lanshu straight to the production brigade's office to find Captain Niu from before.","The captain showed them around the village, looking at the village's grain and medicinal herbs.","Guan Wenjun brought up the orchard in the forestry center and said he wanted to go take a look.","Captain Niu said, It is no problem if you want to go to the orchard, but I need to talk to Lao Wu in advance and have him tie up the dogs beforehand. How about this, we will go there tomorrow morning.","Guan Wenjun nodded and came back to whisper to Qiao Lanshu, I do not think there is any problem with that orchard. Captain Niu knows about Lao Wu keeping dogs, so it must be out in the open. I think you are overthinking it.","Qiao Lanshu also hoped she was overthinking it.","If that person was really hiding in the forestry center, were Qin Yuanzheng and Si Zhemao heading in the wrong direction?","She and Guan Wenjun had been at the forestry center for almost two days, yet they had not seen Si Zhemao come over, and no one knew where Qin Yuanzheng was hiding.","As for the explosion, there was no telling when it would happen.","Qiao Lanshu kept her heart in her throat, remaining very silent these past few days and hardly speaking.","The two of them wandered around the village, then ate at Captain Niu's house. Finally, with Guan Wenjun carrying a bag of medicinal seedlings and Qiao Lanshu holding a notebook with ten pages of notes, they walked together toward the forestry center's dormitory.","Even though they had come under disguised identities.","The work that needed to be done still had to be completed meticulously.","After all, the letter of introduction Guan Wenjun brought when he came out was issued by the South Suburb Forestry Center in Longcheng.","The garrison troops at the South Suburb Forestry Center, specifically Battalion Commander Zhao Jiannong, had told Guan Wenjun that he must complete the work and bring back some saplings and medicinal seedlings worth researching and planting.","If Qiao Lanshu had not accompanied him to help with the record-keeping, Guan Wenjun really would not have been able to handle it alone.","On their way back, it was already three or four in the afternoon.","Guan Wenjun comforted Qiao Lanshu in a low voice, saying, You do not need to worry too much. Lao Qin's abilities are unquestionable. He will definitely be fine.","Saying that, Guan Wenjun muttered softly again, Neither of them came here. Maybe this is not the target location...","At this moment, Qiao Lanshu nudged him with her elbow and made a hushing gesture.","Guan Wenjun paused and looked ahead.","He saw a man wearing a bamboo hat and a forest ranger's vest walking toward them on the mountain path ahead.","The man was somewhat thin, slightly hunched over, and looked to be in his forties or fifties. He was carrying a load of manure on a shoulder pole, walking along the mountain path toward the forestry center.","Qiao Lanshu and Guan Wenjun exchanged a glance, and both tacitly fell silent, saying nothing more.","The man carrying the load stopped to rest at the entrance of the forestry center. Seeing Guan Wenjun and Qiao Lanshu, he took the initiative to strike up a conversation, You must be the comrades from the forestry center who came for the exchange and study this time, right?","Guan Wenjun nodded. That is me. Are you the forest ranger?","The forest ranger nodded. Yes. My dogs did not bite you this morning, did they?","Guan Wenjun was speechless.","So this man was Lao Wu, the forest ranger who kept the dogs.","Lao Wu looked quite amiable and kept apologizing to Guan Wenjun, saying that he had been working in the orchard at the time and had not noticed anyone approaching. By the time he realized it, it was too late, and the dogs were already chasing Guan Wenjun all over the mountain.","To express his apologies, he even brought over a bag of dried dates and handed it to Guan Wenjun, telling him to take it back to eat.","Guan Wenjun declined, but the man insisted on pressing it into his hands.","In the end, he came away holding a bag of dried dates, and Lao Wu carried his manure back into the mountains.","Guan Wenjun and Qiao Lanshu exchanged a glance, both feeling a bit deflated.","Guan Wenjun said in a low voice, This Lao Wu is actually quite a nice person. It seems we misunderstood him.","Qiao Lanshu nodded silently.","This Lao Wu looked just like Captain Niu and the other fellow villagers: kind, simple, and hardworking.","His local accent was also very heavy, and he did not seem to warrant any suspicion.","Guan Wenjun said in a low voice, \"I wonder how Lao Qin and the others are progressing with their investigation. If there's still no progress by tomorrow, we'll have to go to town and meet up with Si Zhemao.\"","If that happened, whether the matter succeeded or not, it would have nothing to do with Guan Wenjun anymore.","He had originally hoped to earn some merit, but now it seemed he just didn't have that kind of luck.","After the two returned to the dormitories, Xiao Zhou the ranger, who had gone to town on errands, also drove back on a tractor.","This tractor was used for hauling goods in the forestry center and was usually parked right at the entrance of the dormitory area.","Xiao Zhou the ranger got down from the tractor, carrying a bag of flour and some biscuits in his hands.","He had gone to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy food, since they had guests, after all.","Seeing Guan Wenjun and Qiao Lanshu, he immediately said, \"Comrade Guan, I heard you were chased by dogs when you went into the mountains this morning? Are you alright?\"","Guan Wenjun said, a bit embarrassed, \"Even you know about that?\"","He had thought Xiao Zhou wouldn't know. \"I'm fine. I just accidentally wandered into the orchard and got chased all the way back by dogs. But I wasn't hurt, so there's no need to worry.\"","Xiao Zhou finally breathed a sigh of relief and said with a smile, \"As long as you're not hurt. If you want to go to the orchard, I can take you there tomorrow. Oh, right, you two comrades, how about steamed buns for dinner tonight? I just bought some flour.\"","What else could Guan Wenjun say? He just followed along to help make the steamed buns.","That night, Guan Wenjun slept in Xiao Zhou's room next door, as usual.","Xiao Zhou was a bit speechless at the couple. He asked Guan Wenjun in a low voice, \"Comrade Guan, you guys are married, so why are you still sleeping in separate rooms?\"","In the darkness, Guan Wenjun said with a profound look on his face, \"You don't understand. A married man has to shoulder a lot of things.\"","As he spoke, he patted his shoulder and said, \"Heavier than a mountain, deeper than the ocean, understand?\"","Xiao Zhou: \"...\"","Was getting married really that heavy of a burden?","It was enough to make him afraid of marriage.","He had always thought that life with a wife would be pretty wonderful.","Finally, Guan Wenjun said with a profound expression, \"You'll understand when you get married.\"","He would understand that his and Comrade Xiao Qiao's relationship was not as simple as an ordinary married couple.","Guan Wenjun closed his eyes, tugged at Xiao Zhou the ranger's blanket, and comfortably went to sleep.","...","Meanwhile, at this very moment, Qiao Lanshu still couldn't fall asleep.","Ever since Qin Yuanzheng had left to carry out his mission, she hadn't slept well for three nights in a row.","As she lay on the kang, she suddenly heard a dog bark coming from the mountains.","She had heard dogs barking last night too, but that had come from the village, not the mountains.","This time, it came from the mountains, and it was very brief. The dog only barked twice before falling silent.","A bad premonition suddenly rose in Qiao Lanshu's heart.","Although she didn't know why, she trusted her instincts.","She quickly got off the kang, threw on her coat, and grabbed her hat and gloves.","Then, she blew out the oil lamp in the room.","The room was pitch black, and so was the courtyard. Because the dormitory area was located right at the foot of the mountain, the night winds were fierce.","She opened the door a crack and slipped out quietly. The howling mountain wind roared in her ears, and the sudden drop in night temperature chilled her to the bone.","Qiao Lanshu quickly closed the door, then circled around to the back of the house. She walked forward for a while before knocking on Guan Wenjun's window.","She knocked several times in a row until Guan Wenjun's vigilant voice rang out: \"Who is it?\"","Qiao Lanshu was just about to speak when she suddenly paused; Xiao Zhou the ranger was also in the room.","In a moment like this, where the enemy was in the dark and they were in the light, it was better to be careful with everything.","Thinking this, Qiao Lanshu knocked on the window twice more.","Then she turned and quietly ran back. Using a ladder, she climbed up onto the roof.","Afterward, she pulled the ladder up onto the roof and laid it flat, ensuring there were no ladders left around. Only then did she lie flat on the roof, put on her hat and gloves properly, and begin quietly pulling apart the dried grass on the roof.","The roof was covered with dried grass meant for insulation and windproofing.","She parted the dried grass and hid herself within it, not forgetting to press the ladder beneath her body.","After doing all this, she lay motionless. Despite the freezing weather, she was sweating all over from the tension.","She hoped she was just overthinking it, but she couldn't shake the feeling that the dog's bark just now was not right.","If something really was wrong, then Guan Wenjun would just have to fend for himself; she couldn't manage that much.","Actually, she could have hidden in the mountains, but the mountain paths were hard to navigate. If she fell into a pit, she would be in real trouble.","Moreover, there were dogs in the mountains, and dogs had a very keen sense of smell.","At least dogs couldn't fly; they couldn't get up onto the roof.","As Qiao Lanshu lay there, her mind drifted back to the gun from that afternoon.","Unfortunately, the hunting rifle from the afternoon wasn't in her hands; it was in Ranger Zhou's room.","Guan Wenjun hadn't been asleep to begin with; he had been thinking about this mission all along.","When he heard the window being knocked, he immediately threw on his coat and got off the kang.","And the first thing he did was grab the hunting rifle hanging on the wall.","Ranger Zhou hadn't fallen asleep either. He sat up and looked at Guan Wenjun in the dark, asking in a low voice, \"Comrade Guan, what's wrong?\"","As he spoke, he glanced at the hunting rifle in Guan Wenjun's hands, his eyes showing a mix of surprise and vigilance.","Guan Wenjun whispered, \"There was some noise out back just now, did you hear it?\"","Xiao Zhou whispered back, \"It sounded like someone knocking on the window?\"","Guan Wenjun nodded. Suddenly, he made a shushing gesture and said to Ranger Zhou, \"I think I hear footsteps, do you hear them?\"","Xiao Zhou was so scared that he sat frozen on the kang. He whispered, \"No? Comrade Guan, don't scare me. I've been here for two or three years and nothing has ever happened. It's the middle of the night, footsteps... Could it be Comrade Xiao Qiao getting up?\"","Guan Wenjun shook his head, \"It doesn't sound like it... No, I have to go take a look.\"","With Qiao Lanshu all alone next door, Guan Wenjun couldn't help but worry about her.","He grabbed the gun, opened the door, and went out. Xiao Zhou followed behind him and suddenly shouted loudly, \"Comrade Guan, put the gun down, it's too dangerous.\"","Guan Wenjun was about to answer when suddenly, he saw someone run out of Qiao Lanshu's room. Guan Wenjun's expression darkened; he aimed the gun at the figure and fired a shot with a bang.","He missed. It was too dark, and the person ran into the dark mountain forest.","Guan Wenjun broke out in a cold sweat from the shock.","He fired two more shots, bang, bang, at the spot where the figure had disappeared.","Then, he quickly ran into Qiao Lanshu's room, shouting in panic, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao! Qiao Lanshu! Are you in the room?\"","He searched around the room but didn't see anyone. Pressing his back against the wall, he didn't dare rush back out, instead shouting out the door, \"Qiao Lanshu! Where are you? Make a sound if you can hear me!\"","His voice was loud, echoing continuously through the pitch-black mountains surrounding them.","It was dead silent all around; there was only the howling wind, and no one answered him.","Not long after, Ranger Zhou arrived at the door in a half-crouch, calling out to him in a low voice, \"Guan, Comrade Guan, what just happened? Why did you fire the gun? We're not allowed to shoot guns here.\"","Guan Wenjun's eyes were rimmed with red, tears welling up and threatening to spill. He spoke in a low, heavy voice, \"Qiao... my wife is missing, and you're really talking to me about this right now? Damn it, you need to hide too. I just saw someone come into this room, and I have no idea if they are armed.\""]},{"number":163,"title":"Chapter 163: Orchard Explosion","paragraphs":["When Xiao Zhou heard Guan Wenjun say this, he quickly ran into the room, squatted behind him, and said nervously, \"Comrade Guan, what did you just see? Is there really a thief?\"","Guan Wenjun had no idea if it was a thief, but he subconsciously felt that something was wrong.","He whispered, \"It might not be as simple as a thief. The other party has gone into the mountain, and we can't rush in blindly. Hurry to the village and notify the production team. Have the captain bring the commune members over with torches. We have to go into the mountain and search!\"","Xiao Zhou said hesitantly, \"It's late at night, and it's very dangerous to go into the mountain. Why don't we wait until tomorrow...\"","Guan Wenjun suddenly turned around, grabbed Xiao Zhou by the collar tightly, and said coldly, \"My wife is missing, are you blind? We must go into the mountain to search tonight, otherwise, I'm afraid your whole village won't be able to bear the responsibility.\"","Guan Wenjun's face was gloomy and his tone was fierce, which startled Xiao Zhou.","He hurriedly said, \"I know, I know. Comrade Guan, don't be impulsive. Maybe your wife is hiding nearby. Why don't you look around? I'll go to the village to call for help. I'll go right now.\"","Only then did Guan Wenjun let go of him. Xiao Zhou quickly got up, rummaged through the room for a flashlight, and ran towards the village.","In fact, many people in the village were not asleep.","They had also heard the gunshots.","Many people had already lit oil lamps, come out of their houses, and were looking in the direction of the forestry farm.","After all, Guan Wenjun had just fired two shots, and the sound was so loud that it could be heard miles away.","Therefore, when Xiao Zhou ran into the village, he didn't even need to call for people. Captain Niu of the production brigade had already gotten up.","Meanwhile, Guan Wenjun squatted in the room, struggling with whether he should go out and look for Qiao Lanshu.","He had just seen a dark figure run out of this room, heading straight in the direction of the forestry farm.","He suspected that the forest ranger from the forestry farm had come over.","As for why he came, there could be many reasons.","For example, the other party might have seen Qiao Lanshu in the afternoon, been attracted by her appearance, and wanted to take advantage of the night to come over and do something inappropriate.","Or, the other party was the spy they had been looking for. Because Guan Wenjun was discovered by the dog when he went into the mountain in the morning, the other party suspected that Guan Wenjun knew some information, so he came over overnight, ready to silence him.","Although Guan Wenjun didn't have much experience in handling cases, he wasn't stupid. At this moment, he quickly sorted out the cause and effect.","He felt that it was highly likely that the other party came to silence him under the cover of night.","Because if it was purely for beauty, there was no need for the other party to take such a risk.","After all, that forest ranger Lao Wu was not young anymore, and Qiao Lanshu was now Guan Wenjun's wife, and her identity was a grassroots cadre who came here to exchange work.","That Lao Wu couldn't possibly risk his life for beauty, right?","There were so many girls in this village. If he was really that kind of person, he would have been arrested long ago for molesting women, and wouldn't have stayed in the orchard for more than ten years with a pretty good reputation.","During the day, Captain Niu even praised Lao Wu, saying that he was quite hardworking and dutiful.","Having figured this out, Guan Wenjun suddenly felt a bit uncomfortable.","It was all because of him that he alerted the enemy and harmed Qiao Lanshu.","So, where on earth did Qiao Lanshu go?","That dark figure ran alone and didn't take anyone else with him. Logically speaking, Qiao Lanshu should still be in the room.","However, Guan Wenjun wandered around the room a few times, rummaging through boxes and cabinets to find her, but he couldn't find her.","He jumped out of the window to the back of the house, looked around, and shouted for a long time, but no one answered him.","Guan Wenjun hugged his gun, squatted at the base of the wall, and wept silently. \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, where on earth have you gone? I've let you down. I've harmed you. When we go back this time, Lao Qin will definitely tear me to pieces...\"","As he spoke, he muttered again, \"No, if I can't find you, I won't go back. How could I have the face to go back...\"","At this moment, Qiao Lanshu was lying on the roof, hiding in the haystack on the roof, silently listening to Guan Wenjun's crying below.","She thought in her heart with wonder: Director Guan is actually crying?","It's amazing. Guan Wenjun, who has always been vain, would actually cry.","Qiao Lanshu originally wanted to call out to Guan Wenjun, but her sixth sense was still vigilant.","She always felt that the person who had just sneaked into her room hadn't gone far.","That person should be hiding near the entrance of the forestry farm, and the weapon in his hand was unclear.","It was uncertain whether the other party had a gun, nor was it certain what the other party's purpose was.","Qiao Lanshu didn't dare to make a sound now, lest she be discovered by the other party.","If she were alone, she might not be so cautious.","But she still had a child in her belly.","For the sake of the child, she couldn't take any risks.","Qiao Lanshu silently apologized to Guan Wenjun in her heart, thinking that she would wait until the people from the village came.","Things were not quite right.","This development had already exceeded her expectations.","Guan Wenjun couldn't find Qiao Lanshu anywhere around, so he hid in the room with his back against the wall. He didn't come out of the room until Captain Niu brought about twenty young men over, and the torches they held illuminated the surroundings brightly.","The firelight was too bright, and Qiao Lanshu silently buried herself deeper into the haystack.","Right now, she didn't trust anyone here except Guan Wenjun.","Including Xiao Zhou, Captain Niu, and the other people in the village.","Guan Wenjun came out of the room with red eyes. He had to borrow manpower from the village, otherwise, he couldn't handle this matter alone.","With red eyes, he questioned Captain Niu, \"Captain Niu, are all the people in your village here? Did anyone come here in the middle of the night? My wife is missing! I just saw with my own eyes someone running into my wife's room. After being discovered by me, he hid in the direction of the forestry farm. I suspect he kidnapped my wife!\"","Xiao Zhou said nervously, \"Well, I can testify that someone really came over. I even heard someone knock on the window. It's been more than half an hour, and Comrade Xiao Qiao's whereabouts are still unknown.\"","Captain Niu was extremely anxious.","He was the captain of the village's production team. Once something happened in the village, he would be the first to bear the brunt.","Hearing this, he immediately said, \"Comrade Guan, don't worry. I'll have everyone in the village gather right now! Let's see if anyone sneaked out in the middle of the night.\"","With that, he arranged for someone to run back to the village, turn on the broadcast overnight, and gather the whole village.","Another half an hour passed. Everyone in the village was there, even the elderly and children. No one was missing.","Guan Wenjun said with a dark face, \"Then it must be that forest ranger Lao Wu! Come in with me. I want to see if Lao Wu is in the mountain.\"","Administrator Xiao Zhou quickly said, \"But it's quite dangerous to go into the mountain at this time, and Lao Wu has a dog there.\"","Hearing this, Captain Niu immediately said seriously, \"No matter how dangerous it is, we have to go in! Didn't you say a female comrade is missing? If she ran into the mountain and got lost, it would be troublesome.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Zhou hurriedly said, \"That's right, I have a flashlight here. Let's all go into the mountain and look for her together.\"","With that said, Xiao Zhou ran forward with a flashlight. \"I am familiar with these mountains, I will lead the way for you.\"","Guan Wenjun followed closely behind, while Captain Niu led his men, marching forward in a mighty contingent.","Guan Wenjun then said to Captain Niu, \"Captain Niu, leave a few people here at the dorms. I'm afraid my wife might come back in a while and find no one here.\"","Guan Wenjun was still being very thoughtful.","He worried that if Qiao Lanshu found her way back on her own, what would happen if she ran into bad people again?","Captain Niu was very cooperative. He immediately arranged for three young men with torches to go back and guard the dormitory area.","The mountain forest on a winter night was actually not as dangerous as one might imagine.","Because they had strength in numbers and carried torches, wild animals and beasts would avoid them.","The weather was so cold and the mountains so desolate, unlike the lush mountains in the south where paths had to be cleared, and there were certainly no venomous insects blocking their way.","The mountain path was not that difficult to walk on. Furthermore, because this was a forestry farm, there were no traps around. The forestry administrators knew of the few pits in the mountains, and Xiao Zhou led them to avoid them all.","Just as they reached halfway up the mountain, suddenly, in the orchard deep in the forest, several wolfhounds began barking madly.","Guan Wenjun's legs went weak at the sound of the barking. He immediately stopped in his tracks and whispered, \"What's wrong? Did the dogs spot us?\"","The administrator Xiao Zhou swallowed hard and said, \"I, I don't know. Probably not? There's still a whole hill between us.\"","Captain Niu looked at the orchard not far away, listening to the continuous fierce barking of the dogs. He frowned and said, \"What is Lao Wu doing? Why are the dogs barking so fiercely...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, a loud boom suddenly came from the direction of the orchard!","In an instant, the earth shook and the mountains swayed; the whole ground was trembling.","The wooden cabin over at the orchard had exploded.","Everyone was shaken so hard they couldn't stand still. Several people fell to the ground, dropping the torches in their hands.","After his initial shock, Captain Niu hurriedly roared at them, \"Put out the damn torches! The weather is dry, be careful of a forest fire!\"","Under normal circumstances, bringing torches up the mountain was not allowed.","If it weren't for the fact that none of them had flashlights and they were afraid someone was missing in the mountains, they wouldn't have entered the mountains with a bottle of water and a torch each.","Now everyone was pale and weak in the knees from the explosion.","Captain Niu, worried about starting a forest fire, took down the canteen hanging at his waist and put out his own torch first.","The other young men were scrambling in fear from the distant explosion. Whatever Captain Niu told them to do, they hurried to do it.","Soon, they all used the water from their canteens to extinguish their torches.","Now, the only source of light at the scene was the flashlight in Xiao Zhou's hand.","Xiao Zhou swallowed nervously and said, \"Captain Niu, we need to put out the fire at the orchard. There was an explosion.\"","Captain Niu obviously knew that. He said in a deep voice, \"Then what are we waiting for? Hurry in and put out the fire!\"","There were mountain streams in the mountains, and an artificial reservoir dug in the orchard.","Both Xiao Zhou and Captain Niu knew this.","Guided by the light of the flashlight, the group ran toward the orchard.","Guan Wenjun also ran very fast. He didn't know why the orchard suddenly exploded.","But he knew that Lao Wu's identity was indeed not simple!","He even wondered if he had been discovered when he came to the orchard in the morning, and the other party wanted to destroy the evidence, so they simply blew up their own wooden cabin?","Everyone rushed to the orchard. The wooden cabin had just exploded, and fierce flames were burning it, making crackling sounds.","Surrounding the cabin was an open clearing, and stones were paved at the door, so the flames did not spread in a short time.","This was a good thing; otherwise, once it spread, this entire mountain wouldn't be enough for it to burn!","Captain Niu led his men to carry water and create a firebreak before starting to extinguish the flames.","Two deep craters had been blasted around the original cabin, and the surrounding area reeked of a terrible scorched smell.","When the fire was mostly put out, Guan Wenjun walked around the two deep craters.","Those dogs had actually been killed in the explosion.","There were no human corpses inside the cabin, and as for other things, nothing was found.","As Guan Wenjun walked into a corner, someone suddenly covered his mouth and pulled him into the darkness.","Guan Wenjun was about to struggle when he heard the person speak: \"It's me.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"!!!\"","Hearing this voice made Guan Wenjun feel guilty. He whispered, \"Lao Qin, why are you...\"","Qin Yuanzheng covered his mouth again and whispered, \"A lot of explosives were planted in the cabin. I just defused some of them, but I couldn't finish in time.\"","He was almost caught in the blast himself. Fortunately, he had experience in mine clearance and managed to jump out the window in time.","It was a pity it still blew up.","He had been very worried about starting a forest fire.","Fortunately, Guan Wenjun brought the villagers in and put out the fire just in time, preventing it from spreading.","Guan Wenjun cursed in a low voice, \"These damn spies really don't care about human lives. If a forest fire spread here, the village would also suffer. Who knows how many crops would be burned.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was dressed entirely in black, carrying a large backpack.","He whispered to Guan Wenjun, \"We didn't catch the person. Si Zhemao has already taken people to block every intersection. You go back to the village now and lead people to search there. I'm heading down the mountain first.\"","Guan Wenjun nodded. He hesitated to speak, looking at Qin Yuanzheng with an expression that looked like he was about to cry.","Qin Yuanzheng stared at him and said in a deep voice, \"What time is it for this? Spit it out!\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun hurriedly said, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao came over with me this time. Tonight, she, she suddenly went missing. I originally brought people into the mountains to find her, but I don't think she came up the mountain. However, we couldn't find her around the dormitory area either...\"","Bang!","Before Guan Wenjun could finish his sentence, Qin Yuanzheng punched him to the ground.","Hearing the noise, Xiao Zhou immediately called out, \"Comrade Guan, what's wrong? Who are you talking to?\"","Saying that, Xiao Zhou came over with the flashlight.","Guan Wenjun quickly shouted, \"I'm fine! It's just too dark, I accidentally tripped. I'm fine.\"","As Guan Wenjun spoke, he turned his head and realized Qin Yuanzheng had already disappeared.","Guan Wenjun rubbed his swollen face and silently got up from the ground.","Xiao Zhou quickly came over. He shone his flashlight around Guan Wenjun but found nothing suspicious.","Confused, he said, \"Comrade Guan, who were you just talking to? Were you talking?\"","Guan Wenjun said in a muffled voice, \"I'm looking for my wife. I don't know where she is. If I can't find her, I won't want to live anymore.\"","Xiao Zhou: \"...\"","Xiao Zhou wiped the dark soot off his face and said to Guan Wenjun, \"Comrade Guan, don't worry too much. I don't think Comrade Xiao Qiao went into the mountains. Why don't we go back and look for her again?\"","After all, they hadn't heard Qiao Lanshu calling for help all the way up the mountain.","There was only this one path in the forestry farm. Qiao Lanshu couldn't possibly have taken an unconventional route, could she?"]},{"number":164,"title":"Chapter 164: Unable to Distinguish Friend from Foe","paragraphs":["The explosion in the orchard was truly terrifying.","After Captain Niu led the crowd to put out the fire, he looked at the pitch-black crater on the ground and felt a wave of fear wash over him.","He looked at Xiao Zhou, his voice trembling slightly as he said, Xiao Zhou, Lao Wu... could Lao Wu have...","Xiao Zhou's expression was equally grave. Captain Niu, we haven't found Lao Wu either. Maybe he wasn't in the mountains today...","Captain Niu sighed, speaking with a heavy heart, Who knows if there are more explosives here. We shouldn't go any further. Let's head back immediately. We need to go to town overnight to report this to the police. Let the public security officers or the Revolutionary Committee take over. This isn't something we can handle.","The presence of explosives and an explosion in the mountains made even Captain Niu, an old farmer who had worked the village lands for decades, realize that something was terribly wrong.","Guan Wenjuan knew that Qin Yuanzheng and Si Zhemao had both arrived. Si Zhemao had already blocked all the intersections in the village, which meant that Lao Wu definitely couldn't escape.","Lao Wu was definitely still in the village, but no one knew where he would hide. This was extremely dangerous because there were too many people in the village. What if he decided to blow up the village...","Guan Wenjuan immediately found Captain Niu and said to him sternly,","Captain Niu, this Lao Wu is very suspicious. The explosives definitely have something to do with him. Since he isn't in the mountains now, he must have run into the village. You need to find him quickly, tie him up, and interrogate him. Otherwise, if he's still carrying explosives, the people in the village will be in danger.","Hearing this, Captain Niu was so frightened that he hurriedly urged the young men around him to go down the mountain. Quick, quick, quick! Hurry down the mountain and back to the village. Find the forest ranger, Lao Wu! Hurry up, let's go!","While Captain Niu was in a frantic rush, he still said to Guan Wenjuan, I don't think Lao Wu is that kind of person. He's honest and simple-minded, and he's worked in the forestry center for nearly twenty years. He planted that whole orchard himself. How could he blow up the mountain? He wouldn't. He definitely wouldn't.","Captain Niu was letting his emotions guide him, believing that Lao Wu wouldn't do such a thing and had no motive to do so.","But Guan Wenjuan was not one to be swayed by emotion. He gave a cold snort and said with a dark expression,","Whether he would or not, we'll only know after we catch him and interrogate him! If he has nothing to hide, why would he run away in the middle of the night? Besides, he raised five or six vicious wolfhounds. Who else could get in there besides him? No one would dare go in, so where do you think those explosives came from?","Guan Wenjuan's words left Captain Niu completely speechless.","As he walked down the mountain by the moonlight, his face fell, and he said with some panic, Lao Wu shouldn't have... He planted that orchard with his own hands. He shouldn't have...","Perhaps because he was too tense, Captain Niu tripped over a rock and fell to the ground as he walked.","A few young men rushed over to help him up. Captain, are you okay?","Captain Niu stood up and said in frustration, I'm fine. Where's Xiao Zhou? Hurry up and lead the way! Where's your flashlight?","Xiao Zhou quickly grabbed his flashlight and ran to the front to lead the way. Here, here! Captain, I'm here. Just follow behind me.","The mountains were pitch black, and the sounds of wild beasts occasionally echoed from afar. Guan Wenjuan even heard a wolf howl. Going up the mountain in the middle of the night was quite frightening.","Fortunately, there were many of them, so they weren't too afraid.","The group walked to the foot of the mountain. Emerging from the forestry center and seeing the lit-up dormitory area not far away, everyone breathed a sigh of relief.","The three young men from earlier were still waiting in the dormitory area. As soon as Captain Niu came down, he quickly asked, You've been guarding here for so long, have you seen anyone else? Did you see the female comrade who came for the exchange?","The three men quickly shook their heads. No, Captain. There's no one here.","Captain Niu asked anxiously again, What about the forest ranger, Lao Wu? He wasn't in the mountains, so he should have come out. Did you see him?","The three young lads shook their heads again.","Captain, the three of us have been here for two hours, and we haven't seen a single soul.","By the way, Captain, was there an explosion in the mountains just now? What exactly happened?","Despite the freezing weather, Captain Niu was sweating profusely from anxiety.","He wiped his forehead, shook his head, and said, It was explosives. Explosives blew up the wooden cabin in the mountains, and Lao Wu's whereabouts are unknown...","What they didn't know was that the Lao Wu they were talking about had already started his journey overnight to leave the village the moment the explosion happened in the mountains.","To avoid being discovered, he didn't dare drive the forestry center's tractor, choosing instead to flee the village on foot.","There were three roads leaving the village. One was a mountain path right by the forestry center, but he didn't dare take that route.","He took the village road directly. After rushing for an hour, he suddenly realized that the village road was blocked.","Several men were standing around the pitch-black mountain road.","A dark car was parked by the side of the road.","Lao Wu immediately realized something was wrong!","He didn't dare go any further. In a panic, he could only turn back and take the other village road, but of course, he was intercepted there as well.","Lao Wu knew he had been exposed.","He actually hadn't expected the wooden cabin to explode so early.","According to his plan, he originally wanted to go down the mountain, kill Guan Wenjuan first, and then take Qiao Lanshu as a hostage, leaving the village overnight to flee for his life elsewhere.","After all, from the moment Guan Wenjuan entered the mountain and was chased by the dogs, he knew Guan Wenjuan's identity was not simple.","But what he miscalculated was that besides Guan Wenjuan and Qiao Lanshu,","There was actually a third person who sneaked into his wooden cabin in the dead of night and detonated all the landmines he had planted inside!","Once the cabin exploded, he lost the upper hand in trying to escape.","The villagers, as well as these people from the outside, would definitely come to catch him.","Now, he could only fight to the bitter end.","Lao Wu ran back and forth twice, finding that all the roads out of the village were blocked.","He didn't know how he was discovered, but he had several informants. If even one of them was exposed, his information would be leaked.","He just didn't know who exactly had exposed his information.","In the darkness, Lao Wu returned to the vicinity of the forestry center.","There were many people around the forestry center, all from the village. Captain Niu had arranged for people to go back and broadcast a message, asking the whole village to help find Lao Wu.","At the same time, the young men who had come down from the mountain were also assigned to join the search.","It was a sleepless night. Everyone in the village heard the broadcast, and the young and strong men came out of their houses to help look for him. The originally pitch-black and quiet village was now lit up with torches everywhere.","Lao Wu crouched near the dormitory area. Looking at the current situation, he knew that things were going to be difficult for him this time.","He saw Guan Wenjuan, but he didn't see Guan Wenjuan's wife.","That docile woman—he still didn't know where she was hiding.","And the person who triggered the landmines in his cabin had yet to show themselves.","Lao Wu hid patiently for over half an hour. He watched as the people in the dormitory area returned to the village, leaving only Guan Wenjuan, Xiao Zhou, and Captain Niu at the scene.","Suddenly, Lao Wu dashed out from the shadows and fiercely pounced on Xiao Zhou.","Captain Niu jumped in fright. He shouted in shock, \"Lao Wu! What are you doing? Let go of Xiao Zhou right now!\"","The flashlight in Xiao Zhou's hand dropped to the ground. His neck was put in a chokehold by Lao Wu, and a gun was pressed against his head!","Guan Wenjun immediately aimed his hunting rifle at Lao Wu and roared, \"Let him go! Lao Wu, don't keep making mistakes! Let Xiao Zhou go, put down your weapon, and maybe we can still show you some leniency!\"","Lao Wu's skinny arm tightly strangled Xiao Zhou's neck.","Unable to breathe, Xiao Zhou's face turned red as he desperately clawed at Lao Wu's arm.","Lao Wu struck Xiao Zhou's head with the gun and hissed, \"Quiet down! Or I'll shoot you dead right now!\"","Suffocating, Xiao Zhou's limbs instantly went weak. He didn't dare to struggle anymore, terrified of angering Lao Wu and getting his brains blown out.","Captain Niu's hands trembled with nervousness.","Good heavens, what on earth was going on!","How could such a thing suddenly happen in his perfectly fine little village? Lao Wu had worked at the forestry center for over twenty years, could speak the local dialect, and got along very well with the villagers.","Lao Wu was already considered a local; everyone knew him.","He was so thin and had such an honest, simple personality.","How did he suddenly start playing with explosives? And a gun!","Captain Niu's voice choked up a bit; he was truly distressed. He asked Lao Wu, \"Lao Wu, what is this all for? Why are you doing this?\"","At this moment, where was Lao Wu's usual honest and simple demeanor?","In the dark, his expression was gloomy, cold, and full of hostility.","He stared at the hunting rifle in Guan Wenjun's hands and said coldly, \"Put the gun down!\"","Saying that, he pulled Xiao Zhou in front of him, using him as a human shield. \"If you don't put it down, I'll shoot him.\"","Guan Wenjun didn't dare to clash with him head-on, but he didn't lower his gun either. He said in a deep voice, \"Tell me, what exactly do you want?\"","Lao Wu slowly backed up until he reached the forestry center's tractor. Then, he said to Captain Niu, \"Go get the tractor's crank handle and start the engine.\"","Captain Niu glanced at Guan Wenjun, and then Lao Wu suddenly became furious. He unbuttoned his coat, revealing several grenades inside, and shouted, \"If you dawdle any longer, we'll all die together! I'll blow this whole place up!\"","Captain Niu was stunned. His face was pale, and his lips trembled. \"Lao... Lao Wu, don't get worked up. Don't be rash.\"","Saying that, he hurriedly ran over, inserted the crank handle into the front of the tractor, and cranked it hard a few times. The tractor started up with a putt-putt-putt sound.","Lao Wu sat on the tractor. Holding Xiao Zhou tightly by the neck with one hand and steering with the other, he stepped on the gas and drove the tractor away.","Guan Wenjun immediately chased after him, shouting loudly, \"Wait a minute, where is my wife? Where did you take my wife?\"","Furious, Guan Wenjun fired two shots, bang bang, at the tractor's cargo bed.","This scared Captain Niu so much he almost fell to his knees. Captain Niu said nervously, \"Comrade Guan, Comrade Guan, don't be impulsive! He's covered in explosives! And he has a hostage; Xiao Zhou is still in his hands!\"","Guan Wenjun kept shouting, \"My wife! Where did you hide my wife?\"","Guan Wenjun kept chasing from behind, and Lao Wu angrily cursed, \"I don't know! I haven't seen her!\"","Guan Wenjun cursed back, \"Bullshit! You liar, I'm going to take you down with me!\"","Lao Wu: \"...\"","Lao Wu quickly stepped harder on the gas pedal, and the tractor chugged forward and sped off.","Captain Niu pinned Guan Wenjun down tightly. \"Comrade Guan, don't be impulsive. Let him go first...\"","Captain Niu was also out of options. He said agitatedly,","\"I have to be responsible for the villagers. If his explosives go off, everyone in this area will suffer. Comrade Guan, you're a city person, you don't know how hard it is to grow grain in the village. Look around here, look at this place! It's all farmland, all crops! If he blows it up, what will our whole village eat in the future?\"","Guan Wenjun was firmly pinned to the ground by him and didn't struggle.","With red eyes, Guan Wenjun said, \"Then what about my wife? My wife is missing, where am I supposed to find her?\"","Captain Niu: \"Didn't Lao Wu say it? He doesn't know either. Could it be that your wife hid herself?\"","Guan Wenjun actually believed that it wasn't Lao Wu's doing. If Lao Wu had taken Qiao Lanshu, then he would be holding Qiao Lanshu as a hostage right now.","Instead of Xiao Zhou.","Qiao Lanshu watched the tractor drive away, and only then did she begin to analyze the situation in her mind.","In her previous life, Qin Yuanzheng said he had saved someone he shouldn't have, which was why he got injured in an explosion.","Could that person be Xiao Zhou?","Was the hostage in her previous life Xiao Zhou?","Qiao Lanshu slowly sat up from the haystack and began to recall everything about Xiao Zhou.","To be honest, there was nothing suspicious.","The only suspicious thing was that when Xiao Zhou came back from the town, his very first question was to ask Guan Wenjun if he had been chased by a dog.","He had just returned from the town, so how could he know that Guan Wenjun was chased by a dog...","Qiao Lanshu sat there and analyzed for a good while. She saw Guan Wenjun, pinned to the ground by Captain Niu, start crying again.","Captain Niu was also crying. Two grown men were lying on the ground, each crying louder than the other.","Qiao Lanshu, lying on the roof, shouted in Guan Wenjun's direction, \"Director Guan, Director Guan, Guan Wenjun!\"","Guan Wenjun sat up with red eyes. \"Why are you calling me?\"","As he spoke, he froze, then suddenly lifted his head and looked toward the roof.","Then, he saw Qiao Lanshu lying on the roof, completely clean and unharmed, staring at him. \"Director Guan, come here for a second.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun was stunned for a good while and couldn't react.","It was Captain Niu who suddenly said, \"Little lady, how did you climb up to the roof? Do you know that your husband has been frantically searching for you all night?\"","Qiao Lanshu said without changing her expression, \"I know, but I have my reasons. Director Guan, stop spacing out and come over here quickly. I have something to tell you.\"","With that, she slowly lowered the ladder that had been pressing on her body. Once she made sure the ladder was stable, she prepared to climb down from the roof.","Guan Wenjun wiped the corners of his eyes. He still looked a bit dazed, and also a bit angry.","But he still ran over quickly and helped hold the ladder steady for Qiao Lanshu.","Guan Wenjun didn't say a word, and Qiao Lanshu knew he was angry.","But she didn't regret it either. She couldn't possibly come down from the roof and run around with a bunch of grown men when she couldn't tell friend from foe, could she?","As soon as Qiao Lanshu got down from the roof, without waiting for Guan Wenjun to speak, she hurriedly asked, \"Director Guan, if the target of the mission is here, does that mean Brother Zheng and the investigators are here too? Where can I find Brother Zheng? I have something I want to tell him.\""]},{"number":165,"title":"Chapter 165: How is Comrade Qin Holding Comrade Guan’s Wife","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun originally wanted to question Qiao Lanshu about why she had hidden on the roof without making a sound, knowing full well that he was going crazy looking for her, yet she didn't even call out to him.","Guan Wenjun felt a bit resentful in his heart.","But at this very moment, as soon as Qiao Lanshu asked a question, he immediately stopped caring about all that.","He looked at Qiao Lanshu and asked her curiously, How did you know they would come here? You even guessed this?","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Qiao Lanshu said in a low voice, There was an explosion on the mountain, and Lao Wu even took a hostage and ran away. If those two still haven't noticed, then they are about as clueless as you.","Guan Wenjun: ...","Guan Wenjun felt that Qiao Lanshu was mocking him, but he felt guilty and didn't dare to mock her back.","He scratched his head and whispered, Si Zhemao took his men to block the road. Lao Qin was just on the mountain, but now I don't know where he ran off to.","Qiao Lanshu instantly stomped her foot in anxiety. She quickly said, Did he go to save the hostage? No, we have to hurry over there!","Saying that, Qiao Lanshu pushed Guan Wenjun away and sprinted toward the dirt road at the village entrance.","In the mountain village right now, the night was pitch black.","The cold winter wind was strong, howling as it blew. The chill seemed to seep into one's bones, and exposed faces ached from the biting wind.","As a Southerner, Qiao Lanshu was very afraid of the cold, but right now, she couldn't feel it at all.","Compared to the physical cold, her heart felt even colder.","Qin Yuanzheng was a soldier. He was here on a mission to capture enemy agents.","If someone was taken hostage by a spy, he would definitely go save them.","This was his duty and obligation.","However, Qiao Lanshu felt there was something wrong with Xiao Zhou. Whether to save him and if he should be saved was still open to question.","No matter what, she had to stop Qin Yuanzheng.","The Lao Wu from earlier was covered in explosives.","She didn't know if the Qin Yuanzheng from her past life had been injured by those explosives.","But this time, regardless of whether it was true or not, she was going to stop Qin Yuanzheng.","Guan Wenjun felt that Qiao Lanshu was truly hopelessly love-struck.","Before Qin Yuanzheng arrived, she had been incredibly cautious all by herself.","Staying awake in the middle of the night, she astutely knew to climb onto the roof, hide the ladder, and then lie up there in absolute silence for two or three hours.","But look at her now. As soon as she heard Qin Yuanzheng was here and going to save the hostage, she started panicking.","She was no longer lying on the roof or hiding in the room; she just ran straight onto the pitch-black village road.","Captain Niu shouted loudly from nearby, Oh my, little girl, stop running, stop running! It's dangerous over there. Lao Wu's tractor hasn't gone far yet! He is covered in explosives.","Even Captain Niu was scared and didn't dare to follow, yet he watched as a young girl like Qiao Lanshu actually chased in the direction of the tractor.","He was completely dumbfounded.","Guan Wenjun quickly chased after her. He grabbed Qiao Lanshu's arm to stop her from running further and said fiercely, Qiao Lanshu! Why are you running? It's pitch black, you can't even see the road clearly. Where are you going? If you fall, what about your belly...","He paused, then lowered his voice, Can you please be a little careful? If something happens to you, wouldn't Qin Yuanzheng hack me to death?","Qiao Lanshu hadn't been running for long before she was panting heavily. Running in this freezing weather was strangely exhausting.","She tightly gripped Guan Wenjun's arm, her eyes red. She wanted to cry but forcefully held it back, trying hard not to let her tears fall. She said anxiously, No, I have to chase after him. I have to find Brother Zheng. I have to tell him not to save that person, there's something wrong with him.","Qiao Lanshu had barely slept for three days and hadn't been able to eat properly either.","Now, after running for a bit, she felt a little dizzy and her legs were weak.","Seeing her slowly sliding toward the ground, Guan Wenjun couldn't care less. He quickly reached out, grabbing her arms with both hands and letting her lean against his back to barely stay standing. He said nervously:","Don't faint! Please don't let anything happen to you. I'll go find Qin Yuanzheng, I'll go tell him. Can you just go back to the dorm and rest for now?","Even at a time like this, Guan Wenjun was still trying to sow discord:","Let me tell you, that guy Qin Yuanzheng is not only petty, he's also cold-blooded! The only reason he's with you is because you're young, pretty, naive, easy to fool, and can give him children. If something goes wrong with your body, he will definitely abandon you and marry some commander's daughter. When that time comes, you won't even have a place to cry, I'm telling you.","Guan Wenjun really couldn't stand Qiao Lanshu's love-struck brain.","She was completely devoted to Qin Yuanzheng, and for his sake, she was starting to go crazy.","Guan Wenjun couldn't exactly describe how he felt. In short, his heart felt like it was stuffed with sour lemons, and he was even starting to find Qin Yuanzheng an eyesore.","Qiao Lanshu choked back a sob and said, You're talking nonsense. Brother Zheng is not that kind of person.","As she spoke, she pushed Guan Wenjun away and continued walking forward along the village road. My Brother Zheng is responsible and loyal. He is kind, steady, honest, and patriotic. He loves me the most in the whole world. No matter how you try to sow discord, it won't work.","Guan Wenjun: ...","Guan Wenjun grabbed his head with both hands, raging in sheer impotence, Ahhhhh! I've really had enough of you two! I'm not looking after you anymore, I'm going back!","With that, he made a show of turning around to leave. However, Qiao Lanshu, who was ahead, suddenly slowed her pace, grabbed onto a tree by the side of the road, and slowly slid down.","Guan Wenjun: ...","Guan Wenjun: Damn it! Are you really fainting?","Saying that, Guan Wenjun quickly ran over, just about to pick up Qiao Lanshu who had slid to the ground.","At that moment, someone was faster than him.","Qin Yuanzheng, who had appeared out of nowhere, suddenly rushed in front of him and picked Qiao Lanshu up a step ahead of him.","Guan Wenjun was stunned. He looked left and right. This village road was a mountain path, flanked by mountains on both sides. Ahead was the pitch-black mountain road, and a few dozen meters behind was the entrance to the forestry farm and the forestry farm dormitory area.","He asked in shock, Lao Qin, where did you come from?","Qin Yuanzheng was still dressed all in black. His black insulated windbreaker was covered in scorched plant ash, and he smelled entirely of gunpowder smoke.","His face was covered with a black cloth, exposing only his eyes and eyebrows.","He held Qiao Lanshu in his arms and said in a low voice, I just took my men to chase the tractor. Now I'm back to find my wife.","He guessed that Qiao Lanshu hadn't gone into the mountains, so he hadn't bothered looking for her there at all.","He had just led his men along the mountain path, chasing the tractor for a distance. Once he confirmed that only Lao Wu and Xiao Zhou were on the tractor, and that Lao Wu had a gun and explosives on him, he ordered his subordinates to continue tracking them while sending someone to notify Si Zhemao.","After that, he came back here first to find Qiao Lanshu.","If Qiao Lanshu hadn't been here, he probably would have chosen to save the hostage first.","But now, he had to come back and save his wife first.","After all, Lao Wu's cover was blown, and he wouldn't be able to run far.","But if something happened to his wife, it would be irreversible.","Guan Wenjun still wanted to say something more.","But he saw that Qiao Lanshu hadn't actually fainted. She was just dizzy and weak, making her legs too soft to stand.","As soon as she saw Qin Yuanzheng, she hugged him and cried, her tears pouring down like a flood.","Guan Wenjun was completely dumbfounded.","Wait, wasn't Comrade Xiao Qiao quite brave?","She had just argued with him for ages without shedding a single tear, but now that she saw Qin Yuanzheng, the tears from her love-struck mind finally couldn't be held back and just poured out?","Qin Yuanzheng originally wanted to properly interrogate Guan Wenjuan.","His delicate little wife was supposed to be staying comfortably at home. Someone would bring her meals, and someone would chat with her. She wouldn't have to suffer from hunger or cold, nor endure the exhaustion of traveling. All she needed to do was lie at home, listen to the radio, and look at sweaters or something.","Her little life was quite beautiful.","He had arranged everything perfectly.","But in the blink of an eye, his wife had followed Guan Wenjuan into these mountains.","He was incredibly angry; the look he gave Guan Wenjuan was practically murderous.","But Guan Wenjuan also felt quite wronged; he surely had his reasons.","Although Qin Yuanzheng had already made up his mind that no matter the reason, he would beat Guan Wenjuan up first before doing anything else.","However, the little wife in his arms was crying so miserably. Qin Yuanzheng had never seen Qiao Lanshu cry like this before.","His heart ached terribly. He immediately held Qiao Lanshu in his arms, used his sleeve to wipe her tears, and coaxed her in a low voice, \"Wife, what's wrong? Are you hurt somewhere?\"","As he spoke, he dropped to one knee on the ground. Holding Qiao Lanshu with one hand, he used the other to feel her arms and legs, and then her stomach, asking softly, \"Where are you hurt? Where do you feel uncomfortable?\"","Qiao Lanshu sniffled and choked out, \"Brother Zheng, my stomach is uncomfortable.\"","Qin Yuanzheng's expression darkened a bit, and he asked calmly, \"Your stomach is uncomfortable? How does it feel?\"","Qiao Lanshu cried, \"My stomach is hungry. I'm so hungry that I'm dizzy.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Beside them, Guan Wenjuan, whose palms were sweating from nervousness: \"...\"","Guan Wenjuan rolled his eyes and silently stood up.","He had really had enough of the sour stench of romance.","The smell was too strong; he was going to suffocate from it.","Qin Yuanzheng immediately carried Qiao Lanshu and started walking back. He said softly, \"I'll take you back to the forestry farm dormitory first, and then make you something to eat, okay? By the way, I haven't asked you yet, why did you follow Guan Wenjuan here? This place is so dangerous, didn't he tell you?\"","Qiao Lanshu leaned into Qin Yuanzheng's embrace and reached out to grope around his body. After feeling his chest and arms, her mischievous little hands slipped under the hem of his shirt, tracing along his waist and abdomen toward his back.","Qin Yuanzheng was incredibly ticklish, and all the muscles in his body tensed up.","He whispered, \"Stop messing around, there's an outsider watching.\"","The outsider Guan Wenjuan: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu's eyes were swollen, and her voice was hoarse. Her hands didn't stop moving, feeling all over Qin Yuanzheng's chest and back.","Her hands were ice-cold as they wandered all over his body. Qin Yuanzheng felt bad that her hands were so cold, but he also couldn't handle her teasing like this; it was making him very uncomfortable.","Qiao Lanshu didn't notice the changes in Qin Yuanzheng's body at all. She only thought that normally when she was with Qin Yuanzheng, his muscles were soft. Why did they feel so rock-hard right now?","Qiao Lanshu said in a low voice, \"I heard an explosion in the mountains earlier. Were you there at the time? Did you get hurt by the blast?\"","As she spoke, her hand started to unfasten his belt. From the looks of it, she was going to continue feeling further down.","Qin Yuanzheng's entire body instantly went rigid. He held Qiao Lanshu with one arm and pressed down on his belt with the other hand. In the darkness, he stared deeply at Qiao Lanshu and whispered:","\"I'm fine, I'm not hurt. My whole body is perfectly fine! Take your hands back and stop messing around, okay? When we get back in a bit, I'll strip naked and let you look, alright?\"","Having felt Qin Yuanzheng's chest and back, Qiao Lanshu confirmed that he really wasn't injured, and her previously anxious heart finally settled.","Only then did she nod. Belatedly feeling a bit embarrassed, she nodded obediently, \"Okay.\"","Qin Yuanzheng then carried Qiao Lanshu and walked briskly toward the dormitory area.","He was worried that his wife was starving, and at the same time, he cursed Guan Wenjuan in his heart. That useless guy actually failed to even keep his wife's stomach full.","By the time they hurried back to the dormitory area, Captain Niu was still guarding the area and hadn't left.","He was quite happy to see that Guan Wenjuan had returned.","However, when he saw Guan Wenjuan's wife being held in the arms of a strange man in black clothes, while Guan Wenjuan merely followed silently behind, his expression turned to shock.","He looked at Qin Yuanzheng, then at Guan Wenjuan. After hesitating for a moment, he couldn't help but speak up. He asked, \"Comrade Guan, what happened to you guys? Who is this male comrade? Why is he carrying your wife? What's wrong with your wife?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"???\"","Guan Wenjuan: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu guiltily shrank her head back, buried her face in Qin Yuanzheng's chest, and pretended she had passed out and couldn't hear anything!","Qin Yuanzheng's face instantly darkened. He turned his head and glared at Guan Wenjuan.","Guan Wenjuan gulped and quickly said, \"Everyone here knows that Comrade Xiao Qiao and I are husband and wife.\"","As he spoke, he even shot a look at Qin Yuanzheng and added, \"We husband and wife came to the forestry farm to exchange work, didn't you know?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","At this moment, what else was there for Qin Yuanzheng not to understand?","Guan Wenjuan and Qiao Lanshu had pretended to be a married couple to come here and carry out a mission.","Qin Yuanzheng remained gloomily silent. Guan Wenjuan knew he was upset, but Guan Wenjuan had no other choice either.","This was all Qiao Lanshu's idea; it had nothing to do with him.","Captain Niu saw that their expressions were off, so he lowered his voice and asked Guan Wenjuan, \"Comrade Guan, what exactly is going on? Who is this man?\"","Guan Wenjuan coughed, lowered his voice, and said, \"Him? He's my colleague. He specifically came over today to meet up with me.\"","Captain Niu glanced at the tall, burly, and fiercely imposing Qin Yuanzheng, and said suspiciously, \"Is that so?\"","Guan Wenjuan nodded silently: \"Of course!\"","Captain Niu continued, \"Since he's your colleague, why is he holding your wife? Is this colleague a proper colleague?\"","Guan Wenjuan: \"...\"","The aura radiating from Qin Yuanzheng grew colder and colder.","Carrying Qiao Lanshu, he walked expressionlessly to the dormitory area and asked her in a chilling voice, \"Comrade Guan's wife, is it? Tell me, which room have you two husband and wife been staying in these past two days?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu shrank her neck and pointed a finger at a room.","Qin Yuanzheng walked over with a dark face and kicked the door open with a loud bang.","Qiao Lanshu shrank her neck again.","Guan Wenjuan immediately turned around and walked away. \"I just thought about it, and I still need to go after Lao Wu. We can't let him just run away like this. Captain Niu, you should bring some men and chase after him with me.\"","Compared to the explosives on Lao Wu, he was actually much more afraid of an angry Qin Yuanzheng.","After all, the explosives might not necessarily blow him up, but Qin Yuanzheng would definitely beat him to death."]},{"number":166,"title":"Chapter 166: If something happens to you, I'll remarry and take the kid with me.","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun said he was going to chase after Lao Wu, but he was just saying it.","By this time, Lao Wu had already driven the tractor away, holding the hostage and escaping several kilometers.","Without a vehicle by his side, how could he chase someone with just his two legs?","Captain Niu said melancholically, \"Lao Wu has escaped. We have to go to town overnight to report to the police; otherwise, if something happens, they will hold me accountable.\"","Sighing heavily, he continued:","\"Tell me, what is that Lao Wu after? Isn't it good enough to just stay in the forestry center? He has been here for over twenty years. Even if he wasn't born and raised here, this place is basically half his hometown. How could he be so cruel? To actually get so many explosives and just blow things up like that. Half the orchard is gone. What good does this do him?\"","With his simple mind, Captain Niu couldn't figure out why Lao Wu suddenly wanted to blow up the wooden cabin in the orchard.","Guan Wenjun could roughly guess.","Lao Wu must have realized he was exposed, which was why he blew up the cabin.","He had too many things in the cabin. He couldn't take them away, but he couldn't let others find them either, so he simply blew them up.","That way, he could also conveniently kill anyone who had sneaked into his cabin.","Then, even if Lao Wu was caught, there would be no evidence to put him on trial.","However, his miscalculation was that Qin Yuanzheng had already collected some evidence before the cabin exploded. It was those dogs that delayed Qin Yuanzheng from clearing the explosives; otherwise, the cabin wouldn't have exploded at all.","Qin Yuanzheng felt it was a pity that some evidence and materials were not salvaged in time.","Qin Yuanzheng carried Qiao Lanshu into the room. He looked around and didn't see Guan Wenjun's belongings, so his anger immediately subsided a bit.","He placed Qiao Lanshu on the kang bed, then went to check the stove. Several hours had passed, but the kang was still warm.","So Qin Yuanzheng didn't light the fire for the kang.","He sat opposite Qiao Lanshu, her eyes following his every movement.","Qiao Lanshu asked, \"Brother Zheng, if I hadn't come, would you be off saving the hostage right now?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He didn't blame Qiao Lanshu. He felt now wasn't the right time; when they got home, he would definitely have to punish this little wife of his properly.","Qin Yuanzheng said, \"Even though you're here, I still have to go save him. The other party drove the tractor toward the town, and Si Zhemao's men might not be able to stop him. I have to go over and assist secretly.\"","Qin Yuanzheng planned to follow Lao Wu first to see where he would run to.","His superiors' orders were to capture him alive, so he couldn't just snipe him from the dark.","This mission was a bit tricky. First, he had to rescue the hostage, and second, he had to capture Lao Wu alive.","Qin Yuanzheng said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Don't worry, I'll stay here with you for a while and leave later. I hid a motorcycle in the mountains, so I'll ride it over.\"","In this era, motorcycle production was very low, far less than tractors.","But motorcycles were indeed more useful than tractors, and they were suited for mountain roads.","Cars, on the other hand, were not suitable for mountain roads.","As soon as Qiao Lanshu heard that he still had to go over later, she quickly grabbed his sleeve and said, \"Brother Zheng, I think there's something wrong with that hostage. He's very likely in cahoots with Lao Wu. If you go to save him, what if he turns around and hurts you?\"","Could it be that in her previous life, Qin Yuanzheng was injured by explosives precisely because he saved Xiao Zhou, only to be backstabbed by him?","Otherwise, knowing that Lao Wu had explosives on him, a cautious person like Qin Yuanzheng should have avoided the blast.","Sure enough, upon hearing Qiao Lanshu say this, Qin Yuanzheng's expression immediately turned serious.","He sat up a bit straighter, looked at Qiao Lanshu, and asked solemnly, \"Are you sure? How did you come to this conclusion? Tell me.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had been carrying out his mission in the dark, looking for clues, and collecting information and materials on the spies.","He had never interacted with Administrator Xiao Zhou, nor had he been in contact with anyone in the village.","From his perspective, he only knew that the suspect, Lao Wu, had hijacked a young forestry center administrator.","And as a soldier, he was obligated to rescue the hostage.","When he arranged for people to track the tractor's whereabouts and sent someone overnight to notify Si Zhemao, the information he provided was always that the suspect had a large amount of explosives strapped to his body and had taken a villager hostage, requiring a plan to rescue the hostage.","But if this hostage was an accomplice of the suspect, then their plan would have to be altered.","Qiao Lanshu said hesitantly, \"Actually, I can't be one hundred percent sure, but that administrator is indeed very suspicious. Let me analyze it for you from my perspective.\"","Since it concerned Qin Yuanzheng, Qiao Lanshu didn't dare to be careless.","She recounted the process of her interactions with Xiao Zhou over the past two days, as well as her suspicions about him tonight.","Qin Yuanzheng said in a deep voice:","\"So you're saying, he didn't take you to the orchard, and he reminded you that there were wolfdogs in the orchard, telling you not to go near. When Guan Wenjun returned from the orchard in the morning, Xiao Zhou had just come back from out of town, yet he already knew about him being chased by dogs.","Therefore, you deduce that Xiao Zhou has been helping Lao Wu cover things up, preventing people from approaching the orchard. On the morning Guan Wenjun was chased by dogs, Xiao Zhou was very likely with Lao Wu and didn't go to town?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded:","\"There's one more thing. I just remembered that tonight, Lao Wu came to my room. But I was already hiding on the roof at the time, so he missed me. However, I saw with my own eyes that he rushed into my room with a clear target.","How did Lao Wu know which room I lived in? He hasn't been to the dormitory area these past two days. I always feel that the relationship between Lao Wu and Xiao Zhou is closer than what we see. Perhaps there is some connection between the two of them...\"","Under normal circumstances, if Lao Wu wanted to launch a sneak attack, shouldn't he be looking for people room by room?","He didn't; his target was very clear.","At that time, Qiao Lanshu was watching from the roof and saw a tall, thin dark figure walk out from the mountain road and quickly run to the door of her room.","At that moment, she was so frightened that her heart stopped for a second, and all the hairs on her body stood up.","It was too terrifying. Fortunately, her sixth sense was right, helping her avoid a crisis.","This was also the reason why she kept hiding on the roof and didn't dare to come down.","She was frightened by that dark figure who sneaked into her room, so as a result, she didn't quite trust anyone in the village, including Administrator Xiao Zhou.","Thinking about it now, perhaps her intuition was correct.","Qin Yuanzheng suddenly stood up. He opened the door, looked at Guan Wenjun, who was squatting not far away chatting with Captain Niu, and called out to him, \"Guan Wenjun, come in for a second.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Wait, it was currently the perfect time for the husband and wife to be affectionate with each other, so why was he calling him over?","Why was he feeling so guilty?","Guan Wenjun thought Qin Yuanzheng was coming to question him about the fake husband and wife matter.","So as soon as he came over, he immediately said, \"Lao Qin, calm down for a second and listen to me. I've been sleeping in the same room as Xiao Zhou these past two days. I haven't even stepped foot into Comrade Xiao Qiao's room. Comrade Xiao Qiao, please, say something!\"","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng's tightly furrowed brows did not relax.","Instead, his face darkened further, and he said, \"You didn't enter her room, but that Lao Wu did.\"","Guan Wenjun looked shocked. \"Ah? How did you know about this?\"","Qin Yuanzheng had been wondering earlier; since Qiao Lanshu and Guan Wenjun came here posing as a married couple, they should have been staying in the same room.","Guan Wenjun was young and strong, while Lao Wu was a frail old man nearing fifty. How did he dare to sneak into their room in the middle of the night for a surprise attack?","Did he bring a gun?","But using a gun to kill someone in the middle of the night would expose his identity. Since he was targeting Guan Wenjun and Qiao Lanshu, he should have wanted to keep his identity hidden.","All these illogical points suddenly made perfect sense now.","Lao Wu knew that Qiao Lanshu was alone in the room.","He knew that Xiao Zhou and Guan Wenjun were sleeping in the same room.","Qin Yuanzheng's face looked terrible, but at this moment, he couldn't bring himself to scold Qiao Lanshu for being disobedient and traveling all this way to such a dangerous place.","Because the information Qiao Lanshu provided him was indeed very useful, even crucial.","Qiao Lanshu had taken such a huge risk only because she was worried about him. He felt somewhat touched, yet also a bit angry.","In short, he felt he wasn't worth Qiao Lanshu taking such a risk. If anything happened to her, how could he live with himself for the rest of his life?","Qin Yuanzheng's expression was incredibly complex.","He glanced at Guan Wenjun and said, \"Come inside, I have something to ask you.\"","Guan Wenjun followed Qin Yuanzheng into the room. Captain Niu felt the atmosphere between them was a bit strange and was too embarrassed to follow them in, so he continued to squat outside.","Qin Yuanzheng brought Guan Wenjun into the room and then asked him about Xiao Zhou, the administrator.","He asked if there was anything unusual about him during the two days they spent together.","Guan Wenjun mentioned a few things, and then asked, \"Why, do you think there is a problem with Xiao Zhou?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"From the sound of it, he is indeed highly suspicious.\"","Guan Wenjun thought for a moment and said, \"Tonight, when I came out with my gun, if Xiao Zhou hadn't yelled and screamed, I might have shot that guy dead.\"","When he came out with the gun at that time, his intention was to take a shot and knock the opponent down first.","But Xiao Zhou might have been frightened and started screaming, which exposed the fact that Guan Wenjun had a gun.","So the dark figure quickly hid in the bushes and then ran off into the mountains.","Causing him to miss the best opportunity.","Guan Wenjun recounted this incident as well. As the three of them sat in the room and analyzed the situation, they immediately felt that Administrator Xiao Zhou was very suspicious.","Guan Wenjun said with some frustration, \"This Xiao Zhou looks completely normal. I really didn't notice any issues with him before. These people sure know how to disguise themselves!\"","Xiao Zhou had explicitly claimed to be an educated youth, so Guan Wenjun never suspected a thing.","Qin Yuanzheng formed a plan in his mind. He stood up and said to Guan Wenjun, \"This matter is of utmost importance. I must leave right away to rendezvous with Si Zhemao. You stay here with my wife and take good care of her. Don't run around anymore. I will be back to meet up with you by twelve noon tomorrow at the latest.\"","Hearing Qin Yuanzheng say this, Guan Wenjun knew the matter was settled. It seemed he would also get a share of the credit this time!","Guan Wenjun felt delighted inside. He said, \"Lao Qin, don't worry, I will definitely take good care of your wife!\"","Qin Yuanzheng said in a deep voice, \"Then go make something for my wife to eat first. She's hungry.\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun actually had no idea how to cook.","But at this very moment, he couldn't possibly admit that.","He immediately said, \"Alright, I'll go right now!\"","With that, he ran outside and found Captain Niu. \"Captain Niu, do you know how to make noodles? Or steam buns or something?\"","Captain Niu immediately replied, \"Sure do. What's up, Comrade Guan? Are you hungry? How about I go back to my house and get some for you?\"","Guan Wenjun shook his head. \"No need, how could we use your family's rations? There's flour here, could you help make some noodles?\"","Captain Niu was currently worrying about the situation with Lao Wu. No one could sleep, and he didn't want to go home either. After all, he would just be anxious if he went back, so it was better to stay here at the forestry farm and wait for news.","Therefore, he stood up and said, \"Making wheat-based food is my specialty. Comrade Xiao Guan, if you don't know how, I can teach you.\"","Guan Wenjun didn't really want to learn. He just said, \"Then I'll just tend the fire and boil the water for you.\"","Making noodles was too complicated; he just didn't have the brains for it.","Qin Yuanzheng returned to the room, looked at Qiao Lanshu, and said softly, \"Wait for me here. I'll come pick you up tomorrow morning.\"","Qiao Lanshu knew that Qin Yuanzheng had to go. After all, this was his mission; even Si Zhemao and Guan Wenjun were just assisting him.","Qiao Lanshu looked at him with concern. \"You must be careful. Watch out for their explosives, and make sure you don't get hurt, okay?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded, walked over to cup her face, kissed her, and said softly, \"The information you provided is very helpful to me. Don't worry, I will be careful.\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at Qin Yuanzheng. She was silent for a moment before adding, \"Brother Zheng, if you don't take good care of yourself, and if some accident happens...\"","She paused, then gritted her teeth and said, \"I'll take your child and remarry, you hear me?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng's expression darkened. He stared at Qiao Lanshu for a while and said in a low voice, \"You wouldn't dare.\"","He glanced at Qiao Lanshu's belly, and after a few seconds, he added, \"Don't worry, I will definitely come back in one piece. When the time comes, we will thoroughly settle the score about you and Guan Wenjun playing pretend husband and wife this time.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Seeing that it was about time, Qin Yuanzheng stood up, reached out to rub Qiao Lanshu's hair, and said softly, \"I'm leaving now. Rest well.\"","Qiao Lanshu quickly got down from the kang and followed Qin Yuanzheng to the door.","Her gaze was full of reluctance to part, as if he might never return.","Qin Yuanzheng's heart softened again.","He pulled a pistol from his waist, handed it to Qiao Lanshu, and said softly, \"Keep this for self-defense.\"","Saying that, he first unloaded the bullets, and then showed Qiao Lanshu how to use it. \"Pull this here, then press this, and that's it. Did you get it?\"","Qiao Lanshu had learned it, but she didn't take it.","When carrying out a mission, having an extra weapon meant an extra chance of survival.","Qiao Lanshu pushed the gun back and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, they have hunting rifles here, and I know how to use them. Keep this one for your own self-defense. Remember, whatever you do, don't let anything happen to you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng inspected the hunting rifle Qiao Lanshu mentioned.","This hunting rifle was used by hunters for catching prey; it wasn't a military-grade weapon.","However, the method of operation was quite similar. Qin Yuanzheng was somewhat surprised that Qiao Lanshu actually knew how to use it.","He suddenly realized that his little wife seemed to hold quite a few surprises that he didn't know about.","But now was not the time to ask about such things.","He handed the hunting rifle to Qiao Lanshu and told her, \"I will be going now. Don't stay by yourself. Hurry and go stay with Guan Wenjun.\"","Earlier, he had been angry that Guan Wenjun and Qiao Lanshu were sharing a room, yet now he was the one urging them to stay together.","At the end of the day, Qin Yuanzheng's concern for Qiao Lanshu's safety far outweighed his jealousy."]},{"number":167,"title":"Chapter 167: The Dust Settles","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng left in a hurry overnight.","Qiao Lanshu followed him to the open clearing outside the dormitory, standing there and watching him leave.","Dressed in all black, it wasn't long before his silhouette blended perfectly into the dark night, no longer visible.","Qiao Lanshu stood there, her expression showing a mix of worry and reluctance to part.","Captain Niu was in administrator Xiao Zhou's room kneading dough, getting ready to make noodles.","Guan Wenjuan was already crouching in front of the stove, stoking the fire and bringing the water in the pot to a boil.","Hearing the commotion, he walked out and saw Qiao Lanshu standing at the door in a daze, like a wife waiting for her husband's return.","Feeling a bit helpless, he walked out and said to her, \"Hurry up and come inside. Didn't you say you were hungry? Captain Niu is cooking noodles for you.\"","Guan Wenjuan had come here this time supposedly to assist Qin Yuanzheng and Si Zhemao when necessary.","As it turned out, he wasn't even given a chance to help.","A perfectly capable man with nowhere to put his skills to use, he was reduced to crouching here, tending the fire and cooking noodles.","Guan Wenjuan said to Qiao Lanshu, \"If that Xiao Zhou really is a spy, Comrade Xiao Qiao, then you've rendered a great service.\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't make much of it. She replied, \"I came here on my own accord, not through any organizational arrangement. It's best if I can help, but if I can't, I just try not to hold you guys back. As for rendering a great service, it really doesn't matter to me.\"","Guan Wenjuan led Qiao Lanshu into administrator Xiao Zhou's room. Captain Niu had already pulled the noodles and dropped them into the boiling pot.","He turned around, saw Qiao Lanshu and Guan Wenjuan enter, and asked, \"Hey, Comrade Guan, where did your colleague go? Leaving in the middle of the night like this?\"","As he spoke, Captain Niu cast a highly complicated look at Qiao Lanshu.","After all, that man had just carried Comrade Guan's wife into the room, and the two had been alone in there for quite a while.","As the female comrade's husband, Comrade Guan hadn't even dared to utter a single word of protest.","He only dared to crouch at the courtyard gate with him. He was simply too cowardly.","The way Captain Niu looked at Comrade Guan and Qiao Lanshu was full of suspicion.","Qiao Lanshu wasn't in a good mood right now, so she didn't bother to explain.","Guan Wenjuan brought a small stool for Qiao Lanshu, having her sit next to the table, and poured her a cup of hot tea. He said very politely, \"Here, Comrade Xiao Qiao, have some hot tea. The noodles will be ready soon, just bear with the hunger a little longer.\"","Captain Niu: \"...\"","Captain Niu really couldn't understand it. He just felt that Comrade Guan must love his wife too much.","Even after all this, he was still absolutely devoted to her.","The fact that Qiao Lanshu could sense something was wrong with administrator Xiao Zhou was a very important piece of information.","Guan Wenjuan knew how crucial such information was during a mission.","Sometimes, it was exactly these kinds of details that could maximally reduce casualties among the mission personnel.","Therefore, he was very polite, even highly respectful, towards Qiao Lanshu right now.","He knew Captain Niu had misunderstood the situation.","But until the dust settled, he couldn't tell Captain Niu the truth either.","He walked over to the stove, sat on a small stool, and said to Captain Niu, \"Captain Niu, my colleague from just now is with the inspection team. He has already headed out overnight to help track down Lao Wu.\"","Hearing this, Captain Niu suddenly got nervous and said, \"No way? He went to chase after Lao Wu just like that? Did you tell him that Lao Wu is covered in explosives?\"","Guan Wenjuan nodded. \"I told him. He will be careful.\"","Captain Niu immediately started worrying again. \"Sigh, this is something we can't handle. Lao Wu, he... he's too dangerous, sigh...\"","Captain Niu didn't know what else to say.","He just kept sighing heavily, silently cooking the noodles as he did so.","He cooked a large pot of noodles and scooped them out into a basin.","There were also napa cabbages, sweet potatoes, and potatoes in the room, all of which administrator Xiao Zhou had just brought back from the town yesterday.","Captain Niu stir-fried some sweet and sour cabbage, then brought out a bottle of soybean paste for Guan Wenjuan and Qiao Lanshu to mix with their noodles.","In the middle of the night, they just had to make do with this. Captain Niu wasn't in the mood to make anything else anyway.","However, his noodle-making skills were quite good. The noodles were uniform, distinct, and very chewy.","Having been busy all night, Guan Wenjuan was also hungry. He first served a bowl for Qiao Lanshu, then served one for himself, and squatted next to her to start eating.","Qiao Lanshu was indeed hungry. Since arriving here, she hadn't been in the mood to eat, and she had been even more afraid to sleep at night.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng tonight had relaxed her tense heart a bit, and she began to feel exhausted and hungry.","She took a bite of the noodles and asked Captain Niu, \"Captain, aren't you going to eat?\"","Now, the one with no appetite was Captain Niu.","Captain Niu squatted in front of the stove, rolled a cigarette using a torn piece of newspaper, and said while smoking, \"At a time like this, how could I possibly eat? Who knows what's going on with Lao Wu, and Xiao Zhou hasn't been rescued yet. When this news spreads tomorrow, I reckon I'll be taken in for questioning. Sigh, tell me, what kind of mess is this?\"","He had only enjoyed a few years of peaceful life before a spy was discovered hiding in the forestry farm.","Not only did that guy blow up the orchard, but he also strapped explosives all over his body, hijacked a hostage and the forestry farm's tractor, and fled.","He was too useless as a captain, always half a beat too slow in handling things. He feared he would be arrested and interrogated by the public security comrades later.","After all, the fact that a spy could stay in the forestry farm for over ten years was an extremely serious matter in itself.","As the village's captain, he bore an undeniable responsibility.","Seeing his poor complexion, Guan Wenjuan ate his noodles and comforted him, \"Captain Niu, don't be so upset. Actually, if you think about it from another angle,\"","He paused, slurped another mouthful of noodles, and continued:","\"When the time comes, you won't be the only one taken in for questioning. There's also your village party secretary, all the administrators at the forestry farm, several leaders above the forestry farm, the personnel department staff who originally recruited Lao Wu, and the various leaders in your town. They will all have to be taken in for questioning. With so many people, there's nothing to worry about. At least you'll have company.\"","Captain Niu: \"...\"","He silently glanced at Comrade Guan and told him, \"Comrade Guan, you might as well not have comforted me. Hearing that just makes me panic even more.\"","People from the village, the forestry farm, and the town—everyone was going to be taken in for questioning and investigation. They might even have their backgrounds investigated all over again.","It might even be handed over to the Revolutionary Committee to take charge.","Once something was dug up, wouldn't public parading through the streets closely follow?","He was doomed. The more Captain Niu thought about it, the more panicked he became. He didn't even have the heart to smoke anymore.","He had been an honest and simple farmer his whole life, yet near the end of it, he had to face such a hurdle.","Captain Niu squatted by the door, took a deep drag of his cigarette, and started sighing heavily again.","...","The people in the village also stayed awake all night, everyone worried that there might still be leftover explosives in the mountains.","Several administrators from the forestry farm had originally already taken their leave to go home and prepare for the Spring Festival.","But now, they too had received notices and were rushing back to the forestry farm overnight.","No one knew what to do; they could only wait helplessly.","Waiting for the public security comrades who went to hunt down Lao Wu to bring them good news.","After Qiao Lanshu finished a bowl of noodles, she returned to the room, lay down on the kang, covered herself with a quilt, and prepared to sleep.","Guan Wenjun followed her into the room, no longer caring about the old rule that men and women should not be too close.","Guan Wenjun didn't close the door; it was left wide open.","He didn't dare to close it, afraid that if Qin Yuanzheng questioned him later, he wouldn't be able to explain himself!","He sat on a chair, poured himself a cup of hot water, and watched as Qiao Lanshu got straight onto the kang to sleep without even taking off her coat. Surprised, he asked, \"You're going to sleep just like that?\"","Qiao Lanshu hadn't slept much for three days, and now she was getting sleepy.","She yawned, wrapped herself in the quilt, rolled over to face away from Guan Wenjun, and said, \"What else is there to do but sleep? There's nothing going on right now, right? Do you need something?\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun: \"My main task right now is to protect you. Didn't you hear Old Qin give me the order?\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't answer him because she had already fallen asleep.","Guan Wenjun was still talking:","\"I didn't want to come in either, but didn't Old Qin tell me to stay with you and not separate? He was afraid you might run into some trouble... Sigh, I wonder how things are going on their end. Has Lao Wu been caught? And that Xiao Zhou, why did he collude with Lao Wu? I've been thinking about it for a long time and still can't figure it out. Tell me, what is an educated youth like him after?\"","Guan Wenjun waited for a while but didn't hear Qiao Lanshu's voice.","He put down his water cup and called out to her, \"Hey? Comrade Xiao Qiao, are you asleep?\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun stood up, walked over to take a look at Qiao Lanshu, and then muttered, \"You really fell asleep? You really have a carefree heart.\"","Muttering to himself, Guan Wenjun sat back down on the chair.","Thinking about it carefully, he felt that Qiao Lanshu was quite a fascinating person, or at least, quite smart.","When encountering danger, she ran faster than anyone else and hid better than anyone else.","Now that the crisis was resolved, she ate and drank her fill, and went straight to bed.","Leaving him alone as her private bodyguard, unable to rest, only able to stay in the room and guard her.","Captain Niu couldn't sleep. It just so happened that the other three administrators of the forestry center had arrived, so he stayed in the courtyard chatting with them.","These three administrators were different from Lao Wu and the others. Lao Wu was a loner; he had no parents and was unmarried.","Xiao Zhou was an educated youth from out of town and had no family here either.","So the two of them were left on duty at the forestry center, spending the Spring Festival there.","The other three were locals, so they all took time off to go home for the Spring Festival.","Who knew something like this would happen? The villagers had called the three of them back in the middle of the night.","After Captain Niu explained the whole story to them, the three administrators were stunned.","The four men sat in a row on the steps outside the door, each holding a cigarette, and spoke silently: \"This Lao Wu, it's one thing if he seeks his own death, but why did he have to drag us down with him?\"","\"It's a pity about that orchard. They are all jujube trees, and jujubes are really expensive this year.\"","\"Captain, can we still go home and say goodbye to our families? Please don't let them arrest us right now.\"","Captain Niu said with a lack of confidence, \"Say goodbye to what? We haven't done anything wrong, so we have nothing to fear! Lao Wu is the one who committed the crime, what does it have to do with us? We will definitely be fine, don't worry.\"","Although that was true.","The four of them still sat in a row smoking, their faces full of melancholy.","Guan Wenjun glanced at them, shook his head, and sighed.","...","At eight o'clock the next morning, Qiao Lanshu still hadn't woken up.","Guan Wenjun was so sleepy that his eyes were bloodshot. He squatted at the door, leaning against the house, holding a cup of strong tea, and watched the people walking around in the courtyard.","As soon as the day broke, the village party secretary and some young and strong men from the village all came over.","A group of people stood in the courtyard, chattering away. It was very noisy.","Captain Niu didn't forget to arrange for two female commune members from the village to start a fire and make breakfast. After all, Guan Wenjun and Qiao Lanshu still had to eat. They were city cadres here on a business trip, and Captain Niu didn't dare to neglect them.","Thirty or forty people stood in the courtyard talking, their voices very loud.","Guan Wenjun turned his head and looked toward the kang. Qiao Lanshu still wasn't awake.","She was really something. Even with all this noise, she could still sleep.","Guan Wenjun closed the door, came out of the room, and stood on the steps at the door to continue drinking tea.","Drinking strong tea all night didn't make him any more energetic; instead, he felt even more exhausted.","Seeing him come out, Captain Niu hurried over and asked, \"Comrade Guan, do you have any channels to get some news? How are Lao Wu and the others doing now?\"","Guan Wenjun shook his head. \"If you want to ask, you have to go to the police station in town. Right now, I'm in the same boat as you. Aside from waiting for my colleagues to return, there's nothing else I can do.\"","Captain Niu said anxiously, \"As soon as it was light, I arranged for someone to go to the police station in town. They probably haven't arrived yet at this time. Sigh, I'm worried to death.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had said he would come to pick up Qiao Lanshu before noon, so Guan Wenjun wasn't too anxious.","Qiao Lanshu was even less anxious. Out of the dozens of people present, she was the only one who could sleep.","She hadn't even woken up yet.","At around nine o'clock, Guan Wenjun squatted at the door of Qiao Lanshu's room, holding a bowl of wild vegetable dough drop soup and an ear of corn, eating his breakfast.","Qiao Lanshu still hadn't woken up. She could really sleep!","As long as she didn't wake up, Guan Wenjun didn't dare go anywhere; he only dared to guard the door for her.","Leaving everything else aside, with dozens of men in the courtyard, Guan Wenjun wouldn't dare leave Qiao Lanshu's side.","With Qiao Lanshu's looks, it would be quite hard for her not to attract attention.","At this moment, the sound of a car came from afar.","A young man suddenly shouted, \"Look, a car! A car is coming!\"","Everyone swarmed to the intersection, staring at the approaching car in the distance.","Guan Wenjun also stood up abruptly, the ear of corn still dangling from his mouth. He took two steps forward and stood on his tiptoes to look toward the intersection.","It was a car they had never seen before.","The car slowly stopped at the intersection of their forestry center, and then a tall, fully armed man with his face covered got out of the car.","Seeing the gun slung over the man's back, the crowd silently took several steps back. \"Captain, who is this?\"","Captain Niu recognized him. \"Oh my, Comrade Guan, isn't this your colleague?\"","It was too dark last night to see clearly.","He actually hadn't known that this man was carrying a gun!","Also, he silently wondered to himself, were city forestry centers this particular?","Did administrators have to carry weapons when they traveled?","One slung on the back, one tucked in the waist, and one strapped to the leg?","It looked quite terrifying."]},{"number":168,"title":"Chapter 168: How Vulgar","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng had just finished his business. Without even sparing a moment to take a sip of water, he hurriedly drove back to pick up Qiao Lanshu.","Now that the mission was completed, there was no need for Qin Yuanzheng to hide anything anymore.","The list of villagers in this village had been in Si Zhemao's hands since last night. Together with the people from the township government, they had already conducted a simple filtering and screening of everyone.","The final result was exactly as Qiao Lanshu had said. Besides Lao Wu, Xiao Zhou was indeed the most suspicious.","Xiao Zhou was an educated youth from a big city, but he had no parents and grew up in an orphanage.","Moreover, it seemed that he was a child born during the war, forced upon a local girl by enemy soldiers.","He indeed carried half of the enemy country's bloodline in his veins.","It was unknown whether those people had found him after he grew up and what they might have promised him.","After all, this kind of case was not happening for the first time.","In order to infiltrate from the inside out, those people would abandon some children as orphans, who would then be picked up and adopted by orphanages or farmers.","When the children grew to be teenagers, they would come find them, make them acknowledge their ancestry, and have them serve their country.","As long as such children hid well, they were very difficult to discover.","Si Zhemao was an investigator specializing in catching spies and special agents, and this was not the first time he had encountered such a case.","Therefore, he handled this matter very quickly.","Since it was confirmed that the hostage on the vehicle did not need to be rescued, it became much easier to deal with.","Because Lao Wu had explosives on him, they could not let him reach the town or the village; they could only intercept him on the mountain road.","The best method was a long-range sniper shot to blow out the tractor's tires and cripple Lao Wu's hands.","Lao Wu noticed something was wrong and threatened them by strangling Xiao Zhou's neck. Upon realizing this trick was useless, Lao Wu pushed Xiao Zhou off the vehicle and drove the tractor madly toward a nearby village.","There were many villages at this time. In densely populated areas, walking just one or two kilometers along a mountain road would lead to a village.","Lao Wu knew he was doomed, so he did not want to fall into the hands of Si Zhemao and the others.","He wanted to fight to the bitter end and drag a few innocent people down with him.","Seeing that the tractor had already entered the village entrance, neither Si Zhemao's men nor the military troops dared to approach, considering Lao Wu was covered in explosives.","Qin Yuanzheng made a prompt decision. He aimed at Lao Wu's head and, just as Lao Wu was about to escape the firing range, shot him right in the temple.","Although the higher-ups had ordered to capture him alive, there was no other way in this situation. He could only finish it with one shot to avoid greater losses and casualties.","As for Xiao Zhou, after being pushed off the tractor, he was injured from the fall. His forehead was bleeding, and his arm was fractured.","Hearing the gunshot, Xiao Zhou saw Lao Wu tumble from the tractor's driver seat not far away and crash onto the ground, blood spilling everywhere.","Xiao Zhou trembled all over, his face pale as he cried out for help, \"Help, help, save me!\"","Si Zhemao put away his binoculars and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Tie up this Xiao Zhou. I have to interrogate him personally.\"","Saying this, Si Zhemao waved his hand. Two people stepped out from behind him and headed down the mountain to apprehend Xiao Zhou.","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent for a moment before saying, \"Hold on!\"","Si Zhemao asked, \"What's wrong? That Lao Wu is already dead, but this Xiao Zhou must be taken back alive, otherwise how am I going to explain this to the higher-ups?\"","Qin Yuanzheng said in a low voice, \"First, rule out whether he has explosives on him.\"","Si Zhemao slapped his forehead. \"If you hadn't mentioned it, I would have damn near forgotten. This kid is also a suspect; we need to treat him with caution.\"","Qin Yuanzheng added, \"I'll go over and take a look.\"","Si Zhemao nodded. \"Alright, be careful.\"","Qin Yuanzheng then led four or five people and headed down the mountain.","Seeing the group of fully armed men in black walking over, Xiao Zhou's heart instantly pounded wildly.","Xiao Zhou was still young; naturally, he did not want to die.","However, the shock of Lao Wu's death on him was indescribable.","It was as if he had only just realized that the Grim Reaper had always been standing right behind him. The moment he revealed a flaw, his fate would become just like Lao Wu's.","He shouldn't have been exposed yet, right?","Xiao Zhou thought in terror.","For people like them, once exposed, they would have to commit seppuku.","Right, Lao Wu had stuffed explosives into his arms, ordering him to blow up the investigator this time. Among the group of men in black coming over now, was there an investigator?","Just as Xiao Zhou's mind was in turmoil, Qin Yuanzheng aimed his gun at him. \"Don't move!\"","Sitting on the ground with a fractured arm and a bloody face, Xiao Zhou quickly raised his good hand, swallowed hard, and said, \"Comrade, I am innocent. I am a hostage. Please save me, my arm is broken.\"","Qin Yuanzheng did not approach immediately. His gaze was fixed tightly on Xiao Zhou. \"Take off all your clothes and walk over here naked.\"","Xiao Zhou was speechless.","Xiao Zhou looked at them guiltily. \"Comrade, it's... it's too cold. Can I not take them off?\"","The soldiers behind Qin Yuanzheng cocked their guns. The dark muzzles pointed at Xiao Zhou as they shouted sternly, \"Cut the crap! Take them off quickly!\"","The group was about six or seven meters away from Xiao Zhou, all pointing their guns at him.","In the howling cold wind of the winter night, Xiao Zhou stood up trembling and began to undress.","He had just taken off his padded jacket and placed it on the ground when Qin Yuanzheng suddenly shouted, \"What is that?\"","Wrapped inside the padded jacket was a package enclosed in newspaper, and its shape looked highly suspicious.","Seeing that he could no longer hide it, Xiao Zhou suddenly reached out and dug into his pants pocket.","Subsequently, with a bang, Qin Yuanzheng fired a shot, hitting his arm.","Following that, there were two more bangs. Both of Xiao Zhou's legs were shot. He fell to his knees, his face pale, his limbs suddenly unable to move.","Taking advantage of this opportunity, the group fiercely lunged forward, directly stripped off Xiao Zhou's clothes, and tied him up tightly.","Afterward, they searched Xiao Zhou's clothes and pants, discovering two hand grenades and two packs of explosives.","These were given to him by Lao Wu. Before throwing him off the vehicle, Lao Wu had given him one final order: to blow up the investigator.","When Qin Yuanzheng saw these, he felt a lingering fear in his heart.","If Qiao Lanshu had not told him about Xiao Zhou's abnormalities, he might have tried his utmost to rescue this hostage.","At that time, there was no telling what would have happened...","Xiao Zhou was pinned to the ground, tied up so tightly he resembled a rice dumpling.","He stared dead at Qin Yuanzheng, his eyes filled with both terror and unwillingness. Staring at Qin Yuanzheng, he asked, \"Are you the investigator this time? What is your name?\"","Qin Yuanzheng confiscated the two hand grenades and the two packs of explosives. Then, he glanced at Xiao Zhou and said, \"I am not the investigator. However, you will be able to see him very soon.\"","Given Si Zhemao's interrogation methods, Xiao Zhou would probably remember Si Zhemao for the rest of his life.","Xiao Zhou was speechless.","Xiao Zhou was taken away, and the aftermath of the incident was handled by Si Zhemao.","Qin Yuanzheng could finally take Qiao Lanshu home.","The one who reaped the biggest harvest this time was undoubtedly Guan Wenjuan.","He had done practically nothing and was simply carried to success by the two big shots, Si Zhemao and Qin Yuanzheng.","He didn't put in the hard work, but he still got a share of the credit.","...","Qin Yuanzheng arrived at the entrance of the dormitory area and looked at the group of villagers standing in the open space outside.","He pulled down the black cloth covering his face, glanced at Captain Niu who was standing at the very front, and asked,","\"Why is everyone gathered here? The mountains haven't been thoroughly searched yet, and we can't rule out the possibility of leftover explosives. It's best if the villagers don't gather around. Have them return to the village and stay there. We need to set up police tape around the orchard and the forestry center to keep people out. Mountain patrols will only resume when an official notice is issued.\"","Hearing this, Captain Niu nodded subconsciously, \"Yes, yes, comrade. I understand. I'll give the orders right away. Actually, Comrade Guan warned us last night not to let anyone into the mountains, so I already made an announcement over the loudspeakers. I'll have someone set up the warning lines right now.\"","Pausing for a moment, Captain Niu asked again, \"Um, comrade, what's the situation with Lao Wu and Xiao Zhou?\"","Everyone fell silent instantly, all eyes fixed on Qin Yuanzheng.","No one had been able to sleep the entire night; they all just wanted to know how the situation had unfolded.","Where on earth did Lao Wu run off to with all those explosives?","Qin Yuanzheng's footsteps faltered and he stopped. For now, this matter could not be spread around.","Because Si Zhemao still needed to investigate the people in the surrounding villages and towns. Furthermore, he had to look into the social connections of Lao Wu and Xiao Zhou to uncover all their superiors and subordinates.","In this era, news traveled slowly. As long as the information didn't leak and people in other places remained unaware, Si Zhemao still had room to maneuver.","Qin Yuanzheng walked up to Captain Niu. After a second of silence, he said, \"Lao Wu took Xiao Zhou hostage and fled. We have already dispatched people to hunt them down. You don't need to worry about this. Go back to the village first, go to work as usual, and act like nothing happened. Just wait for further notice from the town's public security bureau.\"","Upon hearing this, the crowd immediately broke out into a cacophony of chatter.","Captain Niu's expression was quite complicated upon hearing the news. He said, \"Lao Wu has a lot of explosives on him. You have to stay close on his tail; don't let him harm anyone else.\"","Qin Yuanzheng felt that Captain Niu was a pretty decent guy. He nodded, \"Rest assured, we know.\"","With that, he turned around and walked toward the houses in the dormitory area.","Captain Niu wanted to ask a few more questions, but seeing Qin Yuanzheng walk away, he didn't have the courage to call out to him.","After all, his intuition told him that this tall, fully armed, and majestic-looking man was far from simple.","He definitely wasn't an ordinary forestry cadre.","He looked more like someone from a special forces unit.","Captain Niu didn't know what else to do now, so naturally, he just followed Qin Yuanzheng's instructions.","He immediately told all the villagers to return to the village, asked the village party secretary to help soothe their emotions, and then assigned tasks so everyone could go work in the fields.","After all, the crops in the fields couldn't be left unattended.","The villagers in the courtyard slowly dispersed.","Qin Yuanzheng walked over and saw Guan Wenjun standing at the door to Qiao Lanshu's room.","Holding a bowl of dough drop soup in one hand and a corncob in the other, Guan Wenjun approached Qin Yuanzheng and asked in a low voice, \"Is it taken care of?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"The older one is dead, and the younger one was captured alive. My mission is complete, and I can go back.\"","Guan Wenjun breathed a sigh of relief. He knew that with Qin Yuanzheng taking action, there would definitely be no problems!","Qin Yuanzheng then asked, \"What is Comrade Xiao Qiao doing?\"","Trailing behind him, Guan Wenjun replied, \"She ate a bowl of noodles in the middle of the night yesterday and then went back to her room to sleep. She hasn't woken up since. She must be exhausted. She sure can sleep.\"","Qin Yuanzheng said, \"She only went to sleep in the middle of the night, and it's not too late right now. She really should get more rest.\"","Standing at the door, Guan Wenjun finished the porridge in his bowl and asked, \"Lao Qin, can I catch a ride in your car to town later? My car is still parked at the town school's playground.\"","Qin Yuanzheng replied, \"No, you need to stay here and assist Si Zhemao with the investigation.\"","Guan Wenjun had thought he could finally go home. Hearing this, he looked as if the sky had fallen. \"Why? Shouldn't the aftermath be the investigators' job?\"","Qin Yuanzheng explained, \"Strictly speaking, it's the responsibility of the Revolutionary Committee and the Public Security Bureau. You need to lead a team into the mountains to check for leftover explosives. You also need to carefully screen the forestry center administrators and the villagers again. The job isn't done, so you can't leave yet.\"","Guan Wenjun was speechless.","After all that, Qin Yuanzheng was the only one who got to go home.","Actually, if this were in the past, Qin Yuanzheng would have stayed behind to help with the investigation too.","But wasn't Qiao Lanshu here now?","He just wanted to take his wife home first. He'd leave the rest of the cleanup to Guan Wenjun.","Guan Wenjun was exactly in need of opportunities, so this was the perfect chance for him to prove himself.","...","Qin Yuanzheng entered the room and saw Qiao Lanshu lying on the kang bed with her eyes closed, wearing a thick padded jacket and wrapped in a quilt.","He walked in, sat on the edge of the bed, and called out softly, \"Wife, wake up. We can go home now.\"","Hearing his voice, Qiao Lanshu's eyelids fluttered, and she immediately opened her eyes. \"Brother Zheng? You're back?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. Before he could speak, he saw Qiao Lanshu sit up groggily and, without a word, start stripping off his clothes.","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","He grabbed her hands and whispered, \"The door is still open. Are you in that much of a hurry?\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't stop, continuing to pull at his shirt. \"Take your clothes off so I can see if you're hurt.\"","This time, Qin Yuanzheng really wasn't injured.","Because Lao Wu was carrying a lot of explosives, he and his men had tracked and sniped from a distance without getting close.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu's anxious demeanor, he couldn't bear to refuse her, so he said, \"Wait a moment, let me go shut the door.\"","Then, he walked over to close the door while simultaneously taking off his clothes and removing his gear.","Standing at the doorway, Guan Wenjun was speechless.","His mouth fell open slightly as he stared at Qin Yuanzheng in disbelief. \"Are you... are you two in that much of a rush? How about eating some breakfast first? Exercising on an empty stomach isn't very good for you, is it?\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't bother explaining, simply saying, \"Leave some food for Xiao Qiao, thanks.\"","With that, he shut the door.","Guan Wenjun was completely speechless.","Immediately after, Guan Wenjun heard Qiao Lanshu's voice from inside the room: \"Brother Zheng, hurry up and take them off. You have to strip completely naked.\"","Qin Yuanzheng coaxed her softly, \"Alright, alright, I'm taking them off now. Do I need to take my pants off too?\"","Qiao Lanshu replied, \"Of course. It won't work if you don't take off your pants. You have to take everything off.\"","Guan Wenjun placed his bowl on the ground, covered his ears with both hands, and looked up at the sky.","Damn, how vulgar!"]},{"number":169,"title":"Chapter 169: Never crawled through the bushes before, huh","paragraphs":["Inside the room, Qin Yuanzheng was very obedient to his wife.","When his wife told him to strip naked, he unloaded all his gear and took off his shirt and pants.","All that was left on his body was a pair of black briefs.","With broad shoulders, a narrow waist, long legs, and a body full of firm, lean muscle, his physique was quite spectacular.","Even though they had been together for so long and already had a child, Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but blush when she saw Qin Yuanzheng like this.","Standing by the edge of the kang bed, Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu. He reached out, hooked a finger into the waistband of his briefs, and tugged it while looking at her, asking deliberately, Chief, should I take this off too?","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Her face instantly turned red. Getting down from the kang, she glared at him. You can take it off if you want. It's up to you.","That glare of hers instantly made his blood surge, and his body gave her a salute.","However, this wasn't their own home, and neither the time nor the place was appropriate.","Qin Yuanzheng held himself back.","He said in a low voice, I'll take it off when we get back, okay?","Qiao Lanshu smiled, blushing. She circled Qin Yuanzheng twice and really didn't see any wounds on him.","Her anxious heart finally settled completely.","She walked behind Qin Yuanzheng, reached out to stroke his lower back, and then slowly slid her hands forward until they reached his abdomen, poking him in the belly button.","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","He pressed down on her mischievous little hand, staring at her with heavy breathing. Is this how you perform a physical examination? Looking with your eyes isn't enough, you have to use your hands to touch?","Qiao Lanshu said seriously, Of course. I need to see if you have any internal injuries. Even though you look fine, what if you have internal injuries and just aren't telling me?","Saying that, she deliberately pressed on his pectoral muscle and looked up at him. Does it hurt here?","Qin Yuanzheng said in a hoarse voice, It doesn't hurt, but it's definitely not very comfortable.","The smile on Qiao Lanshu's face froze, and she immediately looked at him with concern. Really?","She pressed it again as she spoke. Why is it uncomfortable? Do you really have an internal injury?","Qin Yuanzheng whispered in her ear, It doesn't hurt, but it tickles a bit. The more you press, the more it tickles.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","She quickly withdrew her hand.","Only then did she realize she had been pressing on some indescribable spots.","Forget it, if it was really like that, she could only touch Qin Yuanzheng's face, since everything below the neck was indescribable.","Qiao Lanshu realized that Qin Yuanzheng was deliberately teasing her.","She reached out and pinched his waist. That's for making fun of me.","Qin Yuanzheng's whole body tensed up. He quickly grabbed her hand and pressed it against his crotch. Chief, how about checking here too? It's even more uncomfortable here.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu suddenly gave him a light slap.","Qin Yuanzheng let out a muffled groan, bending over slightly, and stared at Qiao Lanshu while panting heavily. Good hit, want to hit it again?","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qin Yuanzheng held her hand down. How is one slap enough? Hit it a few more times, why don't you? Use more force, vent your anger.","With her hand held by him, Qiao Lanshu now knew for sure that Qin Yuanzheng was perfectly fine.","Not only was he uninjured, but he was also full of vigor.","He had been on a mission for three or four days, yet his energy was still so high.","She tried to pull her hand back but couldn't. Held down by him, Qin Yuanzheng leaned in close and asked in a low voice, What's wrong, Chief? Are you done hitting?","Qiao Lanshu really couldn't stand him anymore and whispered, Don't call me Chief, aren't you ashamed?","Qin Yuanzheng then asked, If I don't call you Chief, should I call you Comrade?","Qiao Lanshu covered his mouth and whispered, Hurry up and put your clothes on. We can talk about things when we get home.","Qiao Lanshu was truly unable to handle this.","Once Qin Yuanzheng started acting shameless, she stood no chance.","Qin Yuanzheng also knew this wasn't appropriate, otherwise, he would have stripped completely bare and carried Qiao Lanshu onto the kang by now.","Thinking of Guan Wenjun guarding outside, and Captain Niu, as well as the fact that Qiao Lanshu hadn't eaten breakfast yet and was probably hungry.","He finally let go, releasing Qiao Lanshu, and bent down to pick up his clothes and start dressing.","Qiao Lanshu sat by the table, undid her somewhat messy braids, and re-braided them.","While tying her hair, she watched Qin Yuanzheng get dressed.","Truth be told, Qin Yuanzheng got dressed quickly and neatly, which was quite pleasing to the eye.","Qiao Lanshu suspected that beauty was in the eye of the beholder, because no matter how she looked at him, she found Qin Yuanzheng very handsome and attractive.","Qiao Lanshu kept staring at Qin Yuanzheng, making him feel a bit overwhelmed by her gaze.","He put all his clothes on and strapped his gear back on.","While doing this, he was also looking at Qiao Lanshu.","After getting pregnant, Qiao Lanshu had become a bit plumper. Her chin wasn't as pointed as before, and her cheeks were round and rosy, making her look like a sweet, soft, white steamed bun.","Suppressing certain unspeakable desires, Qin Yuanzheng put on his gloves, walked up to Qiao Lanshu, and asked, Are you hungry? Should I go get you something to eat?","Qiao Lanshu happened to be hungry, so she nodded. Okay, I want to eat with you.","Qin Yuanzheng smiled and ruffled her hair, messing up the hair she had just tied.","Qiao Lanshu didn't get angry; she just smiled and watched Qin Yuanzheng open the door and walk out.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng went out, he saw Guan Wenjun sitting on the front steps, covering his ears with both hands and looking up at the sky.","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't help but give him a light kick, frowning as he asked, What are you doing sitting here? With all that stuff at the Public Security Bureau and the Revolutionary Committee, why aren't you going to work?","Guan Wenjun was speechless.","Guan Wenjun turned his head and looked at Qin Yuanzheng with a shocked expression. That fast? No way, Old Qin, you can't be that weak, right? It's only been half an hour! You're already done?","As Guan Wenjun spoke, he looked at Qin Yuanzheng's strong physique with a strange expression, muttering, Could the rumors outside about you being impotent actually be true?","Qin Yuanzheng's face darkened, and he immediately went to kick him again.","Guan Wenjun reacted quickly and jumped out of the way.","He darted into the yard and said to Qin Yuanzheng, Old Qin, don't worry, I will definitely keep this a secret for you! I absolutely won't tell anyone! Just based on the fact that I benefited from you this time, our past grievances are wiped clean. You can put your mind at ease!","With that, Guan Wenjun ran off.","He had just thought he would have to guard the door for Qin Yuanzheng for at least two hours.","But in the end, he was done in half an hour.","Sigh, poor Old Qin. All that tall and strong physique was for nothing.","What a waste of such a beautiful and soft little wife.","Just because of this, Guan Wenjun felt that he couldn't hold onto his past grudges with Qin Yuanzheng anymore.","Since Qin Yuanzheng was practically impotent, he would just let him be.","Guan Wenjun left, leaving Qin Yuanzheng feeling baffled by his behavior.","But Qin Yuanzheng couldn't be bothered to care about Guan Wenjun.","He went to the next room and saw Captain Niu still stoking the fire at the stove, so he asked, Captain Niu, is there any food left?","Captain Niu quickly replied, Yes, yes, Comrade. There's wild vegetable dough drop soup, and some steamed corn. Oh right, I just made some steamed buns, why don't you take a few to eat?","Originally, there were no steamed buns in the morning.","But after Qin Yuanzheng returned, Captain Niu's heart finally settled down.","Thinking that Qin Yuanzheng hadn't eaten yet, he hurried over to steam some buns, mainly to ensure this leader ate and drank well, leaving a better impression of them.","Qin Yuanzheng happened to be hungry too. He served two bowls of dough drop soup, took two ears of corn, and four steamed buns. He said to Captain Niu, \"I'm going to take these buns to eat on the road. Food is precious, and I shouldn't just take it for free. Please accept these food stamps.\"","Saying this, Qin Yuanzheng pulled out a two-jin national food stamp from his pocket and handed it to Captain Niu.","Captain Niu hurriedly waved his hands. \"No, no, no need. Comrade, you've helped us a great deal this time. Treating you to a meal is the least we can do. How could I take your food stamps?\"","Qin Yuanzheng insisted on giving him the food stamp. \"Captain Niu, please just take it. We get subsidies for carrying out missions, I can't eat your buns for free here.\"","Saying this, Qin Yuanzheng stuffed the food stamp into his hand and walked away carrying the food.","Captain Niu: \"...\"","Captain Niu chased him to the door, watching Qin Yuanzheng carry the food into Qiao Lanshu's room.","He looked around again. Comrade Guan was nowhere to be found, having disappeared without a trace.","Captain Niu: \"...\"","Captain Niu sighed. Forget it, this matter couldn't be blamed on Comrade Guan.","If anyone's wife caught the eye of such a fully armed leader, they wouldn't have the slightest room to resist either.","Although young Comrade Guan lacked a backbone and ran away fast, he had already done his best.","...","Qin Yuanzheng returned to the room with the food, only to see that Qiao Lanshu had somehow gone back to lying on the kang bed.","Qin Yuanzheng placed the food on the table and walked over to look at her. \"Wife, why are you lying down again?\"","Qiao Lanshu sniffled and smiled. \"I'm fine, just feeling a bit tired, like I might be getting sick.\"","Qin Yuanzheng frowned. He immediately sat down beside Qiao Lanshu and reached out to touch her forehead.","It was slightly hot.","Qin Yuanzheng immediately grew tense. \"You have a fever! We need to see a doctor.\"","Qiao Lanshu said softly, \"I'll just drink some hot water and sweat it out. I probably just caught a cold, it's nothing major.\"","She was pregnant now, so there were many things she couldn't consume, especially medicine.","She didn't want to take medication, afraid it would affect the baby.","Qin Yuanzheng also thought of this.","He spoke calmly, \"Get up first and finish the dough drop soup. In a bit, I'll drive you to the county clinic to get checked out. They have traditional Chinese medicine doctors there. Getting some herbal medicine to steep in water will also help.\"","Steeping certain Chinese herbs in boiling water and drinking it like tea could treat throat inflammation, sore throats, colds, and abdominal pain or diarrhea.","Qin Yuanzheng had a strong physique and rarely got sick, so he hardly ever took medicine.","But when his mother used to be ill, she often bought Chinese medicine to drink.","He helped Qiao Lanshu sit up and had her drink a bowl of wild vegetable dough drop soup. He drank a bowl himself and ate two steamed buns.","He wrapped the remaining two ears of corn and two buns in kraft paper, put them in his pocket, and carried Qiao Lanshu out the door. \"Let's go. We're heading to the county town now. After seeing the doctor, we'll go home.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, wrapping her scarf around her cheeks.","Captain Niu stood in the courtyard, watching them with a complex expression, utterly dumbfounded.","These two weren't even pretending anymore, right out in the open in broad daylight...","Qin Yuanzheng suddenly called out, \"Captain Niu.\"","Captain Niu, who was just criticizing them in his head, suddenly stood up straight. \"Here!\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"I'm leaving now. For the remaining matters, just coordinate with the town police station.\"","Captain Niu quickly said, \"Okay, okay, understood. Take care, comrade, and have a safe trip.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded, carried Qiao Lanshu into the car, and then stepped on the gas, driving out of the village.","Halfway there, Qin Yuanzheng also saw Guan Wenjun.","Guan Wenjun was sitting on an ox cart, slowly making his way toward the town.","His car was still parked in town. He had business to attend to next and needed to drive, otherwise it would waste too much time.","From a distance, he saw Qin Yuanzheng's car approaching.","Guan Wenjun's eyes lit up, and he immediately waved. \"Old Qin! Stop the car, give me a ride!\"","Qin Yuanzheng rolled down the window and told him, \"Not going the same way.\"","Saying that, he stepped on the gas and left.","Leaving Guan Wenjun with a face full of dust.","Guan Wenjun started cursing again, \"Qin Yuanzheng, you bastard! What do you mean not going the same way? If you don't want to give me a ride, just say so!\"","Qin Yuanzheng really wasn't going the same way. Worried about Qiao Lanshu being sick, he had taken a shortcut to the county town this time and wasn't passing through the town.","Qiao Lanshu dozed off groggily in the car. By the time they arrived at the county town, an hour had already passed.","Qin Yuanzheng carried her into the county clinic.","The doctor inside examined Qiao Lanshu and said it wasn't a big problem, just a low-grade fever. However, since she was pregnant, medication wasn't recommended, and he told them to observe her for a day.","Qin Yuanzheng still felt uneasy, so he found a pharmacy, bought some cinnamon twigs and perilla leaves, put them in his thermos, and steeped them in water for Qiao Lanshu to drink.","Qiao Lanshu hugged the thermos cup, sleeping heavily. Whenever she woke up, she would take a couple of sips and then go back to sleep.","Qin Yuanzheng drove slowly, glancing at Qiao Lanshu from time to time.","Having drunk a lot of water, Qiao Lanshu felt the urge to use the restroom. She whispered, \"Brother Zheng, I want to...\"","Qin Yuanzheng asked bluntly, \"Need to pee?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Although Qin Yuanzheng spoke crudely, he never talked like this in front of outsiders.","He was only like this in front of Qiao Lanshu, so much so that whenever Qiao Lanshu heard him speak this way, she had a bit of a conditioned reflex.","Qin Yuanzheng kept his eyes on the road, but it was as if he knew exactly how Qiao Lanshu would react.","He chuckled and pulled the car over.","The roads at this time were all very difficult to travel on.","They were mostly mountain roads, and the majority were yellow dirt paths. There were very few cars, and the road was empty with no one around.","Qin Yuanzheng parked by the side of the road, opened the door for Qiao Lanshu, and said, \"Come on down, I'll go with you.\"","Out here in the middle of nowhere, there obviously wouldn't be any toilets. If she wanted to go, she could only find a spot by the side of the road.","Qiao Lanshu had never done such a thing before. She stood by the road, looking back and forth, her face turning slightly red. Caught in an awkward dilemma, she didn't move for a long while.","Qin Yuanzheng stood beside her, looking at her, and asked in a low voice, \"What's wrong? Want me to help you?\"","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu said, \"Brother Zheng, here... isn't this a bit inappropriate?\"","Having traveled extensively outside, Qin Yuanzheng didn't think there was anything inappropriate about it.","However, Comrade Qiao was an intellectual and a girl from a working-class family, so she probably wasn't used to doing this.","He scooped Qiao Lanshu up in his arms and walked toward the woods by the road, laughing. \"Comrade Little Qiao, you've never sneaked into a grove before, have you? Come on, I'll take you in.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\""]},{"number":170,"title":"Chapter 170: Going Home","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng took Qiao Lanshu into the woods inside, and only then did Qiao Lanshu relax a bit and relieve herself.","Qin Yuanzheng stayed by her side to guard her the whole time.","When she was done, he carried her out in his arms, smiling as he asked, \"Is sneaking into the woods thrilling?\"","Qiao Lanshu glared at him and scolded, \"You're so inappropriate.\"","Qin Yuanzheng replied self-righteously, \"It's enough for me to be proper with outsiders. How can I be proper with my own wife?\"","If they were truly proper, they wouldn't be sleeping on the same bed, let alone having a child.","Qin Yuanzheng teased Qiao Lanshu for a while. After returning to the car, he asked her again, \"Do you feel any better? Both of these medicines are for catching a cold, and pregnant women can drink them. I asked the doctor, and he said you can just drink it like water.\"","Qiao Lanshu had already drunk half a bottle. The water was hot, and the sun had come out, making her sweat slightly. \"I feel a bit better, but I'm still really tired.\"","Anyone would be tired after barely sleeping or eating for three days.","Not to mention a pregnant woman like her.","Qin Yuanzheng started the car and told her, \"We're still about two hours away from home. Go back to sleep, and eat something if you get hungry.\"","In these times, even with money, it was hard to find anything to buy outside.","Fortunately, Qin Yuanzheng had brought steamed buns and corn, otherwise both of them would have gone hungry.","Qiao Lanshu continued to sleep in the car. When she woke up again, they had indeed returned to Longcheng.","After spending several days outside, eating and sleeping poorly while constantly on edge, Qiao Lanshu finally breathed a sigh of relief upon returning. She felt as though every cell in her body was exhausted.","She looked at Qin Yuanzheng, thinking to herself: This time, we should have avoided the incident where Qin Yuanzheng gets injured, right?","Qin Yuanzheng parked the car in the yard and helped Qiao Lanshu out. Looking at her pale face, he asked, \"Do you want me to carry you up?\"","He thought Qiao Lanshu would shake her head and refuse. After all, she was very thin-skinned and afraid of being seen.","However, this time, Qiao Lanshu actually didn't refuse. She slumped softly against Qin Yuanzheng's body and whispered, \"Yes, Brother Zheng, carry me on your back.\"","Qin Yuanzheng squatted down and carried her on his back.","After getting home, Qiao Lanshu changed her clothes and said she wanted to take a bath.","After all, she hadn't bathed during the few days they were away.","She felt so dirty.","Qin Yuanzheng hadn't bathed either during the trip. He went to heat up some water, and while doing so, he washed all the dirty clothes they had changed out of and hung them out on the balcony.","Qiao Lanshu ate a little something, placed the thermos steeping the Chinese medicine by the edge of the kang bed, and went back to sleep on the kang.","Truly, there is no place like home.","Back in her own home, lying on her own kang bed, Qiao Lanshu pulled up the blanket and rolled over in sheer satisfaction.","Less than half an hour after Qin Yuanzheng returned, someone knocked on the door.","Qin Yuanzheng had just finished washing the clothes and was about to mop the floor.","He shook the water off his hands and went to open the door.","Outside stood a guard he recognized from the headquarters building.","The guard said politely, \"Regiment Commander Qin, Commander Li heard you're back and is asking when you'll be heading over to report on your work.\"","Commander Li had been extremely anxious these past few days. He knew how dangerous this mission was, worrying both that his subordinates might get injured and that the enemy spies might escape.","Although Si Zhemao had also gone, his department was not in the same system as the military, so Commander Li was solely waiting for Qin Yuanzheng to return and report.","As a result, Qin Yuanzheng had returned safe and sound, but instead of going straight to the headquarters building to report, he had directly carried his wife home.","Commander Li was beside himself with anxiety.","Unable to sit still, he sent someone over to urge Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng told the guard, \"I need to tidy up the house a bit. It will take about an hour.\"","As he spoke, he glanced at the time. It was already four in the afternoon, so he added, \"I'll go report at five. You can head back first.\"","The guard nodded, turned, and left.","In his heart, however, he was grumbling about Qin Yuanzheng—the very first thing he did after returning from a mission was actually household chores.","After the guard left, Qin Yuanzheng continued sweeping and mopping. Once the water was heated, he poured it into a wooden tub, adjusted the temperature, and called Qiao Lanshu over to bathe.","Qin Yuanzheng had wanted to take a bath with his wife, but remembering he still had to report for work, he had to give up the idea.","He was also hoping to tease his bathing wife a little, but another knock came at the door.","Qin Yuanzheng was truly exasperated.","He told Qiao Lanshu, \"Soak by yourself for a bit. I'll go out and see who it is.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded.","Outside the door was Xiao Li from the logistics department.","Xiao Li was a female comrade. Seeing Qin Yuanzheng at home, she didn't go inside. Holding a bit of mutton, along with some radishes and cabbage, she smiled and said,","\"Regiment Commander Qin, I'm here to cook for Comrade Little Qiao. You don't need to busy yourself; hurry up and go report to the Commander. If there are any chores left undone, just tell me, and I promise to get them done for you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng felt utterly helpless.","He could only say, \"There's nothing else to do. Little Qiao is taking a bath, and she's going to sleep right after. Just cook her some soft noodles later. I'll be back early.\"","Xiao Li immediately replied, \"Understood, I guarantee to complete the mission!\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at the bathroom door.","Although he wanted to stay with Qiao Lanshu for a while longer, Commander Li was clearly rushing him.","Qin Yuanzheng gave Qiao Lanshu a few instructions, reminding her to remember to take her medicine, rest well, and eat on time, assuring her he would be back early.","Only then did he head out.","Xiao Li waited until he left before entering the house. Through the bathroom door, she said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Comrade Little Qiao, Regiment Commander Qin really cares about you.\"","It was truly hard to tell that the usually cold and aloof Regiment Commander Qin actually had such a fussy, motherly side.","Just reminding Qiao Lanshu to take her medicine, Qin Yuanzheng had repeated it three times a moment ago.","Even Xiao Li had gotten tired of hearing it.","Inside, Qiao Lanshu smiled as she bathed and said, \"Brother Zheng is just a very thoughtful person. He's wonderful.\"","It was precisely because Qin Yuanzheng was so good that Qiao Lanshu had longed for him across two lifetimes, in her past life and her present one.","If it hadn't been for Qin Yuanzheng, she wouldn't have stayed in this city in this lifetime at all.","...","Qin Yuanzheng went to report on his work and didn't return until after eight o'clock in the evening.","By this time, Qiao Lanshu had already finished dinner and was preparing to rest.","Before Xiao Li left, she had filled the thermos with hot water for her. Qiao Lanshu had stuffed the Chinese medicinal herbs Qin Yuanzheng bought for her into the thermos herself. Then, she drank the medicine while listening to the radio, holding a high school textbook in her hands to read.","When Qin Yuanzheng returned and opened the door, he saw Qiao Lanshu half-lying on the sofa in thin clothes. The warm yellow light shone on her, giving off a cozy glow that made her look incredibly gentle and demure.","Looking at her, Qin Yuanzheng felt a fiery heat in his heart. He took off his coat, walked over, pressed directly onto Qiao Lanshu, and held her down for a kiss.","Qin Yuanzheng hadn't shaved for three or four days, so his stubble was very prickly.","Qiao Lanshu let out a soft cry and tried to speak, but Qin Yuanzheng didn't give her the chance to open her mouth.","The two of them made out intimately for quite a while before Qin Yuanzheng finally let go of Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu could finally breathe; she had almost suffocated just now.","Under the warm light, her watery eyes glared playfully at Qin Yuanzheng as she whispered, \"Didn't I tell you to shave your beard before getting intimate with me?\"","Otherwise, the stubble hurt too much.","Qin Yuanzheng reached out to gently stroke her belly and said, \"I want you to shave it for me.\"","Qiao Lanshu immediately sat up. \"Alright, sit here and wait. I'll go get the razor.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was a bit surprised. \"Do you know how?\"","Since they got married, he had never let Qiao Lanshu shave his beard.","He figured that an eighteen-year-old girl like her wouldn't know how to do such a thing.","What he didn't know was that in her previous life, Qiao Lanshu had shaved him countless times.","So her skills were actually quite practiced.","Qiao Lanshu came out holding the razor and asked softly, \"Brother Zheng, do you have to be on duty during the New Year?\"","Most people in the military couldn't go home for the Spring Festival.","As a regiment commander, Qin Yuanzheng probably didn't have any time off either.","Thinking of this, Qiao Lanshu felt a little disappointed.","However, she quickly cheered up. Remembering that Qin Yuanzheng hadn't been injured in an explosion in this life and was perfectly healthy, she knew that was better than anything else.","She couldn't ask for too much.","So, she became happy again and smiled, \"When the time comes, you can just come home early to keep me company. Or, you can take me to your office in the mining area. I can read books there and definitely won't disturb your work.\"","Qin Yuanzheng's expression softened, feeling deeply touched.","What did he ever do to deserve a good wife like Qiao Lanshu?","Although he wanted to spend more time with her, he really had to be on duty this year.","He sat there, tilting his chin up slightly to let Qiao Lanshu gently shave his beard, and whispered,","\"For this year's Spring Festival, I let the two deputy commanders and Staff Officer Lin go home. As for the battalion commanders below them, they drew lots. Over the past few years, they were the ones who went back for the holidays while I stayed on duty. Before, it was because I wasn't married, but this time it's because you're pregnant. When you give birth, I'm going to take a long leave, so they'll have to do the work then.\"","His subordinates all knew that his wife was due to give birth after the New Year. Otherwise, Qin Yuanzheng would have taken her back to his hometown to visit his parents this Spring Festival.","Qin Yuanzheng had already arranged his work so that after Qiao Lanshu gave birth, he could stay with her for at least two months.","Two months would be enough time for her to rest and recover.","As they talked, Qiao Lanshu shaved Qin Yuanzheng's beard completely clean.","Her movements were gentle, afraid of hurting him.","But in reality, Qin Yuanzheng had thick skin and wasn't afraid of her hands slipping at all.","After she finished, Qin Yuanzheng went to look in the mirror. He turned back to Qiao Lanshu, who was washing her hands, and asked in a low voice, \"How do you know how to do this? Have you shaved someone before?\"","Qiao Lanshu originally wanted to shake her head, but after thinking about it, she nodded. \"Yeah, I suppose.\"","Qin Yuanzheng's brows furrowed, and he grew a little displeased. \"Who? Your father? Even if it's your father, it's not really appropriate for you to do this, is it? Don't you have a stepmother?\"","Seeing his expression, Qiao Lanshu burst into laughter. She finished washing her hands and walked out. \"It wasn't my dad. It was a tall and handsome man.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","He felt a pang of sour jealousy.","Whatever happened before his wife married him was in the past, and he had no right to interfere.","But hearing her say that still made him feel uncomfortable.","Qin Yuanzheng pressed, \"How tall? How handsome?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"As tall as you, and as handsome as you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng scoffed coldly, \"Really? I don't believe it.\"","Qiao Lanshu walked into the room with a smile and climbed onto the bed. \"Don't believe it then, but there is such a man anyway.\"","Qin Yuanzheng stood at the door, his dark gaze fixed on her for a moment. Then, he took off his clothes, strode onto the bed, and pinned her down. \"Not going to tell the truth, huh?\"","His hand slipped up under the hem of her clothes and gave a slight squeeze. \"Are you going to tell me?\"","Qiao Lanshu dodged while laughing, \"I'll tell you, I'll tell you! It was in a dream, I shaved someone in a dream...\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"Last time with the driving, you said you learned it in a dream. Now, shaving a man's beard was also learned in a dream?\"","As he spoke, his hands continued to cause mischief, making it impossible for her to dodge or push him away. She said pitifully, \"It's true, it's really true, I'm not lying to you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng believed her, but he said, \"I haven't punished you yet for sneaking behind my back to pretend to be a married couple with Guan Wenjun. Take your punishment properly tonight, and no crying.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","She was doomed. Qin Yuanzheng really wanted to teach her a lesson, tormenting her for a long time.","Afraid of hurting the baby in her belly, they only actually went all the way twice. The rest of the time, he used all sorts of tricks to tease and bully her.","Qiao Lanshu begged for mercy all night and promised she would never dare do it again.","Only then did Qin Yuanzheng let her go.","This little troublemaker, did she really think he had no way to deal with her?","In the middle of the night, Qin Yuanzheng got up to pour her some water, coaxing her softly, \"Go back to sleep in a minute, hurry up and hydrate.\"","He was afraid his little wife would get dehydrated. After all, between crying and doing that, she hadn't stopped all night.","Qiao Lanshu shot him a resentful glare, sat up, and drank from the cup in his hand.","Qin Yuanzheng chuckled softly at her. \"If you don't want me to bully you, be a little more obedient in the future. Don't sneak out behind my back again. I was really worried about you, you know?\"","If she had just been wandering around the city, it would have been fine.","But this time, Qiao Lanshu had followed Guan Wenjun into the mountains.","They were executing a mission to catch enemy spies. How dangerous was that?","Even now, Qin Yuanzheng still felt a lingering fear when he thought about it.","Although he hadn't scolded her a single time on the way back, it didn't mean he didn't care.","He had kept it in mind all along.","After finishing the cup of water, Qiao Lanshu quickly lay back down, wrapping the quilt tightly around herself as she muttered, \"You only know how to bully me...\"","She had no idea where he had learned so many tricks; it was simply too embarrassing.","Using his mouth and hands was one thing, but he even brought out strips of cloth, claiming he was going to interrogate her and forbidding her from struggling or escaping.","She began to suspect that Qin Yuanzheng had some sort of special fetish.","But he hadn't had this many tricks in their past life. Was it because the Qin Yuanzheng of her past life was more steady, and his health hadn't been as good?","Qiao Lanshu complained resentfully, \"You're not allowed to bully me like this anymore... Besides, once we have the baby, you won't be able to bully me like this anyway. After all, the child will be watching.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng's face instantly fell.","In the dark, he let out a long sigh.","Sigh, how did they suddenly end up having a child?","If he had known it was this easy to get pregnant, he would have...","Alas, his world of just the two of them only had a little over four months left."]},{"number":171,"title":"Chapter 171: Spring Festival","paragraphs":["As the Spring Festival approached, many families hung red lanterns at their doorways, and pasted images of door gods and couplets on their gates.","Many people had returned to their hometowns for the new year, leaving the neighborhood much emptier than usual.","Next door, Zhao Jiannong and Huang Erling had taken their two daughters back home for the holidays.","Zhao Jiannong hadn't been home for three years, and his vacation time this year was hard-earned, so he had bought train tickets early and left with his wife and children.","Neither Qiao Lanshu nor Qin Yuanzheng had family here. In past years, Qin Yuanzheng had always spent the Spring Festival alone, but things were better now—he had a wife.","Rushing before the new year, Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu wrote letters to their respective families, sharing the news of Qiao Lanshu's pregnancy, and sent them some new year goods.","The new year goods Qiao Lanshu sent to her family were prepared by Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng had prepared two identical sets of new year goods to send to both sets of parents.","Standing outside the post office, looking at the festive red lanterns lining the streets, Qiao Lanshu said, \"Brother Zheng, how do you think your family will react when they find out I'm pregnant?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was already thirty, and previously there had been rumors that he was infertile.","Yet this year, not only had he married a wife, but he was also going to have a child.","Qiao Lanshu didn't know what his family would think.","In her past life, she had only met Qin Yuanzheng's parents twice. Because they lived so far away, and since his parents were older and in poor health, they had gone south for their retirement, making it quite difficult to meet.","However, Qin Yuanzheng's parents were quite amiable and treated Qiao Lanshu fairly well.","Now, the elderly couple hadn't retired yet and were still relatively young.","They only had one son, Qin Yuanzheng. Knowing that he was having a child, they would probably be overjoyed, right?","Qin Yuanzheng wrapped an arm around Qiao Lanshu's shoulders, looking at her visibly swelling belly, and said softly, \"They should be very happy. They'll probably ask for time off to come see us.\"","Qiao Lanshu asked, \"Didn't you say it's very far? Will they come?\"","It was winter, snowing frequently, and transportation wasn't very convenient. Moreover, the trains were slow. Qin Yuanzheng had been stationed here for many years, and his parents had never visited.","However, if they heard that Qiao Lanshu was going to have a baby, they would probably make the trip.","Qin Yuanzheng said, \"I told them in the letter not to come. Next autumn, I'll take you back to visit.\"","Pausing for a moment, Qin Yuanzheng added, \"Oh, right, when the time comes, I'll also make time to accompany you back to Yangcheng. Didn't you say you wanted to go back and see your father?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"I do want to go back a bit.\"","Even if she wasn't going back to see her father, she still wanted to visit Yangcheng.","After all, it was the place where she grew up, her hometown. Having not been back for so long, she missed it.","She still found it somewhat difficult to get used to the climate and food here.","After leaving the post office, Qin Yuanzheng took Qiao Lanshu for a stroll in the department store. He bought her a coat and a brown checkered scarf.","They also went to browse the baby products section.","There were quite a lot of baby items. Some didn't require ration coupons, while others did. Qiao Lanshu had the necessary coupons; after all, she was pregnant and had applied for maternity subsidies.","She had gradually made some baby clothes, and they already had diapers. When she saw feeding bottles for sale, she immediately grabbed one.","Qin Yuanzheng had never seen such a thing before. He asked, \"What is this? A feeding bottle?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"Yes, for feeding the baby milk. Let me see how much it is...\"","When she checked the price, she was shocked. \"Five yuan?\"","A single feeding bottle actually cost five yuan. That was so expensive.","In these times, how many babies actually used feeding bottles?","This thing was indeed uncommon.","Qin Yuanzheng took the bottle in his hand, inspected it, and said, \"Let's buy one. It's not a consumable item, so it can probably be used until the child is three, right?\"","So Qiao Lanshu bought the feeding bottle. Seeing a rattle drum and a small wooden carved figurine, she bought one of each as well.","In short, whenever she saw anything related to babies now, she wanted it all and wanted to buy everything.","The couple strolled around the department store for over an hour. By the time they came out, it had started to snow.","They bought some more new year goods and carried them over to Yang Wenyan's house, where they had their New Year's Eve dinner.","After dinner, Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen, along with Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu, sat on the sofa. The four of them listened to the radio while cracking melon seeds, drinking tea, and chatting.","In the northern winters, the air was dry and things caught fire easily, so one had to be careful with fire. Even during the new year, setting off fireworks and firecrackers was strictly forbidden in mountainous areas and within the city.","However, down by the nearby river, many people braved the bitter cold to set off firecrackers.","Deng Xiaozhen had hung red lanterns on the balcony early on, making the place look festive.","She said with some regret, \"I'm not used to not going back home for the new year this year.\"","Yang Wenyan glanced at her and teased, \"What's wrong? Are you not used to not having someone to argue with this year?\"","This year, Yang Wenyan had intentionally stayed here for the new year. His food factory had gone on holiday early, so he could have actually returned to the countryside.","But the reason he didn't go back was that his parents were constantly urging him to have a child, and Deng Xiaozhen still hadn't managed to get pregnant.","Because of this issue with having an heir, Deng Xiaozhen's relationship with her parents-in-law was quite poor, especially the relationship between mother-in-law and daughter-in-law, which was rather terrible.","Deng Xiaozhen had a very fiery temper, and she was not the type to let herself be taken advantage of.","Yang Wenyan's mother had repeatedly criticized her over the issue of an heir, mocking her with veiled insults.","Every time Deng Xiaozhen went back, the old lady would let out the family's hens and deliberately call Yang Wenyan to collect the eggs, sarcastically comparing Deng Xiaozhen to a hen that couldn't lay eggs.","Caught between his mother and his wife, Yang Wenyan sometimes found it very difficult.","After thinking it over this year, he simply decided not to go back for the new year. He and Deng Xiaozhen would spend it in the city, and since Qin Yuanzheng and his wife were also here, the four of them could celebrate together.","It was the first time Qiao Lanshu had heard about Yang Wenyan's family matters, and she was somewhat surprised.","Indeed, every family has its own difficult scriptures to read.","After complaining about her awful mother-in-law for a long time, Deng Xiaozhen mentioned her younger brother, who had taken his wife back home for the new year this year. Since she couldn't have a child, she could only hope that her brother Deng Weijun would have one soon to make her parents happy.","Yang Wenyan then asked Qin Yuanzheng if he had any plans to go home, who would take care of the child after Qiao Lanshu gave birth, and whether Qiao Lanshu was going to resign.","Since the topic had come up, Qin Yuanzheng said, \"Cousin, after the new year, I plan to look for a nanny to help take care of the child and cook. If you and sister-in-law know of any suitable candidates, please help introduce them.\"","Upon hearing this, Yang Wenyan immediately said, \"Don't worry about that. I'll definitely ask around for you.\"","Deng Xiaozhen also added, \"Since both of you have to work, you really do need to find someone experienced to help out...\"","Saying this, Deng Xiaozhen trailed off.","She had originally wanted to say that if they really couldn't find a suitable person, she could take time off to go over and take care of Qiao Lanshu herself.","But since she had never had a child herself, she really didn't know how to take care of a mother who had just given birth, let alone a newborn baby.","Thinking of this, she sighed and said, \"I've heard that newborns are quite difficult to look after. Someone without experience really wouldn't be able to handle it.\"","The four of them chatted for over an hour. Seeing that it was getting late, Qin Yuanzheng took Qiao Lanshu back home.","This was the first New Year he and Qiao Lanshu had spent together, and he hoped that they would spend countless more New Years together in the future.","Until they grew old.","Qin Yuanzheng held Qiao Lanshu in his arms and said softly, \"There's a dinner gathering at the military base tomorrow. Come with me.\"","Many soldiers had stayed behind at the mining area's military base. Qin Yuanzheng hadn't joined them for the New Year's Eve dinner, so he absolutely had to go tomorrow on the first day of the New Year.","Qiao Lanshu nodded. She didn't have anything else to do anyway, so she might as well tag along with Qin Yuanzheng.","Suddenly thinking of something, Qiao Lanshu asked Qin Yuanzheng, \"By the way, have Director Guan and the rest finished their business? Are they back yet?\"","\"No,\" Qin Yuanzheng replied.","Neither Guan Wenjun nor Si Zhemao had returned yet. The two of them would have to spend this Spring Festival in the mountains."]},{"number":172,"title":"Chapter 172: Letter from a Friend","paragraphs":["The next day, Qin Yuanzheng went to the mining area troops by himself first and had lunch with the people there. In the afternoon, he came back to pick up Qiao Lanshu and took her to the state-run restaurant.","Today's dinner was a gathering for the cadres of the 21st Regiment.","Several deputy regiment commanders, battalion commanders, the political commissar, as well as the project designers and engineers, all sat down to eat together.","Those with family members brought them along.","Many of them knew that Qin Yuanzheng had gotten married and had attended his wedding banquet, but there were still some who had just returned from out of town and had never met Qiao Lanshu.","Young Company Commander Yang was also there today. He was quite familiar with Qiao Lanshu, and when he saw her coming over, he greeted her.","Others also chimed in, calling Qiao Lanshu \"Sister-in-law.\" She felt a bit embarrassed because, among everyone present, she was probably the youngest.","Seeing those deputy regiment commanders, battalion commanders, and several engineers coming over to call her \"Sister-in-law,\" she felt a little awkward.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng saw these people, he knew they were deliberately teasing his wife.","Most of these men worked here alone while their families remained in their hometowns. Not many could bring their families to live with them on the base, and more importantly, many were still unmarried.","Now that it was the New Year, and seeing their regiment commander's wife arrive, of course they had to make a fuss and tease them a bit.","So, they came over one by one to call her \"Sister-in-law,\" and each of them even prepared a red envelope, saying it was for their regiment commander's future child.","Qiao Lanshu felt awkward and didn't accept them.","Qin Yuanzheng, being thick-skinned, took the red envelopes one by one and said, \"At least you guys are sensible enough to know to give red envelopes.\"","Saying that, he handed the thick stack of collected red envelopes to Qiao Lanshu: \"Keep them, wife. They're all yours.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Xiao Yang also gave a red envelope. He wasn't married yet, and he had even gone on a blind date with Qiao Lanshu before.","He walked over to Qiao Lanshu and pulled out a chair for her: \"Sister-in-law, please take a seat.\"","Qiao Lanshu thanked him and sat down.","Taking advantage of Qin Yuanzheng talking to someone else, Xiao Yang sat next to Qiao Lanshu and lowered his voice, saying, \"Sister-in-law, let me tell you a secret. Among the people eating today, there is your romantic rival.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at Xiao Yang with a surprised expression. If she hadn't been familiar enough with him, she would have suspected she misheard.","She lowered her voice and asked, \"What romantic rival?\"","She had been married to Qin Yuanzheng for almost half a year; how had she never heard that he had any romantic debts?","Although he had gone on quite a few blind dates in the past, hadn't those all been resolved?","How did a romantic rival suddenly pop up?","Xiao Yang explained to Qiao Lanshu, \"It's like this. Our regiment commander previously dated Deputy Commander Yang's daughter. The two almost got their marriage certificate, but later, because of his infertility issue, the whole thing fell through.\"","Qiao Lanshu knew about this. It happened quite a long time ago, right when Qin Yuanzheng was first diagnosed with infertility, which was at least four years ago.","Qiao Lanshu suddenly realized, \"That Miss Yang is also here eating today?\"","Xiao Yang nodded with a serious expression. \"She was studying out of town before and reportedly just returned here at the end of the year. Oh, right, she's a nurse at the military district hospital. We often see her when we go for our medical checkups.\"","In short, everyone was quite familiar with her. In the past, many people thought Nurse Yang and Regiment Commander Qin were a great match, a very suitable pair. After things fell through between them, many people in the troops still felt it was a pity.","But they didn't feel it was a pity anymore, because everyone felt that Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng were a much better match.","After all, since getting married, Qin Yuanzheng no longer worked overtime for no reason. He went home right on time every day, and he was no longer as irritable and short-tempered.","Everyone in the mining area troops had a much easier time because of his transformation.","Qiao Lanshu wanted to ask a few more questions, but Qin Yuanzheng, who was nearby, saw her talking to Xiao Yang. They seemed to have been talking for quite a while, and both looked quite happy.","Qin Yuanzheng's face fell slightly. He stopped talking to the others, walked straight over to Qiao Lanshu, pulled out a chair, and sat down. He first glanced at Xiao Yang and said, \"Got a lot of free time, do you?\"","Xiao Yang immediately stood up. \"Commander, I'm going to help move the liquor, so I won't bother you anymore.\"","With that, Xiao Yang hurried off to move things.","At this time, there was no alcohol ban in the military.","Plus, it was the New Year, and it was rare for everyone to gather together for a meal, so the logistics department ordered a lot of liquor, and it was all good stuff.","Xiao Yang was a company commander and usually managed quite a few people in the military.","But here, he was almost the lowest-ranking officer. If he didn't move things, who would?","Besides, the way their regiment commander was staring at him was not right at all, as if he were trying to abduct Comrade Xiao Qiao.","Where would he get the guts to do that?","Qin Yuanzheng sat next to Qiao Lanshu, looking down at her, and found that she was also sizing him up with her eyes.","Qin Yuanzheng raised an eyebrow and asked in a low voice, \"What's wrong? Are you not used to this? After we finish eating in a bit, we'll leave first.\"","Qiao Lanshu leaned close to him. He instinctively reached out to put his arm around her, then bent his waist and lowered his head to listen to her speak.","Qiao Lanshu asked him in a low voice, \"Brother Zheng, which one is Nurse Yang?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng's face instantly darkened, and he turned his head, about to go find Xiao Yang.","Qiao Lanshu continued, \"I heard she's a nurse at your military district hospital, a pretty nice person, and quite familiar with you guys?\"","Qiao Lanshu tilted her head slightly, looking at Qin Yuanzheng with her smiling, dark eyes.","Her gaze made Qin Yuanzheng feel inexplicably guilty.","He felt that Qiao Lanshu making this kind of expression was incredibly cute, making him unable to resist the urge to hug and kiss her.","But this wasn't an appropriate place, so he just coughed and explained in a low voice, \"Did Xiao Yang say something to you?\"","Qiao Lanshu immediately replied, \"Don't blame Xiao Yang. This matter of yours wasn't a secret anyway, everyone knows about it. You didn't even tell me she was coming to eat with us today.\"","Qin Yuanzheng explained in a low voice, \"There is absolutely nothing between her and me. Besides, this happened several years ago, so I didn't think there was anything worth mentioning.\"","In his heart, Qin Yuanzheng truly felt there was nothing to talk about.","He had indeed gone on blind dates before, and even came close to discussing marriage, but when it came to truly talking about feelings and romance, he had never been with anyone other than Qiao Lanshu.","He explained it to Qiao Lanshu once more: \"Back then, it was Deputy Commander Yang who took a liking to me and introduced his daughter to me. I was still a battalion commander at the time, only in my twenties, and I didn't understand much about relationships, so I just followed the arrangements of my superiors. Before my medical checkup, Nurse Yang and I had only met a total of three times and had one meal together.\"","Saying this, he made sure to emphasize again, \"We had a very pure friendship. I never even held her hand, I'm telling the truth.\"","Qiao Lanshu had actually already heard these things from her cousin-in-law, Deng Xiaozhen.","Qin Yuanzheng had also explained it to her before.","She actually didn't mind Qin Yuanzheng's past. After all, Qin Yuanzheng's age and rank were plain to see.","He was so outstanding and handsome; it was only normal for people to like him.","As a young girl from the south, she felt lucky just to be able to be with Qin Yuanzheng.","After all, if it weren't for his supposed infertility, Qin Yuanzheng would have had a wife and kids long ago, and it never would have been Qiao Lanshu's turn.","Qiao Lanshu was just teasing him on purpose, wanting to make him a little anxious. After all, he looked quite cute when he was like that.","Before Qiao Lanshu could speak, Qin Yuanzheng pinched her ear and asked in a low voice, \"Are you still angry?\"","Qiao Lanshu gently shook her head.","Right at that moment, the Nurse Yang they had been talking about, Comrade Yang Cui, walked in.","She didn't come in alone; she arrived with several other nurses and doctors.","They were all comrades from the military district hospital. Some of the women had previously participated in social mixers with the troops.","Since three or four of the nurses were military family members, they simply decided to come to this gathering together.","As soon as Nurse Yang entered, she looked around. When she spotted Qin Yuanzheng, her eyes lit up, and she immediately walked over. \"Commander Qin, long time no see. I heard you got married?\"","As she spoke, she noticed Qiao Lanshu, who was being held in Qin Yuanzheng's embrace.","Qiao Lanshu slowly sat up straight and looked Nurse Yang up and down.","Nurse Yang was twenty-five years old and quite tall. She had short hair, delicate features, and carried a faint scent of disinfectant.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded, took Qiao Lanshu's hand, and said, \"Yes, this is my wife, Comrade Qiao Lanshu.\"","He then turned to Qiao Lanshu. \"This is Nurse Yang, Comrade Yang Cui.\"","Comrade Yang Cui's father was the deputy commander of the local military district, meaning she could have her pick of any of the talented young men in the army.","Back then, she had chosen Qin Yuanzheng. However, because of his supposed infertility, her parents refused to agree to the marriage.","Yang Cui herself hadn't minded, because she truly liked Qin Yuanzheng.","Unable to defy her parents, she had no choice but to give up on him. However, over the past few years, she had remained unmarried.","She originally thought that once she got older and became a spinster, her parents might no longer oppose her marrying Qin Yuanzheng.","In the end, she had only gone away for a six-month study program, and upon her return, Qin Yuanzheng was not only married but even had a child on the way.","Yang Cui couldn't even describe the bitter taste in her heart.","She looked at Qiao Lanshu and tried to force a smile, but she simply couldn't.","She just nodded and said, \"Hello. I heard you're pregnant. Have you gone for a check-up? How many months along are you?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and replied, \"I've had it checked. It's almost five months now.\"","By the time spring ended and summer arrived, she would likely give birth.","A summer delivery was good. It wouldn't be cold, nor would the weather here be too hot. The air wouldn't be dry, making it the perfect climate for her postpartum confinement.","Yang Cui looked at Qin Yuanzheng, then at Qiao Lanshu, and suddenly asked, \"Yours is a military marriage. Did you two do a premarital medical check-up?\"","Qiao Lanshu paused and looked up at Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng's expression darkened. \"Thank you for your concern. We already did.\"","With that, he turned around, poured a cup of hot water for Qiao Lanshu, and squeezed her hand. \"Are you cold? Drink some hot water.\"","Qiao Lanshu took the hot water and held it, but didn't drink.","She muttered in her heart: they hadn't actually done a premarital check-up, had they?","She remembered they hadn't.","Why did Qin Yuanzheng say they had?","Looking at Qin Yuanzheng's expression, Nurse Yang knew he was unhappy.","Moreover, it was obvious he no longer wanted to speak to her.","Nurse Yang felt a pang of sorrow.","She had been so close to marrying Qin Yuanzheng.","It was all her parents' fault for disagreeing. Now look, Qin Yuanzheng's wife was clearly able to get pregnant.","He never had infertility at all.","Feeling embarrassed, Nurse Yang cast one last, highly complicated look at Qiao Lanshu before turning around and sitting at the next table.","Qiao Lanshu took a sip of water and looked at Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng said softly, \"Ignore others. Drink more water and eat more food. Once you're full, we'll go home.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and stayed silent.","She more or less understood now. Nurse Yang asking about the premarital check-up was likely because she suspected the child wasn't Qin Yuanzheng's.","After all, getting pregnant so soon after marriage was rare, even for ordinary people without fertility issues.","When Qiao Lanshu first got pregnant, there had been no shortage of gossip about this.","She didn't care about the rumors. After all, she was living her life with Qin Yuanzheng, not with the gossips.","As long as the two of them knew the child was theirs, that was enough. Everyone else was just a passing traveler in their lives.","The meal was lively and bustling. The military officers who normally didn't dare to pressure Qin Yuanzheng into drinking took advantage of the New Year to line up and offer him toasts.","Qiao Lanshu looked at him with concern, terrified he would get drunk.","Qin Yuanzheng stood up, raised a small glass of liquor, and toasted everyone directly. He said,","\"Everyone has worked hard this past year. I should be drinking to my heart's content with you all, but as you know, my wife is pregnant. It's dark and the roads are slippery, and I have to drive her home later. So, I won't be joining you in drinking. I offer this glass to everyone, wishing you all a Happy New Year and all the best.\"","With that, he downed the small glass of liquor in one gulp.","Someone said, \"Oh, Commander, you're dodging drinks again.\"","Another said, \"For the sister-in-law's sake, let's let the Commander off the hook this time. Come on, come on, let's drink among ourselves.\"","\"Yeah, our Commander has to take care of his wife. Let's spare him this time. It won't be too late to get him to drink when the baby turns one month old.\"","Saying so, the group let Qin Yuanzheng go and grabbed their commissar to start pouring drinks for him instead.","Qin Yuanzheng watched them fool around, shook his head, returned to put down his glass, and asked Qiao Lanshu, \"Are you full?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"I'm full.\"","Qin Yuanzheng said, \"It's getting late. Let's head back.\"","Qiao Lanshu also wanted to go back early.","After all, Nurse Yang kept staring at her from time to time, and she really disliked being watched like that.","The two left the state-run restaurant. When they returned to the military residential compound, the guard stopped them and handed them a package and a letter.","\"Commander Qin, Sister-in-law, this package was sent from Yangcheng. It was delivered even during the New Year, so I was worried it might be urgent. You should take it back and check it quickly.\"","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng exchanged a glance. Qin Yuanzheng took the package; it wasn't very heavy.","He then took the letter and handed it to Qiao Lanshu. \"Take a look. Is it a letter from our dad?\"","Qiao Lanshu glanced at it and said in surprise, \"It's not from my dad.\"","She lowered her voice. \"It's from a friend of mine.\"","Qiao Lanshu had a childhood friend in Yangcheng. They were the same age and went to elementary school together, but parted ways during middle school.","Because that girl's parents wouldn't let her study anymore.","Before Qiao Lanshu came to Longcheng to find her husband, she had said goodbye to that girl, who had been very envious of her.","Envious that Qiao Lanshu had a military officer husband and could accompany him on his deployment.","Meanwhile, she herself might not be able to find a good family to marry into.","Qiao Lanshu hadn't expected her to send a letter.","Qiao Lanshu pondered for a moment. At this point in her past life, she had been too busy just trying to survive to know whether her best friend had sent her a letter.","Perhaps she had?","She spoke up, \"This friend of mine must have run into some trouble. Otherwise, knowing her personality, she never would have written to me.\"","After all, mailing a letter meant buying stamps, which cost money. Not to mention, sending it from so far away made the postage even more expensive."]},{"number":173,"title":"Chapter 173: Qiaolan Scholar Arrives","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu read through the letters carefully.","There were two pages in total. The handwriting wasn't beautiful, but it was very neat.","Her good friend told her that her family was arranging a marriage for her. She didn't want to get married because she felt the man was too old, and more importantly, he had a bad temper and wasn't good-looking.","However, the man's family was wealthy and willing to pay a high bride price, so her family was forcing her into the marriage.","She had secretly asked someone to issue a letter of introduction for her, claiming she was going to visit a newlywed friend—namely, Qiao Lanshu.","She estimated that by the time Qiao Lanshu received her letter, her letter of introduction would be ready, but she wasn't sure when she would be able to buy a train ticket.","She might not even be able to make the trip successfully.","But she wrote in the letter that even if she couldn't come to find Qiao Lanshu, she would run away. She was absolutely determined not to just marry herself off so casually.","That was the gist of the letter. Qiao Lanshu read it over and over, feeling a bit melancholy. \"I wonder how Meimei is doing now.\"","It usually took about ten days for a letter to travel from Yangcheng to Longcheng.","And that was not accounting for holidays, rain, snow, or other unforeseen circumstances.","Zhong Mei had sent this letter more than half a month ago. Now that it was the New Year, Zhong Mei was probably still at home.","When Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu returned home, he opened the box he was carrying and saw several packets of Yangcheng local specialties inside.","A packet of dried radishes, a small jar of pickled sour plums, a bag of pork lard candy, and a packet of sweet rice cakes.","They were all food items. Qin Yuanzheng took them out. \"Did that Zhong Mei send all these to you?\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"She sent them. She knows I love pickled sour plums.\"","Seeing Qiao Lanshu looking a bit down, Qin Yuanzheng said, \"Don't be sad. Didn't she say she was coming to find you?\"","Qiao Lanshu handed the letter to Qin Yuanzheng to read. \"She said she wants to come and will secretly get a letter of introduction, but it's still uncertain whether she can actually make it.\"","As Qin Yuanzheng read the letter, he frowned and asked, \"Why is her family forcing her to get married?\"","Being an only child and a man, Qin Yuanzheng truly didn't understand Zhong Mei's predicament.","Qiao Lanshu only had a younger half-brother who was still quite young. When she was little, she didn't have a stepmother or a brother yet.","So she had a pretty good childhood, and her father treated her well. Even after her stepmother and brother came along, her father was still willing to support her education through high school.","But Zhong Mei's situation was different.","She said softly:","\"Zhong Mei is the eldest in her family. She has two younger sisters and a younger brother. Her family's living conditions are very average. Although they are city folks, her father's salary isn't high, and her mother is a temporary worker. She also has grandparents, an uncle and aunt, and two male cousins...","A large family of twelve people all living in one house. Not to mention how crowded it is, they often don't have enough to eat, and there are many conflicts... She dropped out of school before graduating from elementary school, only finishing the fifth grade, and then went out to work as a temporary worker to earn money.\"","Zhong Mei was quite pretty, with a round face, big eyes, and a little snaggletooth when she smiled. Qiao Lanshu always thought she was very cute.","It was probably because of her good looks that her family was rushing her into marriage, right?","Qiao Lanshu sighed. \"If I had known, I would have sent her some money. She probably doesn't have money for a train ticket.\"","In her previous life, after Qiao Lanshu married Qin Yuanzheng, she had written to Zhong Mei, but the letters were returned. She only found out after asking around that Zhong Mei had married far away.","This time, after being reborn, she hadn't initially thought to contact Zhong Mei.","Later, after marrying Qin Yuanzheng, she sent a letter to Zhong Mei at the same time she wrote to her father.","But it had been several months, and Zhong Mei hadn't written back. She had assumed Zhong Mei had already gotten married.","Thinking about it now, Zhong Mei probably felt stamps were too expensive, which was why she hadn't replied.","Qin Yuanzheng put down the letter he had just finished reading and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Since she wrote to you, she probably already has a plan in mind, so don't worry. If she really does come over, I can help find her a job.\"","With a job, Zhong Mei could stay here and wouldn't have to be sent back.","That way, she could avoid her family's pressure to marry.","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu immediately said, \"That's right! You can even introduce her to a military officer, just like you did for me back then. Then she can accompany the army.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng coughed and said, \"That's all in the past, let's not bring it up again.\"","Every time he thought about how enthusiastically he had tried to set Qiao Lanshu up with someone back then, he felt like a fool.","People in the army were still spreading the story to this day.","Staff Officer Lin would use this incident to mock him from time to time.","Every time Qin Yuanzheng heard them bring it up, he suffered in silence, forced to swallow his frustration.","Alas, he couldn't even empathize with his past self now.","When they went to bed at night, Qiao Lanshu babbled on about how they would settle her good friend Zhong Mei once she arrived and what kind of job they would find for her.","She also mentioned sending money to Zhong Mei; life would always be a bit easier with some money in hand.","With these things on her mind, Qiao Lanshu woke up early the next day. She got up to write a reply to Zhong Mei and also wrote a letter to her father, Qiao Bingzhang, asking him to deliver ten yuan to Zhong Mei, treating it as a loan from her father.","Qin Yuanzheng saw this and asked her, \"Why are you having your father deliver the money? You could just send it directly to Zhong Mei.\"","Qiao Lanshu put the two letters into their respective envelopes before replying, \"Zhong Mei has endless chores to do every day. What if this letter is intercepted by her family? The money would never reach her hands.\"","Qin Yuanzheng came over, gave Qiao Lanshu a hug, and said, \"You really think of everything.\"","Qiao Lanshu was indeed a thoughtful, considerate, and sweet girl.","The more Qin Yuanzheng thought about it, the more he loved her. He held her affectionately for quite a while before taking her to the post office to mail the letters.","However, after the letters were sent out, there was no response again.","Qiao Lanshu waited for more than half a month and still didn't receive a reply, so she wrote another letter to Zhong Mei. Then, the New Year holiday passed.","...","The ice and snow melted, the weather warmed up, and it was time for them to go back to work.","It had been over a month since they first went into the mountains to catch spies, yet Si Zhemao and Guan Wenjun surprisingly still hadn't returned.","Qin Yuanzheng had earned merits and was already thirty years old. The higher-ups intended to promote him. After the New Year, he would no longer be a regimental commander, but a brigade commander.","Qin Yuanzheng's promotion didn't actually bring much change to their own little family.","Days passed one by one, and life went on just as before.","Qiao Lanshu would write to Zhong Mei from time to time. When at work, she would find time to read books, learn how to make clothes, and sew a few extra sets of clothes for her baby.","Time flew by quickly.","A month before Qiao Lanshu's due date, she took her maternity leave early.","Her belly had grown large, and she had to hold it every day while walking. Qin Yuanzheng was on edge all day long, terrified that she might have an accident.","However, he couldn't stay home every day to accompany her, so he discussed it with Qiao Lanshu and had her take time off to stay at home and prepare for childbirth when she was eight months pregnant.","Although Qiao Lanshu was in great shape during her pregnancy, with no morning sickness, bloating, or swelling.","She ate and slept well every day, and even had the energy to go to work. Wang Xue and Huang Erling from next door were very envious of her condition.","Qiao Lanshu stayed at home to await delivery, and the nanny, Auntie Shi, took care of her.","Auntie Shi was a Longcheng local. She was introduced by the family member of a military officer after Qin Yuanzheng asked around at the base.","Auntie Shi was in her forties, tall and sturdy, with a darker complexion. She worked briskly and had decent cooking skills.","She just didn't know how to cook Southern dishes, but she was great at making pastries and noodles. Qiao Lanshu wasn't a picky eater either; she only asked Auntie Shi to use less oil, salt, soy sauce, and vinegar so the food would be lighter, and she enjoyed eating it.","Today, as usual, Auntie Shi stayed at home with Qiao Lanshu. It was the Start of Summer, and the trees in the yard were sprouting green buds. Auntie Shi strolled with Qiao Lanshu in the yard and said, \"Xiao Qiao, your due date is in just a few days. Talk to Chief Qin tomorrow and ask him to take a few days off to stay home with you.\"","Auntie Shi always called Qin Yuanzheng \"Chief\" and Qiao Lanshu \"Xiao Qiao.\"","It couldn't be helped; Xiao Qiao was so young, not even as old as Auntie Shi's son.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Brother Zheng said that once he finishes his work today, he'll start taking leave tomorrow.\"","Auntie Shi nodded. \"It's the Start of Summer today. I saw sweet melons for sale at the supply and marketing cooperative. I'll go buy a few later for you to taste. Oh, right, I also saw edamame. You know edamame, right? It's nutritious. I'll buy some to boil, and you can snack on it when you're free...\"","When Auntie Shi started talking about food, she would ramble on endlessly. \"I also saw purslane. These are leafy greens you can't get in winter. I'll buy some to make steamed buns for you. Speaking of steamed buns, I don't know how they'll taste. If not, I'll just make dumplings. Since you're about to give birth, we can bring them to the hospital...\"","Before Auntie Shi could finish speaking, Qiao Lanshu suddenly felt that something was wrong.","She stopped abruptly, reaching out to clutch her stomach, her face turning slightly pale.","Seeing her stop moving and noticing something was wrong, Auntie Shi immediately grew anxious. \"What's wrong? Xiao Qiao, is your stomach hurting?\"","Qiao Lanshu felt a dropping sensation in her abdomen, with pain coming in waves. She nervously grabbed Auntie Shi's arm, her eyes turning red. \"Auntie, my... my stomach is starting to hurt.\"","Auntie Shi had a loud voice, and she shouted, \"Why is it hurting now? Are you about to give birth?\"","With that, Auntie Shi immediately yelled to the guard at the neighborhood gate, \"Comrade Guard! Xiao Qiao is about to give birth! Quick, drive the car over and take her to the hospital!\"","Other people strolling in the neighborhood heard the commotion and hurried over to help.","\"Oh my, she's about to give birth? Hurry, hurry, take her to the hospital. We don't have a midwife here.\"","\"Brigade Commander Qin probably doesn't know yet, right? I'll go to the base to deliver a message. Auntie Shi, you take her to the hospital first. We really don't have a midwife here.\"","...","One of the guards at the gate quickly ran out, drove out a certain officer's car parked in the yard, and took Qiao Lanshu to the hospital.","Qiao Lanshu originally thought she still had at least eight or nine days before giving birth.","But it just had to happen on the Start of Summer.","She was quite nervous. Sitting in the car, her face was pale, and her hands were trembling.","Auntie Shi comforted her, \"It's okay, it's okay. Don't worry. I've given birth to three children, and aren't I perfectly fine? It just hurts a bit. Bear with it, and it will be over soon. Don't be nervous.\"","Qiao Lanshu was still nervous. She already didn't have a mother, and her father was thousands of miles away.","With no family by her side, she felt a bit sensitive. Thinking about this made her feel sad and want to cry.","Moreover, Qin Yuanzheng wasn't by her side either.","Auntie Shi took out a bag from her pocket. The bag contained sweet fried dough twists, coated in icing sugar.","The dough twists were deep-fried, oily, and sugary. In these times, many people were reluctant to spend money on them.","Auntie Shi kept some in her pocket every day for Qiao Lanshu to eat as snacks.","She took them out now to give to Qiao Lanshu. \"The pain has just started. Take a deep breath, don't be nervous. Come, eat something. No rush, it'll probably hurt for a few more hours.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","She was about to be scared half to death by Auntie Shi's remark about hurting for a few more hours.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"Is it going to hurt for a few hours? Giving birth is so hard.\"","Auntie Shi chuckled, even though she felt she shouldn't laugh.","She held Qiao Lanshu's hand and said, \"It starts with labor pains, and it's a gradual process. You won't give birth immediately. Don't be afraid, okay?\"","Meanwhile, Qin Yuanzheng, who was discussing work with engineers at the mining site, saw a guard running over hurriedly.","Qin Yuanzheng immediately had a premonition.","He instantly shoved all the blueprints in his hands to Staff Officer Lin beside him and strode over. Before he even got close, he heard the guard say, \"Regi... no, Brigade Commander, Comrade Xiao Qiao is about to give birth! She's been taken to the hospital.\"","Without a word, Qin Yuanzheng immediately took large strides forward. After just two steps, he started running.","He ran faster and faster, but after a few steps, he quickly stopped, grabbed a random person, and said, \"You, drive for me. Take me to the military hospital right now.\"","The soldier he grabbed quickly nodded and ran behind Qin Yuanzheng.","After getting into the car, Qin Yuanzheng felt his hands trembling slightly.","He had originally wanted to drive himself, but he was too nervous. His heart was beating fast, and his hands were shaking. He felt he couldn't drive.","The soldier driving said, \"Brigade Commander, is sister-in-law giving birth so soon? Didn't they say there were still about ten days left?\"","Qin Yuanzheng had almost finished arranging his work and was ready to take leave tomorrow to go home and accompany her for the birth.","But today, she suddenly went into labor.","It was truly shocking.","Qin Yuanzheng placed his hands on his knees, straightened his back, and his entire body was tense. He didn't speak.","Because of his current emotions, he really didn't know what to say.","He was very panicked.","The soldier driving smiled again and said, \"But this is a good thing. Congratulations, Brigade Commander! Congratulations on becoming a father.\"","At this moment, Qin Yuanzheng slightly composed his thoughts, nodded, and said, \"Thank you.\"","In truth, Qin Yuanzheng was quite worried about Qiao Lanshu.","He heard that giving birth was very difficult and extremely painful.","His wife was the most delicate and the most afraid of pain. She was probably terrified right now.","He had to get to the hospital quickly to see how his wife was doing.","In his current state of mind, he had no time to think about whether it was a boy or a girl.","He only worried about how Qiao Lanshu was doing. Was she already crying from pain in the hospital?","Qin Yuanzheng remained tense for a moment before saying in a deep voice, \"Drive faster.\"","The soldier driving quickly nodded. \"Yes, I will try my best. But this is the urban area, there are many pedestrians, so we have to obey the speed limit.\"","Qin Yuanzheng's expression remained tight, and he didn't speak again.","He knew he was just losing his composure out of concern and was getting a bit anxious.","But his wife was about to give birth; how could he not be anxious?"]},{"number":174,"title":"Chapter 174: Have You Chosen a Name Yet","paragraphs":["When Qin Yuanzheng rushed to the hospital, Qiao Lanshu had already entered the delivery room.","Auntie Shi was outside the delivery room talking with Huang Erling. Seeing Qin Yuanzheng approach, Auntie Shi hurried over and said, \"Oh, Chief, you're finally here! Xiao Qiao has gone into the delivery room. I need to hurry back and pack some things; we'll need them when Xiao Qiao gives birth.\"","Even though Qin Yuanzheng had been mentally preparing himself for the past nine months, he was still incredibly nervous now that the day had actually arrived.","He stood there, nodding with a tense expression, and asked, \"How is Xiao Qiao?\"","Auntie Shi replied, \"She's fine. The doctor said she's in good condition, but giving birth isn't an easy process, so we might have to wait patiently.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He stood there staring at the doors of the delivery room, his body perfectly straight, and didn't speak for a long while.","Auntie Shi hesitated for a moment before repeating, \"Then, Chief, I'll head back first to pack?\"","Without looking at Auntie Shi, Qin Yuanzheng kept his eyes fixed on the delivery room doors and nodded. \"Alright, thank you for your trouble, Auntie Shi.\"","Auntie Shi quickly agreed and rushed out of the hospital to go home and pack.","After all, Qiao Lanshu had gone into labor so suddenly this time that Auntie Shi hadn't had the chance to prepare anything.","Huang Erling had initially heard that Qiao Lanshu was experiencing stomach pains, so she had hurried over with Auntie Shi.","Now that she saw Qin Yuanzheng had arrived, she didn't leave, but she didn't dare speak to him either.","Given Qin Yuanzheng's expression, Huang Erling figured he probably wasn't in the mood to talk anyway.","Before long, Wang Xue and Deng Weijun, along with their cousin-in-law Deng Xiaozhen, also arrived. They all came carrying items like dried noodles, canned goods, or eggs.","They had all heard that Qiao Lanshu was about to give birth, and since they had just gotten off work, they decided to come over together to check on her.","Qin Yuanzheng was anxious, but he had managed to calm down a bit by now and greeted them one by one.","Looking at his expression, Deng Xiaozhen knew he was nervous and comforted him, \"Don't worry, Xiao Qiao will definitely have a smooth delivery. She's always been in good health.\"","Qin Yuanzheng pursed his lips, standing there completely tense. Hearing Deng Xiaozhen's words, he only nodded but said nothing.","He had already been standing there for an hour, and there was still no news from the delivery room. He was burning with anxiety.","He felt that standing outside the delivery room, waiting for Xiao Qiao to give birth, was even more nerve-wracking than going into battle.","Qiao Lanshu had arrived at the hospital around three or four in the afternoon, and it wasn't until past seven in the evening that she finally delivered the baby.","Giving birth for the first time was indeed an ordeal. There were no other complications, it was just incredibly painful.","Fortunately, it was a natural birth, and everything went smoothly without any other issues.","The doctor wrapped the baby in swaddling clothes and brought him over for her to see. \"Quick, take a look. Is it a boy or a girl?\"","Qiao Lanshu was pale, her entire body trembling slightly—whether from weakness or cold, it was hard to tell.","With red-rimmed eyes, she stared at the baby. This was the child she had fought so hard to bring into the world.","The wrinkled newborn didn't look like anyone in particular yet, but looking at the eyebrows and nose, there was a faint resemblance to Qin Yuanzheng.","Qiao Lanshu asked softly, \"Doctor, is it a boy or a girl? Is the baby healthy?\"","Holding the baby with one arm, the doctor smiled and pulled the swaddle back a bit for Qiao Lanshu to see. \"Take a look for yourself, is it a boy or a girl?\"","Qiao Lanshu took one look and immediately found it amusing. \"So it's a boy.\"","She had actually had a vague feeling that it would be a boy, and sure enough, her intuition was right.","The delivering doctor placed the tiny baby on her chest and smiled, saying, \"Alright, the family members can come in now.\"","The delivery room doors opened, and a nurse came out, calling, \"Who are the family members of Comrade Qiao Lanshu?\"","Qin Yuanzheng stood there, and before he could even open his mouth, Deng Xiaozhen anxiously called out, \"Right here, right here! We all are.\"","The nurse smiled and said, \"The delivery went smoothly, both mother and child are safe. You can come in and see the baby and the mother now.\"","Immediately after, another doctor came out holding the baby and asked, \"Who is the husband of Comrade Qiao Lanshu?\"","Qin Yuanzheng's voice was strained and hoarse as he replied, \"I am.\"","Seeing him in a military uniform with an imposing aura, the doctor wasn't surprised. After all, when they arrived, the registration card had already stated that Qiao Lanshu was a military dependent.","The doctor smiled, brought the baby over, and handed him to Qin Yuanzheng. \"Congratulations, congratulations, you're a father! Your wife has given you a son.\"","His entire body somewhat stiff, Qin Yuanzheng took the baby.","Such a tiny child, so light, looking as if he wasn't even as big as the palm of his hand.","This was actually a little life, born from his wife's womb—his son.","So tiny, how on earth was he going to raise him?","Qin Yuanzheng stood there completely stiff, holding the baby in his arms, and didn't move for quite a while.","It wasn't until he heard the doctors say, \"Everything is fine, we can wheel the mother back to the ward,\"","that he suddenly snapped back to reality. His hands stiffly holding the infant in his arms, he hurried to the door of the delivery room and asked nervously, \"Doctor, what about my wife? Is my wife okay?\"","A nurse smiled and said, \"Don't worry, your wife is fine. Let's go, we're heading back to the ward now.\"","Qiao Lanshu lay on the hospital bed as the nurses wheeled her out of the delivery room.","Qin Yuanzheng quickly followed. He looked down at Qiao Lanshu, who looked haggard, her face pale, and even her lips so white they lacked any trace of color. His heart ached beyond measure.","He walked alongside the bed, asking as they went, \"Wife, how are you feeling?\"","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng, and the baby held in his arms, Qiao Lanshu finally felt at ease.","Not having seen Qin Yuanzheng earlier, she hadn't dared to sleep, terrified that someone else might take the baby away.","Although the possibility was very low, she just couldn't help but let her imagination run wild.","It was always better to be cautious about everything.","Now, seeing Qin Yuanzheng holding the baby, she smiled and said softly, \"Brother Zheng, I'm fine.\"","As she spoke, she closed her eyes. \"I'm going to sleep for a bit. I'm so tired.\"","From the onset of contractions to giving birth, several hours had passed. Qiao Lanshu was utterly exhausted and weak all over. She was so tired that she fell asleep the moment she closed her eyes.","Looking at her frail state, Qin Yuanzheng felt a wave of regret wash over him again.","If he had known what giving birth entailed, he wouldn't have let her have a child so soon. His wife was still young; he didn't know if giving birth this early would have any lasting effects on her body.","Auntie Shi had also returned to the hospital. She was carrying a large bag filled with various daily necessities, and in her hand, she held a thermal lunch box.","Inside the thermal box was the sweet potato and millet porridge she had cooked for Qiao Lanshu, along with some steamed buns and the like.","She walked beside Qin Yuanzheng and whispered, \"Chief, how about I hold the baby?\"","From the moment Qin Yuanzheng first held the baby, his two arms had been like rigid machinery, stiffly frozen without a single movement.","The baby lay in his arms, both eyes closed, and it was hard to tell if he was asleep or what.","Wang Xue and the others had all gone back; only Huang Erling and Deng Xiaozhen remained there.","Seeing Auntie Shi carrying so many things, Deng Xiaozhen said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Let me hold the baby. Let me rub off some of your good luck; I've been wanting to have a big, chubby boy myself.\"","However, having been unable to conceive for a long time, Deng Xiaozhen felt quite frustrated inside.","Qin Yuanzheng knew they wanted to help. After all, as a grown man, he didn't know how to take care of a baby or even how to hold one. Besides, he wanted to focus on taking care of Qiao Lanshu, like wiping her sweat.","After entering the hospital room, Qin Yuanzheng carefully placed the baby into Deng Xiaozhen's arms.","Deng Xiaozhen and Huang Erling sat on the empty hospital bed nearby, holding the baby with extreme care. Not daring to speak loudly, they murmured in low voices, discussing who the baby looked like.","Auntie Shi began to organize the things she had brought. Aside from food, she had brought Qiao Lanshu a change of pajamas, slippers, underwear, and other personal clothing.","She also brought daily necessities like a toothbrush and towels.","Including the baby's little clothes, tiny socks, diapers, formula, and baby bottles, she had brought absolutely everything, paying attention to every single detail.","Watching from the side, Huang Erling remarked, \"Auntie Shi, you really are meticulous and thoughtful. No wonder Regiment Commander Sun introduced you to Brigade Commander Qin. You really are experienced and careful.\"","Auntie Shi didn't look overly pleased by the compliment, as if she were already used to being praised.","Afraid of waking Qiao Lanshu, she lowered her voice and said, \"It's only what I should do. Xiao Qiao is young, and Commander Qin is usually busy. Since they don't have any elders at home, I just have to think ahead a bit more. Having a baby is a major event; we can't afford to be careless at all.\"","Deng Xiaozhen had never taken care of a child either, so this was an eye-opening experience for her. She asked Qin Yuanzheng, \"Yuanzheng, have you named the baby yet?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was sitting by Qiao Lanshu's bed. Feeling that her hands were very cold, he felt anxious and covered her with two blankets.","He gently smoothed out Qiao Lanshu's hair. Hearing Deng Xiaozhen's question, he shook his head and said, \"Not yet.\"","Today was the Beginning of Summer. He thought about just naming the baby Qin Lixia.","But he was afraid that when Xiao Qiao woke up, she would scold him for being too casual and giving the child such a simple name.","Qin Yuanzheng said softly, \"It is better to wait for Xiao Qiao to wake up and let Xiao Qiao name him.\"","After all, this was the child that Xiao Qiao had risked her life to bring into the world."]},{"number":175,"title":"Chapter 175: The Extremely Troublesome Mother of My Cousin","paragraphs":["After knowing that Qin Yuanzheng had arrived, Qiao Lanshu closed her eyes and fell asleep, sleeping soundly until the following afternoon.","Giving birth was more painful than she had imagined, but fortunately, everything went smoothly. When she woke up, she only felt hungry; otherwise, she felt pretty good.","Opening her eyes, she felt a warm weight in her arms. Looking down, she saw a wrinkled little baby resting against her chest.","Qiao Lanshu's heart stirred, and her gaze softened as she looked at the child.","The newborn was all wrinkled with bright red skin, not looking particularly pretty; but he was so tiny and soft, bound to her by blood. She looked at him again and again, reluctant to look away.","She was so absorbed in staring at the little baby on her chest that she completely failed to notice the person beside her.","Qin Yuanzheng hadn't slept all night. Seeing Qiao Lanshu wake up and then stare fixedly at the baby without even realizing he was right there, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't help but feel a little sour.","It seemed that in his wife's heart, he was no longer the most important person.","More importantly, he was now a father. He actually had a child with Qiao Lanshu.","His mindset hadn't shifted that quickly; he had felt like he was dreaming all night.","Qin Yuanzheng quietly stared at Qiao Lanshu for quite a while before calling out softly, \"Wife.\"","Hearing his voice, Qiao Lanshu finally looked up. She saw Qin Yuanzheng sitting by the bed, still wearing his crisp military uniform. However, he was unshaven and had dark circles under his eyes, clearly showing he had stayed up all night.","Seeing him, Qiao Lanshu immediately smiled. She lowered her voice and whispered, \"Brother Zheng, look, our baby.\"","Qin Yuanzheng followed her gaze and nodded with gentle eyes. \"The little brat is sleeping quietly now, but he kept me up all night.\"","Not long after being born, the baby had started pooping. The doctor called it meconium. It was pitch black and had given Qin Yuanzheng quite a fright.","Later, the baby cried. Auntie Shi said he was hungry and mixed a little formula for him, but the baby didn't like it.","Qin Yuanzheng had been so nervous he was covered in sweat.","Compared to taking care of a baby, he would truly rather go to war.","It was just too difficult.","Qiao Lanshu asked, \"Brother Zheng, have you picked a name for the baby yet?\"","Qin Yuanzheng reached out to pull the blanket up for her, then brushed some stray hair from her face before replying, \"I haven't decided yet. Do you have any ideas?\"","Actually, during the months of her pregnancy, the couple had discussed baby names quite a few times.","But they had never settled on one.","Because neither of them was particularly good at naming. They had flipped through the dictionary, but couldn't find anything they really liked.","Qin Yuanzheng paused for a moment, then suggested, \"How about Aiguo?\"","Upon hearing this name, Qiao Lanshu immediately shook her head. \"Let's not. So many people are named that.\"","Just glancing at the employee roster at the food factory, you could easily find several people named Aiguo.","Qin Yuanzheng tried again, \"Then how about Lixia?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng knew she didn't like it. Seeing her expression, he couldn't help but chuckle. \"I'm not great at this naming thing. How about we look through the dictionary together?\"","Qiao Lanshu held the little baby in her arms, looking at his wrinkled face.","She fell silent for a moment before saying, \"How about Qin Qiao'an?\"","Having experienced her past life, Qiao Lanshu knew how hard-won peace and stability were in this life.","She hoped that their family of three would be safe, sound, and have smooth sailing from now on.","Qin Yuanzheng thought the name Qiao'an sounded quite southern; at any rate, it didn't sound like a typical rough northern man's name.","It sounded quite gentle and refined when spoken.","But since his wife liked it, he naturally had no objections.","Moreover, Qiao was his wife's surname. Combining both their surnames with An for peace—he also felt it was a very good name.","He nodded immediately and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"It's a great name. I like it a lot.\"","With the name settled, the couple went back to staring at the baby for a long time.","Truth be told, even though the child was already born, neither of them had fully adjusted to their new reality.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"Brother Zheng, I really never imagined that we would have a child together.\"","When she first got together with Qin Yuanzheng, she truly hadn't thought about bearing him a child.","And so quickly, too.","They had only been married for about a year, and now their baby was here. It felt a bit surreal.","Just then, Auntie Shi returned from the cafeteria carrying lunchboxes. She had originally wanted to go home, cook, and bring the food over.","However, Qin Yuanzheng thought that would be too much trouble, so he asked her to get food from the hospital cafeteria and bought her plenty of meal tickets.","Auntie Shi walked in with a smile and said, \"Oh my, Xiao Qiao, you're finally awake. You must be hungry, right? Hurry, I bought you some porridge and mutton buns. Sit up and eat a little.\"","Having kept watch for a day and a night, Qin Yuanzheng stood up and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"I'll go home first to take a shower and tidy up the house. The doctor said you can be discharged and go home tomorrow.\"","Mother and son were safe and sound, and everything was normal, so the doctor said they could go home anytime.","They just needed to make sure she didn't catch a draft, along with a few other instructions for her postpartum confinement period.","With that, Qin Yuanzheng headed back first.","He planned to take a shower, check in on the troops at the mining area, and then officially start his leave.","Auntie Shi set the food on the small table and smiled at Qiao Lanshu. \"Xiao Qiao, you have no idea. When you were giving birth yesterday, Commander Qin was terrified. He stood motionless at the door of the delivery room like a statue. Nobody dared to speak to him.\"","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu pictured Qin Yuanzheng standing perfectly still outside the delivery room, his face taut with tension.","She couldn't help but chuckle softly and said, \"What a pity. I didn't get to see him like that.\"","As Auntie Shi laid out the pumpkin and millet porridge, mutton buns, and noodles with meat sauce, she remarked, \"You really found yourself a good husband, Xiao Qiao. It's obvious Commander Qin is deeply affectionate, devoted, and family-oriented. No wonder you were willing to marry so far from home; it was definitely worth it.\"","Saying this, Auntie Shi came over and reached out to take the baby. \"I'll mix some formula for the little one. You eat your food first.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded, sat up in bed, and picked up a mutton bun to eat.","Holding the baby in one arm and mixing the formula with the other, Auntie Shi asked, \"By the way, Xiao Qiao, have you named the baby yet?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and replied, \"Yes, his name is Qin Qiao'an.\"","Auntie Shi immediately beamed. \"Oh my, taking after both his parents' surnames? What a wonderful name! Then his nickname will be An'an? That sounds so lovely, doesn't it, An'an?\"","...","After Qiao Lanshu and Auntie Shi finished their meal, An'an also finished his formula and quickly fell asleep.","Qiao Lanshu didn't have much breast milk yet. Even when An'an nursed for a long time, he couldn't get much, so he mostly had to rely on formula.","In the afternoon, many colleagues and friends came to visit Qiao Lanshu.","Wang Xue brought along several female comrades who were on good terms with Qiao Lanshu. Each of them brought things like eggs and canned goods as gifts for her.","Deng Weijun also came over with Wang Haitang. They got married during the New Year and hadn't returned to Wang Haitang's family home yet.","They spent the New Year at the Deng family's place. After the holiday, the young couple returned to the city for work, and they were currently living a pretty good life.","Deng Weijun bought a few white-skinned sweet melons for Qiao Lanshu. These melons were very sweet and crisp; you could eat everything from the skin to the pulp, and it was currently the peak season for them.","The supply and marketing cooperative sold them, but they were expensive—pricier than apples and pears—so ordinary people were usually reluctant to buy them.","Deng Weijun specifically bought them for Qiao Lanshu to eat. After all, she had just given birth, which was a major life event!","Qiao Lanshu said to him, \"Why did you buy such expensive melons? Take them back with you later and save them for Haitang.\"","Since getting married, Haitang seemed less timid than before. She quickly said, \"Sister-in-law, please don't be so polite with us. Just keep them for yourself; you need to nourish your body.\"","Seeing them being so polite, Auntie Shi felt too embarrassed to point out that postpartum women shouldn't eat raw or cold foods.","However, sweet melons were good things. If she used them to boil goat's milk for Xiao Qiao, it would probably taste quite good.","Before Deng Weijun and Haitang left, Deng Xiaozhen and Yang Wenyan arrived along with Qin Yuanzheng.","Deng Xiaozhen's face was a bit pale, and she didn't seem to be in the right state of mind.","As soon as she came over, she went to look at the baby and smiled at Auntie Shi, saying, \"This baby is so handsome. He has the exact same big eyes and double eyelids as Xiao Qiao, but his nose looks like his dad's. He'll definitely grow up to be a handsome young man.\"","Auntie Shi smiled and replied, \"Of course. With such a handsome father and beautiful mother, the child is bound to be good-looking too.\"","As the two of them chatted with Qiao Lanshu, the hospital room became a bit crowded.","The three men—Qin Yuanzheng, Yang Wenyan, and Deng Weijun—stood out in the hallway.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Yang Wenyan and asked, \"Cousin, what was going on just now? Who were you and my cousin-in-law hiding from?\"","On his way to the hospital earlier, Qin Yuanzheng had seen Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen coming out of the cooperative carrying a bag of eggs and two packets of noodles, clearly intending to visit Qiao Lanshu.","But they were sneaking around as if they had done something wrong, so Qin Yuanzheng went straight over to them.","Yang Wenyan frowned, sighed, and said, \"It's because my mom is here. She... she brought my aunt, along with my cousin and his wife.\"","Qin Yuanzheng hadn't quite figured out the situation yet. Although he and Yang Wenyan were cousins, he wasn't very familiar with Yang Wenyan's family affairs. After all, he had been in the army for many years and hadn't joined in the New Year family visits.","Standing nearby, Deng Weijun suddenly realized what was happening. He frowned angrily and said, \"Brother-in-law, your mom and your aunt are here again? What do they want this time?\"","Deng Weijun was clearly not very fond of Yang Wenyan's mother, aunt, and those other relatives.","He said, \"Don't tell me they're here to make you divorce my sister again?\"","Deng Weijun felt extremely irritated.","Both he and his sister were from the village. His sister, Deng Xiaozhen, was indeed lucky to marry Yang Wenyan, who came from an urban worker's family.","Back then, even before Yang Wenyan became the factory director, many people already looked down on Deng Xiaozhen and often gossiped about her.","Now that Yang Wenyan was the factory director, and had even helped Deng Weijun transfer his household registration and find a job, the relatives on the Yang family's side were even more dissatisfied.","They often asked Yang Wenyan for help, but most of the time, he refused them.","However, it was hard for him to refuse his own biological mother.","Yang Wenyan said in a low voice, \"Weijun, keep your voice down. Don't get worked up. When my mom and the others came over this time, they didn't mention making me get a divorce.\"","Deng Weijun still felt something was off. He looked at Yang Wenyan and asked in confusion, \"They used to constantly say my sister couldn't have children and kept forcing you to divorce. They came all the way to the city this time, and they actually didn't bring it up?\"","In the past, they always brought it up, looking down on Deng Xiaozhen and demanding that Yang Wenyan divorce his wife, spouting sayings like 'there are three forms of unfilial conduct, and having no descendants is the worst.'","The Qing Dynasty was long gone, and the New China had been established for decades, yet these people were still living in ancient times.","In the past, Deng Weijun was young and had indeed benefited from Yang Wenyan's connections, so he hadn't dared to say much.","It was always Deng Xiaozhen arguing with those people.","But time and time again, even if Deng Weijun had a mild temper, he was now starting to get angry.","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng instantly grew serious. He asked, \"Cousin, what exactly is going on? Aunt is making you and my cousin-in-law get a divorce?\"","Deng Weijun's face darkened, and he sneered, \"It's not the first time. They've brought it up at least three times. They complain that my sister hasn't had a child and is holding my brother-in-law back. They say that since he's a factory director, lots of young women would throw themselves at him, and he could have as many kids as he wants.\"","Yang Wenyan's face instantly darkened, and he said sternly, \"Weijun!\"","Deng Weijun stood there with a dark expression and stopped talking.","Since they were talking about this right outside the hospital room, the women inside naturally heard them too.","Wang Haitang looked at Deng Xiaozhen with some concern.","Deng Xiaozhen was holding An'an in her arms, her eyes red, and she remained silent.","Auntie Shi and Qiao Lanshu exchanged a glance. Neither of them spoke for a moment, just listening to the men outside continue their conversation.","Yang Wenyan said in a deep voice, \"Xiaozhen and I truly love each other. We've been married for five or six years and have a deep bond. Not even my own mother can tear us apart.\"","Yang Wenyan wasn't a factory director from the very beginning. He used to work at the grassroots level, which was very exhausting, working day and night. Being alone in the city with no one to look after him, life hadn't been that easy.","At that time, Deng Xiaozhen was just a temporary worker, and she had a younger brother still in school, so her life was also difficult.","When they met, it was during the loneliest and hardest times of their lives.","Yang Wenyan said softly:","\"Life was hard back then. We couldn't even get enough to eat and had to tighten our belts and drink water to feel full every day. It was so cold in the winter, and we didn't even have charcoal for a fire at home. I think Xiaozhen might be malnourished and her body suffered from the freezing cold, which is why it's hard for her to conceive. I've been looking for traditional Chinese medicine doctors to help her condition her body over the past two years. I'm not in a hurry about having a child, and Weijun, you shouldn't worry either. I've never said I wanted to divorce your sister.\"","Deng Weijun was raised by his sister when he was little.","She was the one who paid his school fees, so he was very close to her.","Although he wasn't always very reliable, he cared deeply for his sister and worried about her being bullied.","Now, hearing Yang Wenyan say this, he squatted on the ground with red eyes, remaining silent.","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng finally understood. It turned out that his aunt, Yang Wenyan's mother, was forcing Yang Wenyan to divorce and remarry.","The reason was that Deng Xiaozhen couldn't have children.","Qin Yuanzheng asked in a low voice, \"Cousin, your mom came again today?\"","It wasn't easy to make a trip to the city; it was too far.","Their visit this time probably meant they were going to stir up trouble again.","Yang Wenyan smiled bitterly and nodded: \"Xiaozhen and I didn't go back home for the New Year, remember? My mom got anxious when she saw we weren't coming back. This time, she came over with my aunt, my cousin, and his wife. Oh, right, they even brought along my cousin's newborn third child.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Yang Wenyan: \"She didn't come to force me to get a divorce this time. She brought the baby over and said she wants me to adopt him.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly felt a deep sense of empathy.","Because he had remained unmarried for so long, coupled with his infertility, people back in his hometown had also suggested giving him a child to adopt."]},{"number":176,"title":"Chapter 176: Not Bold Enough","paragraphs":["Yang Wenyan was only a little over a year older than Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng was thirty this year, and he had previously been relentlessly pressured to get married.","Although Yang Wenyan was married, he still didn't have any children. Seeing that he was already thirty-one, and even Qin Yuanzheng, who had infertility issues, had become a father, Yang Wenyan's family grew even more anxious.","Hearing the word adoption, Qin Yuanzheng instinctively felt a wave of disgust.","After all, he had also been pressured by his relatives back in his hometown to adopt a child from the extended family.","With a dark expression, he said, Cousin, you need to think this through. If you don't want to do it, you should make it clear to Auntie as soon as possible. Handle it cleanly once and for all, and don't let it drag on endlessly.","Yang Wenyan gloomily took out a Daqianmen cigarette, lit it with a match, and stood in the corridor smoking with a deep frown.","Qin Yuanzheng kept a straight face: We're in a hospital. Put the cigarette out.","Yang Wenyan was speechless.","He silently stubbed out the cigarette.","Qin Yuanzheng used to smoke occasionally, but after getting together with Qiao Lanshu, he quit completely.","Now, he also found the smell of smoke choking. Afraid of bothering his wife and child inside, he reached back and shut the ward door.","Seeing the door close, the women in the room exchanged glances.","Deng Xiaozhen placed the baby in the cradle, sat down on a nearby chair, and wiped her tears with her sleeve.","Qiao Lanshu said sympathetically, Cousin-in-law, don't be too sad. When it comes to adopting a relative's child, if you don't like the idea, you must refuse. This isn't something you can compromise on.","Auntie Shi brought out some fried dough twists and sunflower seeds to treat Deng Xiaozhen and Wang Haitang, chiming in,","Comrade Deng, please don't think I'm being too nosy, but I feel you should wait until you're forty to even consider adopting. You're still young and can still have kids of your own, so don't rush it. Those people who want you to adopt their kids are just eyeing your family's money and the fact that your husband is a factory manager, aren't they? Stand your ground and don't compromise.","Wang Haitang sat silently beside Deng Xiaozhen without saying a word, thinking to herself how terrifying the older generation could be. They had to meddle in everything their children did, which was incredibly annoying.","Deng Xiaozhen sighed and whispered, That's what I think too. But without a child of my own, I always feel inferior.","Deng Xiaozhen naturally had a fiery temper and feared nothing. Since getting married, she had gotten into plenty of arguments with her in-laws.","Even when Wang Haitang's family came over, she was capable of scolding them away.","However, lacking a child made her feel guilty deep down, so she couldn't muster up her usual tough attitude.","When Yang Wenyan's mother came knocking, Deng Xiaozhen had gotten into a huge fight with her. After Yang Wenyan returned home, he made an excuse about needing to go to the supply and marketing cooperative to buy meat and vegetables for dinner, quickly taking Deng Xiaozhen away to hide.","Even now, those relatives were still lingering at Yang Wenyan's house.","Deng Xiaozhen cried silently for a while before saying fiercely, If Yang Wenyan dares to adopt, I'll divorce him!","Everyone was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu remained silent, though she secretly approved of this decision.","Auntie Shi, being older, didn't quite agree. Xiao Deng, don't be impulsive. If you get a divorce, you might not find such a good man again.","Auntie Shi's family was of average means. She knew that these days, jobs were hard to find and money was hard to earn.","So she urged Deng Xiaozhen not to act rashly and avoid a hasty divorce.","Out in the corridor, Yang Wenyan knocked and opened the door. Seeing Deng Xiaozhen inside, he said to her,","Xiaozhen, we've been out for a long time. How about this: I'll go back and talk to my mom first. Once they leave, I'll come pick you up. They'll have to go to a guesthouse when it gets dark anyway, so they definitely won't bother us tonight.","After all, it was his own mother; Yang Wenyan couldn't just ignore her. Having hidden outside for so long, he still had to go back and check.","Red-eyed, Deng Xiaozhen asked him, How many days is their letter of introduction good for?","Yang Wenyan replied, I don't know, I haven't asked yet. I'm guessing just one day. The village wouldn't issue an introduction letter for too long.","Deng Xiaozhen sneered, Then until they leave, I'll go stay at Weijun's place. Come find me only after they're gone.","Yang Wenyan thought about it and could only nod. Alright, I'll go back and take a look first.","At a time like this, Yang Wenyan didn't want Deng Xiaozhen to go back either, as it would just lead to more arguing. The main issue was that Deng Xiaozhen felt insecure about not having a son, so she couldn't win an argument against those relatives anyway.","Sigh.","Sighing inwardly, Yang Wenyan said goodbye to Qin Yuanzheng, turned around, and left the hospital. He went to the cooperative to buy some meat and vegetables, then headed home.","After Yang Wenyan left, Deng Xiaozhen also departed with her brother, Deng Weijun, and Wang Haitang.","Auntie Shi sighed endlessly in the ward, bringing up gossip about the neighbors.","Every family had its own cross to bear—if not about money, it was about children, inheritances, or conflicts between mothers-in-law and daughters-in-law.","Those without kids argued, those with only daughters and no sons argued, those with daughters-in-law argued, and those without daughters-in-law argued too.","After lamenting for a while, Auntie Shi added, My youngest son is eighteen this year. He still doesn't have a job and isn't married. Sigh, as a mother, I'm worried sick too.","Qin Yuanzheng had already looked into Auntie Shi's family background.","Her husband was a construction worker. Her eldest son was about twenty; after finishing middle school, he went to the countryside as an educated youth.","Her second son was eighteen. He didn't have to go to the countryside, but he hadn't found a job either. He was quite lazy, refusing to do hard labor at the construction site, and instead stayed home asking his parents for money every day.","She also had a daughter who was still in middle school. According to Auntie Shi, even after graduation, it was uncertain whether she'd be able to find a job.","These days, jobs in the city were getting harder and harder to come by.","Many people retired early, preferring to give up their pensions just to pass their jobs on to their children.","The children were still young and needed something to do, otherwise they wouldn't be able to find a wife.","Auntie Shi sighed and said, It's frustrating not having kids, and it's frustrating having them. Sigh, life really isn't easy.","Thinking of the expression on Deng Xiaozhen's face when she left, Qiao Lanshu also sighed silently, not knowing what to say.","Qin Yuanzheng walked into the room and immediately went to check on the baby.","Seeing Auntie Shi holding a bottle to feed the baby, he quickly walked over and said softly, Let me do it.","As a new father, he was currently overflowing with paternal love. Holding the baby in one hand and the bottle in the other, he gently placed the nipple in the baby's mouth, sitting by the bed and watching his child drink.","Auntie Shi also warmed up a cup of goat's milk for Qiao Lanshu.","Seeing this, Qin Yuanzheng smiled and said, You mother and son drinking milk together—it's quite a harmonious picture.","Qiao Lanshu looked at him with a smile. Do you want some?","Saying this, she offered him the cup.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at the goat's milk in her hand, and then cast a meaningful glance at Qiao Lanshu's chest.","Qiao Lanshu's face instantly turned red. She gave him a reproachful glare and scolded, The baby is right here, be serious.","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","Feeling a bit wronged, he said, I didn't even say anything.","Qiao Lanshu muttered under her breath, Even if you don't say it, I know exactly what you're thinking.","Qiao Lanshu spoke, then lowered her voice, \"What will happen to Cousin and his wife? They won't really get a divorce, will they?\"","Qiao Lanshu felt that if Yang Wenyan couldn't handle his own mother, given Deng Xiaozhen's fiery temper, a divorce was highly likely.","Qin Yuanzheng, holding the baby, said without even lifting his head, \"Cousin just isn't decisive enough. The dumbest but easiest way would be for him to just hide out somewhere. In a few days, when his aunt's and the others' introduction letters expire, they'll naturally have to leave. Otherwise, he needs to be more forceful—take his mother back home, have his father and brothers keep a close eye on her, and stop her from coming to the city in the future. That would work too.\"","Qin Yuanzheng's personality was very dominant. His family only ever dared to casually mention the idea of adoption to him; they would never dare actually bring a child to his doorstep.","If they ever dared to do such a thing, Qin Yuanzheng would march them straight to the police station and report them for child trafficking. Let's see if they'd ever dare to come back after that.","Qiao Lanshu looked at Qin Yuanzheng and smiled. \"Cousin is actually quite smart; he's just a bit blindly devoted to his parents.\"","...","Meanwhile, Yang Wenyan bought some fresh vegetables from the supply and marketing cooperative, along with some cookies and melon seeds, and brought them home.","When he arrived home, his mother and aunt were sitting and talking. Mother Yang opened the door and saw him. She immediately looked behind him. Not seeing Deng Xiaozhen, her face instantly fell. \"Why are you back alone? Where is Deng Xiaozhen? Didn't she come back with you?\"","Carrying the groceries inside, Yang Wenyan said, \"Xiaozhen had some things to take care of at the factory. She went to work overtime.\"","Mother Yang sneered. \"Is she working overtime? Or is she hiding from us? Tell me, did she throw another fit with you?\"","Yang Wenyan replied dismissively, \"Nothing of the sort, Mom. Xiaozhen has a good temperament; she wouldn't throw a fit with me.\"","His aunt, still holding melon seeds in her hand, said while cracking them, \"I say, Wenyan, you are a factory manager now. Why are you keeping that shrew around? If you had just listened to us, gotten a divorce, and married another wife, we wouldn't have had to make this trip today.\"","With that, his aunt turned her head and called out to her son and daughter-in-law, \"Eldest, Eldest's wife, come here quickly. Bring the baby over and let your brother have a look.\"","Yang Wenyan glanced at his older cousin and his cousin's wife, feeling a surge of irritation.","He said, \"I'll go start cooking. You haven't eaten yet, you must be hungry.\"","Hearing this, his aunt knew immediately that Yang Wenyan was unwilling.","She hurriedly took the baby from her daughter-in-law's arms, walked up to Yang Wenyan, and said,","\"Oh my, there's no rush to cook. Look at this child, isn't he adorable? How about having him as your son? We are close relatives. I am your own aunt, and this is my own grandson. Adopting my own grandson to be your son is not like taking in some stranger from the outside. What else could you possibly be dissatisfied with?\"","Mother Yang immediately chimed in, \"Exactly! If you aren't willing to adopt, then divorce that woman surnamed Deng!\"","Before coming over today, they had already discussed it thoroughly: they would either make Yang Wenyan get a divorce and remarry, or have him adopt his aunt's grandson as his own son.","Either way, they were determined to force Yang Wenyan to compromise.","Hearing Mother Yang say this, his aunt was actually a bit displeased; she much preferred the idea of Yang Wenyan adopting her grandson.","Originally, before coming, she had been a bit reluctant. After all, it was a grandson, not a granddaughter. Even though they already had two grandsons at home, who would ever complain about having too many grandsons?","However, after arriving here and seeing their spacious and clean courtyard, the small house equipped with heating, all sorts of beautiful tableware, sofas, tables and chairs, as well as a bicycle, a radio, and a sewing machine...","His aunt's mind started working.","Where in the countryside could one find such fine things?","Back in their village, her children couldn't even afford to eat cookies.","Look at this place—the table was laden with cookies, melon seeds, candies, and other delicious treats.","She had just taken a peek into the kitchen and found that they actually stocked both cornmeal and refined white flour!","Such a standard of living was something they wouldn't even dare to dream of back in the village!","His aunt quickly urged, \"Wenyan, since you and your wife still have feelings for each other, then don't get a divorce. Listen to your aunt, adopt this child. He is a child related to you by blood; what is there to dislike?\"","She paused for a moment, then added, \"Look, the child's facial features even look a bit like yours.\"","Yang Wenyan lowered his head and looked at the baby. The child was only a few months old, chubby and robust, looking very cute.","Yang Wenyan liked children too, so he couldn't help but take a few extra glances.","His aunt immediately tried to shove the baby into his arms. \"Hold the baby. Come on, give him a hug.\"","Yang Wenyan didn't take the child. His hands were still full of groceries, and he walked straight toward the kitchen. \"Aunt, let's talk about this later. Xiaozhen and I are still young, we will definitely have our own children. If we adopt now, what happens if we have our own child later? Wouldn't that be a mess?\"","His aunt looked at Mother Yang and said, \"Sister, this son of yours is stubborn enough. They've been married for seven or eight years and haven't had a child. I don't think they'll ever have one. These young people don't understand, but as a mother, you can't be ignorant of this.\"","Mother Yang began to feel anxious as well. She walked into the kitchen, glared at Yang Wenyan, and said angrily, \"Eldest! I've said it, you either get a divorce or you adopt! Otherwise, now that I'm here, I'm not leaving!\"","Yang Wenyan: \"...\"","While washing the vegetables, Yang Wenyan said, \"Mom, what's the rush? It's not like you don't have grandchildren to hold. Haven't Second Brother and Third Brother both had kids?\"","Mother Yang's eyes grew red with anger. \"You said it yourself, your younger brothers and sisters have all had children. As the eldest, you still don't have a son or a daughter. Tell me, are you doing right by me?\"","Yang Wenyan was even more speechless. \"Mom, me not having children is my own business. As long as I am filial to you and provide for you and Dad in your old age, that's enough. You should worry less about other things.\"","He continued, \"I'm only 31, and Xiaozhen is just 27. We are still young. Maybe she'll get pregnant this year. Why are you so anxious? Besides, even if we really did need to adopt, we should wait until we're in our forties to consider it, right? When the time comes, you won't even need to say a word; I'll take Xiaozhen to find a child to adopt myself, and I guarantee you'll be satisfied.\"","It would have been better if he hadn't spoken. As soon as he did, Mother Yang became furious. \"She's already 27, and you have the nerve to say she's young? When your mother was 27, you were already 10 years old, did you know that?\"","Yang Wenyan: \"...\"","Outside the kitchen, his aunt, holding the baby, stood in the living room. She looked at her daughter-in-law and lowered her voice, \"What's the matter, are you still giving me attitude? Look at the sofa here, look at the cookies and candies. Do we have these things in our village? I brought my grandson here to enjoy a good life, so don't you dare make a scene, do you hear me?\"","The daughter-in-law sat on the sofa, looking at the child held in her mother-in-law's arms, daring to feel angry but not daring to speak.","They kept making a scene at Yang Wenyan's house right into the evening. Yang Wenyan steadfastly refused to give in, but his mother and aunt were not about to compromise easily either.","Seeing that it was getting late, his mother and aunt simply decided to stay the night at his place.","Yang Wenyan's cousin and his wife ended up sleeping in the living room.","They refused to even stay at a local guesthouse, completely unwilling to part with their money.","In the middle of the night, the baby cried incessantly. The noise kept Yang Wenyan awake the entire night. Annoyed and restless, he lay there wondering what he was going to do tomorrow.","He had to figure out a way to send these people packing as soon as possible."]},{"number":177,"title":"Chapter 177: Discharged from the Hospital","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu was discharged from the hospital and returned home on the fifth day after giving birth.","The doctor had originally said she was fine and could go home early to begin her postpartum confinement.","But Qin Yuanzheng was worried, so they stayed in the hospital for a few extra days.","By the time she was discharged, even though it was already the beginning of summer, the climate in Longcheng was still somewhat cold, with a huge temperature difference between morning and evening.","Qin Yuanzheng brought a hat, gloves, and a scarf for Qiao Lanshu, along with one of his own military overcoats, bundling her up tightly.","He wrapped her up so thoroughly that only her eyes were visible, and asked in a low voice, Does it still hurt when you walk?","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. Not much anymore.","Her body's ability to recover surprised her; she had previously thought that she would need to rest for a very long time after giving birth.","But she was able to get out of bed and walk on the very same day, and by the third day, she barely felt any pain.","It was just that her body was still weak, and she needed to go home and lie down to rest.","Qin Yuanzheng said softly, I'll carry you out.","With that, he suddenly bent down and scooped Qiao Lanshu into his arms, carrying her all the way out of the hospital, drawing the attention of quite a few doctors and nurses.","Auntie Shi carried a bag on her back, which was filled with the daily necessities they had used over the past few days.","With her hands free, she held the baby. The baby was wrapped in swaddling clothes, and Auntie Shi used a small blanket to shield the baby's eyes, afraid that the glaring sunlight outside would make the little one uncomfortable.","As they were leaving, some nurses began whispering among themselves, Is that Regiment Commander Qin? I heard he finally had a child at an older age. He must be thrilled, right?","Someone corrected her, He's not a Regiment Commander anymore, you should call him Brigade Commander. He just got promoted this year.","Another said with evident envy, What a young Brigade Commander. That southern girl is so lucky. She traveled thousands of miles to find her fiancé, only to be deceived. Everyone thought she was destined for a hard life, but look what happened? She actually married Brigade Commander Qin and even gave birth to a son for him, a man everyone thought was infertile! Now, Brigade Commander Qin is going to spoil her to the heavens, isn't he?","So, this is fate. Not everyone is blessed with such luck. As they say, fate brings people together from a thousand miles away, but without it, you can't even hold hands with the person right in front of you.","Just as the nurse finished speaking, a colleague next to her nudged her arm with an elbow.","The group looked up and saw Nurse Yang standing nearby. Having overheard their discussion, her face looked terrible.","They exchanged awkward glances and instantly fell silent, lowering their heads and scurrying back to their posts to work.","Nurse Yang was exactly the person they had just referred to as the one who couldn't hold hands with the person right in front of her.","Although Qin Yuanzheng had gone on blind dates with several female comrades, Nurse Yang was the only one who had ever reached the stage of discussing marriage with him.","After all, Nurse Yang's father was the Deputy Commander of the local military region.","Under the circumstances at the time, if the Deputy Commander took a liking to a certain Battalion Commander and wanted him as a son-in-law, it was practically a done deal.","The Battalion Commander would have no reason, nor the courage, to easily refuse.","And yet...","Nurse Yang walked forward with a dark expression, trying her best to ignore the murmurs around her.","She felt miserable inside, but her proud and competitive nature kept her from showing her emotions.","As she passed by the hospital's main entrance, she couldn't resist casting a glance outside.","That single glance allowed her to see the tall and broad Qin Yuanzheng, dressed in a crisp, tailored military uniform, carrying the petite Qiao Lanshu in his arms in a princess hold.","Qiao Lanshu was wrapped in his military overcoat, a hat on her head, bundled up so tightly from head to toe that not even a finger was exposed.","Qin Yuanzheng had broad shoulders and a wide back, completely shielding Qiao Lanshu. From Nurse Yang's angle, she could only see Qiao Lanshu's hands wrapped around Qin Yuanzheng's neck. Their faces were incredibly close, and Qin Yuanzheng was slightly bent over, his head lowered as if he were whispering sweet nothings to her.","An unspeakable bitterness swelled in Nurse Yang's heart. She withdrew her gaze, feeling a twinge of hatred, yet not knowing who she should even hate.","She felt that she would probably never get married in this lifetime.","Because she would never again meet a man as good as Qin Yuanzheng.","...","Qin Yuanzheng didn't drive himself this time; he had his guard drive the car.","He took the baby from Auntie Shi's arms and let her sit in the passenger seat.","He and Qiao Lanshu sat in the back.","The car windows were tightly shut, yet he still asked Qiao Lanshu anxiously, Are you cold? Is there a draft coming through the window?","People with weak bodies are very sensitive to changes in the weather.","Before Qiao Lanshu had the baby, she could sleep at home with the windows open and never thought the wind was too strong.","But now, even with the car windows tightly shut, she could still clearly feel the howling cold wind seeping in from outside.","Qin Yuanzheng and Auntie Shi certainly didn't feel it; they might even find it stuffy.","No wonder women weren't supposed to be exposed to the wind after giving birth and had to lie in a sealed room for their postpartum confinement.","Skipping confinement was definitely not an option.","Qiao Lanshu pulled the collar of the overcoat a bit tighter around herself and said, There is a bit of a draft, but it's okay. I'm very warm wrapped in your coat.","Qin Yuanzheng looked at the window. He gently placed the baby in Qiao Lanshu's arms, then took off his own jacket and draped it over her. Is that better?","Qiao Lanshu nodded and couldn't help but laugh. Do I look really strange like this?","Wrapped in layer after layer, the clothes on her body must have weighed several pounds.","Afraid of tiring Qiao Lanshu, Qin Yuanzheng quickly took the baby back. Holding the baby in one arm, he reached out his other hand to rub Qiao Lanshu's head, whispering, How is it strange? You look very cute like this.","Hearing him say this, Qiao Lanshu instantly blushed with embarrassment.","She could see Auntie Shi and the guard smiling in the front seats!","Qiao Lanshu looked at Qin Yuanzheng and whispered, You really look like a father now. You're holding the baby like a true pro.","The very first time Qin Yuanzheng held the baby, he stood there, too afraid to move, his arms stiff as boards.","But now, he could expertly hold the baby with just one arm.","His arms were thick and strong. After the little baby finished drinking milk, he would just lie on his arm to sleep, and as Qin Yuanzheng gently rocked his arm, it practically worked as a cradle.","Qin Yuanzheng whispered to Qiao Lanshu, Of course. I specifically learned from Auntie Shi.","Infants were so soft and fragile; Qin Yuanzheng hadn't known how to hold one or where to even begin. It was only after Auntie Shi taught him that he figured it out.","Qin Yuanzheng added, I've asked for a month's leave. I'll take care of the baby for this month, so you can just focus on resting at home. I'll have Auntie Shi look into some recipes and make you more nutritious meals to help your body recover.","Being older, Qin Yuanzheng naturally thought things through more thoroughly. His heart ached for Qiao Lanshu, as she had become a mother at the tender age of nineteen.","She was still so young—practically a child herself—and yet she already had a baby.","Every time Qin Yuanzheng thought about this, he felt an overwhelming surge of tender affection for her.","He continued, Since you don't have a lot of breastmilk, why don't you just nurse during the day, and at night we can let An'an drink formula or goat's milk? I've already brought back a female goat from the base. We can have Auntie Shi milk it and boil the milk for the baby.","Sure enough, the political commissar at the base had great foresight, having sent him a female goat so early on.","Qin Yuanzheng, now that he had a child, suddenly became quite chatty. And as for those chickens, ducks, and geese I am raising at the military base, I have already asked the canteen staff to stew a chicken for you every day so you can have chicken soup daily.","Before Qiao Lanshu could even get a word in, Qin Yuanzheng lowered his voice and started discussing things with her again. Now that we have a child and a sheep to raise, I was thinking, how about we stop living in the apartment building and move to the courtyard next door?","The apartment building they currently lived in was newly built, specifically allocated for military officers. When they first got married and moved in, the rooms were brand new and had never been lived in before.","The adjacent courtyards, on the other hand, were older houses originally built as large communal compounds. After being assigned to the military, they were renovated and partitioned with new walls. Some courtyards housed two or three families, while other smaller ones accommodated only a single household.","Qin Yuanzheng had his eye on one of those smaller courtyards. Because of its size, it could only house one family.","Aside from the main hall used as a living room and the kitchen, there were only two rooms. The rooms were quite small and featured built-in heated brick beds, known as kangs.","He reasoned with Qiao Lanshu, The advantage of these places is the little yard. We can use it to grow vegetables and raise a dog or our sheep. Later, when the baby is older, he will have space to play without being cooped up in an apartment. Plus, those courtyards have perimeter walls and guards at the main gates, so the security is just the same.","There are quite a few downsides, too. It is an old house, so before we move in, we will need to do some serious repairs. The walls, the roof, the floors, and the yard all need work. Also, the house is not very big. I went to take a look, and neither of the two rooms is very spacious. Both kangs will need to be rebuilt, and the flues will probably have to be modified. It will take quite a bit of effort.","Worried that Qiao Lanshu might dislike the idea, Qin Yuanzheng quickly added, Central heating has been connected over there too, so you do not have to worry about being cold.","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu asked, If it is a private courtyard, why hasn't anyone moved in?","Qin Yuanzheng replied softly, Because it is old. When there are such beautiful, new apartments available, who would choose to live in a small courtyard like that? I never thought about bringing you to live in an old place either, but now that we have a child, things are different.","Huang Erling and Zhao Jiannong also had two children, but they had still chosen to live in the apartment building.","In this day and age, with nice apartments available, many people truly did not like living in courtyards.","After all, many of them had lived in large communal courtyards and had grown up in that environment. The people living there would often argue and clash over trivial matters.","The soundproofing was poor, the toilets were shared, and in some places, even the kitchens were communal, meaning people had to line up just to cook.","Who would ever want to live in a courtyard after experiencing all that?","The small courtyard Qin Yuanzheng had his eye on had been vacant for two months. He had gone to see it twice and then asked the logistics department to keep an eye on it and hold it for him.","He figured that since Qiao Lanshu had given birth, they needed to bring the sheep over to raise it. Also, the chickens, ducks, and geese kept at the base would be better off raised in their own yard. When they wanted to eat one, they could just slaughter it, which would be much more convenient.","It was now the beginning of summer, and the weather was warm. He also planned to have Auntie Shi plant some vegetables in the yard for Qiao Lanshu and the baby to eat.","Right, he also planned to plant an apple tree in the yard, and a persimmon tree, and oh, a jujube tree...","These were all things that women and children loved to eat, and they were nutritious. However, the yard was not very big. Would there be enough room to plant them all?","As he spoke, Qin Yuanzheng fell deep into thought again.","Watching his expression, Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, I support you. A small courtyard it is. It actually sounds quite nice, and having a little yard to grow vegetables in is a bonus.","In the future, they could close the courtyard gate and safely let their child play in the mud. If they lived in an apartment building, it would not be nearly as convenient.","Qin Yuanzheng kissed Qiao Lanshu on the cheek and murmured, Then it is settled. You just rest at home and focus on your postpartum confinement. While I have some free time, I will take a few engineers over to fix the place up.","He wanted to renovate the courtyard beautifully.","Although it was a private courtyard, its location was a bit out of the way. He would need to raise the height of the perimeter walls and replace the glass with new panes...","Qin Yuanzheng was already mentally planning how to renovate the small space.","What he did not mention was that, despite it being a somewhat old courtyard, other people had actually inquired about it before.","Relying on the fact that he now had a child, Qin Yuanzheng brazenly asked them to reserve the yard for him.","However, he would also vacate his current apartment so it could be reassigned to someone else.","The courtyard was a bit far from their current apartment building, separated by several other buildings and large communal compounds. If Qiao Lanshu wanted to come back and visit in the future, she would have to walk for quite a while.","Along the way, the couple finalized their plans to move, and before they knew it, they had arrived back at the military residential compound.","As usual, Qin Yuanzheng carried Qiao Lanshu back home in his arms. Auntie Shi followed closely behind, carrying the baby.","The guard helped carry their bags and luggage.","Once they were home, Qin Yuanzheng gently placed Qiao Lanshu on the kang, immediately laid the baby down beside her, and then rushed off without stopping to seal the windows.","The windows were already closed, but worried about drafts, Qin Yuanzheng took some strips of cloth and tightly stuffed all the edges around the frames.","After finishing that, Qin Yuanzheng went to pick up the keys to the small courtyard next door and took some people over to inspect the place.","After all, he was still entirely fixated on bringing the mother sheep back, as that was his little baby's food supply."]},{"number":178,"title":"Chapter 178: The Child Was Left Behind","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng had been busy for several days in a row before he finally managed to get that dilapidated little courtyard mostly repaired.","He had brought along a few engineers from his unit to help with the work. The engineers were experienced, physically fit, and worked with agility.","They repaired the roof and the walls, and even repaved some of the floor tiles.","The glass in all the windows had been shattered, so new panes had to be cut and installed.","Once all of this was done, the next step was to find someone to rebuild the heated brick bed, known as a kang.","When Qin Yuanzheng first got married, he had hired Uncle Huang to build their kang.","Naturally, he bought cigarettes and liquor to invite him over again this time.","Uncle Huang happily strolled around the courtyard and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"This courtyard is great. It is much more spacious than the apartment building you live in. When the baby grows up, they will be able to play in the yard.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was wearing an old blue Dacron shirt speckled with mud. He followed Uncle Huang into the house and smiled, saying, \"The main reason is that I also have a sheep to raise. It wouldn't be very convenient without a courtyard.\"","Speaking of this, Qin Yuanzheng's thoughts began to wander.","Qiao Lanshu was not producing enough breast milk. The doctor had said it would gradually increase after a while and advised him to give her massages when he had the time to help clear the ducts.","He had not dared to act rashly these past few days because Auntie Shi was in the next room with the baby.","But after all these days, Qiao Lanshu's milk supply was still very low, not even enough to feed one baby.","What was going on? Did she really need a massage to clear things up?","As Uncle Huang walked into the house and inspected the kang, he said, \"You are going to milk the sheep, right? Goat milk is good. It is nutritious for the baby. The powdered milk you buy nowadays might not be as nutritious, and some children do not even like to drink it.\"","Uncle Huang held the traditional mindset of the older generation: no powdered milk could compare to human breast milk or the milk of cows and goats.","It was better for little babies to drink some goat milk.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded silently.","He was no longer just a husband; he was now a father, and he felt the burden on his shoulders grow heavier.","Uncle Huang inspected the kangs in both rooms and told Qin Yuanzheng, \"These bricks are still good and can be reused, but we need to get a few bags of yellow mud. I will also rebuild the flue for you.\"","He estimated for a moment before adding, \"We will build one today, and I will come back for the other one tomorrow.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"Alright, I will have someone bring the yellow mud over.\"","There was mud at the construction site. When Qin Yuanzheng first set his sights on this small courtyard, he had already started finding ways to stockpile bricks, stones, wood, and yellow mud.","Now, he just needed to have someone transport it from the military base.","Two engineers helped him tidy up the yard, dividing it into left and right sections with a stone-paved path down the middle for walking.","Vegetables could be planted in the dirt on both sides.","The enclosing walls had, of course, been rebuilt. Along the base of the walls, they could plant creeping vines, like grapes.","An engineer in the yard asked him, \"Brigade Commander, didn't you say you wanted to plant apple trees? Where are we getting the saplings?\"","Qin Yuanzheng replied, \"We will go to the South Suburb Forestry Farm and ask Zhao Jiannong for them. I have already spoken to him. We will get one apple tree sapling and one persimmon tree sapling.\"","He paused and looked around the yard. He actually wanted to plant a jujube tree too, but the yard was not very big, and planting too many trees would take up too much space.","He remained silent for a moment before saying, \"Let us just take these two for now. I will think about the others later.\"","Having a courtyard was a good thing, but it was a bit small.","Qin Yuanzheng actually wanted a large courtyard.","However, there were no large private courtyards available here at the moment. All the large courtyards were shared compounds, with two or three families living together.","Qin Yuanzheng did not want to live in a shared compound.","After making arrangements in the yard, Qin Yuanzheng went back inside to help Uncle Huang build the kang. As he helped, he said, \"Uncle Huang, there is still some space in the backyard. Could you help me build a washroom there?\"","This house had both a front and back yard.","The front yard was already designated for a vegetable patch, tying up the sheep, and raising chickens, leaving no extra space.","So, it had to be in the backyard.","Qiao Lanshu loved to be clean and bathed often, so a dedicated washroom had to be built.","Uncle Huang nodded. \"Sure, that is simple. Pick a spot, and I will head over there once I finish building the kang.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was busy with this for several days and had no time to concern himself with the affairs of his cousin, Yang Wenyan.","As a result, his cousin's wife, Deng Xiaozhen, came over again one day.","She arrived at Qiao Lanshu's house, sat on the sofa in the living room, and complained to Qiao Lanshu and Auntie Shi, \"They want to adopt a child, but Yang Wenyan disagreed. So they came to my factory and insisted that I agree to it. I took a leave of absence today; I didn't dare go to work.\"","Deng Xiaozhen worked at a textile factory, a fact known to both her maiden family and her in-laws.","Yang Wenyan hid at the factory all day working and would not even come home for lunch.","Mother Yang felt they could not just keep stalling like this. Coupled with the fact that his Eldest Aunt kept speaking ill of Deng Xiaozhen in front of Mother Yang, they went straight to the textile factory early that morning.","Qiao Lanshu really had not expected that someone with Deng Xiaozhen's fiery, unyielding temper would end up at a disadvantage in this matter.","Sitting on the kang with her baby in her arms, she opened the bedroom door and said to Deng Xiaozhen, who was sitting on the living room sofa, \"Cousin, things cannot go on like this. If you keep hiding, they will only push harder.\"","Deng Xiaozhen smiled bitterly. \"Even Yang Wenyan is at a loss, so I have even less of an idea of what to do.\"","The main issue was that not having a child was her sore spot. She felt in the wrong and guilty about it, so she did not dare clash head-on with her mother-in-law.","Auntie Shi, who was cooking in the kitchen, chimed in, \"Oh my, what a disaster this will be if it continues. They have already been here for several days. If this drags on, you won't be able to outlast them.\"","Qiao Lanshu added, \"They are staying at your house, eating and drinking without a worry, and they don't have to pay for lodging. Doesn't that mean they can stay as long as they want? Cousin, I think you should first make them go back to the village, and then you can go find a highly skilled doctor to get checked out, and strive to have a big, chubby boy this year.\"","Deng Xiaozhen was speechless.","She sighed, \"But they refuse to leave. What should we do?\"","Qiao Lanshu carried the baby over and whispered, \"The travel letters of introduction they brought might not be valid for this long. Why don't you just go to the police station and report them for staying illegally? While your cousin is at the factory, hurry up and have the police send them away.\"","Qiao Lanshu continued in a low voice, \"Besides, we all know Deputy Bureau Chief Li at the police station. If you feel awkward going to him, I can have Brother Zheng go. How about that?\"","Deng Xiaozhen thought about it and nodded. \"Alright, let us do that first.\"","She had actually been considering divorcing Yang Wenyan.","But for one thing, she and Yang Wenyan had been together for many years and truly shared a deep bond.","For another, she just could not resign herself to it.","Deng Xiaozhen stood up and said, \"I will go to the police station right now!\"","Not long after Deng Xiaozhen left, Yang Wenyan came rushing over to their door. After hearing what Qiao Lanshu had to say, Yang Wenyan changed his route and hurriedly sprinted toward the police station.","Meanwhile, Deng Xiaozhen had already gone to the public security bureau to report her mother-in-law and the others for overstaying illegally.","Then, two officers from the bureau followed Deng Xiaozhen home and forcefully inspected the introduction letters of Mother Yang and the rest.","The introduction letter issued by the production brigade was only valid for a total of three days.","However, they had already been staying in the city for six days.","The public security officers strictly ordered them to return to the countryside immediately, warning that they would be arrested otherwise.","Deng Xiaozhen didn't go back inside; she hid outside. It just so happened that Yang Wenyan was also not at home.","Mother Yang and the others were only bullies at home, only daring to vent their anger on their daughter-in-law. Now, facing the public security officers, they didn't even dare to speak loudly.","She had to explain to the officers, Comrade officers, can we leave tomorrow? My son is the director of the food factory. He went to work and hasn't come back yet. I have to wait for him to return to let him know. We can't just leave without saying goodbye, right? What do you say?","The officers exchanged a glance and could only nod. Alright, but you must leave tomorrow, understand?","Mother Yang nodded hastily. Yes, yes, we will leave first thing tomorrow morning.","After the officers left and the door was closed, Mother Yang and Eldest Aunt looked at each other in dismay. Mother Yang said, No, we have to hurry up and leave tomorrow. What if we get arrested and sent to a labor camp?","Eldest Aunt, still holding her grandson, said unwillingly, We can leave, but we're leaving the child to them. I've already brought the child all the way here anyway. How can I take him back?","Mother Yang frowned, somewhat hesitant. But Wenyan hasn't agreed yet.","Eldest Aunt replied, I think he agrees; it's just that Deng Xiaozhen who disagrees. Once we leave and leave the child here, could Wenyan really ignore him? Don't you know your own son's character? He will definitely take care of the child.","While the two of them discussed this, they didn't even bother to ask the opinion of the son and daughter-in-law standing right next to them.","The daughter-in-law listened from the side and nudged her husband with her elbow.","Her husband couldn't help but speak up, Mom, since my cousin doesn't want the child, how about we take the child back first and talk about it later?","Eldest Aunt's face instantly darkened, and she said angrily, Of course not! When the child gets older, Wenyan will want him even less. It's better to take this opportunity to leave the child with him and finalize the adoption. Don't be sad, either. This is for your son to have a good life. What is there for you to be unhappy about?","They said they would do it, and they actually did. Early the next morning, before dawn, they left the child in the house, and the four of them grabbed their bags and headed out.","Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen hadn't returned the night before. Knowing they were leaving today, the couple had deliberately avoided them.","The couple had stayed at the guest house right across from their own home.","Deng Xiaozhen couldn't sleep the entire night. She kept getting up from time to time to stand by the window and check if they had left yet.","Seeing this, Yang Wenyan said, Don't worry. Even if they are going to leave, they have to wait until dawn. Otherwise, it's too cold in the early morning, and the child wouldn't be able to bear it.","Deng Xiaozhen sneered, With your mother's and your Eldest Aunt's character, do you really expect them to be that kind-hearted? They even dared to make a scene at my workplace. Would they leave so obediently?","Deng Xiaozhen continued, adding, They will definitely cause more trouble!","By then, it was already 5:30 in the morning. The sky was still dark, and Deng Xiaozhen was just about to go back to bed to rest for a while.","Suddenly, she caught sight of four people walking out of the courtyard gate opposite them.","Wasn't it exactly her mother-in-law, his Eldest Aunt, and his cousin and cousin-in-law?","Deng Xiaozhen pressed her face against the glass and said in surprise, Wow, they really are coming out right now.","She continued, frowning slightly, That's strange. Where is the child? Why aren't they carrying the child?","Upon hearing this, Yang Wenyan immediately got up as well. Putting on his coat, he said, Could they have strapped the child to their backs?"]},{"number":179,"title":"Chapter 179: Fine, I'll raise the child.","paragraphs":["It was just barely dawn, and most people in the streets hadn’t even gotten out of bed yet.","Those who were up were busy making breakfast at home or cleaning the house, so the streets were quiet and nearly empty.","On the entire street, only Yang Wenyan’s aunt, his mother, and his cousin and his cousin’s wife could be seen—just four people in total.","As tough as they acted in front of Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen, they were practically quails in front of the public security officers.","The officers had only said a few words to them, and yet, early this morning before dawn, they had already packed their bags and were heading back to the countryside.","Even though they knew perfectly well that Deng Xiaozhen and Yang Wenyan were deliberately avoiding them, they didn’t dare take the time to cause trouble at the factory.","But leaving so quickly made Deng Xiaozhen’s impression of her mother-in-law even worse.","In the first few years after marrying Yang Wenyan, every time she went back to his hometown, she tried her best to be a gentle and obedient daughter-in-law, putting up with her mother-in-law’s behavior.","But after all these years, she had finally seen the truth.","She would never be able to get along peacefully with this mother-in-law. The best thing was to avoid seeing her altogether—otherwise, one day, a fight was bound to break out.","And then she’d be labeled unfilial on top of everything else—that was a disgrace she couldn’t afford.","Yang Wenyan looked at his mother and aunt, scanning left and right, his brows furrowed tight: “Where’s the child? Where did the child go?”","Deng Xiaozhen looked carefully too. Soon, her face darkened as she said, “Come on, let’s hurry back home and check. If they left the kid at our place, what are we supposed to do?”","Yang Wenyan: “...”","Yang Wenyan said grimly, “No way, right? Leaving a child alone at home—aren’t they worried something might happen?”","Deng Xiaozhen laughed coldly, “Once they get to the station, they’ll find someone to send word to us at the factory. By the time we rush home, they’ll already be on the bus and gone. Don’t you see? They’re leaving the kid for us to take care of!”","As she spoke, she hurriedly put on her shoes and coat, urging Yang Wenyan, “Quick, let’s go.","If we don’t get back in time, it’ll be too late.”","Yang Wenyan looked again at the four figures on the road. He noticed that his cousin’s wife kept looking back, glancing repeatedly in the direction of his house.","Yang Wenyan had a bad feeling.","It seemed his wife might be right—the child could very well be left at his home.","Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen rushed out of the guesthouse and ran across the street toward the compound.","Deng Xiaozhen ignored her mother-in-law and the others entirely, speeding up and sprinting home on her own.","The four of them—Mother Yang and the rest—saw the couple. Mother Yang’s sister immediately shouted, “Hey! So you were hiding from us, huh? Why aren’t you hiding anymore?”","Yang Wenyan stopped, panting, and said, “Mom, are you... are you heading back to the countryside?”","Mother Yang, seeing her own son avoid her and only show up now, was furious. She walked up to him, raised her hand, and slapped him hard on the back several times, scolding, “Your mother came all this way to see you, and you’ve been hiding from me for days! You unfilial son—you’ll drive me to an early grave!”","Yang Wenyan explained, “Mom, I’m not deliberately avoiding you. Work at the factory has been hectic—I’ve had to put in overtime every day. I really didn’t mean to stay away. Besides, didn’t I buy flour and vegetables for the house? You all ate well enough these past few days, didn’t you?”","The food was indeed very good. And precisely because the lodging was comfortable and the meals plentiful, and everything in the city seemed so pleasant, his aunt was dead set on leaving the child behind.","If she didn’t have her grandson formally adopted by Yang Wenyan, what excuse would she and her son and grandchildren have to come to the city and enjoy its benefits in the future?","She thought that if her son and grandsons ever wanted to find jobs in the city, they could turn to Yang Wenyan for help.","Since Yang Wenyan would have adopted her own grandson as his son, it would only be right for him to arrange jobs for his cousin’s brothers, wouldn’t it?","Mother Yang, on the other hand, hadn’t thought that far. She was just fixated on the fact that Yang Wenyan refused to divorce and had no son. In her mind, if he went back to the village without a son, people would mock him—and her as his mother would lose face in front of the neighbors too.","She snorted and said, “Enough, don’t give me that. You think I don’t know what’s going on in your head?”","Then she added, “I left the child at your place. Since you’re back now, we don’t need to send anyone to the factory to deliver a message. You take good care of him. He’s less than a year old—he doesn’t know anything yet. Raise him, and he’ll only know you as his father. Treat him like your own, and he’ll support you in your old age...”","Yang Wenyan glanced at his aunt standing behind his mother, as well as his cousin and his cousin’s wife, and thought to himself, That’s far from certain.","It wasn’t just that he didn’t want to adopt a child at all—even if he ever decided to, he would never adopt one from relatives like these.","Don’t think he didn’t know what his aunt was scheming.","If he took in this child, he’d be saddled with supporting his aunt’s entire family from then on.","If his aunt needed money, she’d come to borrow it—should he lend it or not?","If her children needed schooling or work and asked for his help, should he help or refuse?","He was over thirty now, had worked at the factory for years, and had seen all kinds of people.","Mother Yang trusted her sister because she was her own blood, so she didn’t think deeper about it.","Besides, in her view, since her sister had ‘given’ Yang Wenyan a son, it wasn’t a big deal for him to lend a hand now and then.","Yang Wenyan cut her off, “Mom, stop it. This isn’t right. I’ll go get the child first. Wait for me.”","His aunt immediately said, “No need—the child is yours now. Just take care of him. We’re in a hurry to catch our bus, so we can’t wait for you.”","With that, she tugged at Mother Yang, urging her to leave.","Just then, Deng Xiaozhen came bustling out of the house, carrying the child in her arms.","She didn’t say a word to them. As soon as she came out, she called loudly to Yang Wenyan, “Yang Wenyan! Come here, quick. We’re going to the Women’s Federation office.”","Saying this, she started walking toward the street with the child. His aunt’s heart suddenly sank with a bad feeling. She rushed after her, “Hey! Wait! What are you doing taking my grandson to the Women’s Federation office?”","Deng Xiaozhen laughed coldly, “I’m handing the child over to the Women’s Federation, of course. You abandoned a young child—gave birth but won’t raise him. I can’t do anything to you, but do you think the Women’s Federation will be helpless? When they bring the child to your village, let’s see who ends up disgraced.”","His aunt immediately laughed, “Abandoned? This isn’t abandonment. His name has already been added under Yang Wenyan’s in the family genealogy. If anyone’s abandoning him, it’s Yang Wenyan!”","Deng Xiaozhen was shocked, “What did you say? You even changed the genealogy without telling us?”","Yang Wenyan’s face darkened as he stared at his mother, “Mom! How could you change the genealogy? Why didn’t you ask me first?”","Mother Yang looked at her sister-in-law with confusion: \"When did the family register get changed? That hasn’t happened.\"","Her sister-in-law quickly said, \"Oh, of course the family register hasn’t been changed yet, but if the women’s federation folks really show up, changing the register is just a few strokes of the pen, isn’t it? Sis, you can’t let your daughter-in-law boss you around like this, can you?\"","Mother Yang caught on instantly and glared fiercely at Deng Xiaozhen: \"Go ahead, keep stirring up trouble! Keep it up, and we’ll go back and change the family register!\"","Deng Xiaozhen wasn’t intimidated. Holding the child, she said with a smile, \"Fine, you’re all forcing me like this, huh? Alright then, we’ll just adopt this child.\"","Yang Wenyi: \"??\"","Yang Wenyi stared at Deng Xiaozhen in shock, then said anxiously, \"Wait, honey, what are you doing?\"","Deng Xiaozhen, holding the baby with a smile, said to Yang Wenyi,","\"We both have to work, and there’s no one to watch the child, so we’ll just let him lie at home. If he’s hungry, thirsty, or crying, we won’t bother. We’ll check on him when we get back from work. Surely this child is tough and will survive;","Sure, there are plenty of kidnappers in the city who steal kids, but this one has good luck, so he probably won’t get snatched. And cars sometimes drive through and hit people, but this kid—he’s lucky, so he probably won’t get run over, right?","Oh, and in the winter, the snow is so deep. I’ve heard stories of kids falling into ditches and freezing to death at night. But this child, I reckon he’ll be fine—he’s lucky, don’t you think?\"","As she spoke, Deng Xiaozhen got more worked up: \"And there’s a river not far from us. I heard someone drowned there not long ago. Apparently, kids drowning is pretty common—a few every summer, isn’t that normal...\"","Her sister-in-law couldn’t stand it anymore and shouted, \"What nonsense are you spouting? You—dare you treat this child that way!\"","As soon as she finished, the child’s biological parents, Yang Wenyi’s male cousin and his wife, couldn’t hold back any longer.","The couple hurried over and snatched the child back.","The male cousin’s wife’s eyes were already red, on the verge of tears.","The male cousin scowled at his mother: \"Mom, if they don’t want to take in the child through adoption, then so be it. Why are you forcing them? This is my flesh and blood. Would you be happy if he later drowns or gets hit by a car?\"","Deng Xiaozhen watched them coldly.","They’d stayed at their place freeloading for days, and this male cousin hadn’t said a word. Now that she hinted at harming the child, the biological father finally panicked.","Deng Xiaozhen crossed her arms and sneered, \"What are you saying? If your child comes with me, he’ll be lucky! Drowning, getting hit by a car—none of that will happen, don’t you worry!\"","Then she added, \"At worst, when we’re at work, we’ll leave him alone at home. He might go hungry or cold, but that’s nothing serious—he won’t die from it, right, Auntie?\"","Her sister-in-law pointed at Deng Xiaozhen, furious: \"You venomous woman, how can you be so cruel? You deserve to die without an heir!\"","Deng Xiaozhen’s face darkened at that. She said coldly, \"Anyway, if you insist on leaving the child here, I’ll raise him. But don’t you dare complain if something happens to him later.\"","With that, Deng Xiaozhen glared at Yang Wenyi, turned around, and stormed off angrily.","Yang Wenyi: \"...\"","Yang Wenyi scratched his head, thinking his wife’s trick was ruthless, but it worked.","Judging by his male cousin and his wife’s faces, they clearly wouldn’t leave the child here anymore.","Sure enough, they grumbled for a long time, while Mother Yang and the sister-in-law chewed Yang Wenyi out for hours.","But the male cousin and his wife, as the child’s biological parents, had originally hoped he’d enjoy a better life in the city.","Now, with the risks of accidental death, hunger, and cold, leaving a little baby alone at home all day—how pitiful would that be? Anyone would feel sorry for him, let alone his own parents.","In the end, the male cousin and his wife had a fight with the sister-in-law, and the four of them headed to the station, pretending to get along, and took the bus back.","Nearly a week had passed, and the matter was finally resolved. Yang Wenyi sighed, went home, didn’t see Deng Xiaozhen, and headed to work.","When Yang Wenyi got off work in the evening, though, he went to find Qin Yuanzheng.","Arriving at Qin Yuanzheng’s place, he said, \"I heard there’s an old traditional Chinese doctor in the provincial capital who hasn’t practiced in a long time, but his son is in the military. You know his son, right? I was wondering if you could ask him to see me and my wife.\"","Yang Wenyi had made up his mind to finally treat their infertility.","He needed to know what was wrong.","Otherwise, as the years passed without kids, it just wasn’t sustainable.","Qin Yuanzheng had only returned from the small yard next door a while ago and just finished his bath. Hearing Yang Wenyi’s request, he nodded: \"I know who you mean. No problem—I’ll go ask in person tomorrow.\"","Then Qin Yuanzheng asked, \"By the way, where’s your wife? Why didn’t she come with you?\"","Yang Wenyi smiled bitterly: \"She’s staying at Weijun’s place right now. She’s been mad at me these past few days, even talking about divorce. Ah, forget it. Remember to help me ask. I still need to go to Weijun’s place to pick her up.\"","Divorce wasn’t an option these days.","As the director of a food factory, a divorce could become a political stain.","Besides, he felt they’d have a child eventually—it was just a matter of timing.","...","After Yang Wenyi left, Qin Yuanzheng went back inside.","By this time, the baby had already drunk his goat’s milk and was put to bed by Auntie Shi, sound asleep.","It had been over ten days since Qiao Lanshu gave birth. She felt no physical discomfort, just a bit weak, and lying around all day made her back sore.","At the moment, Qiao Lanshu was sitting on the edge of the bed, reading that day’s Dragon City Daily.","To avoid disturbing the baby, she hadn’t listened to the radio for days.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng come in, she asked, \"Did my cousin just leave? Is the adoption matter settled?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded: \"It’s settled. He asked me to help find a traditional Chinese doctor.\"","Then he briefly explained what had happened at Yang Wenyi’s place.","After that, he climbed onto the kang bed and pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms, burying his face in her chest and taking a deep breath. Quietly, he said, \"Honey, you smell like milk.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\""]},{"number":180,"title":"Chapter 180: I'll Just Have a Taste","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng had recently been busy leading a team to repair the small courtyard next door. He left early and returned late during the day. Aside from worrying about Qiao Lanshu and their baby, which prompted him to come back at noon to eat and hold the child, he spent all his other time doing carpentry and earthwork in the courtyard.","Holding Qiao Lanshu in his arms, he said in a great mood, The courtyard is pretty much done. The roof, walls, floors, the perimeter wall, window glass, and so on are all finished. The yard outside is also fixed up. I laid a stone path and turned the soil on both sides. In a couple of days, let us have Auntie Shi go over and plant some vegetables. Is she not really good at growing them?","He continued, I planted an apple tree and a persimmon tree. What else do you want to plant? Just tell me, and I will go get the saplings from the South Suburb Forestry Farm. Oh, right, I also had Uncle Huang rebuild the heated brick beds in the two rooms. After letting them dry out for a day or two, I will buy some kraft paper to paste over them. Once you finish your postpartum confinement, we can move in.","Hearing Qin Yuanzheng say this, Qiao Lanshu felt a sense of longing and anticipation.","A private courtyard all to themselves, even though the house was a bit small, it had a yard, which was very rare and precious.","Nestled in Qin Yuanzheng's embrace, listening to the steady heartbeat in his chest, Qiao Lanshu thought for a moment and whispered, When I went to the Longxing Town Forestry Farm with Director Guan before, I saw a lot of flower and herbal seedlings there. Never mind the herbs, but could we plant flowers in our yard? I want to plant two peony bushes. Do you think they would survive?","In this day and age, to ensure grain production, there was not even enough space to plant fruit trees, let alone flowers. Who would be willing to plant them?","Most people filled their yards entirely with vegetables and fruit trees; very few were willing to grow flowers.","However, Qin Yuanzheng felt that in Yangcheng, where it was like spring all year round, fruit trees were planted on both sides of the streets, and flowers could be seen everywhere. Once spring arrived, the whole city was a vibrant tapestry of blooming flowers.","It was not like Longcheng, where the weather was freezing for nearly half the year, leaving everything bare, gray, and dusty.","Let alone beautiful flowers, you could not even see a blade of green grass.","The thought of Qiao Lanshu marrying him from so far away, committing to him at such a young age, and living thousands of kilometers away from her hometown made his heart ache for her.","Holding her tight, he kissed her on the lips and murmured, Peonies, right? Alright, I will look for some seedlings and plant them by the base of the wall.","Even though he secretly felt that planting flowers was quite useless, he was more than willing to offer this kind of highbrow elegance to Qiao Lanshu with his own two hands, even if a rough-around-the-edges guy like him did not quite understand it.","It did not matter if he liked it or not; as long as his wife liked it, that was enough.","Qiao Lanshu smiled happily and added, I also want to plant a peach tree. Peach blossoms are beautiful, and peaches are delicious. We can make canned peaches, peach jam, and even sun-dried peaches. Our child will definitely love eating them in the future.","Qin Yuanzheng thought for a moment and nodded. Sure, let us plant a peach tree in the backyard. The backyard is smaller than the front yard. I built a bathing room there, and in the remaining space, I put up a simple animal shed to keep sheep, raise chickens, and such. But we can plant one next to the shed; there is enough room. When the peach tree grows up, it can even provide some shade.","Saying this, Qin Yuanzheng smiled again. Looking down at Qiao Lanshu's rosy little face, he leaned in and whispered, How about that? It is nice having our own little courtyard, is it not? You can plant whatever you want.","Qiao Lanshu reached out and pushed his face away. Zheng-ge, how many days has it been since you shaved? Don't come so close.","Qin Yuanzheng hadn't shaved for seven or eight days. He was naturally full of testosterone; not only was his body hair thick, but his beard also grew incredibly fast.","After just a few days without shaving, his face was already covered in heavy stubble.","With Qiao Lanshu's hand blocking his chin, he deliberately rubbed his prickly beard against her palm, asking as he did so, What's wrong? Are you tired of me? Now that I have a beard, I'm not as handsome anymore, am I?","Although Qin Yuanzheng was a rough and rugged man, he knew he was decent-looking.","He never used to care much about his image, but ever since marrying Qiao Lanshu, he had started paying a lot of attention to his appearance.","Because Qiao Lanshu didn't like him having a beard, he would shave every two or three days to keep his face clean and smooth.","Of course, that was except for the times he deliberately wanted to tease her. On those occasions, he would intentionally wait until after they had spent the night together to shave.","He had genuinely been too busy these past few days. After all, he was fixing up a new home for himself, his wife, and their child. He was thrilled and full of energy.","He had simply forgotten to shave. He hadn't even cut his hair in a while, and he could feel it getting a bit too long.","Qin Yuanzheng's stiff bristles pricked Qiao Lanshu's palm, making it sting a little.","She quickly pulled her hand back and looked at him with a smile, teasing, Zheng-ge, I thought you didn't care about your image. Turns out I was wrong? You care about looking good too?","Seeing her smile made Qin Yuanzheng's heart feel warm. He said in a low voice, I don't care in front of others, but I definitely care in front of you. What if you think I'm ugly and too old, and end up running off with another man?","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu nestled into his arms, giggling uncontrollably. No way, I've never minded your age.","Qin Yuanzheng pinched her beaming little face and glared at her playfully. You're definitely secretly thinking I'm an old man, aren't you?","It was actually Qin Yuanzheng himself who was self-conscious about it, which was why it was on his mind.","One moment he worried he wasn't handsome enough, and the next he worried he was too old.","Qiao Lanshu didn't care about any of that at all.","She held his face, planted a kiss on his lips, and comforted him, That's not true. If I didn't like you, I wouldn't have gotten together with you in the first place. Don't overthink it. Back then, you tried to set me up with so many men, but I didn't fall for any of them, did I? In my heart, none of them can compare to you.","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","He realized that Qiao Lanshu had become a bit mischievous lately.","She would constantly bring up the fact that he used to try and find her a boyfriend.","She brought it up from time to time, just to remind him of how foolish he had been back then.","As Qin Yuanzheng began to tug at Qiao Lanshu's clothes, he murmured, So, I guess I'm just lucky that you chose me.","As Qiao Lanshu was laughing, she suddenly realized something wasn't right.","Someone's hands were starting to knead her like dough again.","She quickly grabbed his hands, her face flushing red as she looked at him. Zheng-ge, what are you doing now?","Qin Yuanzheng leaned in close to her ear and whispered, Didn't you say you weren't producing enough milk? An'an drinks formula at night and goat's milk in the morning. Is your milk not even enough for two of his meals?","Qiao Lanshu's face instantly turned even redder. She was worried about it too; she didn't know why, but she just wasn't producing milk.","She had heard that if possible, breastfeeding was definitely the best option, as breastfed babies were less likely to get sick.","Qiao Lanshu whispered to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Auntie Shi cooks rice porridge for me every day, along with goat's milk and soy milk. She says drinking more soups and liquids makes it easier to produce milk, but my supply just hasn't been very much. I don't know what's going on.\"","Qin Yuanzheng said as his hands gently kneaded, \"Didn't the doctor say you need a massage to clear the blockages? It will come in soon. Starting tonight, I will massage you every day. It will definitely work.\"","With that, he began massaging Qiao Lanshu with a completely serious expression.","Qiao Lanshu could not help but feel that Qin Yuanzheng's technique was a bit improper, but since he was her husband, she could not be too fussy about it.","It was still better than getting a doctor to do it, which would definitely make Qiao Lanshu feel embarrassed.","Qin Yuanzheng was indeed being a little improper. After massaging for a few minutes, he suddenly stopped and stared at her chest for quite a while.","Seeing that he had stopped moving, Qiao Lanshu looked at him in confusion. \"Brother Zheng, what is it?\"","Although Qin Yuanzheng's massage technique was not very professional, it was actually quite comfortable.","Qin Yuanzheng stared deeply for a long moment before suddenly saying, \"Wife, are you curious about what this tastes like?\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","She knew Qin Yuanzheng was not being serious. His mind was always filled with strange and peculiar thoughts all day long.","She had no desire to know what it tasted like.","Qin Yuanzheng just came right out and said, \"Let me try.\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless again.","Blushing, Qiao Lanshu felt her entire body tense up slightly. Feeling shy, she reached up to cover her face.","Qin Yuanzheng had said he wanted to try.","But his attempt lasted quite a while. After a long moment, he leaned in close to Qiao Lanshu and whispered, \"It is actually sweet. No wonder An'an loves to drink it.\"","Qiao Lanshu pushed him with a red face. \"Stop messing around, I want to sleep.\"","If she did not go to sleep soon, she was afraid Qin Yuanzheng might suddenly get thirsty again, and that would not do.","She whispered, \"There is not even enough for An'an to eat. If you are thirsty, go drink some water.\"","Qin Yuanzheng could not help but laugh. He said, \"Of course I know I have to leave it for An'an.\"","At this point, he sighed again, holding Qiao Lanshu in his arms, and whispered, \"Wife, how did we suddenly end up with a child? I am not dreaming, am I?\"","Even now, Qin Yuanzheng still felt a bit dazed by it all.","Indeed, things in the world were unpredictable, and life was truly marvelous.","Just a year ago, he was being urged by all sorts of people to go on blind dates and was mocked for being infertile. He had even prepared himself for a lifetime of loneliness.","Back then, if someone had told him that in just one year, he would be married with a child and have a warm, loving family, he absolutely would not have believed it.","He held Qiao Lanshu in his arms, his heart aching for her as she was still doing her postpartum confinement and her body had not yet fully recovered.","He immediately stopped his teasing, reached out to gently pat Qiao Lanshu's back, and whispered, \"Be good and go to sleep. You do not need to worry about An'an. I will go check on him in a bit. When he wakes up in the middle of the night to drink his formula, I will go watch him too. You just sleep well.\"","Qiao Lanshu was indeed sleepy, so she closed her eyes and prepared to sleep.","She felt that Qin Yuanzheng was not only mature, steady, and caring, but also very attentive.","He probably knew that Qiao Lanshu was always thinking about An'an and was worried about leaving Auntie Shi alone to take care of the baby and do the midnight feedings, which was why she would always wake up several times during the night.","Now that Qin Yuanzheng had said this, Qiao Lanshu felt at ease and would not need to wake up in the middle of the night anymore.","Qiao Lanshu quickly fell asleep. Qin Yuanzheng tucked her in securely, turned off the room's electric light, and lit a small oil lamp, placing it on the nightstand.","Then, he filled a thermos with water and set the cup on the nightstand as well, ensuring Qiao Lanshu would have something to drink when she woke up.","After finishing these tasks, he headed to the bathroom, recalling how Qiao Lanshu had complained about his beard.","He took out his razor and meticulously shaved off all his facial hair.","Once clean-shaven, he examined himself in the mirror from different angles. Even though he was already thirty this year, his face was still quite handsome.","His features were sharp, his eyes deep-set, and his nose bridge high and straight. It was just that when he kept a straight face, his aura came off as somewhat fierce.","He smiled at his reflection. Hmm, not bad. He looked decent when he smiled.","Just then, he heard the sound of Auntie Shi mixing milk powder outside, and he immediately walked out.","Auntie Shi and An'an stayed in the guest bedroom next door. An'an was only about ten days old and needed to be fed every two or three hours.","During the day, Qiao Lanshu would feed An'an three or four times.","At night when everyone was sleeping, Auntie Shi would mix infant formula for An'an. After all, goat's milk was only fresh if it was milked in the morning.","At this time, they did not have a refrigerator at home, and the weather was gradually warming up. Fresh milk was difficult to preserve, and Auntie Shi was worried about An'an getting an upset stomach.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng approach, Auntie Shi smiled and said, Chief Qin, are you here to see An'an?","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He walked over, picked up the freshly awakened An'an, gently rocked him in his arms, and asked in a low voice, How many times a night does An'an need to drink formula?","Auntie Shi finished mixing the formula and walked over with the baby bottle, saying, The child is still small. He wakes up three or four times a night, and he has to drink every time, otherwise he will be too hungry to sleep.","Newborns were the easiest to take care of. They ate and slept, slept and ate, rarely crying or making a fuss. They just lay quietly in bed.","But starting from the second month, they would not be so easy to look after.","Fortunately, Auntie Shi had previously worked as a nanny for other military officers' families. Having raised two or three children before, she had plenty of experience and knew exactly what to do, truly helping Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu a great deal.","Qin Yuanzheng said to Auntie Shi, It is going to be hard on you these next few months, Auntie. Once this month is over, I have to go back to work. I will have to trouble you to take care of Xiao Qiao and An'an. So I was thinking of giving you a ten-yuan raise every month. I hope you take good care of the mother and child. Xiao Qiao is young and lacks life experience, so Auntie, please guide her when the time comes.","Auntie Shi's original salary was fifty yuan, which was already quite high.","After all, the regular workers in the factories currently only made forty yuan.","Her salary was already ten yuan higher than those official workers.","With Qin Yuanzheng adding another ten yuan, that would make it sixty yuan.","A salary of sixty yuan was at the level of a factory supervisor!","Auntie Shi immediately said, Chief, there is no need, no need at all. Fifty yuan is more than enough, you do not need to raise it. Rest assured, I will definitely take good care of the mother and child. I guarantee I will raise them to be plump and healthy, so you will not have to worry about a thing!","Watching Auntie Shi feed An'an, Qin Yuanzheng said, I am giving you a raise because you deserve it. Xiao Qiao likes you a lot too, so let us just settle it at that.","Saying that, he bid farewell to Auntie Shi and returned to the room next door to rest.","The pay raise was meant to encourage Auntie Shi to take even better care of Xiao Qiao and the baby, as well as to keep her around.","These days, a good nanny was hard to find.","Auntie Shi had been working at his house for over a month now, and after observing her carefully, he was very satisfied.","Qiao Lanshu also mentioned that Auntie Shi was great, she had a reliable character, excellent cooking skills, and plenty of experience with children.","What more was there to say?","He would increase her pay to keep her. He planned to have Auntie Shi help raise the child until they were three years old.","...","The night passed quietly. Early the next morning, Qin Yuanzheng headed out bright and early once again.","This time, however, he did not go to the small courtyard next door. Instead, he made arrangements for someone to go to the South Suburb Tree Farm to find Zhao Jiannong and request two peony seedlings along with a peach tree sapling.","He instructed them to bring the saplings back and plant them in the yard, planning to inspect their work when he returned that evening.","Afterward, he left for the day. He had to accompany Yang Wenyan and his wife, driving them to a neighboring city to see an old traditional Chinese medicine doctor.","After all, Yang Wenyan and his wife had been unable to conceive for a long time. They needed some medical conditioning; things simply could not go on like this."]},{"number":181,"title":"Chapter 181: Really Pregnant","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng had reached out in advance to the son of the old traditional Chinese medicine doctor, who was also in the military region.","Although they weren't in the same unit, they were in the same military region and knew each other.","After a brief conversation, the other party naturally wouldn't refuse to help.","However, the old gentleman lived in the neighboring city, which wasn't exactly close to Longcheng. It would take a two-hour drive to get there.","Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen both took time off work and set out with Qin Yuanzheng.","Deng Xiaozhen had obviously gotten into an argument with Yang Wenyan; the two of them didn't speak a word to each other the whole way.","When Yang Wenyan tried to talk to her, she ignored him completely.","Feeling awkward, Yang Wenyan sat in the car sighing continuously.","Qin Yuanzheng had no intention of interfering in their marital issues, so he didn't say much during the drive either.","Yang Wenyan asked, \"I heard this old gentleman is in his seventies and hasn't seen patients in a long time. I wonder if he can really help us regulate our bodies.\"","He thought to himself that if it weren't officially forbidden, he would have loved to go into the mountains to pray to the Child-Giving Guanyin.","Qin Yuanzheng replied, \"Whether it works or not, it's good to have him take a look. After all, he's a veteran doctor with plenty of experience. He can at least give you some advice.\"","Yang Wenyan nodded. He turned to look at Deng Xiaozhen again and asked ingratiatingly, \"Xiaozhen, do you want some water?\"","With that, he offered her his thermos.","Deng Xiaozhen rolled her eyes at him and didn't take it. \"Drink it yourself if you want it.\"","So annoying.","Deng Xiaozhen was in a terrible mood right now.","On one hand, she felt a sense of inferiority for not being able to have a child all this time, feeling that she had let Yang Wenyan down. After all, he was under a lot of pressure too.","On the other hand, she felt she wasn't at fault. Having a child wasn't a one-person job; it takes two to tango.","However, after years of marriage, reaching their current situation was indeed a problem.","If they still didn't have a child in the next two or three years, they might actually end up getting a divorce.","Melancholy, frustration, and conflicted feelings weighed heavily on her, making her so restless that she didn't want to talk to Yang Wenyan at all.","So, she simply leaned against the car window and stared outside, finding it irritating to even glance at him.","Yang Wenyan: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng drove on, and around ten o'clock in the morning, he brought them to the gate of the old gentleman's courtyard.","Dressed in his military uniform, Qin Yuanzheng stepped forward to knock on the door.","Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen carried gifts in their hands, including eggs, canned goods, biscuits, and brown sugar.","After all, this was an introduction through a comrade in the military. With Qin Yuanzheng bringing them personally, the old doctor was purely doing them a favor out of goodwill.","He definitely wouldn't charge a fee, so Yang Wenyan had bought plenty of gifts instead.","No matter what, they had to be thorough with their etiquette; the rest was up to fate.","The old doctor's son had already informed his family in advance. So, as soon as they arrived, they were greeted with a smile and led inside: \"You must be Brigade Commander Qin from the 21st Regiment, right? Come on in, the old man is playing chess in the courtyard.\"","Speaking of which, Qin Yuanzheng had already been promoted to Brigade Commander, but he remained with the 21st Regiment because the construction project at the mining area wasn't finished yet. He figured he would be transferred out of the mining area once the project was completed in the latter half of the year.","However, Commander Li had already mentioned that the transfer would stay within the same military region. No matter where he was moved, he would still be under Commander Li, so Qin Yuanzheng didn't pay the transfer much mind.","As long as it wasn't a cross-region transfer, it was fine. Otherwise, he would have to move, and all the painstaking effort he put into renovating his little courtyard would have been for nothing.","The old doctor was in the courtyard playing chess with a good friend. Hearing that Qin Yuanzheng had brought the patients, he led the three of them into the house to sit down and had someone brew tea for them.","After exchanging pleasantries, the old doctor said to Yang Wenyan and his wife, \"Let me check your pulses first.\"","The old gentleman usually started by observing the patient's complexion, eyes, tongue coating, and so on. Following that, he liked to take their pulse, as a pulse reading could reveal quite a lot.","Yang Wenyan sat down nervously and let the old doctor take his pulse.","The old man checked his pulse for quite a while with a serious expression, which frightened Yang Wenyan considerably.","But he didn't dare to speak, afraid of interrupting the old doctor's train of thought.","Stroking his beard, the old doctor withdrew his hand, glanced at Yang Wenyan, and said, \"You have a bit of a kidney deficiency.\"","Yang Wenyan: \"...\"","Without looking at Yang Wenyan's face, which had turned the color of pig liver, the old doctor added, \"You can get up now. Let your wife come over.\"","Blushing, Yang Wenyan gave his seat to Deng Xiaozhen.","Deng Xiaozhen's face was also full of tension. She hoped the old doctor wouldn't diagnose her with a kidney deficiency too, as that would be incredibly embarrassing.","Come to think of it, was there a connection between kidney deficiency and infertility?","Could her inability to have a child all these years be because of Yang Wenyan's kidney deficiency?","As the old doctor took Deng Xiaozhen's pulse, he stroked his beard. After a long moment, his hand paused. He looked at Deng Xiaozhen, then at Yang Wenyan, and suddenly asked, \"What exactly did you come to seek medical help for today?\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng found it somewhat amusing. He looked at Yang Wenyan's flushed face and said with a smile, \"Old sir, they are here to seek help for having a child. They've been dealing with infertility for years and wanted to see how to regulate their bodies.\"","As he spoke, he deliberately added, \"However, regarding the kidney deficiency, please help treat that as well. That's not a minor issue either.\"","Yang Wenyan's vision nearly went black. He glared at Qin Yuanzheng, thinking to himself that this cousin of his was truly merciless.","At a time like this, he still had to deliberately make fun of him.","The old doctor inhaled sharply. He looked at Deng Xiaozhen and said, \"Aren't you already pregnant? Did you not know?\"","Everyone: \"???\"","At this, let alone Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen, even Qin Yuanzheng was shocked.","Deng Xiaozhen's hands trembled with excitement. She stammered nervously, \"R-really? I'm pregnant? Doctor, shouldn't you check my pulse again?\"","Beside her, Yang Wenyan was completely stunned. He stood there, looking back and forth between Deng Xiaozhen, the doctor, and Qin Yuanzheng.","His lips parted again and again, but he couldn't manage to utter a single word for the longest time.","An immense wave of joy washed over him, leaving him completely frozen. He even thought he was having auditory hallucinations.","Excitement, pleasant surprise, bewilderment, and sheer disbelief.","Qin Yuanzheng was equally shocked. He stood there, looking at the doctor. \"Sir, are you sure there is no mistake? My cousin-in-law is pregnant?\"","The old gentleman nodded. He said to the three of them, \"I'd estimate it's been almost two months. It's still early, so you must rest well to protect the fetus. Your body is deficient in both qi and blood, so it wasn't easy for you to conceive this child. You need to take some medicine to stabilize the pregnancy. I'll write you a prescription, and you can take it to a pharmacy to get it filled when you get back.\"","With that, ignoring their shocked and disbelieving expressions, the old doctor simply picked up a blank sheet of paper, dipped his brush in ink, and began writing the prescription.","The calmest person in the room was the old gentleman himself.","After all, everyone else had long been stunned silly.","Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen looked at each other. Both of their faces were etched with shock, and after the shock passed, their minds went completely blank.","Qin Yuanzheng, however, reacted quickly. He looked at Yang Wenyan with a smile, reached out to pat him on the shoulder, and said, \"Congratulations, Cousin and Cousin-in-law. Your wish has finally come true.\"","Yang Wenyan still couldn't quite believe it, but the old doctor had already written the prescription, and he didn't dare question the elderly man any further.","The couple looked at each other, both seeing the same skepticism in each other's eyes.","Standing before the old doctor, they listened carefully and attentively to his instructions on how to protect the pregnancy, how to take the medicine, and so on.","Finally, the old doctor also advised them to go to a hospital for a proper prenatal check-up.","The couple agreed to everything, one by one, and then followed Qin Yuanzheng out of the courtyard.","Seeing the couple looking so distracted, Qin Yuanzheng smiled and said, \"Cousin, Cousin-in-law, what's wrong with you two? Are you dumbstruck with joy?\"","Yang Wenyan stammered, \"I, I... I mean, honey, are you really pregnant?\"","As he spoke, he quickly reached out to support Deng Xiaozhen, his eyes fixed on her stomach.","Deng Xiaozhen's eyes suddenly grew red. She reached out to touch her belly and whispered, \"I don't know either...\"","Deng Xiaozhen had suffered from malnutrition as a child, and after she started working, she often went hungry, so her health had never been very good.","Because of this, her menstrual cycle was irregular. Sometimes it came once every two or three months, and sometimes once every four or five months.","She had no way of using that to tell if she was pregnant.","Besides, she didn't have any pregnancy symptoms at all.","Looking at the couple's bewildered expressions, Qin Yuanzheng knew they were probably just overwhelmed with excitement.","He made a prompt decision and said, \"Let's go. We're heading back to Longcheng to get you checked out at the military hospital.\""]},{"number":182,"title":"Chapter 182: Go See the New Home","paragraphs":["Among the three of them, Qin Yuanzheng was the only one who still managed to remain rational and calm.","Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen were both somewhat stunned. Long after getting into the car, they were still discussing the old gentleman's medical skills. Is that doctor's pulse reading really that accurate? Am I really pregnant?","Yang Wenyan was in a very complicated state of mind. He was actually thrilled and incredibly excited.","However, he forced his emotions down, afraid that if he celebrated too early, a trip to the hospital might prove it was all a misunderstanding and his wife wasn't actually pregnant.","He comforted Deng Xiaozhen, saying, Of course the old doctor's pulse reading is accurate. He is very famous, didn't you know? He used to be the director of our provincial traditional Chinese medicine hospital. He just went back home to retire and doesn't practice publicly anymore.","Although traditional Chinese medicine was currently being overshadowed by Western medicine, ordinary people still placed a lot of trust in it. Things passed down from their ancestors certainly couldn't be wrong.","He added, Besides, observation, auscultation, inquiry, and pulse-taking are just the basic skills of these doctors. Taking a pulse is the simplest part; he definitely wouldn't make a mistake.","Yang Wenyan rambled on for a long time. In truth, his mind was completely blank, and he could not even remember what he had just said.","Deng Xiaozhen was not really listening to him either. They were each talking to themselves, and what the other person said did not matter at all.","What mattered was knowing the other person was sitting right beside them, and being able to hear each other's voices. That was enough.","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent the entire way, just listening to the couple talk. He could tell that this pregnancy was indeed incredibly important to Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen.","He could not help but think back to when Xiao Qiao got pregnant. He had been terrified back then too, and his very first reaction was utter disbelief.","He simply did not believe that Qiao Lanshu was pregnant. At first, he suspected the doctor had made a mistake, and later, he worried that Qiao Lanshu might have fallen ill.","Thinking of this now, he found it quite amusing.","Two hours later, Qin Yuanzheng parked the car at the main entrance of the Longcheng Military Region Hospital.","He went inside with Yang Wenyan and Deng Xiaozhen.","By the time Deng Xiaozhen came out from her examination, an hour had already passed.","She really was pregnant. Just as the old gentleman had said, she was almost two months along.","Because her menstrual cycle had always been irregular, she had not paid much attention to it even after missing two months.","She never expected that she had actually conceived.","Deng Xiaozhen and Yang Wenyan wept tears of joy, holding each other and crying for quite a while.","Qin Yuanzheng could not stand their overly affectionate display, so he said to Yang Wenyan, Cousin, I will head back first then.","He had not seen his wife and child for most of the day, and he missed them dearly.","Right now, Yang Wenyan also just wanted to take his wife home so she could get some proper rest. The couple needed to properly digest this wonderful news.","He quickly nodded. Alright, drive safely. Your sister-in-law and I are going to head back too. Since this happened so suddenly today, we will not be going to the factory.","Besides, he was in no mood to work right now anyway.","After leaving the hospital, Qin Yuanzheng went straight home.","It was already past three in the afternoon. The round trip had taken quite a bit of time, and he suddenly realized he had not even eaten lunch yet.","When he arrived home, the house was completely quiet. He looked around the living room and saw that Auntie Shi was not there. Peeking into the bedroom, he saw Qiao Lanshu sitting up in bed, leaning against the headboard, with their little one sleeping soundly beside her.","Qiao Lanshu was holding a high school textbook, reading.","Hearing the noise, she looked up, saw Qin Yuanzheng, and smiled. Brother Zheng, you are back?","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He walked over, cupped Qiao Lanshu's face to give her a kiss first, then looked at the sleeping baby and asked in a low voice, Where is Auntie Shi?","Qiao Lanshu replied, Auntie Shi said there was nothing much to do this afternoon, so she went to the yard next door to plant some vegetables.","Auntie Shi did not have the habit of taking afternoon naps. After eating lunch and washing the dishes, seeing the baby was asleep, she did not rest for long before deciding to go next door to garden.","Qiao Lanshu had also wanted to go over to the little yard next door to take a look. However, she had not yet finished her postpartum confinement period. The weather here was cold and the wind was strong, so she figured it was best not to go out and catch a chill.","Qin Yuanzheng had already taken off his outerwear and changed into comfortable home clothes. He climbed onto the heated bed and lay down beside Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu asked, Are you going to sleep? Are you not going out?","Qin Yuanzheng stretched out an arm, pulled Qiao Lanshu into his embrace, and said, Since Auntie Shi is not home, I will not go out. I need to stay and keep you two company.","He did not feel comfortable leaving Qiao Lanshu, who was still in confinement, alone at home with their newborn baby.","Conveniently, taking advantage of Auntie Shi's absence, he held Qiao Lanshu and shared some intimate moments with her for a while. Afterward, he told her about Deng Xiaozhen's pregnancy.","Qiao Lanshu was pleasantly surprised. Really? Then cousin and sister-in-law have finally seen the light at the end of the tunnel and gotten their wish.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. He was genuinely happy for his cousin from the bottom of his heart.","Days passed by, and Qiao Lanshu finally finished her confinement period.","The weather on this day was bright and sunny. Qiao Lanshu had been cooped up in the house for over a month without stepping outside. Even someone like her, who did not particularly enjoy going out, felt like she was going crazy from being shut in.","It just so happened that the little yard next door in the military housing complex had already been tidied up by Qin Yuanzheng.","Taking advantage of the beautiful weather, Qin Yuanzheng carried the baby, held Qiao Lanshu's hand, and brought Auntie Shi along to go see their new place.","Auntie Shi was even more excited than the couple. Wearing an apron, oversleeves, and a straw hat to block the sun, she said to Qiao Lanshu, Xiao Qiao, let me tell you, the vegetables in the yard have already sprouted and grown quite tall. I water them twice a day, so they grow incredibly fast. It will not be long before you can eat the vegetables I grew.","Back when Auntie Shi lived in the countryside, she used to fill her private plot with all kinds of melons, fruits, and vegetables.","Later, when she came to the city to work as a nanny for military officers, she had not planted any vegetables for at least three or four years.","Now that she finally had an employer with a yard, Auntie Shi was overjoyed.","She said, Ordinary folks like us just love having a yard. A yard is wonderful; you can plant so many things.","After filling the vegetable beds on both sides of the yard, she even planted a row of chives along the base of the wall. She made sure to drop a few vegetable seeds into every available crack.","After all, if you did not plant vegetables, weeds would just grow there anyway.","Outside the enclosing wall, she also planted a row of cabbage seedlings right against the base, fully embracing the principle of wasting absolutely nothing.","She lowered her voice and said to Qiao Lanshu, The people living here are all from the military. Everyone has high moral standards and no shortage of food. Even if we plant vegetables outside the wall, we do not have to worry about anyone stealing them. Back in the countryside, that would never work. The vegetables I planted in my private plot would always get stolen, and they always came to steal them at night. It was infuriating.","Qiao Lanshu rarely went to the countryside, having grown up in Yangcheng. Listening to Auntie Shi talk about this, she was reminded of the time she went to Longxing Town with Guan Wenjun.","She smiled and said, Speaking of which, I have been to a village too, over in Longxing Town.","As she spoke, she suddenly turned to Qin Yuanzheng beside her and asked, By the way, Brother Zheng, has Director Guan still not returned?","Several months had passed. She had not seen Guan Wenjun during the Lunar New Year, and now the baby was already born, yet Guan Wenjun still had not appeared.","Given Guan Wenjun's personality, this did not make sense.","If he knew Qin Yuanzheng had become a father, he definitely would have visited the hospital.","After all, even Staff Officer Lin and Xiao Yang had come to visit, bringing along eggs and other things to help Qiao Lanshu recover her health.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"He and Si Zhemao should be back soon, probably in the next few days.\"","Qiao Lanshu was truly shocked this time. \"No way? From before the New Year until now, it's been at least five months, hasn't it?\"","No, it should be almost half a year by now.","After all, she had already given birth to her child and even finished her postpartum confinement.","That was quite a long time.","Qin Yuanzheng said, \"Two spies, that's no small matter. They also have their superiors and subordinates, as well as certain individuals who have already infiltrated government departments... The situation is not that simple. Closing the case in half a year is already considered fast.\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu thought about it. It was already 1976, and the college entrance examination would be reinstated next year.","Of course, for Guan Wenjun, the college entrance examination wasn't the focal point; the end of the revolution was his ultimate goal.","If he didn't come back soon to use his connections, transfer departments, and secure his job, it really would be too late for him.","Thinking of this, and considering that Guan Wenjun had helped her quite a bit, Qiao Lanshu asked Qin Yuanzheng, \"Then for this case, does Director Guan get credited with a meritorious service?\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. \"Yes.\"","It was precisely because there was an opportunity to earn merit that Guan Wenjun had done everything in his power to go there.","Otherwise, what had he been working so hard for these past six months?","Qiao Lanshu breathed a sigh of relief and said, \"That's good. When he comes back, he'll definitely be able to secure his job.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at Qiao Lanshu, reached out to hook his arm around her neck, pulled her into his embrace, and asked, \"You seem to care a lot about him?\"","Qiao Lanshu blushed. \"I do not.\"","Auntie Shi looked at the couple, smiled, and took the baby from Qin Yuanzheng's arms. She opened the courtyard door and went inside to water her vegetable garden.","Seeing Auntie Shi smiling, Qiao Lanshu's face turned even redder. She whispered, \"We're outside, mind your manners.\"","The smile on Qin Yuanzheng's face faded slightly, even though he knew Comrade Xiao Qiao definitely wouldn't have feelings for Guan Wenjun.","After all, Guan Wenjun couldn't compare to him in any aspect.","But seeing Qiao Lanshu care about the other man like this still made him a little unhappy.","Qiao Lanshu could tell that Qin Yuanzheng was displeased.","This man, how was his jealousy getting worse and worse?","She had thought he would become a bit more mature after becoming a father.","Smiling, Qiao Lanshu walked up to the courtyard.","She looked around and noticed that although the location of this small courtyard was a bit far from the military residential area, it was a detached single-family home, separated from the crowded communal courtyard next door by a small alley.","At this time, many courtyards were built closely together, with some even sharing a wall. A detached little courtyard like this was indeed rare.","Qin Yuanzheng smiled and said, \"Well, are you satisfied? This courtyard was empty for two months and was almost assigned to someone else. Fortunately, that family thought it was too dilapidated and didn't want it.\"","This courtyard had indeed been too run-down. Qin Yuanzheng had brought a few engineering soldiers from the unit and worked for twenty days straight to repair everything.","Even the heated brick beds in the two rooms had been completely rebuilt, and the stove in the kitchen had been reconstructed with new bricks.","It was safe to say that it was almost no different from building a brand-new house."]},{"number":183,"title":"Chapter 183: Going to the Labor Reform Farm","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng took Qiao Lanshu for a walk around the yard, and then brought her into the house.","The house had naturally been completely renovated and looked brand new.","There was a main room, with a bedroom on the left and right, and a kitchen at the back.","Next to the kitchen was the newly built shower room.","Out of the shower room was a small backyard, where a simple wooden livestock shed had been set up. Qin Yuanzheng had already brought the sheep over and tied it in the backyard.","As for the few chickens he kept at the mining area troops, he hadn't brought them back yet.","He said to Qiao Lanshu, \"I deliberately kept those hens and didn't eat them. I want to raise them in the backyard so they can lay eggs every day for you and the child to eat.\"","Now that Qin Yuanzheng had a child, he was considering more and more things.","He even knew to raise hens to save eggs for the child.","Qiao Lanshu really liked this new home. Although living in an apartment building was very comfortable, the space was still too small.","In the past, when it was just the two of them, they didn't feel it and even thought it was quite cozy.","But now that they had a child, a nanny, and some poultry to raise, living in a house with a yard was definitely more comfortable.","She walked around the front and back yards a few times, then wandered around inside the house. Liking it very much, she asked Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, when are we moving?\"","Qin Yuanzheng said, \"At the end of this month. We have to vacate the apartment by early next month.\"","After all, there were still people waiting in line to be allocated housing.","After the couple finished looking at the new house, they took a detour back. The guard at the gate handed them two letters.","The letters were sent from Yangcheng. One was from Father Qiao, and the other was from her good friend Zhong Mei.","Qiao Lanshu had been waiting for Zhong Mei's letter for a long time. Months had passed, and her child was already born, but she still hadn't received a reply from Zhong Mei.","She was actually very worried in her heart.","She had previously written to her father, asking him to give Zhong Mei some money, but she didn't know if her father had done so.","In her past life, she couldn't even protect herself, didn't receive Zhong Mei's letter, and naturally, Zhong Mei couldn't have come to Longcheng to seek refuge with her.","Back then, she didn't know how Zhong Mei was doing, whether she had followed her family's arrangements and gotten married.","Anxious, Qiao Lanshu opened Zhong Mei's letter first. The letter had two pages, both fully written.","Zhong Mei had only attended elementary school, so her handwriting wasn't very neat, and some complex characters were written crookedly.","In the letter, she first congratulated Qiao Lanshu on her pregnancy and said she wanted to be the child's godmother in the future.","Then, she proudly mentioned that she had managed to get a letter of introduction before her blind date and had already boarded a northbound train. She expected to arrive in Longcheng in about three days!","When the time came, she would go directly to the food factory in Longcheng City to find her!","Qiao Lanshu was startled. Looking at the contents of the letter, Zhong Mei had obviously sent it out before she even gave birth.","How long ago was that?","She quickly checked the dates of sending and receiving.","Sure enough, the letter was sent out ten days ago and had been delayed along the way, only reaching her hands now.","The crucial point was that no one from the food factory had come to inform her that someone was looking for her.","Qiao Lanshu had a good relationship with the uncle at the food factory's gate. If someone had really come to seek refuge with her, the factory would definitely have let her know.","Frowning, Qiao Lanshu had a bad premonition.","Seeing that her expression was wrong, Qin Yuanzheng stepped forward and asked in a low voice, \"What's wrong? Did something happen at home? Let me see the letter.\"","Qiao Lanshu handed the letter to him, her face full of worry. \"It's not my family, it's my friend. Zhong Mei, whom I mentioned to you before. She seems to have come, but there's been no news until now. I'm a bit worried. Could she have taken the wrong path? Or did she not get on the train at all?\"","Qin Yuanzheng frowned slightly and took the letter to read. The time was indeed a bit long. No matter how slow the train was, it couldn't possibly take ten days.","After all, it was the beginning of summer now. The weather was good, and there were no heavy snowfalls blocking the roads.","The trains were running normally.","Qin Yuanzheng remained silent for a moment, then said, \"Don't worry. I'll go to the food factory to ask now. I'll also check the two guesthouses in the city and the police station. Write down her information for me, and I'll have an answer by this afternoon. If she came to Longcheng, we will definitely find her.\"","Unless she hadn't made it to Longcheng, in which case they would have to send a telegram or call the train station in Yangcheng to ask.","Qiao Lanshu nodded. Then, she opened the letter sent by Father Qiao.","Knowing that she had given birth, Father Qiao asked about her health and the child's condition. He also mentioned that he had remitted one hundred yuan to her so she could buy milk powder and clothes for the baby.","Furthermore, Father Qiao stated in the letter that he had gone to Zhong Mei's house to look for her. As a result, Zhong Mei's family surprisingly said that she had been arrested and sent to a labor camp.","She was sent from the spring-like Yangcheng to a farm in the Great Northwest to open up wasteland.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Stunned, she murmured, \"What happened to Zhong Mei? Why was she suddenly sent to a labor camp?\"","Didn't she say she was coming to Longcheng to seek refuge with Qiao Lanshu?","Instead, she was sent directly to the Great Northwest for reform through labor.","Speaking of which, although the Great Northwest was very far from Yangcheng, it wasn't too far from Longcheng.","However, it would still take over ten hours by train.","Qin Yuanzheng leaned over and looked at the letter written by Father Qiao. He said with some surprise, \"Labor camp? Because of fighting and brawling?\"","Seeing this reason, Qin Yuanzheng was genuinely astonished.","He couldn't help but look at Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu had the appearance of a good, obedient girl. She had fair skin, a soft personality, and almost never spoke loudly.","Yet, her best childhood friend first talked about running away from home, then about traveling thousands of miles to Longcheng to seek refuge with her.","And now, she had even been sent to the Great Northwest for labor reform because of fighting?","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't help but say, \"This friend of yours is quite fierce, isn't she?\"","Qiao Lanshu exchanged a glance with Qin Yuanzheng, her own face full of bewilderment.","She hesitated and said, \"Zhong Mei rarely fights. I bet she was definitely framed by someone!\"","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","He felt that this was probably not a misunderstanding, nor was it a false accusation.","It was highly likely that Zhong Mei was genuinely sent to the labor farm for fighting.","Moreover, this brawl must not have been a minor incident. Either she had severely injured someone, causing a very negative impact, or the person she fought had a strong background and could easily retaliate against her, even sending her to the cold and arid Great Northwest for labor reform.","Qiao Lanshu looked at Qin Yuanzheng eagerly.","Qin Yuanzheng's heart softened, and he immediately said, \"Don't worry, I'll go look into it. There are only two labor farms in the Great Northwest, and I know where they are. I'll go ask.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and quickly added, \"Once you find out, we'll buy train tickets and go see her.\"","She really couldn't stop worrying about Zhong Mei.","She was perfectly fine, so how could she be sent to a labor camp?","Qiao Lanshu would rather she had gotten married than be sent to a labor camp.","The environment at the labor camp was incredibly harsh, with heavy farm work to be done every day. Moreover, it was a mixed bag with all sorts of people.","Qiao Lanshu was afraid that Zhong Mei would be taken advantage of and wouldn't be able to endure the bitter cold and hunger there.","Fortunately, the weather was warming up now. The Beginning of Summer had already passed, so it shouldn't be that cold over there.","When Qin Yuanzheng wanted to investigate something, he was always very quick.","By making a few calls to the military district over there to ask his comrades, or directly calling the town public security bureau and revolutionary committee where the farm was located, he could quickly find out Zhong Mei's information.","Within three days, Qin Yuanzheng had found the information.","After confirming that Zhong Mei was in the labor camp, Qiao Lanshu immediately asked Qin Yuanzheng to buy train tickets, then packed their things, ready to take the train to visit Zhong Mei.","As for the child, An'an was already two months old, and Auntie Shi was already very adept at taking care of him.","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu took Auntie Shi and the baby to Yang Wenyan's house.","They entrusted the child to Deng Xiaozhen.","After Deng Xiaozhen found out she was pregnant, she immediately resigned and stayed at home to rest and protect the fetus.","Although her pregnancy was very stable and continuing to work wouldn't actually have an impact.","But she and Yang Wenyan valued this pregnancy too much, so they preferred to earn less money and wait until the child was born.","As the factory manager, Yang Wenyan had no problem supporting his wife and child.","Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu explained their purpose to them, and Deng Xiaozhen immediately held the baby in her arms and said with a smile, \"No problem, of course there's no problem. It's a good opportunity for me to learn how to take care of a child from Auntie Shi, so I won't be in a rush after I give birth.\"","Deng Xiaozhen's mother-in-law definitely couldn't be counted on.","However, Deng Xiaozhen's mother would come to take care of her during her postpartum confinement.","But after all, the elderly woman hadn't taken care of a child in decades, and she had probably forgotten how to do it.","Qiao Lanshu was actually reluctant to leave An'an, but Zhong Mei's situation was even worse. If she didn't go see her, she really couldn't put her mind at ease.","Qin Yuanzheng naturally wanted to accompany her, so after thinking it over, they could only send the child to Yang Wenyan's place.","Qiao Lanshu said apologetically, \"We'll have to trouble you, cousin and sister-in-law, for these few days. We'll go and come back quickly, expecting to take five days, and at most no more than seven days, we will definitely be back.\"","Deng Xiaozhen had always liked children, and now that she was pregnant, she liked them even more.","She held An'an tightly and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"We are all family, Xiao Qiao, why are you being so polite? Just rest assured. Even if your cousin and I don't know how to take care of children, isn't Auntie Shi still here?\"","Auntie Shi also smiled and said, \"Xiao Qiao, don't worry, I will definitely take good care of An'an for you.\"","With them around, Qiao Lanshu was naturally relieved.","It was just that as a mother, she was a bit reluctant to leave her child.","Qin Yuanzheng said in a low voice, \"Don't worry. Since we are going out, I applied for logistics assistance. Do you remember Xiao Li, who took care of you before? The female comrade from the logistics department. During the few days we are away, she will go over to check on the child and deliver goat milk every noon and evening.\"","Qiao Lanshu was actually quite relieved. She whispered, \"Let's hurry up and go see Zhong Mei, and then come back as soon as possible.\"","If possible, Qiao Lanshu hoped to get Zhong Mei out and have her work directly at the food factory.","Because Qiao Lanshu herself had decided to resign. There was only one year left before the college entrance examination, and the child was still young.","She had saved some money during her year of work, and with Qin Yuanzheng's decent income, she was ready to quit.","She was a regular worker and didn't want to go through the normal resignation process. She wanted to give her job to Zhong Mei and let her take over her position.","This seemed to be allowed, after all, she had seen people sell their jobs before.","That is, selling one's job to someone else could fetch hundreds of yuan, and the personnel department would even stamp and sign it.","Qiao Lanshu silently calculated these things in her mind. After arranging for the child, the next day, she and Qin Yuanzheng boarded the train to the Great Northwest.","...","Meanwhile, at the Luxi Labor Camp in the Great Northwest.","Although it was called a farm, it was actually a vast expanse of wasteland connected to the mountains and forests.","Countless people were reclaiming wasteland, building roads, and constructing irrigation canals here.","They were watched by administrators who were responsible for arranging work and issuing daily tasks. The process was actually quite similar to that of a production brigade;","They also gathered every morning, were assigned tasks, and went up the mountain to work, with specific people in charge of supervising.","The difference was that these people did not earn work points; their labor was unpaid.","The labor camp uniformly provided dormitories, clothing, and meals.","If they could complete their daily labor reform tasks, they would receive normal meals, but if they failed to complete the tasks, their food rations would be deducted.","When Zhong Mei arrived here, except for a full meal on the first day, she had not been able to eat a full meal for the next few days.","Either her work delayed her eating, or she was punished for making mistakes and forbidden to eat.","Son of a bitch, after starving for so many days, she felt like she was going to starve to death.","The reason she was living so miserably was entirely because, on the second day she arrived here, a certain supervisor took a fancy to her.","The supervisor was not a labor reform prisoner; he belonged to the administrators who managed their group of prisoners.","It would have been fine if she had met a normal one, but she just had to encounter an abnormal one.","The supervisor of her team was a lecherous man in his forties, bald, pot-bellied, with very yellow teeth, and extremely ugly.","As soon as Zhong Mei came in, she was targeted by him. On the very night she moved into the dormitory, the administrator knocked on her door.","She didn't know what the administrator wanted to do at the time, so she opened the door. As a result, after saying just a few words, the administrator reached out to touch her.","Zhong Mei was not stupid.","It was precisely because of this kind of thing that she had fought with someone, almost destroying that man's private parts, and was sent here for labor reform.","Yet upon arriving here, she still had to suffer this kind of torment. This man who harassed her was even older and uglier than the one who harassed her back in her hometown.","Without another word, Zhong Mei grabbed a rock and smashed it at the administrator.","The administrator was scared away by her, but then again, her life became difficult.","Zhong Mei carried two baskets with a shoulder pole, the baskets filled with rocks. Sweating profusely and with weak legs, she walked up the mountain under the hot sun.","She had to deliver the rocks up the mountain, where they were building a ditch to draw mountain spring water.","A man walking beside her, also carrying baskets, couldn't help but say when he saw her like this, \"Sister, why don't you go and submit to Supervisor Liu? Let him arrange some lighter work for you. The work you're doing is for men; how can a young girl like you handle it?\"","Zhong Mei was now so hungry that her stomach touched her back, dizzy and seeing stars. She stopped to rest, put the two baskets of rocks on the ground, and didn't reply."]},{"number":184,"title":"Chapter 184: Soft Sleeper on Train","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng boarded the train heading to the Great Northwest together.","Because Qin Yuanzheng was a military officer and enjoyed certain privileges, he had managed to buy two soft sleeper tickets.","In those days, although trains were divided into soft and hard sleepers, the soft sleepers were mostly reserved for government officials, military personnel, or foreign guests. It was very difficult for ordinary people to buy them.","The soft sleeper compartments had doors, and inside were upper and lower bunks, totaling four beds.","Qin Yuanzheng had bought exactly one upper and one lower bunk. Sitting on the two opposite beds were two young men. They wore suits and ties, wore glasses, and looked gentle and refined, like cadres sent out for work.","The four of them simply exchanged glances and greeted each other. Carrying a large bag, Qin Yuanzheng only casually looked them over and did not speak to them.","However, when the two men saw Qiao Lanshu, they couldn't help but take a few extra glances at her.","The weather was getting warmer, so Qiao Lanshu was dressed lightly. She was fresh and beautiful, with large eyes and a cherry-like mouth. Her thick black hair hung loose, making her neck appear even more slender and fair, and her faintly exposed collarbones were quite eye-catching.","Moreover, having given birth just a few months ago, her figure was more voluptuous and charming than before.","That was why the two young men on the opposite beds stared at her a bit longer.","Holding a water bottle in one hand and a bag of dry rations like flatbreads and biscuits in the other, Qiao Lanshu walked straight to her bed upon entering, paying no attention to the two men opposite them.","Qin Yuanzheng, dressed in plain clothes, noticed this. After all, he was inherently sharp, especially when it came to his wife.","He quietly stepped behind Qiao Lanshu, using his broad shoulders and back to shield her completely from view.","Resting a hand on her shoulder, he said softly to her, You sleep on the top bunk, and I'll be right below you. Call me if you need anything, understand?","Qiao Lanshu had also wanted to sleep on the top bunk, considering there were two strange men opposite them.","She smiled and nodded, Okay.","With that, she stepped onto the iron ladder and climbed up in two steps.","Qin Yuanzheng stood below. He was tall; standing there, his shoulders were almost level with the upper bunk.","He watched Qiao Lanshu get up and sit comfortably before placing their luggage on the rack beside the bed.","Originally, Qin Yuanzheng had wanted to share the lower bunk with Qiao Lanshu.","But he was a big man, and the bunk was very small; it couldn't possibly fit two people.","If they squeezed in, his wife definitely wouldn't sleep well. It was a train ride of over ten hours, and she needed a good sleep.","Plus, with two young men opposite them, Qin Yuanzheng felt even more uneasy.","He watched as Qiao Lanshu, holding her water bottle and biscuits, finished tidying up the upper bunk.","Qin Yuanzheng asked in a low voice, Do you want to sleep for a while now?","After all, Qiao Lanshu had only given birth a few months ago. Her body probably hadn't fully recovered yet, and she usually took afternoon naps.","Qiao Lanshu reached out her hand and said, Hand me one of the books I brought. I'll read for a bit first.","Qin Yuanzheng opened his luggage bag, pulled out a high school textbook, and handed it to her.","Then, watching Qiao Lanshu lie down and start reading, he turned his head to glance at the two men opposite them.","He noticed that the two men were occasionally stealing glances at Qiao Lanshu.","Qin Yuanzheng's face immediately darkened.","He remained silent for two seconds, then pulled out his own bedsheet from the lower bunk. Standing up, he tied the bedsheet to the upper bunk, creating a makeshift curtain for Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu knew Qin Yuanzheng was doing this because of the men opposite them.","Sitting on the top bunk, she smiled and teased deliberately, Thank you, brother.","Qin Yuanzheng...","Qin Yuanzheng shot her a warning look and muttered, Rest well. By the time you wake up tomorrow morning, we'll almost be there.","Not calling him husband gave Qin Yuanzheng a slight mood swing.","Forget it, they were away from home. He wouldn't fuss over it with his little wife.","Besides, what was the point of her calling him that in front of outsiders? It was only exciting when she called him that in bed.","The two young men opposite them were engineers heading to the Northwest to participate in a bridge construction project. They were still very young, guided by their mentors, and could be considered young and promising.","The two sat on the lower bunk, looking at Qiao Lanshu's tightly curtained upper bunk, and then glanced at Qin Yuanzheng, who sat opposite them doing nothing but staring right back at them.","Although Qin Yuanzheng was wearing plain clothes, his aura was very intimidating.","With his arms crossed over his chest and his back straight, he neither ate nor drank, nor did he read. He just sat there, staring fixedly at the two of them.","His stare gave the two young men the creeps.","Fortunately, they knew that this kind of soft sleeper cabin couldn't be booked by just anyone.","There was a certain threshold to get in, and coupled with Qin Yuanzheng's imposing manner, they could pretty much guess that he was a military officer.","One of the young men greeted Qin Yuanzheng somewhat awkwardly, Hello there, comrade.","Qin Yuanzheng, with his arms crossed, glanced at him and nodded expressionlessly.","The two young men...","They could tell that Qin Yuanzheng didn't want to talk, so they didn't dare say much more.","Naturally, under Qin Yuanzheng's cold and stern gaze, they didn't dare steal any more glances at Qiao Lanshu. The two of them climbed into their respective beds and took out their books to read.","Seeing that they had settled down, Qin Yuanzheng ignored them.","He stood up and asked Qiao Lanshu in a low voice, Are you hungry? Do you still have water?","Qiao Lanshu nodded. There was still hot water in her bottle, and she had just eaten some biscuits, so she wasn't hungry right now.","She handed the bag of flatbreads to Qin Yuanzheng and whispered, Brother Zheng, you should eat something too. The flatbreads are cold, so have them with some hot water.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded, took the bag, and opened it to take a look. Seeing that there were indeed fewer flatbreads, he knew Qiao Lanshu had already eaten.","So he sat down below and started eating as well.","While they were eating the dry flatbreads on their side, the two young men opposite them went outside to fetch boiling water, then opened a packet of instant noodles and put it into the large enamel mug they carried with them.","After the instant noodles were brewed with boiling water, the aroma spread throughout the cabin.","The instant noodles smelled delicious. At that time, they weren't yet widespread and were quite expensive, costing about fifteen to twenty cents a packet.","They were considered a special supply food. Of course, with such a high price, even if ordinary people could buy them, they would be reluctant to spend the money.","Qin Yuanzheng had eaten instant noodles in the army, but he thought of how Qiao Lanshu had never had them. He was afraid she would be tempted by the smell of their noodles, and right now, he had nowhere to find any for her.","Therefore, while biting into his flatbread, Qin Yuanzheng glared fiercely at the two young men opposite him.","Sure enough, Qiao Lanshu was attracted by the instant noodles. She lifted the curtain, still holding the high school textbook, and looked at the two young men in surprise.","The two young men actually thought Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng were brother and sister. After all, the age gap between them looked quite large, and they didn't really seem like a married couple.","One of the young men warmly asked Qiao Lanshu, Comrade, these are instant noodles. Would you like some?","As he spoke, he took out another unopened packet of instant noodles from his bag and handed it to Qiao Lanshu.","Qin Yuanzheng even stopped eating the flatbread in his hand, staring darkly at the man.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and shook her head. \"Thank you, but no need. I'm already full.\"","The reason she had come out out of curiosity was that she wondered where these instant noodles had been bought.","Having lived two lifetimes, Qiao Lanshu had naturally eaten instant noodles before. In the future, during the economic boom, instant noodles would be considered unnutritious food, and they would be extremely cheap.","Although instant noodles would become ubiquitous later on, they were not yet.","Qiao Lanshu had never seen such a thing in the supply and marketing cooperatives in Longcheng.","She had seen minced pork noodles in the department store, but minced pork noodles and instant noodles were completely different things.","Qiao Lanshu declined the man's kindness and then pulled the curtain shut again.","She had noticed that the way the man was looking at her was a bit too enthusiastic.","At this moment, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly spoke up. He asked the young man opposite him in a fairly polite tone, \"Comrade, how much is one packet of your instant noodles? Can I buy one from you?\"","The young man opposite quickly replied, \"Sure, they are fifteen cents a packet.\"","Saying this, he handed the instant noodles to Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng gave him twenty cents, and the man insisted on giving him five cents in change.","Qin Yuanzheng politely declined it.","He said, \"Thank you, comrade. My wife hasn't had instant noodles before, so this is a good chance for me to buy one for her to try.\"","The young man waved his hand. \"You're welcome. If your sister wants to eat them, I have more here, I can even give you one for free.\"","Qin Yuanzheng suddenly gave a short laugh. He shook his head and said, \"No need. I don't have a sister.\"","With that, he stood up, grabbed his enamel mug and the instant noodles, pulled back the curtain of the upper bunk, and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Wife, I'm going to make the instant noodles for you. Come with me.\"","He certainly didn't feel comfortable leaving Qiao Lanshu alone in this compartment.","Little did he know, as soon as he finished speaking, Qiao Lanshu climbed down from the upper bunk with a smile.","As if he couldn't wait, he lifted Qiao Lanshu down with one arm, making her face turn bright red.","The sweet couple opened the compartment door and headed to the boiler room to get hot water for the noodles.","They completely ignored the two young men they left behind.","The two young men watched them walk out with their arms around each other. They exchanged a glance, both seeing the shock in each other's eyes.","They remained silent for a long moment before they started talking.","One of them whispered, \"They are actually husband and wife? You've got to be kidding me.\"","The other said, \"I really couldn't tell. That guy is almost old enough to be her father, isn't he?\"","...","Fortunately, Qin Yuanzheng didn't hear these words, or he would probably have been furious.","He usually worked in the mining area, exposed to the wind and sun, so his skin was indeed a bit rough. He looked older than Qiao Lanshu, but surely not old enough to be her father!","As he took Qiao Lanshu to the boiler room to make the noodles, he said with some dissatisfaction, \"Do we really look that mismatched? Did they actually believe we were brother and sister?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said softly, \"They are just passersby. It doesn't matter what they think.\"","Qin Yuanzheng walked back carrying the noodles and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"These instant noodles smell pretty good. Try some later. I had them when I was in the army. They're just okay, not as good as regular noodles.\"","Of course, instant noodles weren't as good as hand-rolled noodles. That went without saying.","It was only because they weren't widespread yet that they were sold at such a high price. Fifteen cents a packet was really too expensive!","The fried dough twists made in their food factory were only twenty cents a jin!","Qiao Lanshu muttered, \"Just this once. Please don't ever buy this again. The money for one packet of instant noodles is almost enough to buy a jin of fried dough twists.\"","Fried dough twists were so delicious. The sweet ones had frosting and sesame seeds on them. One bite and they were fragrant and crispy, unbelievably tasty. They could be eaten as a staple food or as a snack.","A jin of fried dough twists would be enough for Qiao Lanshu to eat for several days.","The couple walked through the hard sleeper carriage, chatting as they carried the instant noodles, and returned to their soft sleeper carriage.","Qin Yuanzheng held the enamel mug in one hand and opened the door with the other, about to let Qiao Lanshu inside.","Then, he turned his head and saw that behind them was a three- or four-year-old child who had been following them since who knows when.","This little child was fair and chubby, with big, dark eyes and round, pudgy arms. The child looked like she came from a well-off family that lacked neither food nor clothing.","However, the child was wearing a worn, dirty dress, and the cloth shoes on her feet were covered in dust, making her look quite poor.","The child stared wide-eyed and unblinking at the instant noodles in Qin Yuanzheng's hand, sucking on her right index finger with a face full of longing.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu also noticed the little child. Before she had children of her own, she didn't really pay much attention to kids.","She was rather indifferent to them.","But ever since she got pregnant, she started noticing children. Moreover, now that she was a mother and had An'an, she had developed a mother's tender heart.","Whenever she looked at little children, she found them adorable.","She looked behind the child but saw no adults.","So, she crouched down, looked at the child, and asked, \"Little one, how did you end up here all by yourself? Where are your mommy and daddy?\"","The child sucked on her finger, gave Qiao Lanshu a casual glance, ignored her, and continued staring at the enamel mug in Qin Yuanzheng's hand.","As she watched, the little child said, \"Noodles, noodles smell good.\"","Qin Yuanzheng said expressionlessly, \"You want to eat noodles? Go find your parents.\"","The child shook her head and said, feeling a bit wronged, \"Zhuangzhuang's tummy is hungry. Noodles smell good.\"","Qiao Lanshu stood up and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Is the child lost? How about we accompany her to look for her parents?\"","Saying this, the two stared at the child for another moment.","Qin Yuanzheng, having no other choice, held the noodles and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Let's go. This child probably smelled the instant noodles in the hard sleeper carriage and followed us here. Let's take her back and ask around.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. She stepped forward, took the child's hand, and said, \"Let's go, little one. Auntie will take you to find your parents.\"","The child didn't move. She stood stubbornly at the door of the soft sleeper carriage, staring eagerly at the enamel mug in Qin Yuanzheng's hand, her eyes full of intense longing.","At the same time, her stomach began to rumble.","Qiao Lanshu instantly felt that this little child was very pitiful.","She looked to be only three or four years old. For such a young child to have to travel a long distance with her family, and to be left starving!","She hesitated, then asked Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, how about... we let her eat some noodles first?\""]},{"number":185,"title":"Chapter 185: Jump Out to Find Someone","paragraphs":["Hearing Qiao Lanshu say this, Qin Yuanzheng immediately said in a low voice, \"Let's find the child's parents first.\"","The two of them first took the child for a walk through the hard sleeper carriages.","People in this era were very frugal and could endure hardships. Even for a train ride lasting over ten hours, they might not be willing to spend money on a hard sleeper ticket.","Qiao Lanshu felt that those willing to pay for the hard sleeper carriage must come from reasonably well-off families.","This child looked the part, too—chubby, fair-skinned, and incredibly adorable.","The more Qiao Lanshu looked at the child, the cuter she found him. She reached out to hold the little boy's hand and asked softly, \"Little one, where is your family? Do you remember?\"","The child had no interest in finding his family; his only interest lay in the instant noodles in Qin Yuanzheng's hands.","Let alone the child, when Qin Yuanzheng walked through the hard sleeper carriage carrying the instant noodles, the savory aroma attracted the attention of quite a few people.","Only then did Qin Yuanzheng realize he had made a mistake.","He should have left the instant noodles in his own soft sleeper carriage.","People taking long-distance trains usually brought their own dry rations—dry flatbreads or coarse grain steamed buns that were rock-hard, tasteless, and hard to swallow.","At a time like this, who wouldn't want a bite of savory noodles and a sip of piping hot broth?","Bearing the stares of the crowd, Qin Yuanzheng suddenly felt that the enamel mug in his hands was becoming rather troublesome.","As they passed through two carriages, they indeed heard a woman's voice calling out, \"Gousheng, Gousheng, where did you run off to? Who is Gousheng? He's my son, three years old, about this tall. Yes, have you seen him?\"","Qiao Lanshu paused her steps, staring at the little boy in front of her with wide eyes.","Such a cute child was actually named Gousheng?","You've got to be kidding.","Qiao Lanshu frowned and exchanged a glance with Qin Yuanzheng. Soon, a woman in her forties ran out from the next carriage.","The woman had dark skin and a slightly plump figure. She carried a crossbody bag, wore a gray jacket, and had black cloth shoes on her feet, looking like an ordinary worker.","Her expression was somewhat fierce, and she was cursing the whole way. When she saw the child, her face instantly darkened. She rushed over and roared, \"Where the hell did you go? Didn't I tell you to stay on the bed and not run around? You little bastard, you never listen!\"","As she spoke, she reached out, grabbed the child's ear, and twisted it.","The child was only three years old. Terrified by her, he plopped down onto the floor, and after having his ear pinched like that, he immediately burst into loud wails.","Let alone the child, even Qiao Lanshu was startled by this woman.","She took a half-step back, watching the scene in shock. Then, she quickly tried to stop the woman. \"Hey, don't do that. No matter what, you shouldn't hit a child.\"","Only then did the woman notice Qiao Lanshu. When she saw Qiao Lanshu's face, her eyes lit up, and her expression instantly became rather strange.","However, before the woman could speak, she immediately sensed danger.","So, she tore her gaze away from Qiao Lanshu's face and looked toward the source of the danger.","With one look, the woman shuddered in fear. Based on her experience, the man standing before her was clearly a soldier.","It was all this bastard child's fault, running around blindly while she went to the bathroom. He must have run into the soft sleeper carriages.","Otherwise, in her experience, it was very rare to run into soldiers in the hard sleeper carriages.","Even if she did, they usually traveled in groups and would occupy an entire carriage, in which case she would have stayed far away.","Qin Yuanzheng's gaze was dark and gloomy as he stared at the woman's hand.","The woman found Qin Yuanzheng somewhat familiar. In that instant, her hairs practically stood on end, and her heart almost leaped out of her chest.","Without a word, she scooped up the wailing child from the floor, turned around, and ran back toward the hard sleeper carriage.","The child cried and struggled, but being so young and caught up in his crying, he didn't have much strength.","The woman coaxed the child as she ran away.","Seeing this, Qiao Lanshu frowned and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Brother Zheng, how can a grandmother be so fierce to him?\"","Qin Yuanzheng found it a bit strange. He felt that the way the woman looked at him just now wasn't quite right.","It seemed almost as if she recognized him.","But he was absolutely certain he had never seen this woman before.","Recalling the way the woman looked at Qiao Lanshu also made him very uncomfortable.","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent for two seconds. Then, holding the enamel mug in one hand and pulling Qiao Lanshu with the other, he started walking back. \"Wife, you go back and eat your noodles first. I'll go back and check on them in a bit.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded.","When the two returned to the soft sleeper carriage, the two young men had already finished eating and were sitting on the bottom bunk playing Chinese chess.","Seeing them return, one of the young men smiled and asked, \"What took you so long?\"","Qin Yuanzheng explained expressionlessly, \"There were a lot of people at the hot water room, so we had to line up for a while.\"","Hmph, did they think he didn't know what was going through their minds?","If they were peacocks, they would already be fighting to spread their tail feathers right now.","Qin Yuanzheng originally hadn't wanted to let Qiao Lanshu come back alone, but he felt it was safer here. He didn't know what was up with that woman outside, and he needed to go back and check to put his mind at ease.","So, he said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Go up to the top bunk.\"","Qiao Lanshu was a bit surprised. Weren't they coming back to eat noodles? She could sit on the bottom bunk and eat; there was even a cabinet down there.","But Qin Yuanzheng looked at her with an unquestionable gaze. \"There's a curtain up there. Pull the curtain and sit up there to eat.\"","As he spoke, he cast a wary glance at the two young men behind him.","The two young men: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu felt a bit helpless, yet also somewhat amused.","When they were out and about, she was still very obedient to Qin Yuanzheng.","So, she climbed up to the top bunk and took the enamel mug from Qin Yuanzheng's hands. The instant noodles inside were still piping hot and fragrant. The smell really worked up an appetite.","Qiao Lanshu thought of the child again. He was so hungry; she wondered if his grandmother had prepared any food for him?","If she had known, she would have fed him some noodles first.","Qin Yuanzheng got Qiao Lanshu settled in and pulled the curtain a bit tighter, ensuring that the two young men opposite them couldn't see a thing.","Only then did he turn around, slide open the carriage door, and step out.","The two young men had been intimidated by his gaze. Qin Yuanzheng had been gone for quite a while, yet neither of them had moved their chess pieces.","Naturally, they didn't dare to speak either.","It wasn't until a minute or two later that their tense bodies slowly relaxed.","One of the more talkative young men spoke up again, \"Female comrade on the top bunk across from us, that male comrade just now, he's your husband, right?\"","Holding the instant noodles, Qiao Lanshu hadn't started eating yet. Hearing his question, she smiled and nodded. \"Yes.\"","Hearing her answer, the young man immediately perked up and added, \"He looks really fierce. He's a soldier, isn't he?\"","Speaking of which, he thought to himself: an older husband and a younger wife was indeed a rare combination. Moreover, this female comrade was so young and beautiful, and spoke so gently. No wonder that man was keeping such a close eye on her.","It was understandable.","Qiao Lanshu didn't really want to discuss with them whether Qin Yuanzheng was fierce or not, so she prevaricated, \"He's alright.\"","Hearing her reluctance to chat, the two young men didn't say anything more and went back to playing chess.","...","On the other side, after Qin Yuanzheng left the soft sleeper carriage, he didn't immediately go to the hard sleeper carriage.","Instead, he turned and went to the conductor's office. After communicating with them for a few minutes, a conductor went to the hard sleeper carriage to check tickets and gather information. When he returned...","He said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Comrade, the person you mentioned has no issues. She has a letter of introduction on her. This time, she's taking her grandson from her hometown to the city to join her son. She said the grandson is already three years old and it's time for him to go to kindergarten, so she's taking him to the city.\"","Her documents had all been checked, and they hadn't found anything unusual for the time being.","Qin Yuanzheng nodded and walked out of the conductor's office.","Strange, was he overthinking it?","He walked through three hard sleeper carriages and finally spotted the woman from earlier in the third one, quite a distance from the soft sleeper carriage.","The woman was chatting with the other passengers in her compartment, eating a flatbread with hot water in her hand.","Lying behind her was the little child from earlier. It was unknown if the child had eaten, but he was now sleeping peacefully.","Although he was a baby boy, he was wearing a dusty little dress.","But in this day and age, children were raised rather roughly, so this was quite normal.","Qin Yuanzheng himself had a rather scruffy childhood. The elderly raised children like they were herding sheep or cows; when they had time, they took them to the fields to play in the mud, and when they didn't, they simply tied them up in the sheep pen or cow shed with a rope.","Therefore, Qin Yuanzheng gave the woman a glance, and finding nothing abnormal, he turned and left in silence.","Little did he know that right after he turned away, the woman who had just been nibbling on the flatbread and chatting cheerfully with others immediately stuffed the bread into her pocket.","She stopped chatting with the passengers, hurriedly put on her bag, scooped up the child, and turned to leave.","The passenger sitting across from her said in surprise, \"Eh? You're getting off now? So soon?\"","This woman was very shrewd. Although she had managed to pry into the past three generations of the passenger opposite her, she hadn't revealed a single thing about herself.","She said dismissively, \"Yes, yes, we're about to arrive at the station, I need to get off quickly.\"","With that, the woman ran off with the child in her arms. The passenger opposite her said in confusion, \"Arrived? So soon?\"","The woman hurriedly ran to the train's exit door, anxiously waiting for the train to stop.","There was a station ahead, but it would still be a few minutes before the train stopped.","After all, trains in this era were sluggish and didn't move very fast.","The woman was so anxious she could barely stand it, wishing she could jump off the train right then and there.","In truth, she was just feeling guilty as a thief. After all, she had acted very normally. As long as she didn't lose her composure, what did it matter even if a soldier came over?","She had a guarantee letter and a household register, and this child was on her household register.","What did she have to fear?","...","When Qin Yuanzheng returned to the soft sleeper carriage, his brows were still slightly furrowed.","Qiao Lanshu hadn't eaten the instant noodles in the enamel mug. She had placed a towel on the bed and set the enamel mug on top of it.","She was reading a book while waiting for Qin Yuanzheng to return.","As soon as Qin Yuanzheng came in, he first looked at the two young men.","Seeing that the two young men were obediently playing chess opposite them, he withdrew his gaze and went to find Qiao Lanshu.","The two young men exchanged a glance, both seeing the helplessness in each other's eyes.","Qin Yuanzheng keeping such a close eye on them was putting them under a lot of pressure!","Qiao Lanshu pulled back the curtain, leaned on the railing, and looked at Qin Yuanzheng, asking in a low voice, \"Brother Zheng, did you go take a look? How was it?\"","Qin Yuanzheng stood there, his shoulder leaning against the railing of the upper bunk, and looked up to say quietly to Qiao Lanshu, \"I went to the train crew and asked them to help me investigate. The other party has all her documents, including her household register. That child is indeed her grandson. She is taking her grandson to the city to join her son, saying the child is three years old and needs to be sent to a kindergarten in the city.\"","Hearing this, the worried expression on Qiao Lanshu's face relaxed a bit, and she said, \"Good thing it's his biological grandmother, otherwise...\"","Pausing, she sighed, \"I saw that woman was dressed quite well, so why dress the child in such old clothes? And since it's a grandson, why put him in a dress? I thought he was a little girl at first.\"","Qin Yuanzheng also felt something was wrong, but without evidence, he couldn't just grab someone and accuse them of being a child trafficker.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't speak. Qiao Lanshu quickly brought the enamel mug over and handed it to him: \"Brother Zheng, you haven't eaten yet, right? Hurry up and eat, it won't be good if it gets cold.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was indeed hungry. He took the enamel mug, looked at it, and immediately frowned, \"Why didn't you eat?\"","He had specifically bought it for Qiao Lanshu to eat.","Such fragrant and expensive instant noodles, his wife hadn't tried them yet.","Qiao Lanshu looked at his expression and smiled, \"Alright, then feed me a couple of bites? I just had some biscuits, so I'm not really hungry. I'll just have a taste.\"","Qin Yuanzheng immediately took the chopsticks, picked up a mouthful of noodles, and brought them to Qiao Lanshu's lips.","The couple became intimately affectionate, as if there was no one else around.","The two young men opposite them exchanged a glance and silently lowered their heads to continue playing chess.","Qiao Lanshu had a couple of bites of noodles and then stopped.","Qin Yuanzheng sat on the lower bunk to eat himself. Right at that moment, the train slowly pulled into the station and came to a stop.","This was the second stop on the journey from Longcheng to the Northwest. However, it was a small station, and not many people were getting off the train.","On the other hand, there were quite a few people sending items, so the boarding and alighting areas were a bit chaotic.","Qiao Lanshu looked out the window at the crowded scene of people coming and going. Before she could even begin to sigh with emotion, her sharp eyes suddenly spotted that woman!","She let out a soft \"Eh,\" then leaned over the railing and looked down out the window.","Qin Yuanzheng sharply turned his head to look at her, \"What's wrong?\"","As soon as the words left his mouth, his brow darkened. He slammed the enamel mug onto the table with a bang. Then, he violently yanked open the window of the soft sleeper carriage and jumped straight out.","Qiao Lanshu was stunned. \"Brother Zheng?\"","The two young men were even more shocked.","They quickly lunged forward and pulled the window shut, saying with lingering fear, \"My goodness, why did he open the window? What if people start climbing in with their large and small bags in a moment?\"","The passengers outside didn't care if it was a soft sleeper or not; they would just throw their luggage in and then climb through the window.","Many people even used this method to evade fares. This behavior was very dangerous. The two young men, terrified of encountering people climbing through the windows and throwing bags, hurriedly shut the window.","Qiao Lanshu hurriedly climbed down from the top bunk and hurried over to the window to look outside.","However, the train platform outside was a bustling sea of people. Amidst the dense crowd of travelers dragging their goods and pulling their luggage, jostling shoulder to shoulder, she couldn't find the woman, nor could she catch any sign of Qin Yuanzheng."]},{"number":186,"title":"Chapter 186: Someone started fighting.","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng had been gone for a long time and still had not returned. Outside, the crowd was surging, and there was no sign of him.","As time passed, the train blew its whistle and slowly began to move.","Qin Yuanzheng still had not come back.","Qiao Lanshu was extremely anxious.","The two young men next to her turned to look at Qiao Lanshu. One of them lowered his voice and asked, \"Comrade, did... did your husband ditch you and run away?\"","He asked hesitantly, \"You don't owe any debts back in your hometown, do you?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Hearing his question, Qiao Lanshu did not know whether to laugh or cry.","She turned to look at him and said in a low voice, \"Brother Zheng went to catch a human trafficker, he didn't run away.\"","Originally, Qin Yuanzheng had not found anything suspicious, and since they were on a train, he had not planned to get to the bottom of it.","However, the woman had a guilty conscience. As soon as the train stopped, she grabbed the child and ran.","When Qiao Lanshu had just seen her through the window, the woman was walking in a great hurry, constantly looking back as if she was worried someone was chasing her.","Even Qiao Lanshu could tell something was wrong with the woman, let alone Qin Yuanzheng.","So under the circumstances, Qin Yuanzheng vaulted out the window without a second word.","He was afraid that if he was a step too late, she would escape.","The young man asked in surprise, \"A human trafficker? There was a trafficker outside just now?\"","The other young man said with a serious expression, \"Speaking of which, there really have been traffickers appearing around various train stations lately, and the police haven't been able to catch them. Those traffickers are very smart, disguise themselves well, and run away very fast every time.\"","The young man then said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Then you have to be careful. Those traffickers target young and pretty girls like you.\"","Every year, you hear about girls going missing.","Even though the household registration system is quite strict nowadays.","But no matter how strict the system is, there are always people who find loopholes.","And no matter the era, young and beautiful women are always scarce in the mountains.","In her previous life, Qiao Lanshu had experienced being locked up in a cave dwelling, so she naturally knew what the people in the mountains were like.","She remained silent, just looking anxiously out the window. Watching the train slowly start and move forward, Qin Yuanzheng still had not returned.","She was not worried about Qin Yuanzheng getting lost. This was a city with a train station, and Qin Yuanzheng was a soldier with identification and a letter of introduction on him.","She was just worried that he might have an accident. After all, human traffickers usually operated in gangs, and they were fierce desperadoes with cruel methods.","She was afraid he would get hurt.","She quickly stood up and said, \"I'm going to find the train crew and see if they can delay the departure.\"","Saying that, she hurriedly ran out.","...","Qin Yuanzheng had felt all along that the woman seemed to know him.","At the very least, she had seen him before and knew his identity.","This made Qin Yuanzheng even more suspicious, and he did not know what her background was.","Qin Yuanzheng was fast and chased her all the way outside the platform. Then, he saw the sleeping child casually tossed by the side of the road, while the woman had long since disappeared without a trace.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Someone had already noticed the child lying on the ground.","Before it attracted more attention, Qin Yuanzheng quickly ran over and briefly checked the child's condition.","The child was sleeping deeply and had not woken up even after being thrown down.","Other than that, everything else seemed normal.","Qin Yuanzheng checked his breathing, felt his forehead, and then picked up the child with one arm, running back toward the platform.","He had just heard the train's whistle signaling its departure.","He had to hurry, or he would miss the train.","He could not bear to leave Qiao Lanshu alone on the train, especially one heading to a labor farm in the Northwest.","Qin Yuanzheng rushed back to the train station, watching the train gradually speed up, about to leave the station.","He sprinted forward, holding the child in one arm, grabbed the train window with his other hand, and vaulted sideways into the train.","He had jumped into a hard sleeper carriage. When he came in, he accidentally bumped into other passengers. Amidst their scolding, he carried the child and went to find the train staff.","The child was still sleeping, which was not normal. He guessed the fleeing trafficker had drugged him.","This child was probably abducted from Longcheng, or if not Longcheng, a nearby city.","Looking at the child, his family seemed quite well-off. It was even possible that Qin Yuanzheng knew his family.","This would also explain why the trafficker recognized him; maybe she had spent some time in Longcheng.","Qin Yuanzheng handed the child over to the train conductors, explained the whole situation to them, and asked them to take good care of the child. He told them to feed him when he woke up, hand him over to the police at the next station, and have someone take him to the hospital for a check-up.","Then, when he returned from the labor farm in the Northwest, he would go pick up the child and take him back to Longcheng to find his family.","The train crew knew Qin Yuanzheng's identity, so his words were very credible. There were female comrades among the crew, so taking care of a child was no problem. After all, the next station was only two hours away, and they could just hand the child over to the police then.","After arranging this, Qin Yuanzheng quickly walked toward the soft sleeper carriage.","Just as he entered, he saw Qiao Lanshu walking out, and the two ran into each other.","Qin Yuanzheng immediately hugged her and asked in a low voice, \"Where are you going?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","When Qiao Lanshu realized it was him, she hugged him back tightly: \"You scared me to death when you jumped off the train.\"","Saying that, she quickly asked, \"Was that really a human trafficker? Did you catch her?\"","Qin Yuanzheng frowned and shook his head. \"No, she got away. Time was tight, and I was afraid of missing the train, so I brought the child back first.\"","Qiao Lanshu then looked behind him and asked in confusion, \"Where is the child?\"","Qin Yuanzheng felt a bit helpless. His wife only cared about the child of unknown origin and did not even ask if he was hurt, when he got back, or how he got back...","Forget it, why be petty over a child?","Qin Yuanzheng then told her about the arrangements for the child.","After all, they still had to go to the labor farm in the vast Northwest, and bringing a child would not be convenient.","The child had clearly been drugged and needed to go to the hospital for a check-up. He was too young to endure such a long, arduous journey with them.","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu immediately let out a sigh of relief.","As a mother herself, she could not bear to see such things happen.","If the child had not been recovered, she probably would not have been in the mood to do anything.","She asked softly, \"Was the child abducted from Longcheng too? Could it be a family we know?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"I'm not sure, but the possibility exists because it's highly likely they boarded at the Longcheng train station as well.\"","Not to mention, that woman actually recognized him.","Qiao Lanshu wanted to go check on the child, but Qin Yuanzheng told her the little one was asleep and convinced her not to go. Putting his arm around his wife's shoulders, he led her back to the soft sleeper carriage.","Seeing his return, the two young men in their compartment immediately leaned in. \"Comrade, you're finally back! We heard you went to catch the human traffickers. Did you get them?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"No.\"","The two young men fell silent.","Qiao Lanshu quickly chimed in, \"But the child was safely recovered. He is with the train staff now.\"","The two young men breathed a sigh of relief. They then began talking to Qiao Lanshu about how rampant traffickers had become lately. In their home city, some women had even gone missing, and the police highly suspected they had been abducted.","They chattered on for quite a while. However, noticing Qin Yuanzheng's expression growing increasingly cold, they eventually didn't dare to speak to Qiao Lanshu anymore.","The soft sleeper carriage slowly quieted down.","By this time, evening was approaching. Qin Yuanzheng turned to Qiao Lanshu and said, \"You should go up and rest. It's getting late.\"","With that, he helped Qiao Lanshu up to the upper berth. He remained sitting on the lower berth, feeling no sleepiness at all.","Whenever he recalled the look on that trafficker's face as the man stared at Qiao Lanshu, his expression turned grim.","Human traffickers nowadays were far too brazen, abducting not only children but women as well.","Thank goodness Qiao Lanshu hadn't run into any trouble when she traveled all the way to Longcheng alone to find him.","From now on, she had him to protect her.","...","Whenever Qiao Lanshu took the train alone, she never dared to sleep.","But now, with Qin Yuanzheng guarding the lower berth, she fell asleep with complete peace of mind, even sleeping quite deeply.","By the time she woke up, the sky outside was already bright.","She pulled out the watch hidden in the inner pocket of her clothes and took a look. It was already past seven in the morning.","Their train was scheduled to arrive at the station around half past nine, which meant they had less than two hours to get ready to disembark.","Qin Yuanzheng had been awake for a long time. When he was away from home, his habit was to barely sleep, and even when he did, it was a very light sleep so he could remain alert.","He had gotten up at the crack of dawn to pack their belongings. He also took their thermos to fetch some hot water, preparing to soak a towel for Qiao Lanshu to wash her face and wipe her hands as soon as she woke up.","The two of them looked so loving and affectionate that it made the two young men across from them sour with envy.","After the couple finished packing, they shared some flatbread and biscuits. Qin Yuanzheng also pulled an apple from his bag and gave it to Qiao Lanshu to eat.","Once they finished eating, Qin Yuanzheng slung the luggage bag over his shoulder, held Qiao Lanshu's hand tightly, and left the soft sleeper carriage.","Right before they got off the train, the train staff gave Qin Yuanzheng an update on the child. \"Comrade Qin, the child was sent to the Jingcheng City Public Security Bureau last night. Because he wouldn't wake up, the police officers took him overnight to the nearby military hospital for a checkup. I informed them that you would go pick up the child in a week, and I also left your military unit designation and address with them.\"","This was exactly what Qin Yuanzheng had instructed the night before, so he nodded. \"Alright, understood.\"","When the train doors opened, he led Qiao Lanshu off the train.","Thinking about the child's condition, Qiao Lanshu said with a hint of worry, \"I wonder what kind of drug those traffickers fed him. How could a three-year-old sleep so deeply?\"","Such a small child—it would be terrible if the drug ruined his health.","To this, Qin Yuanzheng could only say, \"If they were planning to sell the child to a childless family, they probably wouldn't give him anything that would permanently damage his health.\"","Unless, of course, they weren't planning to sell him but intended to keep him for begging. That would be a different story entirely.","However, Qin Yuanzheng kept that thought to himself.","There was no point in voicing uncertain speculations and scaring his little wife.","She had just recently become a mother herself and was at her most tender-hearted.","Not long after leaving the train station, Qin Yuanzheng headed straight to the nearby military district and borrowed a car from a comrade.","He then drove for over four hours along winding mountain roads before they finally arrived at their destination.","The midday sun was scorching. The air was thick with gray dust, and looking out, all they could see were endless, rolling mountains and forests.","The yellow mud road was bare, and the surroundings looked like an absolute wilderness.","Taking in the desolate scene, Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but fall silent.","Qin Yuanzheng parked the car. After stepping out, he glanced around, his face showing no sign of surprise.","Qiao Lanshu asked in a low voice, \"Brother Zheng, are you sure we didn't take the wrong road?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head. \"I don't think so. The labor reform farm should be over there. The road is too narrow for the car to pass. Come on, let's walk over and take a look.\"","He parked the car under a large tree by the side of the road, then took Qiao Lanshu's hand. Following a side fork in the road, they walked for about ten minutes until they indeed spotted the sign for the labor reform farm.","After walking for another ten minutes or so, they finally saw an open mountain clearing and a building nestled in the hills.","The entrance of the building was plastered with various notices. An old, weathered plaque bore the words \"XX Prison.\"","The first two characters were so mottled they were unreadable, but the word \"Prison\" could barely be made out.","In this era, prisons were no longer traditional prisons; they were various labor reform farms.","Within the labor farm, inmates were divided into over a dozen teams based on the severity of their crimes. Those with the most serious offenses labored deep within the farm, heavily guarded by armed soldiers at every level.","Ordinary inmates, however, were managed much more loosely, overseen only by regular supervisors.","After all, in these times, a random accusation or a single report could easily get someone sent away for labor reform.","Strictly speaking, many of these people weren't even real criminals.","Even without anyone watching them, these inmates wouldn't dare run away. The labor farm was surrounded by endless, towering mountains. If they escaped, they would never make it out of the mountains and would freeze to death in the winter.","In the summer, they would likely be eaten by wild beasts, or starve and die of thirst after getting lost.","Even if they luckily managed to follow the mountain paths out, the farm supervisors would just chase them down on tractors and catch them in no time.","Furthermore, because the inmates' household registrations had been transferred to the farm, returning home was useless. Without an ID or a registered residence, they would inevitably be sent right back.","While Qiao Lanshu spent some time reading the notices at the main gate, Qin Yuanzheng went forward to negotiate.","Soon enough, a supervisor came out and very politely led them inside.","The supervisor was a man in his forties. He smiled courteously and said, \"Comrades, the Zhong Mei you are here to visit indeed arrived here not too long ago. Her offense wasn't too serious, so she was assigned to Team 12. Right now, she should be up in the mountains digging irrigation ditches...\"","Just as he was speaking, shouts from the inmates echoed from the distance: \"Supervisor! Supervisor! Bad news! A fight broke out in the dormitory area!\""]},{"number":187,"title":"Chapter 187: Labor Reform Camp","paragraphs":["Hearing that there was a fight, Qin Yuanzheng pulled Qiao Lanshu behind him.","It was Qiao Lanshu's first time visiting a labor camp farm, and she was indeed shocked by the surrounding scenery.","It was truly too desolate here. There were mountains everywhere. People had to build roads and canals, transform the wilderness into farmland, and turn the mountain forests into fields for growing crops. This was indeed a massive undertaking.","When Qiao Lanshu was still in school, she had heard that many educated youths sent to the countryside were sent into the mountains to clear land.","Before she went to search for her husband and go down to the countryside, her father had asked her to find her husband, saying that since she grew up in the city and didn't even know how to grow vegetables, she definitely wouldn't be able to endure the hardship of clearing wasteland.","She hadn't believed it at the time.","Now, seeing it for herself, fine, she really wasn't cut out for this kind of work.","But, could Zhong Mei do it?","Was she really here?","The administrator leading them in was from the logistics department. Hearing someone mention a fight, he immediately said, Where is Supervisor Liu? He's on duty today, right? Go find him quickly.","The person opposite said, Oh my, it's Supervisor Liu who got beaten up!","The administrator was speechless.","He immediately couldn't care less about hosting the military officer, Qin Yuanzheng. After all, a supervisor getting beaten was a rather serious issue.","He took off running toward the inside of the farm.","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng were still standing in the outer courtyard. The two exchanged a glance, and Qin Yuanzheng said, Let's go in and take a look. The labor convicts' dormitory area is also inside. We can just go in and ask around to see where your friend lives.","This labor camp didn't have a cafeteria.","Of course, the staff and the military had cafeterias, but the convicts did not. They received grain every month based on their labor, which was actually quite similar to the work point system in the villages.","There was a fixed ration of grain each month, but because food was precious, the portions were small, only enough to barely fill their stomachs. Most people had to dig up wild vegetables in the mountains and boil them into a thin soup with coarse grain flour. Even just drinking water to feel full was better than going to work on an empty stomach.","Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng walked in and followed the mountain path for quite a while. Sure enough, they saw a cluster of low earthen houses.","It was actually pretty good that the convicts here had earthen houses to live in. There were also many cave dwellings inside, which were also for the convicts.","In an open space not far from the dormitory area, a group of people was clamoring, and the scene was quite chaotic.","Before long, Qiao Lanshu saw a middle-aged man being carried out by several people, his forehead and face covered in blood.","Behind these people, a skinny young person was also being escorted over.","Qiao Lanshu originally went over with the mindset of watching the commotion.","As a result, when she took a look, she was stunned. Zhong Mei?","Qiao Lanshu hurried over. Zhong Mei? You really are here. What on earth is going on with you?","Qin Yuanzheng also quickly followed behind her, frowning as he observed Zhong Mei, who was being held down by two patrol members.","Zhong Mei was filthy and covered in dirt all over, her hair a mess. She was very thin, but her eyes were bright, carrying a bit of a ruthless edge when she looked at people.","When she saw Qiao Lanshu, she was also shocked. After the shock passed, she became excited. Lanshu, you really found me! I knew you wouldn't abandon me!","She had previously sent a letter to Qiao Lanshu and was indeed preparing to board a train to Longcheng.","After all, given her situation, she had no one to rely on at home. Her family even wished they could sell her for money.","Besides Qiao Lanshu, she simply had no one else to turn to.","However, half a day after she sent the letter, her family found out. Then they forced her to go on blind dates and make her get married.","That man was also very sleazy. As soon as they met, he started getting handsy, even saying that he had already given her family a fifty-yuan bride price, and that after they got their marriage certificate, he would make up the remaining one hundred and fifty to her family.","So to speak, her family had sold her, and for a mere two hundred yuan.","Zhong Mei disagreed right then and there and got into an argument with the man. When he tried to get handsy with her again, she directly knocked him out.","It was the same this time; that Supervisor Liu had also been knocked out by her.","Qiao Lanshu looked at Zhong Mei with heartache. Having not seen her for a long time, she found that Zhong Mei had gotten even thinner and looked more haggard. She was dirty from head to toe. It seemed that her life in the labor camp was quite difficult.","Qiao Lanshu looked at Zhong Mei affectionately. How did you end up here? What happened to you?","Before Zhong Mei could speak, the administrator standing next to her asked Qin Yuanzheng in shock, Comrades, is she the person you came to visit this time?","Qin Yuanzheng stepped in front of Qiao Lanshu and nodded. Yes, what is going on with her?","The administrator's face looked terrible. Originally, after an assault incident like today's, Zhong Mei would have to be transferred out of Team 12 and into the even harsher Team 10. The convicts in there were all people who had hurt others and had criminal records.","Convicts in Team 12, on the other hand, had no criminal records. Once their labor sentences were up, they could still be assigned to various production teams after getting out.","Now that Qin Yuanzheng and the others were intervening, the administrator didn't immediately continue taking Zhong Mei away.","The administrator said to Qiao Lanshu and Qin Yuanzheng, This Zhong Mei has committed a serious offense. She injured Supervisor Liu from Team 12. You just saw it too; Supervisor Liu's head was covered in blood.","Zhong Mei immediately retorted, That's because he acted like a hooligan toward me! People on the outside who act like hooligans get arrested and sent to labor camps, so why is it fine for him to do it here? Are convicts not human beings?","The administrator said with a dark expression, This is just your side of the story. As for the truth, we still have to ask Supervisor Liu.","Zhong Mei was furious and raised her voice even louder. Why are you taking the side of a hooligan? Are you guys in cahoots? Do you usually harass the female convicts too?","The administrator was speechless.","He nervously glanced at Qin Yuanzheng and said loudly, Don't talk nonsense! How could I possibly do such a thing!","If these were just the relatives of an ordinary convict, it would be one thing, but Qin Yuanzheng was no ordinary person. He was a high-ranking military officer!","The administrator felt there was no need for him to get involved in this mess.","He said huffily, Forget it, I wash my hands of this matter today. When Supervisor Liu comes back, I'll report this incident up the chain, and we'll see how it's handled then.","With that, he hurriedly left, and Zhong Mei was released.","Qiao Lanshu held Zhong Mei's hand, looking her up and down several times before turning to Qin Yuanzheng with worry. Brother Zheng, what should we do about this?","Qin Yuanzheng fell silent for a moment. Before he could speak, he heard Zhong Mei say with a cold sneer, He was the one who got handsy with me first. He harassed me and even withheld my grain rations. I've been here for about ten days and have barely eaten. He withheld all my food. He's the one who should be arrested and sent to a labor camp!","Qin Yuanzheng glanced at Zhong Mei, his mind actually on something else: His wife had such a soft and gentle personality; how did she end up with such a fiery and fierce friend.","It was quite strange that these two girls with such vastly different personalities could become good friends.","As she spoke, Zhong Mei seemed to brush the matter off. She looked Qin Yuanzheng up and down, then leaned in close to Qiao Lanshu's ear and whispered, \"Is this your older husband?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"???\"","Fine, just take this best friend out and shoot her. He didn't want to deal with this anymore.","Zhong Mei noticed Qin Yuanzheng's expression change, so she immediately switched to the Yangcheng dialect to speak with Qiao Lanshu.","As she spoke, she kept sneaking glances at Qin Yuanzheng. Qin Yuanzheng, however, couldn't understand a single word, which made his face turn even colder.","What Zhong Mei actually said to Qiao Lanshu was, \"I have to say, this older man of yours isn't bad at all. He's much better than that Sun Mingyong—taller, more handsome, and richer too.\"","As Zhong Mei continued, she looked at Qiao Lanshu with envy. \"Lanshu, you just have good fate, unlike me...\"","Zhong Mei sighed again at this point.","She felt it was all down to destiny.","Qiao Lanshu had traveled a thousand miles to find her husband only to be deceived. It should have been a stroke of terrible luck, but it turned out to be a blessing in disguise.","She ended up remarrying Qin Yuanzheng and was much better off for it.","But Zhong Mei didn't have that kind of opportunity.","Qiao Lanshu linked arms with her sympathetically and whispered, \"Don't be sad. We'll figure out a way to get you out of here. Once we're back in Longcheng, I'll find you a temp job at the food factory. Then you can settle down and take your time picking a good husband.\"","Zhong Mei sighed and offered a bitter smile. \"Just getting out of here is a pipe dream. How could I even dare to think about finding a partner? Besides, good men aren't that easy to find.\"","As the two talked, their expressions grew somber, and they stood there sighing.","Qin Yuanzheng stood right beside them, feeling a bit uncomfortable.","Having been with Qiao Lanshu for so long, he had never felt any generation gap.","Today, he finally discovered that their gap was language.","In the future, if Zhong Mei went to Longcheng and spoke to Qiao Lanshu in their dialect every day, wouldn't he be left completely in the dark?","And what if one day Qiao Lanshu went back to Yangcheng to visit relatives and spoke to the men there? He still wouldn't understand a thing—he would die of anxiety.","Seeing that Qin Yuanzheng didn't look too happy, Qiao Lanshu asked him softly, \"Brother Zheng, what are you thinking about?\"","Qin Yuanzheng shook his head expressionlessly. \"Nothing. Are you two done chatting? Let's go check out the dormitory area.\"","Zhong Mei immediately said, \"Can we not go back? I share a room with someone there, but she's always making snide remarks every day. It's so annoying.\"","Zhong Mei didn't want to go back for even a second, but she wasn't sure if Qiao Lanshu actually had a way to get her out of here.","So she felt quite melancholic.","Qin Yuanzheng then led the two of them outside. \"Let's go to the guesthouse first then.\"","However, after arriving at the guesthouse, Qin Yuanzheng regretted it.","Because Qiao Lanshu wanted to sleep in the same room as Zhong Mei, leaving Qin Yuanzheng all alone in the room next door.","Qin Yuanzheng stood at the door in disbelief, watching the two of them walk into the room hand in hand. Qiao Lanshu didn't even look back at him once.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\""]},{"number":188,"title":"Chapter 188: We need to call the police first.","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu knew that Qin Yuanzheng didn't want to sleep in a separate room from her.","But wasn't this a special situation?","She definitely had to stay with Zhong Mei.","Qiao Lanshu led Zhong Mei into the guesthouse room, then took a water bottle, biscuits, flatbreads, and other dry rations out of her bag.","In this era, when traveling far from home, one had to bring enough food. Otherwise, you couldn't buy anything to eat while on the road, even if you had money.","Whether buying food at a supply and marketing cooperative or a department store in another town, or eating at a state-run restaurant, national food coupons were required.","However, national food coupons were not easy to exchange for.","Qin Yuanzheng had managed to get some for this trip, but not many. He had exchanged just enough coupons to cover ten days of food for him and Qiao Lanshu.","It was getting dark now, and looking at Zhong Mei, she had probably been starving for a long time.","Qin Yuanzheng took the food coupons and went out to buy food at the labor camp's staff canteen.","Zhong Mei was indeed starving. Seeing the biscuits Qiao Lanshu brought out, she didn't stand on ceremony and immediately said, \"Shushu, you are so good to me. What would I do without you!\"","Before she even finished speaking, she had stuffed her mouth full of biscuits, crying as she ate. \"I've been here for over ten days, and that supervisor has been eyeing me this whole time. He told me to be obedient, or else he wouldn't give me any food.\"","For the past few days, she had been surviving on wild vegetables steeped in boiled water. Sometimes, a few female inmates took pity on her and shared a little of their food.","But not many people shared their food with her. After all, food was precious. Everyone was underfed and worked hard, so no one would easily show such charity.","In less than half a month, Zhong Mei had lost seven or eight pounds. She was already thin to begin with, and now she looked even smaller and frailer, like a bamboo pole.","Qiao Lanshu's face darkened as she asked, \"Told you to be obedient? What did he want you to do?\"","Zhong Mei stuffed another biscuit into her mouth and sneered, \"With his brain, what else could he be thinking? He wanted me to sleep with him.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Which man in a labor camp didn't want a woman?","After all, they were deep in the mountains. It wasn't easy to make a trip out, and they might not leave for years.","They wanted women, but there were very few women in the labor camp. To protect themselves, most of the women had found partners early on.","Young and beautiful women were even scarcer.","When Zhong Mei first arrived, quite a few men had their eyes on her and tried to court her.","However, once Supervisor Liu set his sights on her, all those men backed off. They were terrified of getting on Supervisor Liu's bad side and being assigned the dirtiest and most exhausting tasks. Failing to finish the work was one thing, but having their food rations deducted and going hungry was what they feared most.","Zhong Mei's skin was a bit tanned from the sun, but she was slender and had a pretty face.","It was no surprise that Supervisor Liu had targeted her.","Zhong Mei said viciously, \"Men are all the same. Their minds are entirely controlled by what's between their legs. Other than that, their heads are full of shit. I won't indulge them. I'm not afraid of anyone who comes at me; worst comes to worst, I'll just drag them down to hell with me.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't know what to say. With a face full of melancholy, she sighed deeply.","At this moment, Zhong Mei was truly famished, so much so that she couldn't even bother to worry about her future situation in the labor camp.","While cursing continuously, she kept stuffing biscuits and small fried dough twists into her mouth.","As she ate, she mumbled, \"What is this? It's so good! And what's this? Why is it so fragrant? Shushu, what about this one? This is delicious too! Wow, Shushu, you've really hit the big time. Why do I feel like my future is starting to look bright too?\"","In the past, back in Yangcheng, Qiao Lanshu's family had been quite well-off because her father was a manager at a department store, and she often shared good food with Zhong Mei.","But some of the food she brought this time were things they had never seen in Yangcheng.","Like the sweet sesame fried dough twists, the fragrant and crispy walnut pastries, and the red date and millet cakes that were sticky but deliciously sweet.","In comparison, the biscuits were tossed aside by Zhong Mei.","Zhong Mei said as she ate, \"I really didn't expect Longcheng to have so many snacks. These things are all so delicious.\"","Especially that red date and millet cake—it was made of red dates and millet!","Both red dates and millet were very expensive!","Qiao Lanshu looked at Zhong Mei with a mix of heartache and amusement, telling her, \"Eat slowly. I brought all of these specifically for you. They're all yours.\"","After getting about eighty percent full, Zhong Mei's eating speed finally slowed down.","Qiao Lanshu brought out the water bottle again and poured her a cup of warm water.","Zhong Mei put down the food, picked up the cup to drink, and started crying again as she drank.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu sighed softly, stood up, and hugged her shoulders. She whispered, \"Don't cry. I'll ask Brother Zheng to think of a way. You were forced into this incident. That Supervisor Liu definitely hasn't just done this to you; before you arrived, he must have coerced other female inmates.\"","Saying this, Qiao Lanshu fell silent for a few seconds, then said decisively, \"Before Supervisor Liu comes back and before this matter blows up, Meimei, you have to report this to the police!\"","Zhong Mei said gloomily, \"This is a labor camp. How can we call the police? Any issues are handled by the administrators.\"","Qiao Lanshu suddenly realized, \"Right, I would have forgotten if you hadn't mentioned it... Then I'll go to the police for you. We have to make a big deal out of this. You're the victim. We can't wait for the wicked to sue first, or else you'll become the culprit. We'll accuse Supervisor Liu of hooliganism first and have people investigate. As long as they find out he has coerced other women, he can forget about ever being a supervisor again. He must be sent to labor reform too!\"","Just as Qin Yuanzheng had said, even if a soldier committed a crime, they had to be sentenced by a military court.","The man surnamed Liu was just a lowly supervisor. Abusing his power to coerce female inmates meant he had to be punished as well.","Qiao Lanshu wasn't as impulsive and hot-tempered as Zhong Mei. She had always been calm and composed, so she quickly figured things out.","Zhong Mei had to be the victim. Moreover, they could use this incident to bring up what happened in her hometown, proving that she had been coerced back there as well, which was why she had a trauma response and lashed out instinctively this time.","When the time came, they could go back to Yangcheng to investigate the incident, find a few witnesses to write testimonies proving Zhong Mei was the victim, and just like that, Zhong Mei's name would be cleared, and she could leave the labor camp!","Qiao Lanshu slapped her thigh. \"Yes, that's what we'll do!\"","With a small fried dough twist still stuffed in her mouth, Zhong Mei listened to Qiao Lanshu and asked hesitantly, \"Will that really work? Can I really be acquitted and released?\"","Her labor reform sentence was three years, and she had already prepared herself to stay here for the full three years.","She was only 19. In three years, she would only be 22. She figured that as long as she could endure it, she would definitely live a good life afterward.","After all, nothing could be worse than being in a labor camp.","Qiao Lanshu nodded firmly. \"It will definitely work. Tomorrow, Brother Zheng and I will call Yangcheng and find someone to investigate what happened to you back then. Tell me now, when you were arguing with that man, was there anyone around? If someone can testify for you, that would be even better.\"","At this, Zhong Mei thought carefully for a moment and suddenly said, \"There actually was!\"","She had met that man in a park near her home, and at the time, there were some mobile vendors secretly selling vegetables in the park.","Zhong Mei and Qiao Lanshu had grown up in that area since they were children, so they were familiar with many of the neighbors.","Therefore, as soon as Zhong Mei mentioned it, Qiao Lanshu knew who she was talking about. The two discussed it for a while and decided how to handle the matter.","Qiao Lanshu estimated that she could only stay for three or four days this time, not for long. She wanted to take Zhong Mei with her when she left, so she had to hurry up and get this matter resolved quickly.","After the two had been in the room for over an hour, Qin Yuanzheng came knocking on the door.","Zhong Mei had already eaten her fill, so she asked Qiao Lanshu to get the door while she tidied up the room.","Zhong Mei was able to stay at the guest house this time because Qin Yuanzheng had vouched for her.","Under normal circumstances, labor camp inmates like her were not allowed out.","Qiao Lanshu opened the door and saw Qin Yuanzheng holding two insulated lunch boxes. He looked at Qiao Lanshu and said in a low voice, \"I went to the cafeteria to buy some food. This is for the two of you.\"","He handed one of the insulated containers to Qiao Lanshu.","Qiao Lanshu took it with a smile. \"Thank you, Brother Zheng.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at her with a deep, quiet gaze, wanting to say a few more words to her. However, after taking the container, Qiao Lanshu turned around and was about to leave.","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","With quick reflexes, Qin Yuanzheng reached out and grabbed Qiao Lanshu's arm. Then, under Qiao Lanshu's surprised gaze, he pulled her out the door and walked straight into the room next door.","Qiao Lanshu held the insulated container in one hand while being dragged by Qin Yuanzheng with the other. At first, she was a bit surprised, wondering if Qin Yuanzheng had something to say to her.","Of course, she truly did not expect that a man like Qin Yuanzheng would actually get jealous over Zhong Mei.","Zhong Mei wasn't even a man.","Qin Yuanzheng pulled Qiao Lanshu into the next room, then closed the door. While Qiao Lanshu wore a face full of confusion, he pinched her chin and kissed her.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Just how long had this man been holding back this time?","It did not seem like it had been that long, right?","After kissing Qiao Lanshu for a while, Qin Yuanzheng asked in a low voice, \"Which room are you staying in tonight?\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Naturally, Qiao Lanshu was thinking of staying in Zhong Mei's room next door.","She and Zhong Mei had not seen each other for far too long.","Although to Zhong Mei, they had only been apart for a little over a year.","But to Qiao Lanshu, it felt like a matter of two lifetimes.","In her previous life, when she and Qin Yuanzheng got married, she was already thirty years old, and by that time, she had never managed to get in touch with Zhong Mei.","Looking at Qin Yuanzheng's expression, she smiled and kissed him on the cheek, coaxing him in a soft voice, \"Brother Zheng, just let me sleep with Zhong Mei tonight, okay?\"","Qiao Lanshu knew that Qin Yuanzheng was most susceptible to this tactic of hers.","As long as she softened her voice, looked at him eagerly, and hugged his arm while giving it a little shake, Qin Yuanzheng would surrender.","Sure enough, Qin Yuanzheng could not hold out this time either. He frowned slightly and said, \"Do you really have that much to talk about with her? You have been talking for two hours and it is still not enough? You have to talk to her all night?\"","Good friends who haven't seen each other in a long time, how could they ever run out of things to say?","Even a whole night might not be enough.","Qiao Lanshu sighed softly. \"What happened to Zhong Mei this time was really unexpected. By the way, Brother Zheng, do you know anyone in Yangcheng? I want to call my dad and ask him to find a few neighbors to act as witnesses and write down testimonies proving that Zhong Mei was coerced, but I am afraid that the Revolutionary Committee and the Public Security Bureau will refuse to process it.\"","After all, Zhong Mei's case had already been judged, and she had been sent here for labor reform.","Trying to overturn the case would not be that easy.","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng said, \"In Yangcheng, I really do not know anyone...\"","He paused for a moment as he spoke, then added, \"But regarding the Revolutionary Committee, Guan Wenjun should have some connections. There is also Investigator Si Zhemao; he has carried out missions in both Yangcheng and Hucheng before, so they should both know people there.\"","During the last spy-catching operation, Guan Wenjun had benefited from Qin Yuanzheng's efforts, so if he asked for a favor this time, Guan Wenjun definitely would not refuse.","Qin Yuanzheng said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Guan Wenjun should be back this month. Having him contact the Provincial Revolutionary Committee in Yangcheng should not be a problem.\"","A major reason why Zhong Mei was sentenced and sent to a labor camp was that she had no background.","At the same time, she also had no money.","Meanwhile, the man she had injured came from a well-off family, and his parents were staff members in certain city departments. It was simply too easy for them to deal with her.","Since Qin Yuanzheng said this, it proved that he would go to Guan Wenjun to handle this matter. With their help, this issue would definitely be resolved without a problem.","Qiao Lanshu finally felt relieved. She said happily, \"Then, Brother Zheng, shall we go to the management department of the labor camp to report this tomorrow? I originally wanted to call the police, but there is no Public Security Bureau here.\"","Qiao Lanshu's idea was good, but if they really waited until tomorrow, it would drag on for too long.","Qin Yuanzheng placed the insulated box in his hand on the table and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Although there is no Public Security Bureau here, there are military troops stationed here. Did you not know? A battalion is stationed here. I know the battalion commander here, and I will go talk to him about it right now. By tomorrow morning, the nature of this case can be determined.\"","Just as Qiao Lanshu had said, that Supervisor Liu had forced Zhong Mei to submit by assigning her hard and tiring work, as well as docking her food rations.","He surely must have done this sort of thing plenty of times before.","A simple investigation would reveal everything.","No one had intervened before, presumably because Supervisor Liu also had a certain level of background.","But Qin Yuanzheng did not care what kind of background he had.","Qiao Lanshu moved out of the doorway with anticipation, looking at Qin Yuanzheng happily and asking, \"Then, Brother Zheng, are you going out to handle this now?\"","Qin Yuanzheng was speechless.","Qin Yuanzheng ground his teeth in frustration. This wife of his was truly too wicked; she only knew how to make the ox work, but wouldn't let the ox eat its fill.","He pointed a finger at his own cheek and said, \"Give me a kiss, and I will go.\"","Qiao Lanshu immediately found it amusing.","They even had children together, so how were they still acting like they had just started dating?","Qiao Lanshu stood on her tiptoes, cupped his face, and kissed him once on the left and once on the right. Then she kissed him on the lips and whispered, \"Is this enough, Chief Qin?\"","Of course, Qin Yuanzheng felt it wasn't enough.","But now was not the time for marital intimacy.","So he whispered, \"We will save the rest for when we get back.\"","Saying that, he rubbed Qiao Lanshu's head and escorted her to the room next door before turning and striding away.","Qiao Lanshu watched Qin Yuanzheng's figure leave, and only then did she smile and enter the room.","Inside the room, Zhong Mei sat on the edge of the bed, shaking her head with a sigh. \"Tsk, tsk, tsk. So much for 'infertility.' I bet you'll be pregnant with your second child in less than two months.\"","Call that infertility? That was clearly an insatiable sex drive!"]},{"number":189,"title":"Chapter 189: The Man Who Held It In","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu felt a little embarrassed by Zhong Mei's words.","She and Zhong Mei had grown up together, and they used to share absolutely everything with each other.","But now, having Zhong Mei see her acting so affectionate with Qin Yuanzheng still made her feel rather awkward.","Zhong Mei looked at her with a smile, then sighed and said, Knowing that you are doing well makes me feel both relieved and envious.","Zhong Mei added, When I heard you were going to Longcheng to find your husband, I even tried to stop you. I never expected you to have this kind of destiny. It really seems that everything is preordained.","Qiao Lanshu did not have many friends, and Zhong Mei was her best friend. At the time, Zhong Mei had felt that traveling all the way to Longcheng to find a husband was highly unrealistic.","Given Qiao Lanshu's family background, even if she did not want to go down to the countryside, she could have found a job in the city. After all, her father was wealthy, and if they lacked connections, they could just spend money. Many people bought and sold jobs privately.","Qiao Lanshu sat opposite Zhong Mei and placed the thermos on the table. Brother Zheng bought us some food, let's eat a little first.","At the mention of food, Zhong Mei's eyes lit up. Even though she had already eaten a lot of cookies and fried dough twists, knowing there was food made her feel like she could still eat more.","She was truly traumatized by hunger. Growing up, she rarely had regular meals, and after coming here, she went hungry every single day.","She felt like she had developed an eating disorder from the starvation; whenever she saw food, she just wanted to eat it.","The thermos contained four multigrain buns, a small dish of pickled vegetables, a plate of cold wild greens, and two steamed potatoes.","The two young women from Yangcheng sat there, silently munching on the buns.","Qiao Lanshu took a couple of bites of the wild greens and said, I can't believe these are wild greens. I saw so many of them on the mountain road on my way here, but I thought they were just weeds.","Zhong Mei replied, I think these are dandelions. I saw a lot of people digging them up, saying they were edible. It was my first time hearing that too, but I have to say, they don't taste bad at all.","Qiao Lanshu had never eaten dandelions in Longcheng; she had only ever seen articles and sentences describing them in books.","She never expected that dandelions could actually be eaten.","Drinking warm water, the two of them each ate two buns and finished off the pickles and the cold dish.","The two steamed potatoes were left in the thermos.","Zhong Mei patted her stomach, slumped in her chair, and said, Now I am truly full. I don't want to move at all.","As she spoke, she lay her head on the table and fell asleep within seconds.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu had no choice but to help her friend, who was as thin as a rail, over to the heated brick bed. For a long time now, Zhong Mei's nerves had been tightly wound. Her work was grueling, and she didn't even dare to sleep at night, terrified that Supervisor Liu or other male inmates might break into her dormitory.","Now, she could finally get some proper rest.","Qiao Lanshu took a watch out of her pocket and checked the time. It was only eight o'clock in the evening.","Qin Yuanzheng had not returned yet.","She simply tidied up the room a bit and then stayed in the guesthouse to wait for him.","Qin Yuanzheng didn't come back until past ten o'clock at night.","As soon as he returned, he knocked on Qiao Lanshu's door.","Qiao Lanshu quickly got up to open it, asking in a hushed voice, Brother Zheng, did you finish your business?","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. Seeing that the room was pitch black, he asked, Is your friend asleep?","Qiao Lanshu nodded. She went to sleep at eight. She was exhausted.","Qin Yuanzheng smiled and said, Then come over and sleep in the next room with me.","Qiao Lanshu thought about it. Since Zhong Mei was already asleep, even though she still had a lot she wanted to talk about with her, right now she was more eager to know how Qin Yuanzheng's business had gone.","Qiao Lanshu closed Zhong Mei's door and followed Qin Yuanzheng into the adjacent room.","This guesthouse did not have electric lights.","After all, they were in the mountains, and electricity was hard to set up. The guesthouse currently relied entirely on kerosene lamps.","Qin Yuanzheng lit the kerosene lamp first and placed it on the cabinet next to the bed.","Qiao Lanshu sat on the bed, looking at him eagerly. Brother Zheng, how did things go? Hurry up and tell me.","Qin Yuanzheng did not answer her question. Instead, he whispered, Since we have nothing else to do tonight, why don't we go wash up?","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Under the warm yellow light, Qiao Lanshu shot him a reproachful glance and whispered, This is a guesthouse.","Qin Yuanzheng replied, A guesthouse is exactly the right place to get down to business.","Saying that, he scooped Qiao Lanshu up in his arms and walked toward the washroom. It's been months. We finally have a chance to be alone, with no baby crying and no Auntie Shi walking around. It's the perfect time.","From two months before Qiao Lanshu gave birth up until now, with their baby already a few months old, Qin Yuanzheng had indeed been holding back for a very long time.","Previously, his heart ached for Qiao Lanshu, and he wanted her to get plenty of rest to recover her health.","Later, he was worried about the baby, who always cried at night, so he hadn't been in the mood either.","Now that the couple finally had some time to themselves, Qin Yuanzheng found it a bit hard to control himself.","After giving birth, Qiao Lanshu indeed looked even more alluring. Her figure had become fuller and more curvaceous, and every smile and frown she made held a deep attraction for Qin Yuanzheng.","How could Qin Yuanzheng possibly restrain himself?","****","After the two of them finished washing up and got into bed, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't control himself and went all out right from the start.","Normally, Qin Yuanzheng was incredibly tender with Qiao Lanshu, always restraining himself and trying to be as gentle as possible.","After all, he was very strong, and his little wife couldn't handle too much.","If he didn't hold back a little, what if his wife became afraid of doing this in the future?","But this time, Qin Yuanzheng felt it had been far too long, and he also figured that Qiao Lanshu should be able to take it.","So, right from the beginning, Qin Yuanzheng was fierce.","Qiao Lanshu was completely stunned. She was genuinely bewildered, her entire expression frozen, and it took her quite a while to recover.","Qin Yuanzheng stroked her cheek and whispered, Wifey, you've gained a little weight.","Looking at her small, rosy, and slightly chubby face, he thought she was incredibly cute.","He felt that she was even softer to the touch than before.","Pinching Qiao Lanshu's cheek, he murmured, Wifey, why aren't you saying anything?","Qiao Lanshu remained speechless.","After a little while, Qin Yuanzheng spoke again. Wifey, how are you so fair-skinned? It seems that goat's milk wasn't drank in vain. From now on, you and An'an will drink the goat's milk together. You need the extra nutrition too. If one mother goat isn't enough, I'll just go buy another one.","Anyway, they had a yard at home, so there was plenty of space to raise them.","Qin Yuanzheng then remembered that Qiao Lanshu had been away from home for two days and hadn't breastfed the baby. Although her milk supply wasn't abundant to begin with, after two days, she was probably feeling engorged.","He asked in a low voice, You haven't fed the baby for two days. Are you engorged? Are you uncomfortable? You didn't even tell me, I almost forgot.","Actually, Qiao Lanshu had been planning to mention it to Qin Yuanzheng tonight.","She really was feeling quite painfully engorged.","But she just hadn't had the chance to bring it up yet, had she?","Qin Yuanzheng whispered, Let me help you out.","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Ever since they first got married, Qiao Lanshu had known that Qin Yuanzheng was formidable in every way.","Whenever she was intimate with Qin Yuanzheng before, she always felt like she could barely handle it, often feeling wronged and complaining that he wouldn't go easy on her.","But after this time, she finally realized that, before today, Qin Yuanzheng had actually been going easy on her all along.","After all, this time he really didn't hold back; it was too intense, and Qiao Lanshu soon fell into a deep sleep.","But just a few minutes later, she was woken up again by Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng was incredibly strong, and he was just as forceful when he was drinking...","In her daze, Qiao Lanshu thought to herself that this was really too much to handle.","This time, Qin Yuanzheng had finally eaten his fill and no longer compared himself to a tirelessly working old ox.","There was no man in the world happier than him.","He held Qiao Lanshu and pulled the blanket over her as she slept from exhaustion.","By the dim light of the oil lamp, he could see the many marks left on her fair skin.","Qin Yuanzheng's hands started getting restless again.","After giving birth and resting for so long, not only had Qiao Lanshu's skin become much fairer, but her figure had also grown fuller.","She was naturally slim and usually wore many layers, so her figure didn't seem to have changed much on the outside.","But once she took off her clothes and lay next to him, he noticed differences everywhere.","At the very least, she was definitely different from how she was before having a baby.","His innocent little wife had blossomed into a mature woman.","Qiao Lanshu had originally wanted to ask Qin Yuanzheng about Zhong Mei injuring Supervisor Liu.","But Qin Yuanzheng had been holding back for too long, and he tossed her about so much that she simply passed out.","At first, Qin Yuanzheng felt a bit guilty; it seemed he really had been too rough this time.","But he couldn't help it. It had been nearly half a year; he had endured it long enough.","Besides, with his little wife's figure and sensitivity, just a couple of soft whimpers from her were enough to drive him crazy with desire.","Therefore, after Qiao Lanshu fell asleep, Qin Yuanzheng couldn't resist giving her a long massage, and as he massaged her, he started all over again...","Because of this, Qiao Lanshu didn't sleep well for most of the night.","While half-asleep, she still remembered she needed to remind Qin Yuanzheng to be careful...","She didn't want to have a second child so soon.","But she was so exhausted that she didn't even have the strength to speak, only managing to whimper with her eyes closed.","When Qiao Lanshu woke up the next day, it was already eight in the morning.","Qin Yuanzheng had already gotten up early and gone outside to busy himself with who-knows-what.","Aching all over, Qiao Lanshu climbed down from the kang bed, got dressed, washed up, and went next door to knock. To her surprise, Zhong Mei wasn't awake yet either.","Zhong Mei had been too tired lately, so she slept deeply all night and didn't notice the noises coming from the next room.","She was woken up by Qiao Lanshu's knocking. With messy hair and a yawn, she came to open the door.","She looked at Qiao Lanshu standing outside and took a long moment to process before saying, \"Lanshu, when did you go out? Did we sleep in the same room last night?\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu smiled in embarrassment, glanced at Zhong Mei, and said, \"No, I stayed next door last night.\"","Zhong Mei yawned again and said, \"Alright, since you guys are here to visit, can I take a family visitation leave today? I'm going back to sleep for a bit. Otherwise, I won't get any sleep once I have to go to work tomorrow.\"","With that, she turned back, climbed onto the kang bed, pulled the blanket over her head, and went to sleep.","Qiao Lanshu originally wanted to tell her to eat something, but seeing how exhausted she was, she didn't have the heart to say it.","Forget it, let her sleep a bit longer.","After all, sleep is very important too.","It just so happened that Qiao Lanshu was genuinely tired as well.","Qin Yuanzheng had been too intense yesterday and kept at it for a long time.","Feeling a bit sore in her waist and weak in the knees, she went back to her room and lay down.","Before Qin Yuanzheng returned, she closed her eyes and caught up on some sleep.","Qin Yuanzheng came back around nine o'clock.","He was carrying two insulated lunch boxes; this was the breakfast he had bought from the cafeteria.","Inside was sweet potato porridge and wild vegetable buns.","There wasn't much good food in the mountains, and grain was quite scarce.","The food they usually ate was mostly grown by the labor camp prisoners themselves, but the quantities were small and had to be rationed.","It was early summer, and there were many edible wild vegetables and leaves in the mountains. Some of the prisoners were assigned to gather wild vegetables every day.","In addition to digging for wild vegetables, they also had to plow the fields, plant crops, manage orchards, and so on.","Qin Yuanzheng had originally wanted to buy something nice for Qiao Lanshu, like noodles or meat, but the cafeteria didn't have any.","It seemed Qin Yuanzheng had gone to train. He came back wearing only a tank top, his forehead covered in sweat.","He went to the washroom, wiped his body with a wet towel, changed into clean clothes, and then casually washed his sweaty tank top and hung it by the door.","Qiao Lanshu sat up with a yawn, looked at him, and asked, \"Brother Zheng, where did you go?\"","Seeing that Qiao Lanshu was awake, Qin Yuanzheng immediately stuck to her side.","The look in his eyes as he gazed at her couldn't have been gentler.","That's just how men are—as long as you satisfy them in bed, they'll satisfy you in every other way.","Look at him now, Qiao Lanshu didn't even have to ask further. He sat on the kang bed, leaned close to her, and said softly:","\"Wife, your friend's matter has been resolved. After an investigation, it was found that in the 12th labor squad alone, two female comrades were coerced by Supervisor Liu, and one of them even got pregnant. Early this morning, the military arrested Supervisor Liu while he was still in the hospital. He's been sentenced to six years of labor reform.\"","Qiao Lanshu frowned and said, \"To think such scum could come in and be a supervisor. The management here is far too lax.\"","Qin Yuanzheng pulled Qiao Lanshu into his arms, unable to stop his hands from roaming again. He kissed her cheek, acting incredibly clingy.","He whispered, \"This Supervisor Liu was internally recommended; he has a relative in management.\"","However, they couldn't hold his relative accountable. After all, the relative hadn't committed a crime; Supervisor Liu was the one who broke the law.","And many of the supervisors at these labor camps had all sorts of connections.","Qin Yuanzheng added, \"I've also contacted Yangcheng. Guan Wenjun has returned to Longcheng. I told him about this, and he said to leave it to him—he'll have it sorted out in two days. So let's just wait a bit longer.\"","Qin Yuanzheng now felt that coming out to stay at a guesthouse with Qiao Lanshu was quite nice.","Staying a couple more days wouldn't be bad at all.","Thinking of this, his mind started to wander, and he slipped his hand under the covers.","Qiao Lanshu glared at him, pulled his hand out, and whispered, \"I'm still sore, stop messing around.\"","Qin Yuanzheng asked in a low voice, \"Where are you sore? Your waist or your stomach?\"","Qiao Lanshu was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu wrapped the blanket tightly around herself, blinked at Qin Yuanzheng, and said softly, \"Brother Zheng, I'm going to sleep with Meimei tonight. I'm not sleeping with you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"???\"","Qin Yuanzheng frowned, his expression turning a bit dark as he said, \"No way. We are husband and wife. You are my wife, so of course you have to sleep with me.\"","How could she sleep with someone else? Even if it was a woman, it was out of the question."]},{"number":190,"title":"Chapter 190: He'll Be a Little Rascal Too","paragraphs":["Zhong Mei slept until eleven in the morning. As soon as she woke up, she saw Qiao Lanshu bringing her food.","While sitting at the table eating porridge, she felt as if she were dreaming.","It had been a long time since she lived a life with enough sleep and food.","Qiao Lanshu sat next to her and said, \"Brother Zheng said Supervisor Liu has been arrested. He forced himself on many female comrades, and some even got pregnant. The situation is quite severe.\"","Zhong Mei sneered, \"He hasn't been doing this for just a day or two, and no one ever cared. If you hadn't come this time, I'd still be the one getting punished instead of Supervisor Liu.\"","Zhong Mei couldn't help but marvel at her good luck again.","Although she was all alone with no one to rely on, and her luck had never been great, she had a good friend like Qiao Lanshu, who had a brigade commander for a husband.","She felt that if Qin Yuanzheng's rank wasn't high enough, the garrison troops managing the labor camp might not have even bothered with this matter.","Qiao Lanshu breathed a sigh of relief and told Zhong Mei, \"Regardless, this matter has finally come to an end. As long as you're okay, that's what matters. We can't worry about the rest.\"","In this world, where there is light, there is dark; where there is good, there is bad. They could only look out for themselves and couldn't manage everything else.","With Supervisor Liu arrested and sent for labor reform, the incident of Zhong Mei injuring someone was officially classified.","Zhong Mei was forced into it; she was the victim and wouldn't be punished. Moreover, the management office was going to console the persecuted female comrades.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"In less than two days, you should be able to leave here. Brother Zheng asked someone to contact the provincial revolutionary committee in Yangcheng to help investigate your past case. As long as they can prove you were innocent and forced to act in self-defense, your case will be overturned.\"","If she had told Zhong Mei this two days ago, Zhong Mei wouldn't have believed it.","But now, seeing a well-backed man like Supervisor Liu get arrested for labor reform, what was impossible?","As an ordinary person, Zhong Mei finally experienced what it felt like to have a powerful backer!","She said excitedly, \"Really? You asked for someone's help? Wouldn't that mean owing them a favor? Will this affect you and your husband?\"","Military officers feared owing favors the most, as they were hard to repay.","Qiao Lanshu comforted her, \"Don't worry, that person owes Brother Zheng a favor. Plus, he'll probably need Brother Zheng's help later on.\"","Guan Wenjun had made a significant contribution in the mission to capture spies, so his job arrangement was definitely secured.","However, which department he could enter and what position he could hold still depended on connections and networking.","If he wanted to go to the public security bureau, Qin Yuanzheng could certainly help.","It was already the summer of 1976, and the college entrance exams would resume next year. If he didn't secure his job soon, he'd probably be doomed later.","Hearing Qiao Lanshu say this, Zhong Mei felt relieved.","As long as it didn't affect Qin Yuanzheng.","Although she didn't know much, she understood that military officers had many taboos to avoid.","The people from the management office indeed came to console Zhong Mei. They gave her two extra days off and arranged a planting job for her so she wouldn't have to carry rocks anymore.","Her new job was to grow grain and vegetables.","However, Zhong Mei didn't get to take up her new post, because news from Yangcheng arrived very quickly.","Guan Wenjun acted fast. He contacted the revolutionary committee in Yangcheng, explained the situation, and had people investigate.","In this era, as long as someone was willing and dared to take charge, there was nothing that couldn't be resolved.","A man and a woman went on a blind date, the man got beaten by the woman, and the woman was sent to a labor camp—this case was quite famous locally.","It was quickly found out that the man had acted like a hooligan, and the woman had only fought back in self-defense.","In less than a week, all of Zhong Mei's paperwork was completed.","When she and Qiao Lanshu walked out of the labor camp, she was still in disbelief.","Carrying her worn-out luggage, she said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Can I really leave? Is the paperwork really done just like that?\"","Qiao Lanshu held her arm. Qin Yuanzheng led the way ahead, accompanied by a man in a military uniform and another in a management uniform. The three men walked in front.","Zhong Mei asked again, \"What about my household registration? What should I do with it?\"","When she came here for labor reform, her household registration had been transferred to the labor camp. Now that she was leaving, what about it?","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"I was thinking, why don't you go to Longcheng first? Settle down there, find a job, and then slowly figure out a way to transfer your household registration to Longcheng.\"","Hearing this, Zhong Mei instantly understood what she meant.","If her household registration was transferred back to her hometown, she would have to return there eventually, and she might be forced into an arranged marriage again.","She nodded. \"Okay, I'll listen to you! Maybe I can get married in Longcheng and secure my household registration through marriage? That would save a lot of trouble.\"","Zhong Mei never used to have any thoughts about marriage.","Because of her childhood experiences, she felt that men were no good.","But after spending a week with Qiao Lanshu and her husband, she suddenly felt that some men were actually quite nice; the key was to choose carefully.","If she could find a capable man with a job, she could solve not only her household registration issue but also her housing and employment problems.","After all, many state-owned factories employed family members. If she could enter a factory as a family worker, wouldn't that be perfect?","Even her future children could grow up, attend kindergarten, and study in the factory's compound.","That way, they would be much happier than she was as a child.","She didn't want her children to suffer the same hardships she did when she was young.","Thinking of this, Zhong Mei immediately said, \"I've made up my mind! I'm going to Longcheng to find a man with a job and start a family.\"","Lowering her voice, she asked Qiao Lanshu, \"Am I asking for too much? With my conditions, will it be hard to find someone?\"","Men in the city with decent jobs were quite picky when looking for a partner.","She had no household registration, no job, and no support from her maiden family.","Plus, she had been in a labor camp. She felt that she would either have to marry into a rural village or find a man who also worked as a temporary laborer.","If that was the case, she felt it would be better not to marry at all and just live alone.","Qiao Lanshu comforted her in a low voice, \"Fate is determined by heaven. Who knows, there might just be a man destined for you. Look at me when I first went to Longcheng—I was engaged to someone else, I had no job, and I wasn't a local. But didn't I still find Brother Zheng? That's fate, and you will have yours too.\"","Hearing her say this, Zhong Mei felt hopeful again.","She tidied her dry hair and said with a hint of frustration, \"You're different. You're so beautiful. Even back in school, many male classmates liked you.\"","Zhong Mei and Qiao Lanshu grew up together. Qiao Lanshu had always been beautiful, and all the boys around them liked her, but no one liked Zhong Mei.","Of course, Zhong Mei wasn't jealous of Qiao Lanshu; she wasn't that petty.","She was too busy working odd jobs to earn her food money to even think about such things.","Qiao Lanshu then said, \"Don't sell yourself short, you're very pretty too.\"","It was just that long periods of exhaustion had made her very thin, and the sun had tanned her skin. Coupled with malnutrition, her hair had turned slightly yellow.","Qiao Lanshu squeezed Zhong Mei's fingers, looking at the tiny scars on her rough hands, and added, \"Come rest and recuperate at my house first. In less than two months, you'll be gorgeous.\"","Zhong Mei lowered her voice and said, \"Me, staying at your house? Is that really appropriate? What about him?\"","As she spoke, Zhong Mei gestured with her eyes toward Qin Yuanzheng, who was up ahead.","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice and whispered, \"I'll talk it over with him and have him stay at the mining area's military dorms. He'll agree.\"","Qiao Lanshu was lying; Qin Yuanzheng would never agree.","So, Qiao Lanshu figured that once they got back, she would satisfy Qin Yuanzheng thoroughly, and then, while in his arms, use a mix of coercion and coaxing to kick him out to the military dorms.","She knew Qin Yuanzheng very well. He might look intimidating normally, but he was incredibly easy to coax in bed and always had a soft spot for her.","Zhong Mei couldn't shake the feeling that Qin Yuanzheng wasn't that easy to negotiate with.","But right now, she had truly hit a dead end and could only rely on Qiao Lanshu.","Otherwise, she had nowhere else to go.","After chatting with those two comrades for a while, Qin Yuanzheng patted their shoulders one by one and bid them farewell.","Then, Qin Yuanzheng led Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei along the mountain path to the outside. His car was still parked under a large tree by the fork in the road.","Qin Yuanzheng brushed the fallen leaves off the roof of the car and said, \"Let's go, get in.\"","So, Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei both got into the back seat together.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng shot Qiao Lanshu a glance but said nothing. He opened the driver's side door and silently drove the car out.","Zhong Mei felt that Qin Yuanzheng seemed a bit unhappy.","She lowered her voice and said to Qiao Lanshu in their local dialect, \"Your man doesn't seem very happy. Does he always have such a dark face?\"","She then added, \"He's so fierce. Are all men in high positions like this?\"","It seemed that marrying a military officer wasn't all that great; only someone with a soft personality like Qiao Lanshu could be a good match.","If it were her, she wouldn't be able to stand someone giving her attitude every day.","They would probably end up fighting.","Qiao Lanshu chuckled softly and said, \"He's not usually like this. I guess he's just being a bit serious because he has to drive.\"","As she spoke, both of them sneakily peeked at Qin Yuanzheng.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng drove expressionlessly, listening to the two of them whispering in their local dialect. He had no idea what they were talking about and couldn't understand a single word.","He sighed silently in his heart.","After driving the car into the city, Qin Yuanzheng returned the vehicle.","He then took the two of them to the train station and bought two soft sleeper tickets and one hard sleeper ticket.","As a military officer, he could buy soft sleeper tickets for himself and his family members, but since Zhong Mei wasn't family, she couldn't get a soft sleeper ticket.","Therefore, for the return trip, Qin Yuanzheng arranged for the two of them to stay in the soft sleeper cabin. Once he saw that the two opposite berths were occupied by an elderly couple, he felt reassured and went to the hard sleeper cabin himself.","Zhong Mei felt a bit embarrassed about this.","But she had to admit, her impression of Qin Yuanzheng had improved.","She now felt that Qin Yuanzheng was actually a really good guy.","After all, Qin Yuanzheng could have easily made her go to the hard sleeper, but he didn't.","After taking the train for over a dozen hours, they finally made it back to Longcheng.","At this time of year, it was already sweltering in Yangcheng, but it was still quite cool here in Longcheng.","After the sun went down, it was even a bit chilly.","A guard was already waiting at the train station entrance in a car.","Auntie Shi had also already taken the baby back home.","So the three of them didn't go to Yang Wenyan's place and instead headed straight back to the military residential compound.","Zhong Mei looked around the compound, her eyes filled with curiosity.","After all, it was her first time visiting a legendary military compound, and it looked quite impressive.","The two guards at the gate were carrying rifles, looking absolutely imposing.","Seeing this, she almost wanted to marry a soldier too, but she was very clear-headed. She knew her own conditions weren't great, and it was impossible for her to climb high enough to marry an officer.","It would be better to see if she could find a local Longcheng man, at least to solve her household registration issue first.","Once she got out of the car, Qiao Lanshu didn't even pay attention to Qin Yuanzheng. She just grabbed Zhong Mei's arm and ran eagerly toward the house, saying as she ran, \"Zhong Mei, hurry up and come with me to see my baby.\"","Zhong Mei knew Qiao Lanshu had given birth to a son and was also very happy. The two of them rushed excitedly up to the second floor.","Qin Yuanzheng carried Zhong Mei's backpack and followed behind them, expressionless.","He actually missed the little rascal at home very much too, but being ignored by his wife made him feel quite miserable.","Auntie Shi knew they were coming back today and would be having dinner, so she had steamed buns early on, made wild shepherd's purse dumplings, and cooked sweet potato porridge.","By the time they returned, Auntie Shi was holding the baby and feeding him milk.","Qiao Lanshu introduced Auntie Shi and Zhong Mei to each other, then quickly went to change out of her dirty clothes. After washing her hands, she hurried over and took the baby into her arms. An'an was almost three months old and was growing cuter by the day.","His little face was chubby, he had double eyelids, his skin was very fair, and he even had dimples when he smiled.","Zhong Mei leaned in to look and whispered, \"An'an looks like you, so beautiful.\"","An'an seemed to know that his mommy was back. As soon as he was in Qiao Lanshu's arms, he started giggling, waved his two little hands, and then grabbed a strand of Qiao Lanshu's hair, refusing to let go for dear life.","Holding the baby bottle, Qiao Lanshu said softly, \"You haven't seen Mommy for seven or eight days. Did An'an miss Mommy?\"","Whether An'an understood or not, he just held onto her hair and laughed. He looked exactly like a miniature version of Qiao Lanshu.","An'an was clearly delighted. He clung to Qiao Lanshu without letting go, waving his arms and kicking his little legs joyfully.","Qin Yuanzheng walked over, held down his two legs with one hand, and pretended to be fierce as he said, \"Don't kick Mommy.\"","An'an smelled Qin Yuanzheng's scent, wrinkled his nose, and seemed to make a look of disgust before snuggling closer into his mommy's embrace.","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Auntie Shi stood to the side holding a small towel, wiping the drool from the corner of An'an's mouth. She coughed softly and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Um, Chief Qin, it's been a long and tiring journey back. How about you go take a shower first? I just boiled some hot water.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: ...","Qin Yuanzheng sniffed himself and realized he did indeed reek of sweat.","It couldn't be helped. The hard sleeper on the train was very crowded and hot, with people constantly jostling around. Even he thought he smelled bad.","He had no choice but to say, \"Alright then, I'll go take a shower first.\"","The little brat was going to grow up into a stinky boy himself one day, yet here he was, actually having the nerve to think his old man stank."]},{"number":191,"title":"Chapter 191: Snatching Jobs","paragraphs":["Zhong Mei came to stay temporarily at Qiao Lanshu's house, making it inconvenient for Qin Yuanzheng to stay at home.","Originally, Qiao Lanshu had wanted to coax Qin Yuanzheng a bit, afraid that he might be unhappy.","But she was so happy after returning home that she couldn't bear to let go of An'an once she held him, and was busy teasing and playing with An'an alongside Zhong Mei.","When Qin Yuanzheng came out after taking a shower and saw them like this, he knew that his little wife, now having a child and her best friend, had completely forgotten about him, her husband.","Qin Yuanzheng felt a brief moment of nostalgia for the private world he and Qiao Lanshu once shared.","Then, he greeted Auntie Shi and prepared to head out.","Auntie Shi quickly called out to stop him, saying, Commander Qin, you haven't eaten yet, have you? Have a meal before you go.","Qin Yuanzheng then remembered that he hadn't had dinner yet. He nodded, followed Auntie Shi into the kitchen, packed a lunchbox full of wild shepherd's purse dumplings, and took it with him.","He did indeed have matters to attend to by going out late at night this time.","Having been away from the mining area for seven or eight days, he needed to go back and take a look around to see if anything had happened.","Also, Guan Wenjun had been back for several days, and he needed to go talk to him about the previous spy case.","More importantly, he had to take another trip tomorrow, driving to the public security bureau in the neighboring city to pick up the child they had rescued on the train earlier.","Once Qin Yuanzheng left, Zhong Mei, who had been cautious and tense the whole time, instantly relaxed.","She patted her chest, feeling that Qin Yuanzheng's imposing aura was rather intimidating, which made her a bit nervous.","Qiao Lanshu stood up holding An'an and said to Zhong Mei, Brother Zheng went out to handle some business. He said he'll be gone for two days to do some things in the neighboring city. For these few days, you can sleep with Auntie Shi.","Originally, Qiao Lanshu wanted to sleep with Zhong Mei, but the bed she currently slept in was, after all, shared with Qin Yuanzheng, so it wouldn't be appropriate to have Zhong Mei sleep there too.","It just so happened that An'an only needed to drink milk once in the middle of the night now, so she didn't need Auntie Shi to get up at night; she could just sleep with An'an herself.","Zhong Mei always felt that she was causing trouble for Qiao Lanshu, so she said in a low voice, Lanshu, don't worry, I won't bother you for long. Once I get familiar with Longcheng tomorrow, I'll figure out a way to make some money.","When she said figuring out a way to make money, it definitely meant doing some small-scale speculative business, just as she had done in Longcheng.","Qiao Lanshu quickly stopped her, saying, Meimei, you don't need to rush right now. Just stay at home for these few days, and I'll handle the job situation for you.","Qiao Lanshu was preparing to resign and study for her exams, so she wanted Zhong Mei to go work at the food factory.","However, Zhong Mei's household registration was currently over at the labor camp, classifying her as a non-local rural resident. If she wanted to work here, she could only work as a temporary worker.","In fact, even if Zhong Mei had an urban household registration, she would still have to start as a temporary worker.","Qiao Lanshu had no way to transfer her job to her; after all, Zhong Mei wasn't her relative and couldn't even be considered a family worker.","With Zhong Mei's job on her mind, and since her own leave had coincidentally come to an end, Qiao Lanshu reported for duty at the food factory after staying at home for two days.","...","The people at the food factory who were on good terms with her all came to the warehouse to look for her once they knew she was back at work.","Deng Weijun came by once and brought her a peach.","A short while later, Wang Xue also arrived.","It was still early, and everyone had just started their shifts. Wang Xue was holding a scallion pancake in her hand, strolling over as she ate.","The summer morning was still somewhat cool, but Qiao Lanshu had already opened all the doors and windows for ventilation.","She noticed some other people's belongings on the desk and shelves in the small warehouse.","These belonged to another colleague who had come to cover her position while she was on maternity leave.","Wang Xue walked to the door and called out to her while eating the scallion pancake, Xiao Qiao, I heard you started working again?","Qiao Lanshu was checking her own things in the drawer. Hearing Wang Xue call her, she smiled and walked to the door. Sister, you're here too. Weijun just left. Look, he even brought me a peach.","Wang Xue smiled and said, That young man really knows how to treat people. He gave me one too.","In the past, Deng Weijun would occasionally bring Qiao Lanshu something to eat.","Ever since he married Wang Haitang, whenever he had something delicious, he had also started bringing some to Wang Xue.","Wang Xue stepped into the room and asked Qiao Lanshu in a lowered voice, Xiao Qiao, how come I'm hearing that you're going to resign and quit?","Qiao Lanshu looked a bit surprised. She did indeed have this intention, but she hadn't told anyone else.","She asked in surprise, Sister, who did you hear that from?","Wang Xue pointed inside with her chin and said, From Tian Hemei, of course.","Qiao Lanshu then asked, Who is Tian Hemei?","She had never heard of this person before.","Wang Xue lowered her voice and said, A family worker who hasn't become a regular employee yet. Her husband is a technician in the pickled vegetable workshop. When you were on maternity leave, she happened to get sick and claimed her body was too weak to do heavy labor. So her husband talked to the factory manager and had her cover your position to oversee the warehouse.","Watching the warehouse was a very easy job, and it came with an independent little wooden cabin. With no squad leaders or supervisors directly managing them, who wouldn't want to be a warehouse keeper?","Generally speaking, the warehouse keeper position would be assigned to pregnant women, older employees, or workers in poor health.","However, Qiao Lanshu had originally merited the position because she made a contribution during the fried dough twist embezzlement incident. Combined with the fact that she standardized the warehouse's entry and exit management, Yang Wenyan took the opportunity to transfer her to the warehouse keeper position.","Plus, not long after she started working in the warehouse, she got pregnant, so the workers at the food factory didn't even have time to raise any objections.","Now that Qiao Lanshu had returned after giving birth, Tian Hemei, who was covering her post, was probably worried about losing this job.","So she was going around telling people that Qiao Lanshu was going to resign?","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, I don't even know her. Where did she get the idea that I'm resigning?","Qiao Lanshu was indeed planning to resign, but being schemed against like this still made her a bit unhappy.","Wang Xue finished the scallion pancake in her hand in a few bites and then said, She probably guessed it while chatting with others. Everyone is saying that since you gave birth to a son for Brigade Commander Qin, your status is secure. You can just go home and enjoy your life as an officer's wife without needing to work anymore. They also say that Brigade Commander Qin's work is too busy, so you have to go home and watch the child, and you definitely won't have time to work.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Although what everyone said was indeed true, she still felt a little uncomfortable in her heart.","Wang Xue nudged Qiao Lanshu with her arm and said in a hushed voice,","Tian Hemei just wants to be lazy. After the beginning of spring, the pickled vegetable workshop gets busy. She doesn't want to go back to work and just wants to hang around here, claiming she's in poor health. From what I see, she eats more than I do every day, and her voice is full of energy. She doesn't have a damn illness... I'll stop talking, she's here, and I need to get going. Just ignore her. If anything happens, go find the factory manager, you hear?","With that, Wang Xue turned around and left.","Qiao Lanshu walked her to the door. When she looked up, she indeed saw a rather tall and sturdy woman in her thirties or forties walking toward the warehouse.","The woman was wearing the food factory's work uniform and carrying a vegetable basket in her hand.","This woman was Tian Hemei.","She knew Qiao Lanshu had come to work and saw her standing at the door of the wooden cabin. Her expression was somewhat unsightly.","During the few months she had been filling in here, life had been incredibly comfortable.","Her salary and subsidies were the same as before, but she did not have to work hard, did not have to curry favor with the team leader and supervisor, and did not have to deal with various exams and spot checks.","She really did not want to be transferred away from the warehouse.","But there were also many people who envied and were jealous of her. Over the past two months, many people would occasionally come up to her and remind her that the warehouse keeper, Qiao Lanshu, was coming back to work soon. Once Qiao Lanshu returned, she would have to go back to the pickle workshop to wash and pickle vegetables, and carry heavy pickle jars.","Tian Hemei felt very uncomfortable about this.","She walked up to the warehouse, glanced at Qiao Lanshu, and then smiled, saying, Oh my, you must be Xiao Qiao, right? Back to work today?","Qiao Lanshu looked her up and down, smiling as she nodded. Yes, my maternity leave has been long enough. It is time to come back to work.","Tian Hemei carried her vegetable basket into the wooden cabin. There was only one chair and one desk inside. As soon as she entered, she placed the basket on the desk, plopped down heavily onto the chair, and took the work logbook from the drawer to read.","Qiao Lanshu stood to the side, watching her behavior, and slightly raised an eyebrow.","She did not know what Tian Hemei meant by this. Was she deliberately trying to assert dominance?","But she only found it amusing.","Sensing her gaze, Tian Hemei coughed, put down the notebook in her hand, and explained to Qiao Lanshu, Lately, the inbound and outbound warehouse procedures have gotten a bit complicated. I am afraid you will not understand them, so it is better if I just handle it. You do not need to worry about any of this.","The main job of managing the warehouse was handling inbound and outbound goods, as well as inventory checks and verifications.","If she was not going to let Qiao Lanshu handle these things, did that mean she had no intention of handing over the work to her?","Qiao Lanshu nodded thoughtfully and said, Alright, if there is anything you need me to do, just let me know.","With that, she walked to the innermost part of the cabin, where there was a wooden plank bed.","Qiao Lanshu sat on the bed, picked up a stack of newspapers, and started reading.","Tian Hemei looked at her calm demeanor and felt a bit uncertain. What was the deal with this Qiao Lanshu?","No matter what, the food factory only had one warehouse keeper position.","Between the two of them, one would definitely have to leave.","Was Qiao Lanshu not nervous at all?"]},{"number":192,"title":"Chapter 192: How old is this friend of yours","paragraphs":["Qiao Lanshu, of course, was not nervous. After all, she was a formal employee, and she had planned to resign anyway.","The reason she didn't show it was simply that she didn't want Tian Hemei to celebrate too early.","After all, Tian Hemei didn't look like a sick person at all. There was no need to yield to her on this matter.","Tian Hemei was indeed terrified of losing this position, so she worked incredibly hard all day, not letting Qiao Lanshu lift a finger.","She bustled about all by herself, and when chatting with other colleagues, she subtly hinted at how proactive she was and how beautifully she completed her tasks. Unlike Qiao Lanshu, who just lay inside sleeping on her first day back—how could that be acceptable?","The first three days of Qiao Lanshu's return to work were actually meant for handing over tasks with Tian Hemei. As for which of them would be transferred, the HR department hadn't issued a notice yet, so it remained uncertain.","Normally speaking, however, the one to be transferred would definitely be Tian Hemei.","Therefore, Tian Hemei had been trying her best these past few days to find a way and pull strings to stay in the warehouse.","Unfortunately, when she asked the HR staff, they stated that things had to be done according to standard procedures.","When Tian Hemei asked what the standard procedures were,","HR's reply was to have her quickly hand over the work to Qiao Lanshu. In three days, Tian Hemei was to return to the pickle workshop to cut vegetables. Now that summer was approaching, the pickle workshop was extremely busy. They were short on female workers for chopping vegetables; making pickles every day would leave one's hands covered in calluses!","Tian Hemei went back and discussed it with her technician husband, only to realize that relying solely on connections, she definitely couldn't beat Qiao Lanshu.","After all, the factory manager was Qiao Lanshu's cousin. Everyone knew this.","If it were purely about connections, whose could be stronger than Qiao Lanshu's?","Thus, Tian Hemei figured she had to find a fault at work, make Qiao Lanshu make a mistake, and then use that opportunity to get Qiao Lanshu transferred away.","So the next day, after lunch, when it was time for the afternoon shift, Tian Hemei deliberately made an excuse and arrived half an hour late.","Right at that moment, the staff from the logistics and finance departments responsible for warehouse inventory and stock verification came to Qiao Lanshu with a form: Comrade Xiao Qiao, is Tian Hemei not here?","Qiao Lanshu was sitting on the wooden bed furthest inside, reading a newspaper.","She hadn't brought any books with her these past few days, afraid someone might report her for reading during work hours.","Having nothing else to do, she read newspapers every day, finishing a thick stack of them that she had missed recently.","Hearing the voices, she stood up, walked to the door, and said, Comrade Tian Hemei hasn't returned since lunch. Do you need her for something?","The logistics and finance staff came over with the inventory form and said to Qiao Lanshu, This is the confirmation sheet for our warehouse inventory, which requires the signature of a warehouse keeper. Since you're here, why don't you sign it first? This form needs to be submitted this afternoon.","The warehouse required regular inventory checks; Qiao Lanshu knew this.","However, when Qiao Lanshu used to work here, she always personally followed up on the inventory. She knew exactly where each item was placed, what was stocked, and how much inventory was left.","Therefore, back then, she would definitely sign the forms for the inventory she had personally checked.","But now, she hadn't followed up on this form. Although she could sign it, there was no need to.","Besides, she didn't trust Tian Hemei's character.","Ever since Qiao Lanshu returned to work, Tian Hemei had been very proactive, never arriving late or leaving early.","But today she was dragging her feet. Who knew what she was plotting?","Smiling, Qiao Lanshu said to the finance colleague, I'm sorry, I can't sign this. Although I've started work, Comrade Tian Hemei hasn't handed over the tasks to me yet. To ensure the work goes smoothly and accountability is clear, I cannot sign on her behalf.","Saying that, she walked out of the small wooden cabin and told the two of them, How about this: you wait here for a bit. She'll probably be back soon. I need to go talk to the factory manager about something, so I'll be leaving for a while.","With that, Qiao Lanshu left.","The two comrades held the form and exchanged a glance. What else could they do?","One of them could only wait for Tian Hemei to return, while the other hurried off to look for her.","Tian Hemei had assumed Qiao Lanshu would sign it for her because the form was urgent and had to be submitted that afternoon.","As a result, when she slowly sauntered back to the warehouse, she found that Qiao Lanshu wasn't at her post at all.","Meanwhile, the finance comrade was already fuming. Catching sight of her, she scolded her for quite a while:","Comrade Tian Hemei, during working hours, you should stick to your post! It's been almost an hour, where on earth did you go? Are we going to get any work done or not? Do you expect all departments to revolve around you? You know this inventory work has strict requirements and the accounting must be completed by tomorrow! The form still hasn't been submitted. Are you trying to get me in trouble?","Tian Hemei was merely a family worker, not a formal employee, and could be fired at any time.","The finance comrade wasn't holding back at all while reprimanding her.","There was no helping it; this inventory check was primarily the responsibility of the finance department. If the work wasn't completed on time, they would have their work points deducted.","Feeling nervous, Tian Hemei stammered, Oh, I... I just had something to do...","The finance comrade said sternly, During working hours, staying at your post is your most important duty! Stop talking nonsense and sign this right now!","Tian Hemei: ...","Trying to shirk responsibility, Tian Hemei said, While it's true I should stay at my post, I only left for so long because there was someone else in the same position here. If you were in such a hurry, you should have just asked Qiao Lanshu to sign it for you. Why are you being so fierce?","The finance staff also wanted Qiao Lanshu to sign it, but given what Qiao Lanshu had said, she couldn't exactly put a knife to her neck and force her to sign, could she?","After all, Qiao Lanshu wasn't the one who handled this particular warehouse inventory.","Last year, whenever Qiao Lanshu was in charge of the inventory, the finance staff never had to rush her. She would sign the forms early on and deliver them herself.","She never waited for them to come and press her for it.","The finance staff truly had no time to argue with Tian Hemei anymore.","She tapped the form and urged her, Look at the time, what are you still arguing about? Hurry up and sign.","Tian Hemei: ...","Tian Hemei didn't dare to sign.","She couldn't sign it either. She had deliberately made a small mistake on this form during the inventory check.","The finance department would discover it when they did the accounting.","She had changed the data for one of the items from 11 to 1.","It looked like a casual slip of the pen, but on the financial side, it would result in a loss amounting to hundreds of yuan.","This was no minor error.","After hesitating for a moment, Tian Hemei quickly said, I forgot to double-check it. I'll go verify it one more time, and if there are no problems, I'll sign it for you.","Saying that, she grabbed the form and was about to head into the warehouse to check again.","The finance staff was absolutely furious.","What time was it already?","Where was the time for Tian Hemei to double-check?","She snatched the document back and said angrily, These are the inventory counts you did, what more is there to review? If you won't sign, a fingerprint will do. I don't have time to argue with you here.","Saying that, she grabbed an inkpad, grabbed Tian Hemei's hand, pressed a red fingerprint onto the paper, and then aggressively ran off with the document.","Tian Hemei was speechless.","Panic set in for Tian Hemei, and she quickly chased after her, shouting, Hey, I didn't sign it! A fingerprint doesn't count!","Of course, a fingerprint definitely counted.","After all, in this day and age, many of the deliverymen, porters, and security guards working under the food factory were illiterate.","Sometimes, when a signature was required, they opted for a fingerprint instead, which was convenient, quick, and saved time.","How was Tian Hemei supposed to know the finance department would pull such a trick?","She regretted it to death. If she had known earlier, she wouldn't have tried to pull these stunts.","Meanwhile, Qiao Lanshu went to the factory manager's office. She had already somewhat guessed what had happened with Tian Hemei.","Since she hadn't signed, the finance department would definitely seek her out for a signature. Tian Hemei had probably made a minor mistake.","It was harmless overall, but the impact wasn't great.","Furthermore, she was a dependent worker. This time, she might get fired or possibly demoted to a temporary worker, but her chances of becoming a permanent employee were likely gone.","Qiao Lanshu shook her head and sighed.","Tian Hemei was just too impatient. Qiao Lanshu had indeed been planning to resign and leave, so Tian Hemei wouldn't have had to do anything and still could have stayed at the warehouse.","But now, she probably wouldn't be able to keep her job.","When Yang Wenyan saw Qiao Lanshu come in, he smiled and said, I heard from Yuanzheng that you're planning to resign? Have you thought it through? Jobs aren't easy to find these days.","For a military spouse like Qiao Lanshu, finding a job was actually quite easy; what was difficult was finding a relaxing job that also allowed her to take care of her family.","Being a warehouse manager at the food factory was a great gig!","Yang Wenyan added, Why don't you think about it some more?","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. No, Manager, I've still decided to resign.","If she hadn't known that the college entrance examination would be reinstated next year, she would have continued working as a warehouse manager here.","But since she knew, she absolutely had to take the exam.","She had studied from primary school through high school, spending over a decade in education, and she truly loved reading.","She wanted to test into a university, become an honorable college student, learn more knowledge, and experience a broader world.","Moreover, Qin Yuanzheng was continuously moving up in the ranks. He would be a division commander in the future, and perhaps, when he was old enough, he could climb even higher.","When that time came, she hoped to have her own career achievements, at least enough to match him.","She didn't want to be a dependent dodder flower who could only rely on a man.","Hearing Qiao Lanshu's words, Yang Wenyan nodded and said, Alright then. Fill out a resignation application, give it to me to sign first, and then take it to the personnel department.","After all, Qiao Lanshu had been recommended by Yang Wenyan, so upon her departure, she needed his signature as the factory manager.","Qiao Lanshu nodded. She didn't mention Tian Hemei's situation, but instead brought up another matter. By the way, Manager, I have a friend I'd like to recommend as a temporary worker. Would that be okay?","Qiao Lanshu explained Zhong Mei's situation to Yang Wenyan.","Yang Wenyan was silent for a couple of seconds before replying, Although she went to a labor camp, since her case has been overturned and cleared, it's fine. It just so happens we are busy this summer and have a quota for temporary workers. Bring her to the personnel department to report for duty tomorrow.","Qiao Lanshu's eyes instantly lit up. She smiled and thanked Yang Wenyan before leaving the factory manager's office.","Upon returning, she didn't see Tian Hemei, so she filled out the form herself, handed it in to the personnel department, and as soon as it was time, she immediately got off work and went home.","As for Tian Hemei, she was currently in the finance department's office, arguing with the staff over the data error.","Qiao Lanshu returned home a little after five o'clock, planning to tell Zhong Mei about the job.","Even though it was only a temporary position with a low salary and no housing benefits, at least having a job meant her daily meals were secured, which would allow her to gain a foothold here.","As for future plans, they could take their time figuring that out.","However, when Qiao Lanshu got home, she only saw Auntie Shi and An'an; Zhong Mei was not there.","Surprised, Qiao Lanshu asked Auntie Shi, Where did Zhong Mei go?","An'an was on the sofa playing with a stuffed doll Auntie Shi had sewn, while Auntie Shi was mopping the floor. She replied, That girl Zhong Mei went out this morning. She said she wanted to familiarize herself with the surroundings outside. I was looking after the child and couldn't go with her, but she said she'd be back before dark.","It was only past five o'clock, and the summer days were long; the sun hadn't even set yet.","Qiao Lanshu picked up An'an, teased him a bit, and said helplessly, She's just like that, lacking a sense of security. No matter where she goes, she has to wander around and check things out, saying it's so she can run away if she encounters danger.","Auntie Shi found this amusing.","She tentatively asked Qiao Lanshu, By the way, Xiao Qiao, how old is this friend of yours? She looks quite young, not even as old as my second child.","Auntie Shi had three children: her eldest son was 20, her youngest son was 18, and she also had a daughter who was fifteen or sixteen.","By asking this, Auntie Shi had likely taken a liking to Zhong Mei and wanted to introduce her to her son.","Qiao Lanshu felt it was inappropriate.","As for why it was inappropriate, it was a long story.","It wasn't that Auntie Shi was a bad person; in fact, Auntie Shi was very good, which was why she and Qin Yuanzheng were planning to raise her salary and employ her until An'an was three years old.","Pretending not to understand Auntie Shi's underlying meaning, Qiao Lanshu let out a soft sigh and said, Meimei, she's the same age as me. But don't let her young age fool you; when she was little, she used to fight with the boys all the time. She's much tougher than I am.","The details about Zhong Mei were kept secret by Qiao Lanshu and the others; after all, for the sake of Zhong Mei's reputation, these things were better left unsaid.","They hadn't even told Auntie Shi, only briefly mentioning that she had been framed and almost sent to a labor camp.","So Auntie Shi didn't know the full story.","But now, hearing this, she completely forgot about mopping the floor. Looking shocked, she said, Ah? She fought with boys when she was little? She's that fierce?","Holding An'an, Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, Yes, she's the eldest child in her family, with three younger siblings below her. As the eldest sister, she had to be tough. Look at my cousin-in-law, isn't she really fierce too?","Auntie Shi was speechless.","Thinking of Deng Xiaozhen, Auntie Shi gave an awkward smile and didn't continue the topic about Zhong Mei.","Fighting with men, and being as fierce as Deng Xiaozhen...","Auntie Shi automatically placed herself in the role of a mother-in-law, worrying that if her son really got together with Zhong Mei, he might end up getting beaten by her every day.","As a mother-in-law, she would also be completely suppressed by Zhong Mei.","She definitely wouldn't be able to handle that."]},{"number":193,"title":"Chapter 193: Director of the Women's Federation","paragraphs":["Qin Yuanzheng drove to the neighboring city and brought the little boy he had previously rescued on the train back to Longcheng.","The child had stayed with the chief of the public security bureau in the neighboring city for a few days. Seeing Qin Yuanzheng now, he actually didn't want to leave with him.","The bureau chief whispered to Qin Yuanzheng, \"What exactly is this kid's background? He can really eat! He's only three years old, but he eats more than my ten-year-old. I was afraid he'd burst. He's incredibly wild, too. When he saw the pond outside, he got down on his stomach to drink from it, just like a cow...\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","The chief continued to complain: \"He runs outside every single day. Don't let his short legs fool you; he runs incredibly fast and even knows how to hide from people. He's been here for less than a week and has gotten lost three times. He practically gave me a heart attack. Comrade Qin, if you hadn't come to pick him up, I was ready to send him to the orphanage.\"","Hearing this, Qin Yuanzheng could already imagine just how difficult this child was to handle.","So, after grabbing the child and putting him in the car, Qin Yuanzheng thought about it on the drive back to Longcheng and decided it would be best to hand the kid over to the Women's Federation. He didn't want to get involved in this mess.","As soon as they arrived in Longcheng, Qin Yuanzheng headed straight for the Women's Federation office.","The current director of the Longcheng Women's Federation was a woman named Zheng Wenhui, who had been transferred up from a subordinate county last year. Qin Yuanzheng wasn't very familiar with the Women's Federation, but since women and children fell under their jurisdiction, he figured sending this abducted child to them and then filing a report at the police station would be the end of it.","Qin Yuanzheng parked the car by the side of the road, opened the back door, and took a look inside.","The little boy, whom a certain bureau chief had described as being like a cow, was currently fast asleep on his stomach on the seat, his mouth slightly open and drool covering half his face.","He had eaten all the small pastries bought for him on the road, his water bottle had fallen to the floor, and the seat was covered in crumbs.","Qin Yuanzheng sighed silently.","He simply picked the child up, closed the car door, and strode toward the Women's Federation office.","The child was woken up by the movement. He groggily opened his eyes and, realizing he was in yet another new place, widened his eyes in curiosity and looked around.","Only then did Qin Yuanzheng ask him, \"Niuwa, where are you from?\"","Niuwa's real name wasn't actually Niuwa. He claimed his name was Haye.","People around him listened for a long time but had no idea what a Haye was supposed to mean. It didn't roll off the tongue easily, and if they called him by the wrong name, Niuwa would get angry. Once he got angry, he would run off and disappear again.","So Qin Yuanzheng simply didn't humor him and called him Niuwa outright.","Niuwa looked at Qin Yuanzheng with his dark eyes, a hint of grievance and stubbornness in his gaze.","And then, his short little legs started kicking wildly again; it looked like he was getting ready to make another run for it.","However, being such a tiny person, he hardly had any strength.","Held tightly in Qin Yuanzheng's arms, no matter how much his legs kicked, it was useless.","Niuwa hollered for a long time, yelling at Qin Yuanzheng, \"Let me go! You bastard!\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"???\"","Qin Yuanzheng pointed a finger at him. \"I'm the one who rescued you, and what are you calling me?\"","Niuwa, fearing neither heaven nor earth, glared at him and started yelling again: \"Bastard, bastard, bastard, bastard!\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng took a deep breath, telling himself not to stoop to a child's level.","At first glance, this child clearly came from a well-educated family.","He must have picked up this kind of cursing while wandering the streets recently.","He endured it.","Niuwa: \"Jerk, bullshit, bullshit, bullshit, bullshit!\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng's footsteps paused. The next second, he pressed Niuwa face down and gave him three firm smacks on the bottom.","Niuwa, perhaps used to being spanked, actually looked up at Qin Yuanzheng with a confused expression.","Then, he patted his bottom with his small hand, laughed out loud, and mocked Qin Yuanzheng: \"Loser, you can't even hit hard!\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qin Yuanzheng took another deep breath, pointed at Niuwa, and said, \"Just wait a few more years. You just wait.\"","Niuwa wasn't intimidated in the slightest, after all, he didn't understand what those words meant.","Tucked under Qin Yuanzheng's arm, his legs still kicking wildly and mischievously, he kept muttering, \"Doesn't hurt... loser...\"","Qin Yuanzheng endured it, pretending he hadn't heard a thing.","He arrived at the Women's Federation office just as several comrades were sitting at their desks.","Most of them didn't know Qin Yuanzheng, but the director, Zheng Wenhui, did.","Zheng Wenhui was wearing a white Dacron shirt, black trousers, and a pair of black leather shoes. She looked like she came from a good family and had a refined demeanor.","She stood up, looked at Qin Yuanzheng, and then looked at the child tucked under his arm. A strange look flashed through her eyes.","She stared at Niuwa for a moment, thinking to herself: Wasn't this child sent away?","How did Qin Yuanzheng find him and bring him all the way to Longcheng?","How did this happen...","Zheng Wenhui lowered her head, concealing the emotions in her eyes. With a slight smile on her face, she walked forward and asked in surprise, \"Comrade Qin, what is this...\"","Qin Yuanzheng set Niuwa down and briefly explained the boy's situation to Zheng Wenhui before saying, \"This kid is probably from here in Longcheng. The public security bureau has already filed a report and will follow up with an investigation. Your office will be in charge of settling him in. Buy him some clothes, food, and daily necessities.\"","He then emphasized once more, \"Try not to send him to the orphanage. He's very restless, and if you send him there, he'll easily wander off and get lost.\"","Hearing this, the people from the Women's Federation grumbled internally.","For an abducted child like this, before their biological parents were found, where else could they be sent if not to the orphanage?","They couldn't possibly take him back to their own homes, could they?","An extra person meant an extra mouth to feed.","Besides, such a young child didn't know any better and would require a lot of effort to watch over. If he got lost, whose fault would it be?","Although everyone usually worked quite actively at the Women's Federation, when faced with this kind of situation, they couldn't help but hesitate.","Qin Yuanzheng discussed the child's situation a bit more with Director Zheng Wenhui. They had barely exchanged a few words when the child suddenly took off running.","Qin Yuanzheng reacted quickly, grabbing him by the collar and glaring at him. \"Where do you think you're running? Didn't I tell you that the aunties here are going to help you find your family?\"","Niuwa said stubbornly, \"I don't want to! You're all bad people, bad people.\"","Zheng Wenhui's gaze darkened slightly. She walked forward with a smile and said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Comrade, how about this? Since this child is so difficult to handle, why don't I take him back to my house for now? I happen to have two kids at home, so he'll have some company.\"","Qin Yuanzheng replied, \"You're the director of the Women's Federation. Just arrange things as you see fit.\"","He was just dropping the kid off; he didn't care what Zheng Wenhui did.","Qin Yuanzheng was still busy, so he turned to leave.","He was truly afraid of this Niuwa, and he certainly didn't have time to look after the kid.","Seeing Qin Yuanzheng leave, Niuwa wanted to run away again. Zheng Wenhui immediately walked over, pulled two White Rabbit candies from her pocket, handed them to Niuwa, and coaxed him softly, \"Come here, Niuwa. Auntie has some candy for you, do you want it?\"","Niuwa looked at the White Rabbit creamy candies. Unlike other children who had never had them before, he didn't drool at the sight of them.","However, he was still a child after all, and he liked eating sweets.","So, he reached out, took the two candies, and stuffed them into his pocket.","Zheng Wenhui smiled and asked him again, Niuwa, why don't you come home with Auntie today? Auntie has a big brother and sister at home to play with you.","Seeing this, the other comrades from the Women's Federation also gathered around, looking at Niuwa, the abducted child.","Director, why are you taking the child home? He's only three or four years old; he won't be easy to take care of.","Sigh, our Director is just too kind-hearted. Previously, there was an abandoned elderly person in the district who almost starved to death at home, and it was the Director who brought her food and water.","Someone flattered, Look at our Director's level of awareness. How else could she become the Director? If it were me, I definitely wouldn't want to take a child home; we barely have enough food for ourselves.","Zheng Wenhui stood there, smiling very gently, and said, Alas, this child is also pitiful. Comrade Qin just said that he can't be sent to the orphanage, or he'll run away. It's better to keep him at my house, where my family can help keep an eye on him. With the courtyard gates usually closed, he won't be able to run off.","Saying that, Zheng Wenhui smiled at Niuwa. Alright, Niuwa, will you go home with Auntie now?","Zheng Wenhui led Niuwa out of the Women's Federation by the hand, pondering in her heart what to do with this child.","She knew about the child's abduction.","But now that he had been brought back, if the police really followed the clues and investigated, what if they traced it back to her brother?","The more Zheng Wenhui thought about it, the more she felt she couldn't just sit around and wait for her doom.","So, she bought Niuwa a packet of biscuits. Once Niuwa started eating, he would quiet down and stop making a fuss.","Zheng Wenhui then carried Niuwa and hurried into an alley, stopping to knock on the door of a house.","It was still early, so her brother definitely hadn't gotten off work yet.","But there must be someone at home.","So, after she knocked for a few minutes, sure enough, a woman opened the door.","The woman who opened the door looked somewhat haggard. She was wearing an apron and oversleeves, clearly having just been doing chores.","If Qiao Lanshu were here, she would definitely recognize that this woman was her former colleague, Liu Weihong.","When Liu Weihong saw Zheng Wenhui standing outside the door, she was momentarily stunned. Then, her face took on a polite and reserved expression as she smiled and asked, Wenhui, what brings you here today? Is there something the matter?","As she spoke, Liu Weihong glanced at the child Zheng Wenhui was holding by the hand.","The child had his head lowered, munching crunchily on a biscuit, his mouth covered in crumbs.","Liu Weihong didn't recognize this child.","She knew the two children in Zheng Wenhui's family, and neither was this small.","Could this child be one that Zheng Weigong had with someone else out of wedlock?","Zheng Weigong was the section chief of the supply department. He lacked neither money nor flatterers, and it wasn't as if he hadn't had other women on the outside before.","Even Liu Weihong herself, who had been with Zheng Weigong up until now, still had no official status.","Zheng Weigong had never brought up the topic of marriage. Agreeing to let Liu Weihong live in his house was already an enormous blessing."]},{"number":194,"title":"Chapter 194: The child is missing","paragraphs":["Zheng Wenhui looked down on Liu Weihong.","Previously, Liu Weihong's family background had been quite good. Her father was the section chief of the personnel department, and she herself was a supervisor at the food factory.","With such a status, she was naturally a worthy match for her brother.","But now, her father's identity as a spy had been exposed and he had been arrested, and her younger brother had also been sent to a labor camp.","As for Liu Weihong herself, she had no job and could only rely on Zheng Wenhui's brother, Zheng Weigong, to survive. At the same time, she still had to occasionally provide financial support to her mother.","Because of this, Zheng Wenhui completely despised Liu Weihong.","She felt that both Liu Weihong and her mother were nothing but burdens. Even though her brother was divorced, he was only in his thirties and was the chief of the supply section. What kind of woman couldn't he get?","Zheng Wenhui looked at Liu Weihong with disdain. Crossing her arms over her chest, she asked, Is my brother back yet?","Liu Weihong couldn't stand her condescending attitude, but since she wasn't married to Zheng Weigong yet and lacked a proper status, she didn't dare to argue with Zheng Wenhui.","She nodded silently. Weigong usually gets back around six-thirty. Do you want to come in and sit for a while?","When Zheng Wenhui came over, she had already guessed that her brother wouldn't be back yet.","However, this child was simply a hot potato.","Although Zheng Wenhui knew some of the situation, her brother was clearer on the specific inside details.","In short, the matter regarding this child had to be dealt with as quickly as possible before the police could investigate it.","But the biggest problem right now was that the military knew about this.","This child had been personally brought to the Women's Federation by Qin Yuanzheng, and had been handed over directly to Zheng Wenhui.","Now, she absolutely could not lose this child while he was in her hands; otherwise, her position as the director of the Women's Federation would be over.","So she still had to find her brother, Zheng Weigong. Her brother was very smart and would definitely know what to do.","Zheng Wenhui said irritably, I won't go in. I still have to take the child home and settle him down. When my brother gets off work, tell him to come over to my house tonight. I have something very important to discuss with him. Did you hear me?","This arrogant tone made Liu Weihong's face darken slightly.","She said with a hint of impatience, I know. I'll tell Weigong when he gets back.","Zheng Wenhui emphasized again, Remember, you absolutely must tell him. This matter is extremely important.","Liu Weihong grew even more impatient. I know, I know. I'll have him go look for you.","Zheng Wenhui rolled her eyes at Liu Weihong. She wanted to throw a few sarcastic remarks at her to make her realize her place. She was living in her brother's house, eating and staying there for free, completely relying on him to support her, yet she actually dared to give her attitude.","However, out of the corner of her eye, she suddenly caught a glimpse of something and jolted in shock.","She whipped her head to the side. Huh? Where was the child?","She looked around frantically, spinning in a circle where she stood, and then glared viciously at Liu Weihong, demanding shrilly, Where is the child? Where did the child I just brought go?","Liu Weihong...","Liu Weihong was also dumbfounded.","She had just been focused on talking to Zheng Wenhui. Finding her annoying, she had been busy cursing Zheng Wenhui in her head.","Where would she have the time to pay attention to a child?","Besides, she hadn't given birth herself, let alone taken care of a child. She wasn't used to paying attention to little kids in the first place.","On the contrary, Zheng Wenhui was a mother of two herself, yet she had brought a child and managed to let him run off.","What right did she have to yell at her?","Liu Weihong said with a face full of bewilderment and surprise, I... I don't know! Wasn't he just here eating cookies?","Zheng Wenhui knew that once children had something to eat and play with, they would settle down and not easily run around.","That was exactly why she had specifically gone to buy cookies to coax Niuwa.","But in the end, it only took the time of saying a few words for the child to run away?","Zheng Wenhui searched around the spot two more times.","This alley was very long, with houses on both sides, full of residents.","She was extremely anxious and yelled at Liu Weihong, What are you standing there for? Hurry up and help find the child!","It was Liu Weihong's first time seeing Zheng Wenhui in such a panic.","At this moment, she didn't dare to bicker with Zheng Wenhui over her attitude or tone.","She quickly ran out of the house. The child... he couldn't have run far, right? Could he have gone to play in the neighbor's house?","In these times, families didn't close their doors during the day.","The elderly would sit on the thresholds cooling off, sorting vegetables, or chatting, while the children would dart in and out of the neighbors' houses.","If Niuwa had run into someone's house, they would have to go inside to look for him.","Not caring about much else at this point, Zheng Wenhui and Liu Weihong hurried to ask from door to door if a three- or four-year-old child had run inside.","Some said no, while others said they didn't know and would have to check inside.","After all this searching, at least half an hour had passed.","Niuwa had run off to who-knows-where; he was nowhere to be found.","Zheng Wenhui was so nervous that her face turned pale. It's over, I let the child run away. What do I do now...","At this moment, Zheng Wenhui couldn't help but feel a bit of regret.","Qin Yuanzheng had said that this child was very prone to running away and told her not to send him to an orphanage.","She should have paid more attention back then.","But Niuwa had been so well-behaved while eating the cookies, not moving an inch. She thought the child wouldn't run away anytime soon.","How did he just run off in the span of a few sentences?","What should she do?","Zheng Wenhui's hands were shaking from anxiety. She said to Liu Weihong, No, we can't let this go on. I'll keep looking for the child here. You go find my brother right now and tell him to come back immediately. This matter is of critical importance. Hurry up and go!","Liu Weihong had been helping her look for the child for a long time and was now panting from exhaustion.","Seeing how much importance Zheng Wenhui attached to this child, she couldn't help but grow suspicious. She looked at Zheng Wenhui and asked, What exactly is this child's background?","Taking a step closer, her eyes red, she said, Tell me the truth, what is this child's relationship to your brother? Is he your brother's illegitimate seed from the outside?","Zheng Wenhui...","Zheng Wenhui was so furious at Liu Weihong she nearly fell over backward.","Unable to hold back, she reached out and slapped Liu Weihong across the face, scolding, You pig-brain! That's all you can ever think about. I can't explain this to you!","With that, she turned around and hurriedly ran off to go find him herself.","This matter couldn't be known by the police, much less the military.","Otherwise, once people from those two systems intervened and started investigating, the situation might blow up out of proportion.","She had to beat the police and the military to it by having her brother quickly find the child and send him away.","However, what she didn't expect was that Liu Weihong didn't see it that way.","She felt that Zheng Wenhui's extreme anger meant she had hit the nail on the head.","This little kid was probably really Zheng Weigong's son!","Liu Weihong's eyes were red with anger as she muttered curses, That Zheng Weigong! He coaxed me into being his nanny but refuses to get a marriage certificate with me. He even said I was his only woman right now, but then he turns around and has a son on the outside!","Liu Weihong sat on the threshold, wiping her tears and crying for a long time.","Finally, she stood up again, thinking viciously that since Zheng Weigong was heartless, he shouldn't blame her for being unjust.","She was going to report Zheng Weigong for having improper relations with women and having a child out of wedlock!","The Zheng family didn't treat her like a human being, so she wouldn't let them have it easy either!","With this thought, Liu Weihong closed the front door of her house and hurried toward Zheng Weigong's workplace.","Halfway there, she realized that Zheng Weigong himself was a section chief. If she went to his workplace to report him, what if the report letter ended up in his hands?","No, she had to go to the Revolutionary Committee to report him.","So, she turned around and ran in the direction of the Revolutionary Committee.","...","After Qin Yuanzheng entrusted the child to the Women's Federation, he immediately went home.","He had gone to the neighboring city to pick up the child over the past two days, and had meetings with Guan Wenjun, Si Zhemao, and others to discuss work. He hadn't been home for two days.","He was eager to return home, thinking of his wife and child.","Also, the small courtyard next door had been aired out, and the vegetables Auntie Shi planted in the yard were almost ready to eat.","He planned to go back and move today.","There weren't many things at home. He called two guards to help, estimating that they could finish moving in two or three hours.","When Qin Yuanzheng returned home, Zhong Mei hadn't come back yet.","Qiao Lanshu was sitting on the sofa holding An'an, feeding him with a bottle. Worried about Zhong Mei, she said to Auntie Shi, \"If it's six o'clock in a while and Zhong Mei still hasn't come back, I'll have to go out and look for her.\"","Auntie Shi was sitting next to Qiao Lanshu, knitting a small vest for An'an.","She glanced out the kitchen window while knitting and replied, \"It's still early, just past four. She should be back in a while. When she left this morning, she told me she might not be back so soon.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded. \"I wonder what she went out to do. Could she be lost?\"","Auntie Shi smiled. \"That's unlikely. Our military compound is quite easy to find. Besides, if she really got lost, she could just ask anyone on the road and find her way back. It shouldn't be that she can't make it back.\"","While they were talking, they heard a knock on the door.","Auntie Shi went to open the door and saw Qin Yuanzheng with two guards, as well as Zhao Jiannong and Huang Erling from next door, standing outside.","Qin Yuanzheng came into the house and said to Auntie Shi, \"Auntie Shi, we are starting to move now. Please help pack things up.\"","Hearing that they were moving, Auntie Shi immediately smiled happily. \"Good, good, good, I'll go pack right away. I've already packed some things before, so we can move those over first.\"","Qin Yuanzheng had said before that once Zhong Mei's matter was settled, they could move when he came back.","Taking advantage of his free time now with no missions, he hurried to move.","Auntie Shi had already packed some winter bedding and clothes, tied them tightly with ropes, and put them in snakeskin bags. Now they could be taken out directly for the guards to move over first.","Auntie Shi smiled and said to Qiao Lanshu, \"I've cleaned the yard next door. I have to go over to water the vegetable garden every day, and I've wanted to move in for a long time. Today we can finally move.\"","Qiao Lanshu was also very happy because there was a yard over there, providing more spacious room for activities. In the future, as soon as they stepped out, there would be a vegetable garden, flowers, and trees. Bringing a stool to sit under the tree to enjoy the cool breeze would be incredibly pleasant.","She stood up holding An'an, saw Huang Erling had also come over, and said with a smile, \"Why did Sister Ling come over too? Are you going to help me move?\"","Huang Erling said with a smile, \"Of course! Brigade Commander Qin said that for today's move, he would kill a chicken and a goose to treat the helpers to a meal. I can't miss this feast! I happen to be free and can help you pack and organize things. Just hold the baby and don't worry about anything.\"","Saying that, Huang Erling came over to look at An'an in her arms, took out a colorful knitted yarn sheep from her pocket, and said with a smile, \"An'an, look what this is? This is a little sheep. Is it pretty?\"","This little sheep was knitted with yarn of several colors. The colors looked a bit old, but it was washed very clean.","It was knitted by Huang Erling herself using leftover yarn from knitting sweaters for her two daughters to play with.","Children in this era didn't have many toys from a young age.","If parents had time, they would make some for their children themselves. If not, the kids would just go play with mud at the door.","Huang Erling gave the little sheep to An'an. An'an's attention was indeed attracted by the colors. His big grape-like eyes widened, and he reached out his little hands to grab the little sheep.","Huang Erling teased him for a while, then put the little sheep in An'an's hands and smiled at Qiao Lanshu, \"An'an looks exactly like you, very handsome.\"","Auntie Shi also smiled while packing, \"When An'an grows up, with facial features like Xiao Qiao and a figure like Commander Qin, I don't know how handsome he'll be. I guess all the girls in the surrounding villages will be fascinated by him.\"","Hearing them say this, Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but imagine a face like hers on Qin Yuanzheng's body.","Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but laugh.","The picture was too beautiful; she couldn't think about it anymore.","Qin Yuanzheng was moving the sofa out with Zhao Jiannong. Seeing Qiao Lanshu looking at him and laughing, he wondered: What is this little wife laughing at? The look in her eyes is weird.","Qiao Lanshu held An'an, while Huang Erling carried An'an's daily necessities, and they went over first.","Auntie Shi stayed at home to help pack things.","There weren't many things actually. After all, Qin Yuanzheng and Qiao Lanshu didn't have much. An'an's things were a bit trivial, and Auntie Shi had already packed them up.","The bed and cabinets in the house were not to be moved away. They were originally provided with the house and had to be left for the next tenant.","But the sofa, dining table, chairs in the living room, and Qiao Lanshu's wardrobe were bought when they got married and could be moved to the new home.","There weren't many pots and pans in the kitchen either; they could be put in a box and carried away directly.","Both rooms in the new home had heated brick beds and new cabinets. There were also front and back yards, making the space even larger.","After the things were moved over and organized, they all felt that the house was a bit empty.","With the help of Zhao Jiannong and the two guards, all the things were moved over in less than two hours.","Next, it was up to Auntie Shi, Qiao Lanshu, and Huang Erling to organize and arrange everything.","An'an had already fallen asleep holding the colorful little sheep.","Huang Erling walked around the house and said enviously, \"Xiao Qiao, your yard is really beautiful. Oh my, the vegetables in the yard are growing so well. If I had known, I would have asked Old Zhao to apply for a yard too.\"","Huang Erling regretted it a bit. Why didn't she think of applying for a yard before?","Oh, looking at the vegetable garden in the yard, her eyes were filled with envy."]},{"number":195,"title":"Chapter 195: Guan Wenjun Gets Beaten Up","paragraphs":["By the time Qiao Lanshu finished moving, it was already past six in the evening.","It was summer, so it got dark late. At six o'clock, the sun was just hanging over the mountain peaks, yet to set.","The horizon was painted with golden twilight clouds. Flocks of sparrows fluttered among the surrounding trees, chirping away merrily. It was quite a lively scene.","Zhao Jiannong had brought along two guards to help Qin Yuanzheng arrange the large pieces of furniture, like the sofa, tables, chairs, and cabinets.","Auntie Shi and Huang Erling helped to settle the smaller items.","The living room of this new home was more spacious than their previous apartment. It was perfectly square. The sofa was placed against the wall with a low table in front of it. Against the opposite wall sat a newly crafted low cabinet featuring six large drawers for storing miscellaneous items.","On top of the cabinet sat everyday items like a radio, a thermos, and a kerosene lamp.","The floor was paved with blue bricks, clean and even, so the table sat steadily without wobbling.","Huang Erling helped Qiao Lanshu organize the wardrobe in the bedroom. The bedding on the kang had already been laid out, and little An'an was currently lying there, fast asleep.","Auntie Shi said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Little Qiao, things are mostly put away now. I'm going to start cooking. The commander said he wants to slaughter a chicken and a goose for tomorrow's lunch to treat everyone, so I need to hurry up and prep.\"","It was already six. She had to make tonight's dinner and prep for tomorrow's lunch. After all, Brigade Commander Qin was moving into a new home and hosting his comrades; she definitely couldn't slack off.","Qiao Lanshu nodded and said, \"I'll come help you.\"","Auntie Shi quickly stopped her. \"No need, just keep an eye on An'an. He knows how to roll over now, so don't let him tumble off the kang.\"","With that, Auntie Shi hurried off to the kitchen.","Qiao Lanshu tucked An'an in, then left the room to check on the vegetable seedlings in the courtyard garden.","Huang Erling followed Auntie Shi to the kitchen to take a look. Truth be told, this kitchen was also larger than the one in the apartment building.","The apartment's kitchen had been narrow and long, whereas this one was a neat square, with extra space to store firewood and dry grass.","Qin Yuanzheng had built a large stove here with a massive wok embedded in it. Food cooked over a wood fire would smell unbelievably fragrant.","Qin Yuanzheng had also built this stove with the thought that boiling water for baths would be convenient; one pot would be enough for Qiao Lanshu to take a nice soak.","The newly built bathhouse was just outside, right around the corner from the kitchen. Even in winter, taking a bath would be quite convenient.","Though the bathhouse was small, it was solidly built with bricks. It only had a small window for ventilation. Once the window was closed, it was completely sealed off, keeping the wind out and the warmth in.","After touring the front and back yards, Huang Erling was filled with envy. Even the way she looked at Zhao Jiannong changed.","Zhao Jiannong was standing in the yard chatting with Qin Yuanzheng. Catching Huang Erling's gaze, he quietly said to Qin Yuanzheng, \"Look at that. I told you, with you moving, my wife is definitely going to throw a fuss.\"","Qin Yuanzheng looked at the waist-high apple and persimmon trees newly planted in the yard. He smiled and said, \"Then you should apply for a courtyard too. The surrounding areas are all shared courtyards. Walk around, take a look, and find a suitable one.\"","Zhao Jiannong rolled his eyes at Qin Yuanzheng and replied, \"Give it a rest. You said it yourself, it took you a month or two of asking around just to find this single-family courtyard. The rest are all shared. If we live in the same yard as others, what happens if conflicts arise?\"","Zhao Jiannong continued, \"I grew up in a shared courtyard. Even though most people are nice, there's really no privacy. If you spend a little too long squatting in the outhouse, you'll have old ladies gossiping behind your back. It's just ridiculous.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","And that wasn't even mentioning other things, like how the vegetables in his grandmother's yard were always being stolen. Whenever the old hen laid an egg, someone had to squat nearby and guard it, otherwise, it would be snatched up by someone else in no time.","In short, it was complicated. Zhao Jiannong disliked living in shared courtyards the most. Living in an apartment building now, although a bit cramped, felt pretty good to him.","Their family of four could close their door and live their own lives, and his wife wouldn't have to argue with others every day over trivial matters.","It was just that the military compound here didn't look like a traditional courtyard compound; it was made up of individual apartment buildings.","Actually, he was quite envious of the military compound in the neighboring city. Everyone there had their own single-family courtyard, all enclosed to form one massive compound with guards stationed at the gate. Everyone lived very comfortably.","Qin Yuanzheng had originally intended to invite Zhao Jiannong to stay for dinner at the new house.","But before they could even eat, someone came rushing over to their door.","The visitor was Li Jianlin, the Deputy Director of the Public Security Bureau.","Deputy Director Li was sweating profusely and panting heavily. Standing at the main gate of the courtyard, he first peeked inside. Upon seeing Qin Yuanzheng and Zhao Jiannong, he breathed a sigh of relief and quickly ran in. \"Brigade Commander Qin, you are here! Why did you move so suddenly? I just went over to the other place looking for you, but the guard at the door told me you moved.\"","Seeing Deputy Director Li, Qin Yuanzheng immediately had a bad premonition.","He frowned and asked, \"What's the rush?\"","Qiao Lanshu, who was in the vegetable garden, also walked over curiously. Looking at the sweating Deputy Director Li, she felt a bit worried. Was Brother Zheng going to be sent out on another mission?","Deputy Director Li wiped the sweat from his forehead with his hand and sighed. \"I just received news from the Revolutionary Committee that a child has gone missing! That child was originally with Zheng Wenhui, the director of the Women's Federation. But when Zheng Wenhui took him to see her brother and sister-in-law, the child went missing right at their doorstep.\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu looked at Qin Yuanzheng in surprise and said worriedly, \"Brother Zheng, the child the Women's Federation director lost... don't tell me it's Niuwa, whom you just dropped off?\"","Qiao Lanshu had always been very concerned about the child who had been abducted on the train.","Later, Qin Yuanzheng had made a special trip to the neighboring city to bring the child back and sent him to the Women's Federation. He had told Qiao Lanshu about this.","And now, not even a few hours after dropping him off, the child was lost?","Qin Yuanzheng felt something wasn't right. He asked Li Jianlin, \"Why is the Revolutionary Committee delivering this news? If a child goes missing, shouldn't they come to the Public Security Bureau to find you first? Who reported the case? Zheng Wenhui?\"","Li Jianlin shook his head and said, \"No. The people from the Revolutionary Committee said that Zheng Wenhui's sister-in-law submitted a tip-off letter to them. She reported that Zheng Wenhui's brother, Zheng Weigong, was fooling around with women outside and had even fathered an illegitimate child. She demanded that the supply department severely punish Zheng Weigong. But when they asked her where the illegitimate child was, she said he had gone missing...\"","Deputy Director Li Jianlin spent quite a while explaining the convoluted situation.","Both Qin Yuanzheng and Zhao Jiannong were left completely bewildered.","Zhao Jiannong said, \"What a mess. An illegitimate child is an illegitimate child. How does this connect to your abducted kid? Why don't I understand a word of this?\"","Qin Yuanzheng, however, understood. He mused, \"Are you saying that the Niuwa I dropped off is Zheng Wenhui's nephew?\"","As soon as he said that, he shook his head. \"Impossible. That child doesn't know Zheng Wenhui.\"","Deputy Bureau Chief Li added, \"Since he's an illegitimate child, maybe it's normal that they don't know each other?\"","Qin Yuanzheng still shook his head.","But with this incident happening, he really had to go to the Revolutionary Committee to take a look, as well as the Women's Federation. The child was taken away by Zheng Wenhui, the director of the Women's Federation, and she had to go to the police station to explain the process.","Qin Yuanzheng said to Qiao Lanshu somewhat apologetically, \"I have to head out for a bit.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded and said softly, \"Come back early. I'll have Auntie Shi save some food for you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng nodded. Seeing that the courtyard was already tidied up, he strode away with Li Jianlin.","With Qin Yuanzheng gone, Zhao Jiannong couldn't stay any longer, so he took Huang Erling and immediately took his leave as well.","...","Qiao Lanshu came out of the courtyard and walked around the alley to the outside. Just then, she saw Zhong Mei, who had been out all day, returning.","Qiao Lanshu had already told the guards at the military compound to inform Zhong Mei about their move when she got back.","It just so happened that before Zhong Mei could enter the main gate over there, Qiao Lanshu spotted her.","Qiao Lanshu quickly called out to her, \"Zhong Mei, over here!\"","Zhong Mei was wearing a dusty gray outfit and a straw hat, carrying a basket in her hand.","The cloth shoes on her feet were covered in mud and looked rather dirty.","Qiao Lanshu looked her up and down and asked in surprise, \"Ah Mei, what have you been up to?\"","Zhong Mei looked thoroughly frustrated and said, \"Ugh, don't even mention it. I've had such terrible luck today.\"","Qiao Lanshu went over to take her hand, but Zhong Mei avoided it, saying, \"My hands are dirty. Look, they're covered in dirt.\"","Qiao Lanshu led her toward their new home, saying as they walked, \"Where did you go today? Why are you back so late? I was worried you'd gotten lost.\"","Zhong Mei looked around, and seeing no one nearby, lowered her voice and said:","\"I originally just went out for a stroll today. But later, I heard someone say there were wild vegetables to forage in the suburbs. Those wild vegetables are only available this season, and people love using them to make dumplings. In another half month, they'll be gone. I figured, since I had nothing else to do, why not go get some? I could make a little money selling them, right?\"","Zhong Mei was poor herself. Over the years, she had done odd jobs everywhere, trying to find ways to make money.","You could say she was someone whose eyes lit up at the sight of money.","She had no choice. In her situation, if she hadn't worked hard to save up, she wouldn't have even been able to afford a stamp to write to Qiao Lanshu, let alone buy a train ticket to come stay with her.","But there was a problem here. Zhong Mei was a Southerner; she had absolutely no idea what the wild vegetables in Longcheng looked like.","After arriving in the suburbs, she struck up a conversation with the women foraging for wild vegetables to learn what they looked like.","After that, she started carrying her basket around, picking wild vegetables herself.","When everyone else had left, she was still there picking, even wandering further and further into the distant suburbs to forage.","Of course, her hard work paid off. Carrying a basket full of wild vegetables, she took advantage of the afternoon rush when many people were selling produce and skillfully navigated through the various alleys.","She knew that people engaging in speculative trading all went into the alleys to sell their goods.","Qiao Lanshu truly admired Zhong Mei. She was hardworking, able to endure hardship, and sharp-witted.","She glanced at Zhong Mei's basket. It was completely empty; there wasn't a single wild vegetable left.","She asked in a low voice, \"How did it go? Did you sell them all? How much money did you make?\"","At the mention of this, Zhong Mei's face scrunched up, and she said nervously, \"Lanshu, I think I might have gotten myself into a bit of trouble this time.\"","Qiao Lanshu immediately had a bad feeling about this.","If even Zhong Mei considered it trouble, it had to be a massive disaster.","Qiao Lanshu looked around, quickly grabbed Zhong Mei's arm, and the two jogged back to the small courtyard.","Zhong Mei didn't even have time to admire Qiao Lanshu's new home.","The two squatted in a corner of the courtyard, and Zhong Mei lowered her voice, saying, \"There's a kind of wild weed that looks exactly like those wild vegetables. I couldn't tell them apart, so I picked the weeds along with the vegetables...\"","As she spoke, she said gloomily, \"I was wondering why there were so many growing in those spots and no one wanted them, leaving them all for me. I actually thought my luck had started to turn around after coming to Longcheng.\"","In the end, she was still unlucky, and incredibly so.","Qiao Lanshu didn't rush to speak, knowing that Zhong Mei was impatient. Without needing to be asked, Zhong Mei would spill the whole story like beans pouring from a sack.","Sure enough, Zhong Mei immediately continued with a nervous expression:","\"I had no idea that weed was poisonous and unfit for human consumption. Of course, if I had known it was a weed, I wouldn't have picked it to sell... What's worse, a man walked past the entrance of the alley, saw the wild vegetables in my basket, and asked if I was selling them. I said yes. He asked how much, and I said one yuan. And then, guess what?\"","Qiao Lanshu stared at Zhong Mei with wide eyes. \"What happened?\"","Zhong Mei pulled a bitter face, looking like she was about to cry. She said, \"The guy whipped out a pair of handcuffs from his pocket and tried to arrest me! He said it was bad enough I was engaging in speculative trading, but I was also selling fake goods, and to top it off, selling poisonous fake goods! I was scared to death. I dumped the basket of wild vegetables right over his head and ran for my life.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","After hearing this, Qiao Lanshu also realized this was a serious problem.","But still harboring a sliver of hope, she asked, \"Did you cover your face at the time?\"","Zhong Mei was practically crying now. \"No...\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu pulled Zhong Mei to her feet and comforted her:","\"Don't worry, it'll be fine. Just stay at home for the next few days. In a few days, I'll take you to the food factory to report for work as a temp. Since the guy had handcuffs, he might be a police officer. There are only four officers at the police station in total, and lately, they've been busy searching for a missing child. They definitely won't have time to look for you. Rest assured, you'll be fine.\"","Qiao Lanshu added, \"There are so many people doing speculative trading in the city. Even a lot of police officers go to the black market to buy things themselves. As long as those traders run fast enough, the police never chase them. You just need to relax. This isn't a big deal.\"","Zhong Mei wanted to weep but had no tears. \"I hope so. Sigh, ever since I was sent to the labor camp last time, I've become so timid. I'm just terrified of getting caught and sent back to labor camp again...\"","...","However, Qiao Lanshu was wrong this time.","Zhong Mei's incident was absolutely going to be pursued.","Because the person who tried to arrest her wasn't a police officer, but Guan Wenjun, who had just returned from a mission out of town.","Guan Wenjun had stayed in a village for over half a year. He hadn't just gotten tanned; he had also lost weight.","After returning to Longcheng, he had originally intended to go to the black market to buy some meat or fish to nourish his body.","As a result, right after he walked in and before he could even say two words, he was smashed in the face several times by that girl's vegetable basket.","He was completely dazed by the blows, and the skin on his forehead was broken and bleeding.","Guan Wenjun had always been quite vain about his appearance. Now, on an empty stomach, he had been beaten up by a woman and left dizzy from being smashed in the forehead.","When he returned to the Revolutionary Committee, his subordinates were dumbfounded to see him in such a state. Someone asked, \"Director, did... did someone hit you with a brick?\"","Guan Wenjun: \"...\"","Guan Wenjun gritted his teeth and growled, \"There's this woman... I absolutely must catch her! How dare she commit assault in broad daylight!\"","The vegetable basket was made of woven bamboo, rock-hard with a rather sharp bottom. Smashing it right into someone's face like that—if that wasn't assault, what was?","Whoever did it had better hope he didn't catch them!"]},{"number":196,"title":"Chapter 196: Implementing the Work.","paragraphs":["On her very first day out, Zhong Mei caused trouble and did not dare to leave the house again.","If it were in the past, she certainly would not be afraid.","But had she not just gotten out of the labor camp?","Her household registration was still at the labor camp and had not been transferred back yet. She was terrified, afraid of letting down Qiao Lanshu's good intentions and ruining the rest of her life.","Before, she had no one to rely on but herself, so she could only use extreme methods to protect herself.","But now, with Qiao Lanshu's help, she naturally became more timid and started to value her life.","Besides, Qiao Lanshu's husband was a military officer who highly valued his reputation. She could not afford to implicate the couple.","Therefore, Zhong Mei stayed quietly in the courtyard of Qiao Lanshu's new home. Every day, she accompanied Auntie Shi to plant vegetables, water flowers, and feed the chickens and sheep.","She also helped take care of An'an. After all, An'an was still young and needed to eat six meals a day. She also had to take him out to bask in the sun and watch the chickens and ducks play.","With Zhong Mei's help, Auntie Shi had an easier time. She continued to till the soil in the yard, stuffing vegetable seeds into every nook and cranny.","This way, it would not be long before the small courtyard became even more lush and green.","Qiao Lanshu had not officially resigned yet. Her application had been submitted, Yang Wenyan had signed it, and the process had reached the personnel department.","However, Qiao Lanshu had to wait for a newcomer to hand over her work.","Because the previous worker, Tian Hemei, had been transferred away.","Tian Hemei had originally intended to falsify the inventory data to frame Qiao Lanshu.","This stupid trick did not succeed. Instead, she got herself demoted from a dependent worker to a temporary worker and was transferred to the pickle workshop to make pickles.","Qiao Lanshu worked for a few more days until the personnel department transferred an elderly employee with mobility issues. After handing over her work and handling Zhong Mei's onboarding, she finally left the food factory.","Zhong Mei could only be a temporary worker. The salary for a temporary worker was only 10 yuan, plus a non-staple food ticket subsidy of about 2 yuan.","It was not a lot of money, but Zhong Mei only needed to support herself, so it was enough.","After Qiao Lanshu finished all this and had lunch, she officially resigned.","She did not have many belongings, carrying them out in just one basket.","On her way out of the factory, she saw Tian Hemei.","Tian Hemei had come specifically to block her path. Looking at the things Qiao Lanshu was carrying, she said in disbelief, Qiao Lanshu, why did I hear that you resigned? Did you really resign?","Tian Hemei could not believe it. Since Qiao Lanshu was going to resign anyway, why had she been in such a rush back then?","If she had not caused trouble for Qiao Lanshu and had just worked honestly, would she not have avoided being transferred and demoted to a temporary worker?","Seeing Tian Hemei, Qiao Lanshu acted as if she could not read her expression. She smiled and greeted her, Comrade Tian Hemei, what a coincidence. I heard you are working in the pickle workshop?","Tian Hemei: ...","Tian Hemei's face looked extremely ugly. She questioned Qiao Lanshu, Since you were going to resign, why didn't you say so earlier?","Qiao Lanshu looked at her in surprise and said, On my very first day back at work, everyone in the factory knew I was going to resign. Comrade Tian Hemei, didn't you know?","Tian Hemei: ...","Of course Tian Hemei knew. After all, she was the one who spread the rumor. But she had spread it on purpose; she did not know Qiao Lanshu was actually going to resign.","Besides, Qiao Lanshu had been back at work for a few days, staying in the small wooden cabin with her, yet she had not revealed a single word about it.","Tian Hemei felt both remorseful and furious.","She had truly lifted a rock only to drop it on her own foot. What a mess!","Seeing Tian Hemei's expression, Qiao Lanshu found it amusing.","This just went to show that people should be kind to others and not harbor malicious intentions.","Putting aside Tian Hemei's regret and frustration, Qiao Lanshu had already left the food factory.","Wherever there are people, there will be scheming, let alone in such a large food factory.","It was already summer, and half the year was about to pass.","The college entrance examination would resume next year, leaving Qiao Lanshu with only one year. She needed to focus on her revisions to ensure she passed on her first try next year.","However, she had one problem: her preferred university was in the south, not here. Longcheng only had one university, and it was not what she wanted.","When the time came, would she have to live apart from Qin Yuanzheng?","Thinking of this, Qiao Lanshu sighed again.","She admitted she was being a bit clingy. She relied on Qin Yuanzheng too much and did not want to be separated from him.","Anyway, there was still a year until the exam. She would wait and ask for Qin Yuanzheng's opinion when the time came.","...","Since she had some rare free time today, Qiao Lanshu thought about calling Zhong Mei out to accompany her to the supply and marketing cooperative.","But then she remembered that Zhong Mei had caused trouble earlier and offended the police comrades. Right now, she was still hiding at home like a frightened quail, not daring to go out.","Qiao Lanshu found it funny but also felt a bit worried.","However, it had been a few days, and there was no news of the police catching any female comrades for speculation and profiteering. It should be fine.","Since the job at the food factory was settled, Qiao Lanshu needed Zhong Mei to familiarize herself with the route. She also needed to take her to the factory's personnel department to fill out a form and then rent a room for her.","After all, she was married to Qin Yuanzheng, and it was not appropriate for a young, unmarried girl like Zhong Mei to keep living in their home.","Qiao Lanshu returned home early and talked to Zhong Mei about it.","Wearing a straw hat and holding a hoe, Zhong Mei was weeding the vegetable garden. Having done farm work and chores since childhood, she was highly skilled at growing vegetables and cooking.","She said hesitantly, Lanshu, do you think I can go out now?","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, Of course you can. I have asked around for you these past few days. The police are currently looking for a lost child; I haven't heard anything about them looking for someone involved in speculation... Besides, if you change your clothes and hairstyle, they might not even recognize you.","Zhong Mei was thin. Like Qiao Lanshu, she had a small frame, was slender, and a bit short. But not all the local girls were tall either. They definitely would not recognize her just by her figure.","Furthermore, Zhong Mei did not have any moles or freckles on her face, no distinguishing marks. For someone who had only seen her briefly, how could they possibly recognize her?","Qiao Lanshu felt Zhong Mei was overthinking it. It is fine. How about this: when we go out this time, we will cover our faces. Let us go to the food factory to fill out the form first. Getting your onboarding done is the priority.","Zhong Mei nodded. She also valued the job and did not want to miss this opportunity.","So she went back and changed into a clean set of clothes, burying the dusty gray outfit she had worn that day at the bottom of her trunk.","That day, she had her hair in two braids. Today, she thought about it, gritted her teeth, took a pair of scissors, and directly cut off her two braids!","Qiao Lanshu could not help but exclaim, Oh my, you finally grew your hair long, and you just cut it off like that?","Zhong Mei did not feel sorry at all. She said, If I cut my hair short, he definitely won't recognize me.","She originally did not have bangs, but now she also cut straight bangs.","With bangs and short hair, even she felt that her appearance had completely changed.","Qiao Lanshu looked her up and down and smiled, saying, \"Well, getting a bob haircut makes you look like a completely different person. It feels like we're back in our school days. Now, there's absolutely no way the other party will recognize you, so you can put your mind at ease.\"","Zhong Mei took a hairclip and pinned back the loose strands by her ear. Letting out a sigh of relief, she said, \"Lanshu, I'm really never going to cause trouble again. Just this once was enough to scare me half to death.\"","Although Zhong Mei's skin was on the tanner side, her facial features were quite pretty. With her new straight bangs, she looked even younger and more attractive.","Qiao Lanshu said softly, \"This hairstyle suits you. Let me trim it a bit for you.\"","Qiao Lanshu recalled that she used to have straight bangs too.","Back then, it was the standard student haircut, and all the girls in school wore their hair like that.","Later on, when she got pregnant, she let her bangs grow out and tied her hair up.","After trimming Zhong Mei's hair, the two of them got ready to leave.","The two close friends linked arms, grabbed a basket, and headed out after letting Auntie Shi know they were leaving.","Qiao Lanshu first took Zhong Mei to the food factory. \"My house is relatively close to the food factory, about a twenty-minute walk. Once you start working, I'll go with you to rent a place nearby. It definitely needs to be close, otherwise it'll be freezing when it snows in winter.\"","Qiao Lanshu added, \"I asked my former colleagues, and there are indeed houses for rent around here. The rent isn't expensive either. A larger courtyard, big enough for a family of several people, goes for about three yuan.","But if you rent a smaller courtyard, the rent is much cheaper. There are some for a little over one yuan, and the more expensive ones are around one yuan and fifty cents. Based on a temporary worker's salary of ten yuan, you can easily afford to rent one. Later, when you find a chance to become a regular employee, your salary will increase, starting at twenty-five yuan. So don't be stingy with your money; living comfortably and safely is the most important thing.\"","Zhong Mei nodded, looking at Qiao Lanshu with gratitude. \"Lanshu, thank you. If it weren't for your help, my life would be completely ruined.\"","Zhong Mei was truly grateful to Qiao Lanshu.","She felt she had terrible luck in life. Born into such a family, she had never had a full meal since she was little. By the age of three or four, she was already helping with chores, planting vegetables, and taking care of her younger siblings. As she grew up, she still wasn't treated well, and she couldn't even find a man who loved her to start a normal family.","However, her luck wasn't entirely bad. Fate had allowed her to meet Qiao Lanshu when they were young. They were not only childhood friends but also classmates who grew up together and shared a deep bond.","It really was true that when fate closes a door, it opens a window.","Qiao Lanshu sighed and said, \"These aren't big deals. I just want us both to be well.\"","In her past life, she could barely protect herself, and looking at it now, her fate hadn't been much better than Zhong Mei's.","They were both people with hard lives.","Qiao Lanshu led Zhong Mei straight to the personnel office of the food factory.","In this day and age, jobs were hard to find. City jobs were in high demand, and even a temporary position was very rare.","At the very least, if young people in the city had jobs, they wouldn't have to be sent down to the countryside, nor would they have to wander around the city all day with nothing to do.","Having a job also made it easier to find a marriage partner. Even a temporary job was better than no job at all.","That was why Zhong Mei was so incredibly grateful to Qiao Lanshu, but between close friends like them, there was no need to say too much; they both understood each other's hearts.","Zhong Mei had only attended elementary school, but her handwriting was very neat. After filling out the form, she handed it to the clerk in the personnel office. The clerk smiled and asked Qiao Lanshu, \"Xiao Qiao, why did you suddenly resign? It's really such a pity.\"","That was a warehouse keeper position, after all!","Qiao Lanshu smiled and replied, \"I was just too busy and couldn't manage it. Zhong Mei is also from Yangcheng. She isn't familiar with this place and doesn't have any family or friends here, so I hope you can take good care of her in the future.\"","The personnel clerk smiled and said, \"Don't worry. Since she's your friend, I'll definitely look out for her.\"","Whether the clerk meant it or not, both Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei expressed their thanks.","The personnel comrade informed Zhong Mei to report for duty on the 1st of next month.","Calculating the time, there were only four or five days left. Qiao Lanshu pulled Zhong Mei outside and said, \"We need to hurry up and rent a place. Then we can buy some furniture, and you'll finally be settled down.\"","Zhong Mei was immediately filled with longing.","\"I want to rent a place with a courtyard, somewhere I can bask in the sun... I've never had my own room since I was little. My whole family squeezed into one dark room, and all four of us siblings slept on one small bed. It was so crowded. In the summer, I would just sleep right under the bed... I want my own room so badly. This time, I definitely want to rent a beautiful little courtyard. Even if the rent is a bit more expensive, I'll accept it.\"","Out of her ten yuan, she could take out three yuan for rent. By living frugally on the rest, she might even be able to save a little money.","Zhong Mei's face was full of hope and yearning.","The two friends strolled through the residential area near the food factory, looking for a house.","Zhong Mei grabbed Qiao Lanshu's arm and whispered to her, \"Last time, I was in that alley over there...\"","As she spoke, she pointed to a nearby alley. Qiao Lanshu looked over and indeed saw people going in and out of the alley from time to time. It seemed it really was a black market.","Truth be told, Qiao Lanshu had also bought things in that alley before. The last time she and Wang Xue bought fried dough twists, they were sold right in that alley.","She smiled and said to Zhong Mei, \"You just got here, and you already found that place. You're really something.\"","Zhong Mei said nervously, \"I wonder if that public security comrade is still over there, waiting to catch people...\"","As the two were talking, Qiao Lanshu spotted a familiar face.","She said in surprise, \"Director Guan? What are you doing here?\"","Guan Wenjun had gauze wrapped around his head. He was wearing a white Dacron shirt and black trousers, holding a paper bag made of newspaper filled with sunflower seeds.","He stood leaning against a tree by the street, cracking melon seeds while staring at the alley over there, his eyes dark and gloomy.","Hearing the voice, he turned his head, his eyes lighting up. \"Hmm? Comrade Xiao Qiao? Long time no see! I'm sorry, I haven't given my gift as a godfather for your baby yet. I don't have time right now, but once I'm free in a while, I'll go see my son.\"","Qiao Lanshu didn't dwell on the title of 'godfather.' She pulled Zhong Mei along as she walked over, looking at Guan Wenjun hesitantly. \"Director Guan, what happened to your forehead? Didn't you say you just got back? How did you get hurt again?\"","Guan Wenjun was handsome, had fair skin, and was quite vain. She really never expected there would be a day when his face would get marred.","Speaking of this, Guan Wenjun grew furious.","His expression instantly darkened. Staring at the alley over there, he sneered, \"It's a long story. That son of a bitch better hope I don't catch her!\"","He had been staking out the place for several days, but that son of a bitch hadn't shown up.","He refused to believe it. How could a living, breathing person just vanish into thin air?","Qiao Lanshu felt Zhong Mei suddenly let go of her hand, turn around, and run.","Qiao Lanshu turned her head in surprise. \"Hey, Zhong Mei...\"","Seriously, everything was fine. Why was Zhong Mei suddenly running away?"]},{"number":197,"title":"Chapter 197: The Child Delivered to the Door","paragraphs":["Guan Wenjun's attention was mostly focused on his conversation with Qiao Lanshu, though he occasionally had to divide his focus to glance at the black market alley across the street.","He wanted to see if that profiteering woman who had injured him earlier had shown up.","But in reality, he wasn't entirely confident he would be able to find her again.","After all, any normal person would have gone into hiding after an incident like that; they absolutely wouldn't dare to show their face again.","Furthermore, judging from her clothes and overall appearance, the woman looked like she came from a village.","But there was one thing that was quite strange. Logically speaking, a female comrade from the countryside shouldn't be unable to tell the difference between wild vegetables and weeds.","Even if the two plants looked incredibly similar.","Locals could easily tell them apart. After all, it was a wild vegetable they had eaten since childhood. Even someone like Guan Wenjun, who didn't know how to cook, could identify it.","Therefore, Guan Wenjun had been staking out the area lately for two reasons. First, he was genuinely holding onto his anger and wanted revenge.","Second, he suspected that the woman was a spy!","Ever since he had followed Si Zhemao on that espionage case, they had pulled up the radish and brought out the mud, uncovering a whole network and capturing five spies in a row.","He had been thoroughly shocked.","Some of those spies were peasants, some were sent-down youths, and some were even grassroots cadres.","It was truly terrifying to think about.","Who knew how much of their nation's land had already been infiltrated by these bad elements.","As a result, everyone looked like a spy to him now.","Until he caught the woman who had injured him, he wouldn't even be able to sleep at night.","While talking to Qiao Lanshu, he hadn't paid any attention at all to the girl standing next to her.","That girl seemed to remember something urgent and suddenly ran off in a hurry.","Qiao Lanshu called out to her, then turned to Guan Wenjun and said, My friend suddenly has an emergency, so I need to go with her. I'll take my leave first. By the way, Director Guan, there are a lot of people in your Revolutionary Committee, and you're all very familiar with this area. Could you help keep an eye out for any small courtyards for rent near the food factory? My friend happens to be looking for a place to live. It's just for one girl living alone. If you see anything suitable, please let me know. Thank you!","After hurriedly finishing her sentence, Qiao Lanshu also ran off after her friend.","Guan Wenjun: ...","Guan Wenjun had wanted to chat with Qiao Lanshu a bit longer. Seeing her leave in such a rush, he only had time to nod and say, Sure, leave it to me...","Out of curiosity, Guan Wenjun glanced at Zhong Mei's retreating back. He noticed that the girl had a very thin figure and wasn't very tall, about the same height as Qiao Lanshu.","She also had short hair, so she probably wasn't very old. She might even be a recently graduated female student.","He only took one glance before losing interest, withdrawing his gaze, and continuing to squat on the ground cracking sunflower seeds.","He had just executed a mission for several months and was currently on vacation. Since he had nothing to do all day, he came here to stake out the place.","However, his carefree days were numbered. There was some progress regarding his job placement. There was a vacancy at the Municipal Labor Bureau, and his superiors intended to transfer him there.","Originally, Guan Wenjun had wanted to go to the Public Security Bureau.","The Public Security Bureau only had one deputy chief, Li Jianlin, so if he went there, he would become the chief.","He really liked the Public Security Bureau, but Commander Li said there was already another candidate for the chief position, mentioning that they were going to pick a military officer transitioning to civilian work.","Guan Wenjun lacked the necessary boldness, so the Labor Bureau was a more suitable fit for him.","What else could Guan Wenjun say?","Having a job at all was good enough; he wasn't going to be picky.","...","Qiao Lanshu followed Zhong Mei back and asked in a low voice, \"Zhong Mei, why did you suddenly run off? I was just about to ask Director Guan to help you find a place to live. He has a lot of people working for him and is quite familiar with this area.\"","Zhong Mei's face was a bit pale. She whispered, \"Director Guan? Who is he? A director at the Public Security Bureau?\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Of course not. He isn't a police officer.\"","Zhong Mei clutched her chest and breathed a sigh of relief.","Then, she heard Qiao Lanshu add, \"He is the director of the Provincial Revolutionary Committee.\"","The breath Zhong Mei had just let out caught in her throat, and she gasped sharply!","Zhong Mei's voice grew weak. \"The Revolutionary Committee?\"","She was doomed. That was even worse than the Public Security Bureau.","The Revolutionary Committee was far more terrifying than the police.","She had previously been sent to a labor camp by the people from the Revolutionary Committee, so she was deathly afraid of them.","Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei had been childhood friends. The moment Zhong Mei's expression changed, Qiao Lanshu noticed it.","Qiao Lanshu asked softly, \"What's wrong?\"","Zhong Mei said, conflicted, \"The man who took out handcuffs to arrest me the other day was actually that Director Guan.\"","Zhong Mei didn't know that Director Guan had mistaken her for a spy, which was why he had pulled out the handcuffs.","She hadn't meant to accidentally injure him, but what was done was done, and she felt deeply uneasy about it.","Hearing this, Qiao Lanshu looked shocked. \"Ah? No wonder Director Guan has a bandage wrapped around his head. So it turns out...\"","Qiao Lanshu thought about it for a moment and suddenly found it hilarious.","She stood there laughing, which instantly made Zhong Mei anxious.","She gave Qiao Lanshu a slight push and feigned anger. \"Oh, Comrade Little Qiao, stop laughing! This isn't funny at all!\"","Qiao Lanshu laughed for quite a while before finally stopping. Between chuckles, she said, \"I'm not laughing at you, I'm laughing at Director Guan. I really didn't expect that the person you beat up was actually him.\"","Guan Wenjun cared so much about his reputation and had such a strong sense of pride. He would absolutely never let anyone know that he had been beaten up by a woman.","For him to be staking out that spot, he must have been truly furious.","Qiao Lanshu understood Guan Wenjun's character quite well. She said to Zhong Mei, \"Don't worry. Director Guan doesn't have the time to keep staking out that place to catch you. He just came back not long ago and should be on leave, but his vacation only has a few days left. He will be transferred to a new job soon. I'm not sure which department he's going to, but it definitely won't be the Revolutionary Committee anymore. Once his transfer orders come down and he starts his new position, he'll be so busy his feet won't even touch the ground. When that happens, how could he possibly have the time to catch people for speculation and profiteering? Put your mind at ease. You can let this matter go.\"","Hearing Qiao Lanshu say this, Zhong Mei finally felt relieved.","She had gone through untold hardships to get to Longcheng and find Qiao Lanshu. Seeing that she now had a job, her life finally had some hope.","She genuinely just wanted to live a peaceful and stable life; she had no desire to take another trip to a labor camp.","She said in frustration, \"From now on, I will just work quietly and behave myself. After work, I'll go straight home and never wander around outside again. There are too many people in the city, and it's far too easy to get into trouble.\"","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, \"Alright, don't overthink it. Let's go look around the food factory again. We might just be able to find a house.\"","There were many houses around the food factory. The whole surrounding area was a residential district, mostly consisting of large, shared courtyard compounds.","Zhong Mei felt that living in a shared courtyard was perfectly fine; if she met good neighbors, they could look out for one another.","It was just hard to find one, as most of them were already occupied.","The two of them wandered around the area for a while. Then, as it was getting dark, Qiao Lanshu got ready to head home.","After all, looking at the time, Auntie Shi should be making dinner. She needed to go back and keep an eye on An'an. An'an was only a few months old and at an age where he couldn't be left alone.","As they came out of the alley, a little child suddenly crashed into her legs. Qiao Lanshu let out a cry of surprise, nearly knocked over by the kid.","Zhong Mei quickly grabbed her to steady her, glaring at the child. Whose kid is this? Oh my goodness, is this a briquette from Longcheng come to life?","Zhong Mei reached out to grab the child, but the soot-covered kid hugged Qiao Lanshu's leg and scurried around her to dodge Zhong Mei's hand. He even pointed at Zhong Mei and retorted, You are the briquette!","Zhong Mei was speechless.","Qiao Lanshu was overflowing with maternal instinct these days; seeing a child simply warmed her heart.","Her voice softened unconsciously. Her pants had been smeared black by the child. It looked like dirt, or maybe wood ash, but it didn't really seem like coal dust.","She took the child's hand, took a closer look at him, and immediately recognized him. Niuwa? How did you end up like this?","Niuwa used to be so fair and chubby. How did he turn into a little soot ball after getting lost?","She quickly crouched down and asked softly, Didn't they say they sent you to the Women's Federation director... to a pretty auntie's house? How did you run away? Everyone is looking for you.","Niuwa was very young, but perhaps it was an innate gift—he was extremely sensitive to people's emotions.","He could sense anyone who was impatient or held malicious intent toward him, and his subconscious reaction would be to run away.","Perhaps this was also a survival instinct.","Even though he was only four years old.","This included just now, when Zhong Mei saw him bump into Qiao Lanshu and instinctively glared at him with a bit of fierceness.","He immediately wanted to run away.","But Qiao Lanshu was very kind to him.","The first time they met on the train, he felt that this pretty sister only had good intentions toward him. At the very least, she was different from the others.","So when he saw her this time, he ran over again. He looked at Qiao Lanshu pitifully and said, I am so hungry. I want to eat noodles.","As he spoke, he swallowed hard and reached out to rub his tummy.","He was so hungry. He was so hungry every single day.","Ever since he left home, he hadn't had a full meal.","Qiao Lanshu looked around but didn't see anyone else.","She felt it was quite strange. Didn't Brother Zheng go to the police station?","The Revolutionary Committee, the police station, the Women's Federation... With so many people in these departments, how could they fail to find a single child?","She had only wandered around for a bit and had already found him.","Did those people even go out looking for the child at all?","Qiao Lanshu felt that something was wrong. Zhong Mei asked her in a low voice, Lanshu, do you know this kid?","Qiao Lanshu then told Zhong Mei about the child's situation.","Zhong Mei also found it suspicious. A Women's Federation director deals with women and children all the time, and she has kids of her own. How could she fail to keep an eye on one child? Did she just not care at all?","As long as one paid a little attention, no matter how stubborn a child was, they could be kept out of trouble.","Zhong Mei had raised her younger siblings since she was little, and there were so many naughty kids in the village. As the saying goes, every monkey has its own way of being tied up.","She strongly felt that a Women's Federation director shouldn't make such a mistake.","As Zhong Mei spoke, she asked, Are we going to take this kid to the police station?","Qiao Lanshu squatted on the ground and looked at Niuwa. \"Niuwa, tell us yourself. Do you want to go find the police officers?\"","Niuwa immediately shook his head. He said, \"Haye's tummy is rumbling like thunder, Haye wants to eat noodles.\"","Hearing him speak like this, Qiao Lanshu burst into laughter.","She picked Niuwa up and said, \"Alright then, let's go home and eat noodles first.\"","After all that babbling, the word \"noodles\" was the only one he pronounced clearly.","Zhong Mei was still saying, \"Haye, what does that mean? Is his name Haye? What a weird name.\"","The child's pronunciation was unclear, and the two sisters couldn't understand him either, so they gave up guessing and continued to call him Niuwa.","Qiao Lanshu carried Haye back to her own small courtyard.","Along the way, they didn't see any Revolutionary Committee members, police comrades, or militia patrols out on the streets looking for anyone.","She sighed, thinking it would be best to wait for Qin Yuanzheng to come back before discussing what to do next.","Such a good child couldn't just be left to wander the streets and eventually get abducted.","It was better to take him home first.","Back at the courtyard, Zhong Mei tightly closed the gate before walking in with Qiao Lanshu.","Auntie Shi had already started boiling the sweet potato and millet porridge in the kitchen, and a fresh batch of yellow cornmeal buns was steaming on the stove.","She was holding An'an in one arm and a water dipper in the other, watering the vegetable seedlings in the garden.","Seeing Qiao Lanshu come in carrying a dark, dirty child, she jumped in surprise. \"Oh my, where did this little sheep dropping come from? He's pitch black.\"","Hearing his nickname change from \"little coal ball\" to \"sheep dropping,\" Niuwa immediately pouted.","However, Auntie Shi meant him no harm and was even smiling at him, so he didn't run away.","Qiao Lanshu's clothes had gotten completely dirty from Niuwa. She smiled and said to Auntie Shi, \"Zhong Mei and I went looking for a house today, and we ended up picking up a child on the way. Look, it's a boy, smart and pretty.\"","The family who lost the child must be going crazy with worry, right?","Auntie Shi looked at the child and said hurriedly, \"Where did he go rolling around to get so dirty? I'll go wash him. Come, Zhong Mei, you hold An'an. Xiao Qiao, you go wash up too. Clean yourself up before you hold the baby.\"","Qiao Lanshu nodded in agreement and went to get her clothes first.","Auntie Shi went to the kitchen and took out all the steamed buns that were warming in the pot. The hot water underneath was clean, so she filled two buckets. She carried one bucket to the back for Qiao Lanshu to use in the washroom.","The other bucket she carried straight to the front yard. She took off Niuwa's clothes and washed him with a hot towel.","Niuwa struggled a bit at first; he hated taking baths.","But Auntie Shi was strong. What kind of naughty child hadn't she pinned down before?","She firmly held him down with one hand and scrubbed him, making Niuwa squeal and holler.","Zhong Mei sat nearby holding An'an, watching and laughing.","Even An'an was so happy that he danced with joy, grinning widely.","Angry, Niuwa pointed at An'an and said, \"Little brat, don't laugh at me.\"","Auntie Shi told him, \"Oh, give it a rest. Aren't you a little brat too?\"","Niuwa was a little afraid of Auntie Shi. She was too scary; she pinned him down, scrubbed his whole body red, and even washed his hair. He almost choked on the water and didn't dare to howl anymore.","By the time Niuwa finished his bath, Qiao Lanshu had also finished washing up and came out.","Auntie Shi pointed to the ground and said, \"Look, the water is completely black. Isn't it much better now that you're clean? Such a fair and chubby boy. Do you have a name? If not, I'll just call you Little Pig from now on.\"","Standing stark naked in the courtyard, Niuwa's eyes were red with anger as he shouted loudly, \"Haye is not a pig!\"","First a ball, then a sheep, and now a pig—Niuwa was so mad at them he was about to cry. He wanted to run away, but he didn't have any clothes on.","Being completely bare with his little bird exposed was far too embarrassing. Even though he was only four years old, he still had his pride.","He was simply too embarrassed to make a run for it.","He decided he would wait until he ate some noodles and put his clothes on, and then he would run!","But to his dismay, he heard Auntie Shi say to Qiao Lanshu, who had just come out holding his clothes, \"This kid still has a rebellious look in his eyes. He might try to escape again. Don't give him his clothes. If he's naked, he won't dare to run.\"","Niuwa: \"...\"","Niuwa felt as if the sky had just collapsed. He stared dumbfounded at Auntie Shi.","Was this woman a devil?","Qiao Lanshu was also stunned. She whispered to Auntie Shi, \"Are we really not going to dress him?\"","Auntie Shi laughed and said, \"Look at how shy he is without his clothes. He even knows to cover his little bird. Like this, he absolutely won't run away. In a little while, we'll fill his belly, give him some water, and send him to sleep on the kang bed. Don't worry, the weather is hot right now, so he won't catch a cold. If you feed him and dress him properly now, he might just run off in the middle of the night. Where would we even look for him then?\""]},{"number":198,"title":"Chapter 198: Looking for Someone","paragraphs":["Auntie Shi spoke with such certainty that Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei looked at each other in dismay, and then they both stared at the freshly washed, fair and tender Niuwa.","Niuwa was about to cry from anger. He looked at Auntie Shi with tearful eyes: \"You big meanie.\"","Auntie Shi glared at him: \"What did you say?\"","Niuwa: \"...\"","Niuwa shrank his neck. He ran to Qiao Lanshu, hugged her leg, and said pitifully, \"I want to wear clothes, Haye is so cold.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu felt a bit soft-hearted. This child was really too pitiful. But before she could speak, she saw Auntie Shi come out of the kitchen again, holding two steamed buns in her hands, saying, \"Who wants to eat steamed buns? Hot, delicious steamed buns.\"","Haye swallowed hard, his stomach growling. He walked over without any backbone, stood in front of Auntie Shi, and stared eagerly at the steamed buns in her hands, drooling.","Auntie Shi looked at him with a smile: \"Are you still cold?\"","Haye said pitifully: \"Not cold, I'm so hungry...\"","After all, he was only a four-year-old child. Although he was quite smart, under the temptation of delicious food, he had forgotten everything.","Clothes, running away, none of it was as important as having a full stomach.","Auntie Shi smiled and handed him the two steamed buns, telling him, \"Go inside and sit on the kang bed to eat.\"","Niuwa held a steamed bun in each hand and followed Auntie Shi into the room.","Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei also followed them in. Seeing Niuwa sitting on Auntie Shi's kang, Auntie Shi brought a towel over and wrapped it around Niuwa's stomach.","Auntie Shi smiled and said to Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei, \"Don't worry, he definitely won't leave today. This child is probably tired and sleepy. Once he's full, he'll likely want to sleep.\"","A child of this age, having wandered outside for so long, had probably exhausted his physical strength. He would be able to sleep right after eating his fill.","A four-year-old could also sleep through the night until tomorrow morning. They could figure out how to settle this child then.","Sure enough, Niuwa ate two steamed buns in a row. He wanted to eat more, but Auntie Shi didn't let him, afraid he would overeat.","After all, eating steamed buns and then drinking water could cause a bloated stomach.","Qiao Lanshu took some of An'an's milk powder and mixed a cup for Niuwa to drink.","Niuwa didn't show any surprised expression, as if milk powder was a common thing to him. He probably drank it often at home.","After drinking the milk, Niuwa indeed started to doze off, and it wasn't long before he fell asleep.","Qiao Lanshu whispered to Auntie Shi, \"Auntie, you're amazing!\"","Zhong Mei also said, \"Auntie Shi really has a way with children. If it were me, how could I have thought of not putting clothes on him? I would have just grabbed a rope and tied him up.\"","Hearing this, Auntie Shi covered her mouth and laughed. She said, \"You're right, I thought the same thing. I even have the rope ready.\"","Saying that, she actually took out a roll of red cloth strips from the cabinet.","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Zhong Mei: \"...\"","The two of them stood there, watching helplessly as Auntie Shi took the rope, tied one end to the leg of the cabinet by the kang, and the other end to Niuwa's leg.","Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei came out of the room, unable to hold back their amusement.","Zhong Mei whispered, \"Is that child really that good at running away?\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"Hard to say, but if he hadn't run around, maybe he wouldn't have been abducted. We still need to find Brother Zheng about this, after all, Brother Zheng brought him back.\"","...","Meanwhile, Zheng Wenhui had secretly searched for the child all afternoon, but couldn't find him.","Afraid that the matter would be exposed, she didn't know how to handle it herself.","So she hurriedly went to the Supply Section to look for her brother, Zheng Weigong.","However, she was one step too late. The people from the Revolutionary Committee had arrived there ahead of time.","This time, it wasn't Guan Wenjun who led the team, but the deputy director of the Revolutionary Committee.","They came to question Zheng Weigong, leaving him completely baffled: \"What illicit sexual relations? What illegitimate child? This is slander. Of course, I don't have any.\"","He said, and then calmly added, \"This is absolute nonsense!\"","Although Zheng Weigong cohabited with Liu Weihong and they were not married.","But Zheng Weigong was already divorced and currently single, and Liu Weihong was not married either.","An unmarried man and an unmarried woman, just dating. Usually, no one would ask about this.","Although things were strictly managed now, and cohabitation without a marriage certificate was not allowed.","But Zheng Weigong was also a section chief with a high status. As long as he said he and Liu Weihong were already engaged, no one would bother about it.","Anyway, no matter what, this couldn't be considered as having illicit sexual relations.","Besides, Zheng Weigong and his ex-wife divorced precisely because they didn't have children.","The reason why he and Liu Weihong delayed getting married was also because Liu Weihong hadn't gotten pregnant.","After his previous marriage, Zheng Weigong would only consider marriage when the woman was pregnant.","If there really was a woman outside who had given him a son, how could he let his own son become an illegitimate child?","Long before the child was born, he would have married her into the family and eagerly registered the child in his household.","Zheng Weigong was extremely speechless about this matter, and even too lazy to explain. He had never paid much attention to the people from the Revolutionary Committee anyway.","It was already 1976. In fact, the Revolutionary Committee was not what it used to be, and lacked the deterrent power of previous years.","Zheng Weigong stared at the deputy director of the Revolutionary Committee and added, \"Any random woman comes to report me, and you come to interrogate me without even investigating?","Is this how your Revolutionary Committee handles things? If I randomly arrange a woman to report you for illicit sexual relations tomorrow, will you also be arrested and interrogated? This is not how things are done. I will pretend this didn't happen today. You guys should hurry back.\"","The people from the Revolutionary Committee were originally just doing a routine inquiry. They didn't really intend to arrest Zheng Weigong.","After all, Liu Weihong only made a verbal report. She said the illegitimate child was lost, and she didn't know where the woman who had illicit relations was. Without witnesses or material evidence, the Revolutionary Committee was too lazy to care.","But the problem was that a child was missing. After coordinating with the Public Security Bureau, they found out that the child was rescued from human traffickers by Qin Yuanzheng, so they made the trip.","The deputy director of the Revolutionary Committee explained:","\"Section Chief Zheng, it's like this. The person who came to report you is your current wife, Liu Weihong. Also, your illegitimate child went missing, right at your doorstep, lost from the hands of your wife Liu Weihong and your sister Zheng Wenhui. Regardless of whether that child is your illegitimate son or not, this is a major issue. In order to find the child, I hope you can cooperate with us and explain the child's origins in detail.\"","Hearing this, Zheng Weigong's eyes instantly turned cold and gloomy.","Liu Weihong, this useless piece of trash who always ruined things.","He had long known that Liu Weihong had no brains. Plus, since her father and brother were taken away for labor reform and had lost their utility value, he should have kicked her out long ago.","But he had been busy with work lately, and had some important matters to handle.","It was exhausting not having a woman at home to care for him and attend to his needs.","Finding another young, easily manipulated woman wasn't something that could be done in a single day, which was why he had kept Liu Weihong around.","Well, now this woman had indeed caused trouble for him.","Zheng Weigong was tall with rugged features and a loud voice. He said impatiently, \"What child? I don't know. I've been working overtime these past few days. How would I know where they got a child from? Anyway, it's not my illegitimate son. If he's lost, it's none of my business. If you want to find someone, go look for him. Why are you bothering me?\"","The people from the Revolutionary Committee looked at Zheng Weigong. Seeing his genuine impatience, which didn't seem to be an act, they figured he really didn't know the inside story.","Then...","Could it really be a misunderstanding?","The committee members were unceremoniously shown the door by Zheng Weigong.","As they came out, they happened to see Zheng Wenhui coming to look for Zheng Weigong.","Zheng Wenhui ignored the committee members. She hurried to the section chief's office and saw Zheng Weigong cursing—naturally, at the people from the Revolutionary Committee.","Zheng Wenhui was actually afraid of this brother of hers, but she had to tell him about what happened today.","\"Brother.\"","Zheng Wenhui looked around. After making sure no one was there, she closed the office door and ran up to Zheng Weigong.","Seeing her approach, Zheng Weigong asked in frustration, \"What happened with you this afternoon? They said you lost a child? And that it's my illegitimate child?\"","Zheng Wenhui was speechless.","She stomped her foot in anger. \"Ugh, it's all because of that idiot Liu Weihong!\"","Zheng Wenhui quickly gave a brief account of how she had helped Qin Yuanzheng bring the child over, how Liu Weihong had misunderstood, and how the child had gotten lost.","Finally, she lowered her voice and said to Zheng Weigong, \"Brother, that child is from the Han family. The one you mentioned before, Han Ye.\"","Zheng Weigong paused, his expression immediately turning serious. \"Wasn't this child sent away? How did he come back?\"","Zheng Wenhui said nervously, \"I originally wanted to bring the child to your house for you to deal with, but... it's all Liu Weihong's fault! She suspected the child was your illegitimate son and wouldn't let me in. Then the child took the opportunity to run away. I wanted to quietly find him without alerting the police, but Liu Weihong actually went and reported you...\"","Zheng Wenhui was absolutely furious.","A perfectly good plan was ruined because Liu Weihong had to stick her nose in.","Zheng Weigong's face darkened. \"I've been planning this for so long, and it was just about to succeed... If Han Wenlin really comes to Longcheng to take up his post...\"","Zheng Weigong stood up and said hurriedly, \"No, we still can't let Han Wenlin come over. Try your best to find this child. If you can't find him, muddy the waters so they can't find him either. As long as the child isn't found, the result will be the same.\"","If he was found, they would either have to send the child away, or...","A ruthless look flashed across Zheng Weigong's eyes.","Han Wenlin was transferring to civilian work. Word had it that he was coming to the Longcheng Municipal Public Security Bureau to take up the post of chief.","Han Wenlin knew some of Zheng Weigong's secrets, so naturally, he didn't want Han Wenlin to come. Once Han Wenlin arrived, some of his schemes in Longcheng might be discovered.","Zheng Weigong had been operating in Longcheng for seven or eight years and didn't want to fall short at the final hurdle.","Han Wenlin should have taken up his post long ago, but because his only son went missing, he postponed his official duties and went everywhere asking for help to find the child.","But it was impossible for him to find him.","Because Han Wenlin's hometown was a city hundreds of kilometers away from Longcheng.","Zheng Weigong had gone to great lengths to have someone take Han Wenlin's only son, Han Ye, on several train transfers, planning to traffic him from the north to the deep mountains in the south.","If there hadn't been an accident on the train, and if Qin Yuanzheng hadn't run into him...","Zheng Weigong pulled a long face. He pondered for a long time before saying, \"The child must still be in the city. A four-year-old can't run far. We need to find him as soon as possible. You should go to work as usual lately. If those people find the child, they will send him to your Women's Federation for placement. Contact me when that happens.\"","Hearing her brother say this, Zheng Wenhui breathed a sigh of relief and finally felt settled. She nodded, \"Okay, I'll go back to work right now. I'll tell you as soon as there's any news.\"","Zheng Weigong nodded and hurriedly left the workplace as well, secretly sending people to look for the child.","If all else failed, he would have no choice but to make a move against Han Wenlin directly."]},{"number":199,"title":"Chapter 199: Could It Be That She Has Her Eyes on Me","paragraphs":["When Qin Yuanzheng heard that the child was missing, he immediately went to the police station for a meeting.","After all, he was the one who had rescued the child. Now that the child was lost again, it was inevitable that he would have to dispatch manpower to help search.","When Guan Wenjun returned, he ran into Qin Yuanzheng. He grabbed Qin Yuanzheng and said, \"Brigade Commander Qin, I heard my son is already a few months old, and as his godfather, I haven't even given him a red envelope yet. I happen to be free right now. Aren't you going to invite me over to sit for a bit?\"","Guan Wenjun gritted his teeth as he said the words \"Brigade Commander Qin,\" making his jealousy quite obvious.","Qin Yuanzheng was very annoyed at the moment. Knowing that Guan Wenjun was deliberately taking advantage of him, he didn't bother arguing and simply said, \"It's not a good time these next few days. Let's talk about it later.\"","As he spoke, he glanced at Guan Wenjun's forehead and added, \"You should just focus on recovering from your injuries. Your head was busted open, yet you still have the mood to come out and look for trouble.\"","Guan Wenjun was speechless.","Guan Wenjun relentlessly persisted, \"Hey, just let me go to your house for a meal. I haven't had a hot meal in days. I heard the nanny you hired is quite a good cook. I was even thinking of paying your family a monthly food allowance so I can eat at your place.\"","Qin Yuanzheng was exasperated. He shot him a glance and said, \"Not a chance.\"","Guan Wenjun had always harbored a bit of a crush on Qiao Lanshu. Qin Yuanzheng could barely fend him off as it was, why would he let him come to his house for dinner every day?","What man would agree to that?","At any rate, Qin Yuanzheng definitely would not.","He sneered and said, \"You're not getting any younger. You might as well find a female comrade and get married. It would save you from fooling around all day.\"","Guan Wenjun was only two years younger than Qin Yuanzheng. Qin Yuanzheng was already thirty, which meant Guan Wenjun was twenty-eight.","That was not a young age by any means.","As Qin Yuanzheng spoke, he had already reached his car parked by the road and was preparing to get in.","He had been busy all day, and the child he had managed to rescue with great difficulty was lost again. Although he was irritated, he didn't need to go looking for the child himself.","Leaving the matter to the Revolutionary Committee, the civilian patrol squads, and the police station was more than enough.","Their military unit had other missions to carry out.","However, he still had to go home to eat. Even though he wasn't sleeping at home these past few days, he returned every day for lunch and dinner. After all, he needed to see his wife and son.","To his surprise, Guan Wenjun brazenly opened the car door and got in as well.","He smiled and said, \"Brigade Commander Qin, it's just adding an extra pair of chopsticks. Don't be so stingy. Look, I even bought formula for your son, and I bought some mutton.\"","He held up the items in his hands for Qin Yuanzheng to see.","There were two tins of milk powder and a strip of mutton about two fingers wide.","Who knew where Guan Wenjun had managed to exchange for the milk powder ration coupons, but he had bought two tins at once.","For the sake of the milk powder, Qin Yuanzheng didn't kick him out of the car. He merely said, \"It's getting late. Auntie Shi has probably already finished cooking, and she usually doesn't make extra portions.\"","Guan Wenjun said nonchalantly, \"That's fine, a bowl of hot porridge will do. Since I got back these past few days, I've been eating cold steamed buns with cold water every day. You have no idea how miserable I've been.\"","Qin Yuanzheng couldn't be bothered to entertain him.","It was Guan Wenjun's own fault for being lazy. If he wanted something hot, couldn't he light a fire and cook for himself?","But for the sake of the two tins of milk powder, Qin Yuanzheng didn't mock him, leaving him with a little dignity.","Qin Yuanzheng brought Guan Wenjun home. It was already quite late, and the sky was getting dark.","After entering the small courtyard, Guan Wenjun strolled around it a couple of times.","Then he praised it endlessly, \"Lao Qin, this yard is really not bad. Where else can one find a yard like this? I want to apply for one too.\"","Qin Yuanzheng deliberately jabbed at him, \"Single men can't apply. You don't meet the qualifications.\"","Guan Wenjun was speechless again.","Guan Wenjun was so angry he wanted to curse at him again.","But Qiao Lanshu, hearing the voices, came out at that moment.","There were currently two children in the house, and both were already asleep.","Niuwa slept in Auntie Shi's room, while An'an slept in Qiao Lanshu's room.","The three women had only lit lamps inside the rooms, leaving the courtyard pitch black.","Qiao Lanshu stood on the courtyard steps, looking somewhat surprised. She called out loudly, \"Director Guan? It's so late, why are you here again?\"","As she spoke, Qiao Lanshu turned her head with some concern and looked at Zhong Mei.","Zhong Mei was in the kitchen, bringing out dishes. The moment she heard the words \"Director Guan,\" she jolted, turned around, placed the dish back on the stove, and said to Auntie Shi, \"Auntie, it seems we have a guest today. I'm going to hide in the room for a bit. You all go ahead and eat without me.\"","With that, Zhong Mei hurriedly ran into the house.","Auntie Shi was holding a bowl and serving porridge. Hearing this, she said in surprise, \"Ah? There's no need to hide, right? Let's eat together?\"","However, before Auntie Shi could finish her sentence, Zhong Mei had already bolted.","Auntie Shi was left speechless.","Guan Wenjun handed the milk powder and meat to Qiao Lanshu, smiling brightly as he said, \"I came to see my godson. Where is the child?\"","As he spoke, he walked into the living room. At a glance, he saw a basin of fragrant yellow-flour steamed buns on the dining table. Suddenly feeling ravenous, he hurried over, grabbed one, and started eating.","He hadn't eaten much all day and was truly starving.","Qiao Lanshu placed the milk powder and meat on a shelf next to the living room and said, \"You've come at a bad time. The child is already asleep.\"","Hearing this, Guan Wenjun said with some regret, \"How did he fall asleep so early? What time is it?\"","Chewing on his steamed bun, he added, \"Even if he's asleep, I can still take a look, right? I haven't even seen what the child looks like yet.\"","With that, he walked toward the adjacent room.","Qin Yuanzheng followed behind him and said, \"Keep your voice down and tread lightly.\"","Guan Wenjun nodded and walked quietly into the room.","Qiao Lanshu assumed Zhong Mei was hiding in Auntie Shi's room, so she didn't stop Guan Wenjun.","An'an was just lying on the kang bed; taking a peek wouldn't hurt.","But who would have thought that Zhong Mei, in her extreme panic earlier, had run straight into Qiao Lanshu's room by convenience.","The room wasn't large. It only had a large kang bed, a wooden wardrobe, a table, and chairs.","There was nowhere to hide.","Before she could find a hiding spot, Guan Wenjun walked in, and their eyes met.","Zhong Mei felt the hairs all over her body stand on end.","She stood leaning against the wardrobe, motionless, staring nervously at Guan Wenjun.","A small oil lamp was lit in the room. Guan Wenjun first noticed An'an sleeping peacefully on the kang.","Then, he saw Zhong Mei.","Guan Wenjun was utterly shocked.","The moment Guan Wenjun saw Zhong Mei, he was stunned.","His first reaction was that Qin Yuanzheng, that hypocrite, had finally stopped pretending and was secretly keeping a mistress behind Comrade Xiao Qiao's back.","His second reaction was, oh wait, no, this girl must be Comrade Xiao Qiao's friend.","To avoid any misunderstanding, Guan Wenjun stepped out of the room, finished the steamed bun in his hand, and then said to Qiao Lanshu, \"Comrade Xiao Qiao, your friend is in the room. Why didn't you tell me?\"","If he had known, he wouldn't have gone in. Look how he had terrified that poor girl.","Qiao Lanshu had only just realized that Zhong Mei was in her room.","However, observing Guan Wenjun's expression, she asked tentatively, \"You saw my friend?\"","Guan Wenjun nodded. \"Yeah.\"","Adding to that, he said, \"The steamed buns Auntie Shi makes are exceptionally delicious. I'm going to have another one.\"","Saying this, he went to grab another steamed bun to eat.","Qin Yuanzheng also sat down and took a steamed bun to eat.","After all, Qin Yuanzheng was hungry too. He had been so busy today that he hadn't had a chance to eat anything all day.","Qiao Lanshu looked at Guan Wenjuan's expression again and felt a bit happy inside.","Guan Wenjuan really hadn't recognized Zhong Mei.","It seemed that Zhong Mei cutting her hair short had been useful.","While eating, Guan Wenjuan asked curiously, \"Isn't your friend coming out to eat with us?\"","Qin Yuanzheng also looked at Qiao Lanshu. \"Zhong Mei isn't eating?\"","Qiao Lanshu said in a low voice, \"She's not hungry, let's just leave her be for now.\"","Qin Yuanzheng didn't say anything more.","After Guan Wenjuan had eaten and drunk his fill, seeing that it was already dark outside, he didn't stay long and tactfully took his leave.","As Guan Wenjuan was leaving, he glanced over and saw Qiao Lanshu's friend again, the one named Zhong Mei. She was standing at the door of the room, poking her head out and secretly looking at him.","Guan Wenjuan thought he had seen wrong. He paused his steps and looked over again, only to see the girl pull her head back as if she were shy.","Guan Wenjuan: \"...\"","Hiss, this is getting interesting.","Guan Wenjuan walked out the door, smoothed his hair, and put his hands in his pockets. He thought to himself that he was indeed a handsome and talented man. Wasn't it perfectly normal for a girl to peek at him?","Not to mention, worthy of being Comrade Xiao Qiao's friend, she had good taste.","Thinking this, Guan Wenjuan began to recall what that Zhong Mei actually looked like.","Well, he had only caught a quick glimpse of her in the room just now. She seemed quite thin, with a melon-seed-shaped face, big eyes, and straight bangs. The way she looked at him was a bit nervous and evasive, so it seemed she was just shy.","A pretty nice girl, it was just that...","Guan Wenjuan paused his steps and frowned in deep thought.","It was just that, this girl, seemed as if she looked... a bit familiar.","Could it be...","Guan Wenjuan's expression froze, and his face became a bit serious.","Could it be a destiny from a past life?","...","After Guan Wenjuan left, Zhong Mei still quietly poked her head out to take a look, confirming that he had gone out the door.","Zhong Mei immediately ran out, closed the courtyard gate, and locked it directly.","It was too scary; thankfully he hadn't recognized her.","Zhong Mei had been on edge all evening, not even in the mood to eat.","Auntie Shi was still teasing her, saying, \"Are you that afraid of Director Guan? But after all, he is the director of the Revolutionary Committee, so he is indeed a bit intimidating.\"","Zhong Mei smiled awkwardly, too embarrassed to explain.","Auntie Shi told Zhong Mei to go eat, so Zhong Mei went to the kitchen to eat.","Auntie Shi was cleaning up and washing dishes in the kitchen.","Qin Yuanzheng seized the opportunity to watch An'an in the room with Qiao Lanshu for a while. He even closed the door and hugged Qiao Lanshu to be affectionate for a bit.","He kissed Qiao Lanshu for a moment before whispering, \"When can I come back to live here?\"","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice and said, \"Soon, but Brother Zheng, I have something to tell you.\"","Qin Yuanzheng pressed Qiao Lanshu against the wall, looking at her fair and rosy little face under the warm yellow oil lamp.","His own wife was really getting more and more beautiful the more he looked at her, and he liked her more and more.","He hadn't been able to come back to live recently. Unable to hold his wife to sleep at night, he couldn't fall asleep at all.","Coming back to eat every day was also a rush. He had finally managed to live a life with a wife, a child, and a warm bed, but now he had to face this kind of situation. Qin Yuanzheng felt sour in his heart.","He pinched Qiao Lanshu's cheek and whispered, \"Didn't you say you were renting a house for Zhong Mei? Did you rent one?\"","Qiao Lanshu shook her head. \"We haven't found a suitable one yet. Tomorrow Zhong Mei and I will go out and look again. The work situation has been sorted out. She's a temporary worker for now, and the salary is a bit low, but it's not a big problem. If the money isn't enough, I'll just subsidize her a bit.\"","Qiao Lanshu had saved up some money herself. Added to what her father sent her and what Qin Yuanzheng gave her, she estimated she had over a thousand yuan in total.","She had already made up her mind; she would pay for Zhong Mei's rent.","In the future, when Zhong Mei had the chance to become a regular employee or got married, only then would she be able to completely set her mind at ease.","Qin Yuanzheng hugged Qiao Lanshu and said, \"I'm still waiting for you to make a move.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"...\"","Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but laugh. She actually missed Qin Yuanzheng quite a bit too, but this wasn't the time to be intimate.","She lowered her voice and said, \"Brother Zheng, come with me.\"","Saying that, she went to take another look at An'an. Seeing that An'an was still fast asleep, she led Qin Yuanzheng out of the room and went towards Auntie Shi's room next door.","Qin Yuanzheng asked curiously, \"If we're just talking, why are we going to Auntie Shi's room?\"","Since moving here, Qin Yuanzheng had never been to Auntie Shi's room.","After all, it was where the nanny lived. As a man, Qin Yuanzheng still needed to avoid arousing suspicion, and it was never good to casually barge into someone else's room.","How inappropriate would that be?","Qiao Lanshu lowered her voice and said, \"You'll know once you come in with me.\"","The two arrived at Auntie Shi's room. A small oil lamp was also lit in the room, making the lighting a bit dim.","But right inside the door was the kang bed, so Qin Yuanzheng immediately saw a child lying on it.","Qin Yuanzheng: \"???\"","Qin Yuanzheng's expression paused for a moment. He glanced at Qiao Lanshu, suddenly thought of something in his heart, and took large strides over.","Sure enough, Niuwa, who had gotten lost that afternoon, was currently lying on his stomach on the kang with a bare bottom, sleeping soundly.","Qin Yuanzheng carefully examined Niuwa and saw that there was still a rope tied to Niuwa's foot, suddenly feeling a bit torn between laughter and tears.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"When I went out this afternoon, this child came looking for me himself. I was afraid he would run away again, so I brought him home first.\"","Qin Yuanzheng whispered, \"This kid is pretty smart, knowing to come find you.\"","Qiao Lanshu: \"I'm not familiar with this child either. I've only met him once. Why isn't he afraid of me? When you sent him to the Women's Federation director, why did he run away?\"","Qin Yuanzheng: \"It's hard to say. This child's identity hasn't been found out yet. Otherwise, let's just let him stay at our house for these few days?\"","He discussed it with Qiao Lanshu: \"I'm afraid that if we send him to the Women's Federation, he'll escape again, and then he'll be even harder to find. Besides, I always feel that there are people here in Longcheng targeting this child. It would be better to hide him first and see how the various departments react.\"","At a glance, it was obvious that this child had an unusual background.","If he were from Longcheng, having been missing for so many days, Qin Yuanzheng would have received news of it long ago.","But so far, he hadn't heard anyone in Longcheng mention whose child had gone missing, and there was no news on the local radio or in the newspapers either.","Qin Yuanzheng felt that his previous guess was wrong.","This child might not necessarily be a local.","Qiao Lanshu naturally had no objections. It was just feeding an extra child, which wouldn't cost much.","The main concern was that this child would run around recklessly.","Qiao Lanshu pondered, they couldn't just keep Niuwa without clothes all the time, could they?"]},{"number":200,"title":"Chapter 200: Snatching the Child","paragraphs":["Just like that, Niuwa stayed at Qiao Lanshu's house.","Originally, Qiao Lanshu thought the matter would be settled in three or four days at most.","As a result, several days passed, and the police station still hadn't found any clues about Niuwa's family.","Qiao Lanshu didn't dare take Niuwa out either. This was what Qin Yuanzheng had instructed, saying he was afraid the child might be recognized by certain people and taken away, which would cause more trouble.","Niuwa was kept in the small courtyard every day. After thinking it over, Qiao Lanshu decided to put some clothes on him.","A little pink dress.","This was an old piece of clothing worn by Huang Erling's daughter that she had brought over. The original intention was for Qiao Lanshu to alter it so An'an could wear it.","Auntie Shi said that if they put the little dress on Niuwa, he would be too embarrassed to run around.","Sure enough, Niuwa didn't dare to run around.","Wearing the little dress every day, he fed the chickens and sheep in the yard, and also dug in the dirt. Once, he pulled up all the vegetable seedlings Auntie Shi had just planted.","Auntie Shi was furious. She grabbed Niuwa and gave him a good spanking.","Niuwa cried, his eyes brimming with tears, and that very day he tried to crawl through the dog hole to escape this house.","And then, Niuwa got stuck in the dog hole.","Auntie Shi and Qiao Lanshu, holding An'an, stood there laughing out loud.","Auntie Shi laughed heartily for a long time before saying to Qiao Lanshu, You look at this child. At lunch, he ate two steamed buns and a bowl of milk powder, stuffing his little belly until it was bulging. And now he actually tried to squeeze through a dog hole. Isn't that hilarious?","Qiao Lanshu also chuckled quietly for a while. Stuck in the dog hole, Niuwa cried loudly, his bottom wedged tight, and sobbed to Qiao Lanshu, Auntie Qiao, I was wrong, please save me, boohoo.","Qiao Lanshu was soft-hearted. Holding An'an, she walked over and said to Auntie Shi, Auntie, should we get him out first?","Having laughed enough, Auntie Shi said, You stand back, let me do it.","Saying that, she went over, grabbed Niuwa's legs, gave a gentle tug, and pulled the stuck Niuwa out of the dog hole.","Niuwa had cried until his face was flushed red, his face covered in snot and tears.","As soon as he was pulled out of the hole, he ran over to Qiao Lanshu whimpering, hugged her thigh, and bawled loudly.","Qiao Lanshu, both annoyed and amused, scolded him, Why did you go and crawl into a dog hole for no reason? Are you going to do it again?","Niuwa didn't shake his head, nor did he say he wouldn't do it again; he just kept crying.","Auntie Shi remarked, I have to say, this kid has some backbone. If he doesn't want to do something, he absolutely won't agree to it. I reckon he'll try crawling through it again later.","Niuwa looked at Auntie Shi with some terror and muttered, Bad guy.","Auntie Shi really was too wicked; she had him completely figured out and under her thumb.","How could there be such a terrifying woman?","However, Niuwa was also very easy to coax. When Qiao Lanshu handed him a piece of date cake, he immediately stopped crying. Holding the cake in both hands, he sat on the steps and ate it bite by bite.","While tidying up the vegetable garden, Auntie Shi said, It's been several days, why hasn't this child's family been found yet? Ever since he arrived, our yard has been in absolute chaos, and the chickens in the backyard are nearly bald.","Although her tone was complaining, there was a smile on Auntie Shi's face.","After all, who wouldn't like such a chubby, fair-skinned child who loved to eat and sleep, and was incredibly smart despite being mischievous?","Qiao Lanshu held An'an in her arms, watching him drink from his milk bottle.","She sat down next to Niuwa with An'an in her arms, sighed, and said, Brother Zheng said this child might be from out of town. His home is probably very far from Yangcheng, which is why it's so hard to find them.","In this era, transportation and communication were underdeveloped, making it very difficult for information to spread out of many cities.","The speed of information transmission was very slow.","If two cities were too far apart, it was like looking for a needle in a haystack.","Qiao Lanshu thought for a moment and added, If we really can't find them, it's fine for me to adopt him. That way, An'an will have an older brother.","Auntie Shi smiled and said, Not just you, even I'd want to adopt him. This kid is smart; he'll definitely achieve great things when he grows up.","Auntie Shi continued, I see An'an is quite active too. In the future, he'll surely be a little devil who turns the house upside down.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Looking at the child quietly drinking his milk, Qiao Lanshu couldn't help but smile.","Niuwa had finished his date cake by this time. He leaned over, looked at An'an, and called out, Little devil, little devil.","Qiao Lanshu: ...","Qiao Lanshu sighed and rubbed Niuwa's sweaty little head. Seeing that it was about time, she handed the milk-finished An'an to Auntie Shi, asking her to watch the two children at home while she went to the food factory to pick up Zhong Mei from work.","Then she would go look at houses with Zhong Mei.","The two of them had been house hunting for the past few days and had found a suitable one in a multi-family courtyard. Two families were already living there, and the remaining unit only had two rooms. The previous owner felt it was too narrow for their large family and had moved out.","Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei had already seen it before and both thought it was quite nice. This was their second visit.","Arm in arm, with Qiao Lanshu carrying a vegetable basket, they came out of the food factory, crossed the street, passed through an alley, and arrived at the courtyard.","It was very close to the food factory, not far from Qiao Lanshu's home, and the supply and marketing cooperative was also nearby.","Qiao Lanshu said to Zhong Mei, This courtyard is good. Let's lock it down today.","Zhong Mei nodded, Okay.","The rent was one dollar and fifty cents a month. Zhong Mei actually felt it was a bit expensive; she was used to being frugal and thought renting any place for a dollar would be fine.","But Qiao Lanshu insisted on this one, saying it was safe to live here.","Of the other two households living in the courtyard, one was a family of four: two elderly parents, their son, and daughter-in-law, with no grandchildren yet.","The son and daughter-in-law were both workers at a nearby factory. The old lady didn't work, and the old man was an employee at the waste station.","They all had legitimate jobs, so they seemed like good people.","As for the other household, they hadn't seen them yet.","When Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei arrived there again, the old lady from the next door was just squatting by the courtyard well washing vegetables.","Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei went over to greet her and asked her about the other family.","Seeing that two girls were moving in, the old lady was also happy. After all, who wouldn't want to have hassle-free neighbors?","Young girls are clean and quiet, which was much better than the previous large family of five or six people crammed in here.","The old lady said happily, Oh, a young couple lives in the next room. They also moved in not long ago and work at the nearby garment factory. The couple is very easy to get along with, so you can move in with peace of mind.","Zhong Mei and Qiao Lanshu exchanged a glance, smiled, and thanked the old lady.","Qiao Lanshu even took out a freshly bought melon from her basket and gave it to the old lady.","The old lady refused to take it and insisted on stuffing it back.","Qiao Lanshu smiled and said, We'll be neighbors from now on, and we'll be counting on you to look after us. Please don't be so polite with us, grandma.","The old lady beamed as she accepted the melon, becoming even more welcoming. She said, \"That room has only been vacant for a little over a month, and everything inside is still kept in good order. If you need any help, just come to me. Please don't hesitate to ask.\"","Zhong Mei and Qiao Lanshu agreed, and then went to look around the rooms.","Neither of the two rooms was large. One room had a kang bed, which was quite big, taking up more than half the space. Visually, it could sleep a family of four.","The other room had a stove, but some of the bricks were damaged and needed fixing.","Furthermore, there was no pot on the stove, let alone tables, chairs, benches, bedsheets, or bedding.","Everything would have to be purchased, which would cost quite a bit of money.","However, the house was quite nice. At the very least, it didn't need major repairs, and the kang could still be used without having to be rebuilt.","Qiao Lanshu whispered, \"How about here? Let's go to the Housing Administration Office and rent it today.\"","In these times, most houses were allocated by work units; public housing directly managed by the Housing Administration Office was rare.","Now that they had found a suitable place, Qiao Lanshu felt they should act fast and rent it immediately.","Naturally, Zhong Mei had no objections. She also liked it here very much; she had long wanted a room of her own.","She happily said, \"This place is great! Let's go to the Housing Administration Office right now. I already have the introduction letter from the food factory, and the money is ready.\"","The two walked out of the courtyard happily, but just as they reached the intersection, they saw a woman acting suspiciously, running into the alley with a child in her arms.","Both Zhong Mei and Qiao Lanshu saw her, but Zhong Mei didn't recognize her, while Qiao Lanshu did.","She gasped, grabbed Zhong Mei's arm, and whispered, \"Why does that look so much like Niuwa?\"","Zhong Mei stared in that direction for a moment and whispered, \"It does look a bit like him...\"","But wasn't Auntie Shi keeping a close eye on him? How did Niuwa still manage to run out?","Qiao Lanshu frowned and said, \"The person holding the child is my former colleague, Liu Weihong. Her character isn't very good... Zhong Mei, you go home first to check on Auntie Shi and An'an. I'm worried about them... I'll chase after her to take a look. If it really is Niuwa, I have to bring the child back.\"","Pressed for time and unable to think too much, Zhong Mei nodded after hearing this and quickly ran home.","If Niuwa had been taken away, what if An'an was taken too?","Zhong Mei hurriedly ran home, while Qiao Lanshu went after Liu Weihong.","Although she was also worried about An'an, Zhong Mei wasn't very familiar with Longcheng. If she got lost and lost track of the person, they wouldn't be able to find Niuwa.","Zhong Mei ran home panting, just in time to see Auntie Shi standing at the courtyard gate holding An'an, talking to a neighbor.","Seeing Zhong Mei return, she quickly said loudly, \"Zhong Mei, you're finally back! Oh dear, Niuwa just ran out. I chased after him but couldn't find him. I wanted to go to the police, but An'an is still little, and I didn't dare take An'an out with me...\"","Zhong Mei ran up to her, saw that Auntie Shi was still holding the baby, and quickly pulled her into the house.","Auntie Shi carried An'an back into the courtyard, and Zhong Mei whispered, \"Auntie Shi, stay in the house with An'an and don't go anywhere. Lanshu and I just saw Niuwa. I have to go help Lanshu now. Lock the door and don't go out, understand?\"","Auntie Shi nodded solemnly. \"Don't worry, I know what to do. My job is to take care of An'an, so I definitely won't run around.\"","When Niuwa ran out just now, she had wanted to chase after him, but considering An'an, she decided against it.","To be selfish, she was An'an's nanny, and her duty was to care for An'an.","Niuwa wasn't Brigade Commander Qin's child to begin with, so if he got lost, she wouldn't be the one to blame, right?","Zhong Mei searched around the room, grabbed a carrying pole, and ran out aggressively.","Auntie Shi: \"...\"","Auntie Shi hurriedly followed behind her and called out, \"Hey, be careful! Don't do anything reckless!\"","Zhong Mei didn't say a word, but she shut the courtyard door.","Auntie Shi: \"...\"","Auntie Shi felt the situation was somewhat serious, so she ran to the door again and asked the next-door neighbor to pass a message to Qin Yuanzheng at the mining area troops, telling him to quickly go find Qiao Lanshu and Zhong Mei."]}]);
